y reporter with The New York Times, talks about a recent article he wrote about computer scientists at Dartmouth who developed software tools that can objectively measure the amount of alterations that have been applied to photos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/16/technology/bits-podcast/bits-podcast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/16/technology/bits-podcast/bits-podcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/16/technology/bits-podcast/bits-podcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Talk Podcast: Altered Photos and Shopping Apps', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T00:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29562979-9e14-530d-9ce0-ee3077c0ce6c', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29562979-9e14-530d-9ce0-ee3077c0ce6c'}, {'abstract': 'The London-based architect created an installation for the fair, a gazebo that is “neither a piece of furniture nor a piece of architecture.’’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/garden/david-adjaye-design-miamis-designer-of-the-year-qa.html', 'snippet': 'The London-based architect created an installation for the fair, a gazebo that is “neither a piece of furniture nor a piece of architecture.’’', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2011 Designer of the Year chosen by Design Miami, the annual design fair that runs concurrently with Art Basel Miami Beach, is not just a designer. This year, the selection committee picked an architect — albeit one who works frequently with artists and art collectors.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/garden/01QNA_SPAN/01QNA_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/01/garden/01QNA_SPAN/01QNA_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/garden/01QNA_SPAN/01QNA_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/garden/01QNA_SPAN/01QNA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/01/garden/01QNA_SPAN/01QNA_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Adjaye, Design Miami’s Designer of the Year', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'David Adjaye on Building With the Language of Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adjaye, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE',