ppet': 'I’ll be the one with the beard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My head will join Joe Nocera’s and Carmen Reinhart’s, moderated by Tom Friedman, on Tuesday. The event will be streamed live.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heads Talking On Stage', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T01:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed6c335-f52f-5ae7-a0de-dc867b12d427', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed6c335-f52f-5ae7-a0de-dc867b12d427'}, {'abstract': 'Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor convicted of trying to sell or trade the Senate seat once held by President Obama, should go to prison for 15 to 20 years, federal prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/us/illinois-prison-sought-for-rod-blagojevich.html', 'snippet': 'Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor convicted of trying to sell or trade the Senate seat once held by President Obama, should go to prison for 15 to 20 years, federal prosecutors said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor convicted of trying to sell or trade the Senate seat once held by President Obama, should go to prison for 15 to 20 years, federal prosecutors said in legal papers filed Wednesday. Lawyers for Mr. Blagojevich, a Democrat convicted of 18 corruption-related counts, have indicated they will seek probation when a judge sentences him next week. Mr. Blagojevich is the second consecutive Illinois governor to face prison; George Ryan, his predecessor and a Republican, is serving a corruption sentence. In their filing, prosecutors wrote, “On the heels of one corrupt governor and after running on a campaign to end ‘pay-to-play,’ Blagojevich took office and immediately began plotting with others to use the office of the governor for his personal gain through fraud, bribery and extortion.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Prison Sought for Blagojevich', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Prison Sought For Blagojevich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blagojevich, Rod R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extortion and Blackmail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T01:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5f2b56-0edf-5425-8ee7-a96308c42f56', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5f2b56-0edf-5425-8ee7-a96308c42f56'}, {'abstract': 'Osi Umenyiora’s sprained ankle will keep him out of Sunday’s game against the Green Bay Packers and probably another week or two after that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/sports/football/giants-umenyiora-is-out-but-bradshaw-may-play.html', 'snippet': 'Osi Umenyiora’s sprained ankle will keep him out of Sunday’s game against the Green Bay Packers and probably another week or two after that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Michael Strahan visited the Giants’ practice center Wednesday, and it would have been understandable if Coach Tom Coughlin had tried to give him a uniform. The Giants’ pass defense has gone from feared to fragile over the past few weeks, and the latest development — Osi Umenyiora’s sprained ankle will keep him out of Sunday’s game against the Green Bay Packers and probably another week or two after that — figures to only make things worse.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Lose Umenyiora; Bradshaw May Play', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Lose Umenyiora, but Bradshaw May Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierre-Paul, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boley, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Umenyiora, Osi', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T01:32:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/247d6b3f-05d8-5ce4-b517-524f0e5e0e64', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247d6b3f-05d8-5ce4-b517-524f0e5e0e64'}, {'abstract': 'Cleanup crews with Suncor Energy were trying to contain a small spill near a Denver-area oil refinery on Wednesday after liquid began seeping into a creek this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/business/energy-environment/colorado-spill-near-suncor-energy-refinery-is-investigated.html', 'snippet': 'Cleanup crews with Suncor Energy were trying to contain a small spill near a Denver-area oil refinery on Wednesday after liquid began seeping into a creek this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cleanup crews with Suncor Energy were trying to contain a small spill near a Denver-area oil refinery on Wednesday after liquid began seeping into a creek this week. Suncor was investigating the source of the leak and what precisely was oozing into the creek near its refinery in Commerce City. Workers were trying to keep the liquid from flowing into the South Platte River. Curtis Kimbel, an Environmental Protection Agency coordinator, described the material as a petroleum-type substance. Workers had contained the spill to an area of about 75 yards, he said. The National Wildlife Federation said it was concerned that the material could contain Canadian oil sands crude, which can be difficult to clean because it is so thick.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado: Spill Near Refinery Is Investigated', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colorado: Spill Near Refinery Is Investigated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refineries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Spills', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T01:32:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Frosch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frosch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fac6fe1-0e5c-5106-bd7d-262e81d838e4', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fac6fe1-0e5c-5106-bd7d-262e81d838e4'}, {'abstract': 'Shahid R. Khan, who has an agreement to buy the Jacksonville Jaguars for $760 million, had coveted ownership of a professional sports franchise, particularly an N.F.L. team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/sports/football/shahid-khan-buys-jacksonville-jaguars-and-realizes-dream.html', 'snippet': 'Shahid R. Khan, who has an agreement to buy the Jacksonville Jaguars for $760 million, had coveted ownership of a professional sports franchise, particularly an N.F.L. team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shahid R. Khan, who agreed this week to acquire the Jacksonville Jaguars, has coveted an N.F.L. team for several years. Khan’s love of football was nurtured at the University of Illinois at Champaign-Urbana, and his riches as an auto parts manufacturer made the dream possible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/sports/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/01/sports/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/sports/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID/ALT-Y-JP-SHAHID-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '