hout a firm grasp of each society’s culture and history, discussions of fundamental rights tend to slide toward harsh and automatic conclusions on each side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/opinion/to-understand-china-look-behind-its-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Without a firm grasp of each society’s culture and history, discussions of fundamental rights tend to slide toward harsh and automatic conclusions on each side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shanghai', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Understand China, Look Behind Its Laws', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T02:12:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norm Page', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Page', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/efdd606b-e7f4-550e-8b06-dac6f50ee7f3', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efdd606b-e7f4-550e-8b06-dac6f50ee7f3'}, {'abstract': 'Good news, people! The former governor of Massachusetts really has told the truth at least once.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/opinion/gail-collins-mitt-romney-pardon.html', 'snippet': 'Good news, people! The former governor of Massachusetts really has told the truth at least once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been superexciting watching one outsized, vibrant and deeply strange Republican candidate after another rise to the front of the presidential pack, then crash and burn. But now we’ve got to refresh the storyline.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mitt Romney Pardon', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mitt Romney Pardon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T02:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e2b15be-f065-59a8-bd2e-ad2184353b24', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e2b15be-f065-59a8-bd2e-ad2184353b24'}, {'abstract': 'The moribund economy has driven many middle-class families to apply for school lunch subsidies for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/11/30/more-children-need-a-free-breakfast-lunch-and-dinner/', 'snippet': 'The moribund economy has driven many middle-class families to apply for school lunch subsidies for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I never thought a program like this would apply to me and my kids.” That’s what parents in the Gates Chili school district outside\xa0 Rochester are telling Debbi Beauvais, who administers the school meals program there. In a front-page article on Wednesday, The Times reported that around Rochester and across the country, suburban poverty means that schools are finding themselves serving more free or low-cost lunches — and breakfasts. And last year, when the proportion of students who qualified for free or subsidized lunches in the Hickman Mills C-1 district of Kansas City, Mo., hit 80 percent, the school began offering a third meal after the end of classes, paid for by the state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Children Need a Free Breakfast, Lunch — and Dinner', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch and Breakfast Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T02:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52e8679b-91d0-53f1-bed8-3b85d3b4b7ed', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52e8679b-91d0-53f1-bed8-3b85d3b4b7ed'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Phillips, a former general manager of the Mets, and Bobby Valentine began as allies when working in the Mets’ minor league system in the mid-1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/sports/baseball/regretful-phillips-takes-blame-for-feud-with-valentine.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Phillips, a former general manager of the Mets, and Bobby Valentine began as allies when working in the Mets’ minor league system in the mid-1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Phillips’s tenure as general manager of the Mets was marked by his feud with Manager Bobby Valentine. A few years ago, he would have been challenged to say anything good about Valentine.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr