ose rationale — deficit savings — as they try on Thursday to repeal the public financing option for presidential campaigns. This is the highly effective reform enacted after the Watergate scandal. It is revealing that just as a new era of unbridled corporate and special-interest money engulfs the 2012 elections, Republicans are determined to kill off the public financing option. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watergate? Whatever Was That?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watergate? Whatever Was That?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Election Assistance Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T03:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf59768-84d4-5862-9a58-e3c0b4acc72a', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf59768-84d4-5862-9a58-e3c0b4acc72a'}, {'abstract': 'The F.D.A. denied two petitions asking it to limit the feeding of antibiotics to farm animals, a practice that poses a serious risk to human health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/opinion/bad-call-on-farm-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'The F.D.A. denied two petitions asking it to limit the feeding of antibiotics to farm animals, a practice that poses a serious risk to human health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration last month denied two longstanding petitions asking it to limit the routine feeding of antibiotics to farm animals, a practice that poses a serious risk to human health. Eighty percent of the antibiotics sold in this country are fed to farm animals. The drugs make the animals grow faster, but their overuse increases the likelihood of antibiotic-resistant pathogens. Some antibiotics are used only in animals, but farmers are also using antibiotics vital in human medicine. This is the class of drugs that the petitions, sponsored by several consumer advocacy groups, had hoped to restrict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Call on Farm Drugs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Call on Farm Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamburg, Margaret A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cattle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T03:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/36247dd4-260e-5691-92d4-f2de67ca0ff6', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36247dd4-260e-5691-92d4-f2de67ca0ff6'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of regional economic conditions in the Federal Reserve’s 12 districts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/01/business/economy/most-regions-experienced-modest-growth.html', 'snippet': 'A roundup of regional economic conditions in the Federal Reserve’s 12 districts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A roundup of regional economic conditions in the Federal Reserve’s 12 districts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Most Regions Experienced Modest Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T03:36:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ee82791d-8403-50b7-9113-f7a561c75896', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ee82791d-8403-50b7-9113-f7a561c75896'}, {'abstract': 'The plant’s operator said its latest simulation showed that nuclear fuel may have eroded part of a containment vessel’s concrete floor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/world/asia/meltdown-in-japan-may-have-been-worse-than-thought.html', 'snippet': 'The plant’s operator said its latest simulation showed that nuclear fuel may have eroded part of a containment vessel’s concrete floor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Molten nuclear fuel may have bored into the floor of at least one of the reactors at the stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant, the complex’s operator said Wednesday, citing a new simulation of the accident that crippled the plant in March.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Shows Worse Picture of Meltdown in Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Shows Worse Picture Of Meltdown In Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'maj