rning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/secrets-a-texas-drought-uncovered/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | What items of interest to historians, scientists, anthropologists and criminal investigators have been uncovered in lakes drained by the Texas drought?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHY have lake levels dropped around the state of Texas?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrets a Texas Drought Uncovered', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T09:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c054e08e-9e03-5dcd-a9e3-de857ac22e6d', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c054e08e-9e03-5dcd-a9e3-de857ac22e6d'}, {'abstract': 'A visit by Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton underscored the Obama administration’s cautious efforts to nurture a thaw in the isolated nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/asia/us-will-relax-curbs-on-aid-to-myanmar.html', 'snippet': 'A visit by Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton underscored the Obama administration’s cautious efforts to nurture a thaw in the isolated nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON, Myanmar — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said on Thursday that the United States would loosen some restrictions on international financial assistance and development programs in Myanmar, in response to a nascent political and economic opening in the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/asia/02diplospan/02diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/world/asia/02diplospan/02diplo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/asia/02diplospan/02diplo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/asia/02diplospan/02diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/world/asia/02diplospan/02diplo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Says U.S. Will Relax Some Restrictions on Myanmar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Says U.S. Will Relax Some Restrictions on Myanmar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi, Daw', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T09:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc1cdbdb-dab2-594d-b2b0-b8955bec894f', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc1cdbdb-dab2-594d-b2b0-b8955bec894f'}, {'abstract': 'Why the 62-year-old can’t stay out of the water. Despite the jellyfish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/magazine/marathon-swimmer-diana-nyad.html', 'snippet': 'Why the 62-year-old can’t stay out of the water. Despite the jellyfish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today Diana Nyad is swimming for four hours. She does this four days a week in the 50-meter pool at the Rose Bowl Aquatic Center, in Pasadena, Calif. Her stroke is rhythmic, high in the water. It’s hard to judge how old she is by looking at her. Her back is well muscled. Her legs are girlish — shapely and short. Her skin is as weathered as a crocodile handbag. Her arms are covered with jellyfish scars. When Nyad swims in a pool, she counts in her head, ticking off laps, first in English, then in German, then in Spanish, then in French. (Nyad is fluent in all but German.) The goal is to focus her mind on repetitive thought, as a yogi does with a mantra. But when Nyad swims in the ocean for a long time — 8 or 10 or 12 or even 24 hours — she doesn’t just count, she sings. She’ll do “It Ain’t Me, Babe” 10 times, interspersed with the quatralingual counting, then sing “Paperback Writer,” 10 times, followed by quatralingual counting again. Nyad keeps in her head a playlist of 65 songs. Some are for daytime swimming; others for nighttime. Nyad knows each one intimately, how many seconds each takes, how many strokes. “When I complete 2,000 ‘It Ain’t Me, Babe’s, Bob Dylan version, I know I’ve gone 4 hours and 45 minutes exactly,” Nyad says. “I never lose track.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/magazine/04nyad3_span/04nyad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/magazine/04nyad3_span/04nyad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/magazine/04nyad3_span/04nyad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/magazine/04nyad3_span/04nyad3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/magazine/04nyad3_span/04nyad3_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marathon Swimmer Diana Nyad Takes On the Demons of the Sea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '62 And Life To Go', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nyad, Diana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Weil', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weil', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b00f094f-5b38-543c-bb29-5d68642c0559', 'word_count': 2774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b00f094f-5b38-543c-bb29-5d68642c0559'}, {'abstract': 'A mother describes the surprising effect that the pharmaceutical sleeping drug Ambien has had on her brain-damaged son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001200115/ambiens-wakeful-effect.html', 'snippet': 'A mother describes the surprising effect that the pharmaceutical sleeping drug Ambien has had on her brain-damaged son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mother describes the surprising effect that the pharmaceutical sleeping drug Ambien has had on her brain-damaged son.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/multimedia/video-ambien/video-ambien-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/01/multimedia/video-ambien/video-ambien-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/multimedia/video-ambien/video-ambien-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/01/multimedia/video-ambien/video-ambien-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Awakening', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T10:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Stephanie Sinclair/VII|Brent McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': 'Sinclair', 'lastname': 'VII', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/412cca5b-c141-52be-9a91-a10a1f24eded', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/412cca5b-c141-52be-9a91-a10a1f24eded'}, {'abstract': 'Among leading government officials and presidential candidates, only Jon Huntsman seems prepared to speak out against the excesses of major banks, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/the-huntsman-alternative/', 'snippet': 'Among leading government officials and presidential candidates, only Jon Huntsman seems prepared to speak out against the excesses of major banks, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is the co-author of “13 Bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Huntsman Alternative', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5afe3ddc-6888-5198-9488-9b582db51d4f', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5afe3ddc-6888-5198-9488-9b582db51d4f'}, {'abstract': 'One year ago, FotoEvidence launched its first call for documentary projects. The second begins today. But despite its early success, the Web site’s financial sustainability could prove be a challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/seeking-evidence-through-photography/', 'snippet': 'One year ago, FotoEvidence launched its first call for documentary projects. The second begins today. But despite its early success, the Web site’s financial sustainability could prove be a challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Svetlana Bachevanova recalls sitting at home in Sofia, Bulgaria, and straining her ears as she listened to BBC reports at low volume, to keep neighbors from hearing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Evidence Through Photography', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T10:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/024722d0-b463-508a-b5e5-a27a8de215d4', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/024722d0-b463-508a-b5e5-a27a8de215d4'}, {'abstract': 'A surprising drug has brought a kind of consciousness to patients once considered vegetative — and changed the debate over pulling the plug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/magazine/can-ambien-wake-minimally-conscious.html', 'snippet': 'A surprising drug has brought a kind of consciousness to patients once considered vegetative — and changed the debate over pulling the plug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The moment she saw him, Judy Cox knew her son was dead. It was an October morning in 2008, and she had just stepped out the door to run an errand when she found him lying faceup in the driveway, ghost white, covered in purple splotches. He wasn’t breathing, and when she couldn’t revive him, sh