e to win, but can we quantify it?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/week-13-n-f-l-game-probabilities-injured-quarterback-edition/', 'snippet': 'The backups Caleb Hanie and T.J. Yates give the Bears and the Texans less of a chance to win, but can we quantify it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that time of year when quarterbacks are dropping like flies. There are 9 or 10 teams playing either their second- or third-string passer for one reason or another, depending on who is counted as a starter. Of particular interest are Caleb Hanie and T.J. Yates, the two inexperienced backup quarterbacks playing for winning teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 13 N.F.L. Game Probabilities, Injured Quarterback Edition', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T11:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/577e4dc9-8af6-5e88-afe7-ecc7d4c2f663', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/577e4dc9-8af6-5e88-afe7-ecc7d4c2f663'}, {'abstract': 'Sports for Dorks College Football is an anthology of ideas written by various experts examining a number of innovations taking place in college football.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/inside-the-mind-of-mike-leach/', 'snippet': 'Sports for Dorks College Football is an anthology of ideas written by various experts examining a number of innovations taking place in college football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first of two excerpts The Quad will run from a new book, Sports for Dorks College Football, co-edited by Ferhat Guven and Mike Leach, the former Texas Tech coach hired this week at Washington State. The book is an anthology of ideas by various experts on innovations taking place in college football.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Mind of Mike Leach', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leach, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Tech University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T11:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ferhat Guven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ferhat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Guven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c7a03d-d171-55ac-a5b3-3585103b720a', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c7a03d-d171-55ac-a5b3-3585103b720a'}, {'abstract': 'Le Grand Tasting, running in Paris on Dec. 2 and 3, offers wine connoisseurs and novices the exciting opportunity to taste 350 of the best French and European domains.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/tastings-and-classes-at-paris-wine-fair/', 'snippet': 'Le Grand Tasting, running in Paris on Dec. 2 and 3, offers wine connoisseurs and novices the exciting opportunity to taste 350 of the best French and European domains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Le Grand Tasting — a k a the Great Wines Fair — offers connoisseurs and novices the opportunity to taste 350 of the best French and European domains. Organized by Michel Bettane and Thierry Desseauve, two wine authorities, it takes place on Dec. 2 and 3 at the Carrousel du Louvre (99 rue de Rivoli; carrouseldulouvre.com). Distinguished labels like Veuve Clicquot and Louis Latour; wine-world stars like Hervé Bizeul and Marcel Richaud; and newcomers including Beaucastel, Pichon Comtesse, Angélus and Chateau de Bellet are among the participants this year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tastings and Classes at Paris Wine Fair', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T11:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce18a1e0-433d-5cde-bd6f-afc7abd78780', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce18a1e0-433d-5cde-bd6f-afc7abd78780'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/the-early-word-fall-and-rise/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Fall and Rise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T11:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U