: 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3806a3c8-cf3d-519c-aa55-d2fa9c9536c5'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a bumper crop of guy-focused films in the race, or is it Hollywood business as usual? You tell us.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/is-it-the-year-of-the-dude-film/', 'snippet': 'There’s a bumper crop of guy-focused films in the race, or is it Hollywood business as usual? You tell us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over in our non-bloggy column today, the Bagger explores the idea that there is a bumper crop of dude-oriented films among the Oscar hopefuls this year. “The Descendants,” “Beginners,” “The Tree of Life,” “Margin Call,” “Take Shelter,” “J. Edgar,” “The Artist,” “Midnight in Paris,” “50/50” and “Drive” all deal with fatherhood, or living up to notions of masculine identity, sexuality and power, or bashing someone’s head in. (And let’s not even go near the Michael Fassbender vehicle “Shame” for the moment. We will get to the double entendres for that later, or the good folks at Fox, which is releasing the NC-17 movie, will do it for us.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It the Year of the Dude Film?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f90bc36-6ec5-509e-a7ba-5eab61758657', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f90bc36-6ec5-509e-a7ba-5eab61758657'}, {'abstract': 'Thirty-one days to a new you for the new year — get going.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/final-countdown-beauty-calendar/', 'snippet': 'T