ood reason to forget it these days. Yes, Israeli informality means that it’s still relatively easy for reporters to call high officials on their cellphones at all hours. Yes, the country’s smallness means that they can quickly reach its every corner. But last week the Knesset member Yariv Levin of the Likud Party cast a dark shadow on these advantages by getting a proposed amendment to Israel’s libel law through a first vote. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Libel Law and a Balancing Act', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T14:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34bbe24b-39aa-51f6-b9cf-c38b4272a6ae', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34bbe24b-39aa-51f6-b9cf-c38b4272a6ae'}, {'abstract': 'The development raises the possibility of a strike by the orchestra and chorus.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/talks-break-down-between-city-opera-and-unions/', 'snippet': 'The development raises the possibility of a strike by the orchestra and 