on.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/what-were-reading-322/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Tribune: The wild new incarnation of Next, the ambitious Chicago restaurant that changes its menu entirely every three months, gets four stars from the Tribune. — Julia Moskin ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T15:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67bdc1e0-8d3f-5f35-8409-620c38e6773a', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67bdc1e0-8d3f-5f35-8409-620c38e6773a'}, {'abstract': 'Carmakers reported double-digit gains in November sales, generating their strongest sales rate in more than two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/business/car-buyers-flock-to-us-showrooms.html', 'snippet': 'Carmakers reported double-digit gains in November sales, generating their strongest sales rate in more than two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Auto sales in the United States climbed 14 percent in November as lower gas prices and a wider availability of Japanese models helped the industry achieve its highest selling rate in more than two years, automakers and analysts said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/business/Auto/Auto-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Flock to C