y season than last year, a recent survey found.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/many-consumers-plan-to-spend-less-this-holiday-season/', 'snippet': 'With economic concerns weighing heavily, 42 percent of Americans — and 49 percent of parents — say they plan to spend less this holiday season than last year, a recent survey found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With economic concerns weighing heavily, 42 percent of Americans –and 49 percent of parents — say they plan to spend less this holiday season than last year, a recent survey found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Consumers Plan to Spend Less This Holiday Season', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton Survey Research Associates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T16:28:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb123ab-3e2b-50f2-bfa8-c685a2633246', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb123ab-3e2b-50f2-bfa8-c685a2633246'}, {'abstract': 'Raphaela Neihausen and Thom Powers, who run the Stranger Than Fiction documentary series and the DOC NYC festival, will oversee programming for the first Montclair International Film Festival next year. In the meantime, Mr. Colbert, who sits on the Montclair festival’s board, is happy to talk up the event.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/montclair-film-festival-gains-directors-and-a-cheerleader-named-stephen-colbert/', 'snippet': 'Raphaela Neihausen and Thom Powers, who run the Stranger Than Fiction documentary series and the DOC NYC festival, will oversee programming for the first Montclair International Film Festival next year. In the meantime, Mr. Colbert, who sits on th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cannes. Toronto. Park City, Utah. If these cities can each be the home of a great film festival, then why not Montclair, N.J.? Isn’t it entitled to a little bit of that cinematic luster, too?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Montclair Film Festival Gains Directors, and a Cheerleader Named Stephen Colbert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montclair (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T16:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc9c397-8489-5ac1-837e-a187babc1b05', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc9c397-8489-5ac1-837e-a187babc1b05'}, {'abstract': 'Computer simulations suggest how close the No 1. reactor’s defenses came to being breached.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/fukushima-meltdown-was-more-severe-than-thought-study-says/', 'snippet': 'Computer simulations suggest how close the No 1. reactor’s defenses came to being breached.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Molten nuclear fuel in the No. 1 reactor at Japan’s Fukushima Daiichi plant burned through a steel pressure vessel and three-quarters of the surrounding concrete containment vessel, the reactor’s last substantial internal barrier, a report released by the plant’s operator and the Japanese government says. [The Australian]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fukushima Meltdown Was More Severe Than Thought, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T16:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4eb44be-f467-5758-b050-dd607e540fb5', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4eb44be-f467-5758-b050-dd607e540fb5'}, {'abstract': 'There are many ugly accusations and a lot of unanswered questions surrounding Penn State these days. One question was answered recently by Terry Pegula, a Penn State alumnus who is responsible for bringing Division I hockey to State College. The questions now revolve around the recruits.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/scandals-ramifications-on-penn-state-hockey/', 'snippet': 'There are many ugly accusations and a lot of unanswered questions surrounding Penn State these days. One question was answered recently by Terry Pegula, a Penn State alumnus who is responsible for bringing Division I hockey to State College. The q...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many ugly accusations and a lot of unanswered questions surrounding Penn State these days. One question was answered recently by the Buffalo Sabres owner Terry Pegula, a Penn State alumnus who is responsible for bringing Division I hockey to State College with an $88 million donation in 2010. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scandal’s Ramifications on Penn State Hockey', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pegula, Terry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T16:32:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Caponigri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caponigri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0b2b4c3-833c-5ede-88b6-e1bc1aa45cb1', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0b2b4c3-833c-5ede-88b6-e1bc1aa45cb1'}, {'abstract': 'Charming Shoppes plans to sell its Fashion Bug chain to focus on its Lane Bryant line of plus-size women’s apparel.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/charming-shoppes-puts-fashion-bug-on-the-block/', 'snippet': 'Charming Shoppes plans to sell its Fashion Bug chain to focus on its Lane Bryant line of plus-size women’s apparel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charming Shoppes said on Thursday that it was putting its Fashion Bug chain up for sale to focus on its Lane Bryant line of plus-size women’s apparel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charming Shoppes Puts Fashion Bug on the Block', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CHARMING SHOPPES INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fashion Bug', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T16:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d18436-5d24-5aa4-8b9b-74ee8641247b', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d18436-5d24-5aa4-8b9b-74ee8641247b'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s crackdown on illegal immigration coincides with a surge in the number of Latinos of voting age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/us/politics/with-boom-in-hispanic-voters-obama-sees-opportunity-in-arizona.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s crackdown on illegal immigration coincides with a surge in the number of Latinos of voting age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Republicans in the State Legislature here push a law that would require President Obama to provide his long-form birth certificate in order to get on the Arizona presidential ballot in 2012. The governor uses Facebook to denounce the president’s “backdoor amnesty plan.” Cars traveling on State Route 260 are treated to a giant billboard bearing Mr. Obama’s mug on a mock $100 trillion bill that asks, “But Who Will Pay the Piper?” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/02latinos_span/02latinos_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'wi