 of dependency in Haiti with “durable development.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some good news from Haiti, or at least\xa0some glimmers: International investors and donors are attending an investment forum in the capital, Port-au-Prince, sponsored by the Inter-American Development Bank. As The Miami Herald reported, President Michel Martelly, Prime Minister Garry Cornille, former President Bill Clinton and the head of the I.D.B., Luis Alberto Moreno, have spent the last few days cutting ribbons and making speeches, all to emphasize the idea that reconstruction is gaining momentum and that Haiti is open for business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob the Builder Goes to Haiti', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martelly, Michel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-American Development Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T18:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e88872e8-70ce-569a-9795-597b91911608', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e88872e8-70ce-569a-9795-597b91911608'}, {'abstract': 'A note to readers.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/note-to-readers/', 'snippet': 'A note to readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times has introduced an improved comment system, which will provide threading of comments so you can respond directly to one another, and allow you to share your comments to Twitter and Facebook. Our new system will also offer some of our most engaged readers the opportunity to post their comments on the Web site without moderation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Note to Readers', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T18:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c81bcf8-d05e-5281-9b3e-1f21e580e247', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c81bcf8-d05e-5281-9b3e-1f21e580e247'}, {'abstract': 'An East Village store lost six vaporizers on Black Friday, as captured on surveillance video.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/seen-on-video-a-smoke-shop-theft/', 'snippet': 'An East Village store lost six vaporizers on Black Friday, as captured on surveillance video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Black Friday, as shoppers across the nation busied themselves pepper-spraying and shooting at each other, a quieter but perhaps no less brazen crime was committed at a head shop – er, smoking accessories store — in the East Village. Several young men helped themselves to six vaporizers worth a total of about $2,500 from the store, Smoking Tattoos. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seen on Video: A Smoke Shop Theft', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': 