e': None, 'lastname': 'Light', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b4c7cee-5df2-573e-8b91-e19aa41ea5c1', 'word_count': 1820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b4c7cee-5df2-573e-8b91-e19aa41ea5c1'}, {'abstract': 'The forecast for Tuesday in Miami Beach was for overcast skies, scattered parties and a chance of art as jet-lagged travelers convened for the prelude to Art Basel 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/out-there-art-basel-miami-beach-pregame-show/', 'snippet': 'The forecast for Tuesday in Miami Beach was for overcast skies, scattered parties and a chance of art as jet-lagged travelers convened for the prelude to Art Basel 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The forecast for Tuesday in Miami Beach was for overcast skies, scattered parties and a chance of art as jet-lagged travelers convened for the prelude to Art Basel 2011. The Fairchild Tropical Botanic Garden in Coral Gables hosted its annual brunch, this year for the sculptor Will Ryman, whose monochromatic roses (most recently seen on Park Avenue) are scattered around the grounds in the form of petal chairs and towering, long-stemmed arrangements. Valuable trees and interesting fauna abounded, including a black crocodile and coconut-size baby raccoon mingling in dangerous proximity: what kind of omen is that?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | Art Basel Miami Beach Pregame Show', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T18:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dde47d8-0355-5d6c-87b5-8ea0af72ae6d', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dde47d8-0355-5d6c-87b5-8ea0af72ae6d'}, {'abstract': 'The making of a very unlikely children’s toy for our cover.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/make-me-a-mitt-romney-weeble/', 'snippet': 'The making of a very unlikely children’s toy for our cover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not every day an art director is charged with this task. I came out of the meeting thinking that it seemed easy enough. Break apart Weeble toy. Hire someone to illustrate Romney’s caricature. Piece Weeble together. Photograph. Done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Make Me a Mitt Romney Weeble!’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T18:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caleb Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caleb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6155faf1-45c2-576b-a22d-3b9069a155bb', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6155faf1-45c2-576b-a22d-3b9069a155bb'}, {'abstract': 'Mérida, a languid city of pastel mansions and evening promenades, is in the midst of a restoration boom, and the city’s cultural and restaurant scenes are flourishing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/04/travel/04MERIDA.html', 'snippet': 'Mérida, a languid city of pastel mansions and evening promenades, is in the midst of a restoration boom, and the city’s cultural and restaurant scenes are flourishing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mérida, a languid city of pastel mansions and evening promenades, is in the midst of a restoration boom, and the city’s cultural and restaurant scenes are flourishing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A/04MERIDA-slide-CO0A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Mérida, Mexico', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T18:35:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/80225348-6b31-56e8-bb36-30f532eea889', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/80225348-6b31-56e8-bb36-30f532eea889'}, {'abstract': 'The city, now one of the safest in Mexico, is an architectural jewel, with one of the country’s largest historic centers outside Mexico City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/travel/36-hours-in-merida-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'The city, now one of the safest in Mexico, is an architectural jewel, with one of the country’s largest historic centers outside Mexico City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YUCATECANS are fiercely proud of their culture, sprinkling their Spanish with Mayan words and quick to recount the stories of resistance and revolution that set this region apart from the rest of Mexico for centuries. Somehow, those tales seem a little distant now in Yucatán’s capital, Mérida, a languid city of pastel mansions and evening promenades. The city, now one of the safest in Mexico, is an architectural jewel, and has one of the country’s largest historic centers outside Mexico City. Block after block of houses dating to the mid-19th century and earlier are in the midst of a restoration boom, and the city’s cultural and restaurant scenes are flourishing.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04HOURS1_SPAN/04HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04HOURS1_SPAN/04HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04HOURS1_SPAN/04HOURS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04HOURS1_SPAN/04HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04HOURS1_SPAN/04HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Mérida, Mexico', 'kicker': '36 