at new hit sitcoms are proof that “we’ve reached the End of Comedy.” They watch sitcoms with a critical eye and ultimately choose a writing project that demonstrates a close viewing that treats the shows like literary texts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone’s a Critic: Analyzing Sitcoms as Cultural Texts', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T20:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne, Katherine Schulten and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3168e19b-900d-59e4-9679-37a6352a2ece', 'word_count': 1919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3168e19b-900d-59e4-9679-37a6352a2ece'}, {'abstract': 'Better than boating or diving, paddle boarding is a 360-degree experience, with vistas of land and sea all around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/travel/stand-up-paddle-boarding-in-the-virgin-islands.html', 'snippet': 'Better than boating or diving, paddle boarding is a 360-degree experience, with vistas of land and sea all around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF John would just raise his arms skyward, I would have a better view of him streaking across the Narrows, northward toward Tortola, leaving me far enough behind that I have to squint to see him. He wants to cross the 1.5-mile strait on his paddle board, abandoning United States territory to storm British waters. This is not recommended for those who are likely to give out halfway across, like me, which is why I am still on this side of the divide, straddling my board, in a lagoon off St. John in the United States Virgin Islands.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04EXPLORER1_SPAN/04EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04EXPLORER1_SPAN/04EXPLORER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04EXPLORER1_SPAN/04EXPLORER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04EXPLORER1_SPAN/04EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/travel/04EXPLORER1_SPAN/04EXPLORER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stand-Up Paddle Boarding in the Virgin Islands', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Paddle With One Eye on the Sharks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St John (Virgin Islands)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virgin Islands (US)', 'rank'