ction_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d9aab7-53fb-5b28-9a8e-b441934e0172', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d9aab7-53fb-5b28-9a8e-b441934e0172'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Markovic resigned in December 1991 as his nation broke apart, nearly three years after he became prime minister.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/europe/ante-markovic-last-premier-of-yugoslavia-dies-at-87.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Markovic resigned in December 1991 as his nation broke apart, nearly three years after he became prime minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ante Markovic, who as the last prime minister of Yugoslavia tried to stave off the ethnic warfare that led to the disintegration of that nation, died on Nov. 28 in Zagreb, the Croatian capital. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/europe/MARKOVIC-obit/MARKOVIC-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/europe/MARKOVIC-obit/MARKOVIC-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/world/europe/MARKOVIC-obit/MARKOVIC-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ante Markovic, Last Premier of Yugoslavia, Dies at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ante Markovic, 87, Last Premier of Yugoslavia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T20:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/91cfdd9f-6fc0-56e2-be49-8c83ba54764b', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91cfdd9f-6fc0-56e2-be49-8c83ba54764b'}, {'abstract': 'The National Board of Review releases its winners.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/national-board-of-review-picks-hugo/', 'snippet': 'The National Board of Review releases its winners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s something for everyone – except Brad Pitt, Meryl Streep and Michelle Williams. The National Board of Review picked “Hugo,” Martin Scorsese’s 3D ode to early cinema, as its top film, and named Mr. Scorsese best director, thereby ensuring that Mr. Scorsese will show up for the ceremony on Jan. 10. Also likely to appear: George Clooney, who won best actor for “The Descendants,” which earned a best supporting actress win for Shailene Woodley, who plays Mr. Clooney’s petulant teenage daughter, and a best adapted screenplay award for Alexander Payne, Nat Faxon and Jim Rash. The incomparable Tilda Swinton was named best actress for “We Need to Talk About Kevin,” and Christopher Plummer will take home the best supporting actor trophy for his turn as a father coming out late in life in Mike Mills’ “Beginners,” which could signal the start of his ascent to a best supporting actor nod at the Oscars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Board of Review Picks ‘Hugo’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T20:50:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f834eba5-caf6-5c2e-9e9f-ed5c8517d2e3', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f834eba5-caf6-5c2e-9e9f-ed5c8517d2e3'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: Opera', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/01/blogs/20111201-lens-opera.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: Opera', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: Opera', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/blogs/20111201-lens-opera-slide-2JVX/20111201-lens-opera-slide-2JVX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T20:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/592f3c93-11a0-5bf1-a831-bbfb86f6a9f9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/592f3c93-11a0-5bf1-a831-bbfb86f6a9f9'}, {'abstract': 'The Sundance Film Festival releases lineups for the 2012 edition’s Midnight, Spotlight, Next and New Frontier sections.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/delusional-teenagers-and-other-sundance-offerings/', 'snippet': 'The Sundance Film Festival releases lineups for the 2012 edition’s Midnight, Spotlight, Next and New Frontier sections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Sundance Film Festival, aware that even the most crazed cinema fan cannot digest its girth in one sitting, likes to release its selections in bite-sized pieces. On Wednesday it was the competition lineup. On Thursday came the more esoteric stuff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delusional Teenagers and Other Sundance Offerings', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2748097e-7962-5cd4-9661-2eda368d54b9', 'word_count': 1748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2748097e-7962-5cd4-9661-2eda368d54b9'}, {'abstract': 'The Giving Spree continues with more gifts to give and get from T’s friends and family.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/the-giving-spree-claire-danes/', 'snippet': 'The Giving Spree continues with more gifts to give and get from T’s friends and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who: The actress Claire Danes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Giving Spree | Claire Danes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/778dd501-3592-5207-b67d-0f5671f53d0b', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/778dd501-3592-5207-b67d-0f5671f53d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Joe Manchin, as well as many Times readers, worry that a payroll tax cut extension could hurt workers over the long term.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/dont-worry-about-social-security/', 'snippet': 'Senator Joe Manchin, as well as many Times readers, worry that a payroll tax cut extension could hurt workers over the long term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was surprising this morning to hear Senator Joe Manchin, Democrat of West Virginia, denounce President Obama’s proposal to extend the payroll tax cut. Mr. Manchin, one of the very few Democrats to break with the president on this issue,\xa0said it would jeopardize the future of Social Security.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Worry About Social Security', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70b13c17-4eb6-5464-a7b7-62c29c68d908', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70b13c17-4eb6-5464-a7b7-62c29c68d908'}, {'abstract': 'Military dogs and household pets that have experienced trauma can suffer from a form of canine post-traumatic stress disorder, veterinarians say.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/dogs-and-post-traumatic-stress-disorder/', 'snippet': 'Military dogs and household pets that have experienced trauma can suffer from a form of canine post-traumatic stress disorder, veterinarians say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s well known that post-traumatic stress is one of the major problems facing many veterans returning from the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan. But now researchers are finding that a large number of military dogs may be grappling with the condition as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dogs and Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d3c3b94-cf5f-5f98-abaf-3c270339d62c', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d3c3b94-cf5f-5f98-abaf-3c270339d62c'}, {'abstract': 'We’re putting out a specific call to our readers in Iowa to send in pictures of campaign mailers, beginning with the ones the Romney campaign started sending out over the Thanksgiving holiday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/watching-the-iowa-ground-game/', 'snippet': 'We’re putting out a specific call to our readers in Iowa to send in pictures of campaign mailers, beginning with the ones the Romney campaign started sending out over the Thanksgiving holiday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since we first put out the call  for photos of presidential campaign material, we’ve received several dozen submissions from readers, many of them pictures of grass-roots support for Ron Paul, the Republican congressman from Texas. The billboard shown here is in Wisconsin, and was produced independent of Mr. Paul’s presidential campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching the Iowa Ground Game', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e358659b-8280-5916-9e4a-90060f384b7b', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e358659b-8280-5916-9e4a-90060f384b7b'}, {'abstract': 'The chances that a student at the Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers would cross the finish line to graduation in four years were already poor, but seniors said they have now been told of a new obstacle: a credit problem that could cost some of them their diplomas in June.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/01/jane-addams-h-s-students-fear-they-lack-credits-to-graduate/', 'snippet': 'The chances that a student at the Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers would cross the finish line to graduation in four years were already poor, but seniors said they have now been told of a new obstacle: a credit problem that could cost ...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jane Addams H.S. Students Fear They Lack Credits to Graduate', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T21:10:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS and HADAS GOSHEN', 'person': [