lt, some of the canines used by United States forces in Afghanistan are coming down with post-traumatic stress disorder. And in Iraq, just as the American army is leaving, a large shipment of American dogs has arrived, though the Iraqis have been slow to use them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Soldiers Leave Iraq, Bomb-Sniffing Dogs Stay', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb02d8e-653f-5f21-873f-fddcb1b7c399', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb02d8e-653f-5f21-873f-fddcb1b7c399'}, {'abstract': '“Storytelling in Japanese Art” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art reveals the narrative side of Japanese art in a lavish assortment of hand scrolls, hanging scrolls, screens and books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/design/storytelling-in-japanese-art-at-the-met-review.html', 'snippet': '“Storytelling in Japanese Art” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art reveals the narrative side of Japanese art in a lavish assortment of hand scrolls, hanging scrolls, screens and books.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Storytelling in Japanese Art,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, is a captivating combination of show and tell, read and look. Curatorially speaking, the exhibition takes us gently in hand and, through text panels, captions and diagrams, reveals the narrative side of Japanese art with memorable clarity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02STORY1_SPAN/02STORY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 198, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02STORY1_SPAN/02STORY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 198}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02STORY1_SPAN/02STORY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02STORY1_SPAN/02STORY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02STORY1_SPAN/02STORY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unfurling a Thousand Years of Gods, Demons and Romance', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unfurling a Thousand Years Of Gods, Demons and Romance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'ori