years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wilson Livingood, the sergeant-at-arms of the House of Representatives and known as Bill, is retiring after 17 years. Mr. Livingood, who spent 33 years in the United States Secret Service, was the first person to serve in the position with a significant law enforcement background; the position was historically filled by a political appointee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House’s Sergeant-at-Arms Retires After 17 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:38:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22b90c5a-5f68-5f0b-a6bf-3cc20720ce04', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22b90c5a-5f68-5f0b-a6bf-3cc20720ce04'}, {'abstract': '“Angel Reapers” at the Joyce Theater is the latest theatrical interpretation of the Shakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/dance/angel-reapers-at-joyce-theater-review.html', 'snippet': '“Angel Reapers” at the Joyce Theater is the latest theatrical interpretation of the Shakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spiritual utopian movement known as the Shakers has all but disappeared in America. (The group’s tenet of celibacy does a number on recruitment.) But its allure for artists appears to be holding steady, with choreographers, including Twyla Tharp and Tero Saarinen, especially drawn to the Shaker tradition of worship through movement and song.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02REAPER/REAPERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02REAPER/02REAPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02REAPER/02REAPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Physical Ecstasy of Worship, and the Travails of Those Who Tread Its Path', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Physical Ecstasy of Worship, and the Travails of Those Who Tread Its Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Uhry, Alfred', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Martha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:38:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3964506d-38c3-5caf-9179-a76f90003f5c', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3964506d-38c3-5caf-9179-a76f90003f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Madison Square Presbyterian Church, demolished in 1919, lives on in fragments scattered from Brooklyn to Riverside, Calif.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/design/madison-square-presbyterian-church-fragments-found.html', 'snippet': 'Madison Square Presbyterian Church, demolished in 1919, lives on in fragments scattered from Brooklyn to Riverside, Calif.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madison Square Presbyterian Church was one of New York’s shortest-lived houses of worship. Designed by Stanford White, this Palladian building opened on 24th Street in 1906 and was razed in 1919 to make way for insurance offices. Architects and preservationists mourned its demise and descended on the wreckage for souvenirs.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02SUBANTIQUES-1/2ndSUBANTIQUES-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Madison Square Church Survives in Fragments', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madison Square Church Survives in Fragments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duquette, Tony', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3207ad-57b0-50e8-9fc1-e875b21dac82', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3207ad-57b0-50e8-9fc1-e875b21dac82'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Drain and Naomi Fisher are part of what make up Miami’s art community.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/out-there-miamis-it-couple/', 'snippet': 'Jim Drain and Naomi Fisher are part of what make up Miami’s art community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tropical, blinged-out hedonism aside, there is actually such a thing as community in Miami. After the droves who come for Art Basel pack up and go, there are folks — artists among them — who stick around, living and working here throughout the year. They do tend to be at their busiest during the fairs, and the artists Jim Drain and Naomi Fisher are no exception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | Miami’s ‘It’ Couple', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Naomi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fbb42ef-3d24-511c-b7c4-78e3904b5fb9', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fbb42ef-3d24-511c-b7c4-78e3904b5fb9'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Battle opened his first season as artistic director for the Alvin Ailey troupe with a show that paid homage to his predecessors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/dance/alvin-ailey-american-dance-theater-at-city-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Battle opened his first season as artistic director for the Alvin Ailey troupe with a show that paid homage to his predecessors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater opened its annual season at City Center on Wednesday, it did so under a new artistic director, Robert Battle. But an Ailey gala is a set ritual, a glamorous fund-raiser as much about donors as about dancers, and in conforming to the standard of years past, this one sent a message of continuity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02AILEY2/AILEY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02AILEY2/02AILEY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02AILEY2/02AILEY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Starting a New Era With Graciousness, Taste and Tradition', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting a New Era With Graciousness, Taste and Tradition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc078af6-9211-5d28-ade0-d6175f12572e', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc078af6-9211-5d28-ade0-d6175f12572e'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibition at Scandinavia House presents 48 paintings and drawings, mostly from the first decade of the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/design/luminous-modernism-at-scandinavia-house-review.html', 'snippet': 'A new exhibition at Scandinavia House presents 48 paintings and drawings, mostly from the first decade of the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Armory Show was not the first or only ambitious effort to open American minds to European modern art in the early 20th century. Just two months before that show’s New York debut in February 1913, another big exhibition of progressive art appeared here. Organized by the nascent American-Scandinavian Foundation, “Exhibition of Contemporary Scandinavian Art” offered more than 150 works by Danish, Norwegian and Swedish artists, many of whom favored Post-Impressionist, Expressionist and Symbolist modes that were still viewed with suspicion on this side of the Atlantic. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02LUMINOUS/02LUMINOUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 927, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02LUMINOUS/02LUMINOUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02LUMINOUS/02LUMINOUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shadowy Lure of Scandinavia 