: 'nyt://slideshow/170e4982-2730-5409-8c4a-d605123e593e'}, {'abstract': 'In his directing debut, Ralph Fiennes adds modern weaponry to Shakespeare’s “Coriolanus.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/movies/ralph-fiennes-and-vanessa-redgrave-in-coriolanus-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his directing debut, Ralph Fiennes adds modern weaponry to Shakespeare’s “Coriolanus.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As soon as a thrilling Ralph Fiennes appears on “Coriolanus,” it’s clear why he chose this lesser-known Shakespeare tragedy for his directing debut. Dressed in camouflage fatigues, Mr. Fiennes — as the mythic Roman military hero first known as Caius Martius and later Coriolanus — enters a raucous scene and commands it with just a glare. What power! The city’s hungry, rioting citizens, some carrying protest signs and one holding a camera phone, have descended, demanding food. Martius charges at them and then lets loose the contempt that will aid in his downfall: “What’s the matter, you dissentious rogues, that, rubbing the poor itch of your opinion, make yourselves scabs?”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02CORIO_SPAN/02CORIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02CORIO_SPAN/02CORIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02CORIO_SPAN/02CORIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02CORIO_SPAN/02CORIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02CORIO_SPAN/02CORIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s the Hero of the People, and He Hates It', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Coriolanus'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s the Hero of the People, and He Hates It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiennes, Ralph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Gerard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redgrave, Vanessa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T22:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1b9b19f-e80c-5b17-b71e-d49db6792e0e', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1b9b19f-e80c-5b17-b71e-d49db6792e0e'}, {'abstract': 'The first solo show by Bianca Beck delights in small works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/design/bianca-beck-body.html', 'snippet': 'The first solo show by Bianca Beck delights in small works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Uffner Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bianca Beck: ‘Body’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bianca Beck: ‘Body’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2