amed Matthew Cassel reported on Twitter that he had just witnessed something remarkable: a lone female protester who refused to move as police officers in riot gear charged past her, firing tear gas shells just a few feet from her head.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Activist Stands Her Ground in Bahrain', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b086eeb-7500-51a9-95bd-ef3a78074997', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b086eeb-7500-51a9-95bd-ef3a78074997'}, {'abstract': 'In the Michael Kors prefall collection,Southampton meets Santa Fe.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/just-one-look-michael-kors/', 'snippet': 'In the Michael Kors prefall collection,Southampton meets Santa Fe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Michael Kors pre-fall collection, which was shown earlier this afternoon, paid homage to Ann Taylor — not the retail chain but the Southern socialite whom Kors described as “Nan Kempner on the range.” Graphic country looks came with built-in leather harnesses (rodeo-girl waistlines were key), appaloosa prints and a sinewy Chesterfield coat, all of it accessorized with cowboy hats and silver-studded satchels. Here, a dip-dyed goat-fur vest paired with wool riding shorts and a black leather bandolier bag is Southampton meets Santa Fe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Michael Kors', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wool and Woolen Goods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kempner, Nan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southampton (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86b47c02-1ba1-5af6-97f2-b35f0fb67188', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86b47c02-1ba1-5af6-97f2-b35f0fb67188'}, {'abstract': 'More sanctions were enacted against Syrian individuals and companies in a rising tide of international pressure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/middleeast/united-nations-says-syrian-unrest-amounts-to-civil-war.html', 'snippet': 'More sanctions were enacted against Syrian individuals and companies in a rising tide of international pressure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The United Nations declared Thursday that Syria was in a state of civil war, as the death toll from nearly nine months of bloodshed rose to more than 4,000 people and more soldiers were reported to have defected from the army to join an armed uprising against President Bashar al-Assad. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'United Nations Says Unrest in Syria Amounts to Civil War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Official Likens Unrest in Syria to Civil War, and Death Toll Is Said to Pass 4,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/064d1353-e719-547e-9b73-f14748a02458', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/064d1353-e719-547e-9b73-f14748a02458'}, {'abstract': 'Not everything at a tailgate party needs to be tubular meats or barbecue. Ask any vegetarian.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/tailgating-recipes-puff-pastry-samosas/', 'snippet': 'Not everything at a tailgate party needs to be tubular meats or barbecue. Ask any vegetarian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing we’ve learned about tailgating parties this year is that they’re inclusive — everybody’s welcome. Now we’ve got to feed all of those people, even the vegetarians. Nithya Das, a Giants fan and vegetarian living in Brooklyn, has been to plenty of pregame festivities only to find brats and barbecue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tailgating Recipes: Puff Pastry Samosas', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetarianism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Luttrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luttrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2af294a-f39d-5251-b443-a62a485473c6', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2af294a-f39d-5251-b443-a62a485473c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Nate Wooley Quintet Omega performed songs about friendship at the Brooklyn Lyceum on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/music/nate-wooley-quintet-omega-at-brooklyn-lyceum-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Nate Wooley Quintet Omega performed songs about friendship at the Brooklyn Lyceum on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pursuit of aloneness — in a deep-focus, self-obliterating sense — seems to mean a lot to the trumpeter Nate Wooley. An improviser with a tactile, patient, interrogatory approach to his craft, he belongs to the avant-garde jazz tradition but doesn’t press the issue of lineage. His two most recent albums are solo trumpet recordings: sealed-off worlds of serenely disquieting technique, with and without electronics. His baseline tone is unvarnished and autumnal, but he does so much else, in the realm of scrunches and striations, that it’s a fair question whether he has a baseline tone at all.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02WOOLEY_SPAN/02WOOLEY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02WOOLEY_SPAN/02WOOLEY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02WOOLEY_SPAN/WOOLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02WOOLEY_SPAN/02WOOLEY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02WOOLEY_SPAN/02WOOLEY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Songs About Friendship, Performed With His Pals', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Songs About Friendship, Performed With His Pals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0799c14-ac76-56b2-bf0c-bb17ff469e93', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0799c14-ac76-56b2-bf0c-bb17ff469e93'}, {'abstract': 'The tech reporters and editors of The New York Times are always looking for the most interesting items on the Web. Today’s selection includes items on hacking threats to printers and Siri’s politics.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/todays-scuttlebot-vulnerable-printers-and-siris-politics/', 'snippet': 'The tech reporters and editors of The New York Times are always looking for the most interesting items on the Web. Today’s selection includes items on hacking threats to printers and Siri’s politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s what the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Vulnerable Printers and Siri’s Politics', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a97f20c-aa09-5525-b4c1-9735b434f182', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a97f20c-aa09-5525-b4c1-9735b434f182'}, {'abstract': 'Adele, Bruno Mars, the Foo Fighters and Kanye West garnered the most nominations for the 54th annual Grammy Awards, which will be broadcast from Los Angeles on Feb. 12.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/music/adele-bruno-mars-and-kanye-west-lead-grammy-nominations.html', 'snippet': 'Adele, Bruno Mars, the Foo Fighters and Kanye West garnered the most nominations for the 54th annual Grammy Awards, which will be broadcast from Los Angeles on Feb. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Grammys are a barometer of trends in popular music, then old-school pop songs about unrequited love made a comeback this year. The pop stars Adele and Bruno Mars dominated nominations for the top prizes — to be given out at the 54th annual Grammy Awards in February — while hip-hop and country musicians were largely shut out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02GRAMMYS1_SPAN/GRAMMYS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02GRAMMYS1_SPAN/02GRAMMYS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02GRAMMYS1_SPAN/02GRAMMYS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop Stars Dominate Major Grammy Categories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop Stars Dominate Major Grammy Categories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foo Fighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:24:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f9c7692-e012-5aae-b794-12cff1e495d2', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f9c7692-e012-5aae-b794-12cff1e495d2'}, {'abstract': 'Everything in this show at the Gagosian Gallery was once owned by Robert Rauschenberg (1925-2008), but there is nothing by the artist himself on view.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/design/selections-from-the-private-collection-of-robert-rauschenberg-at-gagosian-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Everything in this show at the Gagosian Gallery was once owned by Robert Rauschenberg (1925-2008), but there is nothing by the artist himself on view.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0 “Selections From the Private Collection of Robert Rauschenberg” at the Gagosian Gallery is a kind of mash note to the art world. Wending through spaces on three floors and numbering 130 items, it testifies both to the loose constellations of artists and to the congeries of artworks, objects and memorabilia that often form just in the process of living around artists, especially important, instinctively generous ones. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RAUSCHENBERG_SPAN/SUBRAUSCHENBERG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RAUSCHENBERG_SPAN/SUBRAUSCHENBERG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RAUSCHENBERG_SPAN/SUBRAUSCHENBERG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RAUSCHENBERG_SPAN/SUBRAUSCHENBERG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RAUSCHENBERG_SPAN/SUBRAUSCHENBERG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Portrait of the Artist as Exuberant Collector', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Portrait of the Artist as Exuberant Collector', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/892d724a-741f-5fd6-81e3-e7791cb15466', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/892d724a-741f-5fd6-81e3-e7791cb15466'}, {'abstract': 'Ry-Ann Hermon was charged with accepting bribes from the same federal agents who were dealing with her boss, Assemblyman William F. Boyland Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/nyregion/boylands-chief-of-staff-arrested-in-bribery-case.html', 'snippet': 'Ry-Ann Hermon was charged with accepting bribes from the same federal agents who were dealing with her boss, Assemblyman William F. Boyland Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chief of staff to William F. Boyland Jr., an assemblyman arrested this week on charges of soliciting and accepting thousands of dollars in bribes from undercover federal agents posing as eager businessmen, was arrested on Thursday in connection with the alleged scheme. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/BOYLAND/BOYLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/BOYLAND/BOYLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/BOYLAND/BOYLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Assemblyman’s Chief of Staff Is Arrested in Bribery Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Assemblyman’s Chief of Staff Is Arrested in Bribery Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Robert M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyland, William F Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af9a3de1-3fb5-5fb1-8fd4-3f6c9b1a8c03', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af9a3de1-3fb5-5fb1-8fd4-3f6c9b1a8c03'}, {'abstract': 'Day 2 of Art Basel proved fruitful with a plethora of festivities and great art.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/out-there-abmb-more-parties-and-yes-some-art/', 'snippet': 'Day 2 of Art Basel proved fruitful with a plethora of festivities and great art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday morning, the 10th edition of Art Basel opened for preview. But first a stop at the Rubell Collection was in order for an experiential snack by the artist/cook/daughter Jennifer Rubell. Her breakfast installation this year is called “Incubation,” with yogurt incubating in a grid of sleek fermentation machines and honey perpetually drizzled from overhead — a commentary, according to the press release, on “the creation of food, the creation of life and the creation of art,” among other things, surely.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | Art Basel, More Parties and, Yes, Some Art', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-01T23:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aed1d77e-457f-5a07-ab96-29b98976d669', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aed1d77e-457f-5a07-ab96-29b98976d669'}, {'abstract': 'Florida State, Stanford, Duke and Wake Forest are the final four of women’s soccer.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/womens-soccer-college-cup-will-produce-a-first-time-champion/', 'snippet': 'Florida State, Stanford, Duke and Wake Forest are the final four of women’s soccer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2011 College Cup, for many, will be a weekend filled with firsts.\xa0 The women’s soccer N.C.A.A. semifinal games take place Friday evening at the Kennesaw State University Soccer Stadium in Kennesaw, Ga. — and though the field is filled with the traditionally successful soccer programs, none of the four remaining teams has yet won a national championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women’s Soccer College Cup Will Produce a First-Time Champion', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Soccer Championships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific-12 Conference', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wake Forest University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d