species remain year round and others, from farther north, settle here for the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/nyregion/bird-watching-at-prospect-park-audubon-center.html', 'snippet': 'Late fall and winter are rich times for bird-watching in New York, where several species remain year round and others, from farther north, settle here for the season.', 'lead_paragraph': '“THERE are rumors of an owl,” Michele Dreger told me in a hushed voice, as if the great bird might hear her and be scared off. “Maybe, maybe, there might be, maybe, an owl.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BIRD1_SPAN/02BIRD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BIRD1_SPAN/02BIRD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BIRD1_SPAN/02BIRD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BIRD1_SPAN/02BIRD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BIRD1_SPAN/02BIRD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winged Migrants in Their Brooklyn Pied-à-Terre', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winged Migrants in Their Brooklyn Pied-à-Terre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birdwatching', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audubon Society, New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Marcus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marcus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e559172-704b-5bee-adbb-765efff8b2ed', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e559172-704b-5bee-adbb-765efff8b2ed'}, {'abstract': '“Outrage,” written and directed by Takeshi Kitano, describes a cycle of destruction and vengeance in a crime organization whose code of conduct is being ignored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/movies/outrage-directed-by-takeshi-kitano-review.html', 'snippet': '“Outrage,” written and directed by Takeshi Kitano, describes a cycle of destruction and vengeance in a crime organization whose code of conduct is being ignored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Outrage,” a new yakuza story from Takeshi Kitano, the assaults on the human body are frequent, brutal and at times accompanied by cruel comedy. One man nearly loses his sight; another surely loses his hearing (chopsticks go where none should); and a third suffers a gruesome, teeth-shattering assault during a dental exam, an attack that suggests that Mr. Kitano may have watched “Marathon Man” in the decade since he directed “Brother,” his last yakuza film. Whatever their inspirations, these baroque spasms of violence — evoking see, hear and speak no evil — are just a few of the tortures that he rains down on his characters like a vengeful, mocking god.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02OUTRAGE_SPAN/02OUTRAGE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02OUTRAGE_SPAN/02OUTRAGE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02OUTRAGE_SPAN/OUTRAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02OUTRAGE_SPAN/02OUTRAGE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02OUTRAGE_SPAN/02OUTRAGE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Violence That Japanese Gangsters Do: Betrayal Among the Yakuza', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Outrage'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Violence That Japanese Gangsters Do: Betrayal Among the Yakuza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitano, Takeshi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f2c570-1704-591d-9d9c-74621ee76a91', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f2c570-1704-591d-9d9c-74621ee76a91'}, {'abstract': 'Whether there’s snow or it’s a no-show, many free walking tours will be taking place at Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/walking-tours-in-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'Whether there’s snow or it’s a no-show, many free walking tours will be taking place at Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the holidays coming up, the Miser has been on the lookout for entertainment to satisfy both visiting in-laws and antsy children on school break. Here is a roundup of group-friendly winter activities that will raise your spirits without gouging your budget:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/O2MISER_SPAN/O2MISER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/O2MISER_SPAN/O2MISER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/O2MISER_SPAN/O2MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/O2MISER_SPAN/O2MISER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/O2MISER_SPAN/O2MISER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Miser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekend Miser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcaf3f4e-15bc-570c-9410-bbe8703ff712', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcaf3f4e-15bc-570c-9410-bbe8703ff712'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers may be asked to return to vote on cuts to offset a shortfall in tax collections.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/negotiations-under-way-for-special-session-in-albany-on-spending-cuts/', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers may be asked to return to vote on cuts to offset a shortfall in tax collections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing an increasingly worrisome budget outlook, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and legislative leaders are in negotiations to return to Albany for a special session later this month, an official briefed on the negotiations said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Negotiations Under Way for Special Session in Albany on Budget Shortfall', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skelos, Dean G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8a82328-6964-5eff-aa7d-6985f0949521', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8a82328-6964-5eff-aa7d-6985f0949521'}, {'abstract': 'The South Korean film “The Yellow Sea” is a morality tale full of shocking images and rousing chase scenes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/movies/the-yellow-sea-from-south-korea-review.html', 'snippet': 'The South Korean film “The Yellow Sea” is a morality tale full of shocking images and rousing chase scenes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This being the season for Oscar puffery and pretention, it’s also the time of the year when moviegoers who yearn for more action and less talk can be forgiven for thinking that what’s missing from the big screen is a good beat down. It could use one: this hasn’t been a memorable year for cinematic action, aside from a quicksilver move here and there and that gone-in-60-seconds moment in “Drive” when Ryan Gosling glides a car into park. But now there’s “The Yellow Sea,” a rush of a movie from South Korea that slips and slides from horror to humor on rivers of blood and offers the haunting image of a man, primitive incarnate, beating other men with an enormous, gnawed-over meat bone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02YELLOW_SPAN/SUBYELLOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02YELLOW_SPAN/SUBYELLOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02YELLOW_SPAN/SUBYELLOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02YELLOW_SPAN/SUBYELLOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02YELLOW_SPAN/SUBYELLOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Blood Runs Freely, but the Dogs Can’t', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Yellow Sea'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Blood Runs Freely, But the Dogs Can’t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Na Hong-jin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65286616-2066-5374-9a04-a0d927825283', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65286616-2066-5374-9a04-a0d927825283'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Wright, left, of Bloggingheads.tv and Mickey Kaus of kausfiles debate raising taxes and the Occupy movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000001202664/bloggingheads-the-3-3-3-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Wright, left, of Bloggingheads.tv and Mickey Kaus of kausfiles debate raising taxes and the Occupy movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Wright, left, of Bloggingheads.tv and Mickey Kaus of kausfiles debate raising taxes and the Occupy movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/opinion/video-bhowsplan/video-bhowsplan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLar