te and went looking to buy, confining her hunt to the Upper East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN an attempt to keep her living costs down in the dozen years she had lived in New York, Jessie Weber lived nomadically. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04SUBHUNT4_395/04SUBHUNT4_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Time-Is-Now Apartment', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Time-Is-Now Apartment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cd3c543-e59f-5af9-880a-d7cddb2c74ad', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cd3c543-e59f-5af9-880a-d7cddb2c74ad'}, {'abstract': 'Under new guidelines, the F.H.A. would be able to back loans up to $729,750 in the nation’s most expensive real estate markets, including New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/realestate/jumbo-loan-limits-changed-again.html', 'snippet': 'Under new guidelines, the F.H.A. would be able to back loans up to $729,750 in the nation’s most expensive real estate markets, including New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LESS than two months after lowering the maximum loan amount that could be backed by the Federal Housing Administration, lawmakers in Washington reversed course just before the Thanksgiving holiday and once again raised that limit, offering home buyers more financing options in a tight credit market.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Higher Loan Limits, Again, for Pricey Markets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Higher Loan Limits, Again, for Pricey Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a248502c-69b2-5e7d-a872-28236aabb34f', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a248502c-69b2-5e7d-a872-28236aabb34f'}, {'abstract': 'In the SEC title game on Saturday, Georgia can show that the conference isn’t just about No. 1 Louisiana State and No. 2 Alabama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/sports/ncaafootball/georgia-has-a-chance-to-put-its-mark-on-the-sec.html', 'snippet': 'In the SEC title game on Saturday, Georgia can show that the conference isn’t just about No. 1 Louisiana State and No. 2 Alabama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS, Ga. — In Southeastern Conference play this season, No. 1 Louisiana State won its eight games by an average of 26.6 points, while No. 2 Alabama’s seven victories came by an average of 29.5. The reason for this dominance was simple: the Tigers and the Crimson Tide are ruthless at the point of attack, that spot where linemen crash into linemen and where being bigger and meaner is often the difference.\xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/sports/y-sec/y-sec-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia Has a Chance to Put Its Mark on the SEC', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia Has a Chance to Put Its Mark on the SEC', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richt, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T00:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9505cf9a-6867-5f6c-b9ff-06099fa4ebba', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9505cf9a-6867-5f6c-b9ff-06099fa4ebba'}, {'abstract': 'Passive, or zero-energy, houses are making their way to the United States from Europe and several are being built in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/realestate/zero-energy-construction-crosses-the-ocean.html', 'snippet': 'Passive, or zero-energy, houses are making their way to the United States from Europe and several are being built in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ENVIRONMENTALLY friendly and conservation-minded building techniques have been around for decades. But only in recent years have standards, like the LEED certification from the U.S. Green Building Council, been developed for builders to follow. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04POST1_SPAN/04POST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04POST1_SPAN/04POST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04POST1_SPAN/04POST1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04POST1_SPAN/04POST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/realestate/04POST1_SPAN/04POST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Zero-Energy’ Construction Crosses the Ocean', 'kicker': 'Posting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Zero-Energy’ Construction Crosses the Ocean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu