arrior’s Heart,” starring Kellan Lutz and Ashley Greene, both of the “Twilight” franchise, is about a prep-school lacrosse player’s development of character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ostensibly an inspirational film about a high schooler’s development of character, “A Warrior’s Heart” is factory-issue jingoism, yielding no surprises and frightfully few insights. Conor Sullivan (Kellan Lutz of the “Twilight” franchise, toting six-pack abs and an empty emotional quiver) is a lacrosse player from California newly arrived at a Virginia prep school. A showboating hothead lacking teamwork skills, he has much to learn. Why, he’s even mystified by the sight of a teammate praying before a game. (Some classmates facetiously address him by the nickname West Coast; others call him, yes, Captain America.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02RDP_WARRIORS/FILM-ROUNDUP-WARRIORS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 856, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lacrosse Player Comes Undone, and Grows', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'A Warrior’s Heart'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lutz, Kellan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T01:10:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89f0a9fe-dcc1-5264-b114-acf1202e334c', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89f0a9fe-dcc1-5264-b114-acf1202e334c'}, {'abstract': 'As an investigation continues into the Chevrolet Volt’s battery pack, General Motors said it would buy back cars if owners were concerned about fire risks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/business/gm-offers-to-buy-back-volts-over-fire-risk.html', 'snippet': 'As an investigation continues into the Chevrolet Volt’s battery pack, General Motors said it would buy back cars if owners were concerned about fire risks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — In a rare move, General Motors said Thursday that it would buy back Chevrolet Volts if owners were concerned about fire risks. It also promised to comply with any changes to its battery pack recommended by federal regulators.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/business/Volt/Volt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Offers to Buy Back Hybrid Volts From Owners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Offers To Buy Back Hybrid Volts From Owners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T01:17:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic and Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non