nnels-keep-humming-underground.html', 'snippet': 'Tunnels built to move drugs into the United States have become an always-operating part of life in Tijuana, as entrenched as cheap pharmacies and strip clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIJUANA, Mexico — Squatting and sweating inside the latest drug tunnel found here in this Pacific border city, it was easy to understand the amazement expressed by Mexican and American officials. This one was a stunner. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02TIJUANA2/02TIJUANA2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02TIJUANA2/02TIJUANA2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02TIJUANA2/02TIJUANA2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02TIJUANA2/02TIJUANA2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02TIJUANA2/02TIJUANA2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raids Don’t Keep Tunnel City From Humming Underground', 'kicker': 'Tijuana Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raids Don’t Keep Tunnel City From Humming Underground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tijuana (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T01:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61a72f1a-07d8-5747-a51b-ed64ad54e67e', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61a72f1a-07d8-5747-a51b-ed64ad54e67e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Kinyarwanda,” Alrick Brown depicts a range of events and people during the months of the 1994 genocide of Tutsis in Rwanda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/movies/kinyarwanda-about-1994-genocide-of-tutsis-in-rwanda.html', 'snippet': 'In “Kinyarwanda,” Alrick Brown depicts a range of events and people during the months of the 1994 genocide of Tutsis in Rwanda.', 'lead_paragraph': '“From my heart, I ask for forgiveness,” a Hutu killer says near the end of the weighty “Kinyarwanda.” Forgiveness would have to be a precious natural resource in Rwanda in 1994, after the genocide that left more than 800,000 dead, mostly Tutsis. Those atrocities are the horrific backdrop of the six linked story lines in this dry but thoughtful drama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Linked Stories From the Months of the Rwanda Massacre', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Kinyarwanda'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'