 Silverstein helped devise a bigger, more visually expansive New York Times and in doing so, influenced the redesign of newspapers from coast to coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/nyregion/louis-silverstein-times-art-director-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Silverstein helped devise a bigger, more visually expansive New York Times and in doing so, influenced the redesign of newspapers from coast to coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When The New York Times began publishing on Sept. 18, 1851, it was the New-York Daily Times. — without a “The” but with a period. When the newspaper took its present name six years later, the hyphen stayed (until 1896), and so did the period, until 1967. That was the year that Louis Silverstein, with the nervous approval of his tradition-minded superiors, got rid of it, ending more than a decade of debate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/SILVERSTEIN1-obit/SILVERSTEIN1-obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/SILVERSTEIN1-obit/SILVERSTEIN1-obit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/SILVERSTEIN1-obit/SILVERSTEIN1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/SILVERSTEIN1-obit/SILVERSTEIN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/SILVERSTEIN1-obit/SILVERSTEIN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, '