e': {'main': 'Bach to Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Appreciations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bach to Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Olga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bargemusic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T03:29:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ba40075-c3f3-5dba-b558-1a55467d5c27', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ba40075-c3f3-5dba-b558-1a55467d5c27'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Wildhorn’s “Bonnie & Clyde” is a modest, mildly tuneful musical biography of Clyde Barrow and Bonnie Parker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/theater/reviews/bonnie-clyde-with-laura-osnes-and-jeremy-jordan-review.html', 'snippet': 'Frank Wildhorn’s “Bonnie & Clyde” is a modest, mildly tuneful musical biography of Clyde Barrow and Bonnie Parker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Clyde Barrow is such a cutup. Why, the boy will do most anything to stir up his sluggish fellow Americans: slap at them, tickle them, shoot them in cold blood. He’ll even punch his fist clean through a wall and drive a big old car right onto the stage, just to try to get a rise out of somebody. But Clyde, honey, t’ain’t nothing you can do to raise the pulse of something that’s as near to dead as the show you’re in.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BONNIE/02BONNIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BONNIE/02BONNIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BONNIE/02BONNIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BONNIE/02BONNIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/02BONNIE/02BONNIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Armed and Amorous, Committing Cold-Blooded Musical', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Bonnie & Clyde'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armed And Amorous, Committing Cold-Blooded Musical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osnes, Laura', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wildhorn, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ost, Tobin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T03:38:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ran