e, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02SAFRICA/02SAFRICA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02SAFRICA/02SAFRICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/world/02SAFRICA/02SAFRICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South African Court Invalidates a Presidential Pick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South African Court Invalidates a Presidential Pick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuma, Jacob G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c69b67e-018c-5cbd-92e6-b77153f273db', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c69b67e-018c-5cbd-92e6-b77153f273db'}, {'abstract': 'A Gambian lawyer, Fatou Bensouda, is expected to succeed Luis Moreno-Ocampo next June as chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court in The Hague.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/europe/the-hague-new-prosecutor-picked-for-international-criminal-court.html', 'snippet': 'A Gambian lawyer, Fatou Bensouda, is expected to succeed Luis Moreno-Ocampo next June as chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court in The Hague.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Gambian lawyer, Fatou Bensouda, is expected to succeed Luis Moreno-Ocampo next June as chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court in The Hague. She emerged as the consensus candidate after the only other finalist, Mohamed Chande Othman of Tanzania, agreed to withdraw, diplomats said. All six cases before the young court are linked to African nations, and the majority of the 119 countries that recognize the court had favored an African candidate. Elections for the prosecutor and six judges will be held at the members’ annual meeting on Dec. 12. Mrs. Bensouda, 50, has been deputy prosecutor at the court, and served at the United Nations tribunal dealing with the genocide in Rwanda and as minister of justice of Gambia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hague: New Prosecutor Picked for International Criminal Court', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hague: New Prosecutor Picked For International Criminal Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bensouda, Fatou', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno-Ocampo, Luis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6575f4b8-9148-5281-951b-d144d52afc23', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6575f4b8-9148-5281-951b-d144d52afc23'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony Davis, who had 15 points and 15 rebounds, and Terrence Jones, who scored 26 points, helped No. 1 Kentucky rout Rutgers at Rupp Arena.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/sports/ncaabasketball/kentucky-rolls-past-st-johns-81-59.html', 'snippet': 'Anthony Davis, who had 15 points and 15 rebounds, and Terrence Jones, who scored 26 points, helped No. 1 Kentucky rout Rutgers at Rupp Arena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LEXINGTON, Ky. — The St. John’s players gathered for strength through the flashing lights and pounding bass rhythms of the Kentucky Wildcats’ intimidating introductions. They faced the biggest challenge of the season in their first game on the road Thursday night, coming off a Nov. 26 loss to Northeastern to take on the No. 1-ranked Wildcats.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/sports/red-storm/red-storm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/sports/red-storm/red-storm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/sports/red-storm/red-storm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kentucky Sinks the Red Storm', 'kicker': "Kentucky 81, St. John's 59", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kentucky’s Freshmen Sink the Red Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calipari, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Kentucky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Terrence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Anthony', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St John's University", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Novak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Novak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff2d2c7a-f3e9-527d-aede-f9a710f2d10f', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff2d2c7a-f3e9-527d-aede-f9a710f2d10f'}, {'abstract': 'A explosion shook a branch of the China Construction Bank late Thursday afternoon in Wuhan, killing two people and injuring more than 10.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/asia/china-explosion-at-bank-kills-2.html', 'snippet': 'A explosion shook a branch of the China Construction Bank late Thursday afternoon in Wuhan, killing two people and injuring more than 10.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A explosion shook a branch of the China Construction Bank late Thursday afternoon in Wuhan, a provincial capital in south-central China, a municipal police official there said, and state media reported that at least two people were killed and more than 10 were injured.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Explosion at Bank Kills 2', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Explosion at Bank Kills 2', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Construction Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9cc6f6c-543b-598e-8e72-bbb69bc4b9da', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9cc6f6c-543b-598e-8e72-bbb69bc4b9da'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Wolf, a leading writer from the former East Germany, explored the weight of history on ordinary people as well as her own struggles with Nazism and life in a Communist society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/arts/christa-wolf-dies-at-82-wrote-of-the-germanys.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Wolf, a leading writer from the former East Germany, explored the weight of history on ordinary people as well as her own struggles with Nazism and life in a Communist society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christa Wolf, a leading writer from the former East Germany whose novels, stories and essays explored the weight of history on ordinary individuals, especially and controversially including her own struggles with the legacy of Nazism and life in a Communist society, died Thursday in Berlin. She was 82.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/WOLF-obit/WOLF-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/WOLF-obit/WOLF-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/arts/WOLF-obit/WOLF-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christa Wolf Dies at 82; Wrote of the Germanys', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christa Wolf Dies at 82; Wrote of the Germanys', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolf, Christa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:48:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Binder and Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Binder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6083071-5445-587c-8f1e-b630a4b341c0', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6083071-5445-587c-8f1e-b630a4b341c0'}, {'abstract': 'The German government will double its financing of the country’s Jewish community from next year on, the Central Council of Jews in Germany said in a statement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/world/europe/germany-funds-increased-for-jewish-organization.html', 'snippet': 'The German government will double its financing of the country’s Jewish community from next year on, the Central Council of Jews in Germany said in a statement.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The German government will double its financing of the country’s Jewish community from next year on, the Central Council of Jews in Germany said in a statement. The group will receive an annual grant of $13.4 million a year, twice the current amount, for rebuilding Jewish life in Germany. The financing is part of an agreement that replaces a 2003 accord that gave the Jewish organization the same legal status as the major churches. The funds will be earmarked for the integration of Jewish immigrants; the training of rabbis, cantors and teachers; the support of religious research centers; and work with young people. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Funds Increased for Jewish Organization', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Funds Increased for Jewish Organization', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:52:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Homola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22438bec-1f95-5cdb-afce-c74deaa03503', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22438bec-1f95-5cdb-afce-c74deaa03503'}, {'abstract': 'The Occupy Wall Street daily roundup.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/01/occupywallst-roundup-day-76/', 'snippet': 'The Occupy Wall Street daily roundup.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Scared to death” by Occupy Wall Street, the\xa0Republican strategist Frank Luntz shared some strategies for discussing the protest movement at the Republican Governors Association convention Wednesday. Among his suggestions: don’t say capitalism (“I’m trying to get that word removed”), and when referring to proposed tax increases on the 1 percent, call it “taking from the rich,” rather than taxing. [Yahoo’s The Ticket]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#OccupyWallSt Roundup, Day 76', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T04:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ff5177-207e-5e76-8a12-49446ba24216', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ff5177-207e-5e76-8a12-49446ba24216'}, {'abstract': 'The international body that 