eared in 14 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'deciduous •\\di-ˈsi-jə-wəs, -jü-əs\\• adjective ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | deciduous', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:10:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4013033d-7861-5449-bb58-eda41bd54c25', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4013033d-7861-5449-bb58-eda41bd54c25'}, {'abstract': 'A recent audit revealed that for the first time, hotel tax revenues are not yielding the amount needed to pay off debt incurred to rebuild Soldier Field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/us/as-tax-receipts-lag-another-hole-opens-in-budget.html', 'snippet': 'A recent audit revealed that for the first time, hotel tax revenues are not yielding the amount needed to pay off debt incurred to rebuild Soldier Field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like any government budget, Mayor Rahm Emanuel’s first annual fiscal plan projects exactly how much the administration expects to reap in 2012 from the recently approved tax and fee increases, including the municipal tax on every hotel room stay.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/sub02cncifsa/sub02cncifsa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/us/sub02cncifsa/sub02cncifsa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima