ringfield earlier this year, is regrouping after an embarrassing outburst by its founder forced a leadership shuffle within the organization.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/02CNCSTAND/02CNCSTAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/02CNCSTAND/02CNCSTAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/us/02CNCSTAND/02CNCSTAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Education Group Tries to Rebound After Diatribe', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Education Group Tries To Rebound After Diatribe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stand for Children', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristen McQueary', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McQueary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8b89d87-ea53-5052-a717-d31cff32158b', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8b89d87-ea53-5052-a717-d31cff32158b'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Gilman’s procedure for examining thoroughbred racehorses in New York became standard at racetracks around the country, improving safety for horses and jockeys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/sports/manuel-gilman-influential-racetrack-veterinarian-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Gilman’s procedure for examining thoroughbred racehorses in New York became standard at racetracks around the country, improving safety for horses and jockeys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Manuel Gilman, a veterinarian whose procedure for examining thoroughbred racehorses in New York became standard at racetracks around the country, improving safety for horses and jockeys and bolstering the sport’s integrity for bettors, died on Nov. 25 in Manhasset, N.Y. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/02gilman-1/02gilman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/02gilman-1/02gilman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/02gilman-1/02gilman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Manuel Gilman, Influential Racetrack Veterinarian, Dies at 91', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manuel Gilman, Racetrack Veterinarian, Dies at 91', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:27:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b16ca99e-dbd1-5150-b027-c23deb9e9414', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b16ca99e-dbd1-5150-b027-c23deb9e9414'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Dave Bing of Detroit had been at odds with City Council members and unions over how to resolve the city’s financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/us/in-detroit-a-bid-to-prevent-a-state-takeover.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Dave Bing of Detroit had been at odds with City Council members and unions over how to resolve the city’s financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing mounting pressure from Michigan’s governor to solve Detroit’s financial crisis, Mayor Dave Bing on Thursday stood beside union representatives and City Council members in a public show of unity, a last-ditch effort to keep the state’s largest city out of state control. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 383, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/us/DETROIT/DETROIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Detroit, an Effort to Prevent a State Takeover', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Ailing Detroit, a Show of Unity in an Effort to Prevent a State Takeover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Richard Dale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bing, Dave', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:27:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9881668a-78e7-5334-9a83-ce7ba78c480a', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9881668a-78e7-5334-9a83-ce7ba78c480a'}, {'abstract': 'Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers is under investigation for allegations that the school gave students credits for multiple courses for taking a single class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/education/problems-with-credits-at-school-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers is under investigation for allegations that the school gave students credits for multiple courses for taking a single class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chances that a student at Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers in the Bronx would graduate in four years were already poor, but seniors there said this week that they had been told of a new obstacle: a problem with credits that could cost some of them their diplomas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Problems With Credits at School in the Bronx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Problems With Credits At School In the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna M. Phillips and Hadas Goshen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d00c12a9-b1a0-5312-b096-bc466f065577', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d00c12a9-b1a0-5312-b096-bc466f065577'}, {'abstract': 'An Internet entrepreneur is betting that people will be willing to pay a lot of money to have an e-mail address that ends in @chicago.com.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/us/my-kind-of-town-and-now-maybe-your-kind-of-domain-name.html', 'snippet': 'An Internet entrepreneur is betting that people will be willing to pay a lot of money to have an e-mail address that ends in @chicago.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Warren writes a column for the Chicago News Cooperative.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Kind of Town, and Now Maybe Your Kind of Domain Name', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Kind of Town, and Now Maybe Your Kind of Domain Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domain Names (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adcf2530-5d1b-5032-9d42-a3e48e1b9f4f', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adcf2530-5d1b-5032-9d42-a3e48e1b9f4f'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/newswallah-in-the-english-language-press-friday-9/', 'snippet': 'Top stories on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The parliamentary panel drafting the anti-corruption bill has abruptly decided to exclude India’s graft-ridden “lower bureaucracy,” the six million municipal workers, policemen and clerks who interact most with the average person, from the proposed Lokpal bill. (Times of India). Expect the anti-corruption group Team Anna, which had fought for a tougher version of the Lokpal, to accuse the government of trying to pass a toothless law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: In the English-Language Press Friday', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:47:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b77028d-e7b7-5f26-8cf5-3361f925b5d9', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b77028d-e7b7-5f26-8cf5-3361f925b5d9'}, {'abstract': 'Chetan and Raj, two cousins from a Mumbai slum, are fashion-conscious child laborers.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/child-labors-fashionable-face/', 'snippet': 'Chetan and Raj, two cousins from a Mumbai slum, are fashion-conscious child laborers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chetan and Sarju wear low-waist, ice-wash, medium-skinny jeans that cost 500 rupees (about $9.60); open-neck cotton shirts with the sleeves rolled up to their elbows (150 rupees); and medium high-top canvas sneakers (300 rupees). Chetan’s sneakers are pink and inscribed with the letters “D&G”. Sarju’s blue sneakers simply say “Sports.” The 17-year-old cousins are from the Mumbai suburb of Jogeshwari.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Child Labor’s Fashionable Face', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baba, Sai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T05:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonia Faleiro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Faleiro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d1004a7-9e9a-57d7-8439-a4d4147706a1', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d1004a7-9e9a-57d7-8439-a4d4147706a1'}, {'abstract': 'The recipe for a substantial presidential campaign is hard to follow.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/can-we-get-serious/', 'snippet': 'The recipe for a substantial presidential campaign is hard to follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To select someone worthy of sitting in George Washington’s chair, sleeping in Abraham Lincoln’s bed and governing from Franklin Roosevelt’s desk, Americans crave a substantial presidential campaign, as long as they don’t have to endure too many boring speeches. Like every human decision-making process, presidential campaigns seesaw between the serious and the silly. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Get Serious?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldwater, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {