 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T07:59:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e34bc2b-16bf-5a1d-ac6b-85dc4dca8318', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e34bc2b-16bf-5a1d-ac6b-85dc4dca8318'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in Boston said Thursday that the Occupy Boston encampment in Dewey Square could stay for now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/us/massachusetts-occupy-boston-camp-allowed-to-stay.html', 'snippet': 'A judge in Boston said Thursday that the Occupy Boston encampment in Dewey Square could stay for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge in Boston said Thursday that the Occupy Boston encampment in Dewey Square could stay for now, extending a temporary restraining order barring the city from removing tents or protesters from the area without a court order. Lawyers representing four demonstrators are seeking an injunction that would offer longer-term protection to the protesters. Judge Frances McIntyre said she would rule by mid-December, at which time the temporary order will expire. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Camp Allowed to Stay', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Camp Allowed To Stay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T08:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1247f3-3838-56a7-9ccf-a1b53fb355c5', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1247f3-3838-56a7-9ccf-a1b53fb355c5'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/news-quiz-dec-2-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Dec. 2, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T08:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenan Christiansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christiansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce635ae4-0af2-5aaa-b256-ae10e2fdf646', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce635ae4-0af2-5aaa-b256-ae10e2fdf646'}, {'abstract': 'On Dec. 2, 1954, the United States Senate voted, 67-22, to condemn Senator Joseph R. McCarthy on two counts for conduct that “tended to bring the Senate into dishonor and disrepute.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/dec-2-1954-anti-communist-senator-joseph-mccarthy-is-condemned/', 'snippet': 'On Dec. 2, 1954, the United States Senate voted, 67-22, to condemn Senator Joseph R. McCarthy on two counts for conduct that “tended to bring the Senate into dishonor and disrepute.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 2, 1954, the United States Senate voted, 67-22, to condemn Senator Joseph R. McCarthy, a Republican from Wisconsin, on two counts for conduct that “tended to bring the Senate into dishonor and disrepute.” The New York Times explained that he was condemned for “contempt of a Senate Elections subcommittee that investigated his conduct and financial affairs, for abuse of its members, and for his insults to the Senate itself during the censure proceeding.”The Senate’s resolution used the word “condemn” rather than the traditional “censure,” which sparked a debate over whether Mr. McCarthy had actually been censured — one senator went so far as to read from Webster’s Dictionary. The Times reported that, when asked if he thought he had been censured, Mr. McCarthy replied, “Well, it wasn’t exactly a vote of confidence.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 2, 1954 | Anti-Communist Senator McCarthy Is Condemned', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T09:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542ba168-80c4-580c-a3f6-6a47b7fcad0d', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542ba168-80c4-580c-a3f6-6a47b7fcad0d'}, {'abstract': 'How is Florida A&M responding to the death of a student?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/hazing-suspected-in-death-of-drum-major/', 'snippet': 'How is Florida A&M responding to the death of a student?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO died at Florida A&M?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hazing Suspected in Death of Drum Major', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T09:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b31fa3f-a925-5be4-a839-323213c86250', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b31fa3f-a925-5be4-a839-323213c86250'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best pair of words to complete a sentence?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/test-yourself-english-dec-2-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best pair of words to complete a sentence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “A Family’s Billions, Artfully Sheltered.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Dec. 2, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T09:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64be0ce0-c5ff-58ca-be72-47e480543974', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64be0ce0-c5ff-58ca-be72-47e480543974'}, {'abstract': 'Times photographs of the opera, on stage and off, reveal the many small moments that go into creating a spectacle.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/intimate-moments-among-grand-gestures/', 'snippet': 'Times photographs of the opera, on stage and off, reveal the many small moments that go into creating a spectacle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How imperfect a pairing it seems: the silent, still, small-scale, black-and-white photograph and the sonorous, tumultuous, extravagant and kaleidoscopic opera.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intimate Moments Among Grand Gestures', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T10:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darcy Eveleigh and David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darcy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eveleigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b8958dc-5eb1-5aba-9c19-c7cbb733eb7a', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b8958dc-5eb1-5aba-9c19-c7cbb733eb7a'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Tell us what items you might pack in a “go-bag” if you were evacuated from your home. Would your items be mostly practical, sentimental or financially valuable?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/what-would-you-put-in-your-emergency-go-bag/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Tell us what items you might pack in a “go-bag” if you were evacuated from your home. Would your items be mostly practical, sentimental or financially valuable?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A “go-bag” is defined by the New York City Office of Emergency Management as “a collection of items you can use in the event of an evacuation,” but in a recent Styles article, a reporter asked some well-known New Yorkers what other items they’d put in their bags besides basic emergency provisions. If you were leaving your home in a hurry in the event of a disaster, what items — irreplaceable because of their practical, sentimental or monetary value — would you make sure to include in your bag? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would You Put in Your Emergency ‘Go-Bag’?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T10:02:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fef95ead-5c59-5784-aa8f-00e2b3a81fe3', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fef95ead-5c59-5784-aa8f-00e2b3a81fe3'}, {'abstract': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany on Friday ruled out a rapid solution to the debt crisis as she sought stronger fiscal cooperation across the euro zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/world/europe/angela-merkel-germany-speech-euro-zone-debt-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany on Friday ruled out a rapid solution to the debt crisis as she sought stronger fiscal cooperation across the euro zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Chancellor Angela Merkel on Friday called for swift action to amend European treaties to address the underlying causes of the debt crisis that has shaken Europe and jeopardized the future of the common currency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03GERMANY/03GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03GERMANY/03GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03GERMANY/03GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03GERMANY/03GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03GERMANY/03GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merkel Seeks Swift Action on What May Be Long Job to Save the Euro', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merkel Seeks Swift Action on What May Be Long Job to Save the Euro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T10:18:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish and Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80381996-38d1-5fee-8846-12d3548b26b5', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80381996-38d1-5fee-8846-12d3548b26b5'}, {'abstract': 'The Taj Mahal diamond is expected to fetch as much as half a million dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/indian-history-and-mystery-in-lizs-jewels/', 'snippet': 'The Taj Mahal diamond is expected to fetch as much as half a million dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A part of Indian history is being auctioned off on December 13th in New York City when the late Elizabeth Taylor’s legendary jewelry will be up for bidding at Christie’s: the Taj Mahal diamond from 1627. Taylor received the stone, which is set as pendant, as a gift on her 40th birthday in 1972 from Richard Burton, whom she was married to at the time. Burton bought it from Cartier for 350,000 pounds, and Taylor had the jeweler replace its original silk chord with an adjustable diamond and ruby chain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian History and Mystery in Liz’s Jewels', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahal, Taj', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T10:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db63e12-c993-5826-89df-544bb5710c97', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db63e12-c993-5826-89df-544bb5710c97'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s middling appeal among moderate voters is not doing as much as it might to help offset his weak poll numbers with the most conservative Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/does-romney-have-a-moderate-problem/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s middling appeal among moderate voters is not doing as much as it might to help offset his weak poll numbers with the most conservative Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney is enduring a tough week. He now trails Newt Gingrich by 20 or more points in some state and national surveys. He had a testy interview with Brett Baier of Fox News, and then compounded the problem by complaining about Mr. Baier’s questioning later. A candidate whose presence in the race probably helped Mr. Romney, Herman Cain, is now in jeopardy of dropping out. Both Democrats and Mr. Romney’s opponents are putting out ads that hit Mr. Romney on what is perhaps his core vulnerability, his reputation for flip-flopping. Meanwhile, one of Mr. Romney’s greatest strengths, his strong positioning in New Hampshire, is at least a bit less certain now following the endorsement of Newt Gingrich by the Manchester Union-Leader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Romney Have a Moderate Problem?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T11:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8b09bb7-9ae9-55bb-9eb6-951ce465664f', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8b09bb7-9ae9-55bb-9eb6-951ce465664f'}, {'abstract': 'On the night of Dec. 5, don’t be nervous if you spot a bishop, angel and devil sitting together in a pub in Prague. Saturday is the celebration of St. Mikulas (Nicholas) — a Czech figure similar to Santa Claus — and while primarily an evening for children, it still brings a smile of remembrance to adults’ faces.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/not-to-be-outdone-by-santa-saint-mikulas-brings-cheer-to-prague/', 'snippet': 'On the night of Dec. 5, don’t be nervous if you spot a bishop, angel and devil sitting together in a pub in Prague. Saturday is the celebration of St. Mikulas (Nicholas) — a Czech figure similar to Santa Claus — and while primarily an evening for ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night of Dec. 5, don’t be nervous if you spot a bishop, angel and devil sitting together in a pub in Prague. Saturday is the celebration of St. Mikulas (Nicholas) — a Czech figure similar to Santa Claus — and while primarily an evening for children, it still brings a smile of remembrance to adults’ faces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not to be Outdone by Santa, St. Mikulas Brings Cheer to Prague', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T11:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacy Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/