protect Syrian civilians from the government’s crackdown, amid warnings that the country is headed toward civil war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/world/1syria-image/1syria-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Says Action Needed to Prevent Civil War in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Human Rights Official Calls for Intervention in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T13:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0451c6-3310-5578-87bd-973a4e2d9bad', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0451c6-3310-5578-87bd-973a4e2d9bad'}, {'abstract': 'Two friends are betting that they can build an application that can accurately predict if it will rain 30 minutes to an hour in the future.  They use weather maps to try to predict how a storm will behave.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/building-a-weather-app-that-sees-the-near-future/', 'snippet': 'Two friends are betting that they can build an application that can accurately predict if it will rain 30 minutes to an hour in the future.  They use weather maps to try to predict how a storm will behave.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Weather forecasts are great at letting you know whether to grab an umbrella before leaving the house — but what if you needed to know if you had enough time to sprint to a car before a thunderstorm hit?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/01/technology/01bits-darksky/01bits-darksky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building a Weather App That Sees the (Near) Future', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'App That Offers Weather Forecast To the Minute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T13:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d158f378-d5d4-5806-be9e-23a276256c90', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d158f378-d5d4-5806-be9e-23a276256c90'}, {'abstract': 'Red herrings and other false steps on “The X Factor.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/x-factor-watch-payback-for-simon-cowell/', 'snippet': 'Red herrings and other false steps on “The X Factor.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Cowell finally paid a price on Thursday night for the weeks of verbal abuse he has hurled at his fellow “X Factor” judges, as they formed a voting bloc against him and tossed the first of his contestants from the competition. To say that he looked displeased at the end would be an understatement. He looked as if he were ready to bust some heads open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X Factor’ Watch: Payback for Simon Cowell', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T13:34:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e98a78bf-82ed-5a39-9cb0-16301ad2f08a', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e98a78bf-82ed-5a39-9cb0-16301ad2f08a'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/opinion-report-ted-stevens/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Ted Stevens', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'r