ritic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Apartment Critic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toy, Vivian S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T15:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian S. Toy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Toy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa0ba49-8a06-5ad5-98b7-58dce06a3a7e', 'word_count': 1437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa0ba49-8a06-5ad5-98b7-58dce06a3a7e'}, {'abstract': 'The star and director of “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy” talk about the look of the film. Their aim: the smell of damp tweed.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/tinker-tailor-and-the-smell-of-damp-tweed/', 'snippet': 'The star and director of “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy” talk about the look of the film. Their aim: the smell of damp tweed.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:47 a.m. | Updated The Bagger has already discussed how difficult it was to adapt “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy,” John le Carré’s classic thriller. But it was also difficult to cast the right actor to play the dour intelligence expert George Smiley, who had been memorably portrayed by Alec Guinness in the 1979 British mini-series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tinker, Tailor’ and the Smell of Damp Tweed', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa15f78-ae6e-5c48-9f27-b4cdfe468551', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa15f78-ae6e-5c48-9f27-b4cdfe468551'}, {'abstract': 'A real estate reporter for The Times who has visited nearly 600 Manhattan apartments fields your questions about buying, selling and related concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/q-and-a-with-vivian-toy-the-apartment-critic/', 'snippet': 'A real estate reporter for The Times who has visited nearly 600 Manhattan apartments fields your questions about buying, selling and related concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:07 p.m. | Updated  We are no longer accepting questions. Stay tuned for Vivian Toy’s answers on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Vivian Toy: The Apartment Critic', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toy, Vivian S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87ffc57c-f021-507f-b149-d7c963ecadea', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87ffc57c-f021-507f-b149-d7c963ecadea'}, {'abstract': 'As the economic downturn drove up the number of middle-class Jews struggling to make ends meet, an Atlanta rabbi started a free-loan program called a gemach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/us/a-traditional-jewish-loan-program-helps-ease-pain-of-tough-economic-times.html', 'snippet': 'As the economic downturn drove up the number of middle-class Jews struggling to make ends meet, an Atlanta rabbi started a free-loan program called a gemach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Hirshy Minkowicz was growing up in a Hasidic enclave of Brooklyn 30 years ago, he often noticed visitors arriving after dinner to meet with his father. They would withdraw into the study, speak for a time, then part with some confidential agreement having been sealed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/us/RELIGION-1/RELIGION-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/us/RELIGION-1/RELIGION-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/us/RELIGION-1/RELIGION-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/us/RELIGION-1/RELIGION-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/us/RELIGION-1/RELIGION-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loans Without Profit Help Relieve Economic Pain', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loans Without Profit Help Relieve Economic Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b3323e3-d962-5e28-af8d-233aa518a1f0', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b3323e3-d962-5e28-af8d-233aa518a1f0'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators examining the 2008 push by Representative Jesse Jackson Jr. to take Barack Obama’s Senate seat found “probable cause” that the Illinois Democrat directed one of his supporters to raise money in exchange for an appointment to the Senate, an investigative report shows.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/ethics-report-lists-probable-cause-in-jackson-investigation/', 'snippet': 'Investigators examining the 2008 push by Representative Jesse Jackson Jr. to take Barack Obama’s Senate seat found “probable cause” that the Illinois Democrat directed one of his supporters to raise money in exchange for an appointment to the Sena...', 'lead_paragraph': 'House investigators examining the 2008 push by Representative Jesse L. Jackson Jr. to take the Senate seat being vacated by Barack Obama found “probable cause” that Mr. Jackson, an Illinois Democrat, directed one of his supporters to raise money for Rod Blagojevich, who was then the Illinois governor, in exchange for the appointment to the Senate, a detailed investigative report released Friday shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethics Office Releases Report on Jackson’s Push for Senate Seat', 'kicker': Non