nswers readers’ questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will 5,000 Passing Yards Eventually Be the Norm?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brees, Drew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Ferguson, D'Brickashaw", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luck, Andrew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Dan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Terrell', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suh, Ndamukong', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbd2c573-46e2-5fe6-ae2a-f2283b93d3eb', 'word_count': 2589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbd2c573-46e2-5fe6-ae2a-f2283b93d3eb'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/weekend-fare-70/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A holiday tradition continues this weekend, when Le Parker Meridien hotel, 119 West 56th Street (between Sixth and Seventh Avenues) in Midtown West, will display gingerbread houses created by bakeries and restaurants across the city in its lobby. The exhibit, which runs through Jan. 6, is free but the public can vote for its favorite with a $1 ticket, to benefit City Harvest, sold at the concierge desk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:18:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/359cbfa9-6a66-5874-99ef-6a921d3bd688', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/359cbfa9-6a66-5874-99ef-6a921d3bd688'}, {'abstract': 'On paper, hydraulic fracturing is a highly-technical subject. It is not a highly technical debate.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/dispatch-from-a-hydrofracking-hearing/', 'snippet': 'On paper, hydraulic fracturing is a highly-technical subject. It is not a highly technical debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Governor Andrew Cuomo’s administration is considering whether to allow drilling companies to blast millions of gallons of water and other chemicals into underground shale formations in New York State to extract natural gas.\xa0 His Department of Conservation put out 2,000 pages of documents about this process, known as hydraulic fracturing or hydrofracking, in September, and wants all public comments by January 11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dispatch From a Hydrofracking Hearing', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ec56efa-33ce-59c0-aaaf-549c871f1a0f', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ec56efa-33ce-59c0-aaaf-549c871f1a0f'}, {'abstract': 'Walter Martin and Paloma Muñez’s snowy T for our holiday issue was inspired by blizzards, namely those of D.W. Griffith and Stanley Kubrick.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/come-and-get-it/', 'snippet': 'Walter Martin and Paloma Muñez’s snowy T for our holiday issue was inspired by blizzards, namely those of D.W. Griffith and Stanley Kubrick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s Sally Singer discovered the work of Walter Martin and Paloma Muñoz, the artists who designed the T for our holiday issue, at the Museum of Art and Design, where a selection of their whimsical snow globes was on display as part of the group show “Otherwordly: Optical Delusions and Small Realities.” Indeed, the duo known for fabricating and photographing miniwinters in glass seemed a perfect fit for the season at hand. Here, the artists talk about their favorite storms, their preferred presents and the resolutions that rarely get made in the new year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Come and Get It!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T16:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00e9ee68-7965-5a1c-8f1e-9f1b431baba3', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00e9ee68-7965-5a1c-8f1e-9f1b431baba3'}, {'abstract': 'The House Agriculture Committee voted to force Jon S. Corzine, the former chief of MF Global, to appear at a hearing, and two other Congressional panels are considering subpoenas.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/house-committee-subpoenas-corzine/', 'snippet': 'The House Agriculture Committee voted to force Jon S. Corzine, the former chief of MF Global, to appear at a hearing, and two other Congressional panels are considering subpoenas.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:02 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Panel Subpoenas Corzine to Testify in MF Global Inquiry', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_k