igh-profile releases — “Hugo,” “The Artist” and “My Week With Marilyn” — the movies are still a favorite topic of the movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/movies/a-season-of-movies-about-movies.html', 'snippet': 'To judge by three recent high-profile releases — “Hugo,” “The Artist” and “My Week With Marilyn” — the movies are still a favorite topic of the movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1937 Frank S. Nugent, a film critic for The New York Times, cast an amusing and jaundiced look at what had become a favorite subject for the movies: Movies! “Before our somewhat astonished eyes,” he wrote, Hollywood “has begun shedding its 7 and 70 veils, dropping a shoulder strap here, discarding a wrap there.” But Nugent, who went on to write films like “The Searchers,” was wise to this crafty tease. In the end “back-studio pictures” like “A Star Is Born,” he wrote, “flounced offstage with protective hands over the greatest of its mysteries.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04DARGIS2_SPAN/04DARGIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04DARGIS2_SPAN/04DARGIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04DARGIS2_SPAN/04DARGIS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04DARGIS2_SPAN/04DARGIS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04DARGIS2_SPAN/04DARGIS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thum