 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T19:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82a9b72f-e07b-5e81-8ff6-c0316e48a720', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82a9b72f-e07b-5e81-8ff6-c0316e48a720'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Rodgers recalls his three years of watching film and leading the Packers’ scout team as critical to his success.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/sports/football/the-education-of-the-packers-aaron-rodgers.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Rodgers recalls his three years of watching film and leading the Packers’ scout team as critical to his success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. — In his rookie season, in 2005, Aaron Rodgers almost never played on Sundays. Instead, he played on Wednesdays, Thursdays, Fridays and Saturdays, in practice, against increasingly agitated teammates.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/jp-rodgers/jp-rodgers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/jp-rodgers/jp-rodgers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/jp-rodgers/jp-rodgers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/jp-rodgers/jp-rodgers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/jp-rodgers/jp-rodgers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Education of a Quarterback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Education of a Packers Quarterback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T19:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a50e59-f46d-534c-9205-c4b8396414fb', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a50e59-f46d-534c-9205-c4b8396414fb'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Crichton returns to the hardcover fiction best-seller list with “Micro,” a techno thriller completed by Richard Preston after Crichton’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Crichton returns to the hardcover fiction best-seller list with “Micro,” a techno thriller completed by Richard Preston after Crichton’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAN VS. NATURE: Michael Crichton died in 2008, but he hasn’t let a little thing like that keep him from the best-seller list. His first posthumous success was “Pirate Latitudes,” a daffy high-seas adventure discovered among his files, which hit No. 2 on the hardcover fiction list in December 2009. Now Crichton returns with “Micro,” a techno-thriller left mostly unfinished at the time of his death; to complete it, his estate turned to Richard Preston of “The Hot Zone” fame. The novel, at No. 6 in its first week, is vintage high-concept Crichton — a group of science graduate students, hoping to score jobs with a nanotechnology start-up, are instead reduced in size to half an inch and have to battle the microfauna in a Hawaiian rain forest. Think of it as “Honey, I Shrunk Jurassic Park,” with spiders in place of T. rex and wasps in place of raptors. Did Preston have a hard time filling Crichton’s shoes? Not really. He told NPR recently that when he was working with an editor on an earlier book, “at one point she put her hands on her head and said, ‘Oh, Richard, you’re just a 14-year-old boy who likes to gross out the girls.’ I think Michael Crichton had something of that in him too.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/books/review/11inside-pic/11inside-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 301, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/books/review/11inside-pic/11inside-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/books/review/11inside-pic/11inside-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': 'TBR', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': No