me': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chick-fil-A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f757b32-f235-5ca6-9a74-48b46992b096', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f757b32-f235-5ca6-9a74-48b46992b096'}, {'abstract': 'The director Henri-Georges Clouzot, the subject of a Museum of Modern Art retrospective, seemed condemned to a life of estrangement. Just look at his films.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/movies/henri-georges-clouzot-retrospective-at-moma.html', 'snippet': 'The director Henri-Georges Clouzot, the subject of a Museum of Modern Art retrospective, seemed condemned to a life of estrangement. Just look at his films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WATCHING a film by the French master Henri-Georges Clouzot, you often feel as if the walls were closing in on you — even when there are no walls. “The Wages of Fear” (1953), the movie that opens the Museum of Modern Art’s Clouzot retrospective on Thursday, takes place almost entirely out of doors, yet it’s as claustrophobic as a stretch in solitary confinement. This picture, which was his first big international success, and which remains one of his most popular, tells the story of four men driving truckloads of nitroglycerine over some very poorly maintained South American roads.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04CLOUZOT_SPAN/04CLOUZOT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04CLOUZOT_SPAN/04CLOUZOT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 231}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04CLOUZOT_SPAN/04CLOUZOT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04CLOUZOT_SPAN/04CLOUZOT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/arts/04CLOUZOT_SPAN/04CLOUZOT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Auteur’s Bleak Visions of Confinement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A French Auteur’s Bleak Visions Of Confinement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clouzot, Henri-Georges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terrence Rafferty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafferty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2d249f4-25d5-5c35-bdb5-d53281805ad4', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2d249f4-25d5-5c35-bdb5-d53281805ad4'}, {'abstract': 'Axion International has developed a process to reuse hard plastic in building materials that are strong enough to supplant steel and concrete, forgoing the trip to a landfill.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/plastic-bottles-reborn-as-a-bridge/', 'snippet': 'Axion International has developed a process to reuse hard plastic in building materials that are strong enough to supplant steel and concrete, forgoing the trip to a landfill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The town of York, Me., is putting up what could be a bridge to a better future, not because of it where it goes but because of what it is made of: plastic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard Plastic Bottles, Reborn as a Bridge', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polymers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:14:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f787fe2f-eb0f-5e4e-98b6-b3e4ceb29727', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f787fe2f-eb0f-5e4e-98b6-b3e4ceb29727'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at a new credit report that contains information about your financial life not captured by most of the traditional credit reporting bureaus.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/a-new-credit-report-tracks-more-of-your-financial-life/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at a new credit report that contains information about your financial life not captured by most of the traditional credit reporting bureaus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Your Money column discusses a new credit report from a company called CoreLogic, which includes all sorts of information about your financial life that is not captured by the reports from the traditional credit reporting agencies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Credit Report Tracks More of Your Financial Life', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbdfe604-e8e3-50b9-b382-453c811ff2f8', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbdfe604-e8e3-50b9-b382-453c811ff2f8'}, {'abstract': 'Designed by John Z. DeLorean, the Banshee has resurfaced on the auction Web site, having failed to sell in previous online auctions and at various collector-car events.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/1964-pontiac-banshee-a-one-of-a-kind-concept-looks-for-love-again-on-ebay/', 'snippet': 'Designed by John Z. DeLorean, the Banshee has resurfaced on the auction Web site, having failed to sell in previous online auctions and at various collector-car events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1964 Pontiac Banshee prototype bears many attributes of a blue-chip collector car, yet blue-chip sale prices have eluded its owner, the longtime Pontiac collector Len Napoli. The one-of-a-kind concept was recently listed by Mr. Napoli on eBay at the buy-it-now price of $750,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964 Pontiac Banshee: A One-of-a-Kind Concept Looks for Love, Again, on eBay', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeLorean, John Z', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pontiac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rory Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e32ac9-28ef-579d-bc77-dad5f140562f', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e32ac9-28ef-579d-bc77-dad5f140562f'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Luc Godard is the director behind the sprawling and subjective eight-part “Histoire(s) du Cinéma.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/movies/homevideo/new-on-dvd-jean-luc-godards-histoire-s-du-cinema.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Luc Godard is the director behind the sprawling and subjective eight-part “Histoire(s) du Cinéma.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of the major works of Jean-Luc Godard, the eight-part essay film “Histoire(s) du Cinéma” has revealed itself slowly over a period of more than 30 ye