tutions, which could lead to difficulty lining up voters behind whomever the party establishment  wants to run for president.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/mistrust-of-institutions-may-touch-g-o-p-itself/', 'snippet': 'Republicans have become less trusting of political and societal institutions, which could lead to difficulty lining up voters behind whomever the party establishment  wants to run for president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the fundamental challenge in analyzing this year’s Republican nomination race is the unusual divergence between the popular support for the various candidates, as can be measured through opinion polls, and their support among the party establishment, as can be measured through endorsements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistrust of Institutions May Touch G.O.P. Itself', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e342071-b056-5066-a80d-d2d459fe5805', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e342071-b056-5066-a80d-d2d459fe5805'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney received the endorsement of Ramesh Ponnuru, a senior editor at National Review, the conservative magazine and Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/high-profile-conservative-endorses-romney/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney received the endorsement of Ramesh Ponnuru, a senior editor at National Review, the conservative magazine and Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich may have The Union Leader of New Hampshire, but on Friday, Mitt Romney landed his own high-profile media endorsement — Ramesh Ponnuru, a senior editor at National Review.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High-Profile Conservative Endorses Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponnuru, Ramesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Review', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c1d89c6-9115-5174-a716-82862e40048f', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c1d89c6-9115-5174-a716-82862e40048f'}, {'abstract': 'In his book “The Foreign Burial of American War Dead,” Chris Dickon notes that 25 dogs were killed in Guam while serving alongside American troops.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/war-dogs-of-guam/', 'snippet': 'In his book “The Foreign Burial of American War Dead,” Chris Dickon notes that 25 dogs were killed in Guam while serving alongside American troops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to our article about military working dogs that get post-traumatic stress disorder and our post Thursday about bomb-sniffing dogs in Iraq, the writer and historian Chris Dickon pointed out that American military working dogs played an important role in World War II. In his book, The Foreign Burial of American War Dead, Mr. Dickon notes that 25 dogs were killed in Guam while serving alongside American troops. Those American-born and bred dogs were buried and reburied in three different locations and have been memorialized on plaques and in ceremonies, Mr. Dickon says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'War Dogs of Guam', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcdfe4fa-5f76-5a51-bbf8-a59d58841aa7', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcdfe4fa-5f76-5a51-bbf8-a59d58841aa7'}, {'abstract': 'Subjects include developments in the Occupy movement, a bribery case, “American Pie” and building blocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/02/nyregion/1202WIP.html', 'snippet': 'Subjects include developments in the Occupy movement, a bribery case, “American Pie” and building blocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Subjects include developments in the Occupy movement, a bribery case, “American Pie” and building blocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/nyregion/1202WIP-slide-A6MQ/1202WIP-slide-A6MQ-jumbo.jpg', 