rhythmic — application statement by Jan. 1, The Choice is glad to suggest a source of inspiration and a road-map for loosening up in the writing process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feel Me Flow: An Invitation to Rhyme', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T21:56:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/975a5e91-78ac-59d5-9a8c-5ac5ce78eb56', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/975a5e91-78ac-59d5-9a8c-5ac5ce78eb56'}, {'abstract': 'The Producers Guild releases its documentary nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/producers-guild-offers-its-documentary-nominations/', 'snippet': 'The Producers Guild releases its documentary nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Documentary-watchers, keep your eyes on “Project Nim” and “Bill Cunningham New York”: both films made the cut for the Academy’s documentary shortlist and today they were also named to the Producers Guild list of candidates. The stories of an ape experiment gone terribly awry and our own beloved street style photographer join “Senna,” “The Union” and “Beats, Rhymes & Life: The Travels of A Tribe Called Quest” on the Producers Guild shortlist. The latter three films did not make the cut for the Oscars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producers Guild Offers Its Documentary Nominations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T22:05:04+0000', 'document_typ