also more art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday brought dramatically high winds to Miami, but also more art. At 10 a.m., the New Art Dealers Alliance (NADA) Art Fair opened its door for preview at the Deauville Beach Resort. Since relocating to the beach a couple years back, NADA has gotten better and better with an influx of very young galleries like West Street and 47 Canal (where Josh Kline’s three consumer-conceptual infusions — “Blue Listerine With Dentyne Ice,” “Mountain Dew With Claratin-D” and “Red Bull With Vivarin” — were displayed on a pedestal in Bodum coffee presses). The Night Gallery, from Los Angeles, took advantage of the fair’s hotel setting, luring collectors and company back to a boudoir (Room 1010) upholstered in black velvet and hung with artwork, all of which was for sale, naturally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | ABMB’s Second Wind', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-02T23:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6513a8cd-0091-5c3a-9a68-1ec3ce0d5cee', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6513a8cd-0091-5c3a-9a68-1ec3ce0d5cee'}, {'abstract': 'The Jaeger-LeCoultre Reverso watch hasn’t changed much in 80 years, but its anniversary marketing has.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/fashion/the-jaeger-lecoultre-reverso-watch-turns-80.html', 'snippet': 'The Jaeger-LeCoultre Reverso watch hasn’t changed much in 80 years, but its anniversary marketing has.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE list of truly classic watches — the timeless icons of the watchmaker’s 