'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/arts/music/daniel-harding-conducts-new-york-philharmonic-in-mahler.html', 'snippet': 'The British conductor Daniel Harding led the New York Philharmonic in a heart-rending account of Mahler’s 10th Symphony, which the ensemble has not played since 1984.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are long past the time when extensive podium experience is regarded as an absolute prerequisite for performance of the symphonic repertory’s grandest works. Even so, when the British conductor Daniel Harding stepped onto the podium at Avery Fisher Hall to lead the New York Philharmonic in Mahler’s 10th Symphony, on Thursday evening, you had to readjust any lingering preconceptions about what a Mahler conductor should look like. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Embracing the Contradictions, Ambiguities and Anguish of Mahler’s Final Work', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Embracing the Contradictions, Ambiguities and Anguish of Mahler’s Final Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harding, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T00:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf1966fb-a194-5e00-ac46-00b331ed1903', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf1966fb-a194-5e00-ac46-00b331ed1903'}, {'abstract': 'With a new complex of its own being built in Hell’s Kitchen, MCC Theater expects to offer more productions and longer runs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/theater/mcc-theater-looks-forward-to-a-home-of-its-own.html', 'snippet': 'With a new complex of its own being built in Hell’s Kitchen, MCC Theater expects to offer more productions and longer runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the greatest frustrations for Off Broadway producers is having a popular show with money-making potential, only to end its run because their theater has another booking. Such was the predicament of the MCC Theater company in recent years with the plays “Grace” and “The Pride,” at its rental, the Lucille Lortel Theater in Greenwich Village.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/JP-MCC/JP-MCC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/JP-MCC/JP-MCC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60