ent Thelonious Monk International Jazz Piano Competition in September. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/SUB-BOWERS/SUB-BOWERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/SUB-BOWERS/SUB-BOWERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/SUB-BOWERS/SUB-BOWERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Pianist, Holding Listeners Close', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Young Pianist, Holding Listeners Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bon Iver', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T00:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ebbbd9f-c9bf-5ac5-8937-c08aa7246b73', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ebbbd9f-c9bf-5ac5-8937-c08aa7246b73'}, {'abstract': 'The Barnard Project is showcasing the stylistically diverse works of its four choreographers and student dancers at New York Live Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/arts/dance/the-barnard-project-at-new-york-live-arts-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Barnard Project is showcasing the stylistically diverse works of its four choreographers and student dancers at New York Live Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The name of the partnering theater may have changed to New York Live Arts from Dance Theater Workshop, but the rest of the Barnard Project remains the same. Dance students from Barnard College and Columbia University get to work with experienced choreographers for a semester. The choreographers get rehearsal space and their pick of dancers. Audiences get a crapshoot. (But don’t they always?)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/BARNARD/BARNARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rearranging a Few Limbs When Not Shaking Bodies', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rearranging a Few Limbs When Not Shaking Bodies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnard College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rethorst, Susan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T00:27:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d8f9c17-8b91-5cf8-aae6-4ad2c5a451e1', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d8f9c17-8b91-5cf8-aae6-4ad2c5a451e1'}, {'abstract': 'Long Island’s best sparkling wines compare favorably with many of their counterparts from California and France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/nyregion/tiny-bubbles-in-big-vintages.html', 'snippet': 'Long Island’s best sparkling wines compare favorably with many of their counterparts from California and France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Long Island’s sparkling wines have become increasingly sophisticated, their prices have steadily risen. Still, the region’s best compare favorably with many of their counterparts from California and France.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Bubbles in Big Vintages', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiny Bubbles in Big Vintages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bedell Cellars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T00:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f864a317-75c6-5da6-a0ad-5b87f753b5ac', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f864a317-75c6-5da6-a0ad-5b87f753b5ac'}, {'abstract': 'Roberto Herrera, the executive chef at Bryant & Cooper, has opened La Casa Latina, where his mother and a brother also work in the kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/nyregion/la-casa-latina-in-westbury-ny-review.html', 'snippet': 'Roberto Herrera, the executive chef at Bryant & Cooper, has opened La Casa Latina, where his mother and a 