g-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miller Takes Risks, and This Time They Pay Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;Terribly Risky&#8217; but Also a Victory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Skiing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Bode', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beaver Creek (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Ski Federation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T01:04:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Skiing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Mutrie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutrie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23015ced-5304-57b6-8898-c3a61f2c122c', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23015ced-5304-57b6-8898-c3a61f2c122c'}, {'abstract': 'At Yale, Johan Zoffany, an 18th-century painter known for pleasant portraits, is realigned with the larger events and movements of his day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/nyregion/at-yale-redefining-an-observer-of-the-british-colonial-empire.html', 'snippet': 'At Yale, Johan Zoffany, an 18th-century painter known for pleasant portraits, is realigned with the larger events and movements of his day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the same way the first sentence of a story sets the tone for a work of literature, paintings hung at the entrance to an exhibition offer crucial clues. The first five canvases on view at “Johan Zoffany, RA: Society Observed” at the Yale Center for British Art take as their subject classical myth, portraiture, colonialism and the French Revolution. This is not a random selection: The curators are being up-front, literally, about realigning Zoffany, a painter known for pleasant portraits and conversation pieces, with the larger events and movements of his day. “Adapting the Eye: An Archive of the British in India, 1770-1830,” a companion exhibition, follows a similar pattern, with a group portrait leading us into an archive of objects and images made during the colonial era.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSCT2/04ARTSCT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Redefining an Observer of a Burgeoning Empire', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redefining an Observer of a Burgeoning Empire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale Center for British Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zoffany, Johan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T01:16:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1780ab43-86e7-552c-b69c-f9a1adb3c67b', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1780ab43-86e7-552c-b69c-f9a1adb3c67b'}, {'abstract': 'Another inadequate jobs report.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/meh-and-i-say-that-with-feeling/', 'snippet': 'Another inadequate jobs report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A belated reaction to today’s employment report (I’ve been closeted in a room with a bunch of men in suits, myself included, talking about the depressed and depressing world.) In a word: meh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meh. And I Say That With Feeling', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T01:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08f3357d-70fa-516e-83b0-8ac5769552a0', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08f3357d-70fa-516e-83b0-8ac5769552a0'}, {'abstract': 'A further look back at the Great Ivy League Nude Photo Scandal, with reader responses.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/02/last-nude-column-for-now-at-least/', 'snippet': 'A further look back at the Great Ivy League Nude Photo Scandal, with reader responses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hey, thanks for the well-considered, enthusiastic, thoughtful, skillfully written responses to last time’s “Posture Pictures” column. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Nude Column (for Now, at Least)', 'kicker': 'Dick Cavett', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T01:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dick Cavett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b3ae902-76c4-5808-8f68-9af73d10d7b2', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b3ae902-76c4-5808-8f68-9af73d10d7b2'}, {'abstract': 'At 28, Brandon Weeden has been a source of stability for No. 3-ranked Oklahoma State, whose game Saturday against No. 13 Oklahoma is for stakes beyond bragging rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/sports/ncaafootball/at-28-weedens-leadership-has-kept-oklahoma-state-clicking.html', 'snippet': 'At 28, Brandon Weeden has been a source of stability for No. 3-ranked Oklahoma State, whose game Saturday against No. 13 Oklahoma is for stakes beyond bragging rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STILLWATER, Okla. — Invoking the image of Brandon Weeden, perhaps in a robe and fuzzy slippers, shuffling down his driveway seemed a strange way to punctuate a pep talk. Yet as Oklahoma State Coach Mike Gundy gauged his team’s psyche after its upset loss to Iowa State, he knew he could rely on Weeden, his senior quarterback, for some much-needed levity.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/sports/sub-weede