reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a184ba9-c0b7-5e29-9b60-8ee574fcb7dd', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a184ba9-c0b7-5e29-9b60-8ee574fcb7dd'}, {'abstract': 'State officials said Friday that they would begin examining Detroit’s finances, a first step in what might ultimately put the state’s largest city under the control of an appointed outside manager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/us/michigan-state-to-study-detroits-finances.html', 'snippet': 'State officials said Friday that they would begin examining Detroit’s finances, a first step in what might ultimately put the state’s largest city under the control of an appointed outside manager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State officials said Friday that they would begin examining Detroit’s finances, a first step in what might put Michigan’s largest city under the control of an outside manager. “While we have long hoped the mayor and City Council would agree on a viable recovery plan, given the mayor’s description of the city’s financial condition and the prospect the city may run out of cash in mere months, it has become clear that a preliminary financial review is not only warranted but necessary,” said Andy Dillon, the state treasurer. The review, which is to start next week, will go on even as Detroit officials try to agree on cuts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: State to Study Detroit’s Finances', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: State To Study Detroit&#8217;s Finances ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations'