es', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Been Down So Long ...', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Been Down So Long ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T01:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/07fa6fff-b13a-564c-94ec-1aa8e8207f8f', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07fa6fff-b13a-564c-94ec-1aa8e8207f8f'}, {'abstract': 'New York State lawmakers have a lot of unfinished business that needs to be done right now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/opinion/while-albany-vacations.html', 'snippet': 'New York State lawmakers have a lot of unfinished business that needs to be done right now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo of New York says he wants to call the Legislature back before the end of the year to deal with a $350 million shortfall in the 2011 budget. That isn’t all that lawmakers left hanging when they raced out of Albany in June. Here are a few matters that can’t wait until the next session starts, likely in mid-January: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'While Albany Vacations', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Albany Vacations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo,