, through Dec. 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman in the middle of Row D, looking up from her program, waved to her friend about 10 seats away. “Judy Garland’s daughter!” she called out. Her friend nodded in appreciation.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/nyregion/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN/04ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Much Like the One You Used to Know', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Much Like the One You Used to Know', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paice, Jill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Millburn (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paper Mill Playhouse', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlin, Irving', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/042f7e4e-0cd6-572c-a030-eaec8fe7e088', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042f7e4e-0cd6-572c-a030-eaec8fe7e088'}, {'abstract': 'Guidelines from the Obama administration focus on the wiggle room in court rulings on affirmative action, suggesting the use of admissions criteria that are often proxies for race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/education/us-urges-campus-creativity-to-gain-diversity.html', 'snippet': 'Guidelines from the Obama administration focus on the wiggle room in court rulings on affirmative action, suggesting the use of admissions criteria that are often proxies for race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration on Friday urged colleges and universities to get creative in improving racial diversity at their campuses, throwing out a Bush-era interpretation of recent Supreme Court rulings that limited affirmative action in admissions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Urges Creativity by Colleges to Gain Diversity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Urges Campus Creativity to Gain Diversity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'R