 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Royal Bank of Scotland Sells Pub Chain to Heineken', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Royal Bank of Scotland Sells Pub Chain To Heineken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heineken NV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galaxy Pub Estate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/77d8705a-55ac-55a4-80e0-e20c11481710', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77d8705a-55ac-55a4-80e0-e20c11481710'}, {'abstract': 'A week after a NATO raid on two Pakistani outposts, American and Pakistani officials are offering competing narratives of what went wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/world/asia/pakistan-refuses-to-help-as-us-sorts-out-fatal-airstrikes.html', 'snippet': 'A week after a NATO raid on two Pakistani outposts, American and Pakistani officials are offering competing narratives of what went wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The American airstrikes that killed two dozen Pakistani soldiers last week were called in during a skirmish in which both sides thought they were under attack by the Taliban, American officials said Friday. But efforts to sort out precisely what happened — and in the process ease the latest crisis to strain the tenuous alliance between the United States and Pakistan — are being hindered by Pakistan’s refusal to cooperate with the American-led military investigation into the attack, the officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03RAID1/03RAID1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03RAID1/03RAID1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03RAID1/03RAID1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03RAID1/03RAID1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03RAID1/03RAID1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan Refuses to Help as U.S. Sorts Out a Fatal Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan Refuses to Help as U.S. Sorts Out a Fatal Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kayani, Ashfaq Parvez', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:11:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b37a2e2-7fc6-595b-ad9b-2633bf259840', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b37a2e2-7fc6-595b-ad9b-2633bf259840'}, {'abstract': 'The Western Digital Corporation raised its quarterly revenue forecast, citing its recovery from flooding in Thailand, setting off a 7 percent gain in its share price Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/business/western-digitals-stock-surges-on-flood-recovery.html', 'snippet': 'The Western Digital Corporation raised its quarterly revenue forecast, citing its recovery from flooding in Thailand, setting off a 7 percent gain in its share price Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Western Digital Corporation, a maker of disk drives and networking products, raised its quarterly revenue forecast, citing its recovery from flooding in Thailand, setting off a 7 percent gain in its share price Friday. Western Digital said after the close of trading on Thursday that revenue in the current quarter would be at least $1.8 billion, above the $1.05 billion to $1.25 billion it forecast in October after flooding in Thailand had devastated factories. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Western Digital’s Stock Surges on Flood Recovery', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Western Digital’s Stock Surges On Flood Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Western Digital Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a1ece7f-0961-5237-946a-8b1f209f124c', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a1ece7f-0961-5237-946a-8b1f209f124c'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department turned over nearly 1,400 pages of internal communications to show that it did not knowingly mislead Congress about Operation Fast and Furious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/us/politics/us-offers-defense-in-operation-fast-and-furious.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department turned over nearly 1,400 pages of internal communications to show that it did not knowingly mislead Congress about Operation Fast and Furious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department on Friday turned over to Congress nearly 1,400 pages of “highly deliberative internal communications” about the drafting of a February letter in an effort to show that agency officials did not knowingly mislead lawmakers in connection with a disputed gun trafficking investigation called Operation Fast and Furious.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Department Counters Claim That It Misled Congress in Gun Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Present Defense In Border Gun Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breuer, Lanny A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grassley, Charles E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e5eb3b5-9a7d-5fff-b0bb-df832ca9abfd', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e5eb3b5-9a7d-5fff-b0bb-df832ca9abfd'}, {'abstract': 'A British spy agency is looking for recruits in a group suspicious of government: hackers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/world/europe/britains-gchq-uses-online-puzzle-to-recruit-hackers.html', 'snippet': 'A British spy agency is looking for recruits in a group suspicious of government: hackers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Psst! Wanna be a spy?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03HACKERS/03HACKERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03HACKERS/03HACKERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03HACKERS/03HACKERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03HACKERS/03HACKERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/world/03HACKERS/03HACKERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Go Online, Beat a Puzzle and Become a British Spy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Go Online, Beat a Puzzle, And Become A British Spy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Codes (Ciphers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cryptography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T02:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e427cb2-fc3a-5cd0-a2a3-12e9da593190', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e427cb2-fc3a-5cd0-a2a3-12e9da593190'}, {'abstract': 'Sundays are work days for Kent Tritle, who is arguably the busiest choirmaster in the city, with varied jobs at St. John the Divine and the New York Philharmonic, as well as other institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/nyregion/kent-tritle-a-choirmaster-who-serves-many-masters.html', 'snippet': 'Sundays are work days for Kent Tritle, who is arguably the busiest choirmaster in the city, with varied jobs at St. John the Divine and the New York Philharmonic, as well as other institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sundays are always work days for  Kent Tritle, arguably the busiest choirmaster in the city, but his commitments hit a crescendo from Thanksgiving to Christmas. Mr. Tritle, 51, is in his first season as music director and organist at the Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine, which has its annual “Cathedral Christmas” concert on Saturday. He is also music director of Musica Sacra and the Oratorio Society of New York and organist for the New York Philharmonic, and has a Sunday program, “The Choral Mix With Kent Tritle,” on WQXR-FM. He lives on the Cathedral Close with his partner, Arthur Fiacco, 56, a cellist; two cats; and a Moluccan cockatoo, Precious. The couple also have a 1906 cottage in Cragsmoor, in the Catskills.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/n