anor and a chilly heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alice Hauptmann is one of those commanding, complacent women who draw you close to make sure you keep your distance. Her surface warmth is so great that, even though you should know better, it’s a shock when you become aware of a core of ice within her that leaves you frostbitten. She’s supremely charming company and she’s scary as hell. It is probably a blessing that they don’t make them like her anymore.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/03ELECTIVE/03ELECTIVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/03ELECTIVE/03ELECTIVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/03/arts/03ELECTIVE/03ELECTIVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Privilege and Poison on the Upper East Side', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Elective Affinities'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privilege and Poison On the Upper East Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caldwell, Zoe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soho Rep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adjmi, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Sarah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T03:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname':