this, saying it is a better model of how the world really works. Business, not government, might create our future societies.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/how-the-internet-is-destroying-everything/', 'snippet': 'One of the authors of “The Cluetrain Manifesto” says the hyperlinked structure of the Internet has destroyed several millennia of Western thought and aspiration. He likes this, saying it is a better model of how the world really works. Business, n...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ongoing argument about whether the Internet is a boon or a bust to civilization usually centers on the Web’s abundance. With so much data and so many voices, we each have knowledge formerly hard-won by decades of specialization. With some new fact or temptation perpetually beckoning, we may be the superficial avatars of an A.D.D. culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Internet Is Ruining Everything', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinberger, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T14:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22496cc6-1731-57f6-a0e1-228da33294ed', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22496cc6-1731-57f6-a0e1-228da33294ed'}, {'abstract': 'Barbecue on the grill and a blues band plays, while Herman Cain decides on his next move.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/in-atlanta-waiting-for-herman-cains-decision/', 'snippet': 'Barbecue on the grill and a blues band plays, while Herman Cain decides on his next move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA – Barbecue is on a grill and a blues band is tuning up to play songs about Herman Cain outside of a large stucco building that used to be a display room for selling floor tiles on the north side of town here. If this is the way a presidential campaign ends, it is certainly a new chapter in the annals of politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Atlanta,  Waiting for Herman Cain’s Decision', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T15:36:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown and Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/935f75d2-f08e-5e82-b446-a9b8b0cb71d2', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/935f75d2-f08e-5e82-b446-a9b8b0cb71d2'}, {'abstract': 'Fox and the bankrupt Dodgers are locked in a rip-roaring lawsuit over a lucrative television contract.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/sports/baseball/bankrupt-dodgers-will-benefit-from-robust-tv-marketplace.html', 'snippet': 'Fox and the bankrupt Dodgers are locked in a rip-roaring lawsuit over a lucrative television contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Los Angeles Dodgers signed their local cable television contract in 2001 with the network now called Prime Ticket, the team could not predict how the business would change in the succeeding years or how the payments would end up being more appropriate for a middle-market baseball franchise.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/sports/04dodgers-GFX/04dodgers-GFX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 191, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bankrupt Dodgers Will Benefit From Robust TV Marketplace', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Either Now or Later, Bankrupt Dodgers Will Benefit From Robust TV Marketplace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank H Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T15:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7e4aabe-a6c0-5726-9e07-0f846ef85e64', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7e4aabe-a6c0-5726-9e07-0f846ef85e64'}, {'abstract': 'A satisfying end-of-the-night meal comes out of the pantry.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/spaghetti-at-midnight-2/', 'snippet': 'A satisfying end-of-the-night meal comes out of the pantry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You went to a holiday party but realize you didn’t actually get much to eat. Or after having Christmas cookies for lunch you went to a play and you’re starving, but none of the post-theater options really appeal. Solution: go home and make a fine bowl of pasta. Everything you need is in your pantry—pasta, olives, capers, garlic, anchovy, hot pepper, olive oil. So much better than take-out or a slice of so-so pizza, and ready in minutes. See how in this week’s City Kitchen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spaghetti at Midnight', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T15:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ddbee9c-82b2-585c-a5ef-cd249181ff63', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ddbee9c-82b2-585c-a5ef-cd249181ff63'}, {'abstract': 'Coaches and players describe Kevin O’Connell as a pseudocoach, sticking close to Mark Sanchez during games and consulting with Coach Rex Ryan’s assistants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/sports/football/kevin-oconnell-third-string-quarterback-aids-jets-on-sideline.html', 'snippet': 'Coaches and players describe Kevin O’Connell as a pseudocoach, sticking close to Mark Sanchez during games and consulting with Coach Rex Ryan’s assistants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — Jets quarterback Mark Sanchez cannot throw a touchdown pass or an interception, visit a nightclub, pose for a magazine or even snack on a hot dog without seeming to stir th