ve Dan Boren’s campaign contributions from the growing oil and gas industry in his state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Dan Boren’s campaign contributions from the growing oil and gas industry in his state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Representative Dan Boren’s Natural Gas Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T19:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/db585142-cebf-5fb4-be8d-71811d0116d2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/db585142-cebf-5fb4-be8d-71811d0116d2'}, {'abstract': 'Debt deflation deja vu.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/irving-fisher-rules/', 'snippet': 'Debt deflation deja vu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adair Turner and I were in a competition over who could praise Irving Fisher’s classic debt-deflation analysis (pdf) more. It’s truly astonishing how relevant it is to current conditions — and how thoroughly conventional wisdom seems determined to ignore its lessons for policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irving Fisher Rules', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T19:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/492656ef-112f-5011-a932-9a127b113189', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/492656ef-112f-5011-a932-9a127b113189'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Donald M. Berwick, in charge of Medicare and Medicaid for the last 17 months, said that 20 percent to 30 percent of health spending is “waste” that yields no benefit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/health/policy/parting-shot-at-waste-by-key-obama-health-official.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Donald M. Berwick, in charge of Medicare and Medicaid for the last 17 months, said that 20 percent to 30 percent of health spending is “waste” that yields no benefit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The official in charge of Medicare and Medicaid for the last 17 months says that 20 percent to 30 percent of health spending is “waste” that yields no benefit to patients, and that some of the needless spending is a result of onerous, archaic regulations enforced by his agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/us/BERWICK/BERWICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/us/BERWICK/BERWICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/us/BERWICK/BERWICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Official Takes Parting Shot at ‘Waste’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Official Takes Parting Shot at ‘Waste’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berwick, Donald M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T19:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c516096-5ed8-520e-b88b-a7b275df0be9', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c516096-5ed8-520e-b88b-a7b275df0be9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gingrich’s  decision to take part in the debate puts pressure on the other candidates to decide whether they will participate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/03/gingrich-accepts-invite-to-debate-moderated-by-trump/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gingrich’s  decision to take part in the debate puts pressure on the other candidates to decide whether they will participate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Herman Cain‘s tumultuous and troubled quest for the presidency seemingly over, the 2012 Republican primary campaign can move on to its next distraction: Donald Trump as a debate moderator. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Accepts Invite to Debate Moderated by Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Electi