ndreds of millions of dollars in profits. At a time of fiscal austerity, these companies are seducing school administrators with promises to cut costs through privatization. Parents who want healthier meals, meanwhile, are outgunned.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Food Industry Eats Your Kid’s Lunch', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Food Industry Eats Your Kid’s Lunch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunch and Breakfast Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson, Robert Wood, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ConAgra Foods Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sodexo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAMARK', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zullo, Roland', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By LUCY KOMISAR', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KOMISAR', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/68db3b1a-9b25-53a6-8ba4-51f9bd7f0292', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68db3b1a-9b25-53a6-8ba4-51f9bd7f0292'}, {'abstract': 'When the police look military: The Occupy movement brings out the martial character of law enforcement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/sunday-review/have-american-police-become-militarized.html', 'snippet': 'When the police look military: The Occupy movement brings out the martial character of law enforcement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIOT police officers tear-gassing protesters at the Occupy movement in Oakland, Calif. The surprising nighttime invasion of Zuccotti Park in Lower Manhattan, carried out with D-Day-like secrecy by officers deploying klieg lights and a military-style sound machine. And campus police officers in helmets and face shields dousing demonstrators at the University of California, Davis with pepper spray.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Police Go Military', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Police Go Military', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/ceda70e8-ee6a-5499-bbd7-2011a76b6502', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceda70e8-ee6a-5499-bbd7-2011a76b6502'}, {'abstract': 'The ever-shifting G.O.P. primary campaign challenges news organizations to keep pace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/opinion/sunday/riding-the-republican-roller-coaster.html', 'snippet': 'The ever-shifting G.O.P. primary campaign challenges news organizations to keep pace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHARD STEVENSON, the political editor who has overseen national election coverage for The New York Times since 2006, was explaining why this presidential contest was not the stunted affair I told him I thought it was.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Riding the Republican Roller Coaster', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riding the Republican Roller Coaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a00c28-10d5-55e8-bcbd-4b4ec1df04b6', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a00c28-10d5-55e8-bcbd-4b4ec1df04b6'}, {'abstract': 'Better a protest movement that casts itself (however quixotically) as the defender of “the 99 percent” than one that just represents Democratic interest groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/opinion/sunday/douthat-the-decadent-left.html', 'snippet': 'Better a protest movement that casts itself (however quixotically) as the defender of “the 99 percent” than one that just represents Democratic interest groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the days when Tea Party activists were crowding town hall meetings and Glenn Beck’s fans were thronging the Washington Mall, a kind of existential despair settled over the American left. The country was mired in an economic crisis that most left-wingers believed was caused by the excesses of free-market capitalism, yet the only major protest movement belonged to the political right. What was the left good for, if it couldn’t even persuade people to take to the streets? Why didn’t American liberalism have a Tea Party of its own?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Decadent Left', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Decadent Left', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/63f8424a-a37f-5939-8189-278a3aee0155', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63f8424a-a37f-5939-8189-278a3aee0155'}, {'abstract': 'Most Americans can get online. But too many can’t afford high-speed access.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/opinion/sunday/internet-access-and-the-new-divide.html', 'snippet': 'Most Americans can get online. But too many can’t afford high-speed access.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the second year in a row, the Monday after Thanksgiving — so-called Cyber Monday, when online retailers offer discounts to lure holiday shoppers — was the biggest online sales day of the year, totaling some $1.25 billion and overwhelming the sales figures racked up by brick-and-mortar stores three days before, on Black Friday, the former perennial record-holder.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/sunday-review/04COVER/04COVER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/04/sunday-review/04COVER/04COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/04/sunday-review/04COVER/04COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Digital Divide', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The New Digital Divide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By SUSAN P. CRAWFORD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'CRAWFORD', 'qualifier': None, 'title