Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By STEVE INSKEEP', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'INSKEEP', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e5e85f-4498-5abe-88f9-e3ec6c53c467', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e5e85f-4498-5abe-88f9-e3ec6c53c467'}, {'abstract': 'Technological advances, training innovations and changing attitudes toward the right to assemble have all shaped the way the police handle the challenges of large demonstrations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/opinion/sunday/riot-gears-evolution.html', 'snippet': 'Technological advances, training innovations and changing attitudes toward the right to assemble have all shaped the way the police handle the challenges of large demonstrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as the styles of protest have changed from one generation to the next, so have the styles of protest policing. Technological advances, training innovations and changing attitudes toward the right to assemble have all shaped the way the police handle the challenges of large demonstrations. During the 1960s and ’70s, police officers treated many protests as a threat to the social order and responded with brute force. In the 1980s and ’90s, demonstrations tended to be less confrontational and the police responded with more accommodating tactics. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/opinion/opart-riot/opart-riot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/02/opinion/opart-riot/opart-riot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/opinion/opart-riot/opart-riot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 970, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/opinion/opart-riot/opart-riot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/opinion/opart-riot/opart-riot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Riot Gear’s Evolution', 'kicker': 'Op-Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riot Gear’s Evolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-03T21:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By CHI BIRMINGHAM and ALEX S. VITALE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BIRMINGHAM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'VITALE', 'quali