win the N.C.A.A. Division III national championship. The title was the second for Ohio Wesleyan and its coach, Jay Martin, who earned his 608th career victory in the final. That set a record for the most wins by any coach at any level in college men’s soccer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio Wesleyan Celebrates After a Week When All Seemed Lost', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T09:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/203e9a6c-7c6d-5eb6-ba18-d6acd2e1ba1c', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/203e9a6c-7c6d-5eb6-ba18-d6acd2e1ba1c'}, {'abstract': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/newswallah-long-reads-edition-12/', 'snippet': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ashok Malik of Tehelka  analyzes the costs and benefits of India’s decision to allow foreign retailers to open stores in the country in an even-handed essay. He argues that many of the opponents of the policy change are trying to “scare Indians by raising the bogey of the foreigner.” But he also points out that allowing foreign retailers will likely also put pressure on some domestic businesses and industries. “Every economic initiative is a mixed blessing,” he writes. “Even if it expands the cake, there will still be some losers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR INDIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T10:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4afbf6c-8aa2-54fb-b9f0-af8061c9f296', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4afbf6c-8aa2-54fb-b9f0-af8061c9f296'}, {'abstract': 'From Dec. 9 to 11, the Chocolate Festival, a celebration of all things chocolate, will descend on London’s Southbank Center Square.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/in-london-a-festival-for-chocolate-lovers/', 'snippet': 'From Dec. 9 to 11, the Chocolate Festival, a celebration of all things chocolate, will descend on London’s Southbank Center Square.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lifelong lover of chocolate, Yael Rose is as happy sipping a cup of hot chocolate as she is nibbling sea-salted caramel or cocoa nibs. “To be honest, I think it’s an addiction,” she said. “There’s something about the smell and colors of chocolate I simply can’t resist every single time.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In London, a Festival for Chocolate Lovers', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T11:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Moskowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42c80269-7fa6-589c-af82-33f80678dd56', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42c80269-7fa6-589c-af82-33f80678dd56'}, {'abstract': 'Giants and Jets fans have been booed recently by players.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/is-it-bad-strategy-for-fans-to-boo/', 'snippet': 'Giants and Jets fans have been booed recently by players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a little bit of turnabout, Giants and Jets fans have been booed recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Bad Strategy for Fans to Boo?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T12:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4c16a65-5c28-567f-ae57-96fc457815d1', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4c16a65-5c28-567f-ae57-96fc457815d1'}, {'abstract': 'Franco Bernabè, the chief executive, is giving the once trend-setting mobile operator something to cheer about as it starts to make inroads in new markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/technology/05iht-italia05.html', 'snippet': 'Franco Bernabè, the chief executive, is giving the once trend-setting mobile operator something to cheer about as it starts to make inroads in new markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — In April 2007, as the global economy was beginning to unravel, Telefónica, the Spanish telecommunications company, led a group of Italian investors who bought a 22.4 percent stake in Telecom Italia, one of the pioneering mobile operators in Europe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steering Telecom Italia With a Steady Hand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telecom Italia Mobile Regains Health With Support From a Spanish Phone Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telefonica S.A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telecom Argentina S.A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telefonica Brasil S.A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telecom Italia S.p.A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'France Telecom S.A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T12:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': "By Kevin J. O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': "O'Brien", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fcee5e7-5e17-5c2b-b5d3-f6d3fab5c8a6', 'word_count': 1719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fcee5e7-5e17-5c2b-b5d3-f6d3fab5c8a6'}, {'abstract': 'During a forum on Saturday night, six Republican candidates responded directly to questions by three attorneys general, and did not address one another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/us/politics/gop-hopefuls-pressed-to-prove-their-conservatism.html', 'snippet': 'During a forum on Saturday night, six Republican candidates responded directly to questions by three attorneys general, and did not address one another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Republican field reshaped by the suspension of Herman Cain’s campaign, six Republican presidential candidates tried to show their conservative credentials during a policy-heavy forum shown on Fox News Channel on Saturday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Cain on Sideline, His Rivals Try to Prove Their Conservatism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Cain on Sideline, His Rivals Try to Prove Their Conservatism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T13:04:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg and Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': No