f-good-will-for-us.html', 'snippet': 'A record 82 percent of Japanese report having friendly feelings toward the United States, results attributed to the American military’s humanitarian effort after the March tsunami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A record 82 percent of Japanese report having friendly feelings toward the United States, according to results of an annual government poll released Sunday, in the first such survey taken since the American military’s huge humanitarian effort last spring in Japan’s tsunami-ravaged northeast. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Poll Finds Record Good Will for U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Poll Finds Record Good Will for U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T13:35:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e0ad72d-c1ef-5ce5-90c6-585d69d29e03', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e0ad72d-c1ef-5ce5-90c6-585d69d29e03'}, {'abstract': 'Comments by a Chinese vice minister suggested that Beijing was in no hurry to help European countries finance their budget deficits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/business/global/china-signals-reluctance-to-rescue-eu.html', 'snippet': 'Comments by a Chinese vice minister suggested that Beijing was in no hurry to help European countries finance their budget deficits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Chinese government over the weekend sought to tamp down international expectations that Beijing might use its large financial reserves to help ease the European debt crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Signals Reluctance to Rescue E.U.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Says It’s Unable To Easily Aid Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T13:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4c43484-2e0d-5000-867a-89def7848a02', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4c43484-2e0d-5000-867a-89def7848a02'}, {'abstract': 'Next stop on his protest agenda: Dimock, Pa., where the controversial natural gas drilling process known as fracking is already under way.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/to-the-battlements-mark-ruffalo/', 'snippet': 'Next stop on his protest agenda: Dimock, Pa., where the controversial natural gas drilling process known as fracking is already under way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major environmental groups are lobbying for strict regulations on natural gas drilling in New York State, which could begin as early as next year. But activists like the actor Mark Ruffalo are seeking an all-out drilling ban, arguing that the country should move quickly toward reliance on renewable energy sources rather than reinforce dependence on a fossil fuel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To the Battlements, Mark Ruffalo', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T15:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2fec272-cc2d-5165-89f3-a09f3900fdc4', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2fec272-cc2d-5165-89f3-a09f3900fdc4'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti of Italy took the steps in an emergency decree, which means they will take effect before Parliament gives its formal approval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/world/europe/mario-monti-of-italy-calls-cabinet-to-consider-austerity-measures.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti of Italy took the steps in an emergency decree, which means they will take effect before Parliament gives its formal approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Telling Italians that the fate of their country and the euro was at stake, Prime Minister Mario Monti unveiled a radical and ambitious package of spending cuts and tax increases on Sunday, including deeply unpopular moves like raising the country’s retirement age. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/06italy_cnd/06italy_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/06italy_cnd/06italy_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/06italy_cnd/06italy_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/06italy_cnd/06italy_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/06italy_cnd/06italy_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy’s Leader Unveils Radical Austerity Measures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy’s Prime Minister Announces Austerity Measures in an Emergency Decree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'na