', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/hockey/05boogaard-sfpic/05boogaard-sfpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/hockey/05boogaard-sfpic/05boogaard-sfpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/hockey/05boogaard-sfpic/05boogaard-sfpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Derek Boogaard: Blood on the Ice', 'kicker': 'Punched Out', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blood on the Ice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fedoruk, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boogaard, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laraque, Georges', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Wild', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:09:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba4fd7f-3291-5f6d-b1a6-ea8929384bef', 'word_count': 4975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba4fd7f-3291-5f6d-b1a6-ea8929384bef'}, {'abstract': 'Performers and other protesters, gather in the theater district for Occupy Broadway, and the Public Theater announces a reprise of Mike Daisey’s new show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/theater/footnotes.html', 'snippet': 'Performers and other protesters, gather in the theater district for Occupy Broadway, and the Public Theater announces a reprise of Mike Daisey’s new show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performers and other protesters, above, gathered in the theater district from Friday night to Saturday for Occupy Broadway, called by the organizers a 24-hour “creative resistance” action to promote the right to assemble in privately owned public spaces. Zuccotti Park in Lower Manhattan, the scene of Occupy Wall Street, is also such a space. ... The Public Theater has announced a five-week reprise of “The Agony and the Ecstasy of Steve Jobs,” Mike Daisey’s exploration of Apple and Mr. Jobs, who died in October. The second round is to run from Jan. 31 to March 4.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/theater/05broadway/05broadway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnotes', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnotes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daisey, Mike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:11:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d875302-b19c-586a-a9e9-7f3910478a44', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d875302-b19c-586a-a9e9-7f3910478a44'}, {'abstract': '“The Heist Project,” a one-woman show created by the dancer Belinda McGuire, was presented at the Joyce SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/arts/dance/heist-project-by-belinda-mcguire-at-joyce-soho-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Heist Project,” a one-woman show created by the dancer Belinda McGuire, was presented at the Joyce SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The suggestion behind “The Heist Project,” a one-woman show created by the dancer Belinda McGuire, is that it shares something in common with a jewel heist. Alas, the choreography on display at the Joyce SoHo on Thursday night — three solos in total— is hardly tempting swag. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/mcguire/mcguire-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/mcguire/mcguire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/mcguire/mcguire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Woman, Three Works', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Woman, Three Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e2657cf-2e6b-5700-a374-d0ddf9b119cc', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e2657cf-2e6b-5700-a374-d0ddf9b119cc'}, {'abstract': 'The Portuguese fado star Camané made his United States debut at the Brooklyn Academy of Music as part of the Next Wave Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/arts/music/camane-sings-fado-at-bam-in-next-wave-festival-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Portuguese fado star Camané made his United States debut at the Brooklyn Academy of Music as part of the Next Wave Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fado, the Portuguese tradition of elegant, emotive songs filled with tragedy and longing, was named to Unesco’s Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list in late November. By happy coincidence the Next Wave Festival at the Brooklyn Academy of Music had scheduled two nights of fado that began Friday with a concert featuring the United States debut of Camané, 44, a major star in Portugal who is one of his generation’s leading fado singers, or fadistas. At this concert fado’s past was never far from its present.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/fado/fado-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':