es.html', 'snippet': 'Chief executives at 36 private colleges earned more than $1 million in 2009, as the median compensation rose to $385,900, according to The Chronicle of Higher Education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Presidents at 36 private colleges earned more than $1 million in 2009, up from 33 the previous year, according to a study by The Chronicle of Higher Education. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private-College Presidents Getting Higher Salaries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private-College Presidents Getting Higher Salaries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chronicle of Higher Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a67a40b0-bda2-5779-a429-25db744e9cc5', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a67a40b0-bda2-5779-a429-25db744e9cc5'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Battle, in his first season as artistic director of Alvin Ailey Dance Theater, is moving into slightly more adventurous territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/arts/dance/alvin-ailey-american-dance-theater-at-city-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Battle, in his first season as artistic director of Alvin Ailey Dance Theater, is moving into slightly more adventurous territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At City Center this month Robert Battle, the new artistic director of Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater, is introducing himself to Ailey audiences. And for at least the first three evenings of the season he has done so in person, speaking from the stage. Amiable and welcoming, he has that part of the job down. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/alvin/alvin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/alvin/alvin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/arts/alvin/alvin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Couples Loving and Fighting Between Multiple Pirouettes', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Couples Loving and Fighting Between Multiple Pirouettes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Rennie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battle, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d80d3ed1-3234-56ae-a92b-6c123aaef704', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d80d3ed1-3234-56ae-a92b-6c123aaef704'}, {'abstract': 'The European Film Awards, voted on by 2,500 members of the European Film Academy, offered its year-end prizes on Saturday in Berlin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/movies/melancholia-picks-up-european-film-awards.html', 'snippet': 'The European Film Awards, voted on by 2,500 members of the European Film Academy, offered its year-end prizes on Saturday in Berlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Film Awards, voted on by 2,500 members of the European Film Academy, offered its year-end prizes on Saturday in Berlin. “Melancholia,” starring Kirsten Dunst, below, from the Danish director Lars von Trier, was named best picture; it also won awards for cinematography and production design. Last year’s big Oscar winner, “The King’s Speech,” which was released in Europe in 2011, earned another best-actor prize for its star Colin Firth; Tilda Swinton took home best actress for playing the mother of a son who goes on a Columbine-style rampage in “We Need to Talk About Kevin.” Susanne Bier won best director for “In a Better World,” which also won best foreign film at the Oscars last year. “Pina,” Wim Wenders’s 3-D take on the choreographer Pina Bausch, won best documentary. Mr. von Trier sent his wife, Bente Froge, to accept the award on his behalf. Ms. Froge said that Mr. von Trier had taken a vow of silence after he made comments sympathizing with Nazis at the Cannes Film Festival. “I should say from Lars that he has no statement for you,” Ms. Froge said, according to The Guardian of London. “But he did ask that I should wave to you in a kind and gentle way.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Melancholia’ Picks Up European Film Awards', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Melancholia’ Picks Up European Film Awards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Film Academy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunst, Kirsten', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Trier, Lars', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-04T23:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/663aed95-5430-535e-82d0-f5da06f0a90b', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/663aed95-5430-535e-82d0-f5da06f0a90b'}, {'abstract': 'John Branch of The New York Times and Todd Fedoruk, a former N.H.L. enforcer, will answer selected questions from readers on Monday about the life of a hockey tough guy and the series, “Punched Out, The Life and Death of a Hockey Enforcer.”', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/fedoruk-and-branch-to-answer-readers-questions/', 'snippet': 'John Branch of The New York Times and Todd Fedoruk, a former N.H.L. enforcer, will answer selected questions from readers on Monday about the life of a hockey tough guy and the series, “Punched Out, The Life and Death of a Hockey Enforcer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Answers can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fedoruk to Answer Readers’ Questions', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': N