ame on both sides of the line, will meet again on Jan. 9 in New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College football’s quarterback-centric offenses, with their multiple formations and 30-plus passes a game, were dropped out of a second-story window Sunday. They landed with a thud, and will have nothing to do with deciding the national championship.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/colleges/colleges-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/colleges/colleges-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/colleges/colleges-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekly Grind Pays Off in a Rematch for the Title', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weekly Grind Pays Off in Rematch for National Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T01:45:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ae8d25b-6fcc-5d39-b15a-3d468ba634e5', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ae8d25b-6fcc-5d39-b15a-3d468ba634e5'}, {'abstract': 'Three days after the city’s latest audacious animal getaway was reported, it appears that New Yorkers have greeted the escape of an eastern box turtle with a collective shrug.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/nyregion/another-animal-escapes-but-this-time-city-shrugs.html', 'snippet': 'Three days after the city’s latest audacious animal getaway was reported, it appears that New Yorkers have greeted the escape of an eastern box turtle with a collective shrug.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They swooned over the Egyptian cobra, gone rogue inside the Bronx Zoo’s Reptile House last March. They cheered the peacock from the Central Park Zoo, who crossed Fifth Avenue to spend an August day on the ledge of an Upper East Side apartment building, only to return, on his own, the following morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/TURTLE/TURTLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/TURTLE/TURTLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/TURTLE/TURTLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/TURTLE/TURTLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su