6:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dc29243-a1f7-5449-a313-87085e10808f', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dc29243-a1f7-5449-a313-87085e10808f'}, {'abstract': 'The Cardinal held on for a 1-0 victory after losing in the final the past two years by the same score.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/sports/soccer/stanford-edges-duke-to-win-its-first-womens-soccer-title.html', 'snippet': 'The Cardinal held on for a 1-0 victory after losing in the final the past two years by the same score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KENNESAW, Ga. — Avenging consecutive 1-0 losses in the N.C.A.A. tournament final, Stanford held on to beat Duke by that same score on Sunday to win its first national title in women’s soccer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05soccer-1/05soccer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05soccer-1/05soccer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05soccer-1/05soccer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanford Edges Duke to Win Its First Women’s Soccer Title', 'kicker': 'Stanford 1, Duke 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stanford Edges Duke to Win Its First Women’s Soccer Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Soccer Championships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T03:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68477211-5b6e-5d97-9bda-3d388149fa71', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68477211-5b6e-5d97-9bda-3d388149fa71'}, {'abstract': 'Summonses ranging from $250 to $1,000 have been issued to those soliciting donations within 50 feet of a monument in the past two months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/nyregion/city-cracks-down-on-washington-square-park-performers.html', 'snippet': 'Summonses ranging from $250 to $1,000 have been issued to those soliciting donations within 50 feet of a monument in the past two months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Colin Huggins was there with his baby grand, the one he wheels into Washington Square Park for his al fresco concerts. So were Tic and Tac, a street-performing duo, who held court in the fountain — dry for the winter. And Joe Mangrum was pouring his elaborate sand paintings on the ground near the Washington Arch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Cracking Down on Performers in Washington Square Park', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Cracking Down on Performers in Washington Square Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T03:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17b3d0ce-217b-55d5-93a1-04e74d8553ff', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17b3d0ce-217b-55d5-93a1-04e74d8553ff'}, {'abstract': 'If neither Newt Gingrich nor Mitt Romney locks up the nomination early, Mr. Gingrich might need to survive a war of attrition of the sort for which he is unprepared at the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/us/politics/gingrich-surges-but-romney-organization-is-stronger.html', 'snippet': 'If neither Newt Gingrich nor Mitt Romney locks up the nomination early, Mr. Gingrich might need to survive a war of attrition of the sort for which he is unprepared at the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Surging in polls is one thing. But as Newt Gingrich seeks to turn his impressive performance in surveys into votes, he is scrambling madly to build the kind of organization that Mitt Romney has methodically put in place for a year, one that will let him compete through all 50 contests, often in multiple states at once. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/us/JP-REPUBS-2/JP-REPUBS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/us/JP-REPUBS-2/JP-REPUBS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/us/JP-REPUBS-2/JP-REPUBS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Surge, Gingrich Faces Major Hurdles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Surge, Gingrich Faces Major Hurdles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value'