k.html', 'snippet': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include the ISM nonmanufacturing index for November and factory orders for October (Monday); consumer credit for October (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims and wholesale trade inventories for October (Thursday); the trade deficit for October and the Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for December (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/business/05Ahead/05Ahead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T03:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a904e2a-d43a-5173-b625-1fa8a5b179ab', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a904e2a-d43a-5173-b625-1fa8a5b179ab'}, {'abstract': 'Clayton Spencer served at Harvard for 14 years in various capacities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/education/clayton-spencer-harvard-vice-president-to-lead-bates-college.html', 'snippet': 'Clayton Spencer served at Harvard for 14 years in various capacities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clayton Spencer, the vice president for policy at Harvard University, has been named the eighth president of Bates College, a small liberal arts institution in Lewiston, Me., effective July 1. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/us/BATES/BATES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/us/BATES/BATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/us/BATES/BATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vice President of Harvard Will Lead Bates College', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vice President Of Harvard Will Lead Bates College', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bates College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T03:17:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc767bed-e961-5114-af27-3a5ae356e691', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc767bed-e961-5114-af27-3a5ae356e691'}, {'abstract': 'After getting C. C. Sabathia to agree to an extension, the Yankees are in no hurry to spend lots of money on signing — or trading for — other arms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/sports/baseball/yankees-interest-in-free-agent-pitchers-is-not-high.html', 'snippet': 'After getting C. C. Sabathia to agree to an extension, the Yankees are in no hurry to spend lots of money on signing — or trading for — other arms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — As baseball executives began to assemble Sunday at the Hilton Anatole for the annual winter meetings, the man with the biggest checkbook in the sport and with a long history of bold off-season transactions was not among the early arrivals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Interest in Free-Agent Pitchers Is Not High', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees’ Interest in Free-Agent Pitchers Is Not High', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T03:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2fad8d6-8d37-5815-93c1-3bd2ed87ef3e', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2fad8d6-8d37-5815-93c1-3bd2ed87ef3e'}, {'abstract': 'For decades, television and radio outlets in New York have put complaints in “public files,” a little-known but rich trove that each must maintain and make available for public viewing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/nyregion/at-radio-and-tv-outlets-a-little-known-trove-of-kudos-and-complaints.html', 'snippet': 'For decades, television and radio outlets in New York have put complaints in “public files,” a little-known but rich trove that each must maintain and make available for public viewing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angered by the tendency of Judith Sheindlin, the television jurist Judge Judy, to address young women as “babies,” an elderly man wrote to WCBS-TV (Channel 2) in protest, proclaiming that it was “Balderdash!” and proceeding, in neat cursive script, to chronicle his marriage, and the war service he rendered, when he was just 21. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/PUBLIC1/PUBLIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/PUBLIC1/PUBLIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/nyregion/PUBLIC1/PUBLIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At TV and Radio Outlets, Little-Known Trove of Kudos and Complaints', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At TV and Radio Outlets, Little-Known, Rich Trove Of Kudos and Complaints', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emmis Communications Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, 