s and work with their hands.  It all starts with a school trip and ends with "pick up."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/04/how-to-use-blocks-to-teach/', 'snippet': 'With building blocks making a comeback, an educator provides some tips for using blocks in the classroom to deepen the understanding of concepts and topics, and provide a time for children to explore, make choices and work with their hands.  It al...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Use Blocks to Teach', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T04:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANGELA DE VINCENZO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DE VINCENZO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51b9bb96-9808-53c8-9e4a-591e482de871', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b9bb96-9808-53c8-9e4a-591e482de871'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of baseball’s winter meetings in Dallas, the Miami Marlins and Reyes agreed to a six-year contract worth $106 million, according to a person with direct knowledge of the agreement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/sports/baseball/reyes-a-longtime-met-is-set-to-leave-for-the-marlins.html', 'snippet': 'On the eve of baseball’s winter meetings in Dallas, the Miami Marlins and Reyes agreed to a six-year contract worth $106 million, according to a person with direct knowledge of the agreement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — Jose Reyes has worn only the blue, orange and white of the Mets, the team that signed him as a 16-year-old in 1999 and the organization with which he has played his entire distinguished career.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05mets-1/05mets-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05mets-1/05mets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/05/sports/05mets-1/05mets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reyes, Longtime Mets Star, Is Set to Join the Marlins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reyes, Longtime Mets Star, Is Set to Join the Marlins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Marlins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDERSON, SANDY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T04:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c155ea3c-eb98-528f-a1f2-507dd4a94fde', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c155ea3c-eb98-528f-a1f2-507dd4a94fde'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft beat Apple to the punch with voice command software that can operate a TV, but by the time Apple TVs show up, probably in 2013, both Apple’s Siri and Microsoft’s voice commands will be far more sophisticated. But that’s only the beginning. Computers will soon be able to read subtle human gestures.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/04/disruptions-a-tv-that-can-read-me/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft beat Apple to the punch with voice command software that can operate a TV, but by the time Apple TVs show up, probably in 2013, both Apple’s Siri and Microsoft’s voice commands will be far more sophisticated. But that’s only the beginnin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Television, and, for that matter, a whole lot of other devices, including cellphones and cars, are about to get more perceptive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/05/technology/05bits-kinect/05bits-kinect-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: A TV That Can Read Me', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Xbox (Video Game System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T04:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}