mports of Iranian petrochemicals amount only to $300 million a year, but the country fears the impact their suspension might have on its trade ties with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/world/asia/us-asks-south-korea-to-cut-petrochemical-imports-from-iran.html', 'snippet': 'South Korean imports of Iranian petrochemicals amount only to $300 million a year, but the country fears the impact their suspension might have on its trade ties with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — A senior American diplomat urged South Korea on Monday to suspend imports of Iranian petrochemicals as Washington tried to rally international pressure on Iran to\xa0stop its nuclear program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Asks South Korea to Cut Petrochemical Imports From Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Asks South Korea to Cut Petrochemical Imports From Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T08:38:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c8c7097-bece-51ba-b528-0982f0f7d860', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c8c7097-bece-51ba-b528-0982f0f7d860'}, {'abstract': 'On Dec. 5, 1933, national Prohibition came to an end, as Utah became the 36th state to ratify the 21st Amendment to the Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/dec-5-1933-ratification-of-21st-amendment-ends-prohibition/', 'snippet': 'On Dec. 5, 1933, national Prohibition came to an end, as Utah became the 36th state to ratify the 21st Amendment to the Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 5, 1933, national Prohibition came to an end, as Utah became the 36th state to ratify the 21st Amendment to the Constitution. The amendment repealed the 18th Amendment, which had taken effect nearly 14 years earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 5, 1933 | Ratification of 21st Amendment Ends Prohibition', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T09:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78bcdc88-f59a-5604-b666-6dcc7a0c30b3', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78bcdc88-f59a-5604-b666-6dcc7a0c30b3'}, {'abstract': 'Can you calculate the number of school lunches served each year if given the per-lunch increase in cost and the total cost increase over five years?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/test-yourself-math-dec-5-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you calculate the number of school lunches served each year if given the per-lunch increase in cost and the total cost increase over five years?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Pete Diamantis at Math for America from the article “Congress Blocks New Rules on School Lunches.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Dec. 5, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T09:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b95824ae-0219-535f-8c56-735cb17e59bf', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b95824ae-0219-535f-8c56-735cb17e59bf'}, {'abstract': 'Moises Saman had been photographing the run-up to the Egyptian elections when the recent riots broke out. He spoke to Lens about the challenges of digging deeper into the story.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/even-in-egypt-a-long-way-to-go/', 'snippet': 'Moises Saman had been photographing the run-up to the Egyptian elections when the recent riots broke out. He spoke to Lens about the challenges of digging deeper into the story.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Moises Saman has been covering the Arab Spring for The New York Times since its beginning in Tunisia. In July, he moved to Egypt — where, for the last four weeks, he has been photographing the run-up to the Egyptian elections. Mr. Saman, a nominee for membership in the Magnum Photos cooperative, spoke with James Estrin and David Furst last Wednesday. This conversation has been edited and condensed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even in Egypt, a Long Way to Go', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'majo