at rifts between friends.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/friendship/', 'snippet': 'The stress and competition of the college admissions process can wear on even the strongest friendships, but keeping application results private can help to combat rifts between friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susannah Griffee, a sophomore at New York University pursuing a double major in journalism and politics, is an intern this fall on The Choice blog and The New York Times Learning Network.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protecting Friendships During the College Admissions Process', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T11:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah L. Griffee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Griffee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538293fc-c739-55a2-8592-f78cc7f0e729', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538293fc-c739-55a2-8592-f78cc7f0e729'}, {'abstract': 'Who will be future inductees in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/what-artists-or-bands-of-today-are-destined-for-the-rock-and-roll-hall-of-fame/', 'snippet': 'Who will be future inductees in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Beastie Boys. Rufus with Chaka Khan. Guns N’ Roses. Heart. The Cure. Do you know these artists? They are among the 15 nominees who, if chosen, will join likes of Elvis, Madonna, the Eagles and hundreds of other music luminaries in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame. Do you think this year’s nominees are good choices? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Artists or Bands of Today Are Destined for the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T11:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6fc19d2-e578-5ddb-96da-33f6e294ff3a', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6fc19d2-e578-5ddb-96da-33f6e294ff3a'}, {'abstract': 'A number of freelance election observers in Russia, with the help of hand-held cameras and smartphones, have become successful at frustrating voter fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/world/europe/russian-parliamentary-elections-criticized-by-west.html', 'snippet': 'A number of freelance election observers in Russia, with the help of hand-held cameras and smartphones, have become successful at frustrating voter fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The shot opens at the top of a flight of stairs and zooms in shakily on a gray-haired man, who sits at a desk furtively checking off what appear to be ballots — a stack of them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/MOSCOW-REFER/MOSCOW-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/MOSCOW-REFER/MOSCOW-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/europe/MOS