85-53df-bd9b-ec66122006ed'}, {'abstract': 'Y&R, which was Young & Rubicam when it opened its doors in 1926 at 285 Madison Avenue, is relocating to 3 Columbus Circle.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/after-80-years-yr-plans-to-leave-madison-ave-for-columbus-circle/', 'snippet': 'Y&R, which was Young & Rubicam when it opened its doors in 1926 at 285 Madison Avenue, is relocating to 3 Columbus Circle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madison Avenue has become synonymous with the advertising industry because so many agencies were originally located there. Now, one that still actually calls Madison Avenue home will be leaving after more than eight decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After 85 Years, Y&R Plans to Leave Madison Ave. for Columbus Circle', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sable, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'COLUMBUS CIRCLE (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T11:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d32e097-a645-5ef2-85eb-61f0100c44c7', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d32e097-a645-5ef2-85eb-61f0100c44c7'}, {'abstract': 'Companies plan to rebuff the Indian government’s latest attempt to tighten the leash on free speech on the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/india-asks-google-facebook-others-to-screen-user-content/', 'snippet': 'Companies plan to rebuff the Indian government’s latest attempt to tighten the leash on free speech on the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian government has asked Internet companies and social media sites like Facebook to prescreen user content from India and to remove disparaging, inflammatory or defamatory content before it goes online, three executives in the information technology industry say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India Asks Google, Facebook to Screen User Content', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Sonia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T11:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49616903-2a44-50bb-a330-6fc72d712d09', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49616903-2a44-50bb-a330-6fc72d712d09'}, {'abstract': 'Most fans could agree that Frank Gore has had a better career than Garrison Hearst and Ricky Watters. But has he been better than Roger Craig?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/gore-has-niners-record-but-where-does-he-rank/', 'snippet': 'Most fans could agree that Frank Gore has had a better career than Garrison Hearst and Ricky Watters. But has he been better than Roger Craig?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a discussion for Niners fans to have: Where does Frank Gore rank on your team’s running back list? Statistically, he’s now No. 1. His 73 yards rushing Sunday gave him 7,396 for his career, moving him past Joe Perry. It’s difficult to compare Gore to Perry given that Perry played some 50 years ago. As for comparing Gore with more modern Niner running backs…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gore Has Niners’ Record, but Where Does He Rank?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T11:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/879810cf-8681-5039-885a-b119c0cf8ea3', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/879810cf-8681-5039-885a-b119c0cf8ea3'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: Are you making enough of an effort to sell to your existing customers?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/this-week-in-small-business-are-consumers-and-jobs-back/', 'snippet': 'Plus: Are you making enough of an effort to sell to your existing customers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: Are Consumers (and Jobs) Back?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T12:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78ca744-6bc7-5dc6-a04f-58d7436a6a82', 'word_count': 1605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78ca744-6bc7-5dc6-a04f-58d7436a6a82'}, {'abstract': 'An emotional win over Duke (22-4-1) to capture the national championship already feels like a program-defining moment for Stanford (25-0-1), which coming into the weekend had fallen short in consecutive College Cup Finals without scoring a goal.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/at-college-cup-a-crowning-moment-for-stanford-women/', 'snippet': 'An emotional win over Duke (22-4-1) to capture the national championship already feels like a program-defining moment for Stanford (25-0-1), which coming into the weekend had fallen short in consecutive College Cup Finals without scoring a goal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four straight trips to the women’s soccer Final Four for Stanford have ended in 1-0 games. Only this time, the Cardinal walked away with the College Cup in hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At College Cup, a Crowning Moment for Stanford Women', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T12:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Beyda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beyda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86952f4b-28b6-5cc8-bd5c-203dc96e7bf7', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86952f4b-28b6-5cc8-bd5c-203dc96e7bf7'}, {'abstract': 'From the Complaint Box: To one reader, even the most foul scents of the city are preferable to a heavy cloak of perfume.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/complaint-box-overperfumed/', 'snippet': 'From the Complaint Box: To one reader, even the most foul scents of the city are preferable to a heavy cloak of perfume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any New Yorker can attest, our city is permeated by smells: curbside garbage, street carts selling nuts or kabobs, impromptu barbecues, fresh marijuana and the odoriferous mélange produced by the subway system, especially in the summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Overperfumed', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smells and Odors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T12:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah J. Dreisinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Dreisinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/023cd813-ffa6-5a70-986b-ddde62eb861c', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/023cd813-ffa6-5a70-986b-ddde62eb861c'}, {'abstract': 'The coal developer Aston Resources says it is in discussions with another Australian miner, Whitehaven Coal, on a potential deal valued at almost $5 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/australian-mining-companies-in-talks-for-5-billion-merger/', 'snippet': 'The coal developer Aston Resources says it is in discussions with another Australian miner, Whitehaven Coal, on a potential deal valued at almost $5 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The coal developer Aston Resources said on Monday that it was in discussions with another Australian miner, Whitehaven Coal, on a potential merger valued at almost $5 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australian Mining Companies in Talks on $5 Billion Merger', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T12:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4b5f67d-4898-5263-bb5f-7f91af65a08d', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4b5f67d-4898-5263-bb5f-7f91af65a08d'}, {'abstract': 'Madonna at the Super Bowl, Chelsea Clinton at large, a new look for holiday books and Mitt Romney keeps the press mostly at bay.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-5/', 'snippet': 'Madonna at the Super Bowl, Chelsea Clinton at large, a new look for holiday books and Mitt Romney keeps the press mostly at bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madonna is to perform during the halftime show at Super Bowl XLVI in Indianapolis, set to air Feb. 5 on NBC, the network announced on Sunday night during its football broadcast. The idea had been in play  for some time, with Madonna seen as fitting the N.F.L.’s trend of looking to older performers since the controversy over the “wardrobe malfunction” of Janet Jackson in 2004. She will collaborate with a team from Cirque du Soleil, the choreographer Jamie King and artists from Moment Factory, The Associated Press reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 5', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baier, Bret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, Laura', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murakami, Haruki', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metallica', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politico, The', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T12:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/177650f7-f2dd-5d25-8fd2-2b8f4653c463', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/177650f7-f2dd-5d25-8fd2-2b8f4653c463'}, {'abstract': 'Any  coach that mismanages timeouts and field position as spectacularly as Dallas Coach Jason Garrett did in the final minutes deserves to lose.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/jason-garrett-too-cautious-in-cowboys-defeat/', 'snippet': 'Any  coach that mismanages timeouts and field position as spectacularly as Dallas Coach Jason Garrett did in the final minutes deserves to lose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget that the regular-season overtime rules prevented the Cowboys from even touching the ball after regulation of a 19-13 loss at Arizona – that was merely karmic justice. Any coach that mismanages timeouts and field position as spectacularly as Dallas Coach Jason Garrett did in the final minutes deserves to lose. First, Garrett seemingly iced his own kicker by calling a timeout just before Dan Bailey’s 49-yard field goal on what would have been the game’s final play. (Bailey made the initial kick, but couldn’t repeat it.) Analyzing timeout usage as it pertains to a kicker’s rhythm is like analyzing how your day might have been different if you’d only brushed your teeth three minutes earlier. It’s a fruitless practice that’s all hindsight and presumption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Garrett Too Cautious in Cowboys’ Defeat', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major':