s, however, by keeping the companies separate, and getting customers comfortable with the new computing world.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/saps-strategy-with-successfactors/', 'snippet': 'The German software company’s $3.4 billion acquisition of SuccessFactors, a maker of  software for cloud computing, is a first step in taking SAP into the cloud. It begins, however, by keeping the companies separate, and getting customers comforta...', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAP made a big move into the cloud computing world over the weekend, buying the human resource management software company SuccessFactors for $3.4 billion. But its first steps after the purchase are going to\xa0 involve a lot of old-time selling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SAP’s Strategy with SuccessFactors', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAP A.G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffce6574-6034-54f0-8cc8-9e1814f5cb74', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffce6574-6034-54f0-8cc8-9e1814f5cb74'}, {'abstract': 'Fifteen of Harry Allen’s shapely Gaia vases, which have been customized by celebrities, will be sold to benefit Housing Works.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/auction-alert-the-goddess-adorned/', 'snippet': 'Fifteen of Harry Allen’s shapely Gaia vases, which have been customized by celebrities, will be sold to benefit Housing Works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gaia, the ancient Greek earth goddess, is being sold to the highest bidder, but it’s for a good cause. A collaboration between the Turkish home accessories company Gaia & Gino, the New York designer Harry Allen and Swarovski Elements has produced “The Goddess Adorned,”\xa0 an auction of 15 of Allen’s shapely Gaia vases, which have been customized by a glittering list of celebrities in the worlds of fashion, design and style, including Ashley and Mary Kate Olsen for  Elizabeth and James, Kenneth Jay Lane, Doo.Ri, Waris Ahluwalia and Allen himself. The vases will be auctioned online for two weeks starting Tuesday to benefit Housing Works, and will be on view at the Swarovski Crystallized concept store, at 499 Broadway in SoHo. The original vase, which was designed by Allen for Gaia & Gino but never produced, was always meant to be “dressed,” with jewelry or ribbons, for instance. “I designed the vase to be transformed,” Allen explains, citing Gaye Cevikel, Gaia & Gino’s fashionable founder, as his inspiration. A number of samples of the vase were made, and Allen had the idea to auction them for charity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auction Alert | ‘The Goddess Adorned’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0827db5a-ad09-5ffe-b041-5a4baddc3245', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0827db5a-ad09-5ffe-b041-5a4baddc3245'}, {'abstract': 'Prince 