f links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Tribune: Can you say: Tavern on the Green in Central Park? Rahm Emanuel, Chicago’s Mayor, is trying to jack up the fees the city gets for the Park Grill at Millennium Park, suing to invalidate a generous 2003 concession deal the city made under former Mayor Richard M. Daley. — Glenn Collins ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/233ace36-25ce-55ef-9e8d-bd83e7a07e75', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/233ace36-25ce-55ef-9e8d-bd83e7a07e75'}, {'abstract': 'As airlines cut back, hotels add perks, higher loan limits again for pricey markets, banking by mobile phone and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/monday-reading-hotels-add-perks-as-airlines-cut-back/', 'snippet': 'As airlines cut back, hotels add perks, higher loan limits again for pricey markets, banking by mobile phone and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Hotels Add Perks as Airlines Cut Back', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:46:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3adf4d0-665e-515a-9d00-7807c9ca7da3', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3adf4d0-665e-515a-9d00-7807c9ca7da3'}, {'abstract': 'A dean of N.F.L. writers put it this way: “What exactly are we watching here, other than the nuttiest story in recent sports history?”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/tebow-numbers-geeks-and-yet-another-victory/', 'snippet': 'A dean of N.F.L. writers put it this way: “What exactly are we watching here, other than the nuttiest story in recent sports history?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his Monday Morning QB at Sports Illustrated’s site, Peter King wrote:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tebow, ‘Numbers Geeks’ and Yet Another Victory', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac9e598d-2be6-51d4-9d29-48b0ad1f7c1f', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac9e598d-2be6-51d4-9d29-48b0ad1f7c1f'}, {'abstract': 'A series of online videos documented the choreographer and his work.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/cunningham-countdown-mondays-with-merce/', 'snippet': 'A series of online videos documented the choreographer and his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday Merce Cunningham will appear on screen in the first public showing of his final interview. It is 18 minutes long and unedited. The interview was filmed in June 2009, the month before his death. When his face first appears on screen – he was 90, had been largely confined to a wheelchair for some years, and in recent months had suffered various medical setbacks – you’re aware of the depredations of age. Then he talks, and it’s evident that the mind was still sharp, the interest in precise verbal articulation still alert, the passion for dance unrelenting. It is an exciting revelation of his unflagging intelligence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cunningham Countdown: A Monday With Merce', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T14:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c52e3723-e61c-5458-b9b1-4f7c7bb9d05c', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c52e3723-e61c-5458-b9b1-4f7c7bb9d05c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a saddle bag turned on its head.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/the-get-mark-cross-madison-mini-doctor-bag/', 'snippet': 'It’s a saddle bag turned on its head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As far as shapes go, the Madison Mini Doctor bag from the all-American leather goods label Mark Cross is an interesting one –– extra-long strap, compact size, structured handles. It’s a saddle bag (the company was established in 1845 as a source for saddles and harnesses) turned on its head. “We want all of our bags to reflect the brand’s legacy and history,” says the company president, Neal Fox, about its strategy and recent re-entry into the marketplace. “This one reflects an especially modern approach to classicism.” At $1,495, it is a princely price to pay for timeless style. The only question is, where to wear it first, Los Angeles or Monaco?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Mark Cross Madison Mini Doctor Bag', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T15:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba68bf7c-7c9d-51cb-9146-8fec884b2ff7', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba68bf7c-7c9d-51cb-9146-8fec884b2ff7'}, {'abstract': 'By midafternoon Monday, Beijing’s main airport had canceled 233 domestic and 17 international flights. Another 400 flights were canceled on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/on-our-radar-smog-grounds-flights-in-beijing/', 'snippet': 'By midafternoon Monday, Beijing’s main airport had canceled 233 domestic and 17 international flights. Another 400 flights were canceled on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thick smog prompts officials to cancel hundreds of flights and shut down some major highways in Beijing. The American Embassy describes current air quality there as “hazardous,” and the official Xinhua news agency says the pollution is likely to reach “dangerous” levels. [Agence France-Presse]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Smog Grounds Flights in Beijing', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T15:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ffcd3bb-62f8-59e2-88be-f54dfb3b8a88', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ffcd3bb-62f8-59e2-88be-f54dfb3b8a88'}, {'abstract': 'Tens of thousands of programmers, writers, accountants and other workers labor at home doing contract work for companies like Google, Hewlett-Packard and NBC. The computers they use contain software that takes snapshots of what they are doing six times an hour. The growing popularity of contract work at large companies means such practices are now commonplace.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/big-brother-in-the-home-office/', 'snippet': 'Tens of thousands of programmers, writers, accountants and other workers labor at home doing contract work for companies like Google, Hewlett-Packard and NBC. The computers they use contain software that takes snapshots of what they are doing six ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tens of thousands of programmers, writers, accountants and other workers labor at home doing contract work for companies like Google, Hewlett-Packard and NBC. The computers they use contain software that takes snapshots of what they are doing six times an hour. The snooping occurs randomly, making it impossible for the computer user to game the system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/technology/02bits-odesk/02bits-odesk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/02/technology/02bits-odesk/02bits-odesk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/02/technology/02bits-odesk/02bits-odesk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Brother in the Home Office', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T15:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/762b5689-eee7-52a7-97c0-d1e537cf6009', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/762b5689-eee7-52a7-97c0-d1e537cf6009'}, {'abstract': 'Remembering the veteran Bollywood actor who died on Sunday at the age of 88.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/the-philosophy-of-dev-anand/', 'snippet': 'Remembering the veteran Bollywood actor who died on Sunday at the age of 88.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dev Anand wasn’t a star. He was a philosophy. The 88-year-old actor, who died of cardiac arrest on December 4, symbolized six decades of Hindi cinema and a spirit that insisted that the show must go on. No matter that the films ceased to seduce or that viewers stopped showing up decades ago. Dev Anand continued to create and despite the mostly substandard quality of his output, he never lost his icon status or the affection of his audience and colleagues. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Philosophy of Dev Anand', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anand, Dev', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T15:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anupama Chopra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anupama', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chopra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc7cef8-dc67-556d-904c-7d1ef02ff5a0', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc7cef8-dc67-556d-904c-7d1ef02ff5a0'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Nov. 28.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/11/28/fashion/street/20111202_streetstyle.html', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Nov. 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Nov. 28.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11