': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Tablet Bites the Dust: Dell’s Streak 7', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T16:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b88799ee-e739-54fd-9a02-fd5b619b2bf1', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b88799ee-e739-54fd-9a02-fd5b619b2bf1'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s welfare minister, Elsa Fornero, was shown breaking down as she began to announce that the pension age will rise.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/welfare-ministers-tears-show-italians-pain-of-austerity/', 'snippet': 'Italy’s welfare minister, Elsa Fornero, was shown breaking down as she began to announce that the pension age will rise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Rachel Donadio reported, Italy’s new government, hastily assembled after Silvio Berlusconi’s departure, announced sweeping austerity measures Sunday night. The package of deep spending cuts and tax increases is intended, said Prime Minister Mario Monti, to “save Italy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Welfare Minister’s Tears Show Italians Pain of Austerity', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T16:55:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ff97403-6d14-5666-bf5a-aa2ce22cf729', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ff97403-6d14-5666-bf5a-aa2ce22cf729'}, {'abstract': 'Amy Winehouse’s posthumous album, “Lioness,” and new releases from Robin Thicke and T-Pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/arts/music/from-amy-winehouses-archives-lioness-new-music.html', 'snippet': 'Amy Winehouse’s posthumous album, “Lioness,” and new releases from Robin Thicke and T-Pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She didn’t leave much behind. That’s the inescapable fact of Amy Winehouse‘s posthumous collection, “Lioness: Hidden Treasures.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 632, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/NEWMUSIC/NEWMUSIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chipper Remnants of a Life Turned Sour', 'kicker': 'New Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chipper Remnants Of a Life Turned Sour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winehouse, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'T-Pain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thicke, Robin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T16:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles, Jon Caramanica and Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f6dfd25-a0dc-5388-8cb8-e1141b3b2b18', 'word_count': 1431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f6dfd25-a0dc-5388-8cb8-e1141b3b2b18'}, {'abstract': 'Austra’s recent sold-out performance at the Echo brought the club to a thundering halt.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/notes-from-the-underground-austra/', 'snippet': 'Austra’s recent sold-out performance at the Echo brought the club to a thundering halt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Austra’s recent sold-out performance at the Echo brought the club to a thundering halt with heavy beats and ethereal vocals, provided by the band’s Katie Stelmanis. Flanked by bejeweled identical twin backup singers, Stelmanis, who previously performed as a solo artist, flaunted her prowess for fronting an act, taking Austra through a tight, deep set, each song better than the last.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Austra', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/234b4225-acfb-59b5-8344-98f4b5e7198f', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/234b4225-acfb-59b5-8344-98f4b5e7198f'}, {'abstract': 'Is Best Buy’s “Game On, Santa” all fun and games until someone loses the meaning of Christmas?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/dear-best-buy-dont-mock-santa/', 'snippet': 'Is Best Buy’s “Game On, Santa” all fun and games until someone loses the meaning of Christmas?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I would like to come straight out and say that I am a delicate flower on the matter of Santa Claus and the “magic of Christmas.” I would prefer that you not show any disrespect to the big guy in a mainstream setting, both because I have children who still believe, and because as much as I worry that Christmas has become a season of getting, I think Santa creates, for kids, an atmosphere of giving, as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Best Buy: Don’t Mock Santa', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f52e19-b4db-5ed9-af50-11372312d064', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f52e19-b4db-5ed9-af50-11372312d064'}, {'abstract': 'Entergy says it plans to sell its electric transmission business to ITC Holdings in a two-step process that avoids taxes.