bility led to another ethical issue. A marketing person for the lifetime-care institution we selected understated its price by $300 a month. Should we hold them to it? We would have come regardless, and we can afford the higher price. DON CELL, CEDAR RAPIDS, IOWA', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spouse’s Bill of Rights', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Spouse’s Bill of Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Group Homes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T17:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0393530d-e560-5dc5-83e6-0652ce9d43ac', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0393530d-e560-5dc5-83e6-0652ce9d43ac'}, {'abstract': 'If ‘crowd-funding’ platforms were allowed to solicit investments, it would create a whole new financing mechanism for new businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/why-start-ups-need-crowd-funding/', 'snippet': 'If ‘crowd-funding’ platforms were allowed to solicit investments, it would create a whole new financing mechanism for new businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you familiar with “crowd-funding?” You should be. I have been following the progress of new crowd-funding platforms in recent months, and it is now clear that this new financing mechanism can help strapped early-stage ventures, especially social enterprises. In case you’re hearing about crowd-funding for the first time, let me bring you up to speed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Start-Ups Need ‘Crowd-Funding’', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T18:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': 