 “The Help.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/when-minny-met-talley/', 'snippet': 'Andre Leon Talley improvises his own Q&A with the stars of “The Help.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Peggy Siegal’s lunch for “The Help” on Friday, what is usually a highly managed affair went off-script, as we noted here, with Billie Jean King getting in on the act. She wasn’t the only guest with something to say. Andre Leon Talley, the Vogue editor and king of pronouncements, played a lively role, commenting, from his seat, about the look of the film, set in the early 1960s, and praising the costume designer, Sharen Davis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Minny Met Talley', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T19:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40fe90e5-9166-542a-964b-65a67f30596c', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40fe90e5-9166-542a-964b-65a67f30596c'}, {'abstract': 'The article in Saturday’s New York Times, “Oh, for the Good Old Days of Rude Cellphone Gabbers,” stirred a vocal response among readers, eager to show their thoughts on the general boorishness of cellphone users. Read a selection of their comments.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/making-noise-about-people-who-talk-to-their-cellphones/', 'snippet': 'The article in Saturday’s New York Times, “Oh, for the Good Old Days of Rude Cellphone Gabbers,” stirred a vocal response among readers, eager to show their thoughts on the general boorishness of cellphone users. Read a selection of their comments...', 'lead_paragraph': ' My article in Saturday’s New York Times, “Oh, for the Good Old Days of Rude Cellphone Gabbers,” stirred a vocal response among readers, many of whom decried the boorishness of cellphone users in all of its many forms in several hundred comments posted over the weekend. The piece was about people who use voice technologies like Siri in the new iPhone 4S to orally search for restaurants, dictate texts and schedule appointments while in public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Noise About People Who Talk to Their Cellphones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voice Recognition Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T19:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3cf7f3f-d6ca-5822-aa69-344c17ea2bde', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3cf7f3f-d6ca-5822-aa69-344c17ea2bde'}, {'abstract': 'A victory Monday night would be a milestone for the New York Rangers–and their eighth straight at home.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/a-magic-number-for-the-rangers-2500/', 'snippet': 'A victory Monday night would be a milestone for the New York Rangers–and their eighth straight at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rangers are seeking the 2,500th victory in club history Monday night when they host the Toronto Maple Leafs at Madison Square Garden. They’re also out for their sixth straight win, their eighth straight at home, and the 13th victory in their last 15 games over all. If they do win, they’ll maintain their position as the team with the N.H.L.’s best overall winning percentage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Magic Number for the Rangers: 2,500', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Zotto, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T19:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f5f3d45-cd35-5734-8a58-e60ddc01547b', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f5f3d45-cd35-5734-8a58-e60ddc01547b'}, {'abstract': 'Thieves stole more than $250,000 using skimmers on Chase A.T.M.’s near Union Square, highlighting the need to be vigilant.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/the-latest-a-t-m-skimmer-scam/', 'snippet': 'Thieves stole more than $250,000 using skimmers on Chase A.T.M.’s near Union Square, highlighting the need to be vigilant.', 'l