 millionaires’ tax imposed in 2009 on individuals who make more than $200,000 drove New Yorkers out of state. The tax is scheduled to lapse on Dec. 31, but Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is negotiating revisions in the tax code with legislative leaders that would raise taxes on wealthier New Yorkers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wealthy New Yorkers Are Staying In State, Census Shows', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beveridge, Andrew A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T20:39:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed64aa1-83c9-52cb-812a-93b1304c014e', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed64aa1-83c9-52cb-812a-93b1304c014e'}, {'abstract': 'New York City education officials are talking to parents this week about how to set pre-K students on the path to college. They are beginning a series of citywide information sessions on the issue for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/05/preparing-for-college-and-kindergarten/', 'snippet': 'New York City education officials are talking to parents this week about how to set pre-K students on the path to college. They are beginning a series of citywide information sessions on the issue for the first time.', 'lead_paragrap