and the Bulls', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Derrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thibodeau, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T20:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78b0dd4f-bc0d-5e5d-a0f9-03f644e84c1c', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78b0dd4f-bc0d-5e5d-a0f9-03f644e84c1c'}, {'abstract': 'Comments by the new president of CCTV drew comparisons with Joseph Goebbels and comes amid an uptick in the official Chinese government language targeting the spread of rumors online and “fake news.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/journalists-should-be-government-mouthpieces-chinas-state-tv-president-says/', 'snippet': 'Comments by the new president of CCTV drew comparisons with Joseph Goebbels and comes amid an uptick in the official Chinese government language targeting the spread of rumors online and “fake news.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new president of China’s largest television network, the state-run organization known CCTV, drew fire over the weekend from Chinese press advocates and others online over comments urging journalists to drop their pretensions of professionalism and submit to being mouthpieces of the government. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Journalists Should Be Government Mouthpieces, Chinese Media Leader Says', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Central Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T20:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9f4b070-823f-5511-a720-3514b323719f', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9f4b070-823f-5511-a720-3514b323719f'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Artists, a nonprofit organization that gives annual no-strings-attached grants to artists, composers, writers and performers has announced this year’s list of recipients who will receive grants of $50,000.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/arts-group-hands-out-grants-to-52-artists/', 'snippet': 'The United States Artists, a nonprofit organization that gives annual no-strings-attached grants to artists, composers, writers and performers has announced this year’s list of recipients who will receive grants of $50,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Artists, a nonprofit organization that gives annual no-strings-attached grants to artists, composers, writers and performers has announced this year’s list of recipients who will receive grants of $50,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arts Group Hands Out Grants to 52 Artists', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee8cdcad-cae8-5cfb-9e2f-ad52e0208de5', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee8cdcad-cae8-5cfb-9e2f-ad52e0208de5'}, {'abstract': 'Sundance Film Festival releases its list of feature and documentary premieres.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/spike-lee-and-other-big-names-make-sundances-list/', 'snippet': 'Sundance Film Festival releases its list of feature and documentary premieres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spike Lee makes his Sundance debut as a director. The former indie queen Parker Posey returns in a big role. Rashida Jones (“Parks and Recreation”) tries her hand at screenwriting. Comedy, comedy and more comedy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spike Lee and Other Big Names Make Sundance’s List', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d978012-204a-5719-b4b7-3769e8453186', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d978012-204a-5719-b4b7-3769e8453186'}, {'abstract': 'Mary L. Schapiro, the S.E.C. chairwoman, wants her agency to be able to seek higher penalties in administrative proceedings, a move that may allow it to avoid having to pursue its cases in federal courts.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/s-e-c-seeks-more-power-but-does-it-need-it/', 'snippet': 'Mary L. Schapiro, the S.E.C. chairwoman, wants her agency to be able to seek higher penalties in administrative proceedings, a move that may allow it to avoid having to pursue its cases in federal courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Judge Jed S. Rakoff of Federal District Court in Manhattan rejected the Securities and Exchange Commission‘s proposed settlement with Citigroup because he did not find it in the public interest, the agency’s chairwoman, Mary L. Schapiro, sought to enhance the S.E.C.’s authority to impose higher financial penalties to deter securities violations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Seeks More Power, but Does It Need It?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d86cf1-3468-5815-ac81-ec6e4d91d652', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d86cf1-3468-5815-ac81-ec6e4d91d652'}, {'abstract': 'Anticipating security threats is not merely a matter of reasoning abstractly about how new technology might raise new risks; it requires an understanding of human nature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/stefan-savage-girding-for-digital-threats-we-havent-imagined-yet.html', 'snippet': 'Anticipating security threats is not merely a matter of reasoning abstractly about how new technology might raise new risks; it requires an understanding of human nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Security is a curious concept, part perception and part prognostication. Webster’s captures both sides of this dichotomy in its definition: “freedom from danger; freedom from fear.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD8/06HEAD8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 256, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD8/06HEAD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD8/06HEAD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Planning Digital Defenses, the Biggest Obstacle Is Human Ingenuity', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Planning Digital Defenses, the Biggest Obstacle Is Human Ingenuity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Malware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spam (Electronic Mail)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b7cc70f-22c8-5852-b89b-076078334025', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b7cc70f-22c8-5852-b89b-076078334025'}, {'abstract': 'Can studies of Earth’s cold times help clarify what lies ahead as greenhouse gases build?', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/more-on-the-sensitive-climate-question/', 'snippet': 'Can studies of Earth’s cold times help clarify what lies ahead as greenhouse gases build?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are some fresh thoughts on the enduring and important questions surrounding \xa0“climate sensitivity”\xa0— how much warming will result from a substantial buildup of greenhouse gases.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More on the ‘Sensitive’ Climate Question', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value