at the polls were far shorter than when the voting began a week before, and at the same time, the Egyptian election commission said that the turnout last week was in fact much lower than initially reported.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/EGYPT/EGYPT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/world/EGYPT/EGYPT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/EGYPT/EGYPT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turnout Falls as Egypt Casts Runoff Ballots', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turnout Falls As Egypt Casts Runoff Ballots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:13:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7e93de-79e6-55d7-88b7-22776e318fc2', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7e93de-79e6-55d7-88b7-22776e318fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Ellis, the executive director of Jazz at Lincoln Center, has told that organization’s board he will step down, a spokeswoman for the jazz organization said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/jazz-at-lincoln-center-director-to-step-down/', 'snippet': 'Adrian Ellis, the executive director of Jazz at Lincoln Center, has told that organization’s board he will step down, a spokeswoman for the jazz organization said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Adrian Ellis, the executive director of Jazz at Lincoln Center, has told that organization’s board he will step down in early January. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center Director to Step Down', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellis, Adrian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/129e791c-0f7f-57c2-ba74-2d1e63757b1b', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129e791c-0f7f-57c2-ba74-2d1e63757b1b'}, {'abstract': 'An outspoken Syrian blogger was reportedly arrested on Sunday on her way to a conference in neighboring Jordan on press freedom in the Arab world.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/syria-reportedly-detains-outspoken-blogger/', 'snippet': 'An outspoken Syrian blogger was reportedly arrested on Sunday on her way to a conference in neighboring Jordan on press freedom in the Arab world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 5:27 p.m. An outspoken Syrian blogger was reportedly arrested on Sunday on her way to a conference in neighboring Jordan on press freedom in the Arab world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Reportedly Detains Outspoken Blogger', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fb1c6d8-4635-5097-8528-64ad49e3bc9b', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fb1c6d8-4635-5097-8528-64ad49e3bc9b'}, {'abstract': 'The Internet is a belief system, a philosophy about the effectiveness of decentralized, bottom-up innovation. And it’s a philosophy that has begun to change how we think about creativity itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/joichi-ito-innovating-by-the-seat-of-our-pants.html', 'snippet': 'The Internet is a belief system, a philosophy about the effectiveness of decentralized, bottom-up innovation. And it’s a philosophy that has begun to change how we think about creativity itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Internet isn’t really a technology. It’s a belief system, a philosophy about the effectiveness of decentralized, bottom-up innovation. And it’s a philosophy that has begun to change how we think about creativity itself. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD7/06HEAD7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 256, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD7/06HEAD7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD7/06HEAD7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Open-Source Society, Innovating by the Seat of Our Pants', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In an Open-Source Society, Innovating by the Seat of Our Pants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Open-Source Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joichi Ito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joichi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c949abb9-0a8b-55b3-a9ef-688a37ac890a', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c949abb9-0a8b-55b3-a9ef-688a37ac890a'}, {'abstract': 'Several artists at Design Miami this year explored a relationship with a big fashion brand.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/design-miami-art-is-still-in-fashion-and-vice-versa/', 'snippet': 'Several artists at Design Miami this year explored a relationship with a big fashion brand.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m from that generation of artists who tries to think very hard about new sets of relationships between people and spaces and how people work with artwork,” said the artist Liam Gillick, who was one of several artists in Miami’s Design District this year exploring a relationship with a big fashion brand. Cross-disciplinary collaborations, often accompanied by pop-up stores, are the name of the game during Art Basel Miami Beach, with often brilliant — and on occasion, less-than-brilliant — results. This year’s brilliant moments included Gillick and Pringle of Scotland; Beatriz Milhazes and Cartier; and Anselm Reyle and Dior.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Design Miami | Art Is Still in Fashion and Vice Versa', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marina Cashdan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cashdan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f54ab4e5-bbf4-5f97-9c02-6a4f3fae7e82', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f54ab4e5-bbf4-5f97-9c02-6a4f3fae7e82'}, {'abstract': 'We are in a world nobody designed or expected, driving full tilt toward — a wall? a cliff? a new dawn? We must choose wisely, as if we could.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/theodor-holm-nelson-on-the-information-superhighway-destination-unknown.html', 'snippet': 'We are in a world nobody designed or expected, driving full tilt toward — a wall? a cliff? a new dawn? We must choose wisely, as if we could.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More and more people are looking to computers to save the world, but the people who run them certainly don’t know how. Nobody’s in charge, not even Google, though everyone in the dot-com world pretends. They’re all too busy with I.P.O.’s and market share, trying to start fads or come up with idiotic names.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD9/06HEAD9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 256, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD9/06HEAD9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD9/06HEAD9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Full Speed Ahead, Without a Map, Into New Realms of Possibility', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Full Speed Ahead, Without a Map, Into New Realms of Possibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theodor Holm Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theodor', 'middlename': 'Holm', 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be071042-19e7-5626-98ca-c3e8b2eeb25b', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be071042-19e7-5626-98ca-c3e8b2eeb25b'}, {'abstract': 'Quantum computing is one of the most exciting things happening in science right now. Just not for the reasons you usually hear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/scott-aaronson-quantum-computing-promises-new-insights.html', 'snippet': 'Quantum computing is one of the most exciting things happening in science right now. Just not for the reasons you usually hear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people hear that I work on quantum computing — one of the most radical proposals for the future of computation — their first question is usually, “So when can I expect a working quantum computer on my desk?” Often they bring up breathless news reports about commercial quantum computers right around the corner. After I explain the strained relationship between those reports and reality, they ask: “Then when? In 10 years? Twenty?”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD3/06HEAD3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 257, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD3/06HEAD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD3/06HEAD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quantum Computing Promises New Insights, Not Just Supermachines', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quantum Computing Promises New Insights, Not Just Supermachines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantum Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:23:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Aaronson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aaronson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8887a167-41a6-58f6-bae1-a9d1966a553e', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8887a167-41a6-58f6-bae1-a9d1966a553e'}, {'abstract': 'Janette Sadik-Khan, the Bloomberg administration official who has become a polarizing figure for leading the quest to make the city ever-more pedestrian, gets her prime-time TV moment.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/transportation-chief-steps-into-prime-time-spotlight/', 'snippet': 'Janette Sadik-Khan, the Bloomberg administration official who has become a polarizing figure for leading the quest to make the city ever-more pedestrian, gets her prime-time TV moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its first few weeks on the air, “Rock Center With Brian Williams,” the new NBC newsmagazine show, has tackled topics of major national import: starvation in Africa, cheating on standardized tests, child abuse in college football.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transportation Chief Steps Into Prime-Time Spotlight', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadik-Khan, Janette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c92ecac9-c7cb-54ab-ba22-908899eb3e6d', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c92ecac9-c7cb-54ab-ba22-908899eb3e6d'}, {'abstract': 'A Google team’s self-driving cars have traveled nearly 200,000 miles on public highways in California and Nevada, 100 percent safely.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/sebastian-thrun-self-driving-cars-can-save-lives-and-parking-spaces.html', 'snippet': 'A Google team’s self-driving cars have traveled nearly 200,000 miles on public highways in California and Nevada, 100 percent safely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jetsons had them in the 1960s. They were the defining element of “Knight Rider” in the 1980s: cars that drive themselves. Self-driving cars appear in countless science fiction movies. By Hollywood standards, they are so normal we don’t even notice them. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06HEAD1/06HEAD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1