to play Latino in “The ____________ With the Hat” at Hartford Theater Works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The casting director for the Hartford production of “The __________ With the Hat” said on Monday that she was not involved with the choice of two white actors to play the roles of two Puerto Rican characters in the play by Stephen Adly Guirgis, who last week went public with his concerns about that production’s casting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting Director Says She Didn’t Pick Actors to Play Latino Roles', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4614e308-c807-5cac-a601-65e0413b0401', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4614e308-c807-5cac-a601-65e0413b0401'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past few years, a curious thing has happened in Riverdale, in the Bronx: Listings have skyrocketed, while sales have dropped.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/nyregion/in-riverdale-more-for-sale-signs-than-sales.html', 'snippet': 'Over the past few years, a curious thing has happened in Riverdale, in the Bronx: Listings have skyrocketed, while sales have dropped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The home required no gentle embellishment, no agent-speak tucked into the description beside the property listing. The five bedrooms and marble center hall were supposed to speak for themselves. The sprawling patio and yard space would look quite at home in one of the wealthy suburban hamlets a few miles to the north.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Riverdale, More ‘For Sale’ Signs Than Sales', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Riverdale, More &#8216;For Sale&#8217; Signs Than Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'RIVERDALE (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:31:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b653b08-10a7-5ae5-8cc5-4066676125f5', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b653b08-10a7-5ae5-8cc5-4066676125f5'}, {'abstract': 'The tech reporters and editors of The New York Times are always on the lookout for the most interesting items on the Web. Today’s selection includes items on a possible criminal charge against a RIM executive in Indonesia and a tech firm that has banned e-mail.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/todays-scuttlebot-too-much-e-mail-and-more-woes-for-rim/', 'snippet': 'The tech reporters and editors of The New York Times are always on the lookout for the most interesting items on the Web. Today’s selection includes items on a possible criminal charge against a RIM executive in Indonesia and a tech firm that has ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s what the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Too Much E-Mail and More Woes for RIM', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36bbab59-f411-5b47-8e01-3b0f30b1fe24', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36bbab59-f411-5b47-8e01-3b0f30b1fe24'}, {'abstract': 'A former trader at the Galleon Group and Morgan Stanley is writing “The Buy Side,” which its publisher describes as “a journey through the trading underworld as well as a look at after-hours Wall Street.”', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/out-of-galleon-scandal-and-wall-st-excess-comes-a-book/', 'snippet': 'A former trader at the Galleon Group and Morgan Stanley is writing “The Buy Side,” which its publisher describes as “a journey through the trading underworld as well as a look at after-hours Wall Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former trader at the Galleon Group has signed an agreement with Crown Business, a division of Random House, to publish a memoir about his career on Wall Street and time spent working for Raj Rajaratnam, the head of Galleon who was convicted of running a huge insider trading conspiracy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Galleon Scandal and Wall St. Excess, a Book', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Prisons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ba870d-71cf-5b2a-835a-061f00b36c69', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ba870d-71cf-5b2a-835a-061f00b36c69'}, {'abstract': 'A new commenting system for The New Old Age.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/about-the-comments/', 'snippet': 'A new commenting system for The New Old Age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past few days, as you may have noticed, we’ve implemented a new commenting system here at The New Old Age. Among its features:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'About Your Comments', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:38:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f9214b4-24dc-50a8-b95f-98fe4687b5af', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f9214b4-24dc-50a8-b95f-98fe4687b5af'}, {'abstract': 'The city has set a February deadline for about 60 churches that had been holding services in city schools pending the appeal. The announcement followed a decision by the United States Supreme Court not to hear a Bronx church’s appeal of a city ban on holding worship services in public schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/05/city-moves-to-halt-church-meetings-at-schools/', 'snippet': 'The city has set a February deadline for about 60 churches that had been holding services in city schools pending the appeal. The announcement followed a decision by the United States Supreme Court not to hear a Bronx church’s appeal of a city ban...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Moves to Halt Church Meetings at Schools', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By SCHOOLBOOK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schoolbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3d3e477-54f5-5d73-b1ae-74a7a757624b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3d3e477-54f5-5d73-b1ae-74a7a757624b'}, {'abstract': 'Among the collection’s multicolor dresses is a springlike silk twill shirtdress with a whimsical poodle print.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/just-one-look-carolina-herrera/', 'snippet': 'Among the collection’s multicolor dresses is a springlike silk twill shirtdress with a whimsical poodle print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guest of honor at Carolina Herrera’s prefall presentation earlier today was none other than her black miniature poodle, Gaspar. “He has been here since this morning,” Herrera said, “he’s the star today.” And the muse, apparently. Among the collection’s multicolor tulle evening dresses, copper-colored sequin sheaths and the tortoiseshell-inspired metallic pencil skirts that Herrera called “lunch looks” was this: a springlike silk twill shirtdress with sweet sleeves featuring –– surprise! –– a whimsical poodle print on a royal blue ground. Fetching, indeed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Carolina Herrera', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrera, Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b46a5f7c-79b0-5ccd-84f3-bc8900895b71', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b46a5f7c-79b0-5ccd-84f3-bc8900895b71'}, {'abstract': 'Alarmed by the prospect of new Western penalties that could crimp its oil exports, Iran issued a shrill warning that such steps would send prices soaring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/world/middleeast/threatened-by-new-sanctions-iran-warns-of-250-oil.html', 'snippet': 'Alarmed by the prospect of new Western penalties that could crimp its oil exports, Iran issued a shrill warning that such steps would send prices soaring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alarmed by the possibility of new Western penalties that could abruptly reduce or even halt its oil exports, Iran issued a warning on Monday that crude oil prices could more than double to $250 a barrel if such sanctions were given serious consideration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran, Facing New Sanctions, Warns of Oil at $250 a Barrel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Penalties May Send Oil Prices Soaring, Iran Warns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T21:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd9c