to an artist known for creating sculptural installations that pay homage to Modernist design.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/scottish-artist-martin-boyce-wins-turner-prize/', 'snippet': 'The prestigious prize, given annually to a British artist under 50 for an outstanding exhibition, goes to an artist known for creating sculptural installations that pay homage to Modernist design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Boyce, an artist known for creating sculptural installations that pay homage to Modernist design, has won this year’s prestigious Turner Prize. The winning entry from Mr. Boyce, 44, was an installation that looks like both an interior space and a municipal park, with trees crafted of geometric aluminum leaves along with a desk, based on a library table by the French modernist designer Jean Prouvé. The desk has letters scratched into its surface, as though they were the carvings of a naughty school child.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scottish Artist Martin Boyce Wins Turner Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Joseph Mallord William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T22:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/510828be-27cb-54a2-8303-e3f7214c5c67', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/510828be-27cb-54a2-8303-e3f7214c5c67'}, {'abstract': 'Over six months, The Times examined the life and death of Derek Boogaard. The last article of a three-part series deta