nications and technology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State of the Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T22:37:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/949d6d59-3494-57f9-b25c-575a062b7780', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/949d6d59-3494-57f9-b25c-575a062b7780'}, {'abstract': 'The city disputes a comptroller’s audit’s claim that its mismanagement of concessions squandered an opportunity to generate more revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/parks-dept-forfeited-millions-in-revenue-audit-says/', 'snippet': 'The city disputes a comptroller’s audit’s claim that its mismanagement of concessions squandered an opportunity to generate more revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City Parks and Recreation Department could have attracted an additional $8.8 million in revenue in the last three fiscal years through better management of its retail, recreational and dining concessions, according to an audit released Monday by John C. Liu, the city comptroller.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parks Dept. Forfeited Millions in Revenue, Audit Says', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':