tion-study photographs of Eadweard J. Muybridge feel oddly ubiquitous right now. They’re featured in the Degas show at the Royal Academy here, in the Danser Sa Vie exhibition at the Pompidou Center in Paris, and they are a central theme in the new piece “Undance” by Wayne McGregor, Mark-Anthony Turnage and Mark Wallinger that completed a too-brief run at Sadler’s Wells on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/UNDANCE/UNDANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/UNDANCE/UNDANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/UNDANCE/UNDANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/UNDANCE/UNDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/UNDANCE/UNDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '3 Modern Collaborators Add a Victorian Shadow', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Modern Collaborators Add a Victorian Shadow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGregor, Wayne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallinger, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turnage, Mark-Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T22:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ec5c06-f16d-53cb-a872-5e6fb3468b39', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ec5c06-f16d-53cb-a872-5e6fb3468b39'}, {'abstract': 'Richmond, Va., the former capital of the Confederacy, is host to multiple museums about the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/06/arts/design/20111216-civil-ss.html', 'snippet': 'Richmond, Va., the former capital of the Confederacy, is host to multiple museums about the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richmond, Va., the former capital of the Confederacy, is host to multiple museums about the Civil War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/design/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/design/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/design/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI/20111216-civil-ss-slide-HNXI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Civil War Through Southern Eyes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T22:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8da33912-8115-56e8-a22f-11089b994bd2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8da33912-8115-56e8-a22f-11089b994bd2'}, {'abstract': 'Oscar de la Renta’s prefall collection featured smart, colorful day dresses and sparkling black-tie gowns.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/just-one-look-oscar-de-la-renta/', 'snippet': 'Oscar de la Renta’s prefall collection featured smart, colorful day dresses and sparkling black-tie gowns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oscar de la Renta’s prefall collection defied all carryall catchphrases and instead knowingly addressed his customers’ great and varied needs with everything from work pants and jackets to smart, colorful day dresses and sparkling black-tie gowns. Here, the latter: a sweeping coral evening dress that, when it lands in stores in May, will be exactly the bright, fluid and summery thing you’ll want to wear indoors or out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Oscar de la Renta', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Renta, Oscar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-05T23:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da93f8a9-addc-54ed-894d-7c05d4c7a9a0', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da93f8a9-addc-54ed-894d-7c05d4c7a9a0'}, {'abstract': 'In Virginia, museums of the Civil War struggle to balance evolving attitudes toward Southern traditions and the “Lost Cause.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/arts/design/museum-of-the-confederacy-and-others-depict-the-lost-cause.html', 'snippet': 'In Virginia, museums of the Civil War struggle to balance evolving attitudes toward Southern traditions and the “Lost Cause.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHMOND, Va. — In the climate-controlled archives of the Museum of the Confederacy, here in the city that was once the capital of the Confederate States of America, thousands of artifacts are carefully laid out in protective drawers. There are rag dolls and lace finery, folded uniforms scarred by bullet holes and sword slashes, well-maintained revolvers and gleaming sabers. Also from the Civil War’s front lines are the cherished rations of long-dead officers: a handful of colorless coffee beans, a block of chewing tobacco with a musky smell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/CIVIL/CIVIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/CIVIL/CIVIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/CIVIL/CIVIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The South Reinterprets Its ‘Lost Cause’', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The South Reinterprets Its ‘Lost Cause’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 2, 'ma