imes.com/2011/12/06/movies/caitlin-plays-herself-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Caitlin Plays Herself,” a DIY meta-production, the director Joe Swanberg plays himself and is something of a foil to the performance artist Caitlin Stainken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the opening scene of the DIY meta-production “Caitlin Plays Herself,” the performance artist Caitlin Stainken defends quick-turnaround techniques and her unfiltered aesthetic as “an attempt to make new work about something that is happening right now.” She’s less interested in the final product, she explains, than in the exploratory process, which you can see in the way she slowly massages her breasts with a washcloth: “Not everything I make is going to be good, you know?”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/filmroundup-2/filmroundup-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/filmroundup-2/filmroundup-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/filmroundup-2/filmroundup-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/filmroundup-2/filmroundup-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/arts/filmroundup-2/filmroundup-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exposing Self (and Skin)', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Caitlin Plays Herself'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo'