se of Painkiller Toradol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pathon, Jerome', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horn, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, Matt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T00:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2277f6-c399-59d9-8809-486d2f59a0ed', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2277f6-c399-59d9-8809-486d2f59a0ed'}, {'abstract': 'Computer science study in Africa shows great promise, with one Ugandan university even charting its own course in many aspects of mobile computing ahead of the developed world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/science/fertile-ground-in-africa-for-computer-science-to-take-root.html', 'snippet': 'Computer science study in Africa shows great promise, with one Ugandan university even charting its own course in many aspects of mobile computing ahead of the developed world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He might have been content simply to teach thousands of university students in Uganda how to use computers, assemble them into networks, manage them and write basic software programs. In a poor African country with one of the world’s fastest-growing populations and rising Internet use, that alone would have been an enormous achievement. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06AFRI1_SPAN/06AFRI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06AFRI1_SPAN/06AFRI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/science/06AFRI1_SPAN/06AFRI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vast and Fertile Ground in Africa for Science to Take Root', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vast and Fertile Ground in Africa for Science to Take Root', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T01:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By G. Pascal Zachary', 'person': [{'firstname': 'G.', 'middlename': 'Pascal', 'lastname': 'Zachary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaa0457e-7fa8-5476-