'headline': {'main': '2 RIM Executives Are Fired for Disturbance on Flight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 RIM Executives Are Fired For Disturbance on Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba330de-1899-530f-94c3-9715746401f3', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba330de-1899-530f-94c3-9715746401f3'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years after they came together as an ethnic professional network, members of the Indus Entrepreneurs are now bankrolling new ventures – and not just those run by people from back home.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/indian-techie-network-bankrolls-start-ups-and-not-just-by-indian-techies/', 'snippet': 'Twenty years after they came together as an ethnic professional network, members of the Indus Entrepreneurs are now bankrolling new ventures – and not just those run by people from back home.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In 1992, a handful of immigrant engineers from the Indian subcontinent who lived in the Bay Area formed a group called the Indus Entrepreneurs — or TiE — with what now seems like a quaint mission: to inspire one another to establish their own technology start-ups and cash in on the Silicon Valley dream. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Network of Indian Entrepreneurs Now Backs Start-Ups', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:37:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bfa198a-5279-5039-acba-9cfe74dbec7d', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bfa198a-5279-5039-acba-9cfe74dbec7d'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets, whose past two victories came on late drives, have led after every quarter in a game only twice this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/sports/football/jets-are-letting-games-go-to-the-last-minutes.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets, whose past two victories came on late drives, have led after every quarter in a game only twice this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, the Jets beat Washington. Or was it Buffalo? Or San Diego? Or did they lose to Denver? Their games are blending together, one barely distinguishable from the next, with every week showcasing their split personality.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/sports/JETS/JETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/sports/JETS/JETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'c