paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Police officers in Los Angeles stormed Augusta Millender’s home early one morning in 2003. They were looking for Ms. Millender’s foster son, Jerry Bowen, and for a shotgun he had used in a domestic assault.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Hear Arguments in a Police Search Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Hear Arguments In a Police Search Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/954dcc85-140f-55b2-a741-3a5da7c3d78e', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/954dcc85-140f-55b2-a741-3a5da7c3d78e'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Aviation Administration head, J. Randolph Babbitt, was charged with drunken driving in Virginia on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/business/faa-chief-on-leave-after-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Aviation Administration head, J. Randolph Babbitt, was charged with drunken driving in Virginia on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The head of the Federal Aviation Administration has been placed on leave after he was arrested over the weekend in Virginia on a drunken driving charge. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.A.A. Chief Goes on Leave After a Charge of Drunken Driving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.A.A. Chief Goes on Leave After a Charge of Drunken Driving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babbitt, J Randolph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afbc693c-2db2-5023-8788-75dd28823e0e', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afbc693c-2db2-5023-8788-75dd28823e0e'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential candidate never tells the American people what it will truly take to cut spending and balance the budget.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/opinion/missing-details-of-mr-romneys-fiscal-plan.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican presidential candidate never tells the American people what it will truly take to cut spending and balance the budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The biggest whopper in Mitt Romney’s fiscal plan comes right at the beginning of the description on his Web site: “We will level with the American people about what it will take to truly cut spending and balance our budget.” Actually, Mr. Romney never tells voters the full cost of his plan to balance the budget while cutting taxes: popular programs would be slashed or eliminated, vital state and local services would disappear, misery would be inflicted on the poor and the working class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Romney’s Missing Details', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Romney’s Missing Details', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e45c99-589d-5023-9ebc-eb8a23ad357b', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e45c99-589d-5023-9ebc-eb8a23ad357b'}, {'abstract': 'Previewing the Dec. 6 games in the UEFA Champions League.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/05/champions-league-tuesday-preview-feet-up-or-feet-to-the-fire/', 'snippet': 'Previewing the Dec. 6 games in the UEFA Champions League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday is essentially a rest day for Barcelona and three other Champions League teams. Barcelona has already won its group, so Coach Pep Guardiola will sit nearly all of his regulars in advance of this weekend’s Clásico against Real Madrid. A breather is also in order for A.C. Milan, Arsenal and APOEL, who are all safely through to the next round.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Champions League Tuesday Preview: Feet Up, or Feet to the Fire', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T02:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b355d5-f619-56c9-b51b-987d76d09de7', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b355d5-f619-56c9-b51b-987d76d09de7'}, {'abstract': 'Hotels are expected to spend $3.5 billion this year to renovate lobbies and rooms and replace sheets and pillows, among other upgrades, 30 percent more than 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/business/hotels-freshen-up-after-postponing-renovations.html', 'snippet': 'Hotels are expected to spend $3.5 billion this year to renovate lobbies and rooms and replace sheets and pillows, among other upgrades, 30 percent more than 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As hotel bookings and prices climb from their recession-era troughs, many chains are taking on the renovations they postponed when money was tight. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/business/Renovate1/Renovate1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sprucing Up at the Inn', 'kicker': 'Itineraries', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sprucing Up at the Inn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '