thousands of the nation’s poorest families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/opinion/a-recipe-for-more-homelessness.html', 'snippet': 'A provision in the Sections 8 Savings Act would undo a good bill by raising rents on hundreds of thousands of the nation’s poorest families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The draft version of the Section 8 Savings Act released earlier this year by the majority staff of the House Financial Services Committee includes several excellent proposals that would cut administrative costs for public housing authorities, allowing them to more efficiently manage the programs that subsidize rents for more than three million of the country’s poorest families. But one damaging provision that crept into the draft would undo all of that good. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/opinion/09fixes-pumpimg/09fixes-pumpimg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 399, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Recipe for More Homelessness', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Recipe for More Homelessness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Section 8 (Housing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T03:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organizat