'main': 'My Health Insurance Rates Just Went Down Again', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T12:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34b5bcf1-7343-5aa1-94d2-d42511e0c68d', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34b5bcf1-7343-5aa1-94d2-d42511e0c68d'}, {'abstract': 'A glimpse at a New York City tax bill reveals a startling new reality: the money is going to Newark. (At least for a few hours each day.)', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/newark-to-receive-billions-of-dollars-from-new-york-city-taxpayers/', 'snippet': 'A glimpse at a New York City tax bill reveals a startling new reality: the money is going to Newark. (At least for a few hours each day.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the next five years, Newark can expect to receive tens of billions of dollars intended for the New York City treasury and paid by New York City taxpayers, it has been learned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newark Receiving Billions From N.Y.C. Taxpayers (for a Few Hours Each Day)', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Property Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Finance (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20436070-10c2-5748-8efa-6359ccefb6a4', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20436070-10c2-5748-8efa-6359ccefb6a4'}, {'abstract': 'It’s tempting to think that we know much more than we did at the start of the year. But expect surprises in the final quarter of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/what-we-think-we-learn-as-an-n-f-l-season-progresses/', 'snippet': 'It’s tempting to think that we know much more than we did at the start of the year. But expect surprises in the final quarter of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tempting to think that we know much more than we did at the start of the season. As of Sunday night, we learned — or, at least, we thought we learned — that San Francisco was really good, that San Diego had gone from unlucky to just plain bad and that the Rams were again one of the league’s doormats. One day later, and maybe the Chargers are getting ready for another late-season run.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We Think We Learn as an N.F.L. Season Progresses', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T12:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'per