reet to Pakistan, is an admirable goal. But tossing in slang or colloquial expressions, a faddish buzzword or some hip lingo from a bygone era is seldom the best solution. Many colloquialisms are almost by definition clichés as well, so they can lower the tone without necessarily freshening the story.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/the-slang-patrol/', 'snippet': 'Enlivening otherwise dry or somber topics, from Wall Street to Pakistan, is an admirable goal. But tossing in slang or colloquial expressions, a faddish buzzword or some hip lingo from a bygone era is seldom the best solution. Many colloquialisms ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slang Patrol', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T13:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9c4036f-150c-5c78-8bc3-4a0166eab74c', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9c4036f-150c-5c78-8bc3-4a0166eab74c'}, {'abstract': 'Enlivening otherwise dry or somber topics, from Wall Street to Pakistan, is an admirable goal. But tossing in slang or colloquial expressions, a faddish buzzword or some hip lingo from a bygone era is seldom the best solution. Many colloquialisms are almost by definition clichés as well, so they can lower the tone without necessarily freshening the story.', 'web_url': 'https://topics.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/the-slang-patrol/', 'snippet': 'Enlivening otherwise dry or s