nyt://article/79ab4533-73bf-5d6c-b67a-46871e006065'}, {'abstract': 'Public workers retiring early in tight times, next-day mail service faces cuts, bad behavior when talking to cellphones and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/tuesday-reading-public-workers-retiring-earlier-in-tight-times/', 'snippet': 'Public workers retiring early in tight times, next-day mail service faces cuts, bad behavior when talking to cellphones and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Public Workers Retiring Earlier in Tight Times', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T14:06:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f02f75c1-a801-5368-9e25-43a7b4c562aa', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f02f75c1-a801-5368-9e25-43a7b4c562aa'}, {'abstract': 'The emir of Kuwait dissolved the parliament on Tuesday, setting the stage for elections in the Gulf nation that has thus far been spared from major protests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/world/middleeast/kuwaiti-leader-dissolves-parliament.html', 'snippet': 'The emir of Kuwait dissolved the parliament on Tuesday, setting the stage for elections in the Gulf nation that has thus far been spared from major protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The emir of Kuwait dissolved Parliament on Tuesday, setting the stage for elections in the oil-rich Persian Gulf nation that has faced some protests but has thus far been spared the revolutionary wave of the Arab Spring.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kuwaiti Leader Dissolves Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kuwait: Parliament Is Dissolved, In Preparation for Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kuwait', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabah, Sabah al-Ahmed al-Jaber al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T14:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b645c05c-1e17-5bc7-86c7-289195e5f2a3', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b645c05c-1e17-5bc7-86c7-289195e5f2a3'}, {'abstract': 'Some fans were hoping that a Van Halen reunion would be announced at a Grammy Awards nomination concert last week; other tea-leaf readers thought that the Beach Boys were getting back together. But despite cryptic promises from the Recording Academy, no announcement was made at all.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/grammys-statement-deepens-mystery-of-promised-band-reunion/', 'snippet': 'Some fans were hoping that a Van Halen reunion would be announced at a Grammy Awards nomination concert last week; other tea-leaf readers thought that the Beach Boys were getting back together. But despite cryptic promises from the Recording Acade...', 'lead_paragraph': '1:16 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grammys Statement Deepens Mystery of Promised Band Reunion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, David Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beach Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Halen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T14:25:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae3981db-497a-57ca-a6e9-3b619f5f04fc', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae3981db-497a-57ca-a6e9-3b619f5f04fc'}, {'abstract': 'Political theater isn’t policy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/policy-indifference/', 'snippet': 'Political theater isn’t policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One crucial thing you need to understand about political journalists is that with some honorable exceptions, they don’t know or care about actual policy. In a way, that makes sense — the skills needed to cultivate contacts, to get the inside scoop on what’s going on in Congressional scheming or campaign war rooms, are very different from the skills needed to interpret CBO spreadsheets. The problem, however, is that all too often political journalists mistake the theater of policy for reality (or don’t care about the difference).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Policy Indifference', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T14:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61a310be-60ce-5520-b0e7-f57afd754d3f', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61a310be-60ce-5520-b0e7-f57afd754d3f'}, {'abstract': 'European Union leaders reacted angrily on Tuesday over the timing of Standard & Poor’s downgrade threat days before a European summit meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/global/germany-calls-sp-threat-a-spur-to-action.html', 'snippet': 'European Union leaders reacted angrily on Tuesday over the timing of Standard & Poor’s downgrade threat days before a European summit meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European Union leaders reacted angrily Tuesday over the timing of a warning of a broad credit rating downgrade days before a European summit meeting. And German officials portrayed the threat by Standard & Poor’s as impetus for leaders to make a deal to rescue the euro. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/EURO/EURO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/business/EURO/EURO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '