ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e87f9e54-795c-56c5-b628-5231bc98b6cd', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e87f9e54-795c-56c5-b628-5231bc98b6cd'}, {'abstract': 'A new Manhattan restaurant will serve food in pitch darkness, to guests who are in the dark about what they’re eating.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/at-dans-le-noir-dining-in-the-dark/', 'snippet': 'A new Manhattan restaurant will serve food in pitch darkness, to guests who are in the dark about what they’re eating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This gives a whole new meaning to “mystery meat.” At Dans Le Noir, which started in Paris eight years ago and has branches in London, Barcelona and St. Petersburg, Russia, customers dine in a pitch-dark room without knowing the details of the menu. The waiters are all blind or visually impaired. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Dans Le Noir, Dining in the Dark', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garment District (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T15:54:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d20852f-46a4-5468-98a1-6af465626fb1', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d20852f-46a4-5468-98a1-6af465626fb1'}, {'abstract': 'The so-called Robin Hood tax — a tiny levy on trades in the financial markets that would take money from the banks and give it to the world’s poor — has attracted an array of influential champions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/global/micro-tax-on-financial-trades-gains-advocates.html', 'snippet': 'The so-called Robin Hood tax — a tiny levy on trades in the financial markets that would take money from the banks and give it to the world’s poor — has attracted an array of influential champions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They call it the Robin Hood tax — a tiny levy on trades in the financial markets that would take money from the banks and give it to the world’s poor. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07robinhood_cnd/07robinhood_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07robinhood_cnd/07robinhood_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07robinhood_cnd/07robinhood_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07robinhood_cnd/07robinhood_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07robinhood_cnd/07robinhood_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Tax on Financial Trades Gains Advocates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Robin Hood Tax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va