s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Lexi Thompson', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Lexi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies Professional Golf Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T16:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5bc551c-7da1-531c-bd66-b2df765a99ab', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5bc551c-7da1-531c-bd66-b2df765a99ab'}, {'abstract': 'The influence of João Havelange, who served in the International Olympic Committee for 48 years and led FIFA for 24, will be felt long after his resignation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/sports/soccer/07iht-soccer07.html', 'snippet': 'The influence of João Havelange, who served in the International Olympic Committee for 48 years and led FIFA for 24, will be felt long after his resignation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a resignation so covert it had to be virtually pried from FIFA and the International Olympic Committee, the Brazilian João Havelange appears to have finally left the scene of high-ranking governance over global sports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07ht-soccer07/07ht-soccer07-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url