t-happy sneakers created for a good cause.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/sunos-new-footprint/', 'snippet': 'A line of supercolorful, print-happy sneakers created for a good cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember what we said about printed shoes this season? Now from Suno, the out-of-Africa label designed by Max Osterweis and Erin Beatty, come five pairs of supercolorful, print-happy sneakers. “By doing this we can further our company’s mission to create jobs within Kenya, and by using excess fabric from past productions we can make darn cute shoes at a really attractive price,” Osterweis says. Darn cute is right. These classic slip-ons and lace-ups not only have names like “clustered caviar” and “bandana flower,” but their soles are made from recycled rubber, too. “And we’re helping baby elephants,” adds Beatty, noting that a portion of all of the shoes’ proceeds will go to the David Sheldrick Wildlife Trust in Kenya. Here’s to walking the walk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suno’s New Footprint', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T17:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd0b5cc8-78d7-5960-8653-1afac9e45eaa', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd0b5cc8-78d7-5960-8653-1afac9e45eaa'}, {'abstract': 'An official said that the governor and legislative leaders had agreed on the principles of a tax package, and were hoping to announce the details shortly.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/tax-deal-expected-between-cuomo-and-l