d5994-5867-5fb2-a273-8b6f55ea7940', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fad5994-5867-5fb2-a273-8b6f55ea7940'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s 2007 “prudence” principle on carbon and climate.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/gingrich-on-climate-the-2007-version/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s 2007 “prudence” principle on carbon and climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Newt Gingrich is a front runner, his foes from both parties are sifting for past statements that clash with his current agenda. On climate, there are plenty of examples of his shifts. I offer some fresh fare — a video interview I conducted with him in 2007 on climate science and policy (related to a much-discussed article of mine on the middle ground in climate policy). It had been off the grid for awhile but is restored here. Have a listen and see whether he’s changed his tune on global warming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich on Climate – The 2007 Version', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T17:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf94f48-b913-5036-97b5-e8e062f287cb', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf94f48-b913-5036-97b5-e8e062f287cb'}, {'abstract': 'What can academics who study the world of travel teach the budget traveler?', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/travel-lessons-from-the-world-of-academia/', 'snippet': 'What can academics who study the world of travel teach the budget traveler?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I’ve said it once, I’ve said it thousands of times: “Substantial Amounts of Domain Importance Heterogeneity exist in the contribution of vacations to people’s Quality of Life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Lessons From the World of Academia', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T17:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0f46611-9225-5a26-8582-c43766c00757', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0f46611-9225-5a26-8582-c43766c00757'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of Southfork Kitchen and the Globe Coffee Lounge talk about why they got into the business and what they know now that they didn’t know then.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/talking-restaurants-and-closings-one-owner-to-another/', 'snippet': 'The owners of Southfork Kitchen and the Globe Coffee Lounge talk about why they got into the business and what they know now that they didn’t know then.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Southfork Kitchen is closed for the season. It took weeks to complete the physical task, what with inventory, cleaning, canceling vendors and preserving whatever foods we could. It’s taking much longer to shut down internally. I miss the hustle and bustle. I miss the staff. Change was never my friend, especially unscheduled change, a change that brought unexpected sadness, a sense of failure and an empty freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Restaurants and Closings, One Owner to Another', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5fa614d-3dd5-5424-aae0-d6e7c1f9af86', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5fa614d-3dd5-5424-aae0-d6e7c1f9af86'}, {'abstract': 'Since the release of the first Android phone in 2008, the Android Marketplace has clocked upward of 10 billion downloads by phone and tablet owners, Google said. It took 20 months to get to the first billion app downloads. Now, a billion applications are installed every month.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/android-marketplace-clocks-10-billion-app-downloads/', 'snippet': 'Since the release of the first Android phone in 2008, the Android Marketplace has clocked upward of 10 billion downloads by phone and tablet owners, Google said. It took 20 months to get to the first billion app downloads. Now, a billion applicati...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Android continues to nip at Apple’s heels. On Tuesday, Google announced that more than 10 billion applications had been downloaded to Android devices from its mobile software shop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Android Marketplace Tops 10 Billion App Downloads', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/741c59ef-e268-5bda-b9ab-d62ea6a3c4cf', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/741c59ef-e268-5bda-b9ab-d62ea6a3c4cf'}, {'abstract': 'Hassan Nasrallah made a rare public appearance on Tuesday in Beirut, reiterating his support for Syria’s government and claiming that his group was better trained and armed than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/world/middleeast/hassan-nasrallah-hezbollah-leader-showcases-defiance-in-rare-appearance.html', 'snippet': 'Hassan Nasrallah made a rare public appearance on Tuesday in Beirut, reiterating his support for Syria’s government and claiming that his group was better trained and armed than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Hassan Nasrallah, the leader of the Shiite militant group Hezbollah, made a rare public appearance on Tuesday in Beirut, reiterating his support for Syria’s government and saying that his group was better trained and armed than ever.', 