ph': 'VILNIUS, Lithuania — The United States and two dozen other nations called for the adoption of a declaration of freedoms in cyberspace at a European security conference here on Tuesday, but the proposal stalled in the face of opposition from Russia and countries that view the Internet as a threat to their political systems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan for Online Freedoms Stalls at European Meeting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan for Online Freedoms Stalls at European Meeting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavrov, Sergey V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vilnius (Lithuania)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0623d9f2-21bb-5352-b824-d068a1232aad', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0623d9f2-21bb-5352-b824-d068a1232aad'}, {'abstract': 'While Newt Gingrich makes gains in South Carolina, Gov. Rick Perry’s support has slipped considerably in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/gingrich-holds-strong-lead-in-south-carolina-poll/', 'snippet': 'While Newt Gingrich makes gains in South Carolina, Gov. Rick Perry’s support has slipped considerably in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although the political world is laser-focused on the coming presidential contests in Iowa and New Hampshire, the South Carolina primary is looming on Jan. 21, and former Speaker Newt Gingrich now holds a commanding lead in the state, according to a new poll released Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Holds Strong Lead in South Carolina Poll', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Thee-Brenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thee-Brenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6fcb732-bff3-5eee-82f1-4d68098d5a8d', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6fcb732-bff3-5eee-82f1-4d68098d5a8d'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: 7 Bill Final', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/06/blogs/20111206-lens-7billion.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: 7 Bill Final', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: 7 Bill Final', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/blogs/20111206-lens-7billion-slide-0KFH/20111206-lens-7billion-slide-0KFH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 91, 'width': 494, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: 7 Bill Final', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b166bf31-2fb4-5d0b-99d4-937615fbc0e7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b166bf31-2fb4-5d0b-99d4-937615fbc0e7'}, {'abstract': 'The new Marni store at 1 Gansevoort Street.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/marni-store-enlivens-sleepy-stretch-of-meatpacking-district/', 'snippet': 'The new Marni store at 1 Gansevoort Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether it is because of its unusual triangular footprint or the fact that a sumptuous Yohji Yamamoto boutique occupied it previously, the new Marni space at 1 Gansevoort Street, (646) 532-6015, empty for many months, seemed destined for a special tenant. Indeed, Consuelo Castiglioni’s quirky Marni Edition designs for women and men, as well as her children’s collection, have enlivened the space and a sleepy stretch of the meatpacking district. Though there are Marni outposts in SoHo and on the Upper East Side, this is the first United States location for Marni Edition, a slightly less expensive line with prices that may still keep us waiting for Ms. Castiglioni’s H&M debut in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marni Store Enlivens Sleepy Stretch of Meatpacking District', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Mainland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mainland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62332255-e110-5917-9bc9-82c92c7d25f6', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62332255-e110-5917-9bc9-82c92c7d25f6'}, {'abstract': 'The Toronto Raptors have useful players who haven’t yet functioned as a team.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/can-the-raptors-turn-it-around/', 'snippet': 'The Toronto Raptors have useful players who haven’t yet functioned as a team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Toronto Raptors were a truly unfortunate team last season, plagued by performance deficiencies in virtually every facet of the game. Their league-worst defense turned the Air Canada Centre into a sanctuary for visiting teams, and the Raps’ offense was only slightly less hospitable. Overall, Toronto managed the fifth-worst efficiency differential in the entire N.B.A. last year, a mark truly representative of their failings in some of the game’s most crucial areas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can The Raptors Turn It Around?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bargnani, Andrea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bayless, Jerryd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colangelo, Bryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Raptors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d22e7a-6418-573d-9d74-860ca5a62316', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d22e7a-6418-573d-9d74-860ca5a62316'}, {'abstract': 'There is “evidence on both sides of the climate change argument,” the Republican presidential candidate says. In advocating action on climate change in past years, he maintains, he only meant that government should help pay for things like nuclear energy.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/on-our-radar-gingrich-on-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'There is “evidence on both sides of the climate change argument,” the Republican presidential candidate says. In advocating action on climate change in past years, he maintains, he only meant that government should help pay for things like nuclear...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years after appearing in a commercial with Representative Nancy Pelosi to warn that human-caused climate change is under way, Newt Gringrich, the Republican presidential hopeful, tells Glenn Beck that there is “evidence on both sides of the climate change argument.” [Huffington Post]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Gingrich on Climate Change', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T18:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61c5ea69-3cfe-582f-93a6-2ceedd0ccfb6', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61c5ea69-3cfe-582f-93a6-2ceedd0ccfb6'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said the plan called for a higher tax bracket for New York State’s wealthiest residents and cuts for the middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/nyregion/cuomo-and-legislative-leaders-agree-on-tax-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said the plan called for a higher tax bracket for New York State’s wealthiest residents and cuts for the middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and legislative leaders announced on Tuesday that they had reached an agreement to overhaul New York State’s income tax, creating a higher tax bracket for the highest-income residents and reducing the tax rate for millions of middle-class residents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/ALBANY/ALBANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/ALBANY/ALBANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image