vied on New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As elected officials in Albany put the final touches on a deal to raise taxes on wealthy New Yorkers, they got a vote of support from the New York City Council finance committee, which passed a resolution Tuesday morning endorsing Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s effort to institute a more progressive tax code.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Council Committee Endorses Cuomo’s Tax Plan', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T19:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36336974-e7b1-506f-9a66-dfffe0a05d6c', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36336974-e7b1-506f-9a66-dfffe0a05d6c'}, {'abstract': 'Three sectarian bombings in Afghanistan; a study shows brain damage in some N.H.L. players; and a poll shows Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney competing for the Iowa Republican caucuses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001210125/timescast--december-6-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Three sectarian bombings in Afghanistan; a study shows brain damage in some N.H.L. players; and a poll shows Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney competing for the Iowa Republican caucuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three sectarian bombings in Afghanistan; a study shows brain damage in some N.H.L. players; and a poll shows Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney competing for the Iowa Republican caucuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/multimedia/video-tc-111206/video-tc-11120