: 'A survey of likely caucusgoers shows Newt Gingrich’s support at 31 percent, with Mitt Romney and Ron Paul closely tied for second place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES – A month before the Republican nominating contest opens here, former Speaker Newt Gingrich holds a substantial lead among voters who say they are likely to participate in the Iowa caucuses, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Surges Ahead in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b031e06-10a4-5b4a-8fb8-091feab5d97c', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b031e06-10a4-5b4a-8fb8-091feab5d97c'}, {'abstract': 'December 6, 2011 - Three coordinated bombings in Afghanistan targeted Shiites celebrating a holy day, in the first such sectarian attacks since the fall of the Taliban in 2001.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000001210134/timescast--attacks-on-afghan-shiites.html', 'snippet': 'December 6, 2011 - Three coordinated bombings in Afghanistan targeted Shiites celebrating a holy day, in the first such sectarian attacks since the fall of the Taliban in 2001.', 'lead_paragraph': 'December 6, 2011 - Three coordinated bombings in Afghanistan targeted Shiites celebrating a holy day, in the first such sectarian attacks since the fall of the Taliban in 2001.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/video-tc-111206-afghanistan/video-tc-111206-afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/world/video-tc-111206-afghanistan/video-tc-111206-afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/world/video-tc-111206-afghanistan/video-tc-111206-afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/world/video-tc-111206-afghanistan/video-tc-111206-afghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | Attacks On Afghan Shiites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2702cdc1-3917-575d-a4d5-1d1e338d980a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2702cdc1-3917-575d-a4d5-1d1e338d980a'}, {'abstract': 'The movie, which will have its premiere on Thursday, follows a young woman around New York City on a quest to get people to dance with her.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/girl-walkall-day-a-q-and-a-with-the-director/', 'snippet': 'The movie, which will have its premiere on Thursday, follows a young woman around New York City on a quest to get people to dance with her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last January, Jacob Krupnick posted online a nearly eight-minute video featuring a young woman with cropped brown hair dancing with abandon on the Staten Island ferry. A few passengers gawk, but for the most part she’s ignored. The video soon went viral. Now, almost a year later, it’s a feature film called “Girl Walk//All Day.” In the last few weeks, chapters of the movie have been released on the Gothamist Web site, while the Dia Art Foundation featured several of the performers at its gala. And on Thursday the film will make its public debut at the Brooklyn Masonic Temple.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "‘Girl Walk//All Day': A Conversation With the Director", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girl Talk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c434de-034b-5eb3-8697-29484b75b147', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c434de-034b-5eb3-8697-29484b75b147'}, {'abstract': 'Rich peacock colors and jersey tees with sporty palm frond appliqués stood out the most at Jason Wu’s prefall presentation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/just-one-look-jason-wu/', 'snippet': 'Rich peacock colors and jersey tees with sporty palm frond appliqués stood out the most at Jason Wu’s prefall presentation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Charles Harper’s Birds and Words” (Ammo) by Charley Harper set the tone at Jason Wu’s prefall presentation, where rich peacock colors and jersey tees with sporty palm frond appliqués stood out most. There were day looks: a double-stripe sweater with skinny pants or leather pencil skirt; a number of knee-length dresses with pockets and belts attached. Meanwhile, dramatic evening looks inspired by a maharajah coffee table book featured lavish details like silver lead collars and floaty, handkerchief hemlines. Here, a glowing blue brocade suit. “It’s a bit darker and more sinister, which I love,” Wu says about the collection. “She totally has a raspy voice!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Jason Wu', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e951fb30-d1a5-56ca-85e5-9633ec26d3ac', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e951fb30-d1a5-56ca-85e5-9633ec26d3ac'}, {'abstract': 'A chef on the Lower East Side has a broad view of Japanese food.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/reviewing-family-recipe/', 'snippet': 'A chef on the Lower East Side has a broad view of Japanese food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What should we call the cuisine offered by chef Akiko Thurnauer at Family Recipe, an idiosyncratic little restaurant on one of the less trafficked blocks of the Lower East Side (and the subject of this week’s $25 and Under)? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Family Recipe', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:08:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/484e44b7-1fa2-5794-b3f2-80a4aa493db5', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/484e44b7-1fa2-5794-b3f2-80a4aa493db5'}, {'abstract': 'Moshe Katsav, who will begin a seven-year term for rape on Wednesday, continued to claim he was innocent of all charges the day before his incarceration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/world/middleeast/moshe-katsav-ex-israeli-president-prepares-for-jail.html', 'snippet': 'Moshe Katsav, who will begin a seven-year term for rape on Wednesday, continued to claim he was innocent of all charges the day before his incarceration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIRYAT MALACHI, Israel — A day after Moshe Katsav, Israel’s former president, turned 66, his modest home in this immigrant town was filled on Tuesday with grandchildren and well-wishers. Phones rang. Neighbors with sun-creased faces offered hugs. Rabbis in tall hats gave their blessings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'captio