, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e461b6-bb81-5a71-aad1-1ca4528190a1'}, {'abstract': 'One television crew working for Britain’s Sky News managed to report secretly from the Syrian city of Homs last week.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/british-tv-crew-reports-from-homs-a-syrian-city-under-siege/', 'snippet': 'One television crew working for Britain’s Sky News managed to report secretly from the Syrian city of Homs last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Anthony Shadid reports, “In one of the worst episodes of sectarian carnage in Syria since the uprising began nine months ago, dozens of corpses were recovered from the streets of Homs this week, some of them dismembered, decapitated and bearing signs of torture, activists and residents said Tuesday.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British TV Crew Reports From Homs, a Syrian City Under Siege', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:13:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5990eac-6064-5e04-88ec-d6d9f977bbea', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5990eac-6064-5e04-88ec-d6d9f977bbea'}, {'abstract': 'A law professor argues that televising proceedings in the Supreme Court would make its job harder. Readers are invited to respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/invitation-to-a-dialogue-cameras-in-the-supreme-court.html', 'snippet': 'A law professor argues that televising proceedings in the Supreme Court would make its job harder. Readers are invited to respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207LETTERShughes/1207LETTERShughes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207LETTERShughes/1207LETTERShughes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207LETTERShughes/1207LETTERShughes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Invitation to a Dialogue: Cameras in the Court?', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Invitation to a Dialogue: Cameras in the Court?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/51228113-352f-5503-91e6-4aa4be8e5ba2', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51228113-352f-5503-91e6-4aa4be8e5ba2'}, {'abstract': 'The Lakers’ interest in acquiring Chris Paul from the Hornets and Dwight Howard from the Magic is a hot topic of the N.B.A. offseason.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/lakers-courting-both-paul-and-howard/', 'snippet': 'The Lakers’ interest in acquiring Chris Paul from the Hornets and Dwight Howard from the Magic is a hot topic of the N.B.A. offseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could the next mega-star team, a sequel to the Miami Heat, be in the works?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lakers Courting Both Paul and Howard?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/870380a5-b0e4-5aad-801c-0b45dd554fe3', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/870380a5-b0e4-5aad-801c-0b45dd554fe3'}, {'abstract': 'Environmentalists argue that the four countries mulling construction of a dam on the river do not fully grasp the potential ecological and economic impacts.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/conclave-opens-on-the-mekongs-fate/', 'snippet': 'Environmentalists argue that the four countries mulling construction of a dam on the river do not fully grasp the potential ecological and economic impacts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Laotians call it Mae Nam Khong, the Mother of Water. The Vietnamese refer to it as Song Cuu Long, or the Nine Dragons River. The Khmer prefer Tonle Thum, or simply Great River. Whatever its name, the Mekong River is a lifeline for millions in the countries touched by its muddy waters, the world’s largest inland fishery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conclave to Open on Mekong’s Fate', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Catfish', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydroelectric Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mekong River', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Siem Reap (Cambodia)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:33:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1ab6a44-cc9e-5215-abaa-95b86d44c908', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1ab6a44-cc9e-5215-abaa-95b86d44c908'}, {'abstract': 'A sleek new restaurant on the Lower East Side, serves rich, comforting Japanese home cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/reviews/family-recipe-nyc-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'A sleek new restaurant on the Lower East Side, serves rich, comforting Japanese home cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON top of the pancake, something was writhing: a clew of bonito flakes in silent riot, the diaphanous curls lurching and shuddering. A diner whipped out her iPhone and started shooting. (“For the kids,” she explained.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07UNDER_SPAN/07UNDER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07UNDER_SPAN/07UNDER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07UNDER_SPAN/07UNDER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07UNDER_SPAN/07UNDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07UNDER_SPAN/07UNDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Family Recipe', 'kicker': '$25 and Under', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bow To Home Cooking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:34:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/663279ea-ce9a-5d75-b8a3-042ecfcf8b92', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/663279ea-ce9a-5d75-b8a3-042ecfcf8b92'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the animation race from the perspective of DreamWorks, which has two contenders for the Annies.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/meanwhile-in-the-race-involving-pandas-and-geese/', 'snippet': 'A look at the animation race from the perspective of DreamWorks, which has two contenders for the Annies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nominations for the Annies, the animation world’s Oscars, were announced on Monday, and it was a good year for DreamWorks. The studio – which won the first-ever animation Oscar, with “Shrek,” in 2002 – has two films in the running for best feature Annie, “Puss in Boots” and “Kung Fu Panda 2,” both considered Oscar hopefuls. The competition is strong though, with “Rango,” from Paramount and Nickelodeon; “Cars 2,” from Pixar; “Arthur Christmas,” from Sony, and “The Adventures of Tintin,” from Steven Spielberg’s Amblin Entertainment, all making the cut. (The complete list of nominations is here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meanwhile, in the Race Involving Pandas and Geese …', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bece31b-f115-57e4-bfd1-d42aef2d8468', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bece31b-f115-57e4-bfd1-d42aef2d8468'}, {'abstract': 'A transcription of President Obama’s speech in Osawatomie, Kan., as released by the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/politics/text-obamas-speech-in-kansas.html', 'snippet': 'A transcription of President Obama’s speech in Osawatomie, Kan., as released by the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following is a text of President Obama’s speech in Osawatomie, Kan. on Tuesday, as released by the White House:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Text: Obama’s Speech in Kansas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/02c934c7-07af-5be4-9562-7d01bc4aff0f', 'word_count': 6048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02c934c7-07af-5be4-9562-7d01bc4aff0f'}, {'abstract': 'Even if the movie is an unmitigated flop, the woman who puts on the New Year’s Eve celebration in Times Square will always have a special link to a Hollywood celebrity.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/morphing-into-hilary-swank-on-new-years-eve/', 'snippet': 'Even if the movie is an unmitigated flop, the woman who puts on the New Year’s Eve celebration in Times Square will always have a special link to a Hollywood celebrity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And now a movie review from Lori Raimondo. More in a moment about why she is supremely well qualified to assess “New Year’s Eve,” the new Garry Marshall film with a cast almost as sprawling as the crowd in Times Square — and why this may be one of the, um, nicest reviews that “New Year’s Eve” is going to get. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morphing Into Hilary Swank on New Year’s Eve', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swank, Hilary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/909b20e8-0b63-5ef1-ad43-d3f977828617', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/909b20e8-0b63-5ef1-ad43-d3f977828617'}, {'abstract': 'In style and content “The Jazz Singer” is undeniably a period piece, schmaltzy and partly calcified by some dated dialogue. But its core themes endure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/theater/reviews/mama-and-papa-versus-life-upon-the-wicked-stage.html', 'snippet': 'In style and content “The Jazz Singer” is undeniably a period piece, schmaltzy and partly calcified by some dated dialogue. But its core themes endure.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Jazz Singer” is best known as the first feature-length talkie, a 1927 cinematic artifact assigned in every introductory film class. Before it was a movie, though, it was a hit Broadway play. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': '