-android-apps-for-a-buck/', 'snippet': 'A one-day promotion from Google means you can get 10 Android apps for a dime apiece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since its appearance in March, Amazon’s Appstore has offered app giveaways to Android users, stealing some thunder from Google’s Android Market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: 10 Android Apps for a Buck', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T20:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a47d906-4b07-5cf4-a458-71fdaa1e2188', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a47d906-4b07-5cf4-a458-71fdaa1e2188'}, {'abstract': 'Infusing his speech with the type of language that has emerged in the Occupy protests, President Obama on Tuesday delivered his most pointed appeal yet for using taxes and regulations to level the economic playing field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/politics/obama-strikes-populist-chord-with-speech-in-heartland.html', 'snippet': 'Infusing his speech with the type of language that has emerged in the Occupy protests, President Obama on Tuesday delivered his most pointed appeal yet for using taxes and regulations to level the economic playing field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSAWATOMIE, Kan. — Laying out a populist argument for his re-elect