o pick on Hollywood. Who says it’s a bastion of liberal thinking that promotes lefitst ideas in movies and on television. And who claims this leads to the brainwashing of Americans, especially children, with liberal values.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Now or Have You Ever Been a Muppet?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puppets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T21:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c8b687-674b-5eab-8250-9c4d60ca7773', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c8b687-674b-5eab-8250-9c4d60ca7773'}, {'abstract': 'Designers have resurrected the turtleneck, tweaking it for the modern age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fashion/the-turtleneck-comes-out-of-its-shell.html', 'snippet': 'Designers have resurrected the turtleneck, tweaking it for the modern age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund awards last month, where the red carpet teemed with actresses and designers dressed in complicated evening numbers of varying slits and cuts, the designer Rachel Roy was covered neck to toe in a floor-length black skirt from her own collection and a sheer, flesh-colored turtleneck by Stella McCartney. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred