reparing to depart for Brooklyn at the end of the season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Here’s Your Logo, What’s Your Hurry?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T22:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/feff0109-a834-5dd8-be12-7511f352f18e', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feff0109-a834-5dd8-be12-7511f352f18e'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Colbert raises the issue of whether one’s daughter can date a corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/colberts-pushes-corporations-are-people-referendum/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Colbert raises the issue of whether one’s daughter can date a corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since August, when Mitt Romney declared that “corporations are people,” Stephen Colbert, the host of “The Colbert Report” on Comedy Central, has taken a particular interest in the matter of corporate personhood, and has argued, among other things, that parents should allow their daughters to date corporations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Co