ion has its downsides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yahoo shareholders should brace themselves again for disappointment. While the board is seeking a deal for the company, Yahoo faces limited options — all with significant downsides and risks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Limited Choices for Yahoo, Each One With Its Own Risks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALIBABA.COM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T22:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbd9d498-e640-5496-be44-5b01e2e05a32', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbd9d498-e640-5496-be44-5b01e2e05a32'}, {'abstract': 'A new panettone is made with Italian olive oil from a company that encourages the public to “adopt” an olive tree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/panettone-made-with-nudo-olive-oil.html', 'snippet': 'A new panettone is made with Italian olive oil from a company that encourages the public to “adopt” an olive tree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Panettone, the yeasty, lightly sweetened mound with a smattering of dried fruits, usually has a shelf life surpassed only by that of fruitcake. But here is a panettone that will be reduced to crumbs in a short time. Scarpato, a pastry company founded in Legnano, Italy, in 1888, is baking a not-so-traditional Christmas version, using organic olive oil in the dough. The result — moist, rich and aromatic — is excellent plain with a glass of sweet wine after dinner, or turned into French toast for breakfast. The olive oil comes from a company called Nudo, which supports a collection of small growers in Central Italy, and encourages the public to “adopt” an olive tree to help the farmers — in return for tins of oil.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF2_PANETTONE/07STUFF2a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF2_PANETTONE/07STUFF2_PANETTONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF2_PANETTONE/07STUFF2_PANETTONE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save a Tree, Eat a Panettone', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save a Tree, Eat a Panettone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olive Oil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T23:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/35739883-6050-57fa-a010-2ba225913c40', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35739883-6050-57fa-a010-2ba225913c40'}, {'abstract': 'Offal and chocolate cake, for example. Just as long as it’s assertive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/poached-fruit-flambe-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Offal and chocolate cake, for example. Just as long as it’s assertive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Typically smoky Islay Scotches may be a little more challenging to pair with food than something from Speyside, but as long as the food is assertive — perhaps briny, meaty, sharp, earthy, even sweet, and especially if it has a whiff of smoke to complement the drink — an Islay will fit right in. Oysters, smoked salmon or other smoked fish, mushrooms, barbecue, cheeses, steak, offal, game, roast chicken, Caesar salad, chocolate cake, the list goes on and on.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07PAIR_SPAN/07PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07PAIR_SPAN/07PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07PAIR_SPAN/07PAIR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07PAIR_SPAN/07PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07PAIR_SPAN/07PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pairings: Poached Fruit Flambé', 'kicker': 'Recipe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T23:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7c8bb8c-2cc2-5249-8c7b-3156c1730fd8', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c8bb8c-2cc2-5249-8c7b-3156c1730fd8'}, {'abstract': 'Brooklyn Republic Vodka has a clean aroma, bright flavor and smooth finish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/brooklyn-republic-vodka-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Brooklyn Republic Vodka has a clean aroma, bright flavor and smooth finish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its name, Brooklyn Republic Vodka, radiates the borough’s prickly pride. And though this crystalline new spirit does not begin life in Kings County, it achieves its clean aroma, bright flavor and smooth finish there. It’s the work of a troika of resident Brooklyn vodka lovers: Gary Shokin, who came to New York from Lithuania some 30 years ago; his daughter Kary Laskin, born and raised in Brooklyn; and Mark Krupkin, originally from Latvia. The vodka starts in Missouri, where it is distilled from corn mixed with organic upstate New York wheat. The overproof distillate is shipped to Brooklyn Republic’s Clinton Hill plant, where it is brought down to 80 proof with filtered Brooklyn tap water, then filtered several more times before being sealed in handsome bottles. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF3_VODKA/07STUFF3_VODKA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 315, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF3_VODKA/07STUFF3_VODKA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUFF3_VODKA/07STUFF3_VODKA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vodka That’s More Eastern Parkway Than Eastern Europe', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Eastern Parkway Than Eastern Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vodka', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T23:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5369a4-42a5-5578-a695-d689b7137177', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5369a4-42a5-5578-a695-d689b7137177'}, {'abstract': 'The panel tasted 20 single malts from Islay, smoky whiskies that demand a sense of wonder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/reviews/whisky-from-islay-scotland-spirits-of-the-times.html', 'snippet': 'The panel tasted 20 single malts from Islay, smoky whiskies that demand a sense of wonder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TASTING whiskies can be a clinical, prosaic task, nosing and assessing, jotting notes, reconsidering, lips compressed in concentration, brow furrowed. Yet, as the spirits panel tasted 20 single malts from Islay, we reminded ourselves to step back a moment, to contemplate with no small amount of awe the magic of what was in the glass. Islay demands a sense of wonder.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07SUBWINE_SPAN/07WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07SUBWINE_SPAN/07WINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07SUBWINE_SPAN/07WINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07SUBWINE_SPAN/07WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07SUBWINE_SPAN/07WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Scotland, Fog and Smoke and Mystery', 'kicker': 'Holiday Drinks | Spirits of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fog and Smoke and Mystery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Islay (Scotland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 