ragraph': 'A new test might allow some women with the earliest phase of breast cancer to forgo the most aggressive treatment, researchers are reporting this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Breast Cancer Test May Help Curtail Treatments', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-06T23:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd92063a-0696-5bbc-851c-99a8509e4542', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd92063a-0696-5bbc-851c-99a8509e4542'}, {'abstract': 'A growing army of budget-priced wines with names like Bitch and Fat Bastard have shoved their way into stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/with-rude-names-wine-stops-minding-its-manners.html', 'snippet': 'A growing army of budget-priced wines with names like Bitch and Fat Bastard have shoved their way into stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S peppery and full of fight. The tannins have grip. The nose takes no prisoners. This shiraz is a bitch.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07RUDE_SPAN/07RUDE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 271, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07RUDE_SPAN/07RUDE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 271}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07R