inal': 'By John Biggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Biggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e89de45c-4c98-5b6f-a03d-2498fdac26ce', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e89de45c-4c98-5b6f-a03d-2498fdac26ce'}, {'abstract': 'You are not stuck with Microsoft Outlook’s default version of the Navigation Pane. If you like to put the buttons in your own preferred order, you can customize it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/tip-of-the-week-changing-outlooks-navigation-pane/', 'snippet': 'You are not stuck with Microsoft Outlook’s default version of the Navigation Pane. If you like to put the buttons in your own preferred order, you can customize it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That column full of buttons (officially known as the Navigation Pane) on the left side of the Microsoft Outlook 2007 and 2010 window makes it easy to jump around among Mail, Contacts, Calendar and the other parts of the program. You are not stuck with the default version of the Navigation Pane, though, and if you like to put the buttons in your own preferred order, you can customize it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Changing Outlook’s Navigation Pane', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e30b2b0-c4c4-5d6e-b4b1-a5c86e6bb024', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e30b2b0-c4c4-5d6e-b4b1-a5c86e6bb024'}, {'abstract': 'A new lab sets Johnson & Wales apart in the culinary arts as students wash glassware, make ice, mix standard drinks and create their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/at-johnson-wales-students-mix-drinks-for-credit.html', 'snippet': 'A new lab sets Johnson & Wales apart in the culinary arts as students wash glassware, make ice, mix standard drinks and create their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the typical culinary classroom, students go through their paces slicing, dicing, butchering and baking. If they mix a martini it will probably be to relax after all the hard work.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUDENTS_SPAN/07STUDENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUDENTS_SPAN/07STUDENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUDENTS_SPAN/07STUDENTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUDENTS_SPAN/07STUDENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07STUDENTS_SPAN/07STUDENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixing Drinks for Credit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixing Drinks For Credit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Wales University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9eb8fb6-95c1-55d2-a0be-dac06e15ade1', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9eb8fb6-95c1-55d2-a0be-dac06e15ade1'}, {'abstract': 'Good-quality wines are now being sold in aluminum bottles and cans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/dining/cans-of-wine-join-the-box-set.html', 'snippet': 'Good-quality wines are now being sold in aluminum bottles and cans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FIRST, winemakers poured their vintages into bottles and corked them. Then they lost the corks and added screw tops. Then they lost the bottles and sold wine in boxes, next to beer and pretzels at supermarkets. And now, winemakers seeking some pop are canning wine.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/dining/07CANNED/07CANNED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {