ge of things pulling at their limited playtime, which, let’s hope, includes some time to build a snowman.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07TOYS_SPAN/07TOYS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07TOYS_SPAN/07TOYS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07TOYS_SPAN/07TOYS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07TOYS_SPAN/07TOYS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07TOYS_SPAN/07TOYS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Technology to Work for Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting Technology To Work for Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbie (Doll)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisher-Price Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e222c04-3d03-5621-956e-0262d4bccc36', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e222c04-3d03-5621-956e-0262d4bccc36'}, {'abstract': 'The new smartphones, sleek and fast, manage to refine and build on the options of their feature-filled predecessors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/smartphones-graduate-to-a-higher-level.html', 'snippet': 'The new smartphones, sleek and fast, manage to refine and build on the options of their feature-filled predecessors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IS that certain someone on your shopping list still carrying a sad little flip phone? Are you?', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07PHONES_SPAN/07PHONES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07PHONES_SPAN/07PHONES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 254}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07PHONES_SPAN/07PHONES_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/personaltech/07PHONES_SPAN/07PHONES_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thum