mes.com/2011/12/11/magazine/riffs-the-year-in-movies.html', 'snippet': '“Drive,” “Bridesmaids,” Chaos Cinema, movies that weren’t movies, hilarious old-person makeup and the sundry objects that were hurled off the screen in 3-D.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Bay’s “Transformers: Dark of the Moon” touched off a debate in film-blogger circles: does this assaultive approach to action-film-making signal the coming annihilation of narrative logic? Or the emergence of a visual grammar that’s 2 fast and 2 furious for fusty old movie grumps to understand? In a much-passed-around video essay, the critic Matthias Stork even gave this aesthetic a name: Chaos Cinema.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/mag-11riff-thumb/mag-11riff-thumb-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 159, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/mag-11riff-thumb/mag-11riff-thumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/mag-11riff-thumb/mag-11riff-thumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Riffs: The Year in Movies', 'kicker': 'The Hollywood Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Riffs: the Year in movies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:31:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Pappademas, Starlee Kine, Mark Blankenship, Gaby Dunn, Dan Kois, Katrina Onstad and Heather Havrilesky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pappademas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Starlee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blankenship', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Gaby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kois', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Katrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onstad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}, {'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Havrilesky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 7}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c19d0543-eacc-5559-b10d-d5ea9dca6524', 'word_count': 2464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c19d0543-eacc-5559-b10d-d5ea9dca6524'}, {'abstract': 'For screen villains, the black-and-white, “us versus them” era is over. Welcome to the uneasy age of us versus ourselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/magazine/a-o-scott-screen-villains.html', 'snippet': 'For screen villains, the black-and-white, “us versus them” era is over. Welcome to the uneasy age of us versus ourselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, one of the defining villains of the age met his end. A generation of children grew up frightened by his legend and haunted by the image of his face. More than just an evildoer, he seemed at times to be the embodiment of evil itself, the ruthless leader of a vast and shadowy network whose very principle was terror. His death was unsurprisingly violent, widely celebrated (with a few qualms expressed here and there) and also curiously anticlimactic. His diabolical charisma — the power of his name alone to inspire shudders of dread and revulsion — dissipated almost instantly. Life resumed its ordinary, anxious course.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/villains-span/villains-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/villains-span/villains-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/villains-span/villains-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/villains-span/villains-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/06/magazine/villains-span/villains-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Own Worst Enemies', 'kicker': 'The Hollywood Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Own Worst Enemies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Two Thousand Eleven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 