re, a clear plastic overlay that sits snuggly on top of an iPad and adds a keyboard to the tablet.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/touchfire-adds-a-physical-keyboard-to-ipad-screen/', 'snippet': 'A programmer and designer have teamed up to build the TouchFire, a clear plastic overlay that sits snuggly on top of an iPad and adds a keyboard to the tablet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The iPad isn’t the easiest gadget to type on. Although it comes with a large on-screen keyboard, some people find it difficult to write large amounts of text, opting instead for a physical keyboard with actual buttons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TouchFire Adds a Physical Keyboard to iPad Screen', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad2ad640-4204-5a19-909a-8736fdff1e30', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad2ad640-4204-5a19-909a-8736fdff1e30'}, {'abstract': 'Two responses to a Sunday Review article, “I’m Sorry: The Scariest Words in Politics.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/when-america-apologizes-or-doesnt-for-its-actions.html', 'snippet': 'Two responses to a Sunday Review article, “I’m Sorry: The Scariest Words in Politics.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'