': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/NBASKEDsilo/NBASKEDsilo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Schedule a Cram Course for Teams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Schedule Is Cram Course for Teams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f25b7778-7349-5d34-a95e-f63c45cf20b8', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f25b7778-7349-5d34-a95e-f63c45cf20b8'}, {'abstract': 'Even when a study calculated presidential life expectancy by subtracting two days of life for every day in office, it found that presidents who died of natural causes lived longer than predicted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/07/health/presidential-aging.html', 'snippet': 'Even when a study calculated presidential life expectancy by subtracting two days of life for every day in office, it found that presidents who died of natural causes lived longer than predicted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even when a study calculated presidential life expectancy by subtracting two days of life for every day in office, it found that presidents who died of natural causes lived longer than predicted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidential Aging Doesn’t Cut Life Short', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e90615d9-81ee-52d8-86f7-fc60b307bfcc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e90615d9-81ee-52d8-86f7-fc60b307bfcc'}, {'abstract': 'When thousands of Defense Department workers moved to the Mark Center in Alexandria, Va., some of their neighbors started feeling less safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/realestate/commercial/a-defense-dept-complex-in-virginia-raises-safety-concerns.html', 'snippet': 'When thousands of Defense Department workers moved to the Mark Center in Alexandria, Va., some of their neighbors started feeling less safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALEXANDRIA, Va. — On a recent Friday afternoon, employees trickled out of two new office buildings here; some waited at bus stops, while others retrieved cars from a sprawling above-ground garage. Traffic leaving the office complex and turning onto public streets was light.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/Mark/Mark-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/business/Mark/Mark-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/Mark/Mark-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Defense Department in Their Midst', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Defense Department in Their Midst', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEXANDRIA (VA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a835334a-8520-5345-bfc9-bd80e0472dac', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a835334a-8520-5345-bfc9-bd80e0472dac'}, {'abstract': 'The Virginia Court of Appeals on Tuesday exonerated Thomas Haynesworth, who was convicted in a series of sexual assaults in 1984.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/virginia-thomas-haynesworth-exonerated-after-27-years-in-jail.html', 'snippet': 'The Virginia Court of Appeals on Tuesday exonerated Thomas Haynesworth, who was convicted in a series of sexual assaults in 1984.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Virginia Court of Appeals on Tuesday exonerated a man convicted in a series of sexual assaults in 1984. DNA evidence showed that the man,  Thomas Haynesworth, could not have committed the crimes in which such evidence had been preserved, and it pointed to another man. Gov. Bob McDonnell released Mr. Haynesworth on parole in March, but Mr. Haynesworth petitioned for full exoneration. Prosecutors in the counties where the assaults occurred supported his effort, as did the commonwealth’s attorney general, Kenneth T. Cuccinelli. The Court of Appeals initially heard the appeal and then asked for further briefs. Shawn Armbrust, executive director of the Mid-Atlantic Innocence Project, said, “After serving nearly 27 years for crimes that he didn’t commit, Mr. Haynesworth has had to register as a sex offender and abide by degrading conditions while the Court of Appeals took nearly nine months to conclude that the attorney general and the prosecutors were right that Mr. Haynesworth didn’t commit these crimes.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: Man Jailed for 27 Years Is Exonerated', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia: Man Jailed For 27 Years Is Exonerated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Innocence Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T00:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e03830-6bec-5b55-994f-d15705f89a5a', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e03830-6bec-5b55-994f-d15705f89a5a'}, {'abstract': 'Immigration officials’ abrupt reversal of temporary leave could affect 1,000 Indonesians who had fled to the United States, an ally said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/nyregion/us-tells-72-indonesians-in-new-jersey-to-leave.html', 'snippet': 'Immigration officials’ abrupt reversal of temporary leave could affect 1,000 Indonesians who had fled to the United States, an ally said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, a community of Indonesians in central New Jersey was spared deportation after a Protestant pastor brokered an unusual agreement with immigration authorities that allowed them to stay in the country temporarily. The agreement was clear: The Indonesians would be able to stay and work, but the permission could be rescinded at any moment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/SUB-IMMIG/SUB-IMMIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/SUB-IMMIG/SUB-IMMIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/SUB-IMMIG/SUB-IMMIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/SUB-IMMIG/SUB-IMMIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'widt