 spent nuclear fuel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — United States and South Korean negotiators on Tuesday resumed their low-key but highly sensitive talks on whether South Korea should be allowed to do what Washington has tried to stop North Korea from doing: enrich uranium and reprocess spent nuclear fuel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and South Korea Renew Talks on Nuclear Technology', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and South Korea Renew Talks on Nuclear Technology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65b538d4-fbfa-50eb-8ea6-223a0cb65abd', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65b538d4-fbfa-50eb-8ea6-223a0cb65abd'}, {'abstract': 'A pledge by Merck to invest $1.5 billion in research and development in China suggests that the pharmaceutical industry’s center of gravity is shifting eastward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/chinas-allure-in-drug-research.html', 'snippet': 'A pledge by Merck to invest $1.5 billion in research and development in China suggests that the pharmaceutical industry’s center of gravity is shifting eastward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drug research tends to follow spending. Take Merck’s pledge on Tuesday to invest $1.5 billion in research and development in China over five years. Citizens of emerging economies are growing wealthier and living longer, while the fiscal health of their governments is robust. Merck’s step suggests that the pharmaceutical industry’s center of gravity is shifting eastward accordingly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/VIEWS/VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Allure in Drug Research', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Allure in Drug Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merck & Company Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and George Hay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d092a14f-6659-5cbf-aa8d-f0e31402a742', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d092a14f-6659-5cbf-aa8d-f0e31402a742'}, {'abstract': 'The architect of the attack on Pearl Harbor had been against going to war with the United States at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/a-reluctant-enemy.html', 'snippet': 'The architect of the attack on Pearl Harbor had been against going to war with the United States at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'San Francisco', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207OPEDweberWEB/1207OPEDweberWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207OPEDweberWEB/1207OPEDweberWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/opinion/1207OPEDweberWEB/1207OPEDweberWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reluctant Enemy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Reluctant Enemy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pearl Harbor (Hawaii)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian W. Toll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Toll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0d6ddd-8900-5392-bf3f-83291c7e4dfb', 'word_count': 1759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0d6ddd-8900-5392-bf3f-83291c7e4dfb'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors in Akron will file charges accusing Richard Beasley, 52, of the murders of three men who were lured to their deaths through a fake Craigslist advertisement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/ohio-charges-planned-in-craigslist-killings.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors in Akron will file charges accusing Richard Beasley, 52, of the murders of three men who were lured to their deaths through a fake Craigslist advertisement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prosecutors in Akron will file charges accusing Richard Beasley, 52, of the murders of three men who were lured to their deaths through a fake Craigslist advertisement, a spokeswoman for Sherri Bevan Walsh, the Summit County prosecutor, said on Tuesday, adding that Ms. Walsh would seek the death penalty. Mr. Beasley, who was arrested this month on other charges and is being held without bail, will also be charged with the attempted murder of Scott Davis, 48, of South Carolina, who responded to the advertisement but escaped after being shot in the arm. The Craigslist advertisement offered $300 a week, a trailer to live in and a stocked fishing pond for someone who would serve as a caretaker on a farm near Caldwell, in Noble County. Brogan Rafferty, 16, was also charged this month in connection with the murders. A Noble County judge will decide next week whether Mr. Rafferty will be tried as an adult. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio: Charges Planned in Craigslist Killings', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio: Charges Planned In Craigslist Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Craigslist', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rafferty, Brogan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:19:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/12ffa618-179f-5373-8c05-11b2eda87860', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12ffa618-179f-5373-8c05-11b2eda87860'}, {'abstract': 'J. Randolph Babbitt was arrested and accused of drunken driving over the weekend, and aviation experts said he was unlikely to be permanently replaced anytime soon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/babbitt-quits-as-faa-chief-after-drunken-driving-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'J. Randolph Babbitt was arrested and accused of drunken driving over the weekend, and aviation experts said he was unlikely to be permanently replaced anytime soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The chief of the Federal Aviation Administration, J. Randolph Babbitt, resigned on Tuesday after being arrested and accused of drunken driving over the weekend. Aviation experts said he was unlikely to be permanently replaced soon, raising concerns about the agency’s progress in modernizing air traffic control, maintaining vigilance on safety and completing a recent reorganization. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.A.A. Chief Leaves Job After Arrest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.A.A. Chief Leaves Job After Arrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babbitt, J Randolph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac32f42-3ada-586b-ab86-3b8bf9511385', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac32f42-3ada-586b-ab86-3b8bf9511385'}, {'abstract': 'As the ballots are counted in the first round of free parliamentary elections since the ouster of President Hosni Mubarak, questions keep coming up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/friedman-egypt-the-beginning-or-the-end.html', 'snippet': 'As the ballots are counted in the first round of free parliamentary elections since the ouster of President Hosni Mubarak, questions keep coming up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fact that the Muslim Brotherhood and the even more fundamentalist Salafist Nour Party have garnered some 65 percent of the votes in the first round of Egypt’s free parliamentary elections since the ouster of President Hosni Mubarak should hardly come as a surprise. Given the way that the military regimes in the Arab world decimated all independent secular political parties over the last 50 years, there is little chance of any Arab country going from Mubarak to Jefferson without going through some Khomeini. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt, the Beginning or the End?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt, the Beginning Or the End?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:22:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/056da8a9-7dbf-5dde-946d-ae741191b9dc', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/056da8a9-7dbf-5dde-946d-ae741191b9dc'}, {'abstract': 'The former senator has been an advocate for better nutrition for more than half a century.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/the-wisdom-of-george-mcgovern/', 'snippet': 'The former senator has been an advocate for better nutrition for more than half a century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George McGovern’s impact on food policy could have been greater, but not through more effort on his part. The 1972 presidential candidate, now 89, was a bomber pilot at the end of World War II when the decision was made to distribute remaining medicine and food to Europeans before heading home. “We were feeding our former enemies two days after bombing them,” he told me over breakfast last week, two days before falling and being hospitalized. “It was an unprecedented gesture of good will.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wisdom of George McGovern', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/551ec6b1-3e2e-567b-b1c7-c5ab9fd2846e', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/551ec6b1-3e2e-567b-b1c7-c5ab9fd2846e'}, {'abstract': 'There are very few folk singer-activist-physicians who are also world-class athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/sports/soccer/george-vecsey-remembers-brazils-socrates.html', 'snippet': 'There are very few folk singer-activist-physicians who are also world-class athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sócrates is dead, at 57. He taught me to love an entire sport, and that is no small thing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/VECSEY2/VECSEY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 448, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/VECSEY2/VECSEY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'h