 the agency’s bungled response to the storm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Council Hears Transit Plans for a Blizzard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transit Chief Details Plans For Handling Next Blizzard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prendergast, Thomas F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Transit Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Stelloh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelloh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e06de14-901d-5518-a3f0-535f3e7166f0', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e06de14-901d-5518-a3f0-535f3e7166f0'}, {'abstract': 'The phrase lives on, and 70 years have not dimmed the meaning and memory of that day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/remembering-pearl-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'The phrase lives on, and 70 years have not dimmed the meaning and memory of that day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only a few days after the attack in December 1941 that the phrase “Remember Pearl Harbor” first appeared in The New York Times. It took barely a week for Hollywood to register it as a movie title. Today that film is justly forgotten. The phrase lives on, and 70 years have not dimmed the meaning and memory of that day. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Pearl Harbor', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering Pearl Harbor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pearl Harbor (Hawaii)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc06f31e-f283-50ba-9cb1-8f3ce38f4bcb', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc06f31e-f283-50ba-9cb1-8f3ce38f4bcb'}, {'abstract': 'The latest plan from Germany and France to secure the euro could make things worse and exacerbate Europe’s fundamental problem: lack of growth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/the-wrong-fix.html', 'snippet': 'The latest plan from Germany and France to secure the euro could make things worse and exacerbate Europe’s fundamental problem: lack of growth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany and President Nicolas Sarkozy of France issued an ultimatum on Monday demanding that all 17 nations using the euro agree to a change in European treaties that would force them to move toward balanced budgets or face sanctions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Fix', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Wrong Fix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '