r-criticism-for-insults-on-facebook.html', 'snippet': 'Politicians and others condemned a group on Facebook whose members, claiming to be New York City police officers, derided the annual West Indian American Day Parade and its participants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politicians and officials criticized the New York Police Department on Tuesday and called for investigations after the release of comments on Facebook in which users claiming to be officers heaped scorn on revelers at the annual West Indian American Day Parade in Brooklyn. But, despite repeated requests, one person refused to comment: the police commissioner, Raymond W. Kelly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Insults Lead to Calls for Inquiries of N.Y.C. Police', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online Insults Lead to Calls For Inquiries Of Officers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Indian-American Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Indian-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T01:52:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Glaberson and Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaberson', 'qualifier': None, '