ment_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/600ad6b4-9230-5b2b-9949-e8dc92ff6bc7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/600ad6b4-9230-5b2b-9949-e8dc92ff6bc7'}, {'abstract': 'The Civil War through the eyes of enslaved children, in audio recordings made when they were adults.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/caught-out-of-time/', 'snippet': 'The Civil War through the eyes of enslaved children, in audio recordings made when they were adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred and fifty years after the Civil War, historians have the benefit of a perspective not accessible in earlier remembrances. One interesting angle is to look at older histories of the war, tracing its place in our national consciousness and rediscovering details that take on new relevance today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caught Out of Time', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karenna Gore Schiff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karenna', 'middlename': 'Gore', 'lastname': 'Schiff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b24557bc-6e70-56ea-a8c0-395c360b1656', 'word_count': 2362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b24557bc-6e70-56ea-a8c0-395c360b1656'}, {'abstract': 'Yani Tseng, 22, is the world’s No. 1 female golfer, a one-name celebrity in Taiwan. But in the United States, a majority of golfers are faint stars, outshined by football, basketball and baseball players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/sports/golf/yani-tseng-a-golf-celebrity-in-taiwan-finds-less-fanfare-in-america.html', 'snippet': 'Yani Tseng, 22, is the world’s No. 1 female golfer, a one-name celebrity in Taiwan. But in the United States, a majority of golfers are faint stars, outshined by football, basketball and baseball players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — It is the all-American girl’s study as conceived by a Hollywood set director. In addition to her growing collection of trophies, Yani Tseng has displayed two dozen Starbucks mugs from all over the world, an ad for a local pizzeria and a plush Angry Bird scowling from a loving cup. Only the 8 ½-by-11 certificate noting Tseng’s completion of a Level 4 English class hints at her deepest roots. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07tseng-1/07tseng-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07tseng-1/07tseng-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07tseng-1/07tseng-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07tseng-1/07tseng-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/07tseng-1/07tseng-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrated in Asia, Little Known in America', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrated in Asia, Little Known in America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tseng, Yani', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ladies Professional Golf Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2416d633-e246-54d2-b735-6df5950474d2', 'word_count': 1615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2416d633-e246-54d2-b735-6df5950474d2'}, {'abstract': 'Emoji, the more elaborate cousins of emoticons, are available to in-the-know smartphone owners via apps, but Apple’s update to its iPhone software paves the way for them to go mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/technology/emoji-in-iphones-signals-a-shot-at-mainstream-success.html', 'snippet': 'Emoji, the more elaborate cousins of emoticons, are available to in-the-know smartphone owners via apps, but Apple’s update to its iPhone software paves the way for them to go mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say you wanted to invite a friend to happy hour. You could send a simple text message, but that would be boring. Instead, why not send a cartoony picture of two clinking beer mugs? ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/subjpEMOJI2/subjpEMOJI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/business/subjpEMOJI2/subjpEMOJI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/subjpEMOJI2/subjpEMOJI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 929, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/subjpEMOJI2/subjpEMOJI2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/business/subjpEMOJI2/subjpEMOJI2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whimsical Texting Icons Get a Shot at Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whimsical Text Icons Get a Shot At Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emojis and Emoticons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ee21e6-5a29-5fd3-9068-bd708af9c644', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ee21e6-5a29-5fd3-9068-bd708af9c644'}, {'abstract': 'In expanding its publishing ambitions, the online retailer is acquiring more than 450 titles from Marshall Cavendish Children’s Books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/amazon-publishing-push-grows-to-childrens-books.html', 'snippet': 'In expanding its publishing ambitions, the online retailer is acquiring more than 450 titles from Marshall Cavendish Children’s Books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon expanded its publishing ambitions on Tuesday by acquiring more than 450 titles from Marshall Cavendish Children’s Books, a niche publisher.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Publishing Push Grows to Children’s Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazon Publishing Push Grows to Children’s Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:07:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5982d70-fef3-5537-90eb-a9711ca451d8', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5982d70-fef3-5537-90eb-a9711ca451d8'}, {'abstract': 'Republican presidential candidates have dismissed President Obama’s foreign policy as too soft, especially when it comes to the Mideast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/us/politics/obama-foreign-policy-a-republican-target.html', 'snippet': 'Republican presidential candidates have dismissed President Obama’s foreign policy as too soft, especially when it comes to the Mideast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A small but revealing episode unfolded in the closing minutes of the last Republican presidential debate. After the candidates were asked to name the national security issue they most worry about, which had not yet been discussed, Rick Santorum cited radical Islamists in Central and South America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Candidates Aim at Obama Foreign Policy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Foreign Policy, G.O.P. Candidates Search for Obama’s Vulnerable Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4379bd28-1fd2-5b83-b30c-78003b2a288c', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4379bd28-1fd2-5b83-b30c-78003b2a288c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Friedman was a ubiquitous presence in and around New York theaters in the 1950s and 1960s', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/theater/leo-friedman-photographer-of-broadway-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Friedman was a ubiquitous presence in and around New York theaters in the 1950s and 1960s', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leo Friedman, whose photograph of an ebullient Carol Lawrence and Larry Kert as lovebirds chasing down a Manhattan street became the enduring emblem of the musical “West Side Story” and the signature image of a career spent taking pictures of actors in action, died on Friday at his home in Las Vegas. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/FRIEDMAN1-obit/FRIEDMAN1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/FRIEDMAN1-obit/FRIEDMAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/FRIEDMAN1-obit/FRIEDMAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leo Friedman, Photographer of Broadway’s Glamour Years, Dies at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leo Friedman, Photographer of Broadway’s Glamour Years, Is Dead at 92', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Leo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4abb5673-cdc4-50e2-a68e-568465bd92c1', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4abb5673-cdc4-50e2-a68e-568465bd92c1'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the Lefevre family traveled to New York from Canada when Mathieu Lefevre, 30, was killed in a hit-and-run accident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/nyregion/after-a-son-is-killed-facing-a-police-rigmarole.html', 'snippet': 'Members of the Lefevre family traveled to New York from Canada when Mathieu Lefevre, 30, was killed in a hit-and-run accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lefevres — mother, father and one of their surviving sons — took the first flight to New York, spent the night with a friend, and the next morning went directly to the city morgue on Winthrop Street in Brooklyn. The second of the Lefevre sons, Mathieu, 30, had been run over by a truck two days earlier, just after midnight on Oct. 19, while he was biking home to Williamsburg. The truck did not stop.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/ABOUT2/ABOUT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/ABOUT2/ABOUT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/ABOUT2/ABOUT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Son Is Killed, Facing a Police Runaround', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Son Is Killed, Facing a Police Runaround', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24df3515-4f8e-5aa3-83b5-ddf788495477', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24df3515-4f8e-5aa3-83b5-ddf788495477'}, {'abstract': 'The winning lottery numbers for Dec. 6, 2011, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The winning lottery numbers for Dec. 6, 2011, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dec. 6, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:20:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cd528b7-4df2-5d46-bd51-87fcbe295da6', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cd528b7-4df2-5d46-bd51-87fcbe295da6'}, {'abstract': 'Two freshmen are competing to be vice chairman of the Senate Republican Conference.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/g-o-p-leadership-job-is-contested/', 'snippet': 'Two freshmen are competing to be vice chairman of the Senate Republican Conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fifth-ranking leadership position for Congressional Republicans is up for grabs, setting the stage for a battle between two freshmen senators. Senator Roy D. Blunt of Missouri announced on Tuesday that he would compete against Senator Ron Johnson of Wisconsin for the job of vice chairman of the Senate Republican Conference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Leadership Job Is Contested', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7c20b7-c2ca-544b-a700-3de77adbb7b8', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7c20b7-c2ca-544b-a700-3de77adbb7b8'}, {'abstract': 'The House and Senate could tighten laws on illegal trades to improve the public’s faith following a report by CBS on stock bets that were made by some members of Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/congress-considers-new-limits-on-insider-trading.html', 'snippet': 'The House and Senate could tighten laws on illegal trades to improve the public’s faith following a report by CBS on stock bets that were made by some members of Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats and Republicans on the House Financial Services Committee on Tuesday advocated new restrictions on insider trading to help lift waning public trust in Congress.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Discusses Enacting Stricter Insider-Trading Laws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Discusses Enacting Stricter Insider-Trading Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43720644-ceeb-51c5-839c-3340c66168d9', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43720644-ceeb-51c5-839c-3340c66168d9'}, {'abstract': 'Magic Johnson, part of a group looking to purchase the team, would contribute an enormous local profile, enthusiasm, millions of dollars and business experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/sports/baseball/among-potential-dodgers-bidders-magic-johnson-brings-more-than-name-recognition.html', 'snippet': 'Magic Johnson, part of a group looking to purchase the team, would contribute an enormous local profile, enthusiasm, millions of dollars and business experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a moment, imagine Magic Johnson, the symbol of Showtime, as a part-owner and the public face of the Los Angeles Dodgers. He stands outside Dodger Stadium greeting fans numbed by the Frank McCourt era. He sits by the Dodgers’ dugout listening to fans telling him how to improve the team. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YDODGERS/YDODGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YDODGERS/YDODGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YDODGERS/YDODGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnson Becomes Face, and So Much More, of Bid for the Dodgers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Johnson Becomes Face, And So Much More, Of Bid for the Dodgers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Earvin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e41120da-ea1a-572e-9e19-76c4db310c02', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e41120da-ea1a-572e-9e19-76c4db310c02'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s new and supposedly fairer tax structure will bring in new revenue, but it will still leave the state with a gap of about $2 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion/albanys-tax-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s new and supposedly fairer tax structure will bring in new revenue, but it will still leave the state with a gap of about $2 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than a month before New York’s so-called millionaires’ tax is set to expire, Gov. Andrew Cuomo has managed to convince Republican legislators to agree to a new, supposedly fairer tax structure. It is expected to bring in about $2 billion in new revenue — or about half of the $4 billion that would have come from extending the income tax surcharge for New York’s wealthier residents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albany’s Tax Deal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Albany’s Tax Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f650ca4-bdda-53fc-8d87-897be7ebe19f', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f650ca4-bdda-53fc-8d87-897be7ebe19f'}, {'abstract': 'Brachytherapy can be completed in a week, but it may not be as effective or safe as conventional radiation treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/health/research/study-questions-brachytherapy-a-breast-cancer-radiation-treatment.html', 'snippet': 'Brachytherapy can be completed in a week, but it may not be as effective or safe as conventional radiation treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A faster form of radiation therapy that is becoming increasingly popular for women with early-stage breast cancer may not be as effective and safe as conventional radiation treatment, according to a study being presented on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Raises Concerns About a Faster Radiation Therapy for Breast Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Raises Concerns About a Faster Radiation Therapy for Breast Cancer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Catheters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'M