wa, but two-thirds remain open to changing their mi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll poll found that Newt Gingrich is rated more favorably than the other candidates among voters who say they are likely to attend the Republican caucuses in Iowa, but two-thirds remain open to changing their minds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa Poll: The Candidates and the Issues', 'kicker': 'THE NEW YORK TIMES/CBS NEWS POLL', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d6d6c5d1-20b0-5654-9884-0f9c7c1094b0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d6d6c5d1-20b0-5654-9884-0f9c7c1094b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Freelancers Union is working to provide protections for “contingent” workers that go beyond just health care.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/06/safety-nets-for-freelancers/', 'snippet': 'The Freelancers Union is working to provide protections for “contingent” workers that go beyond just health care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a follow-up to Friday’s column, “Health Care for a Changing Work Force.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safety Nets for Freelancers', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ebc2779-540c-5fd7-b3af-30fd679549f9', 'word_count': 1640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ebc2779-540c-5fd7-b3af-30fd679549f9'}, {'abstract': 'At some of New York City’s highest-rated public elementary schools, recess is now a time for lunchtime clubs that focus on the extras, like music, arts and computer science. \xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/nyregion/in-high-rated-new-york-city-public-schools-enrichment-instead-of-recess.html', 'snippet': 'At some of New York City’s highest-rated public elementary schools, recess is now a time for lunchtime clubs that focus on the extras, like music, arts and computer science. \xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the art room at P.S. 188 in Bayside, Queens, a group of 9-year-olds was busily putting the finishing touches on an enormous poster for the fourth-grade play. Its topic: saving the Earth. Down the hall in the music room, beneath portraits of Mozart and Bach, classmates were breaking into a spirited rendition of “Hear Those Bells” on fluorescent-colored recorders. Cheerleaders in the gym were perfecting a victory chant, jumping, twisting and stamping their feet. And in the library, children in a Suzuki violin class were toiling away at “Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star,” while their music teacher, a professional violist from Iceland, coached them “to stand straight and tall.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/sub-sb-recess1/sub-sb-recess1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/sub-sb-recess1/sub-sb-recess1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/sub-sb-recess1/sub-sb-recess1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/sub-sb-recess1/sub-sb-recess1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/nyregion/sub-sb-recess1/sub-sb-recess1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Top Public Schools, the Arts Replace Recess', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Top Public Schools, The Arts Replace Recess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Education', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kyle Spencer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kyle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spencer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c3e31f-f8c7-5aa6-8357-e5cf5fbc7514', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c3e31f-f8c7-5aa6-8357-e5cf5fbc7514'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Bettman, the N.H.L. commissioner, defended the physical nature of professional hockey and cautioned against connecting any dots between the brain disease C.T.E. and fighting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/sports/hockey/nhls-bettman-says-the-fans-like-the-level-of-physicality.html', 'snippet': 'Gary Bettman, the N.H.L. commissioner, defended the physical nature of professional hockey and cautioned against connecting any dots between the brain disease C.T.E. and fighting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PEBBLE BEACH, Calif. — The N.H.L. board of directors met for three and a half hours Tuesday and never broached the subject of fighting, Commissioner Gary Bettman said. Fighting is an aspect of the game that has come under scrutiny by others in the wake of the recent deaths of three of the game’s enforcers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YREACT/YREACT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YREACT/YREACT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/sports/YREACT/YREACT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bettman: Fans ‘Like the Level of Physicality’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bettman: Fans ‘Like the Level of Physicality’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boogaard, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T02:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f318265-e64b-5ef0-9859-eff45742e175', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f318265-e64b-5ef0-9859-eff45742e175'}, {'abstract': 'Marketers are buying commercial time during video programming, leading to a prediction that global TV ads will increase 6.7 percent next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/business/media/television-gets-its-moment-in-the-sun.html', 'snippet': 'Marketers are buying commercial time during video programming, leading to a prediction that global TV ads will increase 6.7 percent next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS week, about 2,000 people are attending an annual event known as the UBS global media and communications conference. Based on the presentations so far, perhaps it ought to be renamed the global television and video festival.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima