 2,300 Americans were killed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 7, 1941 | Japan Attacks Pearl Harbor', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:08:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e621176-11ec-59a2-8a81-a4acc02842c6', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e621176-11ec-59a2-8a81-a4acc02842c6'}, {'abstract': 'Why is it useful for astronomers to have made this new finding?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/found-biggest-black-holes-ever/', 'snippet': 'Why is it useful for astronomers to have made this new finding?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO did not believe in the existence of black holes?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Found: Biggest Black Holes Ever', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf4d57e-b74f-5cbd-b4e6-4bdbab5f0bb4', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf4d57e-b74f-5cbd-b4e6-4bdbab5f0bb4'}, {'abstract': 'Given the total number of students served by a program, the percentage who are female, and the percentage who go on to four-year colleges, can you find the number of girls served by the program who go on to four-year colleges?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/test-yourself-math-dec-7-2011/', 'snippet': 'Given the total number of students served by a program, the percentage who are female, and the percentage who go on to four-year colleges, can you find the number of girls served by the program who go on to four-year colleges?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “Learning to Play the Game to Get Into College.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Dec. 7, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25554486-7ecf-5a76-94cc-d7a6344730d3', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25554486-7ecf-5a76-94cc-d7a6344730d3'}, {'abstract': 'Web hosts remove “offensive” information and more, promptly, study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/chilling-impact-of-indias-april-internet-rules/', 'snippet': 'Web hosts remove “offensive” information and more, promptly, study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kapil Sibal’s demand that Internet companies self-censor users’ content is just the latest move by the Indian government to restrict information on Facebook and other social media Web sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Chilling’ Impact of India’s April Internet Rules', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b272682-22ca-518e-8aab-36958b273429', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b272682-22ca-518e-8aab-36958b273429'}, {'abstract': 'Bombers struck Shiite religious observances on Tuesday, in the first such sectarian attacks since the fall of the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/asia/rare-attacks-on-shiites-kill-scores-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Bombers struck Shiite religious observances on Tuesday, in the first such sectarian attacks since the fall of the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A Pakistan-based extremist group claimed responsibility for a series of coordinated bombings aimed at Afghan Shiites on Tuesday, in what many feared was an attempt to further destabilize Afghanistan by adding a new dimension of strife to a country that, though battered by a decade of war, has been free of sectarian conflict. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/world/asia/AFGHAN/AFGHAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/world/asia/AFGHAN/AFGHAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/world/asia/AFGHAN/AFGHAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/world/asia/AFGHAN/AFGHAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/world/asia/AFGHAN/AFGHAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Attacks on Shiites Kill Scores in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rare Attacks on Shiites Kill Scores in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Jhangvi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:50:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49f16891-1eec-5ff5-ab7a-79a1f768d83a', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49f16891-1eec-5ff5-ab7a-79a1f768d83a'}, {'abstract': 'In capitalism, failure is as important as success. But market rules don’t apply to the biggest banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/magazine/adam-davidson-wild-west-of-finance.html', 'snippet': 'In capitalism, failure is as important as success. But market rules don’t apply to the biggest banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Human beings, at heart, are wild animals in love with the thrill of the hunt. I can prove it merely by pointing to the existence of the exchange-traded fund FAZ, which one friend calls “day trader’s crack.” For most of us, the stock market has been moving far too much, far too quickly. For those who buy FAZ, though, that speed is not fast enough.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/magazine/11economy3/11economy3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/magazine/11economy3/11economy3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/magazine/11economy3/11economy3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/magazine/11economy3/11economy3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/magazine/11economy3/11economy3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wild West of Finance', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Not Technically an Oligopoly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T09:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21806b6d-1a8f-5519-b040-24e658467f95', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21806b6d-1a8f-5519-b040-24e658467f95'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian officials are clinging to the claim that they are besieged by a foreign plot, not confronted by a true uprising of the people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/middleeast/syria-bashar-assad-officials-dismiss-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Syrian officials are clinging to the claim that they are besieged by a foreign plot, not confronted by a true uprising of the people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAMASCUS, Syria — During his most recent news conference, Foreign Minister Walid al-Moallem interrupted the flow of questions by waving a small white piece of paper indicating that he had important news. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/world/syria/s