ew Jersey entrance to the Lincoln Tunnel, but this year’s version of the atheist billboard has failed to generate much of a fight so far.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/this-year-atheists-billboard-draws-yawns/', 'snippet': 'Last Christmas season, a billboard war erupted between atheists and Roman Catholics at the New Jersey entrance to the Lincoln Tunnel, but this year’s version of the atheist billboard has failed to generate much of a fight so far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly $40,000 was spent during the last Christmas season on a billboard war between atheists and Roman Catholics at the New Jersey entrance to the Lincoln Tunnel. But so far, this year’s version of the atheist billboard has failed to generate much of a fight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Christmas, Atheists’ Billboard Tries a Softer Tack', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ATHEISTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic League for Religious and Civil Rights', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T12:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15325a3-a386-5350-82ff-6e5704968e79', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15325a3-a386-5350-82ff-6e5704968e79'}, {'abstract': 'Saying debt is bad because of the recent meltdown is like saying fire is bad because of the Chicago fire.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/why-i-swore-off-debt-for-a-while/', 'snippet': 'Saying debt is bad because of the recent meltdown is like saying fire is bad because of the Chicago fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Breakups are never pretty. It was September 2008, and the economy, the stock market, real estate, and my business were all crashing (as did many businesses). Like an engineer figuring out how much oxygen is left in a mine tunnel after a collapse, I turned quickly to cash analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Swore Off Debt (for a While)', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6588a7b7-4932-5569-99ae-2eca01e4812f', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6588a7b7-4932-5569-99ae-2eca01e4812f'}, {'abstract': 'Top American and Chinese military officials began an annual review of major issues in Beijing on Wednesday pledging to seek greater cooperation and trust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/asia/us-and-china-meet-in-annual-military-review.html', 'snippet': 'Top American and Chinese military officials began an annual review of major issues in Beijing on Wednesday pledging to seek greater cooperation and trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Top American and Chinese military officials began an annual review of major issues here on Wednesday pledging to seek greater cooperation and trust in a relationship that, to many, more resembles a budding rivalry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. and China Meet in Annual Military Review', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. and Chinese Military Officials Pledge More Cooperation at Start of Annual Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T12:16:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5041a390-876a-591a-b3c3-f590d4deab81', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5041a390-876a-591a-b3c3-f590d4deab81'}, {'abstract': 'A new culture of activism has helped fuel a citizen effort to repair Karachi’s crumbling infrastructure.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/pakistanis-taking-to-the-streets/', 'snippet': 'A new culture of activism has helped fuel a citizen effort to repair Karachi’s crumbling infrastructure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARACHI, Pakistan — It’s an unusual sight for a Sunday morning: a dozen Karachiites armed with brooms, rakes, sand and rubble crouch along a road on which none of them live or work in order to mend a large, sewage-filled pothole. The workers come in all shapes and sizes: a man in his 80’s uses his walking stick to knock large rocks out of the way; a boy of 12 watches for traffic and waves passing cars to the side of the street. They are members of the Greener Karachi Trust, a volunteer group committed to showing its fellow Karachi dwellers that they needn’t wait for the government to repair the city’s crumbling infrastructure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistanis Taking to the Streets', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potholes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T12:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf735a99-0b83-59ea-8658-707210d2ee6d', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf735a99-0b83-59ea-8658-707210d2ee6d'}, {'abstract': 'Composting kits, herb keepers, video games that acquaint children with energy sources — the range of green gifts has expanded.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/a-wish-list-for-cooks-bug-lovers-and-the-well-shod/', 'snippet': 'Composting kits, herb keepers, video games that acquaint children with energy sources — the range of green gifts has expanded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, we offered several ideas for inspirational green gifts for gastronomes, cyclists, spa rats and others. For those still seeking the perfect holiday present for that environmentally minded someone, here are more suggestions for a range of ages and interest groups. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wish List for Cooks, Bug Lovers and the Well-Shod', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compost', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Food', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Changers GmbH', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charity Navigator', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooking Light', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T12:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_na