l With the Dragon Tattoo,” weighs in on The New Yorker’s breaking the review embargo. If he had his way, there would be no screenings far in advance for critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dragon Tattoo-gate (Denby-Rudin-gate? Rudin-Denby-gate? Ruby-gate?) continues to roll along. In an interview with The Miami Herald, David Fincher, the director of “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,” weighed in on the controversy involving David Denby, a film critic for The New Yorker, positively reviewing his movie before he was supposed to, defying an embargo he’d agreed to – in writing, apparently – and angering the studio, Sony, and the producer Scott Rudin in the process. (There: just saved you having to click a link to get the back story.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Fincher’s Embargo Solution', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:31:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab8526a6-b1a1-5748-ad16-bdf2e819edc7', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab8526a6-b1a1-5748-ad16-bdf2e819edc7'}, {'abstract': 'Grupo Santander of Spain, seeking to bolster its capital reserves, is selling the unit to CorpBanca of Chile.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/santander-to-sell-colombian-unit-for-1-225-billion/', 'snippet': 'Grupo Santander of Spain, seeking to bolster its capital reserves, is selling the unit to CorpBanca of Chile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grupo Santander, seeking to bolster its capital reserves, announced on Wednesday that it would sell its Colombian unit to CorpBanca of Chile for $1.225 billion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santander to Sell Colombian Unit for $1.23 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CorpBanca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grupo Santander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:38:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b927cb6-de19-57d9-95b6-1e045371c217', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b927cb6-de19-57d9-95b6-1e045371c217'}, {'abstract': 'A campaign against co-sleeping sparks controversy, Amazon offers extra discount for price-checking shoppers, travel lessons from the world of academia and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/wednesday-reading-campaign-against-co-sleeping-sparks-controversy/', 'snippet': 'A campaign against co-sleeping sparks controversy, Amazon offers extra discount for price-checking shoppers, travel lessons from the world of academia and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Campaign Against Co-Sleeping Sparks Controversy', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5c170ea-1edd-5bef-a151-4d89f196ea21', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5c170ea-1edd-5bef-a151-4d89f196ea21'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Who but a politician would think the best way to observe one’s birthday is to hit up people for money? Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/its-my-birthday-said-with-hand-outstretched/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Who but a politician would think the best way to observe one’s birthday is to hit up people for money? Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It’s your birthday, so how do you celebrate? Maybe you gather a few close friends. Or you go out for a quiet dinner with your spouse or partner or significant other or lover or whatever term suits your situation and temperament. Or perhaps — it happens — the passage of time has you down, and you just want to be alone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s My Birthday! (Said With Hand Outstretched)', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:43:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b806bb32-abb0-5286-ab11-ea84b807f3c5', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b806bb32-abb0-5286-ab11-ea84b807f3c5'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/opinion-report-european-austerity/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: European Austerity', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1b31c51-bce7-5264-b80b-fcfb30accf64', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1b31c51-bce7-5264-b80b-fcfb30accf64'}, {'abstract': 'George Vecsey asks readers about their first–and lasting–impressions of outstanding athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/when-it-comes-to-the-greats-who-do-you-remember/', 'snippet': 'George Vecsey asks readers about their first–and lasting–impressions of outstanding athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sport endures on first impressions. We all remember the first time we walked into a stadium and saw the green grass. Saw Walter Payton or Barry Sanders break into the clear. Saw Evert and Navratilova pick up where they had left off in the last tournament. Saw Wayne Gretzky slip between two defenders. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When It Comes to the Greats, Who Do You Remember?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gretzky, Wayne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payton, Walter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Barry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Socrates (1954-2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vecsey, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:44:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aa08df8-7506-5a1a-b564-4b3109200dba', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aa08df8-7506-5a1a-b564-4b3109200dba'}, {'abstract': "WNYC listeners weigh in on the controversy stirred up last week by the mayor's comments about doubling class sizes, doubling teacher salaries and firing half of the city's teacher force. One teacher said no matter how good a teacher was, it would be impossible to handle much larger classes, much less all the paperwork generated.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/07/callers-take-issue-with-mayors-teacher-comments/', 'snippet': "WNYC listeners weigh in on the controversy stirred up last week by the mayor's comments about doubling class sizes, doubling teacher salaries and firing half of the city's teacher force. One teacher said no matter how good a teacher was, it would ...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Callers Take Issue With Mayor's Teacher Comments", 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By PATRICIA WILLENS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WILLENS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76d7a4dd-4a70-5b4d-97d9-2717466f8347', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76d7a4dd-4a70-5b4d-97d9-2717466f8347'}, {'abstract': 'Jump rope, freeze tag and the jungle gym, once staples of lunchtime play, are being squeezed out at some of the city’s highest-rated public elementary schools, where recess is now being viewed as prime time for enrichment classes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/07/recess-has-some-new-competition/', 'snippet': 'Jump rope, freeze tag and the jungle gym, once staples of lunchtime play, are being squeezed out at some of the city’s highest-rated public elementary schools, where recess is now being viewed as prime time for enrichment classes.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recess Has Some New Competition', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T13:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd844f69-78e4-5c47-8d61-211e919277fb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd844f69-78e4-5c47-8d61-211e919277fb'}, {'abstract': 'Damien Florébert Cuypers animates our “T,” in Lego block form.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/plastic-fantastic/', 'snippet': 'Damien Florébert Cuypers animates our “T,” in Lego block form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this photograph and stop-motion video, the French-born artist Damien Florébert Cuypers translates his longtime fascination with Legos into a quirky version of our trademark logo. Cuypers, who splits his time between Lyon, Berlin and New York, is refreshingly down-to-earth about working with the toys. “You can end up with some dramatic color/shape structure,” he says. “Or a stupid-looking bunch of bricks.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plastic Fantastic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lego Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T14:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03775f3a-c4b9-5031-990a-489655a6a654', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03775f3a-c4b9-5031-990a-489655a6a654'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/gingrich-and-the-christian-right/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column for Campaign Stops this week argues that religious conservatives should think twice about their flirtation with Newt Gingrich:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich and the Christian Right', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T14:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b3b9d02-9f93-52fb-a8e6-f285b8cb471b', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b3b9d02-9f93-52fb-a8e6-f285b8cb471b'}, {'abstract': 'After central banks cut the interest rate last week, the amount of borrowing soared to more than $50 billion, from $395 million in November.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/business/global/ecb-sees-surge-in-demand-for-dollar-loans.html', 'snippet': 'After central banks cut the interest rate last week, the amount of borrowing soared to more than $50 billion, from $395 million in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Central Bank said demand for three-month dollar loans surged after it cut the cost of the financing almost in half in a coordinated action last week with five other central banks including the Federal Reserve.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dollar-Loan Demand Swells In Europe After Rate Cut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'