_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bb03c00-7084-559f-9682-b554c85f1ace', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bb03c00-7084-559f-9682-b554c85f1ace'}, {'abstract': 'It’s all fine, except for the economy and the people.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/they-have-made-a-desert-and-called-it-adjustment/', 'snippet': 'It’s all fine, except for the economy and the people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It continues to be a source of amazement to see what passes for a success story among austerity advocates. Ireland is proclaimed a huge success despite 14 percent unemployment and a very slow recovery in incomes. And then there’s Latvia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Have Made A Desert, And Called It Adjustment', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T14:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e3002f7-97eb-5d67-abf4-3a7ee94d586d', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e3002f7-97eb-5d67-abf4-3a7ee94d586d'}, {'abstract': 'It’s never been easy to be a fan of the Mets, and certainly the future does not appear to offer anything remotely offering hope.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/a-devil-of-a-time-to-root-for-the-mets/', 'snippet': 'It’s never been easy to be a fan of the Mets, and certainly the future does not appear to offer anything remotely offering hope.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Based on five decades of field research, I’ve reached this careful conclusion: Joan Payson, the original owner of my beloved Mets, probably did something really nasty with the devil atop the dugout at the old Shea Stadium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Devil of a Time to Root for the Mets', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shea Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T14:14:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/230a1a62-dcff-584f-a995-ed9bdde94d30', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230a1a62-dcff-584f-a995-ed9bdde94d30'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times’s Personal Tech Holiday Gift Guide gives readers ideas on what to buy. It also serves as a window into industry trends and the shifting tastes of the American consumer. The guide includes looks at fitness gear, video games and smartphones, three of the hottest categories of the season, as well as essays on the growing power of the consumer armed with knowledge of prices, technology as a wardrobe and the connected home.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/daily-report-holiday-gadgets/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times’s Personal Tech Holiday Gift Guide gives readers ideas on what to buy. It also serves as a window into industry trends and the shifting tastes of the American consumer. The guide includes looks at fitness gear, video games and s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most important period for consumer electronics is, of course, the holiday shopping season. For anyone wanting to understand how the industry is doing in the here and now, there is no better place to study than a holiday buying guide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Holiday Gadgets', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T14:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6706cdd5-6380-56e9-a7dd-07db769c83b5', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6706cdd5-6380-56e9-a7dd-07db769c83b5'}, {'abstract': 'BBC America will show new episodes of “The Hour,” the hit period drama about 1950s British television journalism, next year. The six-hour mini-series adds Peter Capaldi, Tom Burke and Hannah Tointon to a cast that features Ben Whishaw, Romola Garai and Dominic West.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/bbc-adds-more-hours-and-more-characters-to-the-hour/', 'snippet': 'BBC America will show new episodes of “The Hour,” the hit period drama about 1950s British television journalism, next year. The six-hour mini-series adds Peter Capaldi, Tom Burke and Hannah Tointon to a cast that features Ben Whishaw, Romola Gara...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British love their period pieces and meta-media dramas as much as Americans, it appears. The BBC has ordered a sequel to “The Hour,” its hit mini-series about the competitive world of 1950s British television journalism, which will add new cast members and which BBC America will co-produce and broadcast in the United States, that cable channel said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BBC Adds More Hours and More Characters to ‘The Hour’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value':