s major victory for the police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian police on Wednesday arrested a powerful leader of a criminal group based outside Naples, dealing the group, known as the Camorra, one of its most powerful blows in years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gangster in Italy Arrested After 16-Year Manhunt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Crime Chief Arrested After 16-Year Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43b6ddd5-4665-5352-81c3-6952b6c8fba8', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43b6ddd5-4665-5352-81c3-6952b6c8fba8'}, {'abstract': 'While some reviewers have called it racist and mindless, “Intouchables,” the new film by the French directors Eric Toledano and Olivier Nakache, is a big box-office hit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/movies/intouchables-is-a-magnet-for-french-moviegoers.html', 'snippet': 'While some reviewers have called it racist and mindless, “Intouchables,” the new film by the French directors Eric Toledano and Olivier Nakache, is a big box-office hit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — When it was released last month, “Intouchables” seemed an unremarkable, lowbrow French comedy, a small-budget film with actors little known outside France hamming it up in a story about a stodgy, disabled aristocrat and the good-humored ex-con whom he hires as his aide.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/intouchables/intouchables-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The French Flock to a Feel-Good Movie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The French Flock to a Feel-Good Movie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abc8e727-404e-50da-a098-df3c5150fe73', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abc8e727-404e-50da-a098-df3c5150fe73'}, {'abstract': '“I’m happy to bring you the good news about the complete collapse of the global warming movement and the failure of the Kyoto process, as world leaders meet for the United Nations global warming conference,” Senator James Inhofe says in a video message.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/on-climate-change-a-gloat-and-a-warning/', 'snippet': '“I’m happy to bring you the good news about the complete collapse of the global warming movement and the failure of the Kyoto process, as world leaders meet for the United Nations global warming conference,” Senator James Inhofe says in a video me...', 'lead_paragraph': ' DURBAN, South Africa — If anyone at the United Nations climate change conference here wondered why the United States is unwilling or unable to take decisive action on the warming of the planet, they could tune in to the Web site of the Senate Environment and Public Works Committee on Wednesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Climate Change, a Gloat and a Warning', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kyoto Protocol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boxer, Barbara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inhofe, James M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environment and Public Works Committee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durban (South Africa)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'