ry Morgan, Colonel Potter on ‘M*A*S*H,’ Dies at 96', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a45644f2-c3be-5c5c-99f7-418f45dd1eef', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a45644f2-c3be-5c5c-99f7-418f45dd1eef'}, {'abstract': 'A Yoga studio finds lots of referals but has to survive not one but two floods.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/is-it-worth-risking-disaster-for-the-perfect-location/', 'snippet': 'A Yoga studio finds lots of referals but has to survive not one but two floods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We just published a case study that describes the dilemma faced by Pulling Down the Moon, a Chicago business that was hit by not one but two floods in just less than a year. Tamara Quinn and Beth Heller, co-owners of the company, a provider of supplemental holistic services like yoga, acupuncture, and massage therapy to women undergoing fertility treatments, chose to facilitate referrals by subleasing first-floor space just down the hall from one of the country’s biggest fertility clinics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Worth Risking Disaster for the Perfect Location?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Grossmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grossmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/349e6b81-bf19-518d-88d9-b1d37145cf92', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/349e6b81-bf19-518d-88d9-b1d37145cf92'}, {'abstract': 'The opposition to Caitlin Halligan, an experienced and accomplished lawyer, was entirely without substance.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/lousy-filibusters-caitlin-halligan-edition/', 'snippet': 'The opposition to Caitlin Halligan, an experienced and accomplished lawyer, was entirely without substance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty-four Senators voted yesterday to confirm the nomination of an experienced and accomplished lawyer, Caitlin Halligan, to the D.C. Circuit, which in the twisted and blindly ideological world of the United States Senate means she didn’t get confirmed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lousy Filibusters: Caitlin Halligan Edition', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Courts (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halligan, Caitlin Joan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:44:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/979ddbf8-de3e-5323-9a3c-bfd23d15715b', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/979ddbf8-de3e-5323-9a3c-bfd23d15715b'}, {'abstract': 'Getting any quality shuteye on the shuttle? Is your unconscious neighbor on the Q drooling on your kindle?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/share-your-stories-of-sleep-on-the-subway/', 'snippet': 'Getting any quality shuteye on the shuttle? Is your unconscious neighbor on the Q drooling on your kindle?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you slept through your stop only to awaken at the end of the line? New Lots Avenue or 179th Street Jamaica, perhaps? Or do you shudder at the thought of R.E.M. on the IND, for fear of lush workers? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Share Your Stories of Sleep on the Subway', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York-Presbyterian Hospital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T16:47:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de817f9-70e6-5284-a9c3-8986b237bb7c', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de817f9-70e6-5284-a9c3-8986b237bb7c'}, {'abstract': 'A sleep researcher, with the aid of a drowsy straphanger, set out to discover whether dozing underground was worth its while.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/nyregion/to-sleep-on-the-subway-maybe-but-to-dream-poor-chance.html', 'snippet': 'A sleep researcher, with the aid of a drowsy straphanger, set out to discover whether dozing underground was worth its while.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ride on the New York subway can be a sensory overload: musicians perform for change; conductors plead to those who hold open train doors to relent; and passengers, often in unimaginably close proximity, subject one another to all sorts of sights, sounds, smells and touches, preferably inadvertent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/08sleep3/08sleep3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/08sleep3/08sleep3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/08sleep3/08sleep3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/08sleep3/08sleep3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/08sleep3/08sleep3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Sleep on the Subway, Maybe, but to Dream? Poor Chance', 'kicker': None,