ps://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/asia/hamid-karzai-visits-wounded-in-suicide-bombings-and-looks-to-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'At a hospital full of survivors of a series of suicide bombings, the Afghan president promised to pursue the issue with Pakistan, but stopped short of accusing them of involvement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — President Hamid Karzai paid an emotional visit on Wednesday to a hospital full of survivors of a series of suicide bombings claimed by a Pakistani extremist group, and he promised to pursue the issue with Pakistan’s government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/blogs/20111207-lens-massoud-slide-3N0H/20111207-lens-massoud-slide-3N0H-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Karzai Says He Will Talk to Pakistan Over Attacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Karzai Says He Will Talk To Pakistan Over Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Jhangvi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T17:50:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharifullah Sahak and Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharifullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a82b7a-d557-557f-a169-53e982cdc16b', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a82b7a-d557-557f-a169-53e982cdc16b'}, {'abstract': 'Will the rich pay more or less in taxes under a new tax code being considered in Albany?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/tax-cut-or-tax-increase/', 'snippet': 'Will the rich pay more or less in taxes under a new tax code being considered in Albany?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The overhaul of the state’s income tax structure agreed to by Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and legislative leaders will tax income over $2 million (for married couples filing jointly) at 8.82 percent. That is significantly higher than the state’s highest base income tax rate, which is 6.85 percent, but slightly lower than the 8.97 percent rate that for the last three years has been imposed on high incomes under a surcharge that was set to expire Dec. 31. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Cut or Tax Increase?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T17:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e2c71a-2dbd-58b3-9298-23b1c831b9a8', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e2c71a-2dbd-58b3-9298-23b1c831b9a8'}, {'abstract': 'Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor of Illinois, will go to jail for corruption, including trying to sell the Senate seat that President Obama left behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/us/blagojevich-expresses-remorse-in-courtroom-speech.html', 'snippet': 'Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor of Illinois, will go to jail for corruption, including trying to sell the Senate seat that President Obama left behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Rod R. Blagojevich, the former governor of Illinois who for years proclaimed he was innocent of federal corruption charges, apologized on Wednesday for his crimes. He apologized to his trial judge. He apologized to his family. He apologized to the residents of Illinois, who had heard his voice on secretly recorded phone calls as he crassly spoke of what he might get in exchange for a United States Senate seat. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/08blago_cnd/08blago_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/us/08blago_cnd/08blago_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/08blago_cnd/08blago_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/08blago_cnd/08blago_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/us/08blago_cnd/08blago_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blagojevich Sentenced to 14 Years in Prison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blagojevich Draws 14-Year Sentence for Corruption Conviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blagojevich, Rod R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T17:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d555e4-1a9f-5ac0-8e84-bb77f46c397b', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d555e4-1a9f-5ac0-8e84-bb77f46c397b'}, {'abstract': 'A century ago, the Times editorial page slammed Teddy Roosevelt’s speech in Osawatomie.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/2011-versus-1910-an-editorial-change-of-heart/', 'snippet': 'A century ago, the Times editorial page slammed Teddy Roosevelt’s speech in Osawatomie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the marvelous things about my job as the editorial page editor of a 151-year-old newspaper is that I occasionally happen upon curious editorial positions from days of yore. I’m not talking about the paper’s onetime opposition to women’s suffrage, although that was strange.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2011 Versus 1910, an Editorial Change of Heart', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub