51'}, {'abstract': 'The life reports are in. Meet Charles D. Snelling.', 'web_url': 'https://brooks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/the-life-report-charles-darwin-snelling/', 'snippet': 'The life reports are in. Meet Charles D. Snelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following Life Report was submitted in response to my column of Oct. 28, in which I asked readers over 70 to write autobiographical essays evaluating their own lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Life Report: Charles Darwin Snelling', 'kicker': 'David Brooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snelling, Adrienne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snelling, Charles D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phillips Academy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3675bac-39c4-51ae-824b-211547f82782', 'word_count': 5109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3675bac-39c4-51ae-824b-211547f82782'}, {'abstract': 'Mets pitcher R.A. Dickey begins his chronicle of climbing Mount Kilimanjaro to raise awareness of at-risk women and girls in Mumbai.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/a-climb-and-a-cause/', 'snippet': 'Mets pitcher R.A. Dickey begins his chronicle of climbing Mount Kilimanjaro to raise awareness of at-risk women and girls in Mumbai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'R.A. Dickey, the Mets pitcher, will climb Mount Kilimanjaro in January, in part to raise awareness for the Bombay Teen Challenge, an organization that rescues and cares for women and girls in Mumbai who are at risk of being abused and exploited. His posts will appear occasionally in Bats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Climb and a Cause', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Ernest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:17:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By R.A. Dickey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'R.', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Dickey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de3715cc-5183-51df-a69e-2da4228befda', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de3715cc-5183-51df-a69e-2da4228befda'}, {'abstract': 'Raymond W. Kelly called the Facebook page on which officers referred to West Indian Day paradegoers as “savages” “disrespectful of communities that officers have taken an oath to protect.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/police-commissioner-criticizes-insults-of-parade-goers-by-officers/', 'snippet': 'Raymond W. Kelly called the Facebook page on which officers referred to West Indian Day paradegoers as “savages” “disrespectful of communities that officers have taken an oath to protect.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 2:38 p.m. | Police Commissioner Raymond W. Kelly made his first statement on Wednesday about the latest scandal to hit the New York Police Department, condemning the kind of hateful speech attributed to several police officers on a Facebook page dedicated to the unpleasantness of working the annual West Indian American Day Parade in Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Commissioner Criticizes Officers’ Slurs Against Paradegoers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:18:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd3ffc1-0000-5a4c-8d76-1718ac5b9942', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd3ffc1-0000-5a4c-8d76-1718ac5b9942'}, {'abstract': 'Corradino D’Ascanio is the subject of a new exhibition at the Museo Piaggio in Tuscany.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/designer-of-piaggio-vespa-is-honored-by-former-employer/', 'snippet': 'Corradino D’Ascanio is the subject of a new exhibition at the Museo Piaggio in Tuscany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most influential but commonly overlooked designers of the 20th century is getting his due.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Designer of Piaggio Vespa Is Honored by Former Employer', 'kicker'