oadcasting a new campaign ad that seems to contrast Christianity with homosexuality, vows to end what he calls “Obama’s war on religion,” and highlights Mr. Perry’s criticism of overturning the “don’t ask, don’t tell” policy for gays serving in the military.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Ad Focuses on Gays and Christianity', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Log Cabin Republicans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab1a78a2-784a-5fe7-8c36-a41e76e3dadc', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab1a78a2-784a-5fe7-8c36-a41e76e3dadc'}, {'abstract': 'The longtime broadcaster Tim McCarver receives the Ford C. Frick Award from the National Baseball Hall of Fame.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/mccarver-is-honored-by-hall-of-fame/', 'snippet': 'The longtime broadcaster Tim McCarver receives the Ford C. Frick Award from the National Baseball Hall of Fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim McCarver was thinking about his broadcast partners at the Philadelphia Phillies on Wednesday when he won the National Baseball Hall of Fame’s Ford C. Frick Award.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McCarver Is Honored by Hall of Fame', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frick, Ford C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarver, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/232e6f8c-fe34-5038-ae23-4ce922850807', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/232e6f8c-fe34-5038-ae23-4ce922850807'}, {'abstract': 'A report that Jerry Sandusky was rejected for a volunteer coaching post last year after a background check and one examining Penn State’s transparency in recent weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/leading-off-scandal-makes-penn-state-a-fixture-in-headlines/', 'snippet': 'A report that Jerry Sandusky was rejected for a volunteer coaching post last year after a background check and one examining Penn State’s transparency in recent weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Penn State scandal has the dubious distinction of having what seems to be a permanent place in the headlines sections of sports Web sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Scandal Makes Penn State a Fixture in Headlines', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMATEUR ATHLETICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Archie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T18:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Reddicliffe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddicliffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b15c86c6-ee1a-53b8-a2d8-794a4d50a897', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b15c86c6-ee1a-53b8-a2d8-794a4d50a897'}, {'abstract': 'The new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is proposing a simplified format for credit card agreements.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/a-proposal-to-simplify-credit-card-agreements/', 'snippet': 'The new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is proposing a simplified format for credit card agreements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Credit card agreements are typically something you’d want to read only if you suffered from insomnia. A glance at a few lines of the dense type, printed on filmy paper, is sure to help you drift off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Proposal to Simplify Credit Card Agreements', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Date, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T19:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e14b3a98-b2bc-5fcb-8e65-6015ab876fad', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e14b3a98-b2bc-5fcb-8e65-6015ab876fad'}, {'abstract': 'Expertly crafted shoes take time. Exactly how much time is on each pair in Valentino’s spring capsule collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/first-look-valentinos-timestrings-collection/', 'snippet': 'Expertly crafted shoes take time. Exactly how much time is on each pair in Valentino’s spring capsule collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance it’s hard to find a common thread running through Valentino’s spring capsule collection, Timestrings. The studded peep-toe booties, satin flats, polka-dot platforms and bow-embellished kitten heels carry many of the brand’s signatures, but share none of them collectively. What all of the shoes do share is a handwritten time stamp — a numerical record of the amount of time it took to make each pair. For example, the sequence etched into a pair of silver chain wedge heels is 47.41’50”, denoting 47 hours, 41 minutes and 50 seconds. “When we talk about luxury and time, it’s clear that there’s a strong connection between the two,” says Maria Grazia Chiuri, one of the house’s two co-designers. “Time is the new luxury, and luxury does not exist without time and the consciousness of a unique tradition.” Classic Italian craftsmanship still exists (Valentino is known for its old Florentine factories), but in an age of fast everything it’s easy to forget our Old World cobblers: the one devoted to flowers, the one who specializes in crystals and another with expertise in lace, for example. Pierpaolo Piccioli, Chiuri’s design partner, adds, “It’s nice to know that you’re buying a kind of cultural process.” Milled plexiglass and velvet wedges marked 38H? At $1,295, that’s $34 an hour, if you break it down. And yes, it’s worth it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Look | Valentino’s Timestrings Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T19:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a8b1e9-2d40-5e31-a671-bdec608a5247', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a8b1e9-2d40-5e31-a671-bdec608a5247'}, {'abstract': 'The health secretary overruled the Food and Drug Administration’s decision that emergency contraceptives be sold freely over the counter, including to teenagers 16 years old and younger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/health/policy/sebelius-overrules-fda-on-freer-sale-of-emergency-contraceptives.html', 'snippet': 'The health secretary overruled the Food and Drug Administration’s decision that emergency contraceptives be sold freely over the counter, including to teenagers 16 years old and younger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For the first time ever, the Health and Human Services secretary publicly overruled the Food and Drug Administration, refusing Wednesday to allow emergency contraceptives to be sold over the counter, including to young teenagers. The decision avoided what could have been a bruising political battle over parental control and contraception during a presidential election season.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/FDA1/FDA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/us/FDA1/FDA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan to Widen Availability of Morning-After Pill Is Rejected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Overruled On Availability Of After-Sex Pill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebelius, Kathleen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamburg, Margaret A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'n