esday, the Institute of Medicine affirmed some well-known risks but said many others remain unclear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/health/scientific-panel-finds-few-clear-environmental-links-to-breast-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'In a report issued Wednesday, the Institute of Medicine affirmed some well-known risks but said many others remain unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An exhaustive new report meant to address public fears about possible links between breast cancer and the environment finds evidence strong enough to make only a few firm recommendations, most already well known and none with a large proven benefit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/science/CANCER/CANCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/science/CANCER/CANCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/science/CANCER/CANCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientific Panel Finds Few Clear Environmental Links to Breast Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Finds Few Clear Environmental Links to Breast Cancer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dyes and Dyestuffs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Estrogen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bisphenol A (BPA)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T19:19:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07624400-c888-5291-a64c-4acbb73d14b8', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07624400-c888-5291-a64c-4acbb73d14b8'}, {'abstract': 'A recent donation to the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts will give the public more access to memorabilia from Caffe Cino, the birthplace of Off Off Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/theater/donation-to-library-opens-new-portal-to-caffe-cino.html', 'snippet': 'A recent donation to the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts will give the public more access to memorabilia from Caffe Cino, the birthplace of Off Off Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOSEPH CINO didn’t set out to be a pioneer. He began presenting plays at his Cornelia Street cafe on a whim, as an offshoot of the poetry readings that expressed his desire to create a place where artistic types would want to spend time. A dreamer and newcomer to Manhattan by way of Buffalo, he opened that establishment, Caffe Cino, in 1958 and over time became a veritable spokesman for the intimate and uncommercial productions mounted on its shabby, makeshift stage.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11CINO