f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a434ff7-46ae-57e3-9178-e951d2e9bbac', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a434ff7-46ae-57e3-9178-e951d2e9bbac'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan and Hays Holladay use a global positioning network to trigger different themes as a listener wanders through a specific landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001212033/bluebrain-in-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan and Hays Holladay use a global positioning network to trigger different themes as a listener wanders through a specific landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan and Hays Holladay use a global positioning network to trigger different themes as a listener wanders through a specific landscape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/video-bluebrain/video-bluebrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/video-bluebrain/video-bluebrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/video-bluebrain/video-bluebrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/arts/video-bluebrain/video-bluebrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bluebrain in Central Park', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c9a1d635-bfcb-5708-a488-16d822416952', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c9a1d635-bfcb-5708-a488-16d822416952'}, {'abstract': 'Underworld, the electronic dance music duo who has collaborated with the British filmmaker Danny Boyle, will assist Mr. Boyle in producing the opening ceremony of the 2012 Olympic Games in London.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/underworld-to-create-music-for-opening-of-2012-olympics-in-london/', 'snippet': 'Underworld, the electronic dance music duo who has collaborated with the British filmmaker Danny Boyle, will assist Mr. Boyle in producing the opening ceremony of the 2012 Olympic Games in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The members of the electronic dance music group Underworld have been named the musical directors for the opening ceremony of the 2012 Olympics in London, organizers announced on Wednesday. The duo, Rick Smith and Karl Hyde, will work alongside the artistic director, the British filmmaker Danny Boyle, to produce the music for the three-hour performance on July 27. It is not the first time Mr. Boyle has chosen Mr. Smith and Mr. Hyde to provide the soundtrack for one of his projects. The group is perhaps best known for its dance track “Born Slippy,” which first appeared in a scene from Mr. Boyle’s 1996 film “Trainspotting.” Since then, they have created music for four other projects by Mr. Boyle, including a National Theater production of “Frankenstein” that received high praise from critics. Mr. Boyle said the hiring of Underworld to write music for the Games was “the last piece of the jigsaw puzzle” and praised the duo’s creative range. Mr. Hyde said the chance to compose for the Olympics was a great honor. “We want to leave people with a musical memory of the show rather than a purely visual one,” he said in a statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Underworld to Create Music for Opening of 2012 Olympics in London', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/128841fe-8666-595c-a892-2f85440e114e', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/128841fe-8666-595c-a892-2f85440e114e'}, {'abstract': 'Leather dresses; matching socks and bags; and macaroon-like pill boxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/08/fashion/20111208-BROWSING.html', 'snippet': 'Leather dresses; matching socks and bags; and macaroon-like pill boxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leather dresses; matching socks and bags; and macaroon-like pill boxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202/20111208-BROWSING-slide-I202-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping Snapshots: Dec. 8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/aefb2070-ec55-5848-b583-c7601f82c02b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/aefb2070-ec55-5848-b583-c7601f82c02b'}, {'abstract': 'One of fashion’s finest sculptors returns to the Netherlands for a retrospective of his last decade of work.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/21st-century-frocks-azzedine-alaia-at-the-groninger-museum/', 'snippet': 'One of fashion’s finest sculptors returns to the Netherlands for a retrospective of his last decade of work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Azzedine Alaïa has never obeyed the fashion calendar and shows only when he — and his clothes — are good and ready. In fact, in recent years, the designer, who is now in his 70s, has probably had as many runway presentations as museum exhibitions, including the one that opens this weekend at the Groninger Museum in the Netherlands. “Azzedine Alaïa in the 21st Century” focuses solely on his output from roughly the past decade, and yet there is more substance there than many designers could ever hope to achieve in a lifetime, including the fierce tailcoat above and a toothsome evening dress with a zipper that spirals suggestively around the body from the neck to the floor. Always the perfectionist in the pursuit of beauty (he’s often referred to as a “sculptor of women’s bodies”), Alaïa apparently recut or totally remade many of the pieces in the show to the exact proportions of the mannequins. In an open love letter to the designer, Mark Wilson, who curated the exhibition, writes, “I’m sure that certain people may wonder why we are doing this one more time?” referring to a massive Alaïa exhibition at the Groninger Museum back in in 1997-98. Wilson promptly answers his own question: “Because you are the last great couturier working today.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '21st-Century Frocks | Azzedine Alaïa at the Groninger Museum', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alaia, Azzedine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29ab43b7-8242-5fca-bf30-cc472dd0d01f', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29ab43b7-8242-5fca-bf30-cc472dd0d01f'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S.C. men’s water polo team won its fourth consecutive N.C.A.A. championship', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/by-winning-a-fourth-u-s-c-records-a-first-in-water-polo/', 'snippet': 'The U.S.C. men’s water polo team won its fourth consecutive N.C.A.A. championship', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the clock ticked down to the final seconds of the 2011 N.C.A.A. water polo championship game, the U.S.C. fans present started chanting “four-peat,” the U.S.C. fight song rang out through U.C. Berkeley’s Spieker Aquatics Complex and the U.S.C. water polo starters turned to face their fans from their positions in the pool with fists raised. The announcer couldn’t be heard once the clock hit zero and every Trojan player poolside jumped into the water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Winning a Fourth, U.S.C. Records a First in Water Polo', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Polo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Southern California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maheen Sahoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maheen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sahoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e22c77-a3d3-5f46-bb48-4860012a4be4', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e22c77-a3d3-5f46-bb48-4860012a4be4'}, {'abstract': 'In “Extra Virginity,” Tom Mueller reveals the brazen fraud in the olive oil industry and teaches readers how to sniff out the good stuff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/books/extra-virginity-by-tom-mueller-a-word-on-olive-oil-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Extra Virginity,” Tom Mueller reveals the brazen fraud in the olive oil industry and teaches readers how to sniff out the good stuff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few pages into Tom Mueller’s new book, “Extra Virginity,” there’s a funny moment when an olive oil expert holds up a bottle that’s covered with dubious claims: “100 percent Italian,” “cold-pressed,” “extra virgin.” The man shakes his head and says, perhaps with a hint of Don Rickles in his voice, “Extra virgin? What’s this oil got to do with virginity? This is a whore.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/sub-book/sub-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/sub-book/sub-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/sub-book/sub-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Olive Oil’s Growers, Chemists, Cooks and Crooks', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olive Oil’s Growers, Chemists, Cooks and Crooks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olive Oil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mate