her J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T20:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52bd4fb0-df61-5802-a062-ab31bf0c917a', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52bd4fb0-df61-5802-a062-ab31bf0c917a'}, {'abstract': 'The one-man show “Mad Women” at the Club at La MaMa finds John Fleck reflecting on his childhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/theater/reviews/mad-women-with-john-fleck-at-la-mama-review.html', 'snippet': 'The one-man show “Mad Women” at the Club at La MaMa finds John Fleck reflecting on his childhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the countless drag queens who have paid tribute to Judy Garland, you’d think her stardust might be running low. But no, the actor and performance artist John Fleck grabs a handful in his spirited, heartfelt, one-man show “Mad Women” at the Club at La MaMa. Mr. Fleck and three other artists — Karen Finley, Holly Hughes and Tim Miller — were at the center of a controversy over content in the early 1990s when the National Endowment for the Arts revoked their grants. There is no controversy in “Mad Women,” only affection for Garland and bittersweet recollections of Mr. Fleck’s past.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/sub-mad/sub-mad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro