nd a Better Husband Than the Other Guy', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac09f5f-b192-5781-8318-94694271bd60', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac09f5f-b192-5781-8318-94694271bd60'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich, Republican presidential candidate, defends his changing position on global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/caucus-video-gingrich-and-global-warming/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich, Republican presidential candidate, defends his changing position on global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich, Republican presidential candidate, defends his changing position on global warming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caucus Video: Gingrich and Global Warming', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:05:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily B. Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/928d917b-0a1c-5703-8af1-e286f298b249', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/928d917b-0a1c-5703-8af1-e286f298b249'}, {'abstract': 'There’s still a place for minimalism in the fashion world according to Reed Krakoff.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/just-one-look-reed-krakoff/', 'snippet': 'There’s still a place for minimalism in the fashion world according to Reed Krakoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s still a place for minimalism in the fashion world according to Reed Krakoff. His pre-fall collection, which debuted Monday, is wonderfully strict and linear, with fur coats on one end of the spectrum and simple knits on the other. The pieces are two of his strongest offerings. In terms of colors, the clear alligator green and orange-y pink looked surprisingly wearable and cool next to all of the black and tan. Pictured here is a compact wool dress with leather collar and sleeves is finished with the collection’s most effective accessory — a pair of black leather gloves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Reed Krakoff', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:05:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a01c52d9-a0e7-5eea-b89b-15f9c493bd58', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a01c52d9-a0e7-5eea-b89b-15f9c493bd58'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrations from Moscow to Maine, with many in between.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/occupywallst-roundup-day-82/', 'snippet': 'Demonstrations from Moscow to Maine, with many in between.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Protests continued Wednesday in Moscow for a third straight night. On Monday, thousands of demonstrators took to the streets, expressing anger with Vladimir Putin’s ruling party and prompting some to question whether Moscow could become a new Occupy site. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#OccupyWallSt Roundup, Day 82', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'EAST NEW YORK (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07621738-0f9c-5159-b4b0-192518c03115', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07621738-0f9c-5159-b4b0-192518c03115'}, {'abstract': 'If the former chief executive of MF Global does not invoke his Fifth Amendment right before the House Agriculture Committee, there will be many issues worth discussing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/10-questions-for-jon-corzine/', 'snippet': 'If the former