eaps-a-modest-measure-of-success/', 'snippet': 'A Quebec law enacted in 2008 that mandates snow tires on passenger vehicles over the winter months has been credited for a reduction in serious car accidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — It’s the annual crunch time at tire shops and garages throughout the province of Quebec. Drivers must fit passenger vehicles with four winter tires by Dec. 15 and keep them on until March 15, or risk fines of 200 to 300 Canadian dollars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Quebec, Winter Tire Law Reaps a Modest Measure of Success', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4497e46-1996-5a7a-8641-c9ac2e0870a7', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4497e46-1996-5a7a-8641-c9ac2e0870a7'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers just demonstrated the predictable arc of the temper tantrum, so why do we spend so much time worrying about them?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/the-predictability-of-tantrums/', 'snippet': 'Researchers just demonstrated the predictable arc of the temper tantrum, so why do we spend so much time worrying about them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of course you knew that kids have tantrums. But you probably didn’t know that kids who have tantrums mostly have them in a neat, predictable pattern. Michael Potegal, a neurology professor, teamed up with James Green, a developmental psychologist, to look not at what causes tantrums but at how they work. They found three standard phases (video documented on NPR’s Shots blog). Phase 1: yelling and screaming. Phase 2: physical actions. Phase 3: crying and whining. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Predictability of Tantrums', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, JENNY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2be4bae-a1b6-5a4c-982a-b4bcd0ede0cd', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2be4bae-a1b6-5a4c-982a-b4bcd0ede0cd'}, {'abstract': 'As leaders prepared to gather to create a unified approach to save the euro, disagreements emerged among Germany, France and Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/europe/on-eve-of-european-union-summit-meeting-new-rifts-on-euro-emerge.html', 'snippet': 'As leaders prepared to gather to create a unified approach to save the euro, disagreements emerged among Germany, France and Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Disagreements over how to enforce better economic discipline and centralized oversight over nations in the European Union emerged on Wednesday, the day before a crucial summit meeting to deal with the euro crisis, including disputes over how extensively and how quickly to change European treaties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/world/europe/europe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/world/europe/europe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/world/europe/europe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Eve of Key Meeting, New Rifts on Euro Emerge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Eve of Crucial Meeting, New Rifts on Euro Emerge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Rompuy, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73b32ec9-b304-50cf-bee0-e587b00975c5', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73b32ec9-b304-50cf-bee0-e587b00975c5'}, {'abstract': 'A new Apple store will open in Grand Central Terminal on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/mice-and-ipads-and-iphones-in-grand-central/', 'snippet': 'A new Apple store will open in Grand Central Terminal on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple’s newest store, on the busy concourse of Grand Central Terminal, will open to the public on Friday. The company will be offering travelers services designed to speed them through the new store at its elegant perch in the historic station. Read about it in the Bits blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mice, and iPads and iPhones, in Grand Central', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd10775-f7a3-5fca-9b54-351d55bc666f', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd10775-f7a3-5fca-9b54-351d55bc666f'}, {'abstract': 'A new book called “New African Fashion” highlights designers — some established, some fledgling — whose work is African made or inspired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/07/fashion/20111208_africandesigners.html', 'snippet': 'A new book called “New African Fashion” highlights designers — some established, some fledgling — whose work is African made or inspired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new book called “New African Fashion” highlights designers — some established, some fledgling — whose work is African made or inspired.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/fashion/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/fashion/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/fashion/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40/20111208_africandesigners-slide-IL40-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'African Fashion in Its Multifaceted Designs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cf210d8e-f696-5a0f-be1b-0b1cc9c46fb1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cf210d8e-f696-5a0f-be1b-0b1cc9c46fb1'}, {'abstract': 'The current designers looking to the continent for inspiration are avoiding the old clichés.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fashion/africas-new-fashion-influence.html', 'snippet': 'The current designers looking to the continent for inspiration are avoiding the old clichés.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the years since Yves Saint Laurent showed his iconic 1967 “African” collection, fashion designers have repeatedly tapped the heritage of Africa in search of inspiration. Just last season Burberry and Michael Kors were among several labels that mined the continent as a source of ideas. Yet in the popular imagination, especially in the Western hemisphere, African fashion more often than not means animal prints, mud cloth and cowrie shells. In her new work, “New African Fashion” (Prestel; $35), Helen Jennings, a fashion journalist, hopes to broaden that view. Part coffee-table book, part glossary, it highlights designers — some established, some fledgling — whose work is African made or inspired.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08AFRICA2_SPAN/08AFRICA2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08AFRICA2_SPAN/08AFRICA2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08AFRICA2_SPAN/08AFRICA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08AFRICA2_SPAN/08AFRICA2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08AFRICA2_SPAN/08AFRICA2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Designers Take a Fresh Look at Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Designers Take Fresh Look At Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T21:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37ba2c3f-2d38-5e8e-8bfe-3ba94913bfe7', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37ba2c3f-2d38-5e8e-8bfe-3ba94913bfe7'}, {'abstract': 'The tiny club below the Dream Downtown hotel picks up the pace in the early morning hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fashion/electric-room-in-chelsea-boite.html', 'snippet': 'The tiny club below the Dream Downtown hotel picks up the pace in the early morning hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A PUNY bar wedged beneath a sleek hotel, accessed through a garbage-strewn loading dock, doesn’t sound overly compelling. But with cagey calibration, Electric Room, a new lounge under the popular Dream Downtown hotel, has become one of the city’s toughest doors to breach.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08BOITE/08zBOITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':