Big Party For a Big Calendar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calendars', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebab8ff6-ab81-5f16-8588-a49b4c0a02bd', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebab8ff6-ab81-5f16-8588-a49b4c0a02bd'}, {'abstract': 'Romney’s imaginary Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/the-futility-of-bipartisan-outreach/', 'snippet': 'Romney’s imaginary Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama has tried — desperately, and far beyond the point at which it made any kind of sense — to reach out across the partisan divide. He has bent over backwards to be nice to bankers. He has clearly been uncomfortable with any kind of populist rhetoric, although that may finally be changing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Futility Of Bipartisan Outreach', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:28:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/235424af-90c3-5be8-99e6-1d1efb7aaa91', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/235424af-90c3-5be8-99e6-1d1efb7aaa91'}, {'abstract': 'In our latest feature, T tracks what stylish women are wearing to keep warm. Here, Jessica Biel, Angelina Jolie and Liv Tyler cozy up with some winter classics.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/winter-wonders-sunglasses-optional/', 'snippet': 'In our latest feature, T tracks what stylish women are wearing to keep warm. Here, Jessica Biel, Angelina Jolie and Liv Tyler cozy up with some winter classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coat that does the most usually comes in a neutral color — black, white, camel — and leans a little (or a lot) toward one of three classic styles: trench, peacoat or blazer. Here, Angelina Jolie steps out in New York in a crisp white version of the latter with just the slightest bit of sheen; the actress Liv Tyler wears the season’s lengthy proportion on a version of the perennial peacoat; and the actress Jessica Biel pairs black with orange and blue –– note the matching bag and shoes — in the most effortless way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Sunglasses Optional', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47f840c1-91ed-50b3-8123-9e6f20ee0d1d', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47f840c1-91ed-50b3-8123-9e6f20ee0d1d'}, {'abstract': 'The Penguins say Sidney Crosby, who recently returned from a concussion, will sit out two games as a precautionary measure after he took a bit hit in Monday’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/penguins-say-crosby-to-miss-next-two-games-as-precaution/', 'snippet': 'The Penguins say Sidney Crosby, who recently returned from a concussion, will sit out two games as a precautionary measure after he took a bit hit in Monday’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sidney Crosby will be held out of the Penguins’ lineup for the next two games, the team said in a statement released late Wednesday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Penguins Say Crosby to Miss Next Two Games as Precaution', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff96d3b8-a8ed-5c16-a47b-0f14f124b1e3', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff96d3b8-a8ed-5c16-a47b-0f14f124b1e3'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Adams performed plenty of ballads in his solo show at Carnegie Hall on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/arts/music/ryan-adams-at-carnegie-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Adams performed plenty of ballads in his solo show at Carnegie Hall on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Now I’m going to play a ballad,” Ryan Adams deadpanned partway through his solo concert on Tuesday night at Carnegie Hall. The joke was that he had been playing virtually nothing but ballads: one slow, perfectly poised song after another, presented so quietly that listeners leaned forward to catch each delicate moment. Between songs he wisecracked, drawing hoots and guffaws. “I don’t know why I write these kinds of songs,” he said. “I’m not sensitive at all. I’m a bastard.” Then the next song would create another gorgeously hushed communion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/adams/adams-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 655, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/adams/adams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/adams/adams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisecracks, Scattered Among Slow Tunes', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisecracks, Scattered Among Slow Tunes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADAMS, RYAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f03cd6e-6941-582f-ab46-cbd642f5f3eb', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f03cd6e-6941-582f-ab46-cbd642f5f3eb'}, {'abstract': 'A renowned perfumer’s process, now in book form.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/frederic-malle-on-perfume-making/', 'snippet': 'A renowned perfumer’s process, now in book form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you ever walked down Madison Avenue, stumbled upon a grungy overfilled trash can and inhaled the scent of roses? It may very well have been the work of the renowned perfumer Frédéric Malle of Les Editions de Parfums.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frédéric Malle | ‘On Perfume Making’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/992bf1ec-47e7-513f-95bd-5f50162f7c2c', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/992bf1ec-47e7-513f-95bd-5f50162f7c2c'}, {'abstract': 'John Scott added new refinements to this year’s “Messiah” at St. Thomas Church.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/arts/music/john-scott-leads-messiah-at-st-thomas-church-review.html', 'snippet': 'John Scott added new refinements to this year’s “Messiah” at St. Thomas Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For listeners who prefer the historical approach to Baroque style, the annual performances of Handel’s “Messiah” at St. Thomas Church set a standard that is hard to surpass. Granted, there are other period-instrument “Messiah” readings in town, most notably those offered by Trinity Church. (This year’s run begins on Sunday and includes a performance at Alice Tully Hall on Dec. 19.) But where St. Thomas has the edge is in its use of a chorus of men and boys, the younger singers drawn from its own choir school, a British tradition that stretches back beyond the time when Handel worked in England. Not that the superb, fully professional Trinity Choir has any reason to feel second best. But there is a purity in the sound of trained boy sopranos that a mixed adult choir cannot match.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/MESSIAH/MESSIAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venerable Choir and Its Guests Burnish a Holiday Tradition', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venerable Choir and Its Guests Burnish a Holiday Tradition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, John (1956-2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Thomas Church (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df411da-b802-515d-9afa-9626103a5ae9', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df411da-b802-515d-9afa-9626103a5ae9'}, {'abstract': 'As a photographer based in Kabul for Agence France-Presse, Massoud Hossaini has seen violence in the past. But never, he said, like the scene he saw Tuesday in Kabul.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/in-the-midst-of-a-horrific-scene-tears/', 'snippet': 'As a photographer based in Kabul for Agence France-Presse, Massoud Hossaini has seen violence in the past. But never, he said, like the scene he saw Tuesday in Kabul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Massoud Hossaini has never cried like this before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid a Horrific Scene, Tears', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald and David Furst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c3a54cf-9890-5453-a2bc-45028851efe3', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c3a54cf-9890-5453-a2bc-45028851efe3'}, {'abstract': 'Some members of Occupy Wall Street are making a house in East New York livable for a needy family.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/foreclosed-in-brooklyn-house-repairs-as-protest/', 'snippet': 'Some members of Occupy Wall Street are making a house in East New York livable for a needy family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a soggy cluster of balloons floating beside him, a shaggy-haired demonstrator kept watch on Wednesday inside the front gate of a dilapidated two-story home in East New York, Brooklyn. The residential block was mostly empty, except for a police car idling at the curb.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foreclosed in Brooklyn: House Repairs as Protest', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7eeb64-1b9a-5de3-8070-d2a027d4e641', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7eeb64-1b9a-5de3-8070-d2a027d4e641'}, {'abstract': 'An assistant attorney general is accused of  “a complete lack of judgment” in his handling of a gun-trafficking investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/grassley-wants-justice-official-ousted/', 'snippet': 'An assistant attorney general is accused of  “a complete lack of judgment” in his handling of a gun-trafficking investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Senator Charles E. Grassley of Iowa, the top Republican on the Senate Judiciary Committee, called Wednesday for the resignation of the head of the Justice Department’s criminal division, Lanny A. Breuer, in the latest flare-up connected to the disputed gun trafficking investigation known as Operation Fast and Furious.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grassley Wants Justice Official Ousted', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T22:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d70576f-6d86-53e8-aa11-10dbc14a2797', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d70576f-6d86-53e8-aa11-10dbc14a2797'}, {'abstract': 'Alexander Schimpf, a young German pianist, played a recital that ranged from Bach to the contemporary German composer Adrian Sieber at Zankel Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/arts/music/alexander-schimpf-plays-adrian-sieber-at-zankel-review.html', 'snippet': 'Alexander Schimpf, a young German pianist, played a recital that ranged from Bach to the contemporary German composer Adrian Sieber at Zankel Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young pianists can spend years on the contest circuit, competing for medals, cash and concerts, and occasionally getting screen time — pacing nervously backstage, opining about career challenges, perhaps even performing — in the behind-the-scenes documentaries these events inevitably generate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contest Winner Takes Stage', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contest Winner Takes Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'val