'uri': 'nyt://article/e3bdedc1-7942-51c1-bb75-7105bed050f8'}, {'abstract': 'Sites like Groupon and LivingSocial have been sending deals by e-mail. Now they also arrive by smartphone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/technology/personaltech/daily-deals-sent-right-to-your-pocket.html', 'snippet': 'Sites like Groupon and LivingSocial have been sending deals by e-mail. Now they also arrive by smartphone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daily deal services like Groupon, LivingSocial and Gilt have taken much of the work out of bargain hunting. All that’s left is to open one’s e-mail and click on the latest message from one of these services.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/business/08-SMART1/08-SMART1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/business/08-SMART1/08-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/business/08-SMART1/08-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Deals, Sent Right to Your Pocket', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daily Deals, Sent Right to Your Pocket', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LivingSocial.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c75ede5-0e2a-5d99-b55d-06707121d86f', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c75ede5-0e2a-5d99-b55d-06707121d86f'}, {'abstract': 'An experiment monitored a sleepy subway rider’s brain waves on the A Train. The map below shows where the subject drifted in and out of sleep along the route.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/07/nyregion/sleeping-on-the-a-train.html', 'snippet': 'An experiment monitored a sleepy subway rider’s brain waves on the A Train. The map below shows where the subject drifted in and out of sleep along the route.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An experiment monitored a sleepy subway rider’s brain waves on the A Train. The map below shows where the subject drifted in and out of sleep along the route.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nodding Off on the A Train', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8c8599eb-8319-5f