rom bathroom scales to security cameras, but no home theater projectors. Until Epson introduced the Megaplex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everything changed when people started writing their own apps for the iPhone. Suddenly its talents as a phone — which, at least at the outset, weren’t particularly impressive — paled in comparison to its abilities as a computer.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/business/POGUE/POGUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/business/POGUE/POGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/business/POGUE/POGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Screen, Powered by iPhone', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Screen, Powered By iPhone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Digital Audio Players', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Epson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Videophones and Videoconferencing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9482f56-1e6b-54c6-b533-23b91b92ffc6', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9482f56-1e6b-54c6-b533-23b91b92ffc6'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Police Department has increased security at Deutsche Bank’s offices in Manhattan after a letter bomb was sent to the bank’s chief executive in Frankfurt.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/n-y-p-d-steps-up-security-after-deutsche-bank-letter-bomb/', 'snippet': 'The New York Police Department has increased security at Deutsche Bank’s offices in Manhattan after a letter bomb was sent to the bank’s chief executive in Frankfurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Police Department has increased security at Deutsche Bank‘s offices in Manhattan after a letter bomb was sent to the bank’s chief executive in Frankfurt, a police spokesman told DealBook on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Step Up Security After Deutsche Bank Letter Bomb', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ACKERMANN, JOSEF', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank A.G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef5471c6-37a3-579e-af63-81ee4e6f66d0', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef5471c6-37a3-579e-af63-81ee4e6f66d0'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of society’s young women are finding professional niches for themselves in the beauty industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fashion/making-beauty-their-business.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of society’s young women are finding professional niches for themselves in the beauty industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH a swirl of honey-blond hair, feline green eyes and a blue bloodline (her great-grandfather was Marcellus Hartley, the 19th-century philanthropist, whose funeral in 1902 drew Andrew Carnegie and J. Pierpont Morgan), Lauren Remington Platt ticks off all the checkboxes of a successful socialite. She is frequently photographed at fashion galas and charity balls, including the recent M Missoni for OrphanAid Africa party and the fall benefit for the Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08SOCIALITE2_SPAN/08zSOCIALITE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08SOCIALITE2_SPAN/08zSOCIALITE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08SOCIALITE2_SPAN/08zSOCIALITE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08SOCIALITE2_SPAN/08zSOCIALITE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08SOCIALITE2_SPAN/08zSOCIALITE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty as Their Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beauty As Their Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Society and Socialites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c358abbe-452c-5275-bd7f-d918042b9fd5', 'word_count': 1824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c358abbe-452c-5275-bd7f-d918042b9fd5'}, {'abstract': 'One photographer finds terrible beauty in the aftermath of a suicide bombing in Kabul.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/lens-visual-power-in-a-horrific-scene/', 'snippet': 'One photographer finds terrible beauty in the aftermath of a suicide bombing in Kabul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed it, our colleagues on the Lens blog carry a post today about Massoud Hossaini, one of the few photographers at the scene in Kabul, Afghanistan, following a series of coordinated bombings on Tuesday, which also struck the cities of Kandahar and Mazar-i-Sharif, killing at least 63 Shiite worshipers. Taken through his own flowing tears, Mr. Hossaini’s gripping pictures of the aftermath were striking enough to appear on the front page of this newspaper, as well as The Los Angeles Times and The Washington Post. You can read Mr. Hossaini’s very personal recollection of the chaos here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Visual Power in a Horrific Scene', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-07T23:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c80355c-1f8f-55b2-a57d-eeb40471601c', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c80355c-1f8f-55b2-a57d-eeb40471601c'}, {'abstract': 'Device-based disagreements are wedging themselves between otherwise harmonious relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fashion/when-couples-find-gadgets-interfere-with-harmony.html', 'snippet': 'Device-based disagreements are wedging themselves between otherwise harmonious relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE’S an intruder in my marital bed. Bright, colorful, seductive and easy to cradle, it is capturing my husband’s attention at night. And I’ve had enough.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08DEVICES_SPAN/08DEVICES_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/fashion/08DEVICES_