grapher Mario Sorrenti and featuring models in varying states of undress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I received my first Pirelli calendar 12 years ago, through what I assumed was a glitch in the system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2012 Pirelli Calendar Gala: Dressed Up for a Dressed-Down Production', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bocelli, Andrea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brody, Adrien', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jovovich, Milla', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Julianne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Kate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Tom', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pirelli Spa', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corsica', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T00:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard S. Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c50138-15ac-57be-9c48-8fbc40f5a633', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c50138-15ac-57be-9c48-8fbc40f5a633'}, {'abstract': 'Just fill the Slobproof pen with paint and, after covering the offending mark on the wall, rinse the tip and recap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/garden/a-paint-pen-to-touch-up-the-dings.html', 'snippet': 'Just fill the Slobproof pen with paint and, after covering the offending mark on the wall, rinse the tip and recap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Living with what she describes as a family of slobs — at home, her oldest son often vigorously kicks off his shoes, dinging the walls — Debbie Wiener wanted a quick and easy way to touch up the paint, something that didn’t involve hauling out a can and a brush.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08TOOLS_SPAN/08TOOLS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08TOOLS_SPAN/08TOOLS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08TOOLS_SPAN/08TOOLS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08TOOLS_SPAN/08TOOLS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08TOOLS_SPAN/08TOOLS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Paint Pen to Touch Up the Dings', 'kicker': 'Currents | Tools', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scuff Marks and Dings, Be Gone!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T00:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOYCE&ensp;COHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afd31e70-16cc-5d60-bd2f-209a25206da8', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afd31e70-16cc-5d60-bd2f-209a25206da8'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion designer has introduced his new furniture collection at Maxfield Gallery in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/garden/from-rick-owens-fashion-to-sit-on.html', 'snippet': 'The fashion designer has introduced his new furniture collection at Maxfield Gallery in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Anyone creating their own environment is following a utopian vision,” the fashion designer Rick Owens said of his new furniture collection, introduced this week at Maxfield Gallery in Los Angeles. “Mine is a Brutalist fur on a Brutalist rock next to a Brutalist fire in a Brutalist cave.” It includes 15 “shamelessly big” pieces (including chairs, a screen, a couch, a table and a bed), made from materials like black plywood, 500,000-year-old petrified bark and alabaster. “Making furniture is my version of couture: it’s time-consuming artisanal work made in limited quantities in rare materials, customized for my favorite client, my better half, the Hun,” Mr. Owens said, referring to his wife, Michele Lamy. Prices start at about $10,000 (the Boudeuse couch, pictured, is $78,750). Maxfield, 8818 Melrose Avenue, Los Angeles; (310) 275-8818 or maxfieldla.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08FURNITURE_SPAN/08FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08FURNITURE_SPAN/08FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08FURNITURE_SPAN/08CURR6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08FURNITURE_SPAN/08FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08FURNITURE_SPAN/08FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Rick Owens, Fashion to Sit On', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Rick Owens, Fashion to Sit On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owens, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T00:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By RIMA&ensp;SUQI', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c048540-99b5-5ba1-970c-e3df25402c85', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c048540-99b5-5ba1-970c-e3df25402c85'}, {'abstract': 'Discounts on ceramics, books, Christmas accessories and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/garden/sales-at-klein-reid-and-others-deals.html', 'snippet': 'Discounts on ceramics, books, Christmas accessories and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many books are up to 85 percent off at the Bard Graduate Center, Thursday to Sunday and Dec. 15 to 18 (“Knoll Textiles: 1945-2010,” originally $70, is $21); 18 West 86th Street; (212) 501-3023 or bgc.bard.edu.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08DEALS/08DEALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08DEALS/08DEALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08DEALS/08DEALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales at Klein Reid and Others', 'kicker': 'Currents | Deals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sales on Books, Pottery, Soaps and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T00:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By RIMA&ensp;SUQI', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/79b164a1-e029-556f-83cc-6bd0a04a2368', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79b164a1-e029-556f-83cc-6bd0a04a2368'}, {'abstract': 'The latest models connect to the Internet, which means they can be adjusted from afar, and allows them to get information about the weather and adjust accordingly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/garden/home-thermostats-wallflowers-no-more.html', 'snippet': 'The latest models connect to the Internet, which means they can be adjusted from afar, and allows them to get information about the weather and adjust accordingly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COUPLE of months ago, a Silicon Valley start-up invited me to review its new home thermostat. I wasn’t expecting much.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08HOMETECH_SPAN/08HOMETECH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08HOMETECH_SPAN/08HOMETECH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08HOMETECH_SPAN/08HOMETECH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08HOMETECH_SPAN/08HOMETECH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/garden/08HOMETECH_SPAN/08HOMETECH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Thermostats, Wallflowers No More', 'kicker': 'Home Tech', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wallflower No More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thermostats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Conditioning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T00:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Gar