ased by $7.65 billion, a two-year high, as income gains failed to keep up with inflation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumer borrowing in the United States rose in October to the highest level in two years, propelled by gains in nonrevolving debt like auto and student loans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reliance on Credit in Spending Rises in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reliance On Credit In Spending Rises in U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T01:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4412f57-cc3b-54d1-929d-309740eb012d', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4412f57-cc3b-54d1-929d-309740eb012d'}, {'abstract': 'More than 600 people across China have been arrested on suspicion of selling children, according to a statement released Wednesday by the Ministry of Public Security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/asia/china-hundreds-arrested-on-child-selling-charges.html', 'snippet': 'More than 600 people across China have been arrested on suspicion of selling children, according to a statement released Wednesday by the Ministry of Public Security.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More than 600 people across China have been arrested on suspicion of selling children, according to a statement released Wednesday by the Ministry of Public Security. The statement also said 178 children had been freed. There has been greater scrutiny of trafficking in children this year, in part because of news reports by Caixin Century Weekly that shed light on child abductions and child-selling in Hunan Province. Some children were later adopted by foreigners, Caixin reported. Experts say the kidnapping and sale of children is a problem in China because of the country’s one-child policy and the cultural preference among many parents for boys. Families in many areas are fined heavily if they have more than one child and refuse to give up the others, and some officials have abducted children from such families. In addition, some parents are willing to sell girls so they can keep or try to conceive a son as their only child. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Hundreds Arrested on Child-Selling Charges', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Hundreds Arrested on Child-Selling Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T01:40:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e7c5b18-678f-5c00-b993-fd4f35bb5d04', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e7c5b18-678f-5c00-b993-fd4f35bb5d04'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors said state money meant for Parent Workshop, a group founded by State Senator Shirley L. Huntley, was stolen by close associates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/nyregion/four-charged-in-theft-of-state-aid-meant-for-parent-workshop-group.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors said state money meant for Parent Workshop, a group founded by State Senator Shirley L. Huntley, was stolen by close associates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2006, a Queens state senator, Shirley L. Huntley, set up a nonprofit group called Parent Workshop that was intended to help parents navigate the inner workings of New York City’s school system. Then she began funneling state aid to the group, whose executives had close ties to her. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/nyregion/INDICT/INDICT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 542, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '4 Accused in Theft of Aid Meant for Nonprofit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Four Accused Of Stealing Aid Intended For Nonprofit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parent Workshop Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntley, Shirley L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T01:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article'