.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — When Gov. Rick Scott rolled out his budget on Wednesday, it was to a group of reporters at a news conference at the Florida Capitol in a room packed with staff members, a far cry from the Tea Party crowd that cheered him on during his first budget announcement early this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/FLORIDA/FLORIDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/us/FLORIDA/FLORIDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/us/FLORIDA/FLORIDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Budget Adds to School Spending', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida Budget Adds to School Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7758cb78-474e-5cab-8242-d19c1d786132', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7758cb78-474e-5cab-8242-d19c1d786132'}, {'abstract': 'Columbia cannot compete with the likes of Ohio State when looking for a new football coach, but it does have its advantages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/sports/ncaafootball/columbia-in-seeking-football-coach-offers-its-own-perks.html', 'snippet': 'Columbia cannot compete with the likes of Ohio State when looking for a new football coach, but it does have its advantages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early one morning last week, inside Columbia’s subterranean athletic center in Upper Manhattan, M. Dianne Murphy leaned over a conference table and wrapped her fingers around a disposable cup of coffee. There was no time to sleep these days, she said. \xa0\xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/sports/JP-COACH-1/JP-COACH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/08/sports/JP-COACH-1/JP-COACH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/sports/JP-COACH-1/JP-COACH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/sports/JP-COACH-1/JP-COACH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/sports/JP-COACH-1/JP-COACH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions? Private Jet? Columbia Offers New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Millions? Private Jet? Columbia Offers New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivy League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/450c6a5d-ec4c-57e2-8014-cc3526a08e40', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450c6a5d-ec4c-57e2-8014-cc3526a08e40'}, {'abstract': 'Times reporters Scott Shane and David E. Sanger write about the implications of an exposed C.I.A. drone program, which had been among the most covert American intelligence-collection efforts against Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/drone-crash-in-iran-reveals-secret-u-s-surveillance-program/', 'snippet': 'Times reporters Scott Shane and David E. Sanger write about the implications of an exposed C.I.A. drone program, which had been among the most covert American intelligence-collection efforts against Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crash of Stealth C.I.A. Drone in Iran Reveals Secret U.S. Surveillance Effort | The C.I.A. RQ-170 drone that crashed in Iran last week has blown the cover off of one of the United States’ most secret intelligence-collection efforts against the country. While American and Iranian officials dispute the cause of the drone’s demise — Iranian officials say the military hacked into the drone’s control systems, Americans say the drone malfunctioned — an essential question remains: What will happen with the centerpiece of a once covert program, now that the aircraft is in Iran’s hands? Scott Shane and David E. Sanger report that the United States considered it too risky to retrieve or destroy the drone, which leaves open the possibilities that Iran could reverse-engineer the drone’s technology, or turn the aircraft over to China or Russia. You can read the full report here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drone Crash in Iran Reveals Secret U.S. Surveillance Program', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0910deb-d31c-511e-bba2-95d87bcb4490', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0910deb-d31c-511e-bba2-95d87bcb4490'}, {'abstract': 'How New York City, my family (and some sound medical advice) helped me stop wetting the bed.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/always-a-bedwetter-never-a-bride/', 'snippet': 'How New York City, my family (and some sound medical advice) helped me stop wetting the bed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a travel writer for a luxury magazine, I get to sleep in exotic locations on top of memory-foam mattresses with 800-thread-count sheets. It is a major indulgence, since for most of my childhood and my early teens, I slept on the floor on wet sheets and a rubber mat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Always a Bed-Wetter, Never a Bride', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bedwetting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lavanya Sunkara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lavanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sunkara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2860fd4-0bdc-57f6-ae9c-36156cc6ecd5', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2860fd4-0bdc-57f6-ae9c-36156cc6ecd5'}, {'abstract': 'The fact that humans have altered the ecosystem does not have to be seen as a failure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/opinion/the-age-of-man-is-not-a-disaster.html', 'snippet': 'The fact that humans have altered the ecosystem does not have to be seen as a failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SCIENTISTS interested in drawing attention to the human transformation of planet Earth have begun calling the current geological epoch the Anthropocene — the age of man. Naming an epoch is serious business — and in this case the new name is well deserved, given humanity’s enormous alteration of the Earth. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hope in the Age of Man', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hope in the Age of Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Marris, Peter Kareiva, Joseph Mascaro and Erle C. Ellis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kareiva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Erle', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Ellis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/51c51181-57d5-5d3f-aa91-edea16bdf11e', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51c51181-57d5-5d3f-aa91-edea16bdf11e'}, {'abstract': 'While the first session of the 112th Congress was defined by bruising fiscal battles, Democrats and Republicans have now moved to the election-year stage of governing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/us/politics/elections-now-dominating-congress.html', 'snippet': 'While the first session of the 112th Congress was defined by bruising fiscal battles, Democrats and Republicans have now moved to the elec