ired of the status quo and Mr. Putin. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not What Mr. Putin Planned', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not What Mr. Putin Planned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T02:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6c84a6a-e337-51a3-9c4b-9e5c15996b5a', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6c84a6a-e337-51a3-9c4b-9e5c15996b5a'}, {'abstract': 'The decision to restrict emergency contraceptives to girls below the age of 17 without prescription is an example of politics trumping science and sound policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/opinion/politics-and-the-morning-after-pill.html', 'snippet': 'The decision to restrict emergency contraceptives to girls below the age of 17 without prescription is an example of politics trumping science and sound policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once again, the politics of birth control have trumped science and sound public policy. On Wednesday, the Obama administration overruled a carefully reasoned decision by the Food and Drug Administration to make the so-called morning-after pill available without prescription to adolescent girls below the age of 17.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul