ion from Jets headquarters.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/07/jets-consultant-takes-a-closer-look/', 'snippet': 'For the next four weeks – and beyond, potentially – Tom Moore will observe all the action from Jets headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. – In his 49th season of coaching, Tom Moore described himself as a “football junkie.” And for football junkies, this is the best time of year. The postseason is near. Every play of every game is magnified, particularly for teams seeking a playoff berth, teams like the Jets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Consultant Takes a Closer Look', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:03:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b09bd2ab-3855-5220-a145-4c8a013ab271', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b09bd2ab-3855-5220-a145-4c8a013ab271'}, {'abstract': 'Sidney Crosby will be held out of the Penguins’ lineup for the next two games as a precaution, the team said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/sports/hockey/crosby-out-for-two-games.html', 'snippet': 'Sidney Crosby will be held out of the Penguins’ lineup for the next two games as a precaution, the team said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sidney Crosby will be held out of the Penguins’ lineup for the next two games as a precaution, the team said. Crosby appeared to have difficulty putting weight on his right leg after he collided with his teammate Chris Kunitz in the third period of Pittsburgh’s 3-1 loss to the Boston Bruins on Monday. Crosby played the remainder of the game. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crosby Out for Two Games', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crosby Out for Two Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a43e385-fb9b-527b-9f65-8f651a4fb20a', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a43e385-fb9b-527b-9f65-8f651a4fb20a'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey will levy taxes of about 30 percent on Syrian goods after President Bashar al-Assad of Syria suspended a free-trade agreement and imposed taxes on Turkish exports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/europe/turkey-more-trade-measures-imposed-against-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey will levy taxes of about 30 percent on Syrian goods after President Bashar al-Assad of Syria suspended a free-trade agreement and imposed taxes on Turkish exports.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Turkey will levy taxes of about 30 percent on Syrian goods after President Bashar al-Assad of Syria suspended a free-trade agreement and imposed taxes on Turkish exports, Hayati Yazici, the Turkish minister of customs and trade, said Wednesday. Relations between the two countries have deteriorated since August, when Mr. Assad failed to take steps to end a deadly crackdown on dissent. Since then, Turkey has halted joint energy exploration, joined the Arab League’s sanctions against its once-close ally, threatened to expand embargoes, and started shipping routes to Egypt and Lebanon to circumvent Syria, which has blocked Turkish trucks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: More Trade Measures Imposed Against Syria', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: More Trade Measures Imposed Against Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4de0a52-1498-567a-addf-5b9f7cf7d982', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4de0a52-1498-567a-addf-5b9f7cf7d982'}, {'abstract': 'Barely 24 hours after its debut, the United States’ “virtual embassy” in Iran was blocked from view inside the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/world/middleeast/iran-shutters-us-embassy-on-the-web.html', 'snippet': 'Barely 24 hours after its debut, the United States’ “virtual embassy” in Iran was blocked from view inside the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iranians shut down the United States’ Tehran embassy 32 years ago. They shut down its virtual Tehran embassy on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Shutters U.S. Embassy on the Web', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Shutters U.S. Embassy On the Web', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67c76326-a1e6-5e96-9bc1-1f3bff7bb736', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67c76326-a1e6-5e96-9bc1-1f3bff7bb736'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gray was a versatile singer and songwriter who was probably best known for his 1973 soul anthem, “Drift Away.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/arts/music/dobie-gray-singer-known-for-drift-away-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gray was a versatile singer and songwriter who was probably best known for his 1973 soul anthem, “Drift Away.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dobie Gray, a versatile singer and songwriter who had a handful of hits in various pop genres but who was probably best known for his enduring 1973 soul anthem, “Drift Away,” a wistful paean to all songwriters and their songs, died on Tuesday in Nashville. He was believed to be 71.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/music/gray-obit/gray-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/music/gray-obit/gray-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/music/gray-obit/gray-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dobie Gray, Singer Known for ‘Drift Away,’ Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dobie Gray, Singer Known for ‘Drift Away’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a716555-643f-5c20-8e26-9bac2ca5a441', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a716555-643f-5c20-8e26-9bac2ca5a441'}, {'abstract': 'At the request of the Florida Department of Law Enforcement, Florida A&M University said that it was delaying disciplinary action in the wake of the possible hazing death of a marching band drum major.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/us/florida-punishment-delayed-in-drum-majors-death.html', 'snippet': 'At the request of the Florida Department of Law Enforcement, Florida A&M University said that it was delaying disciplinary action in the wake of the possible hazing death of a marching band drum major.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the request of the Florida Department of Law Enforcement, Florida A&M University said on Wednesday that it was delaying disciplinary action in the wake of the possible hazing death of a marching band drum major. Earlier, the university fired its longtime band director, Julian White, and said it would suspend some students in the death of the drum major, Robert Champion. Those moves have been halted for now while the investigation continues into the death. Mr. Champion was found unresponsive on a bus parked outside an Orlando, Fla., hotel last month after a football game. He was vomiting and had complained he could not breathe before he collapsed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Punishment Delayed in Drum Major’s Death', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Punishment Delayed In Drum Major’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Champion, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida A&M University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:23:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e653c4-3bf0-5ffe-9f58-793829c41c68', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e653c4-3bf0-5ffe-9f58-793829c41c68'}, {'abstract': 'An F.B.I. advisory board voted this week to modernize an archaic definition of rape that the agency has used for more than eight decades in its tally of national crime statistics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/us/fbi-board-votes-to-broaden-definition-of-rape.html', 'snippet': 'An F.B.I. advisory board voted this week to modernize an archaic definition of rape that the agency has used for more than eight decades in its tally of national crime statistics.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An F.B.I. advisory board voted this week to modernize an archaic definition of rape that the agency has used for more than eight decades in its tally of national crime statistics. The current definition used by the F.B.I., “carnal knowledge of a female, forcibly and against her will,” has been criticized by law enforcement officials and women’s advocates as far too narrow, with the result that many rapes are excluded from the yearly Uniform Crime Report. The new definition approved by the advisory board, which met in Albuquerque on Tuesday, includes the rape of men and crimes that involve oral or anal penetration or penetration with objects. The definition must be approved by the F.B.I.’s director, Robert S. Mueller III, before it is adopted. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.B.I. Board Votes to Broaden Definition of Rape', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.B.I. Board Votes To Broaden Definition of Rape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:29:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5865ceb5-4de0-54ea-8d5b-620c1de07b68', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5865ceb5-4de0-54ea-8d5b-620c1de07b68'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said Katherine Yun, 25, of Syosset, N.Y., was crossing Broadway on foot near Driggs Avenue when she was struck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/nyregion/woman-killed-by-sanitation-truck-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said Katherine Yun, 25, of Syosset, N.Y., was crossing Broadway on foot near Driggs Avenue when she was struck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sanitation truck struck and killed a woman on Wednesday night in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, the police said. No crime was suspected, they said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Is Fatally Struck by a Sanitation Truck in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woman Is Fatally Struck by a Sanitation Truck in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T04:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5675e478-1459-5bfe-a925-7fcf66020e2d', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5675e478-1459-5bfe-a925-7fcf66020e2d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Stermer was an illustrator who achieved renown and sometimes angered the government as the art director of the influential left-wing magazine Ramparts in the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/arts/design/dugald-stermer-illustrator-and-ramparts-art-director-dies-at-74.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Stermer was an illustrator who achieved renown and sometimes angered the government as the art director of the influential left-wing magazine Ramparts in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dugald Stermer, who achieved renown and sometimes angered the government as the art director of the influential left-wing magazine Ramparts in the 1960s, died on Dec. 2 in San Francisco. He was 74.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/Stermer-obit/Stermer-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/Stermer-obit/Stermer-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/08/arts/Stermer-obit/Stermer-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dugald Stermer, Illustrator and Ramparts Art Director, Dies at 74', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dugald Stermer, 74, Illustrator and Ramparts Art Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'va