 'lead_paragraph': 'Any discussion of the challenge of trying to improve health care and curb costs with computer technology quickly turns to “silos.” Not the kind that store corn in Midwestern farms, obviously.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/07bits-silos-photo/07bits-silos-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/07bits-silos-photo/07bits-silos-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/technology/07bits-silos-photo/07bits-silos-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.E.-Microsoft Venture to Create ‘Windows’ for Health Care', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T05:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a789fe0-87e4-55dc-be68-a9d58059a061', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a789fe0-87e4-55dc-be68-a9d58059a061'}, {'abstract': 'The ingredients that went into I.B.M.’s “Jeopardy!”-winning computer Watson are steadily finding their way into I.B.M. products. The latest entry is being announced on Thursday, a so-called insight platform, which scours millions patents and scientific journals for insights and trends in drug development and discovery.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/ibms-watson-technologies-looks-for-drugs/', 'snippet': 'The ingredients that went into I.B.M.’s “Jeopardy!”-winning computer Watson are steadily finding their way into I.B.M. products. The latest entry is being announced on Thursday, a so-called insight platform, which scours millions patents and scien...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I.B.M.’s Watson computer beat two human “Jeopardy!” champions earlier this year, it was a triumphant demonstration of the company’s technology. It was great for Big Blue’s image, but it was not a moneymaker on its own.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/business/07bits-watson-photo/07bits-watson-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.B.M. Using Bits of Watson for Drug Research', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Profitable Idea From a Victory On u2018Jeopardy!u2019', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supercomputers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AstraZeneca PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bristol Myers Squibb Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': '