n': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/3613c23a-626e-5548-8a50-f68be35534a0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/3613c23a-626e-5548-8a50-f68be35534a0'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Boras represents Prince Fielder, but the frugal Mets aren’t interested. Boras takes some questions about that.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/scott-boras-on-the-thrifty-mets/', 'snippet': 'Scott Boras represents Prince Fielder, but the frugal Mets aren’t interested. Boras takes some questions about that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS – In another economic climate, Prince Fielder might be the perfect addition for the Mets. They are coming off three losing seasons, they could use a power hitter, and Fielder is only 27 years old.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scott Boras on the Thrifty Mets', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boras, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T05:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42efe98f-c85c-5f85-be48-0f0069baa0d3', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42efe98f-c85c-5f85-be48-0f0069baa0d3'}, {'abstract': 'The latest episode of “The X Factor” was supposed to showcase songs picked by viewers, but an unexplained glitch in voting meant the singers had to pick their own songs, just a day before performing them.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/x-factor-watch-a-glitch-and-then-the-singers-are-on-their-own/', 'snippet': 'The latest episode of “The X Factor” was supposed to showcase songs picked by viewers, but an unexplained glitch in voting meant the singers had to pick their own songs, just a day before performing them.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The X Factor” didn’t even try to make its manufactured drama convincing on Wednesday night’s show, which was supposed to include performances of songs chosen by viewers. There was a problem with the public voting, the host, Steve Jones, announced midway through the show, not even making a pretense of giving details or a reasonable explanation. The result, he said: Just 24 hours before going live, each of the five remaining contestants had to prepare a new song of his or her choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X Factor’ Watch: A Glitch and Then the Singers Are on Their Own', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T06:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2040918-2cb9-5dbc-97fe-a3c7b8a5b3fe', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2040918-2cb9-5dbc-97fe-a3c7b8a5b3fe'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on December 8, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/pageoneplus/corrections-december-8.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on December 8, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T06:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbbf6111-e16d-54e0-b379-a1f87fec419c', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbbf6111-e16d-54e0-b379-a1f87fec419c'}, {'abstract': 'Censorship is nothing new in India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/newswallah-censorship/', 'snippet': 'Censorship is nothing new in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian government’s most recent attempt at censorship may be mired in controversy, but it is hardly unusual. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Censorship', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T06:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/437d1d8b-cd45-5b12-90fe-c5eb5ff2aeca', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/437d1d8b-cd45-5b12-90fe-c5eb5ff2aeca'}, {'abstract': 'The FDI debate drew attention away from Lokpal. Was that by design?', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/was-fdi-just-a-smokescreen/', 'snippet': 'The FDI debate drew attention away from Lokpal. Was that by design?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In New Delhi, much like in other capitals, political gossip is often dominated by theorizing about why politicians do the things they do. In Delhi, this theorizing often arrives at an intriguing answer: Indian politicians often do one thing in order to accomplish something else altogether.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was FDI Just a Smokescreen?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T07:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb6c44f-172b-553a-b099-18194f4fefe7', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb6c44f-172b-553a-b099-18194f4fefe7'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/news-quiz-dec-8-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Dec. 8, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T07:52:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenan Christiansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christiansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/240fe24f-8cdf-59d3-834d-206040eb11fa', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240fe24f-8cdf-59d3-834d-206040eb11fa'}, {'abstract': 'On Dec. 8, 1991, leaders of three of the 15 Soviet Republics released a declaration known as the Belavezha Accords which declared that the Soviet Union was to be dissolved and succeeded by the Commonwealth of Independent States.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/dec-8-1991-soviet-republics-declare-end-of-soviet-union/', 'snippet': 'On Dec. 8, 1991, leaders of three of the 15 Soviet Republics released a declaration known as the Belavezha Accords which declared that the Soviet Union was to be dissolved and succeeded by the Commonwealth of Independent States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 8, 1991, leaders of three of the 15 Soviet Republics, Russian President Boris N. Yeltsin, Ukrainian President Leonid M. Kravchuk and the Belarusian leader Stanislav Shushkevich, released a declaration known as the Belavezha Accords, which declared that the Soviet Union was to be dissolved and succeeded by the Commonwealth of Independent States, a loose confederation of former Soviet states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 8, 1991 | Republics Declare End of Soviet Union', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T09:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52dcda23-ce6f-59da-8f38-1470053cb8c8', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt