'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6be5700-ca66-570d-a9cf-18c94c7cc3a5', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6be5700-ca66-570d-a9cf-18c94c7cc3a5'}, {'abstract': 'These days, I find most free public connections to be barely usable.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/the-frustrations-of-trying-to-connect-on-the-go/', 'snippet': 'These days, I find most free public connections to be barely usable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not so long ago, I could handle being without an Internet connection as long as I could check e-mail and do bare-bones browsing on my cellphone. But now that I keep moving more and more of what I do to the cloud, from accounting to scheduling to collaborating to storing books and documents, I find myself practically incapacitated when I’m cut off from a laptop connection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Frustrations of Trying to Connect On the Go', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a38ec7ce-23b2-5f56-818d-44e2276e3cdc', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a38ec7ce-23b2-5f56-818d-44e2276e3cdc'}, {'abstract': 'From tribesmen to billionaire philanthropists, the social value of generosity is already well known. But new research suggests it also matters much more intimately than we imagined, even down to our most personal relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/is-generosity-better-than-sex/', 'snippet': 'From tribesmen to billionaire philanthropists, the social value of generosity is already well known. But new research suggests it also matters much more intimately than we imagined, even down to our most personal relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This column appears in the Dec. 11 issue of The New York Times Magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Generous Marriage', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cd41de1-19b2-5807-95e3-09e1e9cf9b86', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cd41de1-19b2-5807-95e3-09e1e9cf9b86'}, {'abstract': 'How does your relationship rate on the generosity scale?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/quiz-do-you-have-a-generous-relationship/', 'snippet': 'How does your relationship rate on the generosity scale?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does your relationship rate on the generosity scale? Here are four questions researchers from the University of Virginia’s National Marriage Project used to measure generosity, high levels of which are predictive of a stronger relationship. Click on the box in front of your answer and then check your score. And to find out more about how generosity affects your relationship, read the New York Times Magazine column, “The Generous Marriage.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quiz: Do You Have a Generous Relationship?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3a745af-de4b-589d-b041-ac678ff44f6d', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3a745af-de4b-589d-b041-ac678ff44f6d'}, {'abstract': 'A pipeline carrying oil to a refinery in the tense Syrian city of Homs was blown up Thursday, activists and the Syrian news agency said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/blast-hits-pipeline-in-syrian-city.html', 'snippet': 'A pipeline carrying oil to a refinery in the tense Syrian city of Homs was blown up Thursday, activists and the Syrian news agency said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — A pipeline carrying oil to a refinery in the tense Syrian city of Homs was blown up Thursday, activists and the official Syrian news agency said, casting a huge pillar of black smoke over the city’s cloudy horizon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/09syria/09syria-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/09syria/09syria-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/09syria/09syria-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/09syria/09syria-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/09syria/09syria-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blast Hits Pipeline in Syrian City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blast Hits Pipeline in Syrian City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c0394a-6f5c-5f24-bcd2-9ce2addf969b', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c0394a-6f5c-5f24-bcd2-9ce2addf969b'}, {'abstract': 'Jon S. Corzine, the former chief executive of MF Global Holdings and a former United States senator and Democratic governor of New Jersey, defended his decision to invest heavily in European sovereign debt and said he was “stunned” by a huge shortfall in client funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/a-remorseful-corzine-set-to-testify-before-congress/', 'snippet': 'Jon S. Corzine, the former chief executive of MF Global Holdings and a former United States senator and Democratic governor of New Jersey, defended his decision to invest heavily in European sovereign debt and said he was “stunned” by a huge short...', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In testimony before Congress on Thursday, Jon S. Corzine, the former chief executive of MF Global Holdings and a former United States senator and Democratic governor of New Jersey, defended his decision to invest heavily in European sovereign debt and said he was “stunned” by a huge shortfall in client funds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corzine and MF Global Regulators Testify', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d5ab62-4dd5-5c85-89a6-fd20d0982170', 'word_count': 1624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d5ab62-4dd5-5c85-89a6-fd20d0982170'}, {'abstract': 'A $5.6 million sale of a 1,200-acre parcel of pristine forest just east of the Belleayre Ski Center in the Catskills is said to restrict development and storm water runoff into the New York City watershed.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/catskills-deal-benefits-new-york-watershed/', 'snippet': 'A $5.6 million sale of a 1,200-acre parcel of pristine forest just east of the Belleayre Ski Center in the Catskills is said to restrict development and storm water runoff into the New York City watershed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An important state acquisition in the Catskill Park in New York is finally being completed four years after the purchase was brokered under Gov. Eliot Spitzer’s administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catskills Deal for the New York City Watershed', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department of Environmental Conservation (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47d91fb4-a6e8-54ab-821f-75ce016c81cf', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47d91fb4-a6e8-54ab-821f-75ce016c81cf'}, {'abstract': 'European Union members that use the euro agreed to sign a treaty that would require stricter financial and fiscal discipline, but two countries with their own currencies, Britain and Hungary, refused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/business/global/ecb-cuts-rates-for-second-month-in-a-row.html', 'snippet': 'European Union members that use the euro agreed to sign a treaty that would require stricter financial and fiscal discipline, but two countries with their own currencies, Britain and Hungary, refused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European leaders, meeting until the early hours of Friday, agreed to sign an intergovernmental treaty that would require them to enforce stricter fiscal and financial discipline in their future budgets. But efforts to get unanimity among the 27 members of the European Union, as desired by Germany, failed as Britain and Hungary refused to go along for now.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Rates/Rates-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Rates/Rates-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Rates/Rates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Most European Leaders Agree to Work on Fiscal Treaty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Most European Leaders Agree on Fiscal Treaty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T12:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f07f6fb7-7705-5a06-9576-401b7f197294', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f07f6fb7-7705-5a06-9576-401b7f197294'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times is releasing a stand-alone Election 2012 app for the iPhone that brings together the essential political news from The Times and other sources around the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/get-it-now-the-timess-2012-election-app/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times is releasing a stand-alone Election 2012 app for the iPhone that brings together the essential political news from The Times and other sources around the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers of The Caucus are political junkies who need to know the latest from the campaign trail and the halls of Congress — and they don’t want to wait for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get It Now: The Times’s 2012 Election App', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd22cca-6701-514c-8ea8-ee0eb040bfdc', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd22cca-6701-514c-8ea8-ee0eb040bfdc'}, {'abstract': 'In “Young Adult,” Charlize Theron plays a pretty and poised but mean and self-pitying woman who tries to get out of a rut by returning home and reconnecting with her youth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/movies/charlize-theron-in-young-adult-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Young Adult,” Charlize Theron plays a pretty and poised but mean and self-pitying woman who tries to get out of a rut by returning home and reconnecting with her youth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shorter than a bad blind date and as sour as a vinegar Popsicle, “Young Adult” shrouds its brilliant, brave and breathtakingly cynical heart in the superficial blandness of commercial comedy. More radically than “J. Edgar” or even “Greenberg,” this movie, written by Diablo Cody and directed by Jason Reitman, challenges the dreary conventional wisdom that a movie protagonist must be likable. Along the way, it systematically demolishes a china shop full of shopworn sentimental touchstones about — for starters — high school, small-town life, heterosexuality, Minnesota and the capacity of human beings to change, learn and grow.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/movies/young-span/young-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/07/movies/young-span/young-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/movies/young-span/young-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/07/movies/young-span/young-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/07/movies/young-span/young-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once a Prom Queen, Still a Spoiled Princess', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Young Adult'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once a Prom Queen, Still a Spoiled Princess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theron, Charlize', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oswalt, Patton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cody, Diablo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reitman, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.&nbsp;O. SCOTT', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8028b67-1b01-5cfe-8c08-0fab51faf9ad', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8028b67-1b01-5cfe-8c08-0fab51faf9ad'}, {'abstract': 'Trent Richardson, a running back at the University of Alabama, could be the school’s second Heisman winner in three years.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/the-heisman-view-from-alabama-trent-richardson/', 'snippet': 'Trent Richardson, a running back at the University of Alabama, could be the school’s second Heisman winner in three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the day Thursday, The Quad will feature posts about Heisman Trophy contenders by sportswriters at the candidates’ universities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Heisman View From Alabama: Trent Richardson', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heisman Trophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ingram, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Trent', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saban, Nick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auburn University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Conference', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARQUAVIUS BURNETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marquavius', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BURNETT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfc097e7-1a2a-58e0-80ae-c9e7c6c85241', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfc097e7-1a2a-58e0-80ae-c9e7c6c85241'}, {'abstract': 'One of the more overlooked statistics in football is penalty rate, and the Giants have an edge in that department.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/week-14-n-f-l-game-probabilities-cowboys-vs-giants/', 'snippet': 'One of the more overlooked statistics in football is penalty rate, and the Giants have an edge in that department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the more overlooked statistics in football is penalty rate. Penalty yards per play is one of the more consistent attributes of N.F.L. teams, second only to offensive pass efficiency. Penalty rate’s effect on game outcomes isn’t as large as that of other team attributes, but in terms of predicting winners its consistency makes it as important as things like running efficiency and interception rates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 14 N.F.L. Game Probabilities: Cowboys vs. Giants', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bab1a61a-f38a-5b29-b456-0fff78ae7035', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bab1a61a-f38a-5b29-b456-0fff78ae7035'}, {'abstract': 'Political operatives go Hollywood, Romney goes to Iowa (through Fox News), charities go soft-sell and Medvedev goes there on Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-8/', 'snippet': 'Political operatives go Hollywood, Romney goes to Iowa (through Fox News), charities go soft-sell and Medvedev goes there on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Nagourney writes about Jay Carson and Chris Lehane, two former Democratic operatives in Washington who serve as the models for political consultants in different Hollywood movies. The Carson-inspired character was at the heart of “The Ides of March,” directed by George Clooney; Mr. Lehane is a writer and producer of “Knife Fight,” slated for release early next year, which also focuses on a political consultant. Both worked for President Bill Clinton, Mr. Nagourney writes, and “not surprisingly, each movie has an older male candidate who has sexual relations with an intern.” But more generally, he writes that the movies “go beyond the usual Hollywood glorification of political consultants, offering dark and at times unsettling accounts of what is done in the name of winning elections.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 8', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehane, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politico, The', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'v