th-feathers/', 'snippet': 'This week we pair Emily Dickinson’s classic with a series of photos taken by readers for the Lens blog’s “A World at 7 Billion” project. All of the photos we feature were tagged with the word “hope.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week our Poetry Pairing is a little different than usual. We’re matching Emily Dickinson’s classic, “‘Hope’ is the thing with feathers,” with a series of photographs rather than an article.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘Hope’ Is the Thing With Feathers', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten and Susannah Griffee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Griffee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d7bddd3-ec82-5d84-9875-4d0eafa46d8e', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d7bddd3-ec82-5d84-9875-4d0eafa46d8e'}, {'abstract': 'Jon S. Corzine, the former chief of MF Global, is appearing before the House Agriculture Committee on Thursday to answer questions about the collapse of his brokerage firm. The panel began at 9:30 A.M.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/live-blog-house-panel-hearing-on-mf-global/', 'snippet': 'Jon S. Corzine, the former chief of MF Global, is appearing before the House Agriculture Committee on Thursday to answer questions about the collapse of his brokerage firm. The panel began at 9:30 A.M.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Jon S. Corzine, the former chief of MF Global, is appearing before the House Agriculture Committee on Thursday to answer questions about the collapse of his brokerage firm and the disappearance of up to $1.2 billion in customer money. The panel began at 9:30 A.M.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: House Panel Hearing on MF Global', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T13:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ca1348f-c304-5b11-be18-6111422fbabd', 'word_count': 3553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ca1348f-c304-5b11-be18-6111422fbabd'}, {'abstract': 'Yoshiyuki Miyamae of Issey Miyake elaborates on the relationship between his compelling spring collection and O’Keeffe’s ever fresh-looking paintings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/off-the-shelf-one-hundred-flowers/', 'snippet': 'Yoshiyuki Miyamae of Issey Miyake elaborates on the relationship between his compelling spring collection and O’Keeffe’s ever fresh-looking paintings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Shelf | ‘One Hundred Flowers’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84132b30-9794-5228-b11e-4477fffd6379', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84132b30-9794-5228-b11e-4477fffd6379'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of ski resorts’ latest offerings for children.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/ski-resorts-roll-out-features-for-children/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of ski resorts’ latest offerings for children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ski industry is looking to nurture the next generation of downhillers with new attractions for the toddler set and older.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ski Resorts Roll Out Features for Children', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb03f689-ec25-59ba-88ea-2bd89e788384', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb03f689-ec25-59ba-88ea-2bd89e788384'}, {'abstract': 'St. Martin’s Press is defending one of its authors accused of lifting material for a book on Edgar Allan Poe, though critics say there are obvious similarities.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011