ituation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Fiscalizing', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:05:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41b1a77-459d-5958-95ed-4425a7beec27', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41b1a77-459d-5958-95ed-4425a7beec27'}, {'abstract': 'German authorities said Thursday that a suspicious envelope intercepted by Deutsche Bank employees was a letter bomb sent to the bank’s chief executive, Josef Ackermann.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/world/europe/letter-bomb-sent-to-german-bank-chief.html', 'snippet': 'German authorities said Thursday that a suspicious envelope intercepted by Deutsche Bank employees was a letter bomb sent to the bank’s chief executive, Josef Ackermann.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — German authorities said Thursday that a suspicious envelope intercepted by Deutsche Bank employees was a letter bomb apparently sent by an Italian anarchist organization to the bank’s chief executive, Josef Ackermann, one of the most powerful and controversial figures in European banking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter Bomb Sent to German Bank Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letter Bomb Is Sent to German Bank Chief, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bom