ations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TechCrunch', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b17fd48-539d-5a34-bcba-9d9413299b70', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b17fd48-539d-5a34-bcba-9d9413299b70'}, {'abstract': 'David Hallberg, an American who has joined the Bolshoi Ballet, appeared on “The Colbert Report.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/ballet-meets-colbert-in-unusual-pas-de-deux/', 'snippet': 'David Hallberg, an American who has joined the Bolshoi Ballet, appeared on “The Colbert Report.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I was worried; what if I can’t fire back?” David Hallberg said about his pre-show jitters before appearing Wednesday night on “The Colbert Report” on Comedy Central. The dancer, the first American to join the Bolshoi Ballet on a full-time basis, shouldn’t have worried.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballet Meets Colbert in Unusual Pas de Deux', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARNOLD, BENEDICT', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hallberg, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harpootlian, Dick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:50:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad15254b-9430-5837-9287-11cb84d38571', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad15254b-9430-5837-9287-11cb84d38571'}, {'abstract': 'The former senator testifies on the collapse of the financial firm he led.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/corzine-testifies-on-capitol-hill/', 'snippet': 'The former senator testifies on the collapse of the financial firm he led.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jon S. Corzine, the former Democratic senator from New Jersey, is back on Capitol Hill, but this time as a witness, not a politician. Mr. Corzine, also the former head of Goldman Sachs and a former New Jersey governor, had been called to testify Thursday morning about his most recent role as the former head of MF Global Holdings, a brokerage firm whose collapse in October stemmed from the European debt crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corzine Testifies on Capitol Hill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9d271ba-f1a3-5bc5-8797-2e6df74db9b3', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9d271ba-f1a3-5bc5-8797-2e6df74db9b3'}, {'abstract': 'A study finds that over the last 30 years, peak attendance at national parks has moved forward an average of four days — seemingly in tandem with a rise in park temperatures.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/time-for-a-vacation-climate-change-and-the-human-clock/', 'snippet': 'A study finds that over the last 30 years, peak attendance at national parks has moved forward an average of four days — seemingly in tandem with a rise in park temperatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the natural world, scientists have documented a vast range of shifts in biological behavior related to climate change, from birds laying their eggs earlier to bears emerging earlier from hibernation in time for the first blossom of spring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time for a Vacation? Climate Change and the Human Clock', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hibernation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Acadia National Park (Me)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T14:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/583954a9-5ac4-5c43-978e-62f2ec199f30', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583954a9-5ac4-5c43-978e-62f2ec199f30'}, {'abstract': 'Wider availability of morning-after pill is rejected, G.M. re-examines the Volt because of safety concerns, time to scrub the halls and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/thursday-reading-wider-availability-of-morning-after-pill-rejected/', 'snippet': 'Wider availability of morning-after pill is rejected, G.M. re-examines the Volt because of safety concerns, time to scrub the halls and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Wider Availability of Morning-After Pill Is Rejected', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a957bd70-f453-54a8-b422-82c0cff93ca9', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a957bd70-f453-54a8-b422-82c0cff93ca9'}, {'abstract': 'Mundane containers become clever, quirky and surprisingly graceful in Hess’s show at L.A.’s Acme Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/seeing-things-matthias-merkel-hess/', 'snippet': 'Mundane containers become clever, quirky and surprisingly graceful in Hess’s show at L.A.’s Acme Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buckets, trash cans, gas cans, laundry hampers and milk crates. Matthias Merkel Hess, a Los Angeles artist, reimagines mundane containers, made to hold everything from gasoline to dirty socks, as ceramic sculptures that are clever, quirky and surprisingly graceful. In his show “Bucketry,” at L.A.’s Acme Gallery, on view through Dec. 21, he has expanded his quotidian repertory to include several new forms, including those of Styrofoam coolers and laundry hampers, the latter rendered in stoneware in various shapes and sizes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Things | Matthias Merkel Hess', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25665e3d-e1c0-54a1-9ec8-7b5ab6532898', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25665e3d-e1c0-54a1-9ec8-7b5ab6532898'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/what-were-reading-327/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gothamist: A tour of the dining possibilities in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Br