'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS-slide-Q9KK/11HOURS-slide-Q9KK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours: Lake Placid, N.Y.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Placid (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0e94b1b8-ad24-5fcf-b3b6-db06e3e86431', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0e94b1b8-ad24-5fcf-b3b6-db06e3e86431'}, {'abstract': 'Lake Placid has quietly been adding non-Olympic attractions, including farm-to-table restaurants, classier lodgings and a gleaming convention center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/36-hours-lake-placid-ny.html', 'snippet': 'Lake Placid has quietly been adding non-Olympic attractions, including farm-to-table restaurants, classier lodgings and a gleaming convention center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE PLACID can feel cryogenically frozen in time — 1980 to be exact, which was when this secluded pocket of the Adirondacks hosted its second Winter Olympics. The towering ski jumps and toboggan runs, not to mention the “Miracle on Ice” hockey rink, look much as they did when Jimmy Carter was in office. But over the last few decades Lake Placid has quietly been adding non-Olympic attractions, including sophisticated farm-to-table restaurants, higher-grade lodgings and a gleaming convention center. Luckily the downtown has not lost its aura of Adirondack authenticity, with A-frame cottages and unpretentious boutiques drawing plenty of nonskiers. If the town were not smothered in Olympic logos, visitors might forget about its Olympics connections and think they had wandered into an idyllic Swiss hamlet.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN/11HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN/11HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN/11HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN/12HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11HOURS_SPAN/12HOURS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours: Lake Placid, N.Y.', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lake Placid, N.Y.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Placid (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lionel Beehner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lionel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beehner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0159f8-1521-531a-b296-b15bc3352e20', 'word_count': 1394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0159f8-1521-531a-b296-b15bc3352e20'}, {'abstract': 'The veteran director Garry Marshall, in New York for the premiere of his film “New Year’s Eve,” is a fan of Anne Hathaway, but for Oscar host he’s all for Billy Crystal.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/a-veteran-in-billy-crystals-corner/', 'snippet': 'The veteran director Garry Marshall, in New York for the premiere of his film “New Year’s Eve,” is a fan of Anne Hathaway, but for Oscar host he’s all for Billy Crystal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director Garry Marshall’s career has spanned 50 years of television and movies and produced classics and blockbusters from “Happy Days” to “Beaches” and “Pretty Woman.” He is a member of Hollywood’s old guard, which means he’s a transplanted New Yorker with a borscht belt sense of humor, and he’s still on his first wife (49 years and counting). He’s also a veteran of ensemble pieces (“Valentine’s Day”) and light, family-pleasing fare (“The Princess Diaries”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Veteran in Billy Crystal’s Corner', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:28:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f527a0cb-42e6-570d-a651-71bc612c3310', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f527a0cb-42e6-570d-a651-71bc612c3310'}, {'abstract': 'The HBO host Bill Maher will perform a new show, “CrazyStupidPolitics: Bill Maher Live From Silicon Valley,” that will be broadcast free on a new Yahoo! channel that will offer other original comedy programming and licensed content.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/bill-maher-concert-will-introduce-new-yahoo-comedy-channel/', 'snippet': 'The HBO host Bill Maher will perform a new show, “CrazyStupidPolitics: Bill Maher Live From Silicon Valley,” that will be broadcast free on a new Yahoo! channel that will offer other original comedy programming and licensed content.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Explaining why he has joined the growing ranks of comedians seeking to harness the Internet to bring their acts directly to audiences, Bill Maher, the political satirist and host of HBO’s “Real Time With Bill Maher,” naturally invoked a historical metaphor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Maher Concert Will Introduce New Yahoo! Comedy Channel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3862eb2a-67db-5402-a95c-59c0c1d1fe18', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3862eb2a-67db-5402-a95c-59c0c1d1fe18'}, {'abstract': 'A new ProPublica analysis makes clear that money and influence are still factors in presidential pardons.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/need-a-pardon-donate-to-a-congressman-being-white-also-helps/', 'snippet': 'A new ProPublica analysis makes clear that money and influence are still factors in presidential pardons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a decade since the uproar over President Bill Clinton’s eleventh-hour pardon of Marc Rich—the fugitive financier whose ex-wife gave $450,000 to the Clinton Presidential Library—prompted his successor to reform the pardons process. President George W. Bush increased the role of career officials in the Justice Department’s small pardons office in recommending which applications should be granted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Need a Pardon? Donate to a Congressman. Being White Also Helps', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Marc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ProPublica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:35:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b936b703-f044-5219-8bea-67fa20bff156', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b936b703-f044-5219-8bea-67fa20bff156'}, {'abstract': 'The latest trial, had it been more successful, could have paved the way for a new approval.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/new-setback-for-avastin-as-breast-cancer-treatment/', 'snippet': 'The latest trial, had it been more successful, could have paved the way for a new approval.', 'lead_paragraph': '12/9/11 | Updated to correct references to data on disease progression and to the statistical significance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Setback for Avastin as Breast Cancer Treatment', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genentech Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c877647-a44f-52ae-9bc4-022eef98e588', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c877647-a44f-52ae-9bc4-022eef98e588'}, {'abstract': 'In a new play, two women who have waited tables or written about food make fun of that world.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/pig-a-play-roasts-the-food-obsessed/', 'snippet': 'In a new play, two women who have waited tables or written about food make fun of that world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a performance of “Pig: A Restaurant” at the Upright Citizens Brigade Theater in Chelsea on Wednesday night, a deranged celebrity chef unveiled a drink list featuring “bacon-infused bourbon” and “pork cheek bitters.” A locavore praised the taste of edible weeds picked along the Brooklyn-Queens Expressway. And a food publicist fretted that a photographer’s flash might compromise “the integrity of the food’s color story.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pig,’ a Play, Roasts the Food-Obsessed', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T15:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jed Lipinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43f61409-a1c5-50ec-b419-121d146202e2', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43f61409-a1c5-50ec-b419-121d146202e2'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Huntsman on Thursday accused his two leading rivals of being part of a Washington culture that is destroying trust with Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/huntsman-lashes-out-at-romney-gingrich/', 'snippet': 'Jon Huntsman on Thursday accused his two leading rivals of being part of a Washington culture that is destroying trust with Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jon M. Huntsman Jr. on Thursday accused his two leading rivals for the Republican presidential nomination of being part of a Washington culture that is destroying trust with the American people and blocking solutions to the nation’s biggest problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huntsman Lashes Out at Romney and Gingrich', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 