ml', 'snippet': 'The fantasy of Hugh Jackman: your dream lover, your gay best friend, and no embarrassing meltdowns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT takes two to be Hugh. The most adored performer on Broadway at the moment is, without question, Hugh Jackman, both of him. “Hugh Jackman: Back on Broadway,” at the Broadhurst Theater, has created this season’s most virulent case of box office fever by presenting the snazziest single double act New York has known since Alice Ripley and Emily Skinner played Siamese twins in “Side Show” 14 years ago.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11JACKMAN1_SPAN/11JPJACKMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11JACKMAN1_SPAN/11JPJACKMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11JACKMAN1_SPAN/11JPJACKMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11JACKMAN1_SPAN/11JPJACKMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11JACKMAN1_SPAN/11JPJACKMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hugh Jackman Keeps His Pants On', 'kicker': 'Arts & Leisure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hugh Jackman Keeps His Pants On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackman, Hugh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T16:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/671d0aee-d2d8-5e09-a9b3-f36050059711', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/671d0aee-d2d8-5e09-a9b3-f36050059711'}, {'abstract': 'The Big East gets bigger (and, strangely) more western, and the B.C.S. complaining season has begun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/sports/a-case-of-whines.html', 'snippet': 'The Big East gets bigger (and, strangely) more western, and the B.C.S. complaining season has begun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of college sports have to wonder what rabbit hole they stepped into on days like Wednesday, when the headlines are full of developments involving sexual abuse charges against coaches, alongside the news that the Big East just absorbed five teams whose only common trait is that they are east of Guam. Not that they are remotely comparable events, but put them together with the N.C.A.A.’s sudden belief that it can step in and cure everything and more rumblings that a so-overdue-the-fines-are-tripling football playoff is “inevitable,” and well, we’re expecting Alice to join our Wonderland any minute now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Case of Whines', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Case of Whines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c30227f-34ad-5a76-baca-ad20bfc6616a', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c30227f-34ad-5a76-baca-ad20bfc6616a'}, {'abstract': 'One base, one spread, one topping, more than 500 combinations. All of them good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/magazine/the-holiday-finger-food-combination-generator.html', 'snippet': 'One base, one spread, one topping, more than 500 combinations. All of them good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unless you have servants, there is an inclination toward panic when guests drop by, invited or not. I get that. But given that you are likely to entertain at some point in the next two weeks, you might as well arm yourself, by which I mean: buy some stuff. If you lay in a few good-tasting and versatile supplies, you can produce some pretty mean little canapés (or canapé-like creations) without much effort.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '80', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bittman-circular/bittman-circular-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Holiday Finger-Food Combination Generator', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Holiday Finger-Food Combination Generator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T16:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5530efe4-ec91-5b1a-81de-4cb8989a454c', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5530efe4-ec91-5b1a-81de-4cb8989a454c'}, {'abstract': 'Todd S. Stern faced criticism from fellow envoys, activists and one impassioned heckler, Abigail Borah, a student at Middlebury College, over what they saw as foot dragging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/science/earth/us-climate-envoy-seems-to-shift-position-on-timetable-for-new-international-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Todd S. Stern faced criticism from fellow envoys, activists and one impassioned heckler, Abigail Borah, a student at Middlebury College, over what they saw as foot dragging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURBAN, South Africa — Facing sharp criticism from fellow envoys, environmental activists and one impassioned heckler, the chief American negotiator at a climate conference here on Thursday shifted his position — or at least his language — on a timetable for a new set of international talks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/climate/climate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/climate/climate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/world/climate/climate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Climate Envoy Seems to Shift Stance on Timetable for New Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Climate Envoy Seems to Shift Stance on Timetable for New Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Todd D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durban (South Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T16:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/391feb53-0b6d-53c7-838d-9d2e01ddd67e', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391feb53-0b6d-53c7-838d-9d2e01ddd67e'}, {'abstract': 'The Capitals hope a coaching change will be enough to jump-start the star Alex Ovechkin.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/whats-slowing-down-ovechkin/', 'snippet': 'The Capitals hope a coaching change will be enough to jump-start the star Alex Ovechkin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alex Ovechkin looks over his shoulder on the bench, he now sees a new face looking back at him. Bruce Boudreau is out, Dale Hunter is in. Whether there was a rift or not between Boudreau and his star player, it was clear the Capitals needed to make a change. The Capitals have fallen out of the last playoff spot in the Eastern Conference and were showing little signs of growth. So the bench change was made, but will it change things for the just O.K. No. 8?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ovechkin Scores, but Is He Back on Track?', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Dale', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T16:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Caponigri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caponigri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab4b7f15-e048-51f3-ae66-21673f12ebaa', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab4b7f15-e048-51f3-ae66-21673f12ebaa'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Financia