ary elections, which have been dominated so far by Islamist parties. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Audio of Egyptian Military Briefing to Foreign Reporters', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T17:39:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. DAVID GOODMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'GOODMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2929324e-7be3-56b3-9ac6-717c4d8e38ea', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2929324e-7be3-56b3-9ac6-717c4d8e38ea'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: Alex Webb 2', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/08/blogs/20111208-lens-webb-2.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: Alex Webb 2', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: Alex Webb 2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/08/blogs/20111208-lens-webb-2-slide-56XR/20111208-lens-webb-2-slide-56XR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Alex Webb 2', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T17:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c2f69152-1f09-5dfb-a2fd-a38582208f16', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c2f69152-1f09-5dfb-a2fd-a38582208f16'}, {'abstract': 'Vladimir Putin’s bringing back Soviet-style propaganda.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/commissar-putin-speaks/', 'snippet': 'Vladimir Putin’s bringing back Soviet-style propaganda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I said half-jokingly the other day that it’s sometimes hard to tell the difference between Soviet-era Russia and Putin-era Russia. Prime Minister Vladimir Putin has proved me wrong. If you ignore the relatively bountiful supply of toilet paper, it’s impossible to tell the difference. His reaction to the elections on Sunday and his complaints about foreign agitators were straight from Pravda.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commissar Putin Speaks', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T17:42:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c910e00-a3c4-5163-9a85-8e32598d0771', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c910e00-a3c4-5163-9a85-8e32598d0771'}, {'abstract': 'A resident of mainland China was arrested after he spent seven hours paddling through the sea in an effort to witness Taiwan’s upcoming presidential election, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/world/asia/china-resident-swims-to-taiwan-drawn-by-election.html', 'snippet': 'A resident of mainland China was arrested after he spent seven hours paddling through the sea in an effort to witness Taiwan’s upcoming presidential election, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAIPEI, Taiwan — A resident of mainland China was apparently so beguiled by this island’s coming elections and the promise of democracy that he spent seven hours paddling through the sea in an effort to see them with his own eyes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taiwan Vote Draws Mainland Interest, and One Mainlander', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taiwan Vote Draws Mainland Interest, and One Mainlander', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma Ying-jeou', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T17:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5779a04a-330d-5e5b-bd42-0e1551380dfc', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5779a04a-330d-5e5b-bd42-0e1551380dfc'}, {'abstract': 'Staff members at Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers, a large high school in the South Bronx near Yankee Stadium, received news that the Department of Education planned to phase out the school for poor performance, pending a vote by the Panel for Educational Policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/08/city-targets-jane-addams-h-s-for-closing/', 'snippet': 'Staff members at Jane Addams High School for Academic Careers, a large high school in the South Bronx near Yankee Stadium, received news that the Department of Educatio