 continents. An exhibition opens Thursday at Aperture in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Webb’s photographs have the compositional complexity befitting the best street photographers. But instead of wandering among urban canyons or cosmopolitan boulevards — which he has — he has redefined the genre over the course of three decades in dusty border towns and tropical climes where the streets may not even be paved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Webb’s Dialogue With the Streets', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, Norris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T18:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af6f1071-13a9-5c4f-90d5-41bc67b333c9', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af6f1071-13a9-5c4f-90d5-41bc67b333c9'}, {'abstract': 'By throwing cold water on I.M.F. involvement, Mario Draghi scared markets and made it appear that those who expected an effective financing mechanism for Europe are going to be disappointed.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/europe-disappoints-again/', 'snippet': 'By throwing cold water on I.M.F. involvement, Mario Draghi scared markets and made it appear that those who expected an effective financing mechanism for Europe are going to be disappointed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week some smart people thought they knew what was going to happen in Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Disappoints. Again.', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T18:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42bf2b0c-dcc5-57fc-9335-43d9ed2e6840', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42bf2b0c-dcc5-57fc-9335-43d9ed2e6840'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich has made selling books an integral part of his presidential campaign, raising questions of propriety and motive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/us/politics/gingrich-the-front-runner-is-still-selling-books.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich has made selling books an integral part of his presidential campaign, raising questions of propriety and motive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as he widens his lead in the polls, Newt Gingrich spends substantial time on an activity that raised questions about his ultimate motive when he was a back-of-the-pack candidate: selling and signing $25 copies of his books.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/10gingrich/10gingrich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/us/10gingrich/10gingrich-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/10gingrich/10gingrich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/10gingrich/10gingrich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/us/10gingrich/10gingrich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich, Ahead in Polls, Is Still Selling Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Gingrich, Selling Himself to Voters Means Selling Books, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T18:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byl