ri': 'nyt://article/077352cc-d169-5e21-8f61-9bf684caaaca'}, {'abstract': 'The bankruptcy of the Tribune Company had its third anniversary on Thursday. The case, which is expected to be resolved by February at the earliest, has generated  more than $200 million in professional fees.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/fees-climb-in-tribune-company-case/', 'snippet': 'The bankruptcy of the Tribune Company had its third anniversary on Thursday. The case, which is expected to be resolved by February at the earliest, has generated  more than $200 million in professional fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday is the third anniversary of the bankruptcy case of the Tribune Company, which was purchased in a highly leveraged deal by the real estate magnate Sam Zell in 2007 and went broke a year later. The lack of resolution in the $13 billion deal has tested the patience of employees, but according to a report issued on Wednesday by Fitch Ratings, the credit agency, there’s been plenty of upside for the lawyers involved in the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fees Climb in Tribune Company Case', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zell, Samuel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fitch Ratings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T18:29:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id'