he company has $21 billion on hand in cash and securities. The payouts in March will total about $200 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/business/ford-brings-back-dividend.html', 'snippet': 'The company has $21 billion on hand in cash and securities. The payouts in March will total about $200 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The Ford Motor Company on Thursday said it would resume paying quarterly dividends to its shareholders for the first time since 2006, as it closes out its third consecutive profitable year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Ford/Ford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Ford/Ford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/business/Ford/Ford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford, Feeling Secure, To Resume Dividends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ford, Feeling Secure, To Resume Dividends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T19:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd75e81-4785-5224-9793-0feb75adc1ec', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd75e81-4785-5224-9793-0feb75adc1ec'}, {'abstract': 'An average of 1,700 people a day are showing up to — perhaps — ride the slide and take a dip in the sensory deprivation tank.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/despite-higher-admission-fee-holler-show-draws-record-crowds-to-new-museum/', 'snippet': 'An average of 1,700 people a day are showing up to — perhaps — ride the slide and take a dip in the sensory deprivation tank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Museum, which recently raised its general admission price to pay for extra workers to accommodate the crowds for its exhibition of the work of Carsten Höller, said Thursday that the show – a highbrow funhouse with a slide, a sensory deprivation tank and a slow-motion carousel – had become the most highly attended show in the museum’s 35-year history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Higher Admission Fee, Höller Show Draws Record Crowds to New Museum', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Condo, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heilmann, Mary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holler, Carsten', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peyton, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tucker, Marcia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T19:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ken