ieres and splashy afterparties are scheduled for the same night. (Never fear, the Bagger will miraculously figure out a way to be in both places at once.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fight Fans, Get Ready for Thatcher vs. Nobbs', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T19:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57239f26-4082-5dae-ae98-4b5fc1cf5593', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57239f26-4082-5dae-ae98-4b5fc1cf5593'}, {'abstract': 'The Cuban artist’s sculptures subtly refracted the bizarre context of Art Basel Miami Beach through a simple and matter-of-fact visual wit.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/quiet-riot-the-art-of-wilfredo-prieto/', 'snippet': 'The Cuban artist’s sculptures subtly refracted the bizarre context of Art Basel Miami Beach through a simple and matter-of-fact visual wit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quiet Riot | The Art of Wilfredo Prieto', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlena