ack and a certain pepper-spraying cop top the list.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/2011-the-year-in-memes/', 'snippet': 'A look at what photo phenomena and Web trends captivated Internet users in 2011, courtesy of the researchers at Know Your Meme. Rebecca Black and a certain pepper-spraying cop top the list.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What Internet memes and online fads captivated the Web in 2011?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2011: The Year in Memes', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fce8350e-af15-5b88-a4f9-0b1f33fdf30d', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fce8350e-af15-5b88-a4f9-0b1f33fdf30d'}, {'abstract': 'The story of Vail’s never-frozen Epic Mountain burger. Hint: It includes a gondola ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/in-vail-colo-a-burger-that-aims-higher.html', 'snippet': 'The story of Vail’s never-frozen Epic Mountain burger. Hint: It includes a gondola ride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT has always been a challenge to serve good food at ski resorts, where restaurants and cafeterias might be 10,000 feet above sea level. Part of the problem is that much of the food in this snowy environment arrives at the mountaintop, appropriately enough, completely frozen.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11BURGER/11BURGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11BURGER/11BURGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11BURGER/11BURGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Vail, a Burger Gets a Lift', 'kicker': 'Food', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Vail, a Burger Gets a Lift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hamburgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vail (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78b3c92-509d-5c9b-a3f4-a8eb2424cce1', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78b3c92-509d-5c9b-a3f4-a8eb2424cce1'}, {'abstract': 'Becoming one with an urban environment is not something easily achieved through clothes alone, but that’s what Maria Cornejo sought to do with the pieces in her pre-fall collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/just-one-look-maria-cornejo/', 'snippet': 'Becoming one with an urban environment is not something easily achieved through clothes alone, but that’s what Maria Cornejo sought to do with the pieces in her pre-fall collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Becoming one with an urban environment is not something easily achieved through clothes alone, but that’s what Maria Cornejo sought to do with the pieces in her pre-fall collection. The prints –– a photorealistic rendering of the Brooklyn Promenade (abstracted from a picture that Cornejo snapped with her iPhone); a stretched camouflage; a pixilated jacquard that looks equally industrial and luxe––all mimic city landscapes in ways that might let their wearers fit seamlessly into the city’s graphic sprawl. Mix the collection’s stripe-like jacquards, like so, and leave the countryside behind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Maria Cornejo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornejo, Maria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6db376f-116e-5dfc-9c58-55c74f168e0d', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6db376f-116e-5dfc-9c58-55c74f168e0d'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday night’s torrential rainfall had a few unexpected effects at the party for Valentino Garavani’s new virtual museum at the IAC Building.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/star-turnout-for-valentino-rain-or-shine/', 'snippet': 'Wednesday night’s torrential rainfall had a few unexpected effects at the party for Valentino Garavani’s new virtual museum at the IAC Building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday night’s torrential rainfall had a few unexpected effects at the party for Valentino Garavani’s new virtual museum at the IAC Building. For one thing, many of the late-arriving guests were torn between watching the streaming videos of the designer’s career highlights along one wall and the streaming deluge of rain on the West Side Highway, seen through the opposite wall of windows. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Star Turnout for Valentino, Rain or Shine', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:06:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf21389-f7c3-55ec-833b-77cd9c52cc4a', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf21389-f7c3-55ec-833b-77cd9c52cc4a'}, {'abstract': 'The Chilean artist Matta, whose American profile faded as he lived in South America and Europe, is the focus of a centennial celebration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/arts/design/matta-a-centennial-celebration.html', 'snippet': 'The Chilean artist Matta, whose American profile faded as he lived in South America and Europe, is the focus of a centennial celebration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pace Gallery', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matta: ‘A Centennial Celebration’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Matta: ‘A Centennial Celebration’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/20dd1720-22f3-51dd-b94b-1da8c9f8d236', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20dd1720-22f3-51dd-b94b-1da8c9f8d236'}, {'abstract': 'Forty-eight paintings from Kenwood House, including works by Rembrandt, van Dyck and Gainsborough, will be lent to three American museums.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/arts/design/touring-show-of-rembrandt-and-other-kenwood-house-paintings.html', 'snippet': 'Forty-eight paintings from Kenwood House, including works by Rembrandt, van Dyck and Gainsborough, will be lent to three American museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenwood House in North London is known for its extraordinary collection of paintings by Rembrandt, Vermeer, van Dyck and Gainsborough. Its last owner, Edward Cecil Guinness, the first Earl of Iveagh, was a passionate collector who bequeathed Kenwood along with its art to Britain when he died in 1927. A year later the neo-Classical house and gardens opened to the public, and they have been a magnet for tourists ever since, attracting a million visitors a year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09VOGEL_SPAN/09VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09VOGEL_SPAN/09VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09VOGEL_SPAN/09VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09VOGEL_SPAN/09VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09VOGEL_SPAN/09VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Kenwood House, Borrowed Treasures', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Kenwood House, Borrowed Treasures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d6a8cfb-662c-553f-839d-40b245ac5b38', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d6a8cfb-662c-553f-839d-40b245ac5b38'}, {'abstract': 'Corin Hewitt’s installation art at Laurel Gitlen on the Lower East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/arts/design/corin-hewitt-medium-deep.html', 'snippet': 'Corin Hewitt’s installation art at Laurel Gitlen on the Lower East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laurel Gitlen ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corin Hewitt: ‘Medium/Deep’', 'kicker': 'Art In Re