ation-space-control-in-bronx-review.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition by Antoni Muntadas at the Bronx Museum of the Arts explores the protective walls, physical and otherwise, that people raise against the aliens among us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What are we all so afraid of? From spiders to rogue asteroids and beyond, but certainly people would be near the top of any list. Of particular concern would be people who are not like us. Speaking in different languages, dressing oddly, believing in strange gods, motivated by shadowy purposes and desires, they threaten everything we hold dear. So we build walls to keep them away. But since they often live among us, we also create internal systems to police them and keep them under surveillance, lest they conspire and act on their alien intentions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09CONTROL/09CONTROL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09CONTROL/09CONTROL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09CONTROL/09CONTROL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09CONTROL/09CONTROL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09CONTROL/09CONTROL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Sets Us, and Keeps Us, Apart', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Sets Us, and Kee