nyt://article/5cfcbbd4-8cc0-5304-927a-6d893dae1252'}, {'abstract': 'The orchestra’s president sees signs of hope in the new season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/despite-losses-from-strike-detroit-symphony-voices-optimism/', 'snippet': 'The orchestra’s president sees signs of hope in the new season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Detroit Symphony Orchestra detailed the financial effects of last season’s bitter six-month strike on Thursday, citing lost ticket sales and donations, but found optimism in many new audience members and better than expected revenues so far this season. “The signs this fall have been enormously positive,” said Anne Parsons, the president. Another sign was the recent three-year extension given to Leonard Slatkin, the music director, who now will have the title through the 2015-2016 season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Losses From Strike, Detroit Symphony Voices Optimism', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slatkin, Leonard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97657e87-a8b0-5ae5-97b5-b1d4a85c1246', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97657e87-a8b0-5ae5-97b5-b1d4a85c1246'}, {'abstract': 'The free agent Tyson Chandler would command a multiyear dea