n on Thursday at the Rhett Gallery  in Beaufort, S.C.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/the-caucus-click-the-scope-of-history/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry of Texas, the Republican presidential candidate, looked down the barrel of a vintage 1928 Thompson submachine gun on Thursday at the Rhett Gallery  in Beaufort, S.C.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: The Scope of History', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d7b976-35ea-513f-b713-1d14c5c27e76', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d7b976-35ea-513f-b713-1d14c5c27e76'}, {'abstract': 'Hit shows on ABC and Fox produced less-than-stellar ratings, helping CBS to its first win of the season on a Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/cbs-clips-fox-and-abc-on-wednesday-night/', 'snippet': 'Hit shows on ABC and Fox produced less-than-stellar ratings, helping CBS to its first win of the season on a Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time this season, CBS was the No. 1 network in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic on a Wednesday night, narrowly surpassing Fox and ABC while also pulling in the highest number of total viewers. The victory was at least partly the result of some key programs on the other networks underperforming. “Modern Family” on ABC had a below-average showing in the 18-to-49 demo and hit a season low in total viewers — 12.1 million. On Fox, a 90-minute episode of “The X Factor” was also down 11 percent in that demo when compared to last week, and that singing show had 10.6 million total viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS Clips Fox and ABC on Wednesday Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/226c8494-504c-5410-a3b3-5f27b1a69cd7', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/226c8494-504c-5410-a3b3-5f27b1a69cd7'}, {'abstract': 'In The Hague, Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said restrictions threatened basic freedoms and human rights and also international commerce and the free flow of information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/world/at-hague-hillary-rodham-clinton-urges-countries-not-to-restrict-internet.html', 'snippet': 'In The Hague, Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said restrictions threatened basic freedoms and human rights and also international commerce and the free flow of information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton and other international leaders urged countries and private businesses on Thursday to fight increasing efforts to restrict access to the Internet by repressive governments and even some democratic ones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/sub-diplo/sub-diplo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 664, 'widt