ded into three loosely defined, Dickens-inspired categories: past, present and future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Holiday theater divided into three loosely defined, Dickens-inspired categories: past, present and future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3/20111209-HOLIDAY-slide-SND3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Shows, in Many Permutations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fa919577-30dc-535a-b9be-6fc0333125bc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fa919577-30dc-535a-b9be-6fc0333125bc'}, {'abstract': 'Dickens and Tchaikovsky are always on the menu around town, but so are latkes and burlesque.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/theater/a-christmas-carol-and-other-holiday-shows-in-many-permutations.html', 'snippet': 'Dickens and Tchaikovsky are always on the menu around town, but so are latkes and burlesque.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Instead of making Ebenezer Scrooge watch those instructive scenes from his past, present and future, perhaps the ghosts would have completed their Grinch-eradication mission faster if they’d taken him to a show. They might have come up with a list like this one, which divides some of this year’s notable holiday productions into three loosely defined, Dickens-inspired categories: Past (for nostalgia lovers), Present (for current-events followers) and Future (for tech geeks or more adventurous-minded theatergoers). Tiny Tim may have wished God’s blessings on everyone, but be aware that not all these shows are good for families with children.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09SUBHOLIDAY2/09SUBHOLIDAY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 541, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09SUBHOLIDAY2/09SUBHOLIDAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09SUBHOLIDAY2/09SUBHOLIDAY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Theater, in Three Flavors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holiday Theater, in Three Flavors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52395a99-801a-59b4-a9b9-6607585f666f', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52395a99-801a-59b4-a9b9-6607585f666f'}, {'abstract': 'Jurors indicated that they cannot reach a verdict in the corruption case of City Councilman Larry B. Seabrook Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/jury-in-seabrook-trial-says-it-is-still-deadlocked/', 'snippet': 'Jurors indicated that they cannot reach a verdict in the corruption case of City Councilman Larry B. Seabrook Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 5:44 p.m. |\xa0The jury in the federal corruption trial of City Councilman Larry B. Seabrook indicated on Thursday that it remained unable to reach a verdict on any of the 12 counts against him after more than five days of deliberation, and suggested that jurors should be discharged no later than Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jury in Seabrook Trial Says It Is Still Deadlocked', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T21:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser and Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7e17716-c511-5845-b671-9ff3e774ad26', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7e17716-c511-