on the upswing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/new-jersey-pension-fund-commits-up-to-1-8-billion-to-blackstone/', 'snippet': 'The commitment by the New Jersey Division of Investment is the latest signal that the fund-raising climate, at least for the largest private equity firms, is on the upswing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Jersey’s pension fund has committed up to $1.8 billion to funds managed by the Blackstone Group, a big win for the money-management giant and the latest signal that the fund-raising climate, at least for the largest private equity firms, is on the upswing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.J. Pension Fund Commits Up to $1.8 Billion to Blackstone', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Blackstone Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-08T23:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15c19c38-8c4d-5255-b05a-1bbea234805b', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15c19c38-8c4d-5255-b05a-1bbea234805b'}, {'abstract': 'Exhibitions honoring Romare Bearden’s centennial are on view in New York at the Metropolitan Museum, the Schomburg Center and the Studio Museum in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/arts/design/romare-bearden-at-studio-museum-schomburg-and-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Exhibitions honoring Romare Bearden’s centennial are on view in New York at the Metropolitan Museum, the Schomburg Center and the Studio Museum in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Across the country institutions large and small, art-specific and otherwise, are celebrating the Romare Bearden centennial year. There’s a reason for this. In Bearden’s embracing art all borders are down — between personal and universal, town and country, history and myth. Africa, Europe and the Americas too are borderless. Bearden is artist in chief of the modern cosmopolis, griot in residence of the global village. All hail.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09BEARDEN/09BEARDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 756, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09BEARDEN/09BEARDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09BEARDEN/09BEARDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Griot for a Global Village', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Griot For A Global Village', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bearden, Romare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio Museum in Harlem', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}],