': 'nyt://article/44bd49db-56a5-5101-85c9-2768f9fb1a34'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees have upgraded their pitching only around the margins, taking two relievers in the Rule 5 draft.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/no-upgrades-elsewhere-so-yankees-draft-relievers/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees have upgraded their pitching only around the margins, taking two relievers in the Rule 5 draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — A league rival added perhaps the most threatening hitter in baseball, so Yankees General manager Brian Cashman was asked Thursday if he would react to it. The Los Angeles Angels now have Albert Pujols, but would that make Cashman redouble his efforts to add pitching?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Upgrades Elsewhere, So Yankees Draft Relievers', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T01:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e879a066-7fcb-57bc-a15b-d4008ed1ee48', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e879a066-7fcb-57bc-a15b-d4008ed1ee48'}, {'abstract': 'Non-techies find the @ and # symbols on Twitter don’t make much sense. So the company had to figure out a way to keep the site running for people who are more technologically adept and rely on these symbols but also work seamlessly for those who think these characters are substitutes for swear words in comics.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/a-twitter-for-my-sister/', 'snippet': 'Non-techies find the @ and # symbols on Twitter don’t make much sense. So the company had to figure out a way to keep the site running for people who are more technologically adept and rely on these symbols but also work seamlessly for those who t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early days of Twitter\xa0the company’s founders repeatedly said\xa0that expanding the service was like building a rocket ship in\xa0mid-flight. Twitter grew so quickly that it was almost impossible to add new features because engineers spent their time trying to keep the\xa0rocket ship\xa0from stalling — which often happened anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Twitter for My Sister', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Symbols and Symbolism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costolo, Dick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsey, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T01:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3411668d-4222-5259-bcc1-c5b2f99eae28', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3411668d-4222-5259-bcc1-c5b2f99eae28'}, {'abstract': 'The House Judiciary Committee brought forth little new information, but it was the most politically charged session yet about Operation Fast and Furious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/us/politics/holder-clashes-with-republicans-on-fast-and-furi