Wednesday at a hospice on Staten Island. He was 89 and lived in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/books/ROBINSON-obit/ROBINSON-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/books/ROBINSON-obit/ROBINSON-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/books/ROBINSON-obit/ROBINSON-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/books/ROBINSON-obit/ROBINSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/books/ROBINSON-obit/ROBINSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jerry Robinson, Godfather of a Comic-Book Villain, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jerry Robinson, 89, Godfather of a Comic-Book Villain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3b9a098-4a95-5be5-b4b7-9be996e095ae', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3b9a098-4a95-5be5-b4b7-9be996e095ae'}, {'abstract': 'Ian Palmer’s documentary “Knuckle” shows plenty of fights among Irish travelers, but doesn’t delve into their complexities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/movies/knuckle-documentary-about-fighting-irish-travelers-review.html', 'snippet': 'Ian Palmer’s documentary “Knuckle” shows plenty of fights among Irish travelers, but doesn’t delve into their complexities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fighting families in the documentary “Knuckle” are blood relatives with a vengeance. The movie, a no-frills affair from the first-time Irish director Ian Palmer, offers a circumscribed look inside the often-closed world of Irish travelers through their bare-knuckle fistfights. Historically nomads who were once better known as tinkers and described by Yeats as “the people of the roads,” the travelers long lived outside the mainstream, but from their on-camera showboating — as they duke it out, crow about their wins, taunt the losers and bang the drums for the next slugfest — they’re ready for their collective close-up. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN/KNUCKLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN/KNUCKLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09KNUCKLE1_SPAN/KNUCKLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brawling for Money, Clan and Just Because', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Knuckle'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brawling for Money, Clan and Just Because', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb2fbf6-a15b-5c02-8958-efde34b7e987', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb2fbf6-a15b-5c02-8958-efde34b7e987'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will mark the end of the Iraq war this month, and then move on to a campaign in which foreign policy may play only a minor role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/world/middleeast/president-obama-ends-a-war-he-never-wanted.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama will mark the end of the Iraq war this month, and then move on to a campaign in which foreign policy may play only a minor role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In October 2002, a little-known Illinois state senator joined a rally in Chicago against the Iraq war, declaring: “I’m not opposed to all wars. I’m opposed to dumb wars.” It was a defining moment for the young politician, who used this position to set himself apart in the race for the White House in 2008.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/prexy/prexy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/world/prexy/prexy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/prexy/prexy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/world/prexy/prexy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/world/prexy/prexy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wartime Leader Ends a War He Never Wanted', 'kicker': 'White House Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wartime Leader Ends a War He Never Wanted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a2482c7-09fa-5863-86c1-00502cf4074e', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a2482c7-09fa-5863-86c1-00502cf4074e'}, {'abstract': 'Americans got much poorer last quarter, as their collective household net worth suffered the biggest decline in three years.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/08/americans-got-much-poorer-last-quarter/', 'snippet': 'Americans got much poorer last quarter, as their collective household net worth suffered the biggest decline in three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans got much poorer last quarter, as their collective household net worth suffered the biggest decline in three years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Got Much Poorer Last Quarter', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b39c84e6-c5b7-5337-a30e-519b1c28f457', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b39c84e6-c5b7-5337-a30e-519b1c28f457'}, {'abstract': 'The depreciation of the dollar in 1985 started a series of events that led to fraud at the Olympus Corporation, which was later uncovered because of accounting reforms caused by the Enron scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/business/deep-roots-of-fraud-at-olympus.html', 'snippet': 'The depreciation of the dollar in 1985 started a series of events that led to fraud at the Olympus Corporation, which was later uncovered because of accounting reforms caused by the Enron scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blame it on James A. Baker III. The “Plaza Accord” that halted the appreciation of the United States dollar in 1985 was largely his doing, as Ronald Reagan’s Treasury secretary. It set in motion a series of events that led to a huge fraud at the Olympus Corporation, the Japanese maker of cameras and medical imaging equipment, that lasted more than two decades. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deep Roots of Fraud at Olympus', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deep Roots Of Fraud At Olympus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodford, Michael C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:08:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ab02662-71e5-5a2b-a21e-6918a7f09b84', 'word_count': 1527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ab02662-71e5-5a2b-a21e-6918a7f09b84'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,833 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/us/us-military-deaths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,833 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 1,833 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans this week: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/befa9fe3-cd80-5bf3-9436-0a3679a23829', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/befa9fe3-cd80-5bf3-9436-0a3679a23829'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Robert had talent for turning troubled properties into profits, including billions of dollars worth of assets from the collapse of the savings and loan industry in the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/business/joseph-e-robert-jr-investor-in-real-estate-dies-at-59.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Robert had talent for turning troubled properties into profits, including billions of dollars worth of assets from the collapse of the savings and loan industry in the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph E. Robert Jr., an international real estate investor with a talent for turning troubled properties into profits — including billions of dollars’ worth of assets from the collapse of the savings and loan industry in the 1980s — died on Wednesday at his home in McLean, Va. He was 59. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/ROBERT-obit/ROBERT-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/ROBERT-obit/ROBERT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/business/ROBERT-obit/ROBERT-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joseph E. Robert Jr., Investor in Real Estate, Dies at 59', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joseph Robert Jr., 59, Dies; Managed Assets for U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings and Loan Associations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JER Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diana B. Henriques', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/29dd7b6f-f4a9-5ccb-b8b5-6b12db41615e', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29dd7b6f-f4a9-5ccb-b8b5-6b12db41615e'}, {'abstract': 'The latest campaign ads from the Republican primary are so brazen and the politicians so unapologetic that it is only bound to get worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/opinion/race-to-the-bottom.html', 'snippet': 'The latest campaign ads from the Republican primary are so brazen and the politicians so unapologetic that it is only bound to get worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Campaign ads are often deceitful, offensive or infuriating, cynically exploiting religion or families and distorting an opponent’s record. The latest ones from the Republican primary, however, are so brazen and the politicians so unapologetic that it is only bound to get worse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Race to the Bottom', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Race to the Bottom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e7fd20d-4d59-510b-85b3-6d8876665978', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e7fd20d-4d59-510b-85b3-6d8876665978'}, {'abstract': 'In “My Piece of the Pie,” Cédric Klapisch portrays the relationship between a business wheeler-dealer and his housekeeper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/movies/my-piece-of-the-pie-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “My Piece of the Pie,” Cédric Klapisch portrays the relationship between a business wheeler-dealer and his housekeeper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “My Piece of the Pie,” Gilles Lellouche, a handsome, rough-around-the-edges French star who could be the next generation’s Gérard Depardieu, nails the essence of a predatory capitalist shark. Having spent 10 years in London, his swaggering character, Stéphane (in England he’s called Steve), is dispatched to Paris to start a hedge fund. Before he leaves, his Mephistophelean mentor counsels, “Business is not a sport for gentlemen; it’s not for good people.” To which Stéphane assures him, “I’m bad!” And he is.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09MYPIECE_SPAN/MYPIECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09MYPIECE_SPAN/MYPIECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09MYPIECE_SPAN/MYPIECE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09MYPIECE_SPAN/MYPIECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/arts/09MYPIECE_SPAN/MYPIECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prince of the Universe, and His Maid', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'My Piece of the Pie'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prince of the Universe, and His Maid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klapisch, Cedric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b73ba330-0d2a-5949-a75c-09a03047076b', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b73ba330-0d2a-5949-a75c-09a03047076b'}, {'abstract': 'Considering only a tiny sliver of small business owners are especially wealthy, mom and pop have a lot to gain from the payroll tax, paid for by millionaires.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/opinion/the-real-way-to-help-small-business.html', 'snippet': 'Considering only a tiny sliver of small business owners are especially wealthy, mom and pop have a lot to gain from the payroll tax, paid for by millionaires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With only a week to go before Congress adjourns for the holidays, Congress has yet to renew federal unemployment benefits or the payroll tax cut that will expire at year-end. Unfortunately, Republican leaders seem far more interested in advancing their partisan aims than helping millions of struggling American families. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Way to Help Small Business', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Real Way to Help Small Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Susan M', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0330e1c-8054-5719-9172-d6b6f3392b7f', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0330e1c-8054-5719-9172-d6b6f3392b7f'}, {'abstract': 'While Gov. Andrew Cuomo revamped the state income tax code, voters and taxpayers were left out of the debate. This is no way to run a government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/opinion/you-mean-those-people-who-put-me-here.html', 'snippet': 'While Gov. Andrew Cuomo revamped the state income tax code, voters and taxpayers were left out of the debate. This is no way to run a government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York’s legislators began arriving in Albany on Tuesday morning, and, by late Wednesday night, the Legislature had voted to revamp the entire state income tax code. The Senate voted less than half an hour after Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s 19,000 word bill was made public. As for the voters and taxpayers? They were out of the loop. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Mean Those People Who Put Me Here?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Mean Those People Who Put Me Here?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T02:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9d576ba-d7a4-5ca7-9b16-fb6a986fa212', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9d576ba-d7a4-5ca7-9b16-fb6a986fa212'}, {'abstract': 'The contract, agreed on in principle several weeks ago, includes a 12 percent reduction in player salaries, a limit to the length of player contracts and a host of other changes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/sports/basketball/nba-owners-and-players-ratify-labor-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The contract, agreed on in principle several weeks ago, includes a 12 percent reduction in player salaries, a limit to 