 the country has been reflecting on its success as a top trade partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/business/global/chinas-10-year-ascent-to-trading-powerhouse.html', 'snippet': 'As China celebrates its 10th anniversary since joining the World Trade Organization, the country has been reflecting on its success as a top trade partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — As China heads into a weekend of speeches celebrating its 10 years as an official member of the global trade community, the rest of the world may want to contemplate the exported $49 microwave oven and the imported $85,000 Jeep Grand Cherokee.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/WTO/WTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/business/WTO/WTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/WTO/WTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/business/WTO/WTO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/business/WTO/WTO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s 10-Year Ascent to Trading Powerhouse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rise of a Trading Power, in 10 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protectionism (Trade)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T03:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d43973e-b994-5b8e-a462-1b42c14173e7', 'word_count': 1435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d43973e-b994-5b8e-a462-1b42c14173e7'}, {'abstract': 'The American Heritage Dictionary recognized an expression, then got an outcry from an immigrants’ advocacy group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/us/anchor-baby-a-term-redefined-as-a-slur.html', 'snippet': 'The American Heritage Dictionary recognized an expression, then got an outcry from an immigrants’ advocacy group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does the term “anchor baby” mean? If you were to look it up in the American Heritage Dictionary, you would find a new definition since last week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anchor Baby: A Term Redefined as a Slur', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anchor Baby: A Term Redefined As a Slur', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 3,