ital, Tegucigalpa, on Wednesday. On Tuesday, a radio journalist, Luz Marina Paz Villalobos, and her driver were killed. The suspects in both cases were passengers on motorcycles, who got away. The killings come amid a widening scandal of accusations of police involvement in killings and drug trafficking. Mr. Landaverde was an outspoken critic of police and political corruption. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honduras: Killings Prompt a Ban on Motorcycles Carrying Passengers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honduras: Killings Prompt a Ban On Motorcycles Carrying Passengers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T03:35:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/af227370-0463-53fd-886a-d452bdb4832e', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af227370-0463-53fd-886a-d452bdb4832e'}, {'abstract': 'Hotel surveillance footage does little to illuminate what transpired inside the Sofitel hotel suite in the Dominique Strauss-Kahn case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/nyregion/hotel-video-in-strauss-kahn-case-resolves-little.html', 'snippet': 'Hotel surveillance footage does little to illuminate what transpired inside the Sofitel hotel suite in the Dominique Strauss-Kahn case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The surveillance images show Dominique Strauss-Kahn striding from an elevator at the Sofitel New York, standing at the front desk and crossing through the lobby to jump into a taxi.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/nyregion/YDSK/YDSK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hotel Video in Strauss-Kahn Case Resolves Little', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Video in Strauss-Kahn Case Resolves Little', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sofitel Hotels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diallo, Nafissatou', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T03:51:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7ec4652-828b-5cc7-857f-df60533463d3', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7ec4652-828b-5cc7-857f-df60533463d3'}, {'abstract': 'Janet Brown’s many responsibilities are necessary to achieve the life she wants for herself and her daughters. But things took a tragic turn when her mother, visiting from Jamaica, died unexpectedly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/nyregion/a-quest-for-a-better-life-interrupted-by-sudden-grief.html', 'snippet': 'Janet Brown’s many responsibilities are necessary to achieve the life she wants for herself and her daughters. But things took a tragic turn when her mother, visiting from Jamaica, died unexpectedly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet Brown is an expert at stealing naps. The driver’s seat of her minivan often doubles as a mattress, allowing her to sleep briefly during breaks in her duties as a single mother, a full-time student, a chiropractic intern and a counselor. She sleeps two to three hours each night. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quest for a Better Life, Interrupted by Sudden Grief', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Quest for a Better Life, Interrupted by Sudden Grief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica (West Indies)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T03:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba9fb6f5-6260-5075-bbe9-080c1f4bc30c', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba9fb6f5-6260-5075-bbe9-080c1f4bc30c'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s lawmakers will start contending next month with a gap of $2 billion rather than $3.5 billion, and the governor says “50 percent of the budget” is finished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/nyregion/tax-plan-passed-new-york-legislature-faces-smaller-budget-gap.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s lawmakers will start contending next month with a gap of $2 billion rather than $3.5 billion, and the governor says “50 percent of the budget” is finished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and lawmakers declared the income tax overhaul that was approved early Thursday to be a victory for millions of New Yorkers, many of whom will enjoy a modest tax cut next year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Plan Passed, Legislature Faces Smaller Budget Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Plan Passed, Legislature Faces Smaller Budget Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T03:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a064b90f-3a82-5a2d-9bff-072fe87cb7ab', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a064b90f-3a82-5a2d-9bff-072fe87cb7ab'}, {'abstract': 'A brawl broke out after Artem Anisimov pointed his stick at the Tampa Bay net and pretended to fire after scoring a goal in the second period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/sports/hockey/in-a-loss-a-rangers-gesture-leads-to-a-fight.html', 'snippet': 'A brawl broke out after Artem Anisimov pointed his stick at the Tampa Bay net and pretended to fire after scoring a goal in the second period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sniper is a common term for goal scorer, so in that respect perhaps Artem Anisimov’s response was fitting after he put the Rangers ahead with a second-period goal: He pointed his stick at the Tampa Bay net and pretended to fire. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/sports/rangers-1/rangers-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/sports/rangers-1/rangers-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_