n of dogs has prompted efforts to control their activities on streets and parks and in food establishments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call it a sign of the times: At food establishments around San Francisco, fliers are popping up with the words “No Animals Allowed” in bold red letters, and an image of a dog in a circle with a line through it. They are stamped with the official city and county seal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/sub09BCJAMES/sub09BCJAMES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/us/sub09BCJAMES/sub09BCJAMES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/sub09BCJAMES/sub09BCJAMES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/sub09BCJAMES/sub09BCJAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/us/sub09BCJAMES/sub09BCJAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Crackdown Looming as the Dog Population Rises', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Crackdown Looming As the Dog Population Rises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T05:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott James', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'James', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10b462a9-8433-5eb6-afb6-b5f418d5c94a', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10b462a9-8433-5eb6-afb6-b5f418d5c94a'}, {'abstract': 'Nicole Scherzinger deliberately deadlocks the judges to avoid being the one to send a competitor home on “The X Factor.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/x-factor-watch-nicole-scherzinger-casts-the-nondeciding-vote/', 'snippet': 'Nicole Scherzinger deliberately deadlocks the judges to avoid being the one to send a competitor home on “The X Factor.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' If you’re ever the defendant in a bench trial, pray that Nicole Scherzinger is the judge weighing your fate. Turns out she can’t make a decision. You’ll get a mistrial for sure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X Factor’ Watch: Nicole Scherzinger Casts the Nondeciding Vote', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T06:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eba4b34-c644-5158-b54b-2dade912e05d', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eba4b34-c644-5158-b54b-2dade912e05d'}, {'abstract': 'The company that manufactures the Oscars is in a wage dispute with its workers.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/a-behind-the-scenes-dispute-this-time-at-the-oscar-factory/', 'snippet': 'The company that manufactures the Oscars is in a wage dispute with its workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All season long – all two weeks of it, for us – the Bagger has been wondering if Occupy Wall Street would crop up in our Oscars coverage. After all, the Occupy movement has touched on everything from the foreclosure crisis to cultural institutions to Halloween. Why couldn’t there be an Occupy Red Carpets?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Behind-the-Scenes Dispute, This Time at the Oscar Factory', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T06:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1084170f-7a34-5c68-b4f3-a470ad2d1868', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1084170f-7a34-5c68-b4f3-a470ad2d1868'}, {'abstract': 'San Francisco International Airport not only has an extensive program of art exhibitions but also presents live music, like a performance last week by DJ Qbert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/us/live-hip-hop-music-an-airport-amenity-that-can-lure-even-non-travelers.html', 'snippet': 'San Francisco International Airport not only has an extensive program of art exhibitions but also presents live music, like a performance last week by DJ Qbert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Braun had just landed at San Francisco International Airport after a business trip to Florida. But rather than heading directly back to his home in Burlingame, he found himself lingering. “Normally I’m ready to get out of here,” he said, standing next to his roller bag. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/09BCAIRORT/09BCAIRORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/09/us/09BCAIRORT/09BCAIRORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/09BCAIRORT/09BCAIRORT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/us/09BCAIRORT/09BCAIRORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/09/us/09BCAIRORT/09BCAIRORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Hip-Hop Music, an Airport Amenity That Can Lure Even Non-Travelers', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Live Hip-Hop Music, an Airport Amenity That Can Lure Even Non-Travelers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T06:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeanne Carstensen', 'person'