ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2b4ed5cd-e6eb-556e-872b-f4f930a18517'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/morning-take-out-383/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corzine Defends His Actions at MF Global \xa0|\xa0 Jon S. Corzine, who came to Washington in 2001 as a Democratic senator from New Jersey, made a humbling return on Thursday, defending his tenure as MF Global’s top executive and sounding a note of contrition about the brokerage firm’s startling collapse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T13:32:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a1aefb0-0482-55f8-9f6e-0cde48ab59e3', 'word_count': 1853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a1aefb0-0482-55f8-9f6e-0cde48ab59e3'}, {'abstract': 'The acquisition of Blue Coat — the third enterprise software transaction in seven days — is yet another sign that deal-making in the sector is heating up.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/thoma-bravo-acquires-blue-coat-systems-for-1-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of Blue Coat — the third enterprise software transaction in seven days — is yet another sign that deal-making in the sector is heating up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An investor group, led by the private equity firm Thoma Bravo, announced on Friday that it had agreed to purchase Blue Coat Systems, a maker of enterprise security and network software, for $1.3 billion in cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thoma Bravo Acquires Blue Coat Systems for $1.3 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Coat Systems Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thoma Bravo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T13:33:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09e85439-9071-51f2-adb2-35633ac393ee', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09e85439-9071-51f2-adb2-35633ac393ee'}, {'abstract': 'Did they just kill the euro?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/the-summit-to-end-all-summits/', 'snippet': 'Did they just kill the euro?', 'lead_paragraph': 'European stocks are up today, and I have no idea why. I’m with Felix Salmon — this looks like a disastrous meeting. More austerity, more posing of the crisis, wrongly, as being all about fiscal deficits; no mechanism for ECB funding. Somehow southern Europe is supposed to deflate its way to prosperity, while everyone runs a trade surplus, presumably against that potentially habitable planet we’ve discovered 600 light-years away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Summit To End All Summits', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T13:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'sectio