l', 'snippet': 'The Olympic skier on her favorite runs, extreme weather gear and where in the world she most wants to ski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER learning to ski on tiny Buck Hill in Minnesota, the Olympic skier Lindsey Vonn took her first ski trip to Keystone, Colo., when she was 7 years old. Since then, the gold medalist has gone on to ski all over the world, from her home in Vail, Colo., to the frigid slopes of Finland. Here, excerpts from an e-mail exchange on some highs and lows. DANIELLE MATTOON', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11COVER/11cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 877, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11COVER/11COVER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11COVER/11COVER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lindsey Vonn on the Cold and the Cool', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lindsey Vonn On the Cold And the Cool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vonn, Lindsey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Mattoon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mattoon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbcb2177-af77-5a31-bc85-43c447158cd2', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbcb2177-af77-5a31-bc85-43c447158cd2'}, {'abstract': 'Aside from the gear and the travel and the hundreds of dollars on lift tickets, skiing as a family can’t be beat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/on-taking-the-family-skiing.html', 'snippet': 'Aside from the gear and the travel and the hundreds of dollars on lift tickets, skiing as a family can’t be beat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SKIING has never been easy. Fun as all get-out, reliably exhilarating, but a hassle. Triple that if you are trying to pull it off as a family. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CARR_SPAN/11CARR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CARR_SPAN/11CARR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CARR_SPAN/11CARR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CARR_SPAN/11CARR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CARR_SPAN/11CARR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Family Ski Trip: Why Do We Do It?', 'kicker': 'Why We Do It', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid the Boots and Bindings: Family Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:16:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88949a2e-402d-5a87-b889-5c267d8edc4a', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88949a2e-402d-5a87-b889-5c267d8edc4a'}, {'abstract': 'The music consultants for the Oscars telecast will be the composer Hans Zimmer and the hip-hop multihyphenate Pharrell Williams. That’s right.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/the-oscars-music-mash-up/', 'snippet': 'The music consultants for the Oscars telecast will be the composer Hans Zimmer and the hip-hop multihyphenate Pharrell Williams. That’s right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not quite Ice Cube on Eames, but this year’s music consultants for the Oscars are a bit of an odd pairing: the composer Hans Zimmer and the producer and singer Pharrell Williams will take the audience on a “musical journey,” the telecast’s producers, Brian Grazer and Don Mischer, said in a statement released by the Academy on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Oscars’ Music Mash-Up', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffdf2d9e-a3c6-597a-8727-be99076f044d', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffdf2d9e-a3c6-597a-8727-be99076f044d'}, {'abstract': 'New ski clinics for women are aimed at serious skiers and taught by prize-winning experts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/womens-ski-clinics-around-the-united-states.html', 'snippet': 'New ski clinics for women are aimed at serious skiers and taught by prize-winning experts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SKI clinics for women have been around for years, but in past decades the emphasis was more on basic skills than jumping off cliffs, with ample time set aside for shopping or going to the spa. Now women who want to maximize their skills may want to take another look at these multiday programs. In recent years resorts have been adding more and more women-only clinics that are aimed at serious skiers and taught by prize-winning experts. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CLINIC1/11CLINIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 965, 'width': 338, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CLINIC1/11CLINIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CLINIC1/11CLINIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Women-Only Ski Clinics Go Way Beyond the Snowplow', 'kicker': 'Technique', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Women Way Beyond The Snowplow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cindy Hirschfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cindy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirschfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9243abfc-9915-5ff2-87e9-586a915f333f', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9243abfc-9915-5ff2-87e9-586a915f333f'}, {'abstract': 'Cremations boom in tough times, senate blocks head of new consumer agency, twitter tries to simplify its service and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/friday-reading-cremations-boom-in-tough-economic-times/', 'snippet': 'Cremations boom in tough times, senate blocks head of new consumer agency, twitter tries to simplify its service and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Cremations Boom in Tough Economic Times', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2caa8bd8-011e-5bbb-a03e-4853d9988253', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2caa8bd8-011e-5bbb-a03e-4853d9988253'}, {'abstract': 'Gifts from the kitchen can be sweet treats, savory oils, marinated cheese or dry-mix bags of a favorite pancake or muffin recipe.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/holiday-gifts-from-your-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'Gifts from the kitchen can be sweet treats, savory oils, marinated cheese or dry-mix bags of a favorite pancake or muffin recipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of my favorite holiday gifts, both given and received, have come from the kitchen. One year I made homemade bread, flavored with cherries and nuts and twisted to look like a candy cane. A good friend of mine regularly gives decadent raspberry chocolate truffles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Gifts From Your Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d24e88-acdd-5e9b-ab46-c10c3e19c42e', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d24e88-acdd-5e9b-ab46-c10c3e19c42e'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Bird, who directed “The Incredibles,” makes his live-action-feature directorial debut with the $145 million Tom Cruise vehicle “Mission: Impossible — Ghost Protocol.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/movies/brad-bird-directs-mission-impossible-ghost-protocol.html', 'snippet': 'Brad Bird, who directed “The Incredibles,” makes his live-action-feature directorial debut with the $145 million Tom Cruise vehicle “Mission: Impossible — Ghost Protocol.