1-12-09T15:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48895526-a64f-5751-9dfb-c3032172de44', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48895526-a64f-5751-9dfb-c3032172de44'}, {'abstract': 'For years the neglected cousin of more popular Utah resorts, the Canyons has been reborn as Canyons Resort, complete with a snow “beach” and a heated chairlift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/canyons-ski-resort-park-city-utah.html', 'snippet': 'For years the neglected cousin of more popular Utah resorts, the Canyons has been reborn as Canyons Resort, complete with a snow “beach” and a heated chairlift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW years ago, I packed my skis and did something every winter sports enthusiast should do at least once in a lifetime: take a trip to Utah, a place known for its powder. I met a friend in Salt Lake City and spent a week bouncing between four resorts. We flew around aspens at Deer Valley and nailed jump turns off a ridge at Robert Redford’s Sundance Resort. At Snowbird I sailed weightlessly through three feet of the airiest, steepest, untracked powder I’d ever skied.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CANYONS1_SPAN/11CANYONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CANYONS1_SPAN/11CANYONS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CANYONS1_SPAN/11CANYONS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CANYONS1_SPAN/11CANYONS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/travel/11CANYONS1_SPAN/11CANYONS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaching for the Sky in Utah', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reaching for The Sky in Utah', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Neville', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neville', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab27def-cdea-5051-ab1f-75fe244ec6a6', 'word_count': 2860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab27def-cdea-5051-ab1f-75fe244ec6a6'}, {'abstract': 'This slopeside hotel combines the amenities of a luxury hotel with the coziness of a condo, and its ecological ethos is not too self-righteous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/travel/viceroy-snowmass-snowmass-village-colo-hotel-review.html', 'snippet': 'This slopeside hotel combines the amenities of a luxury hotel with the coziness of a condo, and its ecological ethos is not too self-righteous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UPSHOT', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/