: 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c64671-4ff4-5549-99f5-116d0d033a29', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c64671-4ff4-5549-99f5-116d0d033a29'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time in American history, a major political party may be choosing between two leading presidential candidates neither of whom is Protestant. But prejudice remains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/us/politics/on-religion-broad-mindedness-and-bigotry-among-voters.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time in American history, a major political party may be choosing between two leading presidential candidates neither of whom is Protestant. But prejudice remains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in American history, a major political party may be choosing between two leading presidential candidates who are not Protestant. If current polling holds through the Jan. 3 Iowa caucuses and beyond, the Republican nomination will come down to a choice between a Latter-day Saint, or Mormon, and a Roman Catholic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/sub-beliefs2/sub-beliefs2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/sub-beliefs2/sub-beliefs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/us/sub-beliefs2/sub-beliefs2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Faith and Family Values at Issue for Republicans', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faith and Family Values at Issue for Republicans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T15:42:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72cfb295-c7b8-53a6-b51e-4a67ef25e51f', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72cfb295-c7b8-53a6-b51e-4a67ef25e51f'}, {'abstract': 'It’s surprising that there aren’t more vehement public demands for more research on the risks of long-term exposure to Beijing’s worsening air quality.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/now-do-you-see-the-smog/', 'snippet': 'It’s surprising that there aren’t more vehement public demands for more research on the risks of long-term exposure to Beijing’s worsening air quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — This week, as smog forced the closure of roads and the cancellation of flights in northern China, my Beijing landlord called. “The pollution is awful,” he said. “Don’t open your windows, and definitely don’t go outside.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Do You See the Smog?', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords