 County, Conn. “I’m just a dumb American,” she says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BACKGROUND The child of a deep-pocketed, deep-rooted family — she is a member of the Daughters of the American Revolution — she came to New York City via Alabama, Bronxville, N.Y., and Fairfield County, Conn. “I’m just a dumb American,” she says. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth Lee Sample', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elizabeth Lee Sample', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sample, Elizabeth Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7514889-d991-5af5-83ff-7c80954a481c', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7514889-d991-5af5-83ff-7c80954a481c'}, {'abstract': 'A 60-square-mile town, about 70 miles from Manhattan, is among the most inviting places to keep and ride a horse in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/realestate/newtown-conn-living-in-enjoy-the-horses-skip-the-urban-circus.html', 'snippet': 'A 60-square-mile town, about 70 miles from Manhattan, is among the most inviting places to keep and ride a horse in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY may have lost a lot of pastureland to subdivisions over the years, but Connecticut’s horses aren’t galloping off in retreat. There are 11 of them per square mile, according to the College of Agriculture and Natural Resources at the University of Connecticut. That makes the state’s horse population among the densest in the country (Kentucky has a mere eight per square mile).', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/realestate/11LIVING-IN_SPAN/11LIVING-IN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/realestate/11LIVING-IN_SPAN/11LIVING-IN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/realestate/11LIVING-IN_SPAN/11LIVING-IN_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/realestate/11LIVING-IN_SPAN/11LIVING-IN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/realestate/11LIVING-IN_SPAN/11LIVING-IN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enjoy the Horses; Skip the Urban Circus', 'kicker': 'Living In | Newtown, Conn.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enjoy the Horses; Skip the Urban Circus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newton (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T17:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 