in Los Angeles and at shopbop.com. “To be sold in America feels like such an achievement,” says the designer. “If you make it in the U.S., you can make it anywhere.” The collection’s clean white boat neck sundresses, plaid trousers and workman’s denim jackets pair beautifully with her handbags, which come in two basic styles: a two-tone tote and a more structured satchel. “My collection is literally my wardrobe” says Doligé. “I love designers like Poiret and Yves Saint Laurent, but my collection is special to me because I can actually afford to wear it every day!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Press | Laurence Doligé Makes Her Stateside Debut', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T18:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d52379-1e90-579b-bc2e-5a0f2cc509aa', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d52379-1e90-579b-bc2e-5a0f2cc509aa'}, {'abstract': 'MF Global’s former chief executive, Jon S. Corzine, was gingerly questioned by the House Agriculture Committee for almost three hours on Thursday, in the end saying little enlightening about the firm’s collapse or missing customer money.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/corzines-testimony-came-with-plenty-of-caveats/', 'snippet': 'MF Global’s former chief executive, Jon S. Corzine, was gingerly questioned by the House Agriculture Committee for almost three hours on Thursday, in the end saying little enlightening about the firm’s collapse or missing customer money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MF Global’s former chief executive, Jon S. Corzine, was gingerly questioned by the House Agriculture Committee for almost three hours on Thursday, in the end saying little enlightening about the firm’s collapse or the customer money that has gone missing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corzine’s Testimony Came With Plenty of Caveats', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T18:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/049b3319-5404-5af3-95c5-0841083b1f7e', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/049b3319-5404-5af3-95c5-0841083b1f7e'}, {'abstract': 'By handing out citations, the police hope to clamp down on scofflaw bicyclists.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/barrels-and-police-try-to-slow-prospect-park-bicyclists/', 'snippet': 'By handing out citations, the police hope to clamp down on scofflaw bicyclists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bright orange barrels appeared last month, making a short, downhill section of Brooklyn’s Prospect Park seem like a highway construction zone. And still not everybody slowed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Crack Down on Prospect Park Bicyclists', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':