}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/475f4522-837a-5dee-a673-279036bc1568', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/475f4522-837a-5dee-a673-279036bc1568'}, {'abstract': 'Readers share their craziest #mywipeout stories for the Travel section’s special ski issue.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/readers-share-their-mywipeout-stories/', 'snippet': 'Readers share their craziest #mywipeout stories for the Travel section’s special ski issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of the Travel section’s special Ski issue, we’re asking readers to share their craziest #MyWipeOut stories. We want to hear about your death-defying runs, your scariest spills or that time you went off piste and got lost. Leave a comment below or tweet using the hashtag #mywipeout. Next week we’ll post some highlights. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Share Their #MyWipeOut Stories', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5649fe95-6b29-5162-91d9-6b98dc7e13d5', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5649fe95-6b29-5162-91d9-6b98dc7e13d5'}, {'abstract': 'India Ink spoke to Gopal Chandra Misra, the chief fire officer for the Delhi fire department, to find out more about fire safety measures in India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/q-and-a-on-kolkata-hospital-fire/', 'snippet': 'India Ink spoke to Gopal Chandra Misra, the chief fire officer for the Delhi fire department, to find out more about fire safety measures in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India Ink spoke to Gopal Chandra Misra, the chief fire officer for the Delhi fire department, to find out more about fire safety measures in India, in the wake of a fire at a private hospital in Kolkata that killed at least 94, government officials say. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘What Can the Government Do?’', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f3b104e-fa65-5367-8a0d-9074b12f0577', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f3b104e-fa65-5367-8a0d-9074b12f0577'}, {'abstract': 'Minneapolis funk band The Original 7even (formerly known as The Time) have a new song about an old funk topic—Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/america-have-you-heard-the-time-sings-about-twitter/', 'snippet': 'Minneapolis funk band The Original 7even (formerly known as The Time) have a new song about an old funk topic—Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are a few songs in the world that, no matter what, will get people off their seats and onto the dance floor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America, Have You Heard? The Time Sings About Twitter', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:36:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/169f8fa7-b601-514a-ac77-7eae35d51c5d', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/169f8fa7-b601-514a-ac77-7eae35d51c5d'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers sound off on why they don’t have (or don’t use) pretax commuter benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/why-you-dont-have-the-commuter-tax-break/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers sound off on why they don’t have (or don’t use) pretax commuter benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So here is what was easily the most entertaining reporting moment putting together this weekend’s Your Money column about pretax commuter benefits: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why You Don’t Have the Commuter Tax Break', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e67c76d-5dfc-59fb-86d4-9562701649f3', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e67c76d-5dfc-59fb-86d4-9562701649f3'}, {'abstract': 'A person needs to earn at least $150,000 to be considered “rich,” according to the median response of Americans in a new Gallup survey. That’s not quite President Obama’s definition.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/who-counts-as-rich/', 'snippet': 'A person needs to earn at least $150,000 to be considered “rich,” according to the median response of Americans in a new Gallup survey. That’s not quite President Obama’s definition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve written plenty of times about how little Americans know about the distribution of income in the United States, and how many rich people don’t realize they’re rich, at least relative to the rest of the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Counts as ‘Rich’?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:40:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dea159c-1b81-5f79-bd7a-5aea1cc58ca7', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dea159c-1b81-5f79-bd7a-5aea1cc58ca7'}, {'abstract': 'University recruiting sessions by JPMorgan Chase and Goldman Sachs were disrupted this week by stealth protesters from the Occupy Princeton movement.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/an-orange-and-black-eye-for-2-banks/', 'snippet': 'University recruiting sessions by JPMorgan Chase and Goldman Sachs were disrupted this week by stealth protesters from the Occupy Princeton movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Princeton University, the alma mater of financial bigwigs like Carl C. Icahn, is not typically thought of as a hotbed of anticorporate ardor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Orange and Black Eye for 2 Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:43:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5973924-faa4-5d2a-9e67-d5f0b69fc270', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5973924-faa4-5d2a-9e67-d5f0b69fc270'}, {'abstract': 'The editorial director of Newsmax Media said it planned to go ahead with the debate and had “every reassurance” that Donald Trump was still planning to participate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/newsmax-says-trump-debate-is-full-steam-ahead/', 'snippet': 'The editorial director of Newsmax Media said it planned to go ahead with the debate and had “every reassurance” that Donald Trump was still planning to participate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Great Donald Trump Debate (well, maybe slightly less great than its organizers had hoped) is still going forward even with just two committed candidates, its organizers said Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newsmax Says Trump Debate Is ‘Full Steam Ahead’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coz, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ion Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newsmax Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:53:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc2d7c1f-4b82-511f-aa81-25776d4b1fa6', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc2d7c1f-4b82-511f-aa81-25776d4b1fa6'}, {'abstract': 'From Notting Hill, the Duchess’s $100 dress looks like the right response to England’s woes.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/just-getting-on-with-it/', 'snippet': 'From Notting Hill, the Duchess’s $100 dress looks like the right response to England’s woes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the last few days I’ve been in London on assignment, staying at the Portobello Hotel, where — my friend Tim Blanks tells me — he used to visit Nico in the ’70s. “It may have been the first boutique hotel in London,” he said, recalling that the front-desk man in the Nico era wore a cropped Vivienne Westwood top with feather trim.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Getting On With It', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chalayan, Hussein', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westwood, Vivienne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vanity Fair', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zara', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T19:56:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ho