e)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Estabrook, Barry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chick-fil-A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taco Bell Corp', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T21:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d50b346b-60c8-59fb-922d-82133503a33b', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d50b346b-60c8-59fb-922d-82133503a33b'}, {'abstract': '“Batman: The Black Mirror” enters our hardcover graphic books best sellers list at No. 1. The story features Dick Grayson, the former Robin, filling in for the Dark Knight and encountering a new evil.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/batman-soars-to-no-1/', 'snippet': '“Batman: The Black Mirror” enters our hardcover graphic books best sellers list at No. 1. The story features Dick Grayson, the former Robin, filling in for the Dark Knight and encountering a new evil.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Batman: The Black Mirror” enters our hardcover graphic books best sellers list at No. 1. The story features Dick Grayson, the former Robin, filling in for the Dark Knight and encountering a new evil: a man called the Dealer who traffics in the weapons of supervillains. Complicating things is the return of Commissioner Gordon’s son, James, who is a psychopath. The story, written by Scott Snyder and illustrated by Jock, is incredibly compelling and reads even better as a collected edition than it did as single issues. You can read our profile of Mr. Snyder here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Batman’ Soars to No. 1', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Entertainment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T21:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9939480-a258-5cfa-95db-0d0c12ea9f7b', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9939480-a258-5cfa-95db-0d0c12ea9f7b'}, {'abstract': 'The 1944 musical “Meet Me in St. Louis,” starring Judy Garland and directed by Vincente Minnelli, is coming out in a new Blu-ray edition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/movies/homevideo/meet-me-in-st-louis-on-blu-ray.html', 'snippet': 'The 1944 musical “Meet Me in St. Louis,” starring Judy Garland and directed by Vincente Minnelli, is coming out in a new Blu-ray edition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH its bleak, film-noir imagery and barely suppressed undertone of suicidal despair, Frank Capra’s “It’s a Wonderful Life” has somewhat mysteriously assumed an unshakable position as America’s official holiday film. But for those in search of a more vibrant, warmhearted and subtly melancholic seasonal celebration there is Vincente Minnelli’s 1944 musical “Meet Me in St. Louis,” which Warner Home Video will release this week in a superbly restored Blu-ray edition.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11KEHR_span/11KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11KEHR_span/11KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11KEHR_span/11KEHR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11KEHR_span/11KEHR_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/11KEHR_span/11KEHR_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Golden Days of Yore', 'kicker': 'DVD', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Happy Golden Days of Yore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Vincente', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garland, Judy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blu-Ray Disc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T21:48:13+0000