ia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/30fd9b7c-60f1-52eb-9157-b66ac2a91043', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/30fd9b7c-60f1-52eb-9157-b66ac2a91043'}, {'abstract': 'After a week of hard-hitting criticism of his surging rival, Mitt Romney scaled back his assault, contrasting himself with Newt Gingrich but not criticizing him directly.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/romney-taps-brake-on-gingrich-attacks/', 'snippet': 'After a week of hard-hitting criticism of his surging rival, Mitt Romney scaled back his assault, contrasting himself with Newt Gingrich but not criticizing him directly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa — Wrapping up a week of varied and hard-hitting attacks on Newt Gingrich, Mitt Romney on Friday stepped back his assault at a town-hall-style meeting here, contrasting himself with Mr. Gingrich but never forcefully criticizing him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Taps Brake on Gingrich Attacks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T21:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a706d9d0-886e-52bc-80d4-3038d8c62a4a', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a706d9d0-886e-52bc-80d4-3038d8c62a4a'}, {'abstract': 'Dayne Crist played at Notre Dame under Charlie Weis, who was hired by the Jayhawks this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/former-notre-dame-quarterback-to-visit-kansas/', 'snippet': 'Dayne Crist played at Notre Dame under Charlie Weis, who was hired by the Jayhawks this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlie Weis became known as a prolific recruiter when he was the head coach at Notre Dame, luring highly touted prospects like Michael Floyd, Jimmy Clausen and Manti Te’o to campus. In search of his first big recruiting coup as the new coach at Kansas, Weis may go back to one of his highly regarded prospects at Notre Dame: quarterback Dayne Crist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Notre Dame Quarterback to Visit Kansas', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weis, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T21:59:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c580ce1a-5240-5b50-84b4-14978c618b35', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c580ce1a-5240-5b50-84b4-14978c618b35'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Levine cancelled the last remaining dates on his schedule and withdrew from all productions he had planned to lead next season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/james-levine-withdraws-indefinitely-from-conducting-at-the-met/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Levine cancelled the last remaining dates on his schedule and withdrew from all productions he had planned to lead next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Levine, the Metropolitan Opera’s ailing music director, has withdrawn from conducting this season and the next at the house, where he has been a musical force for 40 years, the Met and Mr. Levine said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James Levine Withdraws From Conducting at the Met, Until at Least 2013', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luisi, Fabio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T22:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c94b6ff7-fad9-502a-82c5-d1b6d9fe4bd1', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c94b6ff7-fad9-502a-82c5-d1b6d9fe4bd1'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh is best, but a broiler can crisp ones made in advance.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/latkes-party-planning/', 'snippet': 'Fresh is best, but a broiler can crisp ones made in advance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Latkes really do taste best when savored immediately after frying while they are still crisp-edged and brittle. Still, frying them during your average holiday party can be a somewhat arduous endeavor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latkes Party Planning', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T22:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c543f6d6-250a-5f6c-a7e8-bd73b0e157f4', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c543f6d6-250a-5f6c-a7e8-bd73b0e157f4'}, {'abstract': 'Francisco Costa showed a stunning and focused collection of wool and leather suits, dresses and coats at the pre-fall presentation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/just-one-look-calvin-klein/', 'snippet': 'Francisco Costa showed a stunning and focused collection of wool and leather suits, dresses and coats at the pre-fall presentation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Buy now, wear now,” is a phrase we hear a lot during the pre-fall presentations, with designers showing clothes better suited to summer (when they’ll be delivering to stores) than to the fall they’re prefacing. Not so at Calvin Klein, where Francisco Costa showed a stunning and focused collection of wool and leather suits, dresses and coats (lots of coats), all of which carried their tight seams and rather ’90s silhouettes with terrific poise, and all of which will transition beautifully into chillier climates. Here, a wool felt single breasted coat over a sleeveless dress of the same fabric with a skirt tucked into the softest, rolling pleats says it all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Calvin Klein', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_h