: '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e45ad3-6fa7-56ae-877a-aaff9f0af5a0', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e45ad3-6fa7-56ae-877a-aaff9f0af5a0'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition of collages at the Heckscher Museum in Huntington showcases early works that resonate with the excitement of the new and slightly forbidden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/nyregion/at-the-heckscher-works-torn-from-life.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition of collages at the Heckscher Museum in Huntington showcases early works that resonate with the excitement of the new and slightly forbidden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title “Ripped: The Allure of Collage” hinges on a bit of clever wordplay, suggesting gym-toned bodies and six-pack abs. Of course, collage originally involved torn paper rather than taut muscles. But the hint of sexiness is appropriate, since collage is one of modern art’s most seductive mediums, in which cast-off and non-art materials are assembled into avant-garde objects. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11ARTSLI1/11ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 849, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11ARTSLI1/11ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11ARTSLI1/11ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Heckscher, Works Torn From Life', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At the Heckscher, Works Torn From Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heckscher Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-09T23:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1f42d1-884c-50e5-8608-003d21dbf47a', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1f42d1-884c-50e5-8608-003d21dbf47a'}, {'abstract': 'Westchester will resonate with a rich and varied mix of vocal offerings — musical-theater classics, 20th-century British choral works and jazz versions of seasonal favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/nyregion/holiday-vocal-offerings-abound-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'Westchester will resonate with a rich and varied mix of vocal offerings — musical-theater classics, 20th-century British choral works and jazz versions of seasonal favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FROM a strictly musical perspective, holidays and the human voice are a match made in heaven. As if to prove the point, Westchester County will, in the coming weeks, resonate with a rich and varied mix of vocal offerings — among them musical-theater classics, 20th-century British choral works and jazz versions of seasonal favorites.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11ARTSWE1_SPAN/11ARTSWE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', '