 mountain in the distance, could almost seem cruelly mocking. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/arts/10CENTER/10CENTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 195, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/10/arts/10CENTER/10CENTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 195}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/arts/10CENTER/10CENTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/arts/10CENTER/10CENTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/arts/10CENTER/10CENTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The How of an Internment, but Not All the Whys', 'kicker': 'Museum Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The How of an Internment, but Not All the Whys', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T00:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/417e12d3-6463-51b6-8c2e-ef4e6552f85d', 'word_count': 1531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/417e12d3-6463-51b6-8c2e-ef4e6552f85d'}, {'abstract': 'Those who can locate Il Sogno, tucked in a gauntlet of gas stations and fast food places in Port Chester, will find a warm welcome waiting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/nyregion/il-sogno-in-port-chester-is-a-nice-surprise.html', 'snippet': 'Those who can locate Il Sogno, tucked in a gauntlet of gas stations and fast food places in Port Chester, will find a warm welcome waiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IL SOGNO is in many ways surprising. Tucked within a gantlet of brightly lighted gas stations and fast-food operations, this roadside restaurant hardly shouts its presence. Its location — just past a complicated intersection where Boston Post Road meets Regent Street — creates an additional distraction for first-timers trying to find the place.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINEWE3/11DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINEWE3/11DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINEWE3/11DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warm Welcome, Made in a Whisper', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Port Chester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Warm Welcome, Made in a Whisper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Chester (NY)', 'rank': 1,