ast.html', 'snippet': 'The American forces still in Iraq are continuing their patrols, scouring for explosives and trying to ensure that departing convoys leave safely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Every other American soldier in Iraq, it seemed, was strapping duffel bags to the roofs of armored trucks, dismantling bases and joining the convoys hurtling south through the desert, toward the Kuwaiti border and the promise of home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/world/iraq/iraq-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/world/iraq/iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/world/iraq/iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting to Leave, Last U.S. Troops in Iraq Stay Vigilant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waiting for Their Turn to Leave Iraq, American Troops Stay Vigilant to the Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier'