 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oils and Fats', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condiments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pickles and Relishes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sauces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:41:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan M. Novick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c61695bd-4bcf-52db-a456-c9ba95b1d922', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c61695bd-4bcf-52db-a456-c9ba95b1d922'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government plans to reverse decades of man-made degradation in the Gulf of Mexico. But the question is where will the big money come from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/opinion/rescue-for-the-gulf-of-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government plans to reverse decades of man-made degradation in the Gulf of Mexico. But the question is where will the big money come from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration this week officially began what it hopes will be a sustained push to reverse decades of man-made degradation in the Gulf of Mexico. The trigger for this effort is last year’s disastrous BP oil spill. But the administration’s strategy goes beyond repairing immediate damages, to the task of restoring the entire ecosystem to good health.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescue for the Gulf', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rescue for the Gulf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earmarks (Finance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3fa1ded-ea2e-5fd8-9393-db78462abd55', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3fa1ded-ea2e-5fd8-9393-db78462abd55'}, {'abstract': 'A federal grand jury in Brooklyn indicted a house painter in Edmonton, Alberta, on Friday for aiding in a 2009 suicide bombing that killed five American soldiers in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/world/americas/canadian-sayfildin-tahir-sharif-charged-in-iraq-bombing.html', 'snippet': 'A federal grand jury in Brooklyn indicted a house painter in Edmonton, Alberta, on Friday for aiding in a 2009 suicide bombing that killed five American soldiers in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A federal grand jury in Brooklyn indicted a house painter in Edmonton, Alberta, on Friday for aiding in a 2009 suicide bombing that killed five American soldiers in Iraq. In addition to five murder charges, the suspect, Sayfildin Tahir Sharif, was charged with conspiring to kill Americans abroad and providing material support to a terrorist conspiracy. Mr. Tahir Sharif, 39, who also goes by other names, has been jailed since his arrest in Edmonton in late January. His lawyer, Bob Aloneissi, said Mr. Tahir Sharif denied the charges, adding that officials seem to have exaggerated the impact of his client’s remarks about the war in Iraq. “It’s hard to understand how he had a hand in murder in Iraq when he was here in Edmonton,” Mr. Aloneissi said. An extradition hearing is scheduled for next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canadian Charged in Iraq Bombing', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canadian Charged in Iraq Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edmonton (Alberta)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4ccef06-41f7-5606-a1dd-30bfdaf47709', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4ccef06-41f7-5606-a1dd-30bfdaf47709'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court, facing tight deadlines before next year’s election calendar, stayed orders from a special court in San Antonio that had issued new maps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/us/politics/supreme-court-to-hear-texas-election-district-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court, facing tight deadlines before next year’s election calendar, stayed orders from a special court in San Antonio that had issued new maps.', 'lead_p