aid suspicious transactions appeared to have taken place shortly before the firm filed for bankruptcy and could be connected to its $1.2 billion shortfall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trustee liquidating MF Global’s brokerage unit has spotted suspicious trades in customer accounts that appear connected to a $1.2 billion shortfall, the trustee’s lawyer said Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trades Are Linked to Missing MF Global Funds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giddens, James W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:53:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c97a5870-7a68-52b3-9d04-dc02a3bcd939', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c97a5870-7a68-52b3-9d04-dc02a3bcd939'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration and New York City have raised treatment goals. Progress in preventing infections has stagnated, so the push is clearly needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/opinion/expanding-the-fight-against-aids.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration and New York City have raised treatment goals. Progress in preventing infections has stagnated, so the push is clearly needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Important new findings show that very early treatment of people infected with H.I.V. enhances their health and greatly lessens the likelihood that they will spread the virus that causes AIDS. We welcome the Obama administration’s announcement of a farsighted effort to treat millions more infected people abroad, especially in sub-Saharan Africa. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expanding the Fight Against AIDS', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expanding the Fight Against AIDS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfc8405a-7930-5afe-8ec4-515cbef17cdd', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfc8405a-7930-5afe-8ec4-515cbef17cdd'}, {'abstract': 'Urban Table, which opened in Morristown in April, was conceived as an upscale T.G.I. Friday’s or Houlihan’s; the crowds that have followed highlight the pent-up demand for such a place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/nyregion/at-an-upscale-hangout-a-menu-built-for-speed.html', 'snippet': 'Urban Table, which opened in Morristown in April, was conceived as an upscale T.G.I. Friday’s or Houlihan’s; the crowds that have followed highlight the pent-up demand for such a place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORRISTOWN needed a place like Urban Table: a hangout for young professionals desiring better dinners than the town’s post-collegiate watering holes dish out with their drafts. A place where medical residents and corporate clamberers could tear into a fun meal at a fair price. Where they could enjoy a citified setting that is dressed for success in subway tile, herringbone hardwood floors, hip lighting and artistic touches large and small.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINENJ3/11DINENJ3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINENJ3/11DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11DINENJ3/11DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At an Upscale Hangout, a Menu Built for Speed', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Morristown', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At an Upscale Hangout, A Menu Built for Speed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morristown (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T01:58:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/43525016-f450-5f4a-8785-4a43e2949709', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43525016-f450-5f4a-8785-4a43e2949709'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the European Union installed rules that would make it harder for them to take on high levels of debt without penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/world/europe/euro-zone-agrees-to-reinforce-maastricht-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Members of the European Union installed rules that would make it harder for them to take on high levels of debt without penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — In the fiscal accord reached here on Friday by members of the European Union, the nations that use the euro essentially agreed to go back to Plan A — that is, the principles and rules with which they created their common currency two decades ago. Only this time, they said, they mean it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Zone Agrees to Follow the Original Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deal Reached in Euro Zone To Follow the Original Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T02:02:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d89538c5-f054-5965-ac76-55a201bd3a60', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d89538c5-f054-5965-ac76-55a201bd3a60'}, {'abstract': 'In January, Swatch, the Swiss timepiece maker, will cut back its sales of watch components to competitors, a move that is fanning resentment of Swatch’s clout and size in the industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/business/swatch-group-to-trim-sales-of-watch-parts-to-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'In January, Swatch, the Swiss timepiece maker, will cut back its sales of watch components to competitors, a move that is fanning resentment of Swatch’s clout and size in the industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The Swatch Group may be best known for its playful, plastic watches. But it also produces mechanical movements and other watch components that it sells to most of its rival timepiece makers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/business/SWATCH1/SWATCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/10/business/SWATCH1/SWATCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/business/SWATCH1/SWATCH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/business/SWATCH1/SWATCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/business/SWATCH1/SWATCH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swatch, Supplier to Rivals, Now Aims to Cut Them Off', 'kicker': None, 'cont