enue-winter.html', 'snippet': 'Two sisters convene at Park Avenue Winter to eat some seasonal dishes and discuss books, clothes, parties and the kids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Park Avenue Winter, which changes its name, décor and menu with the seasons, began its ode to winter on Nov. 29. The entrance on 63rd Street gives way to an icily elegant dining room inspired by the Arctic Circle. A murmur of conversation warms the room, as do the chef Kevin Lasko’s offerings.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11TABLE_SPAN/11TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11TABLE_SPAN/11TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11TABLE_SPAN/11TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11TABLE_SPAN/11TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/nyregion/11TABLE_SPAN/11TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chances for Sisterly Connection', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Park Avenue Winter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chances for Sisterly Connection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T02:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ab91dc0-fb42-50e9-b171-eed7d6db83fb', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ab91dc0-fb42-50e9-b171-eed7d6db83fb'}, {'abstract': 'Starbucks experiments with a portable store made of abandoned steel shipping crates.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/a-different-kind-of-container-store/', 'snippet': 'Starbucks experiments with a portable store made of abandoned steel shipping crates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starbucks is about to unveil a new store in suburban Seattle built primarily of four used shipping containers — the large steel boxes used to store goods as they are transported long distances on boats and trucks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Different Kind of Container Store', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffeehouses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T02:29:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d64a10f-c1cc-5f23-b592-aef69cf16796', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d64a10f-c1cc-5f23-b592-aef69cf16796'}, {'abstract': 'The amazing Civil War career of Clara Barton, founder of the American Red Cross.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/09/compassion-under-fire/', 'snippet': 'The amazing Civil War career of Clara Barton, founder of the American Red Cross.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clara Barton, a 39-year-old single woman with New England written all over her dignified demeanor, could not rest easy until she found a way to join the Army. From the first day blood was spilled in 1861 — some of her old Massachusetts schoolmates were among the Yankee soldiers besieged in Baltimore by a mob of Southern sympathizers — the Civil War was what she lived for. She left a job in Washington as a Patent Office copyist for scenes of mass misery that broke all the record books. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compassion Under Fire', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barton, Clara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN RED CROSS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T02:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Stiehm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stiehm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71140c9c-686a-50c7-a1cb-3da0fd21c215', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71140c9c-686a-50c7-a1cb-3da0fd21c215'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s statements go beyond what other conservative Israeli leadership and Republican candidates have said, with experts noting that they might be counterproductive to establishing peace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/us/politics/gingrich-suggests-a-reversal-of-mideast-policy.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s statements go beyond what other conservative Israeli leadership and Republican candidates have said, with experts noting that they might be counterproductive to establishing peace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Does Newt Gingrich believe in a two-state solution to resolve the Israeli-Palestinian conflict? Democratic and Republican administrations since the 1990s have adopted that framework for peace in the Middle East, but Mr. Gingrich suggested that he might break with it, calling Palestinians an “invented” people and the current stalled peace process “delusional.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/10gingrich-span/10gingrich-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/10gingrich-span/10gingrich-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/10gingrich-span/10gingrich-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Suggests a Reversal of Mideast Policy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gingrich Suggests a Reversal of Mideast Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T02:37:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90a538e8-efb4-5f25-be0c-2760293d0b4a', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90a538e8-efb4-5f25-be0c-2760293d0b4a'}, {'abstract': 'The military council’s quick about-face leaves the task of selecting a panel that will write a constitution in the hands of a newly elected Parliament expected to be dominated by Islamists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/world/middleeast/egypt-military-scales-back-influence-on-new-constitution.html', 'snippet': 'The military council’s quick about-face leaves the task of selecting a panel that will write a constitution in the hands of a newly elected Parliament expected to be dominated by Islamists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s military rulers on Friday night appeared to withdraw a plan for extending their influence over the writing of a new constitution, evidently bowing to a chorus of criticism just days after the proposal was unveiled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Military Retracts Plan to Extend Influence Over Constitution', 'kicker': None, 'content