tion and walked into the state social services office here on Monday to demand answers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/SHOOTING/SHOOTING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracing a Mother’s Vagabond Path to Murder and Suicide in Texas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tracing a Mother’s Vagabond Path to Murder and Suicide in Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimmer, Rachelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T05:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90797883-c6e4-59aa-8151-94e8ff415605', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90797883-c6e4-59aa-8151-94e8ff415605'}, {'abstract': 'All the networks, broadcast and cable, are closely covering the Republican primary campaign, but Fox News practically owns and operates it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/us/politics/a-republican-primary-campaign-waged-on-fox-news.html', 'snippet': 'All the networks, broadcast and cable, are closely covering the Republican primary campaign, but Fox News practically owns and operates it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a reason Fox News is beginning to look like a meet-the-candidate pancake breakfast in Council Bluffs, Iowa.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Primary Campaign in Iowa Is Right at Home on Fox News', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Republican Primary Campaign in Iowa Is Right at Home on Fox News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T05:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b50295d8-02a6-5402-8745-a9a563718313', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b50295d8-02a6-5402-8745-a9a563718313'}, {'abstract': 'Juan Rivera was convicted a third time in the rape and murder of an 11-year-old girl even after DNA testing proved he did not have sex with her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/us/conviction-of-juan-rivera-in-1992-murder-reversed.html', 'snippet': 'Juan Rivera was convicted a third time in the rape and murder of an 11-year-old girl even after DNA testing proved he did not have sex with her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conviction of a man in the 1992 rape and murder of an 11-year-old baby sitter, a case that his supporters have long believed was the result of a false confession, was reversed Friday night by an Illinois appellate court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conviction Is Reversed in 1992 Rape and Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Wins Ruling In 1992 Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Juan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T05:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d397737-0b7f-5974-aee4-d78a044d6b4b', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d397737-0b7f-5974-aee4-d78a044d6b4b'}, {'abstract': 'Called “the mother of medicine in Harlem,” Dr. Petioni was a leader of many community organizations promoting health care, housing development and education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/nyregion/muriel-petioni-prominent-harlem-physician-dies-at-97.html', 'snippet': 'Called “the mother of medicine in Harlem,” Dr. Petioni was a leader of many community organizations promoting health care, housing development and education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her last days, Dr. Muriel Petioni summoned to her bedside many of the colleagues, protégés and political allies she had amassed during a lifetime as a Harlem physician and community activist. She gave each a set of marching orders: Make sure the new geriatric center at the hospital has the homey atmosphere we agreed on. Have you recruited new volunteers for the Harlem Elders program, as we discussed? The new clinic on 146th Street — let’s make sure it has the equipment it needs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/nyregion/PETIONI-obit/PETIONI-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/nyregion/PETIONI-obit/PETIONI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/nyregion/PETIONI-obit/PETIONI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Muriel Petioni, 97, Prominent Harlem Physician, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Muriel Petioni, 97, Prominent Harlem Physician, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subje