urs?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After completing work on this weekend’s Hollywood Issue, we asked the staff for their favorite movie villains. Here are ours. Who is yours?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s the Best Baddie of Them All?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T11:28:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02104ac3-d33b-5af0-b47f-76955ad952f8', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02104ac3-d33b-5af0-b47f-76955ad952f8'}, {'abstract': 'Mass protests on the streets of Moscow forced the Kremlin to confront a level of public discontent that has not been seen in Russia in decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/world/europe/thousands-protest-in-moscow-russia-in-defiance-of-putin.html', 'snippet': 'Mass protests on the streets of Moscow forced the Kremlin to confront a level of public discontent that has not been seen in Russia in decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Tens of thousands of Russians took to the streets in Moscow on Saturday shouting “Putin is a thief” and “Russia without Putin,” forcing the Kremlin to confront a level of public discontent that has not been seen here since Vladimir V. Putin first became president 12 years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/world/11russia2-span/11russia2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/world/11russia2-span/11russia2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 