about their gift spending, even as they plan to spend less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Holiday spending is a source of concern and stress for many Americans, even as they plan to spend less money, according to recent CBS News polls. A third say they feel more stress than usual about the amount they plan to spend on gifts, and half are concerned they will not be able to afford the gifts on their list this season. And with these anxieties, few anticipate spending any more this year than last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Spending Stress', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T13:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7bf126d-124c-5377-b8b4-f80e40ce4f84', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7bf126d-124c-5377-b8b4-f80e40ce4f84'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following developments on Saturday in Russia where tens of thousands of demonstrators have gathered in anti-Kremlin protest that are the largest since the fall of the Soviet Union.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/updates-on-protests-in-russia/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following developments on Saturday in Russia where tens of thousands of demonstrators have gathered in anti-Kremlin protest that are the largest since the fall of the Soviet Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede followed developments on Saturday in Russia, where tens of thousands of demonstrators gathered in Bolotnaya Square in Moscow and other cities in what organizers said were the largest anti-Kremlin protests since the fall of the Soviet Union.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on Protests in Russia', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T13:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99b50d9e-1051-538d-9177-bce09a865bea', 'word_count': 1948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99b50d9e-1051-538d-9177-bce09a865bea'}, {'abstract': 'Under Tom Coughlin, the Giants have often struggled on special teams. There has been improvement this season, but not on turning punt returns into good field position.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/sports/football/giants-cant-find-right-formula-for-consistent-special-teams.html', 'snippet': 'Under Tom Coughlin, the Giants have often struggled on special teams. There has been improvement this season, but not on turning punt returns into good field position.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. —This season, when the Giants’ special-teams coaches screened the film from last year’s brutal loss to the Philadelphia Eagles for the first time, the players in the room were appropriately solemn. Those who had lived through DeSean Jackson’s punt return for the winning touchdown winced, while those who did not — like the rookie Jacquian Williams — were nonetheless sensitive to what they were watching. \xa0', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Can’t Find Right Formula for Consistent Special Teams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Can’t Find Right Formula for Consistent Special Teams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T13:50:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37958d42-454b-5a55-afca-95fe6c622db9', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37958d42-454b-5a55-afca-95fe6c622db9'}, {'abstract': 'The ’07 Patriots and ’09 Colts went about their runs at an undefeated season in opposite ways, so there is no blueprint for success that will box in the Packers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/sports/football/packers-may-find-lessons-in-perfection-from-two-that-werent.html', 'snippet': 'The ’07 Patriots and ’09 Colts went about their runs at an undefeated season in opposite ways, so there is no blueprint for success that will box in the Packers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The game had been over for just a few moments, and the players were still struggling out of their shoulder pads when the murmuring finally reached full pitch. For weeks, the Green Bay Packers had existed in a blissful bubble, insulated by their good nature and their distant locale from the ceaseless questions, the ballooning expectations and the mounting fatigue of a chase for football’s most elusive goal. They have been dominant this season but not domineering, oddly under the radar for a defending champion on the path to something even greater. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/packers/packers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/packers/packers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/sports/packers/packers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credi