ic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T20:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Burnett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burnett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1fa778-b095-5812-be5a-906a94c1ea53', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1fa778-b095-5812-be5a-906a94c1ea53'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Logue was a poet, actor, soldier and ice-cream bandit in 85 colorful years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/arts/british-poet-christopher-logue-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Logue was a poet, actor, soldier and ice-cream bandit in 85 colorful years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christopher Logue, an English poet acclaimed for his multivolume modernization of the “Iliad” — a literary endeavor noteworthy for lasting four times as long as the Trojan War itself; even more noteworthy for its use of evocative anachronisms like Uzis, helicopters and aircraft carriers to conjure the world of Homer’s Bronze Age warriors; and still more noteworthy for having been accomplished without his knowing a word of Greek — died on Dec. 2 at his home in London.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/dogLOGUE-obit/dogLOGUE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/arts/dogLOGUE-obit/dogLOGUE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail'