paragraph': 'Let me return for a minute to Kevin O’Rourke’s recent piece on the European summit. Aside from pointing out just how bad an idea the new super-stability pact is, O’Rourke makes an important observation about what the European experience teaches us about macroeconomics:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From Europe', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-10T23:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe15eb42-6d3d-53db-ae9c-98fcc91833a6', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe15eb42-6d3d-53db-ae9c-98fcc91833a6'}, {'abstract': 'Not to be left behind in the luxury four-door-coupe craze, BMW introduced its own take in a Web reveal Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/10/bmw-6-series-gran-coupe-a-response-to-audi-a7-and-mercedes-benz-cls/', 'snippet': 'Not to be left behind in the luxury four-door-coupe craze, BMW introduced its own take in a Web reveal Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the introduction of the 6 Series Gran Coupe, BMW joins a growing list of companies, mostly German, offering swept-back sedans with coupelike silhouettes. Mercedes-Benz, Audi and Volkswagen got there before the 2013 sedan, which is scheduled to go on sale in the United States next summer. The Gran Coupe joins the recently updated 6 Series convertible and coupe models, both of which went on sale earlier this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW 6 Series Gran Coupe: A Swept-Back Response to Audi A7 and Mercedes-Benz CLS', 'ki