pe_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6b4609d3-42e3-5b66-a7ba-52c717fc3550', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6b4609d3-42e3-5b66-a7ba-52c717fc3550'}, {'abstract': 'A conference in South Africa ended with the promise to work toward a new global treaty in coming years and the establishment of a new climate fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/science/earth/countries-at-un-conference-agree-to-draft-new-emissions-treaty.html', 'snippet': 'A conference in South Africa ended with the promise to work toward a new global treaty in coming years and the establishment of a new climate fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURBAN, South Africa — After 72 hours of continuous wrangling, the 17th conference of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change wrapped up early Sunday with modest accomplishments: the promise to work toward a new global treaty in coming years and the establishment of a new climate fund.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Talks in Durban Yield Limited Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Climate Talks Yield Limited Agreement to Work Toward Replacing Kyoto Protocol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durban (South Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kyoto Protocol', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T05:43:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bcd0a67-bf90-5241-9fd7-eb2795bceb02', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcd0a67-bf90-5241-9fd7-eb2795bceb02'}, {'abstract': 'Bettors at Intrade, the political futures market, appear to be wagering that Mitt Romney’s $10,000 moment at Saturday night’s debate won’t pay off for him.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/after-10000-offer-some-bet-against-romney/', 'snippet': 'Bettors at Intrade, the political futures market, appear to be wagering that Mitt Romney’s $10,000 moment at Saturday night’s debate won’t pay off for him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saturday night’s debate will probably be best remembered for Mitt Romney offering a $10,000 bet to Gov. Rick Perry of Texas. Mr. Perry was wise to decline the wager, which concerned the language that Mr. Romney used to describe his support for a health insurance mandate in his book. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After $10,000 Offer, Some Bet Against Romney', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T06:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0259052d-3c6a-5f36-9ae8-9f7a23787d92', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0259052d-3c6a-5f36-9ae8-9f7a23787d92'}, {'abstract': 'Dec. 10, 2011 — Jeff Zeleny reports on the latest Republican presidential debate, with Newt Gingrich the clear front-runner and Mitt Romney offering a $10,000 bet to Rick Perry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001219632/the-caucus--debate-wrap-up.html', 'snippet': 'Dec. 10, 2011 — Jeff Zeleny reports on the latest Republican presidential debate, with Newt Gingrich the clear front-runner and Mitt Romney offering a $10,000 bet to Rick Perry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dec. 10, 2011 — Jeff Zeleny reports on the latest Republican presidential debate, with Newt Gingrich the clear front-runner and Mitt Romney offering a $10,000 bet to Rick Perry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/video-caucus-111210-debate/video-caucus-111210-debate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/video-caucus-111210-debate/video-caucus-111210-debate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/video-caucus-111210-debate/video-caucus-111210-debate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/us/politics/video-caucus-111210-debate/video-caucus-111210-debate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus | Debate Wrap-Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T06:43:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul|Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': 'Werschkul', 'lastname': 'Vijai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2ded4eab-1d62-57aa-9540-78c7554e166b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2ded4eab-1d62-57aa-9540-78c7554e166b'}, {'abstract': 'Nashville’s Mike Fisher, who is married to the country star Carrie Underwood, and Anaheim’s Bobby Ryan came to blows in the third period of the Predators’ 3-2 victory Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/fisher-fights-underwood-cheers/', 'snippet': 'Nashville’s Mike Fisher, who is married to the country star Carrie Underwood, and Anaheim’s Bobby Ryan came to blows in the third period of the Predators’ 3-2 victory Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nashville’s Mike Fisher and Anaheim’s Bobby Ryan came to blows in the third period of the Predators’ 3-2 victory Saturday. Fisher, who the broadcasters noted was usually “pretty evenly tempered,” quickly knocked down Ryan, and the players were sent to the penalty box. Fisher’s biggest fan, his country music star wife Carrie Underwood, was in attendance and cheered him from a luxury box. As the broadcasters said, “Everybody has their breaking points.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fisher Fights; Underwood Cheers', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Underwood, Carrie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T06:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sect