fac-2816e12b7173', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4943b2b0-49cb-5bb1-8fac-2816e12b7173'}, {'abstract': 'Salomón Lerner, Peru’s cabinet chief, quit unexpectedly after failing to resolve a dispute over an ambitious and controversial gold-mining project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/world/americas/top-peruvian-official-quits-amid-protest-over-mining-project.html', 'snippet': 'Salomón Lerner, Peru’s cabinet chief, quit unexpectedly after failing to resolve a dispute over an ambitious and controversial gold-mining project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Peru’s cabinet chief, Salomón Lerner, abruptly resigned Saturday after failing to negotiate a resolution to simmering protests against a large mining project led by an American company, the Newmont Mining Corporation. Peru’s president, Ollanta Humala, replaced Mr. Lerner with his interior minister, Óscar Valdés Dancuart, a former military officer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peru Official Steps Down Amid Fight Over a Mine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peru Official Steps Down Amid Fight Over a Mine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humala, Ollanta', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newmont Mining Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T09:10:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9cae1ba-7fa7-50d3-9fb1-f148a3d2443c', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9cae1ba-7fa7-50d3-9fb1-f148a3d2443c'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Ron Paul, Gov. Rick Perry and Representative Michele Bachmann are among the presidential hopefuls talking about Iowa this week.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/sunday-breakfast-menu-december-11/', 'snippet': 'Representative Ron Paul, Gov. Rick Perry and Representative Michele Bachmann are among the presidential hopefuls talking about Iowa this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the presidential race heating up in Iowa and the payroll tax battle raging on in Washington, the Sunday shows get the latest from five presidential hopefuls and Senate leaders from both parties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, December 11', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T10:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1840cb41-96f6-578a-bf95-df6c31498821', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1840cb41-96f6-578a-bf95-df6c31498821'}, {'abstract': '“The Renaissance in Rome,” which runs at the Fondazione Roma at Palazzo Sciarra until Feb. 12, displays more than 180 works, including some of the Renaissance’s most seminal.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/a-show-explores-romes-role-in-the-renaissance/', 'snippet': '“The Renaissance in Rome,” which runs at the Fondazione Roma at Palazzo Sciarra until Feb. 12, displays more than 180 works, including some of the Renaissance’s most seminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to the Renaissance, Florence is usually given top billing, as the birthplace of a\xa0 movement that spread throughout Europe. But several cities played instrumental supporting roles, including Rome, a new exhibition there makes clear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Show in Rome Explores the City’s Role in the Renaissance', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raphael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Ruggeri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruggeri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f58972f-9219-53b8-af46-35e20ed6b509', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f58972f-9219-53b8-af46-35e20ed6b509'}, {'abstract': 'Google showed off its new Paris headquarters and Karl Lagerfeld introduced an online-only fashion brand at the LeWeb technology conference last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/technology/12iht-leweb12.html', 'snippet': 'Google showed off its new Paris headquarters and Karl Lagerfeld introduced an online-only fashion brand at the LeWeb technology conference last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Eric E. Schmidt, Google’s executive chairman, and President Nicolas Sarkozy of France acted like old friends. Karl Lagerfeld, the head designer at Chanel, introduced a new online-only fashion brand. The Ting Tings gave a private concert at the Louvre for a gathering of the global digerati at the LeWeb technology conference here.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/business/12leweb/12leweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/business/12leweb/12leweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/business/12leweb/12leweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Google Preens in Paris, France Briefly Becomes the Focus of Digital Optimism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Google Preens in Paris, France Briefly Becomes the Focus of Digital Optimism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T12:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbd88baf-cce4-5a4d-9872-3c72b1ab4148', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbd88baf-cce4-5a4d-9872-3c72b1ab4148'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday Review’s Exposures column features the work of Anastasia Taylor-Lind, who documented the “birth encouragement program” in Nagorno-Karabakh.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/paying-for-babies-in-nagorno-karabakh/', 'snippet': 'Sunday Review’s Exposures column features the work of Anastasia Taylor-Lind, who documented the “birth encouragement program” in Nagorno-Karabakh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a couple marries in Nagorno-Karabakh, the government gives them a cash reward of $780. More money comes their way after the birth of their first child — and their second, third and fourth. Families with six children under the age of 18 receive a house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying for Babies in Nagorno-Karabakh', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nagorno-Karabakh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3525d6ef-a655-5728-b6a2-90de53f