wks/', 'snippet': 'Seahawks running back Marshawn Lynch saves his invincibility mode runs for a national audience:', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rams (2-10) at Seahawks (5-7), \uf0218:30 p.m. Eastern, ESPN\uf021Line: Seahawks by 10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Matchup: Rams at Seahawks', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T23:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc0648a-01f0-57c9-8a67-af2cbe22c3bd', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc0648a-01f0-57c9-8a67-af2cbe22c3bd'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of the company in performance at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/12/arts/dance/Pond.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of the company in performance at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of the company in performance at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/arts/dance/Pond-slide-VUQL/Pond-slide-VUQL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/arts/dance/Pond-slide-VUQL/Pond-slide-VUQL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/arts/dance/Pond-slide-VUQL/Pond-slide-VUQL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merce Cunningham Dance Company', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T23:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7fa44150-76a2-5892-947c-b2cd312970e3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7fa44150-76a2-5892-947c-b2cd312970e3'}, {'abstract': 'CBS News said on Friday that it had renewed its contract with Charles Osgood, the longtime anchor of “CBS Sunday Morning,” and had promoted one of the show’s contributors, Mo Rocca.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/arts/television/osgood-signs-to-stay-on-cbs-sunday-morning.html', 'snippet': 'CBS News said on Friday that it had renewed its contract with Charles Osgood, the longtime anchor of “CBS Sunday Morning,” and had promoted one of the show’s contributors, Mo Rocca.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBS News said on Friday that it had renewed its contract with Charles Osgood, below left, the longtime anchor of “CBS Sunday Morning,” and had promoted one of the show’s contributors, Mo Rocca, bottom left. A CBS spokesman confirmed that Mr. Osgood had signed a new contract but declined the specify the length. This fall, when the correspondent Lee Cowan returned to the network from NBC, he was named a substitute for Mr. Osgood, who has anchored “Sunday Morning” since 1994. Mr. Rocca, a satirist who has contributed to the program since 2006, will become a full-time correspondent, the network said in a news release. He will also report for other CBS News broadcasts. Separately he will remain a panelist on NPR’s “Wait Wait ... Don’t Tell Me!” and the host of the Cooking Channel’s “Food(ography).” Last week the evening complement to “CBS Sunday Morning,” “60 Minutes,” named Andrew Cohen to be the program’s first legal analyst. CBS said that Mr. Cohen, who will remain the senior legal analyst for CBS Radio, would “help ‘60 Minutes’ correspondents, producers and executives with law-related stories, including deciphering legal documents, providing sources from the legal community, and otherwise guiding the program’s coverage of legal events and issues.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Osgood Signs to Stay on ‘CBS Sunday Morning’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Osgood Signs to Stay On ‘CBS Sunday Morning’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osgood, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rocca, Mo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T23:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/922954ea-cb08-5c3c-9ce0-f5bd782fdd3b', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/922954ea-cb08-5c3c-9ce0-f5bd782fdd3b'}, {'abstract': 'This week Disney plans to announce “Sofia the First,” a television movie and series centered on a girl princess. Previously all Disney princesses have been adults.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/for-disney-a-younger-princess/', 'snippet': 'This week Disney plans to announce “Sofia the First,” a television movie and series centered on a girl princess. Previously all Disney princesses have been adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Disney princesses exert a powerful hold on the imaginations of many girls, influencing everything from how they play to what they wear. Some parents think they can also send the wrong message to girls — that life isn’t complete without Prince Charming, for instance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Disney, a Younger Princess', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-11T23:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56866c29-3177-5cad-bd0a-cc6a42228039', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56866c29-3177-5cad-bd0a-cc6a42228039'}, {'abstract': 'Alice Reiser, 89, whose husband and two children are deceased, avoids the local senior center, where others swap family stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/nyregion/lonely-after-burying-her-children-neediest-cases.html', 'snippet': 'Alice Reiser, 89, whose husband and two children are deceased, avoids the local senior center, where others swap family stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alice Reiser, 89, wants to talk to her husband and sons, she turns to their photographs. They are all she has left of them, besides memories.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/nyregion/SUB-12NEEDIEST/SUB-12NEEDIEST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/nyregion/SUB-12NEEDIEST/SUB-12NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/nyregion/SUB-12NEEDIEST/SUB-12NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Widow’s Loneliness After Burying Her Children', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Widow’s Loneliness After Burying Her Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Assn for Services for the Aged', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UJA-Federation of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T00:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Farmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4426ac0a-c12f-5a49-a8c9-497c7d2c5d39', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4426ac0a-c12f-5a49-a8c9-497c7d2c5d39'}, {'abstract': 'When the Fed’s policy-making committee convenes on Tuesday, it will consider the idea of publishing a regular forecast of its future decisions on interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/business/economy/fed-to-consider-publishing-a-forecast-on-rates.html', 'snippet': 'When the Fed’s policy-making committee convenes on Tuesday, it will consider the idea of publishing a regular forecast of its future decisions on interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve’s decision three years ago to reduce short-term interest rates to nearly zero made a splash, both because the Fed had never pushed rates so low and because it said that it planned to keep rates near zero “for some time.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/business/Fed/Fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed to Weigh Publishing a Forecast on Rates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed to Weigh Publishing A Forecast On Rates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions 