ule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T00:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/23e8666a-edf8-5743-841a-24de8a64d496', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23e8666a-edf8-5743-841a-24de8a64d496'}, {'abstract': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/business/economic-reports-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include retail sales for November and business inventories for October (Tuesday); import prices for November (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims; the Producer Price Index for November; the third-quarter current account deficit; industrial production and capacity utilization for November; the Philadelphia Fed manufacturing index for December and weekly jobless claims (Thursday); and the Consumer Price Index for November (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/business/12Ahead/12Ahead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name