, 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Astronomy and Astrophysics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hayden Planetarium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T00:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ec2cef6-0c73-571b-b06c-e00b2e233f84', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ec2cef6-0c73-571b-b06c-e00b2e233f84'}, {'abstract': 'A controversial proposition, a receptive president and some surprising support.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/11/rabbi-chaplains-of-the-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'A controversial proposition, a receptive president and some surprising support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rabbi Dr. Arnold Fischel arrived at the White House on the morning of Dec. 11, 1861, prepared to act as a one-man lobby for the constitutional rights of Jews. He had traveled alone from New York, on his own dime, bringing several letters of recommendation from prominent Republicans and one from the Board of Delegates of American Israelites, then just three years old and the country’s only national Jewish organization. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rabbi-Chaplains of the Civil War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T01:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Abbott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abbott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd1322d-6768-5ba8-9b13-06b5c6145e5a', 'word_count': 1795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd1322d-6768-5ba8-9b13-06b5c6145e5a'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Tacopina, a soccer-obsessed New York defense lawyer, is part of a group with big plans for the Italian club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/sports/soccer/as-romas-us-owners-hope-to-make-club-a-global-brand.html', 'snippet': 'Joseph Tacopina, a soccer-obsessed New York defense lawyer, is part of a group with big plans for the Italian club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It all started with some hasty scribbling on the back of a napkin at Stadio Olimpico in Rome.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/sports/YROMA/YROMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 398, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/sports/YROMA/YROMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/sports/YROMA/YROMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Owners Look to Turn A.S. Roma Into a Global Soccer Brand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Owners Look to Turn A.S. Roma Into a Global Soccer Brand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roma (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':