ANTS1211-slide-LX1J/SPTSGIANTS1211-slide-LX1J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Replay: Week 14', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T05:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d9e63d3e-2d82-5726-9c35-04765505ddce', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d9e63d3e-2d82-5726-9c35-04765505ddce'}, {'abstract': 'During an appearance on “60 Minutes,” President Obama kept to populist themes and contrasted himself with presidential candidates in the Republican field.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/in-cbs-interview-obama-makes-case-for-second-term/', 'snippet': 'During an appearance on “60 Minutes,” President Obama kept to populist themes and contrasted himself with presidential candidates in the Republican field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama on Sunday continued his populist fusillade, asserting during an appearance on “60 Minutes” on CBS that Republicans in Congress were protecting the wealthy at the expense of the middle class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In CBS Interview, Obama Makes Case for Second Term', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T05:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6914a67f-7d3f-545d-a650-5a1fa1ce41e6', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6914a67f-7d3f-545d-a650-5a1fa1ce41e6'}, {'abstract': 'Dysfunction is deepening in the Indian Parliament.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/the-long-view-parliamentary-paralysis/', 'snippet': 'Dysfunction is deepening in the Indian Parliament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly three weeks now, the Indian Parliament has resembled a patient in a coma, its faculties frozen, its strength ebbing, with no flickers of consciousness at all. The doctors profess themselves flummoxed. No business has been transacted in the winter session of the upper and lower houses at all; instead, the opposition has substituted debate with stubborn rabble-rousing, while the government has flailed weakly against a phalanx of internal crises.One news report has estimated that the time lost by disruptions and adjournments has already cost the taxpayer more than Rs 250 million. Improbably, this paralysis has even prompted a member of Parliament – Shashi Tharoor, in an article for Tehelka – to propose doing away with his own institution, a public gesture of limp-handed helplessness if there ever was one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Long View: Parliamentary Paralysis', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N