rom Matt Prater are not a formula for sustainable success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A quick tour of Week 14 in the N.F.L.:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 14 Quick Hits: Tebow Wins, and Logic Loses', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T11:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76367a73-ad40-506e-b218-34f48c9be9b0', 'word_count': 1800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76367a73-ad40-506e-b218-34f48c9be9b0'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s opulence contrast with grinding poverty in the rest of the country.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/new-delhis-controversial-birth/', 'snippet': 'The city’s opulence contrast with grinding poverty in the rest of the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few cities of recent vintage have a history as complicated and contested as New Delhi, which turned 100 on Monday. Now the seat of the world’s largest democracy, New Delhi began in 1911 as a grand imperial showpiece meant to stand for eternal British rule over the Indian subcontinent. But during its two decades of construction New Delhi became the stage upon which Indians gained increasing political advantage over a crumbling Raj.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Delhi’s Controversial Birth', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George V, King of Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T11:23:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dinyar Patel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dinyar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5dc8c2f-ec3d-59d3-ad97-bc0734df3161', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5dc8c2f-ec3d-59d3-ad97-bc0734df3161'}, {'abstract': 'The London Stock Exchange Group has agreed to buy the remaining 50 percent of FTSE International it does not already own  for £450 million from the publishing house Pearson.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/london-stock-exchange-buys-remaining-stake-in-ftse/', 'snippet': 'The London Stock Exchange Group has agreed to buy the remaining 50 percent of FTSE International it does not already own  for £450 million from the publishing house Pearson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The London Stock Exchange Group agreed on Monday to buy the 50 percent of the financial index business FTSE International it did not already own for £450 million ($701 million) from the publishing house Pearson.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'L.S.E. Group to Buy Remainder of FTSE', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T11:32:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13f1b5d4-201d-5684-9b7e-8610912bce18', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f1b5d4-201d-5684-9b7e-8610912bce18'}, {'abstract': 'The officer, shot at the scene of a home invasion robbery in Cypress Hills, is the first officer fatally shot in the line of duty since 2007. The mayor called the shooting a “horrible, depraved criminal attack.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/officer-shot-and-critically-wounded-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'The officer, shot at the scene of a home invasion robbery in Cypress Hills, is the first officer fatally shot in the line of duty since 2007. The mayor called the shooting a “horrible, depraved criminal attack.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Click to read the updated version of this article that appears in the newspaper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Shot and Killed in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cypress Hills (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T11:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2bb819d-ab90-577f-b56d-b126c86822ec', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2bb819d-ab90-577f-b56d-b126c86822ec'}, {'abstract': 'There isn’t a more destructive defensive end in football right now than the Giants’ Jason Pierre-Paul.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/the-power-and-grace-of-pierre-paul/', 'snippet': 'There isn’t a more destructive defensive end in football right now than the Giants’ Jason Pierre-Paul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The NBC analyst Cris Collinsworth said it best Sunday night: If Giants defensive end Jason Pierre-Paul is not in the Pro Bowl, there should be an investigation. And this isn’t just because of Pierre-Paul’s otherworldly performance Sunday night, in which he started the game with a safety (the nice thing about a 2-0 score is it sets the table for a lot of lead changes – this game had eight) and finished it with a blocked field goal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Power and Grace of Jason Pierre-Paul', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierre-Paul, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T11:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2af59a-d40b-552e-896d-5eafa3e23e51', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2af59a-d40b-552e-896d-5eafa3e23e51'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Complaint Box, a rant for those who claim to love the earth: Pull over and take a close look at yourselves; you’re not as green as you think.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/complaint-box-pseudo-green/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Complaint Box, a rant for those who claim to love the earth: Pull over and take a close look at yourselves; you’re not as green as you think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everybody is an environmentalist. There are very few who would walk the plank and claim otherwise. These days it is cool to be eco-friendly and green. Most of my friends are. They use eco-friendly products, shun pesticides, chemical fertilizers, eat organically and celebrate Earth Day. Interestingly, most have elephant-sized carbon footprints.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Pseudo Green', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T12:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walter D. Kolos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1fccf36-8b9e-5111-91cc-7a4871737ba9', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1fccf36-8b9e-5111-91cc-7a4871737ba9'}, {'abstract': 'A near certainty — no matter what occurs in the next two weeks — is that the results from the final week of the season figure to be decisive.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/jets-control-their-playoff-chances-now-what/', 'snippet': 'A near certainty — no matter what occurs in the next two weeks — is that the results from the final week of the season figure to be decisive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the Jets, there is an obvious benefit to emerging from the logjam of 7-5 teams in the A.F.C. wild-card hunt to go to 8-5: They now know that if they win their final three games, they will be in the playoffs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Control Their Playoff Chances. Now What?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T12:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3753e328-1ef1-5b93-ab3c-5a6f9444d47d', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3753e328-1ef1-5b93-ab3c-5a6f9444d47d'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: What’s driving you crazy?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/this-week-in-small-business-the-clock-is-ticking/', 'snippet': 'Plus: What’s driving you crazy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: The Clock is Ticking', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'},