/monday-reading-how-to-find-bargain-ski-lift-tickets/', 'snippet': 'How to find bargain ski-lift tickets, fighting poor recycling in other countries, holiday gifts from your kitchen and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: How to Find Bargain Lift Tickets', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T13:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542684fc-929c-540e-8f4e-56b2969ca918', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542684fc-929c-540e-8f4e-56b2969ca918'}, {'abstract': 'Whitehaven Coal has agreed to buy another Australian coal company, Aston Resources, in an all-stock deal that will create one of the country’s largest coal producers.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/whitehaven-coals-buys-aston-resources-for-2-8-billion/', 'snippet': 'Whitehaven Coal has agreed to buy another Australian coal company, Aston Resources, in an all-stock deal that will create one of the country’s largest coal producers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Whitehaven Coal has agreed to buy another Australian coal company, Aston Resources, in an all-stock deal worth about $2.8 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whitehaven Coal Buys Aston Resources for $2.8 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T13:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc9ec717-4e75-5274-a3ec-5744a0968639', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc9ec717-4e75-5274-a3ec-5744a0968639'}, {'abstract': 'An online archive on architecture is about to enter the bricks-and-mortar world.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/quick-look-architecture-asap/', 'snippet': 'An online archive on architecture is about to enter the bricks-and-mortar world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tina DiCarlo, Danielle Rago and Silvia Franceschini are on a mission to change the way people think about architecture. They are the curators of the Archive of Spatial Aesthetics and Praxis, or ASAP, an online archive that was founded by DiCarlo in 2010 with the goal of “collecting and exhibiting architecture as part of a broader social, political and aesthetic discourse.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quick Look | Architecture, ASAP', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias Redstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Redstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e14fd8-7663-569b-9991-70eb80e36926', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e14fd8-7663-569b-9991-70eb80e36926'}, {'abstract': 'The ECB is not coming.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/no-draghi-ex-machina/', 'snippet': 'The ECB is not coming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So last week European leaders announced a plan that, on the face of it, was pure nonsense. Faced with a crisis that is mainly about the balance of payments, with fiscal crisis as a secondary consequence, they supposedly committed everyone to severe fiscal austerity, which would guarantee a recession while leaving the real problem unaddressed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Draghi Ex Machina', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T14:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f087416c-f5b7-5918-a06d-acfb1ec548a3', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f087416c-f5b7-5918-a06d-acfb1ec548a3'}, {'abstract': 'In Monday’s Times, David Streitfeld writes about the early response to the Kindle Fire. Buyers have criticized its glitchy touch screen, clunky controls and slow Web browser. But the device is likely to be a success regardless.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/daily-report-kindle-fire-attracts-critics-and-buyers/', 'snippet': 'In Monday’s Times, David Streitfeld writes about the early response to the Kindle Fire. Buyers have criticized its glitchy touch screen, clunky controls and slow Web browser. But the device is likely to be a success regardless.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In Monday’s Times, David Streitfeld writes about the early response to the Kindle Fire from Amazon.com. Buyers have criticized its glitchy touch screen, clunky controls and slow Web browser. And usability experts have questioned a number of Amazon’s design decisions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su