, 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/us/13scotus_cnd/13scotus_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/us/13scotus_cnd/13scotus_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Court to Weigh Arizona Statute on Immigration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court To Weigh Arizona Statute On Immigration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T15:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc1ac48c-421a-5690-b6cf-78b0f1cd99ce', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc1ac48c-421a-5690-b6cf-78b0f1cd99ce'}, {'abstract': 'Has the unprecedented number of debates might the Republican primary campaign less serious?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/the-trouble-with-debates/', 'snippet': 'Has the unprecedented number of debates might the Republican primary campaign less serious?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since my Sunday column takes on the idea that the Republican Party needs a candidate (i.e. Newt Gingrich) who can out-orate and out-debate the president, I should highlight Fred Barnes’ piece making the case that the unprecedented number of G.O.P. debates has contributed to the policy unseriousness of the campaign to date:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trouble With Debates', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T15:41:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34f98b33-b738-5e15-8e31-9cbd30300c54', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34f98b33-b738-5e15-8e31-9cbd30300c54'}, {'abstract': 'It’s teacher-gift-giving crunch time, but how much is too much — or not enough? And what do teachers really want?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/what-to-give-the-teacher-for-the-holiday/', 'snippet': 'It’s teacher-gift-giving crunch time, but how much is too much — or not enough? And what do teachers really want?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will you give something to your children’s teachers this holiday season? My wholly unscientific survey says that you will — or that if you don’t, you’ll feel guilty about it. These are the weeks when schools send out gift policies, classroom parents take up collections and parents start weighing the options for showing beloved teachers how much they mean to a child (or for checking another obligation off the list, depending on your kid and your perspective). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Give the Teacher for the Holiday', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T15:41:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c643154-47f4-51a9-bad8-d5f8d33f6004', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c643154-47f4-51a9-bad8-d5f8d33f6004'}, {'abstract': 'The looming forces of what is expected to be a drier and even more arid future have combined to create a place in motion, with more dust up and swirling.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/rethinking-the-timeless-colorado-plateau/', 'snippet': 'The looming forces of what is expected to be a drier and even more arid future have combined to create a place in motion, with more dust up and swirling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To many of the hundreds of thousands of visitors who travel each year to the red rock country of the West and to national parks like Arches and Bryce Canyon, the landscape can feel timeless. The strange wind- and water-carved formations speak of ages past, presented to the modern tourist as a finished work, often cast quite literally in stone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking the ‘Timeless’ Colorado Plateau', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Colorado', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T15:55:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9bb85ce-48b9-5b9d-8dfc-06117cfaab3a', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9bb85ce-48b9-5b9d-8dfc-06117cfaab3a'}, {'abstract': 'A veteran of Vietnam questioned Mitt Romney about his views on same-sex marriage and the rights of legally married veterans at a campaign stop in New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/romneys-heated-exchange-with-a-veteran/', 'snippet': 'A veteran of Vietnam questioned Mitt Romney about his views on same-sex marriage and the rights of legally married veterans at a campaign stop in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — A question about same-sex marriage from a Vietnam veteran led to a heated exchange with Mitt Romney on Monday morning as Mr. Romney was making the rounds at a restaurant here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Heated Exchange With a Veteran', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 