_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lahey, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T15:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2682c41f-540a-5155-8648-1e4b735200b7', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2682c41f-540a-5155-8648-1e4b735200b7'}, {'abstract': 'The online giant says the promotion, which encouraged customers to report local retailers’ prices to Amazon, was not aimed at small businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/the-backlash-to-amazons-price-check-promotion-builds/', 'snippet': 'The online giant says the promotion, which encouraged customers to report local retailers’ prices to Amazon, was not aimed at small businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years — since its inception — Amazon has been at implicit war with local brick-and-mortar stores. Last week, the implicit seemingly became explicit when Amazon began a promotion that encouraged customers to check out prices at local retailers and use a specially designed “Price Check” smartphone app to report what they found back to Amazon. Customers who then purchased the same item from Amazon received a 5 percent discount, up to $5. (The deal was available only from Friday night through Saturday, and only for certain kinds of products.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Denies It Has a Small-Business Problem', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T16:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b7e4ebd-7bf8-5da7-a905-8aae102abd0c', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b7e4ebd-7bf8-5da7-a905-8aae102abd0c'}, {'abstract': 'With a handful of motorsport luminaries in tow, the touring Progressive International Motorcycle Show, which stopped in Southern California over the weekend, is giving American riders their first look at models unveiled in Milan last month.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/riders-tigers-and-a-drill-sergeant-at-long-beach-motorcycle-show/', 'snippet': 'With a handful of motorsport luminaries in tow, the touring Progressive International Motorcycle Show, which stopped in Southern California over the weekend, is giving American riders their first look at models unveiled in Milan last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONG BEACH, Calif. — Over the weekend, the Progressive International Motorcycle Show brought out celebrities and the prospect of imprudent speed to the Long Beach Convention Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riders, Tigers and a Drill Sergeant at Long Beach Motorcycle Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '