sterman,” will itself continue to have a home in Dumbo, not far from its current location in that neighborhood. The theater said on Monday that it had signed a three-year lease for a new space at 29 Jay Street, where it plans to open next fall after leaving its longtime base of operations at 38 Water Street following the conclusion of its current season in May.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'St. Ann’s Warehouse Signs Lease for New Space in Dumbo', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Ann's Warehouse", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dumbo (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T18:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31660cdd-f2a3-5062-8021-feefbc4cad31', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31660cdd-f2a3-5062-8021-feefbc4cad31'}, {'abstract': 'In a rare interview with reporters, the incumbent, Joseph Kabila, serenely rejected complaints from his chief rival and outside observers that the election was not credible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/africa/congo-president-kabila-denies-reports-of-election-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'In a rare interview with reporters, the incumbent, Joseph Kabila, serenely rejected complaints from his chief rival and outside observers that the election was not credible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KINSHASA, Democratic Republic of Congo — Rejecting widespread criticism of the recent presidential election here, the incumbent, Joseph Kabila, said Monday that there was no reason to doubt he had been fairly re-elected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congo President Kabila Denies Reports of Election Fraud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President of Congo Denies Reports of Election Fraud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kabila, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carter Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T18:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b91c321-c32f-5276-b680-35ff01127d0e', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b91c321-c32f-5276-b680-35ff01127d0e'}, {'abstract': 'The judge has agreed to the request to stay proceedings in the Justice Department’s lawsuit to block AT&T’s $39 billion takeover of T-Mobile USA, as the two companies weigh their options.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/att-and-justice-ask-judge-to-stay-t-mobile-case/', 'snippet': 'The judge has agreed to the request to stay proceeding