ropean-fleets/', 'snippet': 'European spending on modernizing fleets has actually increased fishing capacity at a time when official policy demanded a reduction, a report says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe’s efforts to limit overcapacity in its fishing fleet have been a costly failure, an official auditor said Monday in a report that raised serious questions about the bloc’s ability to manage its marine resources.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auditor Faults Overcapacity of European Fleets', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T18:50:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24b71f6-2be1-577f-975a-d0fbcecc2b85', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24b71f6-2be1-577f-975a-d0fbcecc2b85'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge on Monday agreed to delay the Justice Department’s challenge to the proposed merger of AT&T and T-Mobile USA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/technology/judge-grants-delay-in-challenge-to-att-merger.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge on Monday agreed to delay the Justice Department’s challenge to the proposed merger of AT&T and T-Mobile USA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — AT&T has one month to tell a Federal District Court judge and the Justice Department whether it will pursue its proposed $39 billion acquisition of T-Mobile USA in its current form, in a modified structure, or if it will drop the deal altogether.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Judge Grants Delay in Challenge to AT&T Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Judge Grants Delay In Challenge to AT&T Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huvelle, Ellen S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc. (AT&T T-Mobile Deal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T18:51:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5359da44-2924-54b4-bce9-48d013aba57c', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5359da44-2924-54b4-bce9-48d013aba57c'}, {'abstract': 'Orson Welles’s Oscar is going on the auction block.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/for-sale-again-orson-welless-oscar/', 'snippet': 'Orson Welles’s Oscar is going on the auction block.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Orson Welles Oscar is back on the block. The Nate D. Sanders auction house here says it is selling the screenwriting Oscar that was awarded to Welles in 1942 for his work, with Herman J. Mankiewicz, on “Citizen Kane.” The statuette was best known in recent years as the subject of a court fight in which Welles’s daughter — having recovered it from a cinematographer who said Welles had given it to him as a gift — defeated an effort by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences to block a sale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Sale (Again): the Orson Welles Oscar', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T18:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eea27513-7d24-5103-91cd-b1763639a1fc', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eea27513-7d24-5103-91cd-b1763639a1fc'}, {'abstract': 'One promise I haven’t kept is to document the actual failure of my business. Fortunately, it has turned around and we are now doing better than we ever have before.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/id-be-happy-to-share-my-thoughts-and-experiences-as-we-go-down/', 'snippet': 'One promise I haven’t kept is to document the actual failure of my business. Fortunately, it has turned around and we are now doing better than we ever have before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 10, 2009, I was sitting at my desk, reading this blog — I think it was a post by Jay Goltz. My business was not doing well. His was struggling, too, but clearly he wasn’t as close to the edge as I was. I sent the following e-mail to the editor of this blog:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘I’d Be Happy to Share My Thoughts and Experiences as We Go Down’', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a14a7f8a-796a-53af-b069-fcaeb0fc513b', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a14a7f8a-796a-53af-b069-fcaeb0fc513b'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway production of the David Ives play “Venus in Fur,” starring Nina Arianda and Hugh Dancy, will transfer to the Lyceum Theater in February.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/an-extension-and-a-move-for-venus-in-fur/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway production of the David Ives play “Venus in Fur,” starring Nina Arianda and Hugh Dancy, will transfer to the Lyceum Theater in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway production of the David Ives play “Venus in Fur,” starring Nina Arianda and Hugh Dancy, will take a break after ending its run at the Manhattan Theater Club’s Samuel J. Friedman Theater on Sunday and resume performances at the Lyceum Theater on Feb. 7, 2012, for a limited engagement through June 17.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Extension, and a Move, for ‘Venus in Fur’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Venus in Fur (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons'