e influential to many filmmakers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘Pulp Fiction’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarantino, Quentin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/068952dd-2a92-5ddb-8247-e25efec80a48', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068952dd-2a92-5ddb-8247-e25efec80a48'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama made his first public comments on the remote-controlled spying aircraft, which has been missing since Dec. 4, and according to Iranians, is in their possession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/middleeast/obama-says-us-has-asked-iran-to-return-drone.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama made his first public comments on the remote-controlled spying aircraft, which has been missing since Dec. 4, and according to Iranians, is in their possession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama said on Monday that the United States had asked Iran to return an American surveillance drone that the Iranians say they captured on Dec. 4. It was Mr. Obama’s first public comment about the drone, a remote-controlled spying aircraft, in a case that has raised American tensions with Iran. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Is Asked to Return U.S. Drone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Is Asked To Return U.S. Drone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dd0268c-5692-569c-8c68-b4bcf710463a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dd0268c-5692-569c-8c68-b4bcf710463a'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich says he will “uphold the institution of marriage through personal fidelity to my spouse and respect for the marital bonds of others.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/gingrich-endorses-marriage-pledge/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich says he will “uphold the institution of marriage through personal fidelity to my spouse and respect for the marital bonds of others.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich became the latest Republican candidate to endorse the so-called marriage pledge, a controversial document put forward by an influential evangelical group in Iowa that opposes same-sex marriage and abortion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Endorses ‘Marriage Pledge’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3d7eecd-648a-5501-875a-537f982a5460', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3d7eecd-648a-5501-875a-537f982a5460'}, {'abstract': 'The European Commission has asked for additional documents on the $12.5 billion deal, and said it would restart its inquiry once they were received.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/technology/google-acquisition-of-motorola-delayed-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The European Commission has asked for additional documents on the $12.5 billion deal, and said it would restart its inquiry once they were received.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European antitrust regulators have suspended their investigation into Google’s acquisition of Motorola Mobility, a maker of smartphones, until Google provides additional evidence in the case, the European Commission said Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Acquisition of Motorola Delayed in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google’s Acquisition of Motorola Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motorola Mobility Hldg Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/333911b8-41eb-5b87-82f7-3d66c2d8631d', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/333911b8-41eb-5b87-82f7-3d66c2d8631d'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Bettman, the N.H.L. commissioner, has said there is not enough data on the causes of brain trauma to justify stiffer penalties for fighting, but some doctors say ample evidence exists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/sports/hockey/in-debate-about-fighting-in-hockey-medical-experts-weigh-in.html', 'snippet': 'Gary Bettman, the N.H.L. commissioner, has said there is not enough data on the causes of brain trauma to justify stiffer penalties for fighting, but some doctors say ample evidence exists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The determination that the hockey enforcer Derek Boogaard had a degenerative brain disease linked to repeated hits to the head when he died in May at 28 has fueled a debate among medical experts over whether the sport should ban fighting.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/sports/