ected-murder-suicide-in-chelsea/', 'snippet': 'The police said a shooting Monday morning at the Fulton Houses on 16th Street “seems to be domestic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two men were fatally shot in a public housing building in Chelsea on Monday morning, the police said. The police said the shooting appeared to be a murder-suicide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Die in Suspected Murder-Suicide in Chelsea', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman and Alice Speri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Speri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ff008d6-c7cd-5c8a-a940-dbe09c227479', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ff008d6-c7cd-5c8a-a940-dbe09c227479'}, {'abstract': 'When children lose teeth, the event has become all about the money you give and the money they get. Is there a better way?', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/rethinking-your-approach-to-the-tooth-fairy/', 'snippet': 'When children lose teeth, the event has become all about the money you give and the money they get. Is there a better way?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Styles section of The New York Times this weekend, Bruce Feiler goes after the tooth fairy. What could be wrong with the tooth fairy? Plenty, he argues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking Your Approach to the Tooth Fairy', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21591807-0e0b-5308-9415-ae2dbb7e58b4', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21591807-0e0b-5308-9415-ae2dbb7e58b4'}, {'abstract': 'Meryl Streep makes her debut as a Vogue cover model, at 62.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/meryl-streep-cover-girl/', 'snippet': 'Meryl Streep makes her debut as a Vogue cover model, at 62.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’d think by this point Meryl Streep would have accomplished every possible feat in her professional life. But early on Monday afternoon, Ms. Streep added one or two more. She was a trending topic on Twitter (at least in New York), off the news of another first: her first Vogue cover, at age 62. Photographed by Annie Leibovitz, she’s sitting in the surf on a beach and later “striding through a crop of organic broccoli sustainably farmed” in upstate New York, according to the accompanying story. In it, she talks about feminism, politics and campaigning for a National Women’s History Museum, for which she donated $1 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meryl Streep, Cover Girl', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c96e14-c883-5cff-a687-eec01d280f27', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c96e14-c883-5cff-a687-eec01d280f27'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney throws the first jab, and Newt Gingrich swings back.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/romney-vs-gingrich-round-ii/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney throws the first jab, and Newt Gingrich swings back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDONDERRY, N.H. — Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney both campaigned hard in New Hampshire on Monday, and the two Republican leaders in the polls looked like they could go 15 rounds before the day was finished. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney-Gingrich Skirmishing Intensifies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freddie Mac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:31:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02d0fb66-cdeb-58ca-9bf2-69fb13f3bddd', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02d0fb66-cdeb-58ca-9bf2-69fb13f3bddd'}, {'abstract': 'The Penguins’ Sidney Crosby, who missed more than 10 months after a concussion in January, collided with a teammate and took a heavy hit in a loss to Boston on Dec. 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/sports/hockey/sidney-crosby-out-indefinitely-as-concussion-symptoms-return.html', 'snippet': 'The Penguins’ Sidney Crosby, who missed more than 10 months after a concussion in January, collided with a teammate and took a heavy hit in a loss to Boston on Dec. 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sidney Crosby, the N.H.L.’s biggest star, said Monday that he was experiencing concussion symptoms again and that he would sit out indefinitely. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/sports/CROSBY3/CROSBY3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/sports/CROSBY3/CROSBY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/sports/CROSBY3/CROSBY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crosby Sidelined Indefinitely by Return of Symptoms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lingering Effects: Crosby Sidelined Indefinitely By Return Of Symptoms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein and Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a783fcb-79a7-5d1b-86f5-fa6376bb9dc2', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a783fcb-79a7-5d1b-86f5-fa6376bb9dc2'}, {'abstract': 'Lens: Maggie Taylor', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/09/blogs/20111209-lens-maggietaylo.html', 'snippet': 'Lens: Maggie Taylor', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lens: Maggie Taylor', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/09/blogs/20111209-lens-maggietaylo-slide-I4N0/20111209-lens-maggietaylo-slide-I4N0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Maggie Taylor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:42:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/703c5669-593f-56c8-9063-da4ccda40fba', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/703c5669-593f-56c8-9063-da4ccda40fba'}, {'abstract': 'When I heard that the talented Swedish photographer Marcus Nilsson was shooting the still-life for my column on glogg, I knew he’d get it just right: he grew up with glogg, after all. He also grew up with pepparkakor — the spicy, buttery gingersnaps that often accompany glogg.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/what-goes-with-glogg-swedish-gingersnaps/', 'snippet': 'When I heard that the talented Swedish photographer Marcus Nilsson was shooting the still-life for my column on glogg, I knew he’d get it just right: he grew up with glogg, after all. He also grew up with pepparkakor — the spicy, buttery gingersna...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I heard that the talented Swedish photographer Marcus Nilsson was shooting the still-life for my column on glogg, I knew he’d get it just right: he grew up with glogg, after all. He also grew up with pepparkakor — the spicy, buttery gingersnaps that often accompany glogg — and offered to share his mom’s recipe. “I was born in spring 1972, and she started making gingersnaps that Christmas,” Nilsson told me. Since then, he said, “she has used the same recipe every year. They’re amazing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Goes With Glogg? Swedish Gingersnaps', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kurzweil, Brett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Amy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kalustyan's", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a549e7cc-83f5-599d-a83f-55270e94ac67', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a549e7cc-83f5-599d-a83f-55270e94ac67'}, {'abstract': 'Honda’s luxury subsidiary will try to upstage competitors like Lexus and Infiniti at the show in July, where the NSX nameplate will be resurrected for a concept supercar.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/acura-prepares-product-blitz-including-nsx-concept-for-detroit-auto-show/', 'snippet': 'Honda’s luxury subsidiary will try to upstage competitors like Lexus and Infiniti at the show in July, where the NSX nameplate will be resurrected for a concept supercar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Acura, a brand that has largely been overlooked by luxury buyers wooed by products from Lexus, Infiniti and the German manufacturers, intends to become a player again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Acura Prepares Product Blitz, Including NSX Concept, for Detroit Auto Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACURA DIVISION OF HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e88e37d5-7907-5ef4-90e9-4006f1d6e4e0', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e88e37d5-7907-5ef4-90e9-4006f1d6e4e0'}, {'abstract': 'In a new documentary, “Eames: The Architect and the Painter,” the filmmakers Jason Cohn and Bill Jersey train their sights on the personal style of Ray Eames — a quirky composite of diffidence and daring.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/ray-eames-how-she-dressed/', 'snippet': 'In a new documentary, “Eames: The Architect and the Painter,” the filmmakers Jason Cohn and Bill Jersey train their sights on the personal style of Ray Eames — a quirky composite of diffidence and daring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To design aficionados the name Charles Eames conjures an image of the screen-idol handsome design visionary, studiedly natty in his tweed coats and bow ties. The figure of Ray, his wife and collaborator, is somewhat more elusive. But now a new documentary, “Eames: The Architect and the Painter,” brings Ray into sharper focus, the filmmakers Jason Cohn and Bill Jersey training their sights on her personal style, a quirky composite of diffidence and daring.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ray Eames: How She Dressed', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3c22ccc-6316-5094-8185-d11ebef9c037', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3c22ccc-6316-5094-8185-d11ebef9c037'}, {'abstract': 'Viewers of a “60 Minutes” segment on homeless families donated more than $1 million, which is heartwarming but not wholly satisfying.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/some-holiday-cheer-for-homeless-families/', 'snippet': 'Viewers of a “60 Minutes” segment on homeless families donated more than $1 million, which is heartwarming but not wholly satisfying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the Sunday between Black Friday and Cyber Monday, “60 Minutes” broadcast a story called “Hard Times Generation.” Homeless teens Arielle and Austin Metzger described living in their dad’s van, brushing their teeth in service stations and “doing what they can to get by” with touching self-possession and gratitude for what they did have — school, their dad, and one another. Younger kids, gathered in small forum at a local school, discussed living without a permanent home — staying up all night in the back seat to watch over a sleeping mother to “keep her safe”; moving into a hotel (and agreeing to repaint all of its rooms) for shelter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Holiday Cheer for Homeless Families', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:58:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57b80b40-1489-5cac-b9b9-2b8a62da5baf', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57b80b40-1489-5cac-b9b9-2b8a62da5baf'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Warfare 3, the first-person shooter video game, reached $1 billion much more rapidly than Modern Warfare 2, an earlier installment of the game, which took took 60 days.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/modern-warfare-3-passes-1-billion-in-sales-in-16-days/', 'snippet': 'Modern Warfare 3, the first-person shooter video game, reached $1 billion much more rapidly than Modern Warfare 2, an earlier installment of the game, which took took 60 days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Modern Warfare 3, the first-person shooter video game, passed $1 billion in sales in just 16 days, according to Activision Blizzard, the game’s distributor. Modern Warfare 2, an earlier installment of the game, took 60 days to reach the same milestone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Modern Warfare 3 Passes $1 Billion in Sales in 16 Days', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACTIVISION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T19:59:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a311874-79fe-5095-8b67-07a2aada0541', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a311874-79fe-5095-8b67-07a2aada0541'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists find evidence that the water distribution systems of aspens in Colorado were damaged during a drought, suggesting that they died of thirst rather than a lack of carbohydrates linked to a halt in photosynthesis.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/learning-how-to-kill-trees/', 'snippet': 'Scientists find evidence that the water distribution systems of aspens in Colorado were damaged during a drought, suggesting that they died of thirst rather than a lack of carbohydrates linked to a halt in photosynthesis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists trying to understand the future of forests on a warming planet have a strange problem: They do not know how to kill trees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning How to Kill Trees', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbohydrates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photosynthesis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest Service', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f24265f-6412-5d60-892e-d3f96b8fd8af', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f24265f-6412-5d60-892e-d3f96b8fd8af'}, {'abstract': 'The Moment grabbed André Saraiva to get the lowdown on what makes a Le Baron party.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/asked-answered-andre-saraiva/', 'snippet': 'The Moment grabbed André Saraiva to get the lowdown on what makes a Le Baron party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French graffiti artist, night-life impresario and hotel entrepreneur André Saraiva this year turned his talents to filmmaking, released a CD with Kitsuné, teamed up with Levi’s to create a jacket for MoCA’s “Art in the Streets” exhibition, became creative director of L’Officiel Hommes and opened a London location of his Paris nightclub, Le Baron. With all this going on, it’s little wonder New York is still waiting for its version of Saraiva’s famously hedonistic club — “my Christmas present to New York” — \xa0rumored to be opening on Mulberry Street before the end of the year. The Moment grabbed Saraiva for a few minutes to get the lowdown on what makes a Le Baron party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | André Saraiva', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lena de Casparis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Casparis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd421e32-b0d2-5cde-b660-21a67111f5fc', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd421e32-b0d2-5cde-b660-21a67111f5fc'}, {'abstract': 'The world sailing championships continued off Fremantle, Australia, and the Arab Games continued in Doha, Qatar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/12/sports/20111212-photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'The world sailing championships continued off Fremantle, Australia, and the Arab Games continued in Doha, Qatar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world sailing championships continued off Fremantle, Australia, and the Arab Games continued in Doha, Qatar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/sports/20111212-photoreplay-slide-HOW7/20111