g them Monday. But I did have a problem: What is our culture, and how could we possibly depict it on a flag?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/12/mama-what-is-our-culture/', 'snippet': "Because of baby sitter/husband communication bobbles, our undecorated flags were apparently sitting on the kitchen table rather than ready for posting outside my twins' prekindergarten classroom. No problem, the teachers said, bring them Monday. B...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Parent: Mama, What Is Our Culture?', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By JODI RUDOREN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RUDOREN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91dbf37d-28b6-54c3-bd52-a5bcf5ab6c50', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91dbf37d-28b6-54c3-bd52-a5bcf5ab6c50'}, {'abstract': 'The number of principals who have signed onto a letter objecting to New York State’s system of teacher evaluations has grown by 150 in the last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/12/protest-reaches-900-principals-and-climbing/', 'snippet': 'The number of principals who have signed onto a letter objecting to New York State’s system of teacher evaluations has grown by 150 in the last week.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protest Reaches 900 Principals, and Climbing', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By SCHOOLBOOK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schoolbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5073035-807f-5d13-9120-6c21307fb70a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5073035-807f-5d13-9120-6c21307fb70a'}, {'abstract': 'Sleep duration varies widely and may be genetically determined, and 1 to 2 percent of people need at least 10 hours a day, said Dr. Ana C. Krieger of Weill Cornell Medical College.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/science/qa-am-i-sleeping-too-long.html', 'snippet': 'Sleep duration varies widely and may be genetically determined, and 1 to 2 percent of people need at least 10 hours a day, said Dr. Ana C. Krieger of Weill Cornell Medical College.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Ever since childhood, I have needed more sleep than most. Why do some people need so much more sleep than others?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13QA/13QA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13QA/13QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13QA/13QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Sleep', 'kicker': 'Q & A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Big Sleep', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':