I playoffs before, will play in the championship game on Saturday against Pittsburg State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of those magical, improbable playoff runs that helps renew faith in the joy of sports, Wayne State University’s football team has pushed itself to the Division II national title game, after having never made the playoffs before this season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Division II’s Football Cinderella: Wayne State', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wayne State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0af2a85-0d26-5698-af39-36435e7aeb19', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0af2a85-0d26-5698-af39-36435e7aeb19'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/drawing-dance-the-cunningham-company-at-the-kennedy-center/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting their two-year Legacy Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brooklyn artist Kenneth E. Parris III is on tour with members of the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, documenting, through a series of drawings and paintings, their two-year legacy tour. After 58 years the company is scheduled to disband on New Year’s Day 2012. This is the 22nd in a series of graphite drawings that Mr. Parris plans to create from the road, providing a front-row seat to the final weeks of the company’s journey. This week’s entry is from the Kennedy Center in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawing Dance: The Cunningham Company at the Kennedy Center', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd928c3b-715a-58f2-b17f-b8ed7197f6c7', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd928c3b-715a-58f2-b17f-b8ed7197f6c7'}, {'abstract': 'At TimesTalks, Jason Reitman discusses getting his start as a director.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/young-adult-and-the-path-not-taken/', 'snippet': 'At TimesTalks, Jason Reitman discusses getting his start as a director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the funnest pit stops on the promotional circuit so far this season have been the ones involving the “Young Adult” crew. Since their collaboration on “Juno,” the writer Diablo Cody and the director Jason Reitman have had a sardonic but sweet vibe; they don’t take themselves too seriously. And there’s a buddy comedy waiting to happen in the rapport between the film’s stars, Charlize Theron and Patton Oswalt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Young Adult’ and the Path Not Taken', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e02bb5b-46fd-50ba-b9d7-ffbdd6a4fc7c', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e02bb5b-46fd-50ba-b9d7-ffbdd6a4fc7c'}, {'abstract': 'Suggestions for helping students understand common expository “text structures” like cause and effect, compare and contrast and problem-solution that appear often in The Times. For each, we include Times examples in both print and multimedia', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/compare-contrast-cause-effect-problem-solution-common-text-types-in-the-times/', 'snippet': 'Suggestions for helping students understand common expository “text structures” like cause and effect, compare and contrast and problem-solution that appear often in The Times. For each, we include Times examples in both print and multimedia', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update | Sept. 2012: We’ll be exploring the new Common Core State Standards, and how teaching with The Times can address them, through a series of blog posts. You can find them all here, in the lesson plan category “Common Core.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compare-Contrast, Cause-Effect, Problem-Solution: Common ‘Text Types’ in The Times', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:38:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e5cca33-5907-52f3-a4b9-6a8fa3f0c066', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e5cca33-5907-52f3-a4b9-6a8fa3f0c066'}, {'abstract': 'Suzy Menkes speaks to designers, from Karl Lagerfeld to Anne Valérie Hash, about the master embroiderer, whose name became synonymous with craftsmanship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000001220621/a-final-farewell-to-franois-lesage.html', 'snippet': 'Suzy Menkes speaks to designers, from Karl Lagerfeld to Anne Valérie Hash, about the master embroiderer, whose name became synonymous with craftsmanship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suzy Menkes speaks to designers, from Karl Lagerfeld to Anne Valérie Hash, about the master embroiderer, whose name became synonymous with craftsmanship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/fashion/video-menkes-lesage-obit/video-menkes-lesage-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/11/fashion/video-menkes-lesage-obit/video-menkes-lesage-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/fashion/video-menkes-lesage-obit/video-menkes-lesage-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/11/fashion/video-menkes-lesage-obit/video-menkes-lesage-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Final Farewell to François Lesage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 