s under 17.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Criticizes Decision on Morning-After Pill', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plan B (Contraceptive)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebelius, Kathleen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bde0973d-25c7-5524-910d-c235afab1f89', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bde0973d-25c7-5524-910d-c235afab1f89'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich vows to uphold the institution of marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/i-solemnly-pledge-to-be-good-as-can-be/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich vows to uphold the institution of marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve reached that phase in the primary season when the candidates start intensely publicizing their private lives. (Usually this comes right before the phase where they berate news organizations for covering their wives and children.) This rite of passage is considerably more comfortable for some candidates than others (and by “others” I mean Newt Gingrich).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Solemnly Pledge to Be Good as Can Be', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf3d6f4b-d415-5e43-a7d0-4a768835b160', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf3d6f4b-d415-5e43-a7d0-4a768835b160'}, {'abstract': 'Jobs and inequality should be the issues.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/unpivoting-obama/', 'snippet': 'Jobs and inequality should be the issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I learned much of what I know about the political economy of the Second Gilded Age from Tom Edsall. Writing for Campaign Stops, Edsall has some important things to say about how economic narratives will play next year. He argues that the polling data', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unpivoting Obama', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3cf924c-f899-556c-9820-ae422f02ee3c', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3cf924c-f899-556c-9820-ae422f02ee3c'}, {'abstract': 'A report commissioned by the wind energy industry projects steep job losses in the sector in 2013 if a tax credit for production is not extended.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/tax-policy-blowing-in-the-wind/', 'snippet': 'A report commissioned by the wind energy industry projects steep job losses in the sector in 2013 if a tax credit for production is not extended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want something from Congress, there are probably only about four shopping days left until Christmas, because most members of the House and Senate seem likely to go home on Friday. One big item on the green list is an extension of the production tax credit for wind energy, and the industry’s trade association, the American Wind Energy Association, released a dire study on Monday about what will happen without it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Policy Blowing in the Wind', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Wind Energy Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navigant Consulting Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T20:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f618d4ff-490a-5930-a498-78a258866cb0', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f618d4ff-490a-5930-a498-78a258866cb0'}, {'abstract': 'While the number of obese babies is not on the rise, some of our standard infant feeding practices and attitudes may need revising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/health/views/the-joy-of-feeding-without-all-the-parental-angst.html', 'snippet': 'While the number of obese babies is not on the rise, some of our standard infant feeding practices and attitudes may need revising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back before computers moved into our exam rooms, I tended paper growth charts ritually at every checkup. Pink for girls, blue for boys. Age on the X-axis, weight on the Y-axis. I paid particular attention to the charts of infants, plotting weight and length and head circumference with my pen month by month to show parents how their babies were growing, to reassure them when they worried that there wasn’t enough breast milk or because their babies were spitting up a little.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13KLAS/13KLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13KLAS/13KLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13KLAS/13KLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joy of Feeding, Without All the Parental Angst', 'kicker': '18 and Under', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Joy of Feeding, Without All the Parental Angst', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Foods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T21:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Perri Klass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/574cd136-133d-5037-bea9-fd3c3d4a4dbe', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/574cd136-133d-5037-bea9-fd3c3d4a4dbe'}, {'abstract': 'After a strong start, the numbers are dropping for “Once Upon a Time.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/fairy-tale-may-be-ending-for-abc-but-sunday-night-football-rolls-on/', 'snippet': 'After a strong start, the numbers are dropping for “Once Upon a Time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it possible that television viewers are no longer entranced by “Once Upon a Time” on ABC? The fantasy drama had a strong premiere and averaged 11.9 million viewers over its first four episodes, but the numbers have steadily dropped over the last month, culminating in series lows in total viewers (8.9 million) and in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic on Sunday night. The series will take a holiday breather and hope to reverse the trend starting Jan. 8.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairy Tale May Be Ending for ABC; ‘Sunday Night Football’ Rolls On for NBC', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None,