c bills and also earn incentive payments from utilities as a reward for its conservation efforts during peak periods, like heat waves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/business/marriott-in-deal-to-reduce-energy-use-at-hotels.html', 'snippet': 'Marriott will save on electric bills and also earn incentive payments from utilities as a reward for its conservation efforts during peak periods, like heat waves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most hotel chains delayed significant energy conservation moves during the economic downturn, but now one, Marriott International, has signed a deal to reduce its hotels’ energy use, particularly during times of peak demand. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/Energy/Energy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power Savings on Auto Pilot', 'kicker': 'Itineraries', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power Savings on Auto Pilot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marriott International Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T21:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Morrissey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrissey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/929b7698-5a1a-505c-b0f2-5061d4de80ec', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/929b7698-5a1a-505c-b0f2-5061d4de80ec'}, {'abstract': 'White Collar Watch questions whether even tougher penalties for corporate crime would help to discourage it.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/the-limits-of-bigger-penalties-in-fighting-financial-crime/', 'snippet': 'White Collar Watch questions whether even tougher penalties for corporate crime would help to discourage it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama, in a speech last week, called for strengthened oversight and accountability of financial firms by increasing the punishments that can be imposed for criminal violations. This comes on top of a recent proposal by Mary L. Schapiro, the chairwoman of the Securities and Exchange Commission, to ratchet up the available civil penalties for violating the securities laws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Limits of Bigger Penalties in Fighting Financial Crime', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farkas, Lee B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goffer, Zvi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T21:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], '