', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T21:48:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason DeParle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeParle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f795c4-0565-5146-9808-e888b0372e98', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f795c4-0565-5146-9808-e888b0372e98'}, {'abstract': 'Black leather belts can add a lot to holiday outfits.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/a-measure-of-restraint/', 'snippet': 'Black leather belts can add a lot to holiday outfits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A STATEMENT black leather belt can be the quick fix you need this holiday season. “With tailored high-waist trousers and a sheer blouse or crisp button-down, a bold belt will cinch the whole look,” said the stylist Kathryn Typaldos. If you’re heading straight out from work, Ms. Typaldos suggests adding a black belt to a tunic or a dress with a waistline. “The belt will add structure and refinement,” she said. These three styles — a wide corset wrap, a belt with a quirky feather trim and a patent leather one with a playful origami animal head — capture just the right amount of flare. Add lipstick and you’re off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Measure of Restraint', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T21:51:20+0000', 'document_type'