, 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. National Team Performance Review: A Seven-Game Snapshot', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Godfrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godfrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01debbc5-b0d4-5a18-adc2-dc932a9c7c43', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01debbc5-b0d4-5a18-adc2-dc932a9c7c43'}, {'abstract': 'At St. Vitus in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, on Sunday, the metal bands Black Cobra, the Body and Zoroaster offered morbid comfort in a cozy room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/arts/music/black-cobra-the-body-zoroaster-at-st-vitus-review.html', 'snippet': 'At St. Vitus in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, on Sunday, the metal bands Black Cobra, the Body and Zoroaster offered morbid comfort in a cozy room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'St. Vitus, a new metal club, opened in the late spring near the northernmost point of Greenpoint, Brooklyn, a block from the Pulaski Bridge. Outside, a black unmarked door. Inside, the Age of Enlightenment: local craft ales, a “bun bar,” a small square room with a stage in back. “What more could you want?” reads a recent comment on the bar’s Yelp page. “You’re standing there watching sludge metal like COFFINWORM live and munching on a vegan sausage bao ... it’s like living the DREAM.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/BODY/BODY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/BODY/BODY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/BODY/BODY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/BODY/BODY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/BODY/BODY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Metal, Doom and Gloom Included', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Metal, Doom and Gloom Included', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:25:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0632579-e745-5f6c-84db-b4ce0b0a9316', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0632579-e745-5f6c-84db-b4ce0b0a9316'}, {'abstract': 'Leon Botstein led the American Symphony Orchestra, which played Liszt and Busoni, with Piers Lane as piano soloist, on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/arts/music/piers-lane-is-soloist-with-american-symphony-review.html', 'snippet': 'Leon Botstein led the American Symphony Orchestra, which played Liszt and Busoni, with Piers Lane as piano soloist, on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 19 years he has conducted the American Symphony Orchestra Leon Botstein has been at his best when his programs have been built around unusual works that deserve to be heard more often. With that as a goal, it’s easy to run off the rails: works that seemed promising on paper, or even in rehearsal, can turn out to have been neglected with good cause. Others may have been worthy but failed to make their mark because inadequate rehearsal time, or other technical issues, made it impossible for the orchestra to show the scores at their best.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/symphony/symphony-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rarely Heard Offerings From Busoni and Liszt', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rarely Heard Offerings From Busoni and Liszt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Botstein, Leon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN SYMPHONY ORCHESTRA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/87756977-9383-5d77-8bb5-f166e1007905', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87756977-9383-5d77-8bb5-f166e1007905'}, {'abstract': 'Fatou Bensouda was chosen to succeed her boss, Luis Moreno-Ocampo, as head of the International Criminal Court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/europe/fatou-bensouda-becomes-lead-prosecutor-at-international-criminal-court.html', 'snippet': 'Fatou Bensouda was chosen to succeed her boss, Luis Moreno-Ocampo, as head of the International Criminal Court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawyer from Gambia, Fatou Bensouda, was named the new chief prosecutor of the International Criminal Court on Monday, making her the future public face and chief strategist of the tribunal responsible for investigating the world’s grave atrocities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/world/HAGUE/HAGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gambian Will Lead Prosecution in Hague', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gambian Will Lead Prosecution In Hague', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bensouda, Fatou', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno-Ocampo, Luis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92ac06b6-d9ea-5e80-8662-bf865d1757fc', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92ac06b6-d9ea-5e80-8662-bf865d1757fc'}, {'abstract': 'The 100th anniversary of the race to the South Pole has prompted a fresh look back and new research.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/science/amazing-race-to-the-bottom-of-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'The 100th anniversary of the race to the South Pole has prompted a fresh look back and new research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred years ago, on Dec. 14, 1911, the Norwegian Roald Amundsen and four companions trudged through fog, bitter cold and lacerating wind to stand at the absolute bottom of the world, the South Pole. Nowhere was there a trace of their British rival, Robert Falcon Scott. No Union Jack mocked them, no ice cairn bespoke precedence. The Norwegians had won the race.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13ANTA4/13ANTA4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13ANTA4/13ANTA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13ANTA4/13ANTA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazing Race to the Bottom of the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazing Race to the Bottom of the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Pole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMUNDSEN, ROALD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Robert Falcon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exploration and Explorers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:28:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Noble Wilford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Noble', 'lastname': 'Wilford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/075f781c-a38b-53f5-ae84-e234cf916a13', 'word_count': 2210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/075f781c-a38b-53f5-ae84-e234cf916a13'}, {'abstract': 'Students from the Yale School of Music performed all nine Prokofiev piano sonatas at Carnegie Hall on Sunday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/arts/music/prokofievs-piano-sonatas-from-yale-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Students from the Yale School of Music performed all nine Prokofiev piano sonatas at Carnegie Hall on Sunday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian pianist Boris Berman is particularly associated with the music of Prokofiev. He has recorded all the Prokofiev solo piano works for Chandos, written a book on the Prokofiev piano sonatas and produced an annotated edition of those nine works. It is only natural that students at the Yale School of Music, where Mr. Berman is chairman of the piano department, would absorb some of his passion for Prokofiev.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Is the Magic Number for Prokofiev', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Is the Magic Number for Prokofiev', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokofiev, Sergei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berman, Boris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f715e6c3-07cb-5ab3-9149-ebd858d874c5', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f715e6c3-07cb-5ab3-9149-ebd858d874c5'}, {'abstract': 'The Paris-Bombay collection by Chanel is a celebration of both India and the craftsmanship of the “petites mains” of France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/11/fashion/13iht-fchanel13-slideshow.html', 'snippet': 'The Paris-Bombay collection by Chanel is a celebration of both India and the craftsmanship of the “petites mains” of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Paris-Bombay collection by Chanel is a celebration of both India and the craftsmanship of the “petites mains” of France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/fashion/13iht-fchanel13-slideshow-slide-GKEX/13iht-fchanel13-