11/12/13/arts/dance/kyle-abrahams-live-the-realest-mc-at-the-kitchen-review.html', 'snippet': 'The story of Pinocchio is buried in Kyle Abraham’s autobiographical exploration of what it takes to become a real boy, “Live! The Realest MC.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, the good parts first. The story of Pinocchio is deeply buried in Kyle Abraham’s autobiographical exploration of what it takes to become a real boy, “Live! The Realest MC.” For the new dance, seen at the Kitchen on Friday evening, Mr. Abraham offers a coming-out tale — his own — showing the difficulty of growing up black and gay in a hip-hop world. There’s no Disney tune in this piece that is mainly set to industrial and electronic music; and though it features an ensemble, he is clearly the star. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/abraham/abraham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/abraham/abraham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/abraham/abraham-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/abraham/abraham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/arts/abraham/abraham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Straddling Two Worlds in Search of Selfhood', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Straddling Two Worlds In Search Of Selfhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abraham, Kyle (1977- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:34:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21f4c67-1beb-5b96-aae4-bdb6c5e06dfc', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21f4c67-1beb-5b96-aae4-bdb6c5e06dfc'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to flak from the left and right about my column praising Newt Gingrich’s stance on immigration reform.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/more-good-newt/', 'snippet': 'Responding to flak from the left and right about my column praising Newt Gingrich’s stance on immigration reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to my column, “The Good Newt,” the incoming missiles are divided so far between readers on the right upset that I support a comprehensive reform of our immigration laws, and those on the left, appalled that I would say anything nice about Newt Gingrich. Also, some flak from readers who see a national ID card – which Gingrich and I consider a prerequisite for seriously enforcing our immigration laws – as the first step toward a police state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More ‘Good Newt’', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2aaba18-662e-5276-8018-6ad99e76d640', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2aaba18-662e-5276-8018-6ad99e76d640'}, {'abstract': "Russians are taking to the streets to oppose Vladimir Putin's presidency. Will the protests dislodge Putin?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2011/12/12/is-the-kremlin-loosening-its-grip/', 'snippet': "Russians are taking to the streets to oppose Vladimir Putin's presidency. Will the protests dislodge Putin?", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Kremlin Loosening Its Grip?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707077d7-676e-5363-ad0d-daa4d66d6423', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707077d7-676e-5363-ad0d-daa4d66d6423'}, {'abstract': 'While efforts continue to bring in $200 million by selling minority stakes, the team got a financial infusion for the second time in a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/sports/baseball/mets-struggling-for-cash-receive-40-million-bank-loan.html', 'snippet': 'While efforts continue to bring in $200 million by selling minority stakes, the team got a financial infusion for the second time in a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The owners of the Mets, needing cash and unable to turn to Major League Baseball for more financial help, received a $40 million loan from a major bank in the past six weeks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/sports/mets/mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 748, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cash-Poor Mets Given $40 Million Bank Loan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cash-Poor Mets Given $40 Million Bank Loan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDERSON, SANDY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Saul B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-12T23:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt and Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3242ee3c-8d81-5aff-a947-e51e80871135', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3242ee3c-8d81-5aff-a947-e51e80871135'}, {'abstract': 'That Wiz Khalifa wo