rt of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the death of the following American on Monday: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:26:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/a256fc18-0066-56aa-9941-1e8105b96d87', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a256fc18-0066-56aa-9941-1e8105b96d87'}, {'abstract': 'Fights in International hockey are rare, and the game is better for it.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/yes-theres-hockey-without-fighting/', 'snippet': 'Fights in International hockey are rare, and the game is better for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recently concluded series of New York Times stories by John Branch on the life and death of Derek Boogaard contains a Large Hadron Collider’s worth of information, but at its core is an examination of the way too many hockey players are developed as fighters in the N.H.L. Still, fans are less and less enamored of fighting, in part because staged fights are the norm, and in larger part because we know the game can be so much better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, There’s Hockey Without Fighting', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's