', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fef2b47-c226-571e-9903-0b470e3246bb', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fef2b47-c226-571e-9903-0b470e3246bb'}, {'abstract': 'Israel on Monday closed a rickety footbridge leading to a holy compound revered by Jews and Muslims after a city engineer determined that it posed an immediate danger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/middleeast/israel-footbridges-closing-draws-ire.html', 'snippet': 'Israel on Monday closed a rickety footbridge leading to a holy compound revered by Jews and Muslims after a city engineer determined that it posed an immediate danger.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Israel on Monday closed a rickety footbridge leading to the holy compound revered by Jews as the Temple Mount and by Muslims as the Noble Sanctuary after a city engineer determined that the wooden walkway posed an immediate danger of fire or collapse. Though it is used only by non-Muslim visitors and Israeli security forces, Palestinian and Muslim authorities condemned the closing, calling it a provocation and a prelude to demolition and construction of a sturdier ramp. Palestinians object to Israel’s carrying out any work at the site in Jerusalem’s Old City on grounds that it is in occupied territory, captured by Israel from Jordan in the 1967 war. Any change in the status quo there has the potential to set off unrest. The bridge, known as the Mugrabi ramp, was erected as a temporary measure in 2004 after an older ramp collapsed. Muslims enter the compound, which houses Al Aksa Mosque, through different entrances. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Footbridge’s Closing Draws Ire', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Footbridge’s Closing Draws Ire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temple Mount (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e84d6f9e-3e51-5c84-843d-291442824486', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e84d6f9e-3e51-5c84-843d-291442824486'}, {'abstract': 'New Canadians must remove face coverings, including niqabs and burqas, at citizenship swearing-in ceremonies, the minister of citizenship and immigration said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/americas/canada-government-bans-veils-at-citizenship-ceremonies.html', 'snippet': 'New Canadians must remove face coverings, including niqabs and burqas, at citizenship swearing-in ceremonies, the minister of citizenship and immigration said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New Canadians must remove face coverings, including niqabs and burqas, at citizenship swearing-in ceremonies, Jason Kenney, the minister of citizenship and immigration, said Monday. He said the new rule would take effect immediately. “Frankly, I found it bizarre that the rules allowed people to take the oath with a veil on,” the Conservative minister said in Montreal. Face covering, particularly by Muslim women, has become a controversial practice in Canada lately. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Government Bans Veils at Citizenship Ceremonies', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Government Bans Veils At Citizenship Ceremonies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Veiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fc82e2-e672-5fe5-a589-2ba68f405235', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fc82e2-e672-5fe5-a589-2ba68f405235'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Robbins, with Paul Nordoff, designed a brand of music therapy for hard-to-reach children that is now used to help people with autism, stroke and Alzheimer’s disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/nyregion/clive-robbins-developer-of-influential-method-of-music-therapy-dies-at-84.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Robbins, with Paul Nordoff, designed a brand of music therapy for hard-to-reach children that is now used to help people with autism, stroke and Alzheimer’s disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clive Robbins, a developer of an influential brand of music therapy designed to help people with various disabilities meet the physical, mental and social challenges that are facts of everyday life, died on Wednesday at his home in Jersey City. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/ROBBINS-obit/ROBBINS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/ROBBINS-obit/ROBBINS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/ROBBINS-obit/ROBBINS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clive Robbins, Developer of a Method of Music Therapy, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clive Robbins, 84, Developer of a Method of Music Therapy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a791ee37-534b-596d-9a95-a9c8e5d34115', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a791ee37-534b-596d-9a95-a9c8e5d34115'}, {'abstract': 'As formerly tough neighborhoods lose their reputations, the bars that once adorned apartment windows are disappearing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/nyregion/in-citys-windows-metal-bars-fade-from-view.html', 'snippet': 'As formerly tough neighborhoods lose their reputations, the bars that once adorned apartment windows are disappearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his 15 years in the South Bronx, Nilo Montalvo says, he has lived in a neighborhood behind bars: vertical rods, child guards, wrought-iron fencing — all wedged into the windows of ground-floor apartments, like his, in a housing project on East 144th Street. “You feel like you’re in prison,” Mr. Montalvo, 64, said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Window Fixtures of Rougher Days Come Down', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Window Fixtures of Rougher Days Come Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T00:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fbd91aa-8fb5-56a5-8ea6-2782fbb8a2fe', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fbd91aa-8fb5-56a5-8ea6-2782fbb8a2fe'}, {'abstract': 'Without a hot toy, retailers are stocking less, leaning on classic items and possibly discounting less in the final days before Christmas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/business/no-hit-toy-to-brighten-retailers-christmas.html', 'snippet': 'Without a hot toy, retailers are stocking less, leaning on classic items and possibly discounting less in the final days before Christmas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Christmas less than two weeks away, the toy industry has no runaway hit — leaving many toy shoppers bored and complicating how stores sell holiday inventory.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/Toys_span/Toysjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType