lobal Inquiry Shifts to Two Trusted Deputies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelow, Bradley I', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steenkamp, Henri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01399b5a-5b6f-5938-9e62-6d12cd9485a0', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01399b5a-5b6f-5938-9e62-6d12cd9485a0'}, {'abstract': 'Law is a subject, not just a practice, and should be treated as such.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/teaching-law/', 'snippet': 'Law is a subject, not just a practice, and should be treated as such.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week marks the last sessions of my Yale law school class on law, liberalism and religion. In the course of the semester my students have learned how to read religion clause cases against the background of long-standing debates in philosophy and theology about the relationship between religious imperatives and the obligations of democratic citizenship. They have become adept at recognizing the arguments behind the arguments the justices are making explicitly. They can see how a case ostensibly about vouchers or school prayer or Christmas trees on courthouse steps is really about whether principle or history should inform a court’s decisions. They can see how a case about head coverings or beards in the military (a topic that has surfaced once again) turns on the distinctions set down in John Locke’s “Letter Concerning Toleration” (1689), a tract the justices may never have read. They can see how the majority and dissenting opinions in a free exercise case often reflect a tension between negative and positive liberty as these terms are defined by Isaiah Berlin, an author the justices will likely not have referenced. They can see how the entire history of religion-clause jurisprudence at once illustrates and is an extended critique of John Rawls’s attempt in “Political Liberalism” to devise a form of government that will be fair to religion while at the same time keeping it at arm’s length.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Law', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/223025dc-6382-5634-859e-c4bb430ef0ff', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/223025dc-6382-5634-859e-c4bb430ef0ff'}, {'abstract': 'Ann Romney likes to tell audiences about “the other side of Mitt that you never hear about.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/us/politics/ann-romney-campaigning-more-actively.html', 'snippet': 'Ann Romney likes to tell audiences about “the other side of Mitt that you never hear about.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Ann Romney switches off shrill TV coverage of the presidential race “all the time.” She is exasperated by the hyperpartisanship of the moment. As for the debates? “Listen,” she said in a rare interview here, “I don’t even want to go to the debates.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/us/politics/ANN/ANN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/us/politics/ANN/ANN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/us/politics/ANN/ANN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaign Sends Romney to the Rescue. Ann Romney.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Campaign Sends Romney To the Rescue. Ann Romney.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f42bd04-4fb0