, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b8d234-9dc6-5786-857e-cfd8358bd79c'}, {'abstract': 'The National Defense Authorization Act that Congress is expected to pass this week is misguided.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/opinion/guantanamo-forever.html', 'snippet': 'The National Defense Authorization Act that Congress is expected to pass this week is misguided.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN his inaugural address, President Obama called on us to “reject as false the choice between our safety and our ideals.” We agree. Now, to protect both, he must veto the National Defense Authorization Act that Congress is expected to pass this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guantánamo Forever?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guantánamo Forever?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles C. Krulak and Joseph P. Hoar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Krulak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Hoar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4940cc38-c368-5fc4-a7f8-7371be904ded', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4940cc38-c368-5fc4-a7f8-7371be904ded'}, {'abstract': 'An officer who had been on the police force for 22 years was shot in the face in a basement apartment that had been robbed in Brooklyn. The officer, Peter J. Figoski, died five hours later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/nyregion/at-scene-of-brooklyn-robbery-a-police-dept-veteran-is-fatally-shot.html', 'snippet': 'An officer who had been on the police force for 22 years was shot in the face in a basement apartment that had been robbed in Brooklyn. The officer, Peter J. Figoski, died five hours later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 911 caller reported a robbery in progress early Monday, and the first officers who arrived at the Brooklyn basement apartment found a tenant bloodied from a beating. They had no idea that the robbers were still there, hiding in a dark room behind them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/JP-COP1/JP-COP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/JP-COP1/JP-COP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/JP-COP1/JP-COP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Dark Brooklyn Doorway, Officer Confronts Gunman, and Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Dark Brooklyn Doorway, Officer Confronts Gunman, and Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Figoski, Peter J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c02dd92-ec3c-5908-b43e-77b106f0b29a', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c02dd92-ec3c-5908-b43e-77b106f0b29a'}, {'abstract': 'Guido Westerwelle, the German foreign minister, called a financial transactions tax positive and invited Britain to return to the fold on the European Union’s economic pact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/world/europe/guido-westerwelle-german-official-backs-tax-vetoed-by-britain.html', 'snippet': 'Guido Westerwelle, the German foreign minister, called a financial transactions tax positive and invited Britain to return to the fold on the European Union’s economic pact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Germany’s foreign minister said Monday that he would like to see a new financial transactions tax imposed on markets in the European Union despite objections from Britain’s government, which vetoed changes in the European Union treaty at the economic crisis summit meeting last week partly in an effort to protect the London-based financial services industry from paying such a tax.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'German Official Backs Tax Vetoed by Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'German Official Backs Tax Vetoed by Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westerwelle, Guido', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:12:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'perso