. Figoski worked the midnight shift in one of New York’s most dangerous precincts, apprehending robbers in and around East New York, Brooklyn, with the instincts of a 22-year veteran. Then he would go home to Long Island to drive his daughters to school.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/nyregion/JP-COP4/JP-COP4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slain Officer Was Devoted to His Daughters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slain Officer Was Devoted to His Daughters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Figoski, Peter J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Figoski, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cypress Hills (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6537abf0-34e0-5d82-8f89-63777b05303e', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6537abf0-34e0-5d82-8f89-63777b05303e'}, {'abstract': 'People don’t trust Congress, that’s for sure. Which professions keep people honest?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/whom-do-you-trust/', 'snippet': 'People don’t trust Congress, that’s for sure. Which professions keep people honest?', 'lead_paragraph': 'People’s faith in Congress continues to sink like a rock. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whom Do You Trust?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1db01a8-ab6e-5a88-9562-facbf3b1bdfd', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1db01a8-ab6e-5a88-9562-facbf3b1bdfd'}, {'abstract': 'How the rise of Newt Gingrich may help the former Utah governor.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/jon-huntsmans-path-to-victory/', 'snippet': 'How the rise of Newt Gingrich may help the former Utah governor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Longtime readers will know that I was initially very skeptical about Jon M. Huntsman Jr.’s chances of winning the Republican nomination. Mr. Huntsman, in my view, had two fundamental challenges that would be very difficult for any candidate to overcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Huntsman’s Path to Victory', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intrade', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:51:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/366e7395-e20e-5b65-9f53-d7da3cc2b31e', 'word_count': 1618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366e7395-e20e-5b65-9f53-d7da3cc2b31e'}, {'abstract': 'In 2009, federal authorities seized Stanford Financial, and the S.E.C. described the company in a court filing as a “massive Ponzi scheme.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/business/sec-files-suit-to-recoup-losses-in-stanford-fraud-case.html', 'snippet': 'In 2009, federal authorities seized Stanford Financial, and the S.E.C. described the company in a court filing as a “massive Ponzi scheme.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Securities and Exchange Commission on Monday sued the Securities Investor Protection Corporation in an effort to help customers who lost money to the Stanford Financial Group file claims for reimbursement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/SIPC/SIPC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Files Suit to Recoup Losses in Stanford Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'S.E.C. Files Suit to Recoup Losses in Stanford Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford Financial Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Investor Protection Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d7f688-f59a-594c-8181-2fce65b45b77', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d7f688-f59a-594c-8181-2fce65b45b77'}, {'abstract': 'Though Martin Marietta Materials is smaller than its intended target, Vulcan Materials, it has some compelling ideas on cutting costs to raise profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/business/when-cost-cuts-make-merger-sense.html', 'snippet': 'Though Martin Marietta Materials is smaller than its intended target, Vulcan Materials, it has some compelling ideas on cutting costs to raise profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rumble in the rock garden may presage more hostile mergers and acquisitions. That’s one way to read the unsolicited $4.6 billion offer that Martin Marietta Materials has made for its larger rival, Vulcan Materials. The all-stock deal probably won’t succeed without some more back-and-forth. But the lesson is clear: if profits cannot be mined from the ground, they can still be found by cutting costs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/Views/Views-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/business/Views/Views-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Cost Cuts Make Merger Sense', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Cost Cuts May Spell Merger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vulcan Materials Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martin Marietta Materials Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Rupee (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T02:57:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and Jeff Glekin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glekin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78b66302-e09f-5bfa-941c-b42d062c1b98', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78b66302-e09f-5bfa-941c-b42d062c1b98'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Gersch shows us how to get, how to get to the answers in this easy Tuesday puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/chips/', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Gersch shows us how to get, how to get to the answers in this easy Tuesday puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — We haven’t seen Jonathan Gersch around these parts for quite a while, but he’s back with a smooth Tuesday grid that made me smile. I was a bit old for “Sesame Street” when it made its debut in 1969, but, ahem, I remember keeping my younger sister company while she watched it, and then doing the same favor for my own kids. Purely to explain the intricate nuances of what was going on, mind you. Not because it was extraordinarily entertaining, even by adult standards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Put Down Some Chips', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88568788-099f-55d1-9112-8e311a99c502', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88568788-099f-55d1-9112-8e311a99c502'}, {'abstract': 'The city of Aurora, Colo., hopes that being the center of a new Congressional district will help propel it from being just a Denver suburb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/us/aurora-colo-tries-to-outshine-its-bigger-neighbor.html', 'snippet': 'The city of Aurora, Colo., hopes that being the center of a new Congressional district will help propel it from being just a Denver suburb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AURORA, Colo. — Second Banana. Tonto to the scene-stealing Lone Ranger. Name the pejorative of disrespect or neglect and this sprawling city, forever in Denver’s shadow as the gawky suburb that outgrew its britches, has probably endured it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/us/jp-AURORA-1/jp-AURORA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Shine in the Shadow of a Neighbor', 'kicker': 'Aurora Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying to Shine In the Shadow Of a Neighbor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Arapahoe County (Colorado)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c29466d-97e5-54ee-b077-43793011c410', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c29466d-97e5-54ee-b077-43793011c410'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement of Mikhail D. Prokhorov’s pursuit of the Russian presidency was greeted with a shrug by league officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/sports/basketball/prokhorovs-candidacy-doesnt-faze-the-nba.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement of Mikhail D. Prokhorov’s pursuit of the Russian presidency was greeted with a shrug by league officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mikhail D. Prokhorov’s foreign roots, business practices and playboy reputation did not prevent him from buying controlling interest in the Nets last year. His political aspirations will not pose an issue to the N.B.A., either.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prokhorov’s Candidacy Doesn’t Faze the N.B.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prokhorov’s Candidacy Doesn’t Faze The N.B.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:06:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a2e3c83-d7e2-56be-af29-cd7e97a4ee6a', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a2e3c83-d7e2-56be-af29-cd7e97a4ee6a'}, {'abstract': 'The latest Republican plan might extend the payroll tax cut and unemployment benefits, but it would do so at the expense of vulnerable Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/opinion/targeting-the-unemployed.html', 'snippet': 'The latest Republican plan might extend the payroll tax cut and unemployment benefits, but it would do so at the expense of vulnerable Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House Republican leadership managed to get one thing right in its bill to extend the payroll tax cut and unemployment benefits. The bill does, indeed, extend the payroll tax cut for another year, but, beyond that, there is a lot to dislike. To help pay for the package, for instance, the bill would cut social spending more deeply than is already anticipated under current budget caps without asking wealthy Americans to contribute a penny in new taxes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Targeting the Unemployed', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Targeting the Unemployed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:10:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/370a2264-e1e3-597e-b221-3c0ed8939b42', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370a2264-e1e3-597e-b221-3c0ed8939b42'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees said they would offer contracts to every unsigned player on their 40-man roster, including Phil Hughes, Dave Robertson, Russell Martin and Brett Gardner.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/12/yankees-look-to-lock-up-youngsters/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees said they would offer contracts to every unsigned player on their 40-man roster, including Phil Hughes, Dave Robertson, Russell Martin and Brett Gardner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees announced on Monday that they would offer contracts to every unsigned player on their 40-man roster, ensuring that key players like Phil Hughes, Dave Robertson, Russell Martin and Brett Gardner will be under their control for another year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Look to Lock Up Young Players', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57631e17-a87a-5082-b007-acc4df4a177c', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57631e17-a87a-5082-b007-acc4df4a177c'}, {'abstract': 'Republican lawmakers are spinning fantasies about the economic benefits and number of jobs created from an oil pipeline from Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/opinion/keystone-claptrap.html', 'snippet': 'Republican lawmakers are spinning fantasies about the economic benefits and number of jobs created from an oil pipeline from Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Keystone XL oil pipeline has become the House Republicans’ weapon of choice in their fight with President Obama over jobs and taxes. Mr. Obama has said he will not make a decision on the pipeline until 2013. The Republicans are insisting that he approve it now and have attached an amendment to a bill extending the payroll tax cut in hopes of forcing his hand.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keystone Claptrap', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keystone Claptrap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T03:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': 