or': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T08:42:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce780220-c5ba-5f5f-8a30-0e9534d1f768', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce780220-c5ba-5f5f-8a30-0e9534d1f768'}, {'abstract': 'On Dec. 13, 1981, authorities in Poland imposed martial law in a crackdown on the pro-democracy Solidarity labor movement.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/dec-13-1981-poland-cracks-down-on-solidarity-movement/', 'snippet': 'On Dec. 13, 1981, authorities in Poland imposed martial law in a crackdown on the pro-democracy Solidarity labor movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 13, 1981, authorities in Poland imposed martial law in a crackdown on the pro-democracy Solidarity labor movement, which had made numerous strikes since August 1980 that challenged the Communist Polish government. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 13, 1981 | Poland Cracks Down on Solidarity Movement', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T09:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd4ecdeb-c1ea-59bf-a780-76c8e0c8c484', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd4ecdeb-c1ea-59bf-a780-76c8e0c8c484'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best antonym for “cantankerous” as it is used in the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/test-yourself-english-dec-13-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best antonym for “cantankerous” as it is used in the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “An AIDS Gala, With Honors and a Few Red Carpet Jitters.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Dec. 13, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T09:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b24e1ea2-9354-5564-88fe-237799587feb', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b24e1ea2-9354-5564-88fe-237799587feb'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | How dangerous is it to be a contestant on “Fear Factor”?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/fear-factor-returns-as-icky-as-ever/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | How dangerous is it to be a contestant on “Fear Factor”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOW long has it been since the most recent season of “Fear Factor” was shown?HOW dangerous is it to be a contestant on the show?HOW many gallons of cow’s blood will be featured this season?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fear Factor’ Returns, as Icky as Ever', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T09:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/609e821d-3633-5e40-8d5b-54975c1bd769', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/609e821d-3633-5e40-8d5b-54975c1bd769'}, {'abstract': 'Maggie Taylor’s whimsical images made with Photoshop will be exhibited in Los Angeles  alongside her husband Jerry Uelsmann’s surreal analog darkroom creations.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/in-her-garden-of-digital-delights/', 'snippet': 'Maggie Taylor’s whimsical images made with Photoshop will be exhibited in Los Angeles  alongside her husband Jerry Uelsmann’s surreal analog darkroom creations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maggie Taylor had never been comfortable photographing people. She was so content shooting still lifes of “stuff” that she collected, that for 10 years she hadn’t even taken her 4×5 camera beyond her garden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Her Garden of Digital Delights', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T10:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eed2f3d-a33f-5353-b49a-5f9627ddccff', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eed2f3d-a33f-5353-b49a-5f9627ddccff'}, {'abstract': 'Do you think that the national conversation on religion is lacking?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/conversations-on-religion/', 'snippet': 'Do you think that the national conversation on religion is lacking?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seizing on the holiday season as an opportunity to talk about spirituality, an Op-Ed writer argues that few people discuss religion in everyday life. He asserts that only devout believers and die-hard nonbelievers raise the subject in conversation. Do you agree? Do you talk about religion with friends? Why or why not?In the Op-Ed article “Americans: Undecided About God?” Eric Weiner laments “the sad state of our national conversation about God”:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Discuss Religion With Friends?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T10:20:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd2872b-95a9-54b6-b49f-a63e07f5ffec', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd2872b-95a9-54b6-b49f-a63e07f5ffec'}, {'abstract': 'José Manuel Barroso said Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain had made requests that would have presented “a risk to the integrity of the internal market” — a reference to the European Union trade area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/europe/european-commission-chief-assails-david-cameron-over-treaty-veto.html', 'snippet': 'José Manuel Barroso said Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain had made requests that would have presented “a risk to the integrity of the internal market” — a reference to the European Union trade area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A senior European official said on Tuesday that Britain’s demands for measures to protect its financial services industry at last week’s summit meeting were impossible to meet and directly responsible for the collapse of a Europe-wide agreement meant to help save the euro.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/europe/14britain-span/14britain-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/europe/14britain-span/14britain-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/world/europe/14britain-span/14britain-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Commission Chief Assails Britain Over Treaty Veto', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top European Official Assails Britain Over Veto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barroso, Jose Manuel Durao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T10:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall and Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'first