 Need It and What It Will Take.”.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Counts as ‘Rich’? Continued', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38994353-201d-5bce-8a4a-2c0b689db2f9', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38994353-201d-5bce-8a4a-2c0b689db2f9'}, {'abstract': 'The Patriots’ Rob Gronkowski is on his way to the best season by a tight end in N.F.L. history.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/rob-gronkowski-and-the-year-of-the-tight-end/', 'snippet': 'The Patriots’ Rob Gronkowski is on his way to the best season by a tight end in N.F.L. history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the postscript is written on the 2011 season, Aaron Rodgers may be remembered as having the best season a quarterback has ever had. We don’t need to wait much longer to acknowledge the same at another position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rob Gronkowski, and the Year of the Tight End', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gronkowski, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T11:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d1cbd01-ebf0-5d44-8403-841573bf7aea', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d1cbd01-ebf0-5d44-8403-841573bf7aea'}, {'abstract': 'The new Tauromaquia exhibition at Obecni dum in Prague features 150 works by Picasso, Goya, Dali and other artists whose works were inspired by bullfighting.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/bullfighting-gets-a-closer-look-in-prague/', 'snippet': 'The new Tauromaquia exhibition at Obecni dum in Prague features 150 works by Picasso, Goya, Dali and other artists whose works were inspired by bullfighting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who has seen a matador in action knows that bullfighting is an art. But the creativity it inspires is not restricted to the ring – artists from Picasso to Dalí to the Czech artist Emil Filla have created works using the sport as a theme. One hundred fifty such pieces are now on view in Prague through April 9 at the Tauromaquia exhibition\xa0 at Obecni dum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bullfighting Gets a Closer Look in Prague', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goya, Francisco de', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T11:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacy Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cfe622-3164-5c42-89e4-100246f0a9da', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cfe622-3164-5c42-89e4-100246f0a9da'}, {'abstract': 'Walking in the footsteps of a 17th century Ottoman traveler could save Turkey from the ravages of modern tourism.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/doing-it-the-evliya-celebi-way/', 'snippet': 'Walking in the footsteps of a 17th century Ottoman traveler could save Turkey from the ravages of modern tourism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Whenever I set out to tour Turkey with my wife, I understand exactly what Diana, Princess of Wales, meant when she complained about there being “three of us” in her marriage. My rival’s name is Evliya Celebi, and he spent much of his life on a horse. He was born 400 years ago and Unesco decided to celebrate his birth this year. I can’t compete.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doing It the Evliya Celebi Way', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T11:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/921bb413-9b2e-5f7b-824c-f1932fc98f5e', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/921bb413-9b2e-5f7b-824c-f1932fc98f5e'}, {'abstract': 'Chelsea Clinton gave an utterly unsatisfying explanation on Monday for why she made her debut as a special correspondent on NBC’s magazine program, “Rock Center with Brian Williams.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/chelsea-clinton-finally-embraces-her-celebrity/', 'snippet': 'Chelsea Clinton gave an utterly unsatisfying explanation on Monday for why she made her debut as a special correspondent on NBC’s magazine program, “Rock Center with Brian Williams.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chelsea Clinton gave a perfectly honed and utterly unsatisfying explanation on Monday for why she has made her debut as a special correspondent on NBC’s magazine show “Rock Center WithBrian Williams.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The TV Watch: Chelsea Clinton Finally Embraces Her Celebrity', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T11:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d130709a-1b2c-5ff1-90e5-1b344190ffef', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d130709a-1b2c-5ff1-90e5-1b344190ffef'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Tebow’s run of late-game success is reminiscent of George Blanda’s improbable stretch in 1970. Blanda gets extra credit: He was 43 years old.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/before-tebow-there-was-blanda/', 'snippet': 'Tim Tebow’s run of late-game success is reminiscent of George Blanda’s improbable stretch in 1970. Blanda gets extra credit: He was 43 years old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Tebow’s late-game performances are already the stuff of legend. He has captivated the nation with a string of last-minute heroics, leaving the public wanting more.\xa0Tebow’s statistics aren’t very impressive, but he is a flavor best enjoyed without serious thought. You have to see it to understand it. And that makes his run reminiscent of an improbable stretch that took place over four decades ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Tebow, There Was Blanda', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanda, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00916e2b-4091-567e-be20-b08767422cbf', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00916e2b-4091-567e-be20-b08767422cbf'}, {'abstract': 'The city is now accepting bids for a lighting initiative that aims to “transform the experience of Lower Manhattan at night.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/in-lower-manhattan-a-light-show-looms/', 'snippet': 'The city is now accepting bids for a lighting initiative that aims to “transform the experience of Lower Manhattan at night.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounds like a scene straight out of Las Vegas or Orlando: streets magically illuminated by an interactive light show, complete with 3-D effects and lights that respond to kinetic pedestrian motion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Lower Manhattan, a Light Show Looms', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economic Development Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a80d2a50-7f4f-581f-a2f7-9cda2dcdcf04', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a80d2a50-7f4f-581f-a2f7-9cda2dcdcf04'}, {'abstract': 'Can a company this small go head-to-head with powerhouses like Macy’s, Nordstrom, Target, Babies “R” Us, and Diapers.com? It isn’t easy. “We are not scared of criticism,” said one of the owners. “We are scared that there might be something that we can do to improve, but we just don’t know about it.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/a-small-retailer-tries-to-compete-with-the-big-boys-online/', 'snippet': 'Can a company this small go head-to-head with powerhouses like Macy’s, Nordstrom, Target, Babies “R” Us, and Diapers.com? It isn’t easy. “We are not scared of criticism,” said one of the owners. “We are scared that there might be something that we...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Little Dudes and Divas is a small business with some very big competition. Started seven years ago by Steve and Susan Karasanti, husband and wife, the company has three employees and sells clothes and accessories for infants and toddlers. Ninety percent of the sales come through the Web site, the rest through a newly opened brick-and-mortar store in Rockaway Park, N.Y., where the company is based.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Small Retailer Compete Online With the Big Boys?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabriel Shaoolian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabriel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaoolian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2addf13b-084a-54d4-8287-7959102e3142', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2addf13b-084a-54d4-8287-7959102e3142'}, {'abstract': 'The nation’s largest cable provider plans to offer BBC to nearly 15 million homes by the end of next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/business/media/bbc-world-news-to-be-available-through-comcast.html', 'snippet': 'The nation’s largest cable provider plans to offer BBC to nearly 15 million homes by the end of next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The BBC will announce on Tuesday a first-of-its-kind deal for Comcast to carry the BBC World News channel, opening the door to wider distribution for the channel within the United States.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/BBC/BBC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/business/BBC/BBC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/BBC/BBC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/business/BBC/BBC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/business/BBC/BBC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'BBC World News to Be Available Through Comcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BBC World News to Be Available Through Comcast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':