ount': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/298dee7a-15b2-5f5a-b285-ac44f49a3397'}, {'abstract': 'The anti-corruption bill, an albatross for more than forty years.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/newswallah-four-decades-of-lokpal/', 'snippet': 'The anti-corruption bill, an albatross for more than forty years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty-three years and at least eight versions of the Lokpal bill later, Parliament still hasn’t reached consensus on who and what, exactly, it should cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Four Decades of Lokpal', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Policy Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:31:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikhila Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikhila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa1ecdd3-f944-512f-816d-b7939f524c70', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa1ecdd3-f944-512f-816d-b7939f524c70'}, {'abstract': 'For months a group of names has swarmed around the creative director’s job at Dior, with the industry joining the buzz. Today, Women’s Wear Daily, quoting industry sources, said Raf Simons is in discussion for the Dior job.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/more-talk-about-that-dior-job/', 'snippet': 'For months a group of names has swarmed around the creative director’s job at Dior, with the industry joining the buzz. Today, Women’s Wear Daily, quoting industry sources, said Raf Simons is in discussion for the Dior job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months a group of names has swarmed around the creative director’s job at Dior, with the industry joining the buzz. Among the names mentioned early on were Marc Jacobs, Riccardo Tisci, Nicolas Ghesquiere, Alber Elbaz. Then in November it was Alexander Wang, Jason Wu and Raf Simons. Today, Women’s Wear Daily, quoting industry sources, said Mr. Simons is in discussion for the Dior job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Talk about That Dior Job', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aca5125-0481-5f5e-a128-d98dca2ee5dd', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aca5125-0481-5f5e-a128-d98dca2ee5dd'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican nomination is shaping up as a fight between the mild-mannered pragmatist and the rhetorical bomb-thrower.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/romney-and-gingrich-a-contrast-in-styles/', 'snippet': 'The Republican nomination is shaping up as a fight between the mild-mannered pragmatist and the rhetorical bomb-thrower.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is the essential difference between Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney and Gingrich, a Contrast in Styles', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/070432ae-76c7-5d3b-be2d-99caa67f2f79', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/070432ae-76c7-5d3b-be2d-99caa67f2f79'}, {'abstract': 'Tapeworm larvae grew four times faster in fish raised at 68 degrees Fahrenheit than in those raised at 59 degrees, researchers report.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/warming-world-abets-a-fish-parasite-study-suggests/', 'snippet': 'Tapeworm larvae grew four times faster in fish raised at 68 degrees Fahrenheit than in those raised at 59 degrees, researchers report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounds almost like science fiction: A parasite manipulates a fish’s behavior to make it seek out warmer water, probably by altering its brain chemistry. In the warmer environment, the parasite’s growth — and its capacity to infect other hosts — kicks into overdrive. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warming World Abets a Fish Parasite, Study Suggests', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T12:58:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josie Garthwaite', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garthwaite', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d4399b-2c72-5f4d-94a0-ba3ee5ee23b7', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d4399b-2c72-5f4d-94a0-ba3ee5ee23b7'}, {'abstract': 'We never say “one” if we really mean “a thousand.” So why, oh why do we so often say “million” when we mean “billion”? The magnitude of the error is the same — we’re off not by one consonant, but by a factor of 1,000.', 'web_url': 'https://topics.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/millions-and-billions/', 'snippet': 'We never say “one” if we really mean “a thousand.” So why, oh why do we so often say “million” when we mean “billion”? The magnitude of the error is the same — we’re off not by one consonant, but by a factor of 1,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions and Billions', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba4c96d5-56dc-5f94-8a3b-db2e98988765', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba4c96d5-56dc-5f94-8a3b-db2e98988765'}, {'abstract': 'We never say “one” if we really mean “a thousand.” So why, oh why do we so often say “million” when we mean “billion”? The magnitude of the error is the same — we’re off not by one consonant, but by a factor of 1,000.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/millions-and-billions/', 'snippet': 'We never say “one” if we really mean “a thousand.” So why, oh why do we so often say “million” when we mean “billion”? The magnitude of the error is the same — we’re off not by one consonant, but by a factor of 1,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions and Billions', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3651b22-8d3d-5bd1-9435-3bc32053d388', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3651b22-8d3d-5bd1-9435-3bc32053d388'}, {'abstract': 'If liberals in Egypt are to stand a chance in this, or any, election, they must connect with the Egyptian people. But can they?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/egypts-liberals-adrift/', 'snippet': 'If liberals in Egypt are to stand a chance in this, or any, election, they must connect with the Egyptian people. But can they?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt’s liberals are spooked. If the two-day voting in the second round of parliamentary elections that begins Wednesday goes the same way the first round did, Islamist parties will dominate the new lower house of Parliament. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Liberals Adrift', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': Non