://article/3e8420d6-d9cb-50fe-b7e0-480a5e4a0956'}, {'abstract': 'The shortage of hard drives and finished personal computers could prove an opportunity for Intel as it fights the onslaught of tablet computers, particularly Apple’s iPad. It has been trying to build a business in the emerging category of ultrathin laptops, which do not use hard drives.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/daily-report-intel-sees-an-opportunity-in-drives-shortage/', 'snippet': 'The shortage of hard drives and finished personal computers could prove an opportunity for Intel as it fights the onslaught of tablet computers, particularly Apple’s iPad. It has been trying to build a business in the emerging category of ultrathi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intel, the world’s largest maker of semiconductors, said on Monday that its revenue this quarter would fall to $13.7 billion, from $14.7 billion, because floods in Thailand had sharply cut the world’s supply of disk drives. Without the drives, manufacturers will make fewer personal computers and computer servers, which means fewer semiconductors will be needed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Intel Sees an Opportunity in Drives Shortage', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69c5d416-fba4-5209-b08f-758779e5c09c', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69c5d416-fba4-5209-b08f-758779e5c09c'}, {'abstract': 'Bookstores bounce back, the Kindle Fire falls a little flat and Chelsea Clinton makes her NBC debut.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-13/', 'snippet': 'Bookstores bounce back, the Kindle Fire falls a little flat and Chelsea Clinton makes her NBC debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bookstores have reported an unexpectedly strong beginning to the Christmas shopping season, lifted by “an unusually vibrant selection,” Julie Bosman writes. It has been a strong year for nonfiction, some booksellers pointed out, starting with the Steve Jobs biography by Walter Isaacson. However, the increased business is also a product of the closing of the Borders Books chain, whose customers are visiting other stores to do their book shopping. Overall sales will take a hit from the loss of Borders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 13', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dowler, Milly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Walter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0805ccc3-0ea6-5ecd-aedc-26c4ff33bd1a', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0805ccc3-0ea6-5ecd-aedc-26c4ff33bd1a'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Death rarely pounces on police officers in the line of duty these days, but it remains an eternal possibility. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/an-officer-falls/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Death rarely pounces on police officers in the line of duty these days, but it remains an eternal possibility. Also, what City Room is reading in other newspapers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Police Officer Peter J. Figoski never stood a chance. He didn’t even have time, the Police Department said, to pull his gun before a man described as a career criminal killed him in Brooklyn Monday morning with a bullet to the face. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Officer Falls', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Figoski, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c4849b0-1bdf-5610-9111-60e5ab1d169b', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c4849b0-1bdf-5610-9111-60e5ab1d169b'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/1