, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:29:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aaf7ba7-75b6-51ff-b16f-b0248b701154', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aaf7ba7-75b6-51ff-b16f-b0248b701154'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of radical Jewish settlers, reacting to a rumor that several of their outposts would be dismantled, attacked an Israeli army base in the West Bank on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/middleeast/radical-jewish-settlers-clash-with-israeli-troops.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of radical Jewish settlers, reacting to a rumor that several of their outposts would be dismantled, attacked an Israeli army base in the West Bank on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Dozens of radical Jewish settlers, reacting to a rumor that several of their outposts would be dismantled, attacked an Israeli Army base in the West Bank on Tuesday, lighting fires, vandalizing vehicles and throwing stones, hours after another group of settlers occupied a border post with Jordan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Settlers Riot, Attacking Israeli Base and Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Settlers Riot, Attacking Israeli Base And Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/337c4cbe-aed7-55ac-bfa8-8735c4c6df13', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/337c4cbe-aed7-55ac-bfa8-8735c4c6df13'}, {'abstract': 'Jerry Sandusky’s autobiography is no longer available from Amazon, but that is not stopping would-be reviewers, who are piling on with sarcastic reviews.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/reviewing-jerry-sandusky/', 'snippet': 'Jerry Sandusky’s autobiography is no longer available from Amazon, but that is not stopping would-be reviewers, who are piling on with sarcastic reviews.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In an earlier era, crowds might have massed in State College, Pa., to vocally proclaim their displeasure at Jerry Sandusky, the former Penn State coach charged with many counts of sexual abuse of young boys. Now, in one of the less-anticipated developments of e-commerce, the mobs gather online to vent while Christmas shopping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Jerry Sandusky', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b30c6b1c-17e5-588e-b309-bc3800c8043b', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b30c6b1c-17e5-588e-b309-bc3800c8043b'}, {'abstract': 'Talking about mean girls with Diablo Cody, screenwriter of “Young Adult.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/what-happens-when-mean-girls-grow-up/', 'snippet': 'Talking about mean girls with Diablo Cody, screenwriter of “Young Adult.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we were saying, the Bagger is a fan of the “Young Adult” crew, which will receive the Vanguard Award from the Palm Springs International Film Festival in January, alongside other Oscar path honorees like George Clooney, Glenn Close, Michelle Williams, Michel Hazanavicius (“The Artist”) and Octavia Spencer (“The Help”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens When Mean Girls Grow Up', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f60e702d-3988-5904-8477-d463ddd93a3d', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f60e702d-3988-5904-8477-d463ddd93a3d'}, {'abstract': 'The police say that they now have five suspects in custody in the Brooklyn robbery that turned into Monday morning’s deadly shooting of Officer Peter J. Figoski.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/5-in-custody-in-robbery-that-led-to-killing-of-officer/', 'snippet': 'The police say that they now have five suspects in custody in the Brooklyn robbery that turned into Monday morning’s deadly shooting of Officer Peter J. Figoski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 4:34 p.m. | The police said on Tuesday that they now have four more suspects in custody in the Brooklyn robbery that turned into Monday morning’s deadly shooting of a veteran police officer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '5 in Custody in Robbery That Led to Killing of Officer', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins and Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca5703c-f025-54f3-89f9-8ec8379090dc', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca5703c-f025-54f3-89f9-8ec8379090dc'}, {'abstract': 'As predicted.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/receding-inflation-in-britain/', 'snippet': 'As predicted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in June, keying off a speech by Adam Posen, I said that British inflation was offering a teachable moment. The headline inflation number was running quite high, but even a bit of analysis showed that this largely reflected temporary shocks, mainly hikes in VAT and commodity prices plus some effects from the depreciation of the pound. Yet there was much hysteria, with many claiming that Britain was on the verge of a 1970s-type inflationary spiral. I concluded,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Receding Inflation In Britain', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T13:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/338e19a2-e3db-5ff8-86fd-66556620bb07', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/338e19a2-e3db-5ff8-86fd-66556620bb07'}, {'abstract': 'A man carrying a variety of weapons created panic at a crowded bus stop in Liège, injuring dozens in an attack that the authorities believe is not related to terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/europe/deadly-grenade-attack-reported-in-belgium.html', 'snippet': 'A man carrying a variety of weapons created panic at a crowded bus stop in Liège, injuring dozens in an attack that the authorities believe is not related to terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIÈGE, Belgium — A man with a history of run-ins with the law lobbed three hand grenades and opened fire at a crowded central bus stop here Tuesday, killing several people, wounding scores and creating a panic before killing himself, officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/BELGIUM/BELGIUM-