om 10-point deficits Sunday, tying an N.F.L. record. Five of those teams trailed by at least 12 points, making Week 14 the first week in history to have so many teams rally from a 12-point deficit to win. Some of the quarterbacks on those teams are getting pretty good at this comeback thing. Scott Kacsmar, who writes the “Captain Comeback” column for Cold, Hard Football Facts (and has contributed his comeback research to Pro-Football-Reference.com), e-mailed me some additional notes on Monday:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week of the Comeback in the N.F.L.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T14:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eecc163-b098-54d9-8fad-a9de71baf0d4', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eecc163-b098-54d9-8fad-a9de71baf0d4'}, {'abstract': 'After several months of reporting on K12, a publicly traded company that manages online learning programs, "a portrait emerges of a company that tries to squeeze profits from public school dollars by raising enrollment, increasing teacher workload and lowering standards," The New York Times reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/13/online-learning-choice-yes-but-a-good-one/', 'snippet': 'After several months of reporting on K12, a publicly traded company that manages online learning programs, "a portrait emerges of a company that tries to squeeze profits from public school dollars by raising enrollment