urce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Beware of Raw Cookie Dough', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T14:40:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06aa7103-f5b0-53e9-abdd-fa553b5218d2', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06aa7103-f5b0-53e9-abdd-fa553b5218d2'}, {'abstract': 'Jon S. Corzine and two former top deputies at MF Global are appearing before the Senate Agriculture Committee to answer questions about the collapse of the brokerage firm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/live-blog-senate-panel-hearing-on-mf-global/', 'snippet': 'Jon S. Corzine and two former top deputies at MF Global are appearing before the Senate Agriculture Committee to answer questions about the collapse of the brokerage firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Congressional inquiry into MF Global continues, a hearing that will focus on the collapse of the commodities brokerage firm and the disappearance of an estimated $1.2 billion in customer money. Jon S. Corzine, the former leader of the brokerage firm who testified before a House panel last week, is appearing before the Senate Agriculture Committee on Tuesday. Lawmakers will also hear, for the first time, from two of Mr. Corzine’s former top deputies: Bradley Abelow, MF Global’s chief operating officer, and Henri J. Steenkamp, the firm’s chief financial officer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: Senate Panel Hearing on MF Global', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea