3e2db', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a599ced-7699-5a5a-a7fe-c7a4bbb3e2db'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans will have to appeal to the right to win the primary race, said David Axelrod,  the president’s chief campaign strategist.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/a-long-republican-battle-the-obama-campaign-likes-it/', 'snippet': 'Republicans will have to appeal to the right to win the primary race, said David Axelrod,  the president’s chief campaign strategist.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:08 p.m. | Updated The full report of this article is available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Team Likes Prospect of Long Republican Fight', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Axelrod, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T15:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e71f3c1-96eb-5811-b43f-045b9ac2486c', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e71f3c1-96eb-5811-b43f-045b9ac2486c'}, {'abstract': 'Not far from the manicured and deserted boulevards of Myanmar’s capital, Naypyidaw, villagers struggle with grinding poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/asia/hopes-and-reality-clash-in-a-new-myanmar.html', 'snippet': 'Not far from the manicured and deserted boulevards of Myanmar’s capital, Naypyidaw, villagers struggle with grinding poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAYPYIDAW, Myanmar — The road leading to Myanmar’s giant Parliament building is 20 lanes wide, well suited for military processions but eerily empty the rest of the time. A half-hour drive away, down this city’s manicured avenues, is another immense edifice, still under construction: a military museum that will serve as a shrine to the country’s generals and admirals. Across the way is a military training academy; farther down the road are rows of barracks and a vast parade ground. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/MYANMAR-1/MYANMAR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/world/MYANMAR-1/MYANMAR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/MYANMAR-1/MYANMAR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/MYANMAR-1/MYANMAR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/world/MYANMAR-1/MYANMAR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surrounded by Poverty, a Lifeless Capital Stands Aloof', 'kicker': 'Naypyidaw Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surrounded by Poverty, A Lifeless Capital Stands Aloof', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Naypyidaw (Myanmar)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T15:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70eb13d0-e331-544d-b335-3df9662ce967', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70eb13d0-e331-544d-b335-3df9662ce967'}, {'abstract': 'Several same-sex couples have been denied the federal adoption tax credit. But the reasons the I.R.S. provided for the denials are not consistent with the law.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/i-r-s-denying-lesbians-legitimate-adoption-credit/', 'snippet': 'Several same-sex couples have been denied the federal adoption tax credit. But the reasons the I.R.S. provided for the denials are not consistent with the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the federal government does not recognize same-sex marriage, such couples are viewed as strangers in many spheres of their financial lives. They need to file separate federal tax returns, for instance. \xa0And sometimes, that can come with certain advantages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S. Denied Lesbians Legitimate Adoption Credit', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T15:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c0bd7f6-e027-5287-927e-5dd006941a3a', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c0bd7f6-e027-5287-927e-5dd006941a3a'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadcast Film Critics Association unveils its nominations, giving “Drive,” “Hugo” and “The Artist” multiple mentions.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/drive-picks-up-momentum-with-broadcast-critics-nominations/', 'snippet': 'The Broadcast Film Critics Association unveils its nominations, giving “Drive,” “Hugo” and “The Artist” multiple mentions.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Drive” careened into a top spot with the Broadcast Film Critics Association, receiving nods for best picture and best director, among 10 nominations over all. Two other films surpassed that: “Hugo” and “The Artist” each earned 11 nominations (including best picture and best director). But “Drive,” Nicolas Winding Refn’s vehicular thriller, has been an outlier thus far in this awards race, though the Bagger thinks it could get some love from members of the Academy, who have been known to reward a violent automotive movie. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Drive’ Picks Up Momentum With Broadcast Critics’ Nominations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T16:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64afb45-852e-5716-b30c-322638918c07', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64afb45-852e-5716-b30c-322638918c07'}, {'abstract': 'Within weeks of opening, the Nashville restaurant has diners abuzz with its bold, daring approach to high-end cuisine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/now-dining-the-catbird-seat-in-nashville/', 'snippet': 'Within weeks of opening, the Nashville restaurant has diners abuzz with its bold, daring approach to high-end cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within weeks of opening, the Catbird Seat has diners in Nashville and beyond abuzz with its bold, daring approach to high-end cuisine. Run by the co-executive chefs Erik Anderson and Josh Habiger (who’ve trained in the world’s top kitchens, including Noma, the Fat Duck and the French Laundry), the restaurant offers a simple menu: one multicourse, prix fixe dinner that changes weekly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Table Talk | The Catbird Seat in Nashville', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fat Duck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Laundry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T16:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45efaf34-ceb6-52c4-90a0-b9d6e23e9e0f', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45efaf34-ceb6-52c4-90a0-b9d6e23e9e0f'}, {'abstract': 'Eggs, Cheddar cheese, yogurt and soy sauce were among the most popular items in American kitchens, whereas mincemeat and artichokes were hard to find, according to a new report.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/whats-in-your-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'Eggs, Cheddar cheese, yogurt and soy sauce were among the most popular items in American kitchens, whereas mincemeat and artichokes were hard to find, according to a new report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s in your refrigerator? There’s a good chance that residing somewhere on its shelves is at least one carton of eggs and a block of Cheddar cheese. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in Your Kitchen?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chee