ed him from the team.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/boston-universitys-trivino-arrested-kicked-off-team/', 'snippet': 'Corey Trivino, a New York Islanders draft pick and a star center for Boston University, was arrested on Sunday on assault charges and Coach Jack Parker dismissed him from the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corey Trivino, a Boston University center and the leading goal scorer in the Hockey East conference, was thrown off the team by Coach Jack Parker after being arrested Sunday on charges of indecent assault and battery. Parker told BU Today that Trivino had been dismissed from the team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston University’s Trivino Arrested, Kicked Off Team', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57edfd40-babe-5d7b-a041-749711510ab7', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57edfd40-babe-5d7b-a041-749711510ab7'}, {'abstract': 'To mark the pullout of American forces from Iraq we asked Iraqis questions about the war and their country’s future. Sgt. Maj. Ahmed Salman wants the army to hold its ground after the Americans leave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001222677/a-soldiers-hope-for-security.html', 'snippet': 'To mark the pullout of American forces from Iraq we asked Iraqis questions about the war and their country’s future. Sgt. Maj. Ahmed Salman wants the army to hold its ground after the Americans leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To mark the pullout of American forces from Iraq we asked Iraqis questions about the war and their country’s future. Sgt. Maj. Ahmed Salman wants the army to hold its ground after the Americans leave.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/world/video-iraqivoices-abu/video-iraqivoices-abu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/12/world/video-iraqivoices-abu/video-iraqivoices-abu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/world/video-iraqivoices-abu/video-iraqivoices-abu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/12/world/video-iraqivoices-abu/video-iraqivoices-abu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "A Soldier's Hope for Security", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:36:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4800261b-049c-5a9a-919b-cdfc6a3fd51b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4800261b-049c-5a9a-919b-cdfc6a3fd51b'}, {'abstract': 'A reporter thinks it might be interesting to revisit his first bylined article of 30 years ago. He learns he made at least two errors in the piece. The reporter cancels plans for a 35th anniversary retrospective.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/a-correction-from-the-way-back-machine/', 'snippet': 'A reporter thinks it might be interesting to revisit his first bylined article of 30 years ago. He learns he made at least two errors in the piece. The reporter cancels plans for a 35th anniversary retrospective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on July 20, 1981, about the failure of the transmitter serving the Columbia University radio station, WKCR-FM, misspelled the name of the station’s general manager. He was Michael Silberstein, not Silverstein. This correction was delayed because we heard from Mr. Silberstein only last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Correction From the Way Back Machine', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Correction Stories', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WKCR-FM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e9fe6f-8d53-55b9-89a5-9719a899a327', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e9fe6f-8d53-55b9-89a5-9719a899a327'}, {'abstract': 'The top American commander in Afghanistan, Gen. John R. Allen of the Marine Corps, said he would emphasize deploying foreign military trainers with Afghan units.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/asia/us-plans-afghan-shift-to-lessen-nato-combat-role.html', 'snippet': 'The top American commander in Afghanistan, Gen. John R. Allen of the Marine Corps, said he would emphasize deploying foreign military trainers with Afghan units.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The senior American commander in Afghanistan said Tuesday that his plans for next year would emphasize deploying American and allied military trainers directly within Afghan security units, which could lessen the direct combat role of NATO and accelerate local forces’ taking the lead in a growing number of missions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/SUB-SUB-KABUL/SUB-SUB-KABUL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/world/SUB-SUB-KABUL/SUB-SUB-KABUL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/SUB-SUB-KABUL/SUB-SUB-KABUL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/SUB-SUB-KABUL/SUB-SUB-KABUL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/world/SUB-SUB-KABUL/SUB-SUB-KABUL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Shift May Push Afghans Into Lead Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Shift May Push Afghans Into Lead Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, John R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/311476b3-9654-52e2-8f49-6d292b4cca69', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/311476b3-9654-52e2-8f49-6d292b4cca69'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. weighed in on the partisan debate over race and ballot access in a speech assessing new state laws that critics say restrict voting rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/us/politics/in-speech-holder-to-critique-new-voting-laws.html', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. weighed in on the partisan debate over race and ballot access in a speech assessing new state laws that critics say restrict voting rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. on Tuesday entered the turbulent political waters of voting rights, signaling that the Justice Department would be aggressive in reviewing new voting laws that civil rights advocates say will dampen minority participation in next year’s elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-HOLDER/jp-HOLDER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-HOLDER/jp-HOLDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-HOLDER/jp-HOLDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holder Signals Tough Review of New State Laws on Voting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holder Signals Tough Review Of State Laws on Voting Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae757daa-4dd0-5bda-bcb7-b8d78b155009', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae757daa-4dd0-5bda-bcb7-b8d78b155009'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry says in an ad that it is taboo to take on the insider culture of Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/new-perry-ad-assails-washingtons-political-correctness/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry says in an ad that it is taboo to take on the insider culture of Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Much of the thrust of Gov. Rick Perry’s campaign message has drifted in recent weeks to his proposal to “overhaul Washington.” It includes stripping federal judges of lifetime tenure — which legal scholars say means getting 38 states to pass amendments rewriting Article III of the Constitution — and he also calls for somehow persuading members of Congress to cut their own salaries by 50 percent to 75 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Perry Ad Assails Washington’s ‘Political Correctness’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T17:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/731641d6-6da1-5e48-8133-20c1d5d11ba7', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/731641d6-6da1-5e48-8133-20c1d5d11ba7'}, {'abstract': 'All told, we figure it will take $301,500 to get started in early 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/inside-our-plan-to-open-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'All told, we figure it will take $301,500 to get started in early 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hunting and gathering in Brooklyn has been swift and successful. An existing restaurant recently became available — a 45-seater with a small garden in the back, located on a bustling street in a cosmopolitan section of the borough. It is in excellent condition, though not perfect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Our Plan to Open in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bridgehampton (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea91fe59-82cf-5409-9674-ae6da056412c', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea91fe59-82cf-5409-9674-ae6da056412c'}, {'abstract': 'Many merchants offer delivery at no charge for purchases made on Free Shipping Day.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/holiday-shipping-dates-free-and-otherwise/', 'snippet': 'Many merchants offer delivery at no charge for purchases made on Free Shipping Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you sat out Black Friday and Cyber Monday, there’s one more holiday-shopping-related date you may want to mark on your calendar: Free Shipping Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Shipping Dates, Free and Otherwise', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LL Bean Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5d6c8d0-139b-5c5c-b954-71a42765e293', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5d6c8d0-139b-5c5c-b954-71a42765e293'}, {'abstract': 'The program accounted for 21.9 percent of all state expenditures in 2009 and 22.3 percent in 2010, and education is getting a smaller slice of the pie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/us/in-downturn-medicaid-takes-up-more-of-state-budgets-analysis-finds.html', 'snippet': 'The program accounted for 21.9 percent of all state expenditures in 2009 and 22.3 percent in 2010, and education is getting a smaller slice of the pie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medicaid has steadily eaten up a growing share of state budgets over the past three years, while education has been getting a smaller slice of the pie.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bigger Share of State Cash for Medicaid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bigger Share Of State Cash For Medicaid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of State Budget Officers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d70002a1-2b7f-5599-94d3-8a0c5014b548', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d70002a1-2b7f-5599-94d3-8a0c5014b548'}, {'abstract': 'Yesterday, Advertising Age published its list of the 10 best magazine covers of 2011, and among their number one from The Times Magazine in August, which featured Andy Samberg channeling both Bjorn Borg and John McEnroe.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/courting-athletes/', 'snippet': 'Yesterday, Advertising Age published its list of the 10 best magazine covers of 2011, and among their number one from The Times Magazine in August, which featured Andy Samberg channeling both Bjorn Borg and John McEnroe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, Advertising Age published its list of the 10 best magazine covers of 2011, and among their number is the one at right, from August, which featured Andy Samberg channeling both Bjorn Borg and John McEnroe for us. You can revisit some behind-the-scenes pictures from its creation here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Courting Athletes', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEnroe, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AGE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sports Illustrated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1749311e-b577-5102-9f05-1d12c76f82d8', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1749311e-b577-5102-9f05-1d12c76f82d8'}, {'abstract': 'Party pants, in updated styles from the resort collections, feel fresh for the holidays.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/bright-lights-for-the-party/', 'snippet': 'Party pants, in updated styles from the resort collections, feel fresh for the holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Party pants, in updated styles from the resort collections, feel fresh for the holidays. Lanvin’s silk-print pants, with a high waist and tapered legs, are shiny and festive, as are Balenciaga’s metallic models, which look rather like track pants, with the contrasting fabric insets down the sides. The British label Reiss also has glittery holiday trousers, cropped with a high waist, in a dark gold sequin print. For style guidance, look to Charlotte Gainsbourg, who, for the premiere of “Melancholia,” wore her Balenciagas with a loose black shirt. For additional options, you might check out the denim brands: AG, Siwy and Genetic Denim all have versions of sequin jeans in stores now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bright Lights for the Party', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c094136-0334-5d5e-84ed-f6f8775de899', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c094136-0334-5d5e-84ed-f6f8775de899'}, {'abstract': 'Forget sentimental jewelry. Street-inspired gothic script charm necklaces send a different message.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/the-get-jennifer-fisher-charms/', 'snippet': 'Forget sentimental jewelry. Street-inspired gothic script charm necklaces send a different message.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an alternative to the sentimental letter-stamped gold coins that have been dangling from necklaces long and short in recent years, the New York-based jewelry designer Jennifer Fisher created these great, street-inspired gothic script charms. “They remind me of the skate and Latino cultures in Santa Barbara, California, where I grew up,” Fisher says. “The Black Letter type style was the predominant font for skin art and tattoos.” Every letter in the alphabet comes in yellow gold, rose gold and diamond pavé, and is sold separately so you can customize your chain. Consider the message above a not-so-subtle hint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Jennifer Fisher Charms', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b01d3458-6d3d-5d45-82f4-52ac57f65217', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b01d3458-6d3d-5d45-82f4-52ac57f65217'}, {'abstract': 'Players at Xavier and Cincinnati have been suspended for the fight at the end of their annual rivalry game and a prosecutor is considering whether further action is warranted.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/xavier-cincinnati-brawl-could-bring-criminal-charges/', 'snippet': 'Players at Xavier and Cincinnati have been suspended for the fight at the end of their annual rivalry game and a prosecutor is considering whether further action is warranted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been three days since the final buzzer sounded on the Xavier-Cincinnati men’s basketball game, but it is clear the reverberations are far from over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Xavier-Cincinnati Brawl Could Bring Criminal Charges', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Enquirer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Cincinnati', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60c59bdd-4618-52f5-8bd3-c105722a37e8', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60c59bdd-4618-52f5-8bd3-c105722a37e8'}, {'abstract': 'Midtown Manhattan is famously overpriced. But it doesn’t have to be.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/can-it-be-done-midtown-on-a-budget/', 'snippet': 'Midtown Manhattan is famously overpriced. But it doesn’t have to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best way to save money in Midtown is to spend more time downtown — advice many a New Yorker has foisted upon visiting friends. But I spend enough time in other people’s cities to know that certain zones get tagged as tourist traps for a reason: they have attractions worth seeing. Such is the case in the heart of Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can It Be Done? Midtown on a Budget', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca141445-e9bd-5a4d-99bf-a8118e1d64cb', 'word_count': 1570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca141445-e9bd-5a4d-99bf-a8118e1d64cb'}, {'abstract': 'Talking with Tom Rothman of Fox Filmed Entertainment about his studio’s Oscar hopefuls.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/the-bold-and-the-hopeful-at-fox/', 'snippet': 'Talking with Tom Rothman of Fox Filmed Entertainment about his studio’s Oscar hopefuls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far it’s a fairly good season for Fox Filmed Entertainment. The studio and its subsidiary Fox Searchlight have released “The Descendants” and “The Tree of Life,” as well as “Martha Marcy May Marlene” and “Shame,” which are earning their stars, Elizabeth Olsen and Michael Fassbender, all the right attention. (Each received a Critics Choice nomination on Tuesday). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bold and the Hopeful at Fox', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T18:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53805fc4-6690-5ef4-bfb3-404473931caa', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538