: 'nyt://slideshow/d81c3605-a7cd-5a7f-83b6-b013aba6f0ac'}, {'abstract': 'Vera Wang cited Jane Birkin and YSL as inspirations for her prefall collection, with both icons’ interpretations of boy/girl sexiness being represented equally.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/just-one-look-vera-wang/', 'snippet': 'Vera Wang cited Jane Birkin and YSL as inspirations for her prefall collection, with both icons’ interpretations of boy/girl sexiness being represented equally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vera Wang cited Jane Birkin and YSL as inspirations for her prefall collection, with both icons’ interpretations of boy/girl sexiness being represented equally. Here, a perfect blend of the two: Birkinesque schoolgirl socks and a Saint Laurent-like bolero paired with a felted chiffon mini and the collection’s most seasonally appropriate accessory, the detachable leather sleeve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Vera Wang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T19:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf8454a-3ffc-5496-9a29-fd90e9bae73e', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf8454a-3ffc-5496-9a29-fd90e9bae73e'}, {'abstract': 'The National Transportation Safety Board said that states should ban all driver use of cellphones and other portable electronic devices, except in emergencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/technology/federal-panel-urges-cellphone-ban-for-drivers.html', 'snippet': 'The National Transportation Safety Board said that states should ban all driver use of cellphones and other portable electronic devices, except in emergencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal agency on Tuesday called for a ban on all cellphone use by drivers — the most far-reaching such recommendation to date — saying its decision was based on a decade of investigations into distraction-related accidents, as well as growing concerns that powerful mobile devices are giving drivers even more reasons to look away from the road.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-DISTRACTED-1/jp-DISTRACTED-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-DISTRACTED-1/jp-DISTRACTED-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-DISTRACTED-1/jp-DISTRACTED-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-DISTRACTED-1/jp-DISTRACTED-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-DISTRACTED-1/jp-DISTRACTED-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Safety Board Urges Cellphone Ban for Drivers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ban On Cell Use By Drivers Urged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T19:13:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Richtel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richtel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dee0d5c9-9f6f-509b-9821-3fc72a55f717', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dee0d5c9-9f6f-509b-9821-3fc72a55f717'}, {'abstract': 'As American forces withdraw from Iraq, we asked Iraqis questions about the war and their country’s future. We start in Baghdad.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/what-iraqis-think-of-the-american-withdrawal-baghdad/', 'snippet': 'As American forces withdraw from Iraq, we asked Iraqis questions about the war and their country’s future. We start in Baghdad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — As American forces start to pull out of Iraq, we asked Iraqis around the country three questions: Will Iraq be better or worse off after American troops leave? What did the Americans achieve in Iraq? And what have they personally lost or gained since the 2003 invasion? Some answered only one or two questions. Although the respondents varied from area to area and across social and religions divides, some clear patterns emerge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Iraqis Think of the American Withdrawal: Baghdad', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj