: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/health/nutrition/curried-cauliflower-soup-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'The deep, spicy flavors of this comforting soup belie how quickly it comes together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It will take you only about 10 minutes to prep the ingredients for this comforting soup. Curry flavors and cauliflower always make a good match.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/science/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Curried Cauliflower Soup', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T19:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ac7e40-8b67-526c-96d2-0e1e74179f81', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ac7e40-8b67-526c-96d2-0e1e74179f81'}, {'abstract': 'Justin Souriau-Levine, an 11-year old, plays the Little Mouse in American Ballet Theater’s production of “The Nutcracker.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/nutrcracker-season-is-here-an-interview-with-american-ballet-theaters-little-mouse/', 'snippet': 'Justin Souriau-Levine, an 11-year old, plays the Little Mouse in American Ballet Theater’s production of “The Nutcracker.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you saw American Ballet Theater’s new production of “The Nutcracker” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music last year, odds are you remember the mouse. Yes, there was new choreography by Alexei Ratmansky, snowflakes and bumblebees, and beautiful dancing by Gillian Murphy, David Hallberg and others. Alastair Macaulay called it, “a production like no other. Made with complete theatrical authority from first to last.” Even so, it was hard to forget the little “Ratatouille”-like creature, scurrying around the stage in Act I with great conviction– he nearly stole the show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Nutcracker’ Season is Here: An Interview With American Ballet Theater’s Little Mouse', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T19:22:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8655a46-5afe-5a54-8972-c4f238d9ace2', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8655a46-5afe-5a54-8972-c4f238d9ace2'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve said that it would take no new steps to boost economic growth this year, citing mounting evidence that the American economy is chugging slowly toward good health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/business/economy/fed-says-economy-is-expanding-moderately.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve said that it would take no new steps to boost economic growth this year, citing mounting evidence that the American economy is chugging slowly toward good health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve said Tuesday that it was closing the books on 2011, maintaining its existing efforts to increase growth but adding no reinforcement amid evidence that the American economy was chugging back toward health.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/business/FED/FED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Takes No Action, Citing Signs of Moderate Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Makes No Changes To Policy On Rates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T19:25:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de662560-b0e4-5923-972a-3d2f58137c45', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de662560-b0e4-5923-972a-3d2f58137c45'}, {'abstract': 'The return of the bug-eating, cow-blood-bobbing game show was good news for NBC Monday night. The ratings for Chelsea Clinton on the network’s newsmagazine weren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/fear-factor-returns-and-makes-a-ratings-splash/', 'snippet': 'The return of the bug-eating, cow-blood-bobbing game show was good news for NBC Monday night. The ratings for Chelsea Clinton on the network’s newsmagazine weren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How much do television viewers like being grossed out? Well, the last time NBC pulled in better ratings than “Fear Factor” at 8 p.m. Monday, George W.