 are no longer in charge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years after Myanmar inaugurated this new capital, Naypyidaw remains austere and often lifeless, a costly monument to military rulers who are no longer in charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/13/world/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/13/world/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/13/world/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw/video-tc-111213-naypyidaw-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "TimesCast | Inside Myanmar's Capital", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:14:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'Kassie Bracken', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kassie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bracken', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0aaa5760-94d0-573a-90f5-f96426863fd8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0aaa5760-94d0-573a-90f5-f96426863fd8'}, {'abstract': 'Christiane Amanpour, who left CNN to anchor ABC’s Sunday morning show, will return to CNN to anchor the evening news on CNN International.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/amanpour-said-to-be-leaving-this-week/', 'snippet': 'Christiane Amanpour, who left CNN to anchor ABC’s Sunday morning show, will return to CNN to anchor the evening news on CNN International.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:15 p.m. | Updated Christiane Amanpour is leaving the anchor chair of ABC’s “This Week” and returning to her old network home, CNN, as the anchor of an evening newscast on CNN International.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amanpour to Leave ABC’s ‘This Week’ and Rejoin CNN', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMANPOUR, CHRISTIANE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb7bb86-c451-51db-86ca-f878b5eeace2', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb7bb86-c451-51db-86ca-f878b5eeace2'}, {'abstract': 'Beloufa, a young French Algerian video artist based in Paris, works in the interstices of fact and fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/out-there-neil-beloufas-brave-new-world/', 'snippet': 'Beloufa, a young French Algerian video artist based in Paris, works in the interstices of fact and fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many artists responding to our duplicitous marketing- and infotainment-driven world, Neïl Beloufa, a young French Algerian video artist based in Paris, works in the interstices of fact and fiction. In “Kempinski (2007),” which was on view last year at the New Museum, Beloufa uses a simple tweak in tense to build an eerie alternate reality. Shot at night in Mali, “Kempinski” features interviews with local inhabitants in rural settings — in a crowd of oxen, in bushes, in dusty courtyards — who speak about things from telepathic communication with stars, animals and machines to teleportation via light and sound, as if they were present-day realities. The scenes are lit by handheld, corded fluorescent lights that could, if you squint, be mistaken for alien technology, and the subjects’ assertions register as farcical deadpan: Beloufa’s tone of choice. The narration plays on a viewer’s superficial ideas of where primitive magic and futuristic science might meet, hinging on that rhetorical switch from “will be” to “is.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | Neïl Beloufa’s Brave New World', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c317ad64-bbe9-5c6e-bf10-553287c162b8', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c317ad64-bbe9-5c6e-bf10-553287c162b8'}, {'abstract': 'What do we need to do to elevate the school performance of poor children?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/should-we-occupy-education/', 'snippet': 'What do we need to do to elevate the school performance of poor children?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dramatic disparities separate the performance of privileged and disadvantaged students, and as complex as the education equation is, one factor — poverty — is consistently associated with lower scores for districts, schools and individual children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We ‘Occupy’ Education?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc955412-9d14-5f57-8afe-38d8a322c3ca', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc955412-9d14-5f57-8afe-38d8a322c3ca'}, {'abstract': 'James Murdoch knew about the legal ramifications from widespread phone hacking at a British tabloid long before he has admitted he knew, according to e-mail messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/europe/2008-e-mail-alerted-james-murdoch-to-hacking.html', 'snippet': 'James Murdoch knew about the legal ramifications from widespread phone hacking at a British tabloid long before he has admitted he knew, according to e-mail messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Rupert Murdoch’s son James received and responded to e-mail messages in 2008 that referred to “a nightmare scenario” of legal repercussions from widespread phone hacking at the tabloid The News of the World, a chain of e-mail messages and replies released Tuesday by a British parliamentary panel shows. It is the first documentation that Mr. Murdoch had been notified of a wider hacking problem long before he has admitted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 801, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/world/HACKING-1/HACKING-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Challenge to a Murdoch Over Hacking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murdoch Son Is Challenged Over Hacking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb24a517-79fc-5b00-8702-78b2020a602c', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb24a517-79fc-5b00-8702-78b2020a602c'}, {'abstract': 'When Kathleen Sebelius overruled the F.D.A. on Plan B, she put politics over science. Now 14 Senators are demanding that she justify her decision.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/politics-beats-science-again/', 'snippet': 'When Kathleen Sebelius overruled the F.D.A. on Plan B, she put politics over science. Now 14 Senators are demanding that she justify her decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a scene you may find familiar: Government experts carefully study a problem, and come to a conclusion based on scientific evidence. They get over-ruled by bureaucrats who seem more concerned about politics than science. This isn’t a historical anecdote from the Bush administration. I’m talking about the Obama administration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics Beats Science, Again', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plan B (Contraceptive)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c72b21-ca50-5262-abce-df77ddf9b457', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c72b21-ca50-5262-abce-df77ddf9b457'}, {'abstract': 'NBC was rewarded for its decision to bring back its gross-out reality competition. HBO, meanwhile, attracted three million viewers to the “Boardwalk Empire” season finale on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/fear-factor-on-nbc-draws-big-audience-in-return/', 'snippet': 'NBC was rewarded for its decision to bring back its gross-out reality competition. HBO, meanwhile, attracted three million viewers to the “Boardwalk Empire” season finale on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a five-year hiatus, NBC’s gross-out competition “Fear Factor” delivered strong numbers for over a two-hour period with an average of 8.6 million total viewers. It also matched the highest 8 p.m. rating in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic for a non-sports program on NBC since February 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fear Factor’ on NBC Draws Big Audience in Return', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Chelsea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20b3cf8e-7ef2-5b61-955e-f7475c25704a', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20b3cf8e-7ef2-5b61-955e-f7475c25704a'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of awards-related news including a date change for “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/dragon-tattoos-new-date-and-other-news-from-the-circuit/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of awards-related news including a date change for “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news today in awards land is all about anticipation. Fans of “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo” – or anybody looking to see whether Denbygate was merited or not – get to scratch their itch sooner: Sony announced on Tuesday — via Twitter — that the film will now open a day earlier, with tickets available to showings beginning at 7 p.m. on Dec. 20. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dragon Tattoo’s’ New Date and Other News From the Circuit', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d8b4d4a-a1fa-5d36-8df3-62bf0222a442', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d8b4d4a-a1fa-5d36-8df3-62bf0222a442'}, {'abstract': 'Considering the Crystal Cox case and creating primers for teenagers about First Amendment rights and limitations on those freedoms.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/freedom-of-expression-online-outlining-the-first-amendment-for-teenagers/', 'snippet': 'Considering the Crystal Cox case and creating primers for teenagers about First Amendment rights and limitations on those freedoms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What are the First Amendment rights? Does freedom of speech mean you people can publish whatever they want on the Internet? In this lesson, students consider what they know about the First Amendment and a court case involving a blogger. They then research the rights and responsibilities of young bloggers and create a primer for teens who blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freedom of Expression, Online: Outlining the First Amendment for Teenagers', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T20:33:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kavanagh and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/580a1eb1-3b7e-5710-961a-2f42bf9029ee', 'word_count': 1542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/580a1eb1-3b7e-5710-961a-2f42bf9029ee'}, {'abstract': 'Wolfgang Ban and Eduard Frauneder, who opened Seäsonal in Manhattan a couple of years ago as both a restaurant and a wine bar, take Austrian favorites on a culinary journey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/dining/seasonal-nyc-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'Wolfgang Ban and Eduard Frauneder, who opened Seäsonal in Manhattan a couple of years ago as both a restaurant and a wine bar, take Austrian favorites on a culinary journey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I AM not one to sneer at the manifest pleasures of a Wiener schnitzel. I have friends, however, who are not nearly so accepting of these simple joys. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14REST_SPAN/14REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14REST_SPAN/14REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,