r dietary needs?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Koshering of the White House', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/488684b8-cacc-5272-ba8e-e05810736eec', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/488684b8-cacc-5272-ba8e-e05810736eec'}, {'abstract': 'Research is under way in Antarctica to study ecological connectivity among streams, lakes, glaciers, soils and weather.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/extreme-ecology-in-a-polar-desert/', 'snippet': 'Research is under way in Antarctica to study ecological connectivity among streams, lakes, glaciers, soils and weather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alia Khan, a graduate student at the University of Colorado, Boulder, writes from the McMurdo Dry Valleys in Antarctica, where she is studying ephemeral glacier fed streams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extreme Ecology in a Polar Desert', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:37:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alia Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b44e9994-f496-579e-a185-a719051c98d4', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b44e9994-f496-579e-a185-a719051c98d4'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs illustrating the persistence of the refrain introduced by the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/we-are-the-99-percent-as-told-in-pictures/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs illustrating the persistence of the refrain introduced by the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as many of the Occupy [Your City/Street Here] encampments around the country have been expelled by local police forces, one of its central refrains — “We Are the 99 Percent” — has become part of the national dialogue. The National Desk invited readers to submit pictures incorporating the phrase and produced a slide show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Are the 99 Percent’ as Told in Pictures', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e55bec2c-e062-55bd-9bdd-355472ef5325', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e55bec2c-e062-55bd-9bdd-355472ef5325'}, {'abstract': 'Junior Flores, 15, was the star of the U.S. under-17 national team in a recent series of friendly matches in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/junior-flores-shines-for-u-s-u-17-team/', 'snippet': 'Junior Flores, 15, was the star of the U.S. under-17 national team in a recent series of friendly matches in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month at the Nike International Friendlies in Florida, the United States under-17 national team drew a lot of attention as it defeated Brazil and Turkey on the way to winning the tournament.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Junior Flores Shines for U.S. U-17 Team', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:46:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sciaretta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciaretta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9ef8a9-dfd6-5481-a539-d367dd6a6676', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9ef8a9-dfd6-5481-a539-d367dd6a6676'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s celebrate the losers of presidential elections who transformed political history in the United States — often more deeply than the men they lost to.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/its-almost-presidents-day/', 'snippet': 'Let’s celebrate the losers of presidential elections who transformed political history in the United States — often more deeply than the men they lost to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eleven years ago today, Al Gore, for one important moment, was the most powerful man in our republic. The day before, the Supreme Court, in a 5-4 vote, halted the partial recount of presidential ballots in Florida that Gore had requested. But that did not mean the 2000 presidential election was over. George W. Bush could not declare victory until Gore conceded defeat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Almost-Presidents’ Day!', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2000', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, Adlai Ewing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Farris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bfc96ab-a1dc-50d4-a24b-16d03b43c6f8', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bfc96ab-a1dc-50d4-a24b-16d03b43c6f8'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Trump won’t be hosting a debate in Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/the-on-again-off-again-donald/', 'snippet': 'Donald Trump won’t be hosting a debate in Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump has announced that he will not, after all, be moderating a debate in Iowa for the Republican presidential candidates with the right-wing magazine Newsmax. He says the party wanted him to promise he wouldn’t run as an independent, and he wants to preserve that possibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The On Again, Off Again Donald', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b008b32f-2801-5a0a-b67e-38345185821a', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b008b32f-2801-5a0a-b67e-38345185821a'}, {'abstract': 'Shares in JPMorgan tumbled after the trustee liquidating MF Global’s brokerage unit affirmed that he might investigate the bank for its actions as the firm collapsed.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/jpmorgan-shares-fall-as-mf-global-trustee-suggests-inquiry/', 'snippet': 'Shares in JPMorgan tumbled after the trustee liquidating MF Global’s brokerage unit affirmed that he might investigate the bank for its actions as the firm collapsed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a couple of ups and downs, shares in JPMorgan Chase were trading in positive territory by Tuesday afternoon. And then they took a quick and sharp tumble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Shares Fall as MF Global Trustee Suggests Inquiry of Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'