ifornia-revenue-shortfall-to-force-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown said the state was about $2.2 billion short of its projected income, which will lead to additional cuts in higher education and health care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The California Legislature passed a budget in June relying on optimistic projections of how much money the state could bring in with a growing economy. But to the surprise of few, not all of that money has materialized.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-CALIFORNIA-2/jp-CALIFORNIA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-CALIFORNIA-2/jp-CALIFORNIA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/us/jp-CALIFORNIA-2/jp-CALIFORNIA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California, With Revenue Shortfalls, Will See More Budget Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California, With Revenue Shortfalls, Will See More Budget Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T21:57:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa96f65-9a7e-5584-af67-8ff590579d00', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa96f65-9a7e-5584-af67-8ff590579d00'}, {'abstract': 'Spider webs, beetles, cicadas and other creepy crawlers inspired Helmut Lang’s designers this prefall season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/just-one-look-helmut-lang/', 'snippet': 'Spider webs, beetles, cicadas and other creepy crawlers inspired Helmut Lang’s designers this prefall season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spider webs, beetles, cicadas and other creepy crawlers inspired Helmut Lang’s Nicole and Michael Colovos this prefall season. In between quintessential Helmut Lang pieces — leather leggings and biker jackets, open-weave linen shirts and asymmetrical jersey tops and dresses — are collection-defining prints based on insects’ exoskeletal-esque wings and amphibious camouflages, as seen on this extremely graphic and sporty chiffon dress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Helmut Lang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, Helmut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7a5e37e-2d8e-503a-bb47-24b176a91bf7', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7a5e37e-2d8e-503a-bb47-24b176a91bf7'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Rhodes’s new book, “Hedy’s Folly,” traces how the glamorous actress Hedy Lamarr and the avant-garde composer George Antheil came to devise a remote-controlled torpedo during World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/books/hedys-folly-by-richard-rhodes-review.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Rhodes’s new book, “Hedy’s Folly,” traces how the glamorous actress Hedy Lamarr and the avant-garde composer George Antheil came to devise a remote-controlled torpedo during World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you hear the one about the actress and the composer who tried to invent a remote-controlled torpedo? It sounds like the opening line of a bar joke, but it’s actually the premise of Richard Rhodes’s slim new book, “Hedy’s Folly.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/jump-book-2/jump-book-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/jump-book-2/jump-book-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/jump-book-2/jump-book-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/jump-book-2/jump-book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/jump-book-2/jump-book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Glamour and Munitions: A Screen Siren’s Wartime Ingenuity', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Glamour and Munitions: A Screen Siren’s Wartime Ingenuity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHEIL, GEORGE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhodes, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamarr, Hedy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fefd623d-f81f-5408-be8e-a75f116c594d', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fefd623d-f81f-5408-be8e-a75f116c594d'}, {'abstract': 'Third Point’s chief, Daniel Loeb, forcefully reiterated his opposition to any plan by Yahoo to sell a minority stake in itself instead of pursuing an outright sale of the Internet company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/loeb-reiterates-opposition-to-a-yahoo-minority-investment/', 'snippet': 'Third Point’s chief, Daniel Loeb, forcefully reiterated his opposition to any plan by Yahoo to sell a minority stake in itself instead of pursuing an outright sale of the Internet company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Yahoo‘s board continues to ponder its next strategic steps, one of its biggest shareholders would like to remind directors that he’s opposed to including any plan to sell a big minority stake to an outside investor consortium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loeb Reiterates Opposition to a Yahoo Minority Investment', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c4d3dfd-030d-52f9-8af2-a9d80eb3319c', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c4d3dfd-030d-52f9-8af2-a9d80eb3319c'}, {'abstract': 'A survey from the National Federation of Independent Business indicates increased optimism.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/small-businesses-plan-to-increase-hiring/', 'snippet': 'A survey from the National Federation of Independent Business indicates increased optimism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our colleagues at the Economix blog have have just published a post about a new National Federation of Independent Business survey indicating that the net share of companies planning to hire workers is at its highest point in 38 months. In fact, the net percentage of companies that say they have already increased their employment in the last three months — that is, the percent saying they increased their staff minus the percent saying they decreased it — was positive for the first time in nearly four years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Businesses Plan to Increase Hiring', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Federation of Independent Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/972fc6db-2868-5ba5-a0b1-02856d7f4c84', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/972fc6db-2868-5ba5-a0b1-02856d7f4c84'}, {'abstract': 'Staged presentation of “Tuck Everlasting” raises hopes for Broadway production', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/tuck-everlasting-musical-sets-sights-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Staged presentation of “Tuck Everlasting” raises hopes for Broadway production', 'lead_paragraph': 'A musical adaptation of the 1975 children’s novel “Tuck Everlasting” is aiming for Broadway next season with the Tony Award winner Casey Nicholaw (“The Book of Mormon”) as director, according to theater executives who attended staged presentations of the show for producers and investors on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Tuck Everlasting’ Musical Sets Sights on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicholaw, Casey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shear, Claudia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a943017-e344-5e9c-9c29-9a8625033a6e', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a943017-e344-5e9c-9c29-9a8625033a6e'}, {'abstract': 'The European division of General Motors said it would not sell the Ampera, the European equivalent of the Volt, until a resolution was reached in the federal fire investigation that began in November.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/investigation-of-chevy-volt-prompts-opel-to-delay-sales-of-ampera/', 'snippet': 'The European division of General Motors said it would not sell the Ampera, the European equivalent of the Volt, until a resolution was reached in the federal fire investigation that began in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Opel Ampera, Europe’s version of the Chevrolet Volt, will sit in showrooms pending resolution by American investigators of a battery fire question related to crash tests of the Volt, according to Andrew Marshall, director of product development communications at Opel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigation of Chevy Volt Prompts Opel to Delay Sales of Ampera', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opel, Adam, AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T22:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary M. Chapman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d27879e-68bb-575e-80ca-663faf5b0b63', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d27879e-68bb-575e-80ca-663faf5b0b63'}, {'abstract': 'What used to be food for Jewish grandfathers is showing up on the menus of restaurants both hip and elegant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/dining/the-little-herring-gets-a-big-role.html', 'snippet': 'What used to be food for Jewish grandfathers is showing up on the menus of restaurants both hip and elegant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a fancy women’s department store in Osaka, Japan, earlier this year, shoppers lined up for one of the latest food fads in the country, jars of pickled herring. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14HERRING_SPAN/14HERRING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14HERRING_SPAN/14HERRING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14HERRING_SPAN/14HERRING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image