he new Yeatman Hotel, an 82-room resort and spa that takes the idea of a wine hotel (see also the Hotel Marques de Riscal) to new heights. Certainly it’s easy to get that impression after a visit to the hotel’s cork and wine museum or after a stay in suites sponsored and decorated by various Portuguese wineries. The Fladgate master suite ($430 per night) features a 50,000-liter port barrel repurposed as a king-size bed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | The Yeatman, Portugal', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T23:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64c116d9-160b-5636-8db5-270f639a2335', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64c116d9-160b-5636-8db5-270f639a2335'}, {'abstract': 'California is stepping up its crusade against cybercriminals. On Tuesday, Kamala D. Harris, California’s attorney general, announced the creation of the nation’s largest e-crime unit, a team of 20 investigators and prosecutors whose sole mission will be to thwart and prosecute cybercrimes like identity theft, Internet scams, computer theft, online child pornography and intellectual property theft across the state.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/california-creates-special-unit-to-fight-computer-crimes/', 'snippet': 'California is stepping up its crusade against cybercriminals. On Tuesday, Kamala D. Harris, California’s attorney general, announced the creation of the nation’s largest e-crime unit, a team of 20 investigators and prosecutors whose sole mission w...', 'lead_paragraph': 'California has long led the nation in technological innovation. A lesser-known fact: It also leads the country in cybercrime.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Creates Special Unit to Fight Computer Crimes', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Unit to Fight Cybercrimes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T23:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f04f128-14c5-5742-8e89-34677d970b7d', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f04f128-14c5-5742-8e89-34677d970b7d'}, {'abstract': 'Eating Mexican food in a basement sporting Vietnamese signs on an alleyway in Chinatown is part of the worldly appeal of Pulqueria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/dining/dining-briefs-pulqueria.html', 'snippet': 'Eating Mexican food in a basement sporting Vietnamese signs on an alleyway in Chinatown is part of the worldly appeal of Pulqueria.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 Doyers Street (Bowery), ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/dining/14BRIEF2_SPAN/14BRIEF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlar