Latin American countries, Apple now operates iTunes  in 51 countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple quietly announced on Tuesday that it had opened its iTunes store in Brazil and 15 other countries in Latin America, including Argentina, Venezuela, Chile, Colombia, Nicaragua and Peru. Apple now operates the iTunes music store in 51 countries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ITunes Opens in Latin America, Challenging Rival Services', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T23:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ded33894-3009-50cf-902f-4dcf2eb17a8a', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ded33894-3009-50cf-902f-4dcf2eb17a8a'}, {'abstract': 'A Mexican pub in Chinatown.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/reviewing-pulqueria/', 'snippet': 'A Mexican pub in Chinatown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pulqueria , one of this week’s Dining Briefs, is the latest venture by Heather and Christopher Tierney, the siblings behind Apothéke. The restaurant and bar is the city’s first to focus on pulque, the fermented agave sap that Mexicans have been drinking since pre-Columbian times, here mixed with fresh juices and smoky mezcal. A lively crowd dines on chef Nacxitl Gaxiola’s friendly, mildly authentic accompaniments: masa gorditos and empanadas, savory little tacos, selections of salsas from throughout Mexico, and larger, more robust plates like pork shank confit. Some of the dishes are a bit too tame, but there’s also a lot of interest. The Yucatecan pumpkin seed spread, sikil pak, and the tuna tostadas are real winners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Pulqueria', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-13T23:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betsy Andrews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betsy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4f5931e-e19d-51b8-bfe5-71ee47122c6a', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4f5931e-e19d-51b8-bfe5-71ee47122c6a'}, {'abstract': 'An all-male dance is the latest from the choreographer Tere O’Connor, at Danspace Project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/arts/dance/tere-oconnors-cover-boy-review.html', 'snippet': 'An all-male dance is the latest from the choreographer Tere O’Connor, at Danspace Project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tere O’Connor’s new dance is an all-male affair. It is performed by four men, features only one woman among its collaborators and even has the title “Cover Boy.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/OCONNOR/OCONNOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/arts/OCONNOR/OCONNOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth':