 for electricity generators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/nyregion/4-8-million-sought-from-morgan-stanley-in-electricity-price-fixing-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department, using the Sherman Antitrust Act, wants Morgan Stanley to settle a case in which it acted as an intermediary for electricity generators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — An electricity price-fixing scandal thought to have cost New York consumers about $300 million has led to a proposed settlement with Morgan Stanley for $4.8 million. But the proposal has brought complaints from a consumer group, which points out that the company took in four times that much in the scheme. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$4.8 Million Sought From Morgan Stanley in Price-Fixing Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$4.8 Million Sought in a Price-Fixing Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Astoria Generating Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T02:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4609a06f-01e9-59cd-95fc-cd8654c00f3a', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4609a06f-01e9-59cd-95fc-cd8654c00f3a'}, {'abstract': 'An imminent trade decision might determine the fate of that smartphone you ordered for the holidays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/opinion/patents-smartphones-and-the-public-interest.html', 'snippet': 'An imminent trade decision might determine the fate of that smartphone you ordered for the holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next week, in a case closely watched both by analysts and retailers, the International Trade Commission will decide whether the handset maker HTC should be allowed to import its products into the United States. The controversy? A claim by Apple that HTC infringed on two of the estimated 250,000 patents covering smartphone technology. If the commission agrees, it is likely to issue an “exclusion order,” which would in effect say “keep out” (of the United States) to HTC’s Android phones during the Christmas season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patents and the Public Interest', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patents and the Public Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HTC Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States International Trade Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T02:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', '