ng and revenue-raising measures in his new budget.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/europe/mario-monti-revises-italian-budget-measures.html', 'snippet': 'In response to complaints from lawmakers and unions, Prime Minister Mario Monti adjusted cost-cutting and revenue-raising measures in his new budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Prime Minister Mario Monti on Tuesday announced changes to a pension overhaul and reintroduced a property tax to gain parliamentary support for a budget that he hopes will calm world markets and rein in Italy’s public debt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Leader Revises Plans for Austerity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Leader Revises Plans For Austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/765a14c7-1b00-5596-b81e-a153c0c8ad06', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/765a14c7-1b00-5596-b81e-a153c0c8ad06'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans have tried to insert scores of policy riders in the 2012 spending bill to pursue ideological goals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/opinion/the-insidious-fine-print-in-the-spending-bill.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have tried to insert scores of policy riders in the 2012 spending bill to pursue ideological goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looks like a small throwaway line in a 2012 spending bill: no federal funds may be used to carry out chapters 95 or 96 of the Internal Revenue Code. A little digging shows that those chapters happen to authorize the presidential election public financing system. A few House Republicans, who have long hated the system, thought they could get rid of it by inserting the line in a bill to keep the government from shutting down this weekend.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Insidious Fine Print', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Insidious Fine Print', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4feb85b-af01-5098-9fa9-57de4f3a7fa5', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4feb85b-af01-5098-9fa9-57de4f3a7fa5'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should reassert federal control of immigration in the Arizona case and stop states from taking immigration policy into their own hands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/opinion/stopping-the-free-for-all-in-immigration-laws.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should reassert federal control of immigration in the Arizona case and stop states from taking immigration policy into their own hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s decision to review a federal court ruling blocking parts of Arizona’s notorious immigration law is troubling. It is arguably premature to take this case because there is no split among the federal appellate courts over states’ powers to enact such laws. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stopping the Free-for-All', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stopping the Free-for-All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, Susan Ritchie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/493e9a6e-402d-50d6-8b10-a23d3bb00749', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/493e9a6e-402d-50d6-8b10-a23d3bb00749'}, {'abstract': 'The Englishman Luke Donald, who last week locked up the money title on the European Tour, had 14 top-10 finishes on the PGA Tour but faltered in the season’s four major tournaments.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/13/donald-is-seeking-validation-in-winning-majors-not-money/', 'snippet': 'The Englishman Luke Donald, who last week locked up the money title on the European Tour, had 14 top-10 finishes on the PGA Tour but faltered in the season’s four major tournaments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Englishman Luke Donald cemented his place in golf history last weekend by becoming the first player to win the money titles on the European and PGA Tours. In a teleconference call with reporters Tuesday, Donald sounded as if he would trade that coup for the one feat that eluded him during a sparkling season that culminated in his winning the PGA Tour player of the year in a vote of his peers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Is Seeking Validation in Winning Majors, Not Money', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Keegan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donald, Luke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13a70858-d9e9-550a-a748-87aed17de698', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13a70858-d9e9-550a-a748-87aed17de698'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Donald Berwick makes a compelling case about the harm caused by partisan demagoguery and about the need for health care professionals to accelerate reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/opinion/advice-from-dr-berwick-a-health-care-visionary.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Donald Berwick makes a compelling case about the harm caused by partisan demagoguery and about the need for health care professionals to accelerate reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Donald Berwick, who was blocked by Republicans from serving a full term as the administrator of the agency that runs Medicare and Medicaid, has been speaking out. He makes a compelling case about the harm caused by partisan demagoguery and about the need for health care professionals to take the lead in implementing reforms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Candid Advice From a Health Care Visionary', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Candid Advice From a Health Care Visionary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berwick, Donald M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/33b160c9-1bfa-5f64-ab6c-d5d244d41360', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33b160c9-1bfa-5f64-ab6c-d5d244d41360'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo should sign the bill now that allow livery cabs to pick up passengers legally in the outer boroughs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/opinion/a-cab-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo should sign the bill now that allow livery cabs to pick up passengers legally in the outer boroughs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any seasoned New Yorker knows, it’s almost impossible to find a yellow cab outside the heart of Manhattan. Instead, livery cars cruise the streets of the outer boroughs and pick up passengers illegally. They haggle over rates, deal in cash and nobody knows whether the city sees any of this money as tax revenue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cab in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cab in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T03:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d05960c3-c776-50cf-88d3-d6fe4fcb6313', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d05960c3-c776-50cf-88d3-d6fe4fcb6313'}, {'abstract': 'The deaths added to a toll that was estimated by a United Nations official at more than 5,000 people since the uprising began in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/world/middleeast/more-than-30-are-killed-across-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The deaths added to a toll that was estimated by a United Nations official at more than 5,000 people since the uprising began in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — At least 32 people were killed across Syria on Tuesday, including seven members of the security forces, amid rising sectarian tensions in some places, opposition groups said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than 30 Are Killed Across Syria as Sectarian Tensions Grow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than 30 Are Killed Across Syria as Sectarian Tensions Grow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 