firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/437d4d45-90aa-5259-8320-5b355ffddc4d', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/437d4d45-90aa-5259-8320-5b355ffddc4d'}, {'abstract': 'A study by Good Jobs First, scheduled to be released Wednesday, shows many states lack safeguards to ensure the money they give to companies creates long-lasting, well-paying jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/us/study-finds-failings-in-some-state-economic-programs.html', 'snippet': 'A study by Good Jobs First, scheduled to be released Wednesday, shows many states lack safeguards to ensure the money they give to companies creates long-lasting, well-paying jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the unemployment crisis grinds on, states are trying to both lure and retain businesses by offering tax breaks, grants, cheap loans — just about anything (short of candy and foot massages) they can think of. But how many jobs do these expensive incentives actually create? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With States Desperate to Keep Jobs, Companies Have Upper Hand, Report Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With States Desperate to Keep Jobs, Companies Have Upper Hand, Report Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'm