ion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T05:34:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b4360d-80b1-5a6e-9c07-e27278f02475', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b4360d-80b1-5a6e-9c07-e27278f02475'}, {'abstract': 'When English Premier League frontrunners Manchester United and Manchester City crashed out of the 2011-12 Champions League last week, they were sent to Europe’s second-tier competition.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/europa-league-preview-yanks-still-in-the-hunt/', 'snippet': 'When English Premier League frontrunners Manchester United and Manchester City crashed out of the 2011-12 Champions League last week, they were sent to Europe’s second-tier competition.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:16 a.m. | Updated When English Premier League frontrunners Manchester United and Manchester City crashed out of the 2011-12 Champions League last week, they didn’t exactly get sent home. No, they were sent to Europe’s second-tier competition, the league formerly known as UEFA and currently called Europa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europa League Preview: Yanks Still in the Hunt', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T05:45:22+0000',