 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13ea5f05-f9dc-59bb-b115-cb1ba7a89c23'}, {'abstract': 'Boris V. Gryzlov, the chairman of Russia’s governing party, United Russia, resigned as speaker of the Duma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/europe/putin-ally-boris-gryzlov-resigns-as-speaker-of-russia-parliament.html', 'snippet': 'Boris V. Gryzlov, the chairman of Russia’s governing party, United Russia, resigned as speaker of the Duma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The chairman of Russia’s governing party, United Russia, resigned from his post as speaker of the lower house of Parliament on Wednesday in an apparent effort to quell some of the uproar over perceived fraud in parliamentary elections last week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/14russia-image-1323863347254/14russia-image-1323863347254-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/14russia-image-1323863347254/14russia-image-1323863347254-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/world/14russia-image-1323863347254/14russia-image-1323863347254-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin Ally Resigns Speaker’s Post Amid Vote Furor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parliament Speaker, Ally of Putin, Resigns From Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gryzlov, Boris V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T11:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3c5e13-2714-5ecc-8210-03de1759cf75', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3c5e13-2714-5ecc-8210-03de1759cf75'}, {'abstract': 'I’m thrilled to be here — and I want to know what you think Motherlode should be, and what topics you want to see us cover.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/meet-the-new-motherlode-blogger/', 'snippet': 'I’m thrilled to be here — and I want to know what you think Motherlode should be, and what topics you want to see us cover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Motherlode? Hardly. It is you who I hope will welcome me. Although I’ve been a reader since the beginning (and occasionally a contributor), stepping into what I think of as the “big boots” of Motherlode is daunting and thrilling. As a writer and blogger, I’ve always thought of Motherlode as, well, the motherlode: the ultimate place to start or join a conversation about the way we raise children now. I’m very happy to be here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the New Motherlode Blogger', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d45569d0-397f-5d50-81c4-28617797e30c', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d45569d0-397f-5d50-81c4-28617797e30c'}, {'abstract': 'But what if there’s a third flood? “We would break our lease and say sayonara,” said one owner.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/despite-two-floods-a-business-decides-to-stay-put/', 'snippet': 'But what if there’s a third flood? “We would break our lease and say sayonara,” said one owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, we published a case study about\xa0two disaster-frazzled entrepreneurs seemingly in need of some of the calming supplemental holistic health services — yoga and massage — that they offer at Pulling Down the Moon, a Chicago business that was hit by two floods within a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite 2 Floods, a Business Decides to Stay Put', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pulling Down the Moon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago River', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':