 lending her celebrity clients editorial polish. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Laura Osnes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c9539d4-e7e1-538c-a12f-37e07e680ff5', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c9539d4-e7e1-538c-a12f-37e07e680ff5'}, {'abstract': 'Olympus avoided delisting by the Tokyo Stock Exchange by posting the more than $1 billion in losses at the center of a decades-long cover-up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/business/global/olympus-restates-earnings-showing-loss.html', 'snippet': 'Olympus avoided delisting by the Tokyo Stock Exchange by posting the more than $1 billion in losses at the center of a decades-long cover-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Hours before a critical deadline Wednesday, Olympus, Japan’s chastened camera maker, released revised financial results, owning up to more than $1 billion in losses it hid for more than a decade. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympus Restates Earnings, Showing Loss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympus Meets Deadline To Revise Its Earnings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodford, Michael C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Stock Exchange', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympus Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c57e1bc1-2fd6-5649-9b55-62916dc302af', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57e1bc1-2fd6-5649-9b55-62916dc302af'}, {'abstract': 'Liquidity trap rules.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/interest-rates-inflation-and-the-way-the-world-works-slightly-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Liquidity trap rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newish commenters here often fail to understand why I highlight things like falling inflation in Britain or the extremely low interest rates at which the governments of non-euro nations can borrow. Is it just I-told-you-so? No. It’s about economic models — how the world works. And of course such models have policy implications.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interest Rates, Inflation, and the Way the World Works (Slightly Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63d68dc8-0821-5ce0-9c89-ee71f9be72ef', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63d68dc8-0821-5ce0-9c89-ee71f9be72ef'}, {'abstract': 'Armed defectors from the Syrian military killed at least eight government troops on Wednesday in an ambush near the city of Hama, opposition groups said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/syrian-army-defectors-ambush-assad-security-force.html', 'snippet': 'Armed defectors from the Syrian military killed at least eight government troops on Wednesday in an ambush near the city of Hama, opposition groups said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian military defectors killed at least eight members of the security forces on Wednesday in an ambush near the city of Hama, in central Syria, according to opposition groups.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Army Defectors Ambush Soldiers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Army Defectors Ambush Soldiers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:21:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd58077-0018-51f0-afcd-c4ad11b4e272', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd58077-0018-51f0-afcd-c4ad11b4e272'}, {'abstract': 'The actors guild reveals its nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/actors-guild-unveils-its-nominations/', 'snippet': 'The actors guild reveals its nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The many critics groups have had their say, now the actors are weighing in with their picks for awards season. Nominations for the Screen Actors Guild Awards were unveiled this morning, with “The Artist,” “The Descendants,” “Bridesmaids” and “Midnight in Paris” all getting nods for outstanding cast performance. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Actors Guild Unveils Its Nominations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:42:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37bc8d06-015a-5604-989a-f2b05c8059c0', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37bc8d06-015a-5604-989a-f2b05c8059c0'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/what-were-reading-331/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SF Weekly: Hooters and San Francisco are breaking up. Somehow we knew it was never going to work out. — Jeff GordinierMSNBC: Smithfield says it will finally stop using confinement pens for its pregnant sows. — Nick Fox', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T14:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19af2d92-e8ce-5a86-9947-adb6d1ffbf24', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19af