: [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marijuana Use Growing Among Teenagers', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regular Marijuana Use by High School Students Hits New Peak, Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T15:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b055de9a-6524-534e-9e43-aedbcdb73de2', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b055de9a-6524-534e-9e43-aedbcdb73de2'}, {'abstract': 'Several of the banks that helped Groupon to go public are hesitant to click buy on the shares of the daily deals site, with six underwriters initiating coverage with neutral or hold ratings.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/groupons-stock-not-necessarily-a-deal/', 'snippet': 'Several of the banks that helped Groupon to go public are hesitant to click buy on the shares of the daily deals site, with six underwriters initiating coverage with neutral or hold ratings.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:17 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Groupon, Faint Praise From Its Underwriters', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T15:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb386392-d612-5378-991d-6f2189f4d28e', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb386392-d612-5378-991d-6f2189f4d28e'}, {'abstract': 'Jerry Sandusky could have waived his hearing long before his alleged victims had arrived at the courthouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/sports/in-sandusky-case-yet-another-sad-strange-turn.html', 'snippet': 'Jerry Sandusky could have waived his hearing long before his alleged victims had arrived at the courthouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the series of sorry spectacles that has been the Jerry Sandusky/Penn State child sexual abuse scandal, we add one of the sorriest yet. To call Tuesday’s preliminary hearing-that-wasn’t a circus would be insulting the actual circus. Under this metaphorical big top, Sandusky’s lawyer all but stood on top of a car with a bullhorn urging everyone to come attend his client’s hearing — including dragging in a set of alleged victims who had to skewer up the courage to testify in open court — and then waived the hearing after they’d all arrived.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Sandusky Case, Yet Another Sad, Strange Turn', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Sandusky Case, Yet Another Sad, Strange Turn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject',