6-5820-a829-d0fe3e55086f', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef3e863-39f6-5820-a829-d0fe3e55086f'}, {'abstract': 'New pop-up editions of “Puff the Magic Dragon,” “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory” and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/14/books/14popups.html', 'snippet': 'New pop-up editions of “Puff the Magic Dragon,” “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory” and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New pop-up editions of “Puff the Magic Dragon,” “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory” and others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14popups-slide-ME3L/14popups-slide-ME3L-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14popups-slide-ME3L/14popups-slide-ME3L-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14popups-slide-ME3L/14popups-slide-ME3L-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14popups-slide-ME3L/14popups-slide-ME3L-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14popups-slide-ME3L/14popups-slide-ME3L-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop-Up Book Roundup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Books', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ffec758f-5952-5feb-9477-2b935b2b255e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ffec758f-5952-5feb-9477-2b935b2b255e'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada may not be a pollster, but he has already decided who President Obama will be facing next year.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/at-least-for-reid-gingrich-is-the-2012-republican-pick/', 'snippet': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada may not be a pollster, but he has already decided who President Obama will be facing next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada may not be a pollster, but he has already decided who President Obama will be facing next year. Mr. Reid, the Democratic majority leader, in describing on the Senate floor his distaste for Republican legislative techniques, alluded to a possible government shutdown, and then proclaimed former Speaker Newt Gingrich as the Republican near-nominee for the 2012 presidential race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Least for Reid, Gingrich Is the 2012 Republican Pick', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0466bbfe-d919-54db-b2d5-7ff080e01a20', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0466bbfe-d919-54db-b2d5-7ff080e01a20'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis from CarGurus.com suggests the best used-car prices can be found around Christmas.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/christmas-a-good-time-to-buy-used-cars-analysis-shows/', 'snippet': 'An analysis from CarGurus.com suggests the best used-car prices can be found around Christmas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re waiting to shop for a used car until after the busy holiday season, you might want to reconsider. An analysis from the automotive Web site CarGurus suggests that you’ll get a much better deal on a used car if you shop close to the Christmas holiday, instead of waiting until later in the winter.Demand for cars tends to flag at the end of the year. That means prices can be attractive, according to a study of seasonal price trends compiled by CarGurus. The site based its analysis on its used-car price index, with has tracked list prices on roughly 12 million used cars since 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christmas a Good Time to Buy Used Cars, Analysis Shows', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:26:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fc58a1e-c9cc-5e9c-8453-736d9b456390', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fc58a1e-c9cc-5e9c-8453-736d9b456390'}, {'abstract': 'A critique of the president’s speech, revisited.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/osawatomie-and-opportunity/', 'snippet': 'A critique of the president’s speech, revisited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Chait had an interesting response to the criticisms that both David Frum and I lodged against the President’s Osawatomie speech. We both suggested that the president offered a plausible description of the middle class’s recent woes, coupled with a weak and potentially counterproductive prescription for how to actually address them. To this, Chait basically conceded the relative thinness of the president’s opportunity agenda, and then went on to argue that it doesn’t really matter because the Republicans are worse:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Osawatomie and Opportunity', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/273b6fd2-58b8-57f6-8ce3-f3fb4bcb148a', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273b6fd2-58b8-57f6-8ce3-f3fb4bcb148a'}, {'abstract': 'Tomas Alfredson, the director of “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy,” discusses a scene from the film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/anatomy-of-a-scene-tinker-tailor-soldier-spy/', 'snippet': 'Tomas Alfredson, the director of “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy,” discusses a scene from the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This holiday season brings two spy thrillers of very different stripes: one in an explosive package (“Mission: Impossible — Ghost Protocol”) and one in which the tensions bubble beneath the surface (“Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy.”) The latter has garnered strong audience interest this past weekend in its limited debut, grossing more than $310,000 in four locations. Based on John le Carré’s novel, “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy” looks at the inner workings of the British secret service in the early 1970s. In her review, Manohla Dargis called the film “a pleasurably sly and involving puzzler — a mystery about mysteries within mysteries.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene: ‘Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alfredson, Tomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumberbatch, Benedict', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Carre, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oldman, Gary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Secret Intelligence Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca874b44-201b-5d1c-a6a1-50ac6bd3e93f', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca874b44-201b-5d1c-a6a1-50ac6bd3e93f'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of a rebellious Chinese village where the authorities have been effectively chased out posted video of their protests.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/video-from-inside-rebellious-chinese-village/', 'snippet': 'Residents of a rebellious Chinese village where the authorities have been effectively chased out posted video of their protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Andrew Jacobs reports, the village of Wukan in the industrial heartland of Guangdong Province in China is in open rebellion against local authorities, residents say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video From Inside Rebellious Chinese Village', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:39:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c21853a8-0275-56e7-a91d-5505a9ff6b96', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c21853a8-0275-56e7-a91d-5505a9ff6b96'}, {'abstract': 'The rise of digital music has taken a toll at the big record companies, but this year the two smallest of the four big music shops still sold for healthy prices.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/the-year-in-media-record-labels-still-carry-a-big-price-tag/', 'snippet': 'The rise of digital music has taken a toll at the big record companies, but this year the two smallest of the four big music shops still sold for healthy prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staff members of The Times’s media news department are highlighting the most significant developments this year in the industries they cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | Record Labels Still Carry a Big Price Tag', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Music Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78ac6f3-c964-5d32-9cdd-2968bf850c34', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78ac6f3-c964-5d32-9cdd-2968bf850c34'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of this season’s pop-up children’s books, including new pop-up versions of “Puff the Magic Dragon” and “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/books/pop-up-book-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'A roundup of this season’s pop-up children’s books, including new pop-up versions of “Puff the Magic Dragon” and “Charlie and the Chocolate Factory.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUESS HOW MUCH I LOVE YOUThe Pop-Up Edition.By Sam McBratney. Illustrated by Anita Jeram. Paper engineering by Corina Fletcher.16 pp. Candlewick Press. $19.99. (Picture book; ages 1 to 5)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14guess-how-much/14guess-how-much-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/14/books/14guess-how-much/14guess-how-much-articleLarge.jpg',