 Occupy Wall Street’s ability to focus political debate on inequality makes the answers to these questions particularly relevant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Politics of the Top 1 Percent', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russell Sage Foundation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Sides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00e1c05b-499a-5d96-a837-13b0fd41a229', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00e1c05b-499a-5d96-a837-13b0fd41a229'}, {'abstract': 'Recent surveys show that while Newt Gingrich is popular among Republican primary voters, he would face a more critical audience among the general electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/new-polls-gingrich-is-less-likable-among-general-election-voters/', 'snippet': 'Recent surveys show that while Newt Gingrich is popular among Republican primary voters, he would face a more critical audience among the general electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While poll after poll this month finds Newt Gingrich to be the preferred candidate among Republicans nationally, and in several early voting states, his unpopularity among all Americans in some of the same surveys underscores the deep challenges he could face in a general election. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Independents a Problem for Gingrich, Polls Find', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T16:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5428743-9144-5e2c-9186-f21ed6176e17', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5428743-9144-5e2c-9186-f21ed6176e17'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said some Israelis would be treated the same way as suspected Palestinian militants, detained at length and tried in military courts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/netanyahu-sets-new-curbs-on-violent-settlers-in-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said some Israelis would be treated the same way as suspected Palestinian militants, detained at length and tried in military courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — After two days of settler violence that shocked much of Israel, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced Wednesday that some radical Israelis would be treated the same way as suspected Palestinian militants — detained for long periods without charge and tried in military courts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/mideast/mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/15/world/mideast/mideast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/mideast/mideast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/mideast/mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/world/mideast/mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Leader Sets Curbs on Settlers for Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Leader Sets Curbs On Settlers For Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T17:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7f4a3e-b115-54c9-bd9b-184d75185c1d', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7f4a3e-b115-54c9-bd9b-184d75185c1d'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of Pylos is planning another Greek restaurant in the East Village spot where he ran Heartbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/boukies-a-greek-spot-to-replace-heartbreak/', 'snippet': 'The owner of Pylos is planning another Greek restaurant in the East Village spot where he ran Heartbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christos Valtzoglou, who already owned Pylos, a well-regarded East Village Greek restaurant with a dramatic ceiling hung with terra-cotta jugs, hired the chef Ingrid Roettele and added a Swiss-German restaurant to his stable. He called it Heartbreak — a prescient name, since it closed in October after a brief run, just two days before Michelin awarded it a star. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boukies, a Greek Spot, to Replace Heartbreak', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michelin Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T17:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_