pulist shock jock, is offering him $1 million to quit the race. Every commentator on the left believes this.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Candidates Like This …', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Gail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T18:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8613203-3ce0-55f3-97c0-c69326bede5d', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8613203-3ce0-55f3-97c0-c69326bede5d'}, {'abstract': 'A new government study of rape and domestic violence found that such attacks may be far more common than previously thought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/health/nearly-1-in-5-women-in-us-survey-report-sexual-assault.html', 'snippet': 'A new government study of rape and domestic violence found that such attacks may be far more common than previously thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An exhaustive government survey of rape and domestic violence released on Wednesday affirmed that sexual violence against women remains endemic in the United States and in some instances may be far more common than previously thought.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 1 in 5 Women in U.S. Survey Say They Have Been Sexually Assaulted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nearly 1 in 5 Women in U.S. Survey Say They Have Been Sexually Assaulted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Justice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stalking (Crime)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T18:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d91a398-aebb-595a-a608-d50d42f67a65', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d91a398-aebb-595a-a608-d50d42f67a65'}, {'abstract': '‘‘David, a frequent customer at Whole Foods, is an avid bagriculturist.’’', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/that-should-be-a-word/', 'snippet': '‘‘David, a frequent customer at Whole Foods, is an avid bagriculturist.’’', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bagri-cul-ture, n.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Should Be a Word', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Foods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whole Foods Market Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T18:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizzie Skurnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Skurnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fdec80f-5276-5a79-9ce0-ba7b4306129a', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fdec80f-5276-5a79-9ce0-ba7b4306129a'}, {'abstract': 'A new Showtime documentary, “A Game of Honor,” explores how players balance football with military commitments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/sports/ncaafootball/documentary-on-army-navy-rivalry-is-under-way.html', 'snippet': 'A new Showtime documentary, “A Game of Honor,” explores how players balance football with military commitments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Navy beat Army for the 10th straight year last Saturday, 27-21, but CBS’s broadcast will not be the last word on the Midshipmen’s victory. Instead, footage from nine video cameras stationed at FedEx Field will form a major part of a new documentary, “A Game of Honor” (Showtime, Dec. 21, at 10 p.m.), that explores how the academies’ players balance football with military commitments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url