t has agreed to decide whether a Chapter 11 debtor can avoid a lender’s right to credit bid when doing a sale under a plan, as opposed to the more famous Section 363.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Court Spotlight on Right to ‘Credit Bid’', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T18:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Lubben', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40940cbb-773c-5f83-b7d7-4b4515cacbe9', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40940cbb-773c-5f83-b7d7-4b4515cacbe9'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama made a trip to Fort Bragg on Wednesday as both the commander in chief and as a presidential candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/us/at-fort-bragg-obama-showers-praise-on-troops-back-from-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama made a trip to Fort Bragg on Wednesday as both the commander in chief and as a presidential candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT BRAGG, N.C. — President Obama observed the end of the war in Iraq on Wednesday before an audience of those who fought in it, telling a crowd of returning war veterans that the nearly nine years of conflict in Iraq, a war now indelibly imprinted on the national psyche, had come to a close.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Praises Troops as He Ends the War He Opposed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Observes End of Iraq War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Bragg (NC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T18:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea029466-1383-5c71-bfc4-a47c56b08f94', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea029466-1383-5c71-bfc4-a47c56b08f94'}, {'abstract': 'Is the new attack ad targeting Mitt Romney funny, or does it cross the line?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/how-should-i-feel-about-the-french-mitt-romney-ad/', 'snippet': 'Is the new attack ad targeting Mitt Romney funny, or does it cross the line?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers who think I always have an opinion loaded and ready to fire may be interested to know that I was stumped this week — by a political ad, of all things. (After 24 years of covering politics for a living, it’s hard even to find them surprising.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Should I Feel About the French Mitt Romney Ad?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ff42840-227b-5a63-83f1-d24d84741ec5', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ff42840-227b-5a63-83f1-d24d84741ec5'}, {'abstract': 'A transcript of remarks made by President Obama and his wife, Michelle, in Fort Bragg, N.C., on Wednesday, as released by the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/us/politics/obamas-speech-to-troops-at-fort-bragg.html', 'snippet': 'A transcript of remarks made by President Obama and his wife, Michelle, in Fort Bragg, N.C., on Wednesday, as released by the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Speech to Troops at Fort Bragg', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45afd75-7ae4-5250-8ecd-ff4bb620128c', 'word_count': 3764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45afd75-7ae4-5250-8ecd-ff4bb620128c'}, {'abstract': 'A basement club in SoHo seems to want to recreate Andy Warhol’s Factory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/fashion/wip-a-nightclub-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'A basement club in SoHo seems to want to recreate Andy Warhol’s Factory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A MODERN reimagination of Andy Warhol’s Factory? That’s the idea, anyway, behind W.i.P., an art-slathered club that opened last month in the basement beneath Greenhouse, another club around the corner. W.i.P. (for Work in Progress) is a venture between Barry Mullineaux, who runs Greenhouse, and an arts outfit called Collective Hardware.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/fashion/15BOITE/15zBOITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/fashion/15BOITE/15BOITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/fashion/15BOITE/15BOITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'W.i.P.', 'kicker': 'Boîte', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'W.i.P.: SoHo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Whitney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whitney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/485ce94d-4389-5251-b83e-d36a024a9ae5', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/485ce94d-4389-5251-b83e-d36a024a9ae5'}, {'abstract': 'Coupons and bargain-hunting Web sites may cut down on holiday shopping at the mall — and may even keep you from setting foot in the mall at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/fashion/shopping-at-the-last-minute-no-worries-online.html', 'snippet': 'Coupons and bargain-hunting Web sites may cut down on holiday shopping at the mall — and may even keep you from setting foot in the mall at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST because you left your holiday shopping to the last minute doesn’t mean you have to pay full price. These coupon and bargain-hunting Web sites may save you time and money at the mall. They may even save you from setting foot in the mall in the first place.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/fashion/15zCOUPONS/15zCOUPONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Shopping at the Last Minute? No Worries Online', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Happy Super-Bargain Big-Sale No-Mall Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc87555-fb06-5dd0-83f4-8f612f3bd1e7', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc87555-fb06-5dd0-83f4-8f612f3bd1e7'}, {'abstract': 'The bespoke British designer’s cozy shop blends into the SoHo landscape. Sadly, it’s only around through Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/last-call-katherine-hookers-pretty-pop-up/', 'snippet': 'The bespoke British designer’s cozy shop blends into the SoHo landscape. Sadly, it’s only around through Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sleek, minimalist, elegant yet cozy and inviting at the same time. Tucked into a little storefront on Thompson Street in the chic art/tea/fashion triangle of New York City’s SoHo, the bespoke British designer Katherine Hooker’s clothing shop blends into the landscape as if it’s been there forever and is here to stay. But neither of those things are true. In some takeoff of Chef Ludo-meets-fashion, Hooker’s first ready-to-wear line and first storefront is a pop-up and will be open in New York only through Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Call | Katherine Hooker’s Pretty Pop-Up', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Ephron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ephron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5cebcd7-0241-52d4-8039-b1e3ade00a6f', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5cebcd7-0241-52d4-8039-b1e3ade00a6f'}, {'abstract': 'The College Board concludes that unless rates rise sharply, the country will not meet its goal of having 55 percent of young adults earn diplomas by 2025.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/completion-rates/', 'snippet': 'The College Board concludes that unless rates rise sharply, the country will not meet its goal of having 55 percent of young adults earn diplomas by 2025.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty percent of people ages 25 to 34 in the United States have college degrees, putting the nation in 12th place among developed countries. President Obama has set an ambitious goal of catapulting the country to first place by 2025, and the College Board, separately, has quantified a complementary goal: to increase the percentage of young adults with degrees from 40 percent to 55 percent by 2025.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diploma Rates Far Short of Goal, Report Says', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6ba99d-b6f3-5506-80db-ca2dc3df35e3', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6ba99d-b6f3-5506-80db-ca2dc3df35e3'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta spoke in glowing terms of the progress made in battling insurgents and stabilizing the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/asia/panetta-says-united-states-and-allies-have-the-edge-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta spoke in glowing terms of the progress made in battling insurgents and stabilizing the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta said Wednesday that the United States and its Afghan and foreign allies had been able to “seize the momentum” in Afghanistan and that they were winning the war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/sub-panetta/sub-panetta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/sub-panetta/sub-panetta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/world/sub-panetta/sub-panetta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panetta Says U.S. Has Edge on Taliban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panetta Says U.S. Has Edge on Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'p