e did not focus on the e-mails that conveyed this information.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/is-james-murdoch-running-out-of-denials/', 'snippet': 'James Murdoch has maintained he wasn’t looped in on how widespread phone hacking was at the newspaper he supervised. Now it is a matter of record that he was, though he says he did not focus on the e-mails that conveyed this information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In almost every Road Runner cartoon, Wile E. Coyote overshoots the edge of a cliff and finds his feet spinning in the air, frantically pawing for the terra firma that he has left behind. Those of us watching know he is about to fall, and even as he continues to flail in midair, deep inside he knows it as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is James Murdoch Running Out of Denials?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crone, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myler, Colin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Gordon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a0ee7e-38a6-5cfb-bf56-bb00eebce5a4', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a0ee7e-38a6-5cfb-bf56-bb00eebce5a4'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Melancon, traded by the Astros, will be used at the back end of Boston’s bullpen, perhaps as a setup man with the occasional opportunity to close.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/astros-trade-melancon-a-former-yankee-to-red-sox/', 'snippet': 'Mark Melancon, traded by the Astros, will be used at the back end of Boston’s bullpen, perhaps as a setup man with the occasional opportunity to close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Yankees traded relief pitcher Mark Melancon to the Houston Astros for Lance Berkman just hours before the trade deadline in 2010, they probably did not envision Melancon winding up in the Boston Red Sox’ bullpen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Astros Trade Melancon, a Former Yankee, to Red Sox', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Lance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:55:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05a79a54-1028-5fc3-afb9-8cdf182dbb5f', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05a79a54-1028-5fc3-afb9-8cdf182dbb5f'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of pages of interviews with Marines, once closely guarded as secrets of war, were meant to be destroyed as the last American troops prepare to leave Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/united-states-marines-haditha-interviews-found-in-iraq-junkyard.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of pages of interviews with Marines, once closely guarded as secrets of war, were meant to be destroyed as the last American troops prepare to leave Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — One by one, the Marines sat down, swore to tell the truth and began to give secret interviews discussing one of the most horrific episodes of America’s time in Iraq: the 2005 massacre by Marines of Iraqi civilians in the town of Haditha.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/15haditha/15haditha-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/15haditha/15haditha-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/15haditha/15haditha-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/15haditha/15haditha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/15haditha/15haditha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Junkyard Gives Up Secret Accounts of Massacre in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Junkyard Gives Up Secret Accounts of Massacre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haditha (Iraq)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T19:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a353654f-da23-5927-889c-a44fe656be26', 'word_count': 1963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a353654f-da23-5927-889c-a44fe656be26'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: A subway rider brings his own seating, a cello and music for fellow passengers.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/n-y-see-a-train-canal-street-1122-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: A subway rider brings his own seating, a cello and music for fellow passengers.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Train, Canal Street, 11:22 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CANAL STREET (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T20:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742c3b5f-ac0d-54f5-8970-f45e13f8c560', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742c3b5f-ac0d-54f5-8970-f45e13f8c560'}, {'abstract': 'The key to Amazon’s success over the years has been its relentlessness. Most retailers hit a cruising speed and stay there. Amazon, for better or worse, keeps accelerating. Amazon’s millions of customers do not mind its aggressive tactics. Yet.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/for-amazon-lashes-and-backlashes/', 'snippet': 'The key to Amazon’s success over the years has been its relentlessness. Most retailers hit a cruising speed and stay there. Amazon, for better or worse, keeps accelerating. Amazon’s millions of customers do not mind its aggressive tactics. Yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Amazon had a secret agenda in 2011 to fuel a backlash against itself, the retailer has scored another triumph. Its refusal to collect sales tax in California despite a new law compelling it to do so prompted some well-publicized criticism not only from politicians but the tech community. Its hiring of ambulances at its Pennsylvania warehouse to wait for workers to keel over in the summer heat conjured up a Dickensian sweatshop. The retailer apparently brought its Kindle Fire tablet to market before it had all the kinks out, disappointing some of its biggest fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Amazon, Lashes and Backlashes', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major':