iterature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theroux, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolano, Roberto', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T21:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah Meadows', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meadows', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd90772-3c17-5a63-89f2-37c5c0041a77', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd90772-3c17-5a63-89f2-37c5c0041a77'}, {'abstract': '“Glee” and “New Girl” on Fox halted recent ratings slides and remained steady in the 18-to-49 demo, but CBS won the night overall with new episodes of “NCIS” and “NCIS: Los Angeles.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/fox-rebound-not-enough-to-fully-eclipse-cbs-on-tuesday/', 'snippet': '“Glee” and “New Girl” on Fox halted recent ratings slides and remained steady in the 18-to-49 demo, but CBS won the night overall with new episodes of “NCIS” and “NCIS: Los Angeles.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fox was barely able to retain its Tuesday night foothold with the 18-to-49-year-old demographic, tying CBS in that ratings category most prized by advertisers. “Glee” and “New Girl” both halted recent ratings slides and remained steady for Fox when compared to last week in the 18-to-49 demo and drew 7 million and 6.8 million total viewers respectively. \xa0 Those Fox shows faced off against new episodes of “NCIS” and “NCIS: Los Angeles” on CBS for the first time in three weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox Rebound Not Enough to Fully Eclipse CBS on Tuesday', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-1