}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2928b27e-6960-573b-aabb-66cac569846a', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2928b27e-6960-573b-aabb-66cac569846a'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Schreier conducted the New York Philharmonic in Handel’s “Messiah” at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-performs-handels-messiah.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Schreier conducted the New York Philharmonic in Handel’s “Messiah” at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great German tenor Peter Schreier and the New York Philharmonic do not share an extensive history, but what they have done together over the years has been noteworthy. Having made his debut as a soloist with the orchestra in 1973 in Dvorak’s Stabat Mater, Mr. Schreier returned just three times in that capacity: in Britten’s “Serenade” and Bach’s “St. John Passion” and “St. Matthew Passion.” In 1998 the Philharmonic presented Mr. Schreier in recital with the pianist Andras Schiff, who was appearing with the orchestra at the time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/arts/phil/phil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/arts/phil/phil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/arts/phil/phil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Philharmonic’s ‘Messiah,’ With Bright Voices and Little Vibrato', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Philharmonic’s ‘Messiah,’ With Bright Voices and Little Vibrato', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': Non