original': 'By Alia Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a895ffc0-73de-5dc4-99ed-db21c18f9383', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a895ffc0-73de-5dc4-99ed-db21c18f9383'}, {'abstract': 'The death of a longtime friend and neighbor of the jazz legend in Queens is a loss for music history and the museum run in his former house.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/feeling-the-loss-of-a-connection-to-louis/', 'snippet': 'The death of a longtime friend and neighbor of the jazz legend in Queens is a loss for music history and the museum run in his former house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Selma Heraldo lived the entirety of her 88 years in a white, two-story house on 107th Street in Corona, Queens, and her life may have been very different had she not gained new next-door neighbors in 1943 — Louis Armstrong and his wife, Lucille.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Queens Block, Losing a Link to Louis Armstrong', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LOUIS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Armstrong, Louis, House Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corona (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T23:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank'