011/12/15/sports/football/nfl-cashes-in-on-its-popularity.html', 'snippet': 'Starting in 2014, CBS, Fox and NBC will spend a combined average of about $3 billion a year — more than 50 percent higher than their current deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its consistently high ratings and its solid grip on the American sports psyche, the N.F.L. knows that broadcast and cable networks will spend ever-rising sums to carry its games.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/sports/BROADCAST/BROADCAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/sports/BROADCAST/BROADCAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/sports/BROADCAST/BROADCAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Latest Network Agreements, the N.F.L. Outdoes Even Itself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Its Latest Network TV Agreements, the N.F.L. Outdoes Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DirecTV', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-14T23:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aef689bd-370f-5268-9a4b-3d393d83779e', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aef689bd-370f-5268-9a4b-3d393d83779e'}, {'abstract': 'Jonas Mekas revisits familiar themes, many deeply personal, in “Sleepless Nights Stories,” which gives viewers a sense of the sweep of his life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/movies/sleepless-nights-stories-by-jonas-mekas-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jonas Mekas revisits familiar themes, many deeply personal, in “Sleepless Nights Stories,” which gives viewers a sense of the sweep of his life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than a half-century, the filmmaker, artist, poet, critic, programmer and ecstatic theologian of cinema Jonas Mekas has been viewing the world through a camera, often in the form of visual diaries. A restless image maker, he seizes moments of beauty and life as it happens in work that bridges outer and inner, the self and the other. The leap across this great divide is crucial: in contrast to the iEverything, me-centric ethos, his movies (initially shot in film, more recently digital) have been at once a way into the world and into his own self. “I make home movies, therefore I live,” he says in his 1969 film “Walden.” “I live, therefore I make home movies.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times',