e it investigates reports of physical violence among band members.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Atlanta-area school district has suspended all high school marching band activities while it investigates reports of physical violence among band members. The decision comes amid growing scrutiny of hazing in marching bands, following the death of a drum major at Florida A&M University last month during what officials have called a hazing ritual. The DeKalb County school district said Wednesday that it was investigating “documented evidence of inappropriate activity” by students last summer. The student who died in the Florida A&M episode, Robert Champion, was a graduate of DeKalb schools, and another band member at Florida A&M told the police this week that she was beaten so severely by fellow students that she was hospitalized. She and the three students accused of hazing her are also graduates of DeKalb schools. Meanwhile, the Florida A&M authorities looking into Mr. Champion’s death opened a new investigation after they uncovered possible employee fraud and misconduct, according to documents released Wednesday, The Associated Press reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: District Suspends Marching Band Activities', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: District Suspends Marching Band Activities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marching Bands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Champion, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida 