saving bill that would allow pharmacies to sell a limited number of syringes to individuals without prescriptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Jersey State Assembly made a sensible, life-saving decision this month when it approved a bill that allows pharmacies to sell a limited number of syringes to individuals without prescriptions. The bill has passed the Senate, and Gov. Chris Christie should sign it into law. It will help New Jersey reduce the spread of H.I.V. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clean Needles in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clean Needles in New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypodermic Needles and Syringes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T03:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3730aa7-c484-5328-bbeb-82d9288e3e3d', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3730aa7-c484-5328-bbeb-82d9288e3e3d'}, {'abstract': 'Deaths due to accidents are much higher than many other developing nations.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/in-india-a-growing-safety-problem/', 'snippet': 'Deaths due to accidents are much higher than many other developing nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s report of more than 100 people near Kolkata dying from bootleg liquor – coming on the heels of a fire in that city that killed more than 90 – is the latest in a steady stream of horrific tragedies that seem to strike with brutal regularity in India. Rail accidents, stampedes at over-crowded religious festivals, bus accidents, building collapses, and a world-record number of traffic fatalities, are among the hazards regularly reported across the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In India, a Growing Safety Problem', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T03:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18faa9b7-3ad3-509d-943a-63f04a8126ec', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18faa9b7-3ad3-509d-943a-63f04a8126ec'}, {'abstract': 'A Senate bill would allow the Food and Drug Administration to force medical implant manufacturers to keep track of their devices’ performance after approval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/business/bill-would-require-more-monitoring-of-implants.html', 'snippet': 'A Senate bill would allow the Food and Drug Administration to force medical implant manufacturers to keep track of their devices’ performance after approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid growing problems with artificial hips and other medical implants, bipartisan legislation was introduced in the Senate on Wednesday that would force manufacturers to track the performance of such products after they were approved for sale.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': 