zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95ba0e6-d1df-571e-bda7-918674f6ad2c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95ba0e6-d1df-571e-bda7-918674f6ad2c'}, {'abstract': 'Israeli authorities reopened a wooden bridge used by non-Muslims to enter the holy compound known as the Noble Sanctuary to Muslims and the Temple Mount to Jews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/middleeast/in-israel-bridge-at-holy-site-is-reopened.html', 'snippet': 'Israeli authorities reopened a wooden bridge used by non-Muslims to enter the holy compound known as the Noble Sanctuary to Muslims and the Temple Mount to Jews.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Israeli authorities reopened a wooden bridge used by non-Muslims to enter the holy compound known as the Noble Sanctuary to Muslims and the Temple Mount to Jews. The Israelis closed the bridge on Monday because they considered it unsafe and wanted to replace it. But any act around the holy compound produces suspicion, and Palestinian and Jordanian officials fiercely objected. The Israelis said they would reinforce the bridge rather than rebuild it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Bridge at Holy Site Is Reopened', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Bridge at Holy Site Is Reopened', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temple Mount (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/53624e9f-1a33-5d7e-ae71-56df65c2b43d', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53624e9f-1a33-5d7e-ae71-56df65c2b43d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hoban, a prolific author, created the “Frances” series of children’s books and the “Riddley Walker” science-fiction novel for adults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/books/russell-hoban-frances-author-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hoban, a prolific author, created the “Frances” series of children’s books and the “Riddley Walker” science-fiction novel for adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russell Hoban, a prolific author who created Frances, a girl who appeared in the guise of a badger in seven books for children, and Riddley Walker, the eponymous narrator of a widely praised postapocalyptic novel for adults, died on Tuesday in London. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/arts/HOBAN1-obit/HOBAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/arts/HOBAN1-obit/HOBAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russell Hoban, ‘Frances’ Author, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russell Hoban, ‘Frances’ Author, Dies at 86', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoban, Russell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4927bdc-61db-518e-9be0-5570f5b0f093', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4927bdc-61db-518e-9be0-5570f5b0f093'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/news-quiz-dec-15-2011/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Dec. 15, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:13:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/029f45a4-eefe-587f-b689-02a1a8602e49', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/029f45a4-eefe-587f-b689-02a1a8602e49'}, {'abstract': 'The Simon Wiesenthal Center has begun “Operation Last Chance II,” focused on finding and prosecuting remaining World War II Nazi war criminals who are still at large.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/world/europe/center-begins-project-focused-on-finding-and-prosecuting-nazis.html', 'snippet': 'The Simon Wiesenthal Center has begun “Operation Last Chance II,” focused on finding and prosecuting remaining World War II Nazi war criminals who are still at large.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Simon Wiesenthal Center has begun “Operation Last Chance II,” focused on finding and prosecuting remaining World War II Nazi war criminals who are still at large, the organization’s chief Nazi hunter, Efraim Zuroff, said at a news conference in Berlin. The new project offers financial rewards of up to $32,900 for information leading to the prosecution and punishment of Nazi war crime suspects. The current drive to reopen hundreds of dormant investigations became possible after a legal precedent was set by the successful conviction of a former camp guard, John Demjanjuk, 91, in May. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Center Begins Project Focused on Finding and Prosecuting Nazis', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Center Begins Project Focused On Finding and Prosecuting Nazis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wiesenthal, Simon, Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuroff, Efraim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Homola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5be86e0-c602-5d40-8831-910bfa4882e2', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5be86e0-c602-5d40-8831-910bfa4882e2'}, {'abstract': 'The University of California, Berkeley says families earning up to $140,000 would be expected to pay no more than 15 percent of their annual income.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/education/berkeley-increasing-aid-to-middle-class-students.html', 'snippet': 'The University of California, Berkeley says families earning up to $140,000 would be expected to pay no more than 15 percent of their annual income.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The University of California, Berkeley, announced Wednesday that it would offer far more financial aid to middle-class students starting next fall, with families earning up to $140,000 a year expected to contribute no more than 15 percent of their annual income, in what experts described as the most significant such move by a public institution. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-BERKELEY-1/jp-BERKELEY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-BERKELEY-1/jp-BERKELEY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-BERKELEY-1/jp-BERKELEY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-BERKELEY-1/jp-BERKELEY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-BERKELEY-1/jp-BERKELEY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Ivies, Berkeley Adds Aid to Draw Middle-Class Students', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Ivies, Berkeley Adds Aid to Draw Middle-Class Students', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5009f040-124d-563e-b7da-7728af5d7a54', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5009f040-124d-563e-b7da-7728af5d7a54'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Amato’s opera company, Amato Opera, was long the brightest star in the constellation of semiprofessional opera companies spread over the city — the Off Broadway of the opera world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/arts/music/anthony-amato-founder-of-amato-opera-is-dead-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Amato’s opera company, Amato Opera, was long the brightest star in the constellation of semiprofessional opera companies spread over the city — the Off Broadway of the opera world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Amato, the founder and artistic director of the Amato Opera Theater, the scrappy, often threadbare and very rarely dull chamber opera company on the Lower East Side of Manhattan that was a mainstay of New York’s cultural life for 61 years, died on Tuesday at his home on City Island, in the Bronx. Mr. Amato, who was also the company’s stage director, music director, prompter, vocal coach, diction coach, caterer, broom pusher and emergency tenor, among other things, was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The N