ippet': 'The United Nations asked donor countries on Wednesday for $7.7 billion to help deal with humanitarian crises in 16 countries in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations asked donor countries on Wednesday for $7.7 billion to help deal with humanitarian crises in 16 countries in 2012, earmarking much of the money for tackling drought and famine in Somalia. The United Nations is hoping to bolster aid to Yemen to $447 million to tackle the effects of conflict and a food crisis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donations Are Sought to Aid 16 Nations', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Donations Are Sought to Aid 16 Nations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d466bff-e3cc-5e25-b96d-c7bf2b14af12', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d466bff-e3cc-5e25-b96d-c7bf2b14af12'}, {'abstract': 'Following a look at how the war has impacted those living in Baghdad, we now turn to the Anbar Province.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/what-iraqis-think-of-the-american-withdrawal-anbar-province/', 'snippet': 'Following a look at how the war has impacted those living in Baghdad, we now turn to the Anbar Province.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As American forces start to pull out of Iraq, we asked Iraqis around the country three questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Iraqis Think of the American Withdrawal: Anbar Province', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell and Baghdad Bureau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Baghdad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bureau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5d771b-cda9-537f-86ab-b4a6d112bc8d', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5d771b-cda9-537f-86ab-b4a6d112bc8d'}, {'abstract': 'Anbar was where instability began in Iraq. It was where stability returned. And it is where instability could start again.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/14/whatever-happened-to-falluja/', 'snippet': 'Anbar was where instability began in Iraq. It was where stability returned. And it is where instability could start again.', 'lead_paragraph': ' FALLUJA, Iraq — Even before the war many people in Falluja did not like Saddam Hussein. They thought he made his decisions without consulting his people, that he was a dictator and they wanted to get rid of him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whatever Happened to … Falluja', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By An Iraqi Employee of The New York Times in Falluja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'An', 'middlename': 'Iraqi', 'lastname': 'Employee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e16cf0d7-a2fb-57dd-bba9-448793a8586e', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e16cf0d7-a2fb-57dd-bba9-448793a8586e'}, {'abstract': 'Some hospitals have begun limiting the use of computers, smartphones and other devices in critical settings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/health/as-doctors-use-more-devices-potential-for-distraction-grows.html', 'snippet': 'Some hospitals have begun limiting the use of computers, smartphones and other devices in critical settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hospitals and doctors’ offices, hoping to curb medical error, have invested heavily to put computers, smartphones and other devices into the hands of medical staff for instant access to patient data, drug information and case studies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-DOCTORS/jp-DOCTORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-DOCTORS/jp-DOCTORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-DOCTORS/jp-DOCTORS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-DOCTORS/jp-DOCTORS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/15/us/jp-DOC