d that the right to vote “is not only the cornerstone of our system of government — it is the lifeblood of our democracy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Two-Step', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attorneys General', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beeson, Ann', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T04:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Beeson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beeson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3593fad-e4c5-55d8-91c0-871e9832da4d', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3593fad-e4c5-55d8-91c0-871e9832da4d'}, {'abstract': 'A study by the Center on Education Policy says that under the No Child Left Behind law, 48 percent of schools would be labeled as failing this year — not 82 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/education/education-secretary-overstated-failing-schools-under-no-child-left-behind-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'A study by the Center on Education Policy says that under the No Child Left Behind law, 48 percent of schools would be labeled as failing this year — not 82 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Obama administration was seeking to drum up support for its education initiatives last spring, Secretary of Education Arne Duncan told Congress that the federal law known as No Child Left Behind would label 82 percent of all the nation’s public schools as failing this year. Skeptics questioned that projection, but Mr. Duncan insisted it was based on careful analysis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Failure Rate of Schools Overstated, Study Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Failure Rate Of Schools Overstated, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T05:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dillon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7caf7308-82a8-5e68-9dd1-fa86f673f9d4', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7caf7308-82a8-5e68-9dd1-fa86f673f9d4'}, {'abstract': 'A total of 115 passenger vehicles were named to the list, which is based on results from crash tests conducted by the organization.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/insurance-institute-names-a-record-number-of-top-safety-picks/', 'snippet': 'A total of 115 passenger vehicles were named to the list, which is based on results from crash tests conducted by the organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second consecutive year, car buyers with safety at the top of their shopping list have a record number of choices at their dealerships. This conclusion was reached by the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety, a nonprofit group financed by the insurance industry, which released its list of Top Safety Picks for 2012 on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurance Institute Names a Record Number of Top Safety Picks', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACURA DIVISION OF HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Insurance Institute for Highway Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen A.G', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T05:01:48+0000', 'd