1916, the French launched a counterattack against German forces that would bring an end to the Battle of Verdun three days later, thus ending the longest and most costly battle of World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/dec-15-1916-frances-decisive-attack-in-battle-of-verdun/', 'snippet': 'On Dec. 15, 1916, the French launched a counterattack against German forces that would bring an end to the Battle of Verdun three days later, thus ending the longest and most costly battle of World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 15, 1916, the French launched a counterattack against German forces that would bring an end to the Battle of Verdun three days later, thus ending the longest and most costly battle of World War I.The New York Times quoted a report released by the French War Office: “The attack started at 10 o’clock. The enemy’s front broke down everywhere to a depth of about three kilometers. …We have taken a great many prisoners, whose exact number has not yet been determined. … We have taken or destroyed numerous pieces of heavy and field artillery and also a considerable quantity of material. … Our success is complete. The troops have given vent to great enthusiasm. Our losses are slight.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 15, 1916 | France’s Decisive Attack in Battle of Verdun', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T09:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b59cffb-ac5a-5447-a90a-eba76636d1b0', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b59cffb-ac5a-5447-a90a-eba76636d1b0'}, {'abstract': 'Sports Illustrated’s annual swimsuit edition hit the newsstands across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/sports-illustrateds-swimsuit-edition-makes-a-modest-splash/', 'snippet': 'Sports Illustrated’s annual swimsuit edition hit the newsstands across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With barely a whisper of marketing, Sports Illustrated’s iconic swimsuit edition made its debut in India two weeks ago. The 100-rupee ($2) issue is packed with sleek foreign models in a variety of swimwear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sports Illustrated’s Swimsuit Edition Makes a Modest Splash', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sports Illustrated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T09:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saritha Rai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97abce55-a2bd-575a-acb5-8ba97e8ccd0d', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97abce55-a2bd-575a-acb5-8ba97e8ccd0d'}, {'abstract': 'The military is departing a country where insurgents continue to attack American soldiers and militants with Al Qaeda still regularly carry out devastating attacks against civilians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/panetta-in-baghdad-for-iraq-military-handover-ceremony.html', 'snippet': 'The military is departing a country where insurgents continue to attack American soldiers and militants with Al Qaeda still regularly carry out devastating attacks against civilians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Almost nine years after the first American tanks began massing