mixed to negative reviews on Amazon’s own site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/15/blogs/15bits-meyers/15bits-meyers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pulp Friction: The Kindle Debate', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T14:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a13fbecc-6005-558f-a7d7-4e792c75e95b', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a13fbecc-6005-558f-a7d7-4e792c75e95b'}, {'abstract': 'The loss of the bookstore chain’s 400 stores to bankruptcy was an ominous sign in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/the-year-in-media-where-will-borders-books-and-customers-go/', 'snippet': 'The loss of the bookstore chain’s 400 stores to bankruptcy was an ominous sign in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staff members of The Times’s media news department are highlighting the most significant developments this year in the industries they cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | Where Will Borders’ Books and Customers Go?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borders Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T14:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb1e9145-31a0-5b0f-98e5-c631bd6b6187', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb1e9145-31a0-5b0f-98e5-c631bd6b6187'}, {'abstract': 'The compromise makes small-business assistance available to more — and larger — companies.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/congress-reaches-deal-to-reauthorize-and-revamp-small-business-programs/', 'snippet': 'The compromise makes small-business assistance available to more — and larger — companies.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The House of Representatives and the Senate have resolved a three-year battle over the future of two important federal initiatives to aid small businesses: the Small Business Innovation Research program and the Small Business Technology Transfer program. On the particulars, the Senate seems to have carried the day, but the House has won long-term changes to the innovation research program that open it up to companies backed by venture capital. In their dispute, the House and Senate have served as proxies for opposing views of the program’s purpose: whether it should funnel funds to small businesses otherwise neglected by the markets, or maximize the return to the economy in job and wealth creation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Reaches Deal to Reauthorize and Revamp Small-Business Programs', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graves, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Small Business Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Venture Capital Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T14:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd451706-3c26-5454-b64c-439f3f36d02e', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd451706-3c26-5454-b64c-439f3f36d02e'}, {'abstract': 'Cosmetic palettes make for perfect holiday gifts, but only if you