s_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d0b08b-9092-59d3-94e1-a0acd5e9aefa', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d0b08b-9092-59d3-94e1-a0acd5e9aefa'}, {'abstract': 'A sequence from “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,” described by the film’s director and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/18/magazine/dragon-tattoo-fincher.html', 'snippet': 'A sequence from “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,” described by the film’s director and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sequence from “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,” described by the film’s director and editors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI/18mag-dragon-slide-RWEI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Assemble a ‘Dragon’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Girl With the Dragon Tattoo, The (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T14:49:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ad3c4c35-985e-52d5-bce9-f6ae0105aa7b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ad3c4c35-985e-52d5-bce9-f6ae0105aa7b'}, {'abstract': 'The director David Fincher and his Oscar-winning editors break down the art of the edit, using a sequence from their forthcoming film, “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/magazine/david-fincher-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo.html', 'snippet': 'The director David Fincher and his Oscar-winning editors break down the art of the edit, using a sequence from their forthcoming film, “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angus Wall has edited the last five movies directed by David Fincher — the three most-recent (“The Curious Case of Benjamin Button,” “The Social Network” and “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo”) in partnership with Kirk Baxter. Earlier this year, Wall and Baxter won the Oscar for Best Achievement in Film Editing for “The Social Network,” and while they each work on outside projects \xad — Wall created the arresting title sequence for HBO’s “Game of Thrones” — they spend much of their time in adjacent rooms, cutting and splicing copious amounts of Fincher’s footage. Wall explains the key to editing like this: “The human brain wants to put things together; it wants to create a narrative.” Their job is to facilitate that desire.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/magazine/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG/dragon-tattoo-fincher-slide-S2IG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Minutes With ‘The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo’', 'kicker': 'Shoptalk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to assemble a ‘Dragon’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T14:49:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gavin Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gavin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bbb741a-1951-5932-94cb-44d5e6e128a5', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bbb741a-1951-5932-94cb-44d5e6e128a5'}, {'abstract': 'In Adhamiya, Samir Nasrat said the war brought worries never felt under Saddam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001223480/a-better-life-under-saddam.html', 'snippet': 'In Adhamiya, Samir Nasrat said the war brought worries never felt under Saddam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Adhamiya, Samir Nasrat said the war brought worries never felt under Saddam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/12/world/video-iraqivoices-adhamiya/video-iraqivoic