_paragraph': 'Stock indexes snapped a three-day decline as data on jobless claims and manufacturing signaling a strengthening economy overshadowed concern over the European debt crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indexes End 3-Day Swoon On Upbeat Economic Data', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indexes End 3-Day Swoon On Upbeat Economic Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dow Jones Stock Average', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381cc921-8135-54c2-afa3-4e3d8a83a45e', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381cc921-8135-54c2-afa3-4e3d8a83a45e'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks for such a warm welcome to Motherlode. Here’s where I think we’ll go next.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/the-future-of-motherlode/', 'snippet': 'Thanks for such a warm welcome to Motherlode. Here’s where I think we’ll go next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m overwhelmed. Thanks for a warm welcome to Motherlode, and for a list of ideas for new topics that will keep me writing and you commenting for a long time (and, not to mention, help me bring in some great guest posters). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Future of Motherlode', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:06:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc15c580-39be-5221-9da6-b04979af7e61', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc15c580-39be-5221-9da6-b04979af7e61'}, {'abstract': 'Leading Off: The N.B.A. finally deals Chris Paul to the Clippers to end the howling, which seems certain to move next to Orlando, even though the Magic say they have taken Dwight Howard off the trading block for now.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/leading-off-paul-fiasco-over-n-b-a-silliness-moves-to-orlando/', 'snippet': 'Leading Off: The N.B.A. finally deals Chris Paul to the Clippers to end the howling, which seems certain to move next to Orlando, even though the Magic say they have taken Dwight Howard off the trading block for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are mildly surprised the N.B.A. finally managed to trade Chris Paul on Wednesday, keep in mind that the N.B.A. had to trade Chris Paul. After nearly a week of unrelenting scorn for playing puppetmaster with the highest profile star on the team the league operates, Commissioner David Stern did the one thing he had to do to turn off that rather uncomfortable klieg light: get the hapless Hornets a respectable deal for Paul. The alternative was an unhappy star taking the court for an ownerless team as an every-other-night reminder that the league’s fantabulous lockout had created something resembling a banana republic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Paul Fiasco Over, N.B.A. Silliness Moves to Orlando', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmgren, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaman, Chris', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kane, Patrick', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCoy, Colt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Chris', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, David', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Browns', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Times-Picayune', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6748ccbd-43a0-5ac3-96a8-4985f8588feb', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6748ccbd-43a0-5ac3-96a8-4985f8588feb'}, {'abstract': 'On Jan. 1, miles that count toward elite status are reset on most airlines; here is what you need to know to top off your frequent flier account.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/travel/managing-your-frequent-flier-account.html', 'snippet': 'On Jan. 1, miles that count toward elite status are reset on most airlines; here is what you need to know to top off your frequent flier account.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S crunch time for top-tier frequent fliers. On Jan. 1, miles that count toward elite status automatically reset to zero on most airlines. That means fliers who weren’t able to collect enough miles or trip segments to maintain their spot in the frequent flier pecking order — typically between 25,000 and 125,000 miles a year, or 30 and 140 segments, depending on the airline — will lose some, or all, of their beloved perks. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18PRAC/18PRAC-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18PRAC/18PRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18PRAC/18PRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save your Elite Flyer Status While You Can', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elites Eye the Finish Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1,