ars/', 'snippet': 'The Golden Globe nominators have a tendency to reward stars, and this year was no different, with nominations for the likes of Angelina Jolie (for director) and Brad Pitt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hollywood Foreign Press has spoken, and guess what? It likes the stars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise! The Golden Globe Nominators Like Stars', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Gerard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Woody', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:29:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ec0e23-cc5c-5d86-a871-5692448888d7', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ec0e23-cc5c-5d86-a871-5692448888d7'}, {'abstract': 'Critics predict one extension will lead to another as politicians balk at raising taxes to their former level, especially if unemployment remains high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/us/politics/payroll-tax-cut-extension-seen-as-peril-to-social-security.html', 'snippet': 'Critics predict one extension will lead to another as politicians balk at raising taxes to their former level, especially if unemployment remains high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For all of the partisan brawling over President Obama’s call to extend a temporary payroll tax cut for 160 million Americans, one concern is bipartisan: a significant minority of Democrats and Republicans say that cutting the taxes that fin