 'snippet': 'Distracted doctoring is latest gadget side effect, tech gifts that aren’t passe, more cars get top safety ranking and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Distracted Doctoring Is Latest Gadget Side Effect', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/def66b01-cbc1-58b4-89aa-614eb1abdb96', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def66b01-cbc1-58b4-89aa-614eb1abdb96'}, {'abstract': 'Officials in Guangdong Province promised to pause and investigate questionable property sales but also threatened punishments for anyone involved in clashes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/world/asia/local-chinese-officials-seek-to-end-village-revolt.html', 'snippet': 'Officials in Guangdong Province promised to pause and investigate questionable property sales but also threatened punishments for anyone involved in clashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Officials in Guangdong Province trying to end a five-day standoff between the police and angry villagers have vowed to temporarily halt questionable property sales and to investigate claims that the local government illegally confiscated farmland for private development, the state news media reported Thursday