g them up even after the protesters left. Via Eater. — Patrick Farrell ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae31722-71a1-5b0b-bae1-89e359760ca8', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae31722-71a1-5b0b-bae1-89e359760ca8'}, {'abstract': 'Seth Rogen talks about the Golden Globe nomination he didn’t get for co-starring in “50/50.” That’s O.K. because  the film itself, which he helped produce, earned other nods.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/seth-rogen-happy-non-nominee-for-his-role-in-5050/', 'snippet': 'Seth Rogen talks about the Golden Globe nomination he didn’t get for co-starring in “50/50.” That’s O.K. because  the film itself, which he helped produce, earned other nods.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My home phone rang, which only happens when something terrible is going on,” Seth Rogen said, of learning that the film he produced and co-starred in, “50/50,” was nominated for the Golden Globe for best comedy this morning. He hadn’t yet talked to his fellow star, Joseph Gordon-Levitt, nominated for best actor in a comedy, when the Bagger spoke to him. “My brain just doesn’t think I should call people this early,” he said. (His publicist’s brain apparently disagreed.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seth Rogen, Happy Non-Nominee for His Role in ’50/50’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fishburne, Laurence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon-Levitt, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogen, Seth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a036d44c-190b-5cfe-84e6-4b0a8c8302ba', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a036d44c-190b-5cfe-84e6-4b0a8c8302ba'}, {'abstract': 'Warren Glover, who was fired as a security director in July, claims that he repeatedly warned his superiors in the N.B.A.’s security department that women in the office were being sexually harassed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/sports/basketball/former-nba-official-says-sex-harassment-concerns-were-ignored.html', 'snippet': 'Warren Glover, who was fired as a security director in July, claims that he repeatedly warned his superiors in the N.B.A.’s security department that women in the office were being sexually harassed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former N.B.A. security official says that he repeatedly warned his superiors that women in the office were being sexually harassed or discriminated against, but that his concerns were ignored and that he was ultimately fired for his actions on the women’s behalf. He is suing the league for lost wages and damages.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/sports/NBA-1/NBA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/sports/