e loose, wise, tough, well written, well sung and more in tune with the debt-stricken American moment than her own record this year.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RATLIFF_SPAN/18RATLIFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RATLIFF_SPAN/18RATLIFF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RATLIFF_SPAN/18RATLIFF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RATLIFF_SPAN/18RATLIFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RATLIFF_SPAN/18RATLIFF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Packing Heat and Singing Sweetly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Packing Heat and Singing Sweetly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deaf Center (Music Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lambert, Miranda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Kris (1980- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yob (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taborn, Craig', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d72db9-c880-5891-ba7f-4432f35e1312', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d72db9-c880-5891-ba7f-4432f35e1312'}, {'abstract': '“Metals,” the 2011 album from Feist, is one record that Jon Pareles kept coming back to all year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/music-of-heartache-mortality-and-success.html', 'snippet': '“Metals,” the 2011 album from Feist, is one record that Jon Pareles kept coming back to all year.', 'lead_paragraph': '1. FEIST “Metals” (Cherrytree/Interscope) Leslie Feist’s songs of heartache, solitude and eventual solace are both handmade and subtly sophisticated on “Metals.” She traded pop gloss for pensive, lingeringly unresolved melodies and arrangements that crest unexpectedly from within, with her own taut electric guitar and apparitions of horns and voices summoning the tensions behind the beauty.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18PARELES2/18PARELES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 766, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18PARELES2/18PARELES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18PARELES2/18PARELES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heartache, Mortality and Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heartache, Mortality and Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feist, Leslie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tune-Yards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liturgy (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T15:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d3711dd-7134-5182-a698-3f974823bfb9', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d3711dd-7134-5182-a698-3f974823bfb9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Carnage,” Roman Polanski’s spry adaptation of Yasmina Reza’s play, two couples show that beneath the surface of civilized behavior lurks animal impulses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/movies/roman-polanskis-carnage-with-jodie-foster-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Carnage,” Roman Polanski’s spry adaptation of Yasmina Reza’s play, two couples show that beneath the surface of civilized behavior lurks animal impulses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not a lot happens, in the usual sense of movie action, in “Carnage,” Roman Polanski’s swift and spry adaptation of Yasmina Reza’s play: voices are raised; whiskey is drunk; leftover fruit cobbler is consumed and (spoiler alert!) vomited. A few slightly more dramatic events have already taken place before the action starts. There has been a playground altercation between two young boys, and a hamster has been removed from a comfortable high-rise apartment and abandoned to its fate on the streets of Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16CARNAGE/16CARNAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16CARNAGE/16CARNAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16CARNAGE/16CARNAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16CARNAGE/16CARNAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16CARNAGE/16CARNAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blood Sport in a High-Rise', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Carnage'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blood Sport In a High-Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polanski, Roman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reza, Yasmina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Jodie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waltz, Christoph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winslet, Kate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reilly, John C', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4db738-a80c-50db-b4bd-69ea3f62c62c', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4db738-a80c-50db-b4bd-69ea3f62c62c'}, {'abstract': 'No treatments have stopped the eczema from coming back, and when I look at the ooze dripping down my arms, I can’t help but think the fault somehow is mine, writes Jen Miller.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/the-painful-cycle-of-eczema/', 'snippet': 'No treatments have stopped the eczema from coming back, and when I look at the ooze dripping down my arms, I can’t help but think the fault somehow is mine, writes Jen Miller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During my latest eczema outbreak, the routine was typical. I wake up and remove from my hands the white cotton socks that prevent me from scratching overnight, then press a tissue to my closed eyes to remove the pus and blood that have accumulated in the folds of my eyelids. In the bathroom, I try not to dwell too long at the sight of myself in the mirror before patting my skin dry and slathering it with lotion. I wrap bandages over the raw and weeping patches in the crooks of my elbows — a stopgap, really, since the bandages will soak through in several hours. I take Benadryl to calm the itching, and ibuprofen to temper the swelling and pain, before heading to meetings in an antihistamine haze. I hope no one stares, but they do. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waking Up With Eczema', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eczema', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jen A. Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jen', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d075dc-82c1-5c4a-8312-38405a9ca948', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d075dc-82c1-5c4a-8312-38405a9ca948'}, {'abstract': 'Silk wide leg pants with a built-in split train, or “spants,” were the highlight of Theyskens’ Theory prefall collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/just-one-look-theyskens-theory/', 'snippet': 'Silk wide leg pants with a built-in split train, or “spants,” were the highlight of Theyskens’ Theory prefall collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They’re calling them “spants,” said a fellow observer at the Theyskens’ Theory prefall collection appointment yesterday afternoon. Spants — like these silk wide leg pants with a built-in split train — are a perfect mix of the designer Olivier Theyskens’s past successes: the long flowing silk skirts (styled with a faded tee) and the super-wide-leg trouser. Also new among the label’s faithful hot shorts, biker jackets and low slung denim pants are crystal-embroidered sheer tops and tights (that slouch in the perfect, grungy way) and a glowing signature print inspired by certain light-catching prisms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Theyskens’ Theory', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theyskens, Olivier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d428def1-f509-5cb8-8950-dc0f26f5d11f', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d428def1-f509-5cb8-8950-dc0f26f5d11f'}, {'abstract': 'A statue was installed near the Japan embassy in Seoul to protest sexual slavery during World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/world/asia/statute-in-seoul-becomes-focal-point-of-dispute-between-south-korea-and-japan.html', 'snippet': 'A statue was installed near the Japan embassy in Seoul to protest sexual slavery during World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The unsmiling teenage girl in traditional Korean dress sits in a chair, her feet bare, her hands on her lap, her eyes fixed on the Japanese Embassy across a narrow street in central Seoul. Within a day, the life-size bronze statue had become the focal point of a simmering diplomatic dispute as President Lee Myung-bak prepared to visit Tokyo this weekend.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/15statue-image2/15statue-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/15statue-image2/15statue-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/world/15statue-image2/15statue-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Statue Deepens Dispute Over Wartime Sexual Slavery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Korea’s Painful Reminder Of Japanese Occupation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations and Restitution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4701abcd-59c8-5c77-8ea0-867b2e20231e', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4701abcd-59c8-5c77-8ea0-867b2e20231e'}, {'abstract': 'Nat Chinen includes albums by Ambrose Akinmusire, Drake, the Roots and St. Vincent, among others, in his favorite releases for 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/ambrose-akinmusire-drake-the-roots-st-vincent.html', 'snippet': 'Nat Chinen includes albums by Ambrose Akinmusire, Drake, the Roots and St. Vincent, among others, in his favorite releases for 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '1. AMBROSE AKINMUSIRE “When the Heart Emerges Glistening” (Blue Note) An earnest young trumpeter with a bracingly original style — shadowy tone, sure attack, surprising turns of phrase — Mr. Akinmusire puts the focus here on the gleam of his crackerjack quintet. It’s a smart dispatch from the new postbop frontier, and the rare album of that description to feel emotionally unarmored.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CHINEN_SPAN/18CHINEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CHINEN_SPAN/18CHINEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CHINEN_SPAN/18CHINEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CHINEN_SPAN/18CHINEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CHINEN_SPAN/18CHINEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sounds That Come From in the Head and on the Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sounds That Come From in the Head And on the Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akinmusire, Ambrose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5bb2751-d918-547b-8e3c-cd6e74353b4b', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5bb2751-d918-547b-8e3c-cd6e74353b4b'}, {'abstract': 'Madonna’s first album in four years is due out in March, the first of a three-album deal with Interscope Records.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/a-new-madonna-album-on-a-new-label/', 'snippet': 'Madonna’s first album in four years is due out in March, the first of a three-album deal with Interscope Records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madonna’s next album will be released on Interscope Records in March, the first in a three-album deal with the label.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Madonna Album, on a New Label', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakira', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interscope Records', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Music Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94262294-d2ff-5b46-b993-bf935e4240c9', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94262294-d2ff-5b46-b993-bf935e4240c9'}, {'abstract': 'For being bold and arresting and virtually impossible to copy, Drake earns the top spot on Jon Caramancia’s best of 2011 list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/from-retro-yuck-to-foodie-rap.html', 'snippet': 'For being bold and arresting and virtually impossible to copy, Drake earns the top spot on Jon Caramancia’s best of 2011 list.', 'lead_paragraph': '1. DRAKE “Take Care” (Young Money/Cash Money/Universal Republic) Here’s a new blueprint: attack from the outside, rewrite the rules, get famous and win, then tear everything up and start again from even further afield. That’s what Drake’s doing on this, his second major-label album, a perversely strange and entrancing collection of piano-driven self-lacerations and anti-anthems. It’s bold and arresting, and virtually impossible to copy.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CARAMANICA1_SPAN/18CARAMANICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CARAMANICA1_SPAN/18CARAMANICA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CARAMANICA1_SPAN/18CARAMANICA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18CARAMANICA1_SPAN/18CARAMANICA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011