': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ab21f01-fd1b-5329-b2bc-f72e6f41aea3', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ab21f01-fd1b-5329-b2bc-f72e6f41aea3'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama won’t veto the dangerous National Defense Authorization Act.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/the-sound-of-one-president-caving/', 'snippet': 'President Obama won’t veto the dangerous National Defense Authorization Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while, the administration encouraged people to think that President Obama would take a stand against the unnecessary and very dangerous provisions that Congress jammed into the annual National Defense Authorization Act. He threatened to veto the whole bill in order to block new rules that would mandate the military custody of most terrorist suspects, and officially sanction their indefinite detention, without due process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sound of One President Caving', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a634de2e-26e4-5f14-886c-b9ef7c9f493c', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a634de2e-26e4-5f14-886c-b9ef7c9f493c'}, {'abstract': 'The great-grandson of Henry Ford was in New York Tuesday to enlist a motor club’s help in recovering a long-lost glass punch bowl, presented to Ford in 1901 after outracing a rival.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/edsel-ford-ii-wants-the-family-punch-bowl-back/', 'snippet': 'The great-grandson of Henry Ford was in New York Tuesday to enlist a motor club’s help in recovering a long-lost glass punch bowl, presented to Ford in 1901 after outracing a rival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edsel B. Ford II, the great-grandson of Henry Ford, left his audience at Sardi’s restaurant on Tuesday with little doubt about what he wanted from them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edsel Ford II Wants the Family Punch Bowl Back', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Henry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford, Henry, Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sardi's", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:44:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Kurczewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurczewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de7288a7-3ff0-57cb-9dc3-9934a9813865', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de7288a7-3ff0-57cb-9dc3-9934a9813865'}, {'abstract': 'The many items left off the Golden Globes nominee list include “The Muppets,” Kirsten Dunst, Melissa McCarthy and more.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/missing-muppets-forgotten-ingenues-and-other-golden-globes-oversights/', 'snippet': 'The many items left off the Golden Globes nominee list include “The Muppets,” Kirsten Dunst, Melissa McCarthy and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along with Seth Rogen, a slew of other worthy stars were left off the Golden Globes tally sheet this morning. The love may be drying up for “Martha Marcy May Marlene” and “Like Crazy,” whose breakout actresses, Elizabeth Olsen and Felicity Jones, were not mentioned. Neither was Gary Oldman, for bringing George Smiley to life (again) in “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy.” Critical and arthouse favorites like the financial thriller “Margin Call” and Terrence Malick’s “Tree of Life” were forgotten (though two “Tree of Life” stars, Brad Pitt and Jessica Chastain, were nominated for the work in other films). And pity Kirsten Dunst, who turned in a possibly career-changing performance with a difficult director in “Melancholia” and so far has no major Stateside statuettes to show for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing Muppets, Forgotten Ingenues and Other Golden Globes Oversights', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunst, Kirsten', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eastwood, Clint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Felicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malick, Terrence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKenzie, Bret', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Bennett', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Elizabeth', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 11, 'maj