try.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/new-jersey-help-line-for-troops-expands-to-nationwide-program/', 'snippet': 'The Defense Department has opened a toll-free, peer-counseling help line for National Guard troops and reservists anywhere in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A peer-group counseling program that has proven successful in New Jersey is being expanded for reservists and National Guard troops nationwide, in part to help stem the continuing problem of suicides within the military, the Pentagon announced this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Help Line for Troops Expands to Nationwide Program', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lautenberg, Frank R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Medicine and Dentistry of New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T16:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/493727c5-9f88-5544-8a0c-3fadec2bada6', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/493727c5-9f88-5544-8a0c-3fadec2bada6'}, {'abstract': 'The University of California, Berkeley, announced that it would devote an additional $12 million annually to financial aid awards for middle-class students, making it the first public school to take such action.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/medina-berkeley/', 'snippet': 'The University of California, Berkeley, announced that it would devote an additional $12 million annually to financial aid awards for middle-class students, making it the first public school to take such action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Thursday’s Times, Jennifer Medina reported that the University of California, Berkeley, will expand its financial aid to middle-class students next fall, seeking to combat economic stratification on campus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berkeley to Increase Aid to Middle-Class Students', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f81476c6-e961-5a55-b0ba-7370ab541049', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f81476c6-e961-5a55-b0ba-7370ab541049'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation that lasted more than two years singled out Sheriff Joe Arpaio as helping to nurture his department’s “culture of bias.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/us/arizona-sheriffs-office-unfairly-targeted-latinos-justice-department-says.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation that lasted more than two years singled out Sheriff Joe Arpaio as helping to nurture his department’s “culture of bias.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — In a strongly worded critique of the country’s best-known sheriff, the Justice Department on Thursday accused Sheriff Joe Arpaio of engaging in “unconstitutional policing” by unfairly targeting Latinos for detention and arrest and retaliating against those who complain.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/SHERRIF/SHERRIF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/us/SHERRIF/SHERRIF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/SHERRIF/SHERRIF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/SHERRIF/SHERRIF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/us/SHERRIF/SHERRIF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Finds Pervasive Bias Against Latinos by Arizona Sheriff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Says Arizona Sheriff Shows Pervasive Bias Against Latinos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARPAIO, JOSEPH M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maricopa County (Ariz)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b509f03-abcb-531e-9347-21484e83ae77', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b509f03-abcb-531e-9347-21484e83ae77'}, {'abstract': 'The collection of coins includes the largest gold coin from the 15th century that survives today and more than 400 Roman coins, including examples struck under Julius Caesar.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/hispanic-society-enlists-sothebys-to-auction-rare-collection-of-coins/', 'snippet': 'The collection of coins includes the largest gold coin from the 15th century that survives today and more than 400 Roman coins, including examples struck under Julius Caesar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare collection of almost 38,000 coins is expected to raise between $25 million and $35 million for the Hispanic Society of America, Sotheby’s New York announced Thursday. The collection, assembled more than 100 years ago by Archer M. Huntington, the founder of the Hispanic Society, will be offered as a single lot in sealed bid auction beginning Thursday and ending next March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hispanic Society Enlists Sotheby’s to Auction Rare Collection of Coins', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hispanic Society of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afdc253c-a676-5d51-a355-08d25d1ba051', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afdc253c-a676-5d51-a355-08d25d1ba051'}, {'abstract': 'It has been a year in the theater for putting new and explosive life into classic vessels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/theater/traditional-theater-sometimes-with-stealth-bombs.html', 'snippet': 'It has been a year in the theater for putting new and explosive life into classic vessels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS was a year for celebrating both the enduring power of traditional theater and the creative stealth bombs that can be planted within it, for putting new and explosive life into classic vessels. “The Book of Mormon,” the year’s biggest hit, is on one level as cheerful and predictable an organic musical as anything Rodgers and Hammerstein might have come up with. But it’s also a sustained act of gleeful subversion. And while plays like “Jerusalem,” “The _______ With the Hat” and “Other Desert Cities” are anything but experimental in form, each seduces its audiences into traveling into places that they hadn’t expected (or thought they wanted) to visit. With one notable exception (the Belarus Free Theater’s galvanizing “Being Harold Pinter”) the shows listed below have the pleasingly familiar surface appearance of the Broadway of decades ago. What lurks in the hearts and minds of the original productions here (the revivals are another matter, but only just) is very much of the 21st century. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18BRANTELY1/18BRANTELY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18BRANTELY1/18BRANTELY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18BRANTELY1/18BRANTELY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18BRANTELY1/18BRANTELY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18BRANTELY1/18BRANTELY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Past, but Looking Forward', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From the Past, But Looking Forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34eb5338-f426-599f-a27d-cb945d2f23c0', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34eb5338-f426-599f-a27d-cb945d2f23c0'}, {'abstract': 'After quickly totting up his list of his favorite nights at the theater in 2011, Charles Isherwood noticed the lineup didn’t include a single revival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/theater/favorite-nights-at-the-theater.html', 'snippet': 'After quickly totting up his list of his favorite nights at the theater in 2011, Charles Isherwood noticed the lineup didn’t include a single revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the second year running I quickly totted up my list of my favorite nights at the theater before noticing, to my happy surprise, that the lineup didn’t include a single revival. This year, perhaps just as remarkably (if less happily), it doesn’t include a single musical either. True, it was hardly a stellar year for either genre. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Without Hype, Playwriting Thrives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Without Hype, Playwriting Thrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0026ea58-a958-50da-bd6a-914588881c11', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0026ea58-a958-50da-bd6a-914588881c11'}, {'abstract': 'Now playing at the Guggenheim: An inflatable twist on the children’s classic “Peter & the Wolf.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/pop-art-peter-the-wolf/', 'snippet': 'Now playing at the Guggenheim: An inflatable twist on the children’s classic “Peter & the Wolf.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s really best to see the work of Jason Hackenwerth in person to appreciate it, since describing what he does —\xa0which is to assemble art out of balloons —\xa0makes him sound a bit like a glorified clown. In truth, Hackenwerth’s latex balloon sculptures have more in common with the variegated, tentacled glass work of Dale Chihuly than with some Bozo’s bicycle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop Art | ‘Peter & the Wolf’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mizrahi, Isaac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94cc58f0-abce-57c4-8cb5-ae1c563be89c', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94cc58f0-abce-57c4-8cb5-ae1c563be89c'}, {'abstract': 'After a two-year investigation, the Justice Department announced that the Maricopa County Sheriff’s Office has engaged in a pattern of misconduct that violates the Constitution and federal law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/16/us/maricopa_documents.html', 'snippet': 'After a two-year investigation, the Justice Department announced that the Maricopa County Sheriff’s Office has engaged in a pattern of misconduct that violates the Constitution and federal law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a two-year investigation, the Justice Department announced that the Maricopa County Sheriff’s Office has engaged in a pattern of misconduct that violates the Constitution and federal law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Department Findings in Investig