l benefit by becoming a federal landmark. But Wrigley Field’s local landmark status has created problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baseball’s two oldest and most iconic ballparks are on divergent paths when it comes to recognizing their historic status. After a decade of renovations, Boston’s Fenway Park is hurtling toward federal landmark recognition — and the tax credits that come with it. Meanwhile, in Chicago, the Cubs contend that Wrigley Field’s local landmark designation is a roadblock to upgrading the stadium and increasing revenue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fenway and Wrigley Find Two Sides to Landmark Status', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Sarah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Preservation Alliance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fenway Park (Boston)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Parks Service', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Register of Historic Places', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wrigley Field (Chicago)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T17:56:21+0000', 'document_type':