rticle/d9fd8564-4b64-5083-9561-3cca91fd4f28'}, {'abstract': 'Viggo Mortensen says he’s happy to be nominated for a Golden Globe for his performance in “A Dangerous Method” but laments that David Cronenberg, his director, was overlooked.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/viggo-mortensen-and-dangerous-methods-fate/', 'snippet': 'Viggo Mortensen says he’s happy to be nominated for a Golden Globe for his performance in “A Dangerous Method” but laments that David Cronenberg, his director, was overlooked.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s a very pleasant surprise,” Viggo Mortensen said of his Golden Globe nomination for best supporting actor for “A Dangerous Method,” directed by David Cronenberg. Emphasis on the surprise: “My movie is doing extremely well in a few theaters,” Mr. Mortensen continued, calling from Madrid, where he is doing the Ariel Dorfman play “Purgatorio,” “but it hasn’t seemed to be very visible” or acknowledged by the awards crowd so far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viggo Mortensen and ‘Dangerous Method’s’ Fate', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cronenberg, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorfman, Ariel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fassbender, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knightley, Keira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mortensen, Viggo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T18:33:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eea97412-4ad3-59b2-8b6a-8f8bde62cb12', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eea97412-4ad3-59b2-8b6a-8f8bde62cb12'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the old guard in the old town are unhappy about the plan, which will honor Doris Duke.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/maya-lin-project-approved-in-newport-despite-objections/', 'snippet': 'Some of the old guard in the old town are unhappy about the plan, which will honor Doris Duke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the objections of a group of vocal opponents the city council of Newport, R.I., voted Wednesday night to approve the use of a small park for a permanent installation being designed by the artist Maya Lin to evoke the city’s past and to honor the heiress Doris Duke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maya Lin Project Approved in Newport Despite Objections', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duke, Doris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Maya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newport Restoration Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New England States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newport (RI)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T18:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7e3945c-fb86-5158-82c4-8d630280e1ec', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7e3945c-fb86-5158-82c4-8d630280e1ec'}, {'abstract': 'Congressional leaders said they had agreed on a spending measure to keep the government running for nine months, but agreement on the payroll tax cut was still elusive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/us/politics/congress-moves-closer-to-a-spending-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Congressional leaders said they had agreed on a spending measure to keep the government running for nine months, but agreement on the payroll tax cut was still elusive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Retreating from their harsh partisan sniping, and perhaps fearing public rebuke, Congressional leaders said Thursday that they had agreed on a large-scale spending measure to keep the government running for the next nine months. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/CONGRESS1/CONGRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/us/CONGRESS1/CONGRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Agree on Spending Bill, Avoiding Shutdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers’ Temporary Deal Averts Government Shutdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T18:39:37+0000