45-5993-b32c-06f92a0bc9c1', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1cbf470-f945-5993-b32c-06f92a0bc9c1'}, {'abstract': 'Penn State, West Virginia and Virginia Tech are among some big-name programs struggling to sell tickets to their bowl games.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/some-big-schools-struggle-to-sell-bowl-tickets/', 'snippet': 'Penn State, West Virginia and Virginia Tech are among some big-name programs struggling to sell tickets to their bowl games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conventional wisdom in the business of bowl games is that big programs bring along lots of fans. But several schools, including Virginia Tech, Penn State, Clemson and West Virginia, are testing that wisdom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Big Schools Struggle to Sell Bowl Tickets', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'West Virginia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T18:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df471cd7-0462-5b7b-b9f5-4cf8e783c1ad', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df471cd7-0462-5b7b-b9f5-4cf8e783c1ad'}, {'abstract': 'When Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta arrived in Baghdad on Thursday for the ceremony to mark the end of the military’s mission in Iraq there, there was one group noticeably under represented: Iraqis.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/a-withdrawal-ceremony-in-iraq-observed-by-few-iraqis/', 'snippet': 'When Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta arrived in Baghdad on Thursday for the ceremony to mark the end of the military’s mission in Iraq there, there was one group noticeably under represented: Iraqis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — When Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta arrived in Baghdad on Thursday for the ceremony to mark the end of the United States military’s mission in Iraq, there was one group noticeably underrepresented: Iraqis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Withdrawal Ceremony in Iraq, Observed by Few Iraqis', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5c1847-08a1-5444-88f7-bad6c710c576', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5c1847-08a1-5444-88f7-bad6c710c576'}, {'abstract': 'After your husband and son give you that stupid telescope for Christmas, here’s how to get what you really want.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/fashion/a-telescope-for-christmas-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'After your husband and son give you that stupid telescope for Christmas, here’s how to get what you really want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband asked me what I wanted for Christmas. I gave him a list of practical items: a sports watch, a spa day. But later, he mentioned that he and my son had done a lot of research about a special gift for me. Curious, I checked our shared e-mail and discovered that he’d bought a $2,500 telescope. This is lovely, but I’m not interested in astronomy. I’d rather use the money for a scheduled home improvement. How do I tell him that his gift is generous but unwanted? (And should I do it now or later?) ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save the Packaging', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save the Packaging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b97ee573-0f04-5317-b365-8cf31272925d', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b97ee573-0f04-5317-b365-8cf31272925d'}, {'abstract': 'So the SAG Awards overlooked him? Now a Golden Globe nominee, Albert Brooks takes to Twitter in response.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/take-that-sag-awards/', 'snippet': 'So the SAG Awards overlooked him? Now a Golden Globe nominee, Albert Brooks takes to Twitter in response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier, Albert Brooks, a Golden Globe nominee for his role in “Drive,” told the Bagger’s colleague Paula Schwartz that he did not consider the nod vindication for being overlooked by the SAG Awards yesterday. “Listen, I don’t do that,” he said. “If you start this whole thing as the barometer of your existence you’re doomed to fail.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Take That, SAG Awards', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Albert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b47bd8d8-c1cd-5468-aa98-62cfb019f2a4', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b47bd8d8-c1cd-5468-aa98-62cfb019f2a4'}, {'abstract': 'Nokia earlier this year teamed up with Microsoft to ship handsets with the new Windows Phone 7 software. Now Nokia has teamed up with T-Mobile. Nokia and T-Mobile executives discussed the new Lumia 710 smartphone.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/qa-tmobile-nokia/', 'snippet': 'Nokia earlier this year teamed up with Microsoft to ship handsets with the new Windows Phone 7 software. Now Nokia has teamed up with T-Mobile. Nokia and T-Mobile executives discussed the new Lumia 710 smartphone.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The struggling phone maker Nokia announced on Thursday that it had teamed up with T-Mobile USA to offer a new phone running Microsoft’s Windows Phone 7 software. Landing in stores Jan. 11, the Lumia 710 will cost $50 with a two-year contract on T-Mobile, with rates starting at $50 a month. Chris Weber, president of Nokia Americas, and Andrew Sherrard, senior vice president of marketing for T-Mobile USA, discussed the strategy behind the phone in an interview. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q.&A.: Nokia and T-Mobile Executives Talk About Windows Phone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33641fdf-7717-5429-8119-9e6e31fdf1ce', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33641fdf-7717-5429-8119-9e6e31fdf1ce'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike at other Occupy sites, the Frankfurt protesters are being careful to make their points without inciting police interference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/business/global/at-occupy-frankfurt-calm-anarchy-has-staying-power.html', 'snippet': 'Unlike at other Occupy sites, the Frankfurt protesters are being careful to make their points without inciting police interference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The Frankfurt version of the Occupy Wall Street movement has many of the trappings of the New York City original, including a tattered cluster of tents, a location close to the beating heart of financial power and a diverse group of activists trying to come up with a unifying demand.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/business/global/16occupy/16occupy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/business/global/16occupy/16occupy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/business/global/16occupy/16occupy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/business/global/16occupy/16occupy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/business/global/16occupy/16occupy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Occupy Frankfurt, Calm Anarchy Has Staying Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Clashes Mar the Calm of Occupy Frankfurt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2dfcfc9-959c-5864-b338-1a73d50a4cea', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2dfcfc9-959c-5864-b338-1a73d50a4cea'}, {'abstract': 'Officials conducted a modest ceremony in Baghdad days before the last troops’ exit, which will end the United States’ most ambitious and bloodiest military campaign since Vietnam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/end-for-us-begins-period-of-uncertainty-for-iraqis.html', 'snippet': 'Officials conducted a modest ceremony in Baghdad days before the last troops’ exit, which will end the United States’ most ambitious and bloodiest military campaign since Vietnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — At a crowded market in the city center here, the flotsam of the war is for sale. Ripped Fuel workout supplement. Ready-to-eat meals, macaroni and cheese “Mexican style.” Pistol holsters. Nothing seems off limits to the merchants out for a quick dinar, not even a bottle of prescription pills from a pharmacy in Waco, Tex., probably tossed out by a departing soldier.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/POSTWAR/POSTWAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/POSTWAR/POSTWAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/POSTWAR/POSTWAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/POSTWAR/POSTWAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/POSTWAR/POSTWAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Marks End to 9-Year War, Leaving an Uncertain Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Marks End to a Long War for an Uncertain Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'maj