aph': 'Iran escalated its confrontation with the United States on Thursday over the captured American spy drone launched from Afghanistan, warning the Afghan government to order a halt to such surveillance flights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop U.S. Drone Flights, Iran Warns Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stop U.S. Drone Flights, Iran Warns Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salehi, Ali Akbar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8d58ad8-6579-567b-a3c6-dc8bb8edad9d', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8d58ad8-6579-567b-a3c6-dc8bb8edad9d'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate the 220th anniversary of the First Amendment, the campaign 1 for All is offering scholarships to students who sent Twitter messages about the First Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/tweeting-your-way-to-a-scholarship/', 'snippet': 'To celebrate the 220th anniversary of the First Amendment, the campaign 1 for All is offering scholarships to students who sent Twitter messages about the First Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many aspiring college students, getting a scholarship requires endless Googling, scrounging letters of recommendation and, of course, writing essays. Or, there is Twitter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tweeting Your Way to a Scholarship', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Amendment Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newseum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f61f3a6-a798-54ad-b9d4-e8dff92b2c31', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f61f3a6-a798-54ad-b9d4-e8dff92b2c31'}, {'abstract': 'Our two favorite entries from the second installment of our Reading Club, on the topic of sex education.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/how-should-schools-teach-about-sex-students-have-their-say/', 'snippet': 'Our two favorite entries from the second installment of our Reading Club, on the topic of sex education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second installment of our Reading Club, we chose the New York Times Magazine article “Teaching Good Sex” by Laurie Abraham, which profiled Al Vernacchio and his novel approach to teaching about human sexuality. We invited students to read the lengthy article and participate in a conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Should Schools Teach About Sex? Students Have Their Say', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:46:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288dfcde-e1e1-5f82-8d7e-9223b23e5cea', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288dfcde-e1e1-5f82-8d7e-9223b23e5cea'}, {'abstract': 'Some polling data this week suggests that Newt Gingrich’s momentum has stopped, and probably reversed itself, particularly in Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/gingrich-momentum-slows-polls-suggest/', 'snippet': 'Some polling data this week suggests that Newt Gingrich’s momentum has stopped, and probably reversed itself, particularly in Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of bad habits when analyzing general election polls can be good ones when it comes to primaries and caucuses. In particular, making inferences about a trend based on just a couple of polls will often lead you astray in the general election. As I wrote about on Tuesday, however, this is probably the lesser of evils when it comes to primaries. Voter preferences can change fast in primaries, and although the polls may or may not track them as accurately as we might like, in the long run you will benefit from being aggressive about trying to discern who has the momentum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Momentum Slows, Polls Suggest', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T19:47:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c51ad7ef-8c8b-5ac2-b181-b72961d85438', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c51ad7ef-8c8b-5ac2-b181-b72961d85438'}, {'abstract': 'Designated fighters were not always part of the picture in professional hockey.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/how-fighting-became-so-ferocious/', 'snippet': 'Designated fighters were not always part of the picture in professional hockey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although fighting has always been accepted in North American hockey and permitted under the N.H.L.’s rules, the role of fighters and the process of dropping the gloves have changed dramatically. In the old days, superstars fought their own battles. Today, there are players with marginal skills and little talent who engage in staged fights that have absolutely nothing to do with the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Fighting Became So Ferocious', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helmets', 'rank': 