ate': '2011-12-15T20:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/81236a3a-ed8d-5741-9104-a3c72fce0c5b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/81236a3a-ed8d-5741-9104-a3c72fce0c5b'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities are investigating a report that a man said to be an armed robber boarded a public bus that was headed to New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/bus-may-have-been-a-getaway-vehicle-the-police-say/', 'snippet': 'The authorities are investigating a report that a man said to be an armed robber boarded a public bus that was headed to New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The authorities are investigating whether an armed robber used a public bus bound for New Jersey as his getaway vehicle after pulling a heist in Upper Manhattan on Thursday, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bus May Have Been a Getaway Vehicle, the Police Say', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39b5376b-569b-5434-806d-9c53dca638e9', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39b5376b-569b-5434-806d-9c53dca638e9'}, {'abstract': 'The simple matter of what to do about a collapsing bridge at the Temple Mount has become yet another reason for Jews and Muslims to quarrel.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/no-water-under-this-bridge/', 'snippet': 'The simple matter of what to do about a collapsing bridge at the Temple Mount has become yet another reason for Jews and Muslims to quarrel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — In most well-managed cities, when a bridge is said to be putting the public at risk, it is closed without controversy until it can be made safe again. Not so in Jerusalem. In most well-managed holy sites, worshipers place a high priority on their safety and won’t stand for shoddy infrastructure. Not so in Jerusalem. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Water Under This Bridge', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temple Mount (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3203bcad-e8a4-5620-bef7-106b671670cb', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3203bcad-e8a4-5620-bef7-106b671670cb'}, {'abstract': 'Russell Brand, the irrepressible and occasionally scandalized British actor, comedian and memoirist, will host a series of six late-night specials for the FX cable network next year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/watch-out-america-russell-brand-is-coming-to-fx/', 'snippet': 'Russell Brand, the irrepressible and occasionally scandalized British actor, comedian and memoirist, will host a series of six late-night specials for the FX cable network next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having risen and fallen and risen again a few times already on the British airwaves, Russell Brand now finds himself in ascendance on American television, where he’ll host a series of late-night specials for the FX cable network next year, FX announced on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch Out, America: Russell Brand is Coming to FX', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Russell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:35:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18da419d-cabe-560e-b1dc-c72e6b07bef7', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18da419d-cabe-560e-b1dc-c72e6b07bef7'}, {'abstract': 'With festivities unfolding in plazas, parks and other public places, travelers are free to join right in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/travel/six-christmas-traditions-from-around-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'With festivities unfolding in plazas, parks and other public places, travelers are free to join right in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christmas trees, Santa Claus and gingerbread lattes are all well and good. But with the homogenizing creep of Yuletide customs, travelers might well worry they’ll go to the trouble of getting somewhere new over the holidays only to find it’s just like everywhere else. Not the six places here. Each has its own way of celebrating Christmas, and with the festivities unfolding in plazas, parks and other public places, travelers are free to join right in.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Christmas Traditions From Around the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Your Mall Santa: Christmas Worldwide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Margolies', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Margolies', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2230c76-b105-5160-8afb-5ec4f7ef1d21', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2230c76-b105-5160-8afb-5ec4f7ef1d21'}, {'abstract': 'In Barcelona there are no candy canes or Santas but, instead, a Royal Mailman and wise men on a ship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALANXMAS.html', 'snippet': 'In Barcelona there are no candy canes or Santas but, instead, a Royal Mailman and wise men on a ship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Barcelona there are no candy canes or Santas but, instead, a Royal Mailman and wise men on a ship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I/18CATALANXMAS-slide-YN1I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christmas in Catalonia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7eece647-62c1-5ab9-a728-5312df0b9dbd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7eece647-62c1-5ab9-a728-5312df0b9dbd'}, {'abstract': 'A video of Yulia Tymoshenko lying in a prison bed has drawn fire after it was shown on national television.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/video-shows-ukrainian-opposition-leader-in-prison/', 'snippet': 'A video of Yulia Tymoshenko lying in a prison bed has drawn fire after it was shown on national television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A video of the jailed Ukrainian opposition leader Yulia V. Tymoshenko lying in a prison bed has drawn fire from her lawyer after it was shown on national television and posted on the Internet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Ukrainian Opposition Leader in Prison', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:41:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d4daf1-f467-5d26-b657-20b2cc50a1d8', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d4daf1-f467-5d26-b657-20b2cc50a1d8'}, {'abstract': 'In Barcelona, there are no candy canes, tinsel or red-nosed reindeer. Instead, you’ll find a Royal Mailman and wise men on a ship. Not to mention a brisk swim in the Mediterranean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/travel/a-catalan-christmas.html', 'snippet': 'In Barcelona, there are no candy canes, tinsel or red-nosed reindeer. Instead, you’ll find a Royal Mailman and wise men on a ship. Not to mention a brisk swim in the Mediterranean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was the Christmas season in Barcelona, but inside the city hall, a 14th-century palace, a scene from “the Arabian Nights” was playing out. Palm trees and satin cushions had turned the Gothic patio into a desert tent, complete with incense and Middle Eastern music. Pages, clad in pantaloons and velvet-trimmed turbans, led each child to the Moorish throne of the Royal Mailman and the bulging satchel he would use to convey their petitions to the Three Kings. Yes, those Three Kings: the magi in the manger with the frankincense and myrrh. Here in the Mediterranean, the North Pole and the jolly guy in the fur-trimmed suit don’t make much cultural sense. And you have to admit that there’s a certain biblical logic to having the Kings rather than Santa bear gifts.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALAN_SPAN/18CATALAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALAN_SPAN/18CATALAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALAN_SPAN/18CATALAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALAN_SPAN/18CATALAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/travel/18CATALAN_SPAN/18CATALAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Catalan Christmas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Catalan Christmas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:43:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Abend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c43e3a32-f7b1-57ab-af21-5b1c04de4b35', 'word_count': 2462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c43e3a32-f7b1-57ab-af21-5b1c04de4b35'}, {'abstract': '“The Iron Lady” and “Albert Nobbs” hold their premieres on the same night, and the Carpetbagger compares and contrasts.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/thatcher-vs-nobbs-round-2-dueling-premieres/', 'snippet': '“The Iron Lady” and “Albert Nobbs” hold their premieres on the same night, and the Carpetbagger compares and contrasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you following the battle of the blondes royale between “Albert Nobbs” and “The Iron Lady?” There was a moment when Lady Ironsides had pulled out ahead, on account of a glamorous Vogue cover, but the Bagger will have to give the latest edge to Nobbsy. Both vehicles – the Meryl Streep film in which she plays Margaret Thatcher, and the Glenn Close passion project in which she plays a male butler in Victorian Dublin – had screenings and glitzy afterparties on Tuesday night. As promised, the Bagger showed at both events. But it was the “Albert Nobbs” affair we returned to, and not just because Lou Reed and Patti Smith were there to watch Sinead O’Connor perform barefoot. More on that later, promise!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thatcher vs. Nobbs, Round 2: Dueling Premieres', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, Glenn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Phyllida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Abi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Lou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a2ed961-0400-56c2-90cc-13819f78441e', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a2ed961-0400-56c2-90cc-13819f78441e'}, {'abstract': 'Chase has adopted a simplified checking account disclosure form.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/chase-adopts-simplified-checking-disclosure/', 'snippet': 'Chase has adopted a simplified checking account disclosure form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chase has become the first big bank to voluntarily adopt a simplified, plain-language checking account disclosure, as proposed by an arm of the nonprofit group Pew Charitable Trusts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chase Adopts Simplified Checking Disclosure', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T20:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e25d81e8-9da5-5e06-aedb-c214eb5c9112', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e25d81e8-9da5-5e06-aedb-c214eb5c9112'}, {'abstract': 'Corporations had argued that state regulations require them only to address significant environmental threats, not do a complete cleanup.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/on-our-radar-superfund-cleanups-in-n-y/', 'snippet': 'Corporations had argued that state regulations require them only to address significant environmental threats, not do a complete cleanup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A court rules that New York State can require companies to return state-designated Superfund sites to the condition in which they existed before they were used for industrial purposes — not simply remove the pollution that poses risks. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar:  Superfund Cleanups in N.Y.', 'kicker':