s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH much of the Island built out, single-family homes aren’t likely to be knocked from their pre-eminent position. But new rental and for-sale communities are increasingly being built in clusters: attached town houses, semi-attached houses and condominium and rental units in town-house-style complexes. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIZONE_SPAN/18LIZONE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIZONE_SPAN/18LIZONE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIZONE_SPAN/lizone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIZONE_SPAN/18LIZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIZONE_SPAN/18LIZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Abandoning the Single Life', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abandoning the Single Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T23:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcelle S. Fischler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcelle', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fischler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d68f140-7cf8-5b95-9a3a-77a97ce58372', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d68f140-7cf8-5b95-9a3a-77a97ce58372'}, {'abstract': 'Convinced it is the wrong time to own a home, Dara and Michael Kass decided to sell their co-op in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and move to a brownstone rental.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/realestate/the-hunt-a-holding-pattern-home.html', 'snippet': 'Convinced it is the wrong time to own a home, Dara and Michael Kass decided to sell their co-op in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and move to a brownstone rental.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DARA KASS grew up in Sheepshead Bay, Brooklyn, in an attached two-family house. (Her grandparents lived downstairs.) Her husband, Michael, grew up in doorman buildings on the Upper West Side. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18HUNT4_395/18HUNT4_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 991, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18HUNT4_395/18HUNT4_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18HUNT4_395/18HUNT4_395-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Holding-Pattern Home', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Holding-Pattern Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brownstones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T23:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44512f88-7568-5ed9-9fa2-572705b45fa8', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44512f88-7568-5ed9-9fa2-572705b45fa8'}, {'abstract': 'The marvel of this American Ballet Theater version of “The Nutcracker,” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, lies in its vision of adults as the transformed potential future of the children who carry the story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/arts/dance/alexei-ratmanskys-nutcracker-at-bam-review.html', 'snippet': 'The marvel of this American Ballet Theater version of “The Nutcracker,” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, lies in its vision of adults as the transformed potential future of the children who carry the story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since “The Nutcracker” in all its many versions is always a tale of transformation, there’s a well-established tradition of making its little heroine grow up to become the adult heroine who dances the Sugar Plum pas de deux. Usually, though, this involves a grown-up dancer playing the little girl in the party of the first scene, which means that, right at the start, we have to suspend disbelief. The central marvel of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Nutcracker” — new last year and returning now to American Ballet Theater repertory at the Brooklyn Academy of Music — lies in its vision of adults as the transformed potential future of the children who carry the story. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What if You Could Meet Yourself as an Adult? These Children Do', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What if You Could Meet Yourself as an Adult? These Children Do', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-15T23:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'l