_paragraph': 'What makes Tom Cruise run — run harder and run faster, leaping from one building and dangling off another, the world’s tallest — as he does to exhausting, unnerving effect in “Mission: Impossible — Ghost Protocol,” his latest exercise in extreme performance? The fourth in the franchise, this “Mission” has a solid cast, including a notable new co-star in Jeremy Renner; a new director, Brad Bird; and a story that’s as nonsensical as any in the series. Mostly, though, it has Mr. Cruise hurtling through the movie as if his life depended on it, which, to judge by the hard line of his jaw, his punishingly fit body and the will etched into his every movement, may be what’s at stake.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16MISSION_SPAN/JPMISSION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16MISSION_SPAN/JPMISSION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16MISSION_SPAN/JPMISSION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16MISSION_SPAN/JPMISSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16MISSION_SPAN/JPMISSION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Off Skyscrapers Sometimes Hurts a Bit', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Mission: Impossible — Ghost Protocol'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling Off Skyscrapers Sometimes Hurts a Bit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bird, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruise, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Renner, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monaghan, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pegg, Simon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/798166e8-9fa3-50f7-8b9c-bddcd6303f17', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/798166e8-9fa3-50f7-8b9c-bddcd6303f17'}, {'abstract': 'Complaints from companies have led to curbs on short-selling in both the United States and Europe, but evidence is lacking that the practice is harmful to the market — and it may help investors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/business/questioning-the-evil-of-short-sales-high-low-finance.html', 'snippet': 'Complaints from companies have led to curbs on short-selling in both the United States and Europe, but evidence is lacking that the practice is harmful to the market — and it may help investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blame the shorts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/n