lead_paragraph': 'Teenagers with itchy typing fingers are shooting out text messages more than any other demographic in the United States, and as a result they’re talking on the phone a lot less, too, according to a survey by Nielsen, the media research firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cellphones Are the New Junk Food', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a328276-f8af-54fe-9a97-d0d7d4db0d47', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a328276-f8af-54fe-9a97-d0d7d4db0d47'}, {'abstract': 'The Chipmunks go on a cruise that ends badly (with the Chipettes along for the ride).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/movies/alvin-and-the-chipmunks-chipwrecked-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Chipmunks go on a cruise that ends badly (with the Chipettes along for the ride).', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is chipmunk gambling. There is seductive dancing by Chipettes wearing only towels. There is a musical gag involving the lyric “whip my tail back and forth.” How “Alvin and the Chipmunks: Chipwrecked” ended up with only a G rating is a mystery.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_ALVIN/FILM-ROUNDUP-ALVIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_ALVIN/FILM-ROUNDUP-ALVIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_ALVIN/FILM-ROUNDUP-ALVIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_ALVIN/FILM-ROUNDUP-ALVIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_ALVIN/FILM-ROUNDUP-ALVIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shipwrecked, and Landing New Personalities', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Alvin and the Chipmunks: Chipwrecked'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shipwrecked, and Landing New Personalities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:12:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d877a0f-33ac-5298-b524-13c6a467eedd', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d877a0f-33ac-5298-b524-13c6a467eedd'}, {'abstract': 'A hook-up and the ensuing anxiety permeate “The Pill,” directed by J. C. Khoury.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/movies/the-pill-directed-by-jc-khoury-review.html', 'snippet': 'A hook-up and the ensuing anxiety permeate “The Pill,” directed by J. C. Khoury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there anything more cloyingly irritating than watching young singles playing a drinking game? It’s the height of sophistication for those who think swapping swallows of booze is the pinnacle of human evolution, but for everyone else it’s just tedious.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_PILL/16RDP_PILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_PILL/16RDP_PILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_PILL/FILM-ROUNDUP-THE-PILL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_PILL/16RDP_PILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_PILL/16RDP_PILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juggling Two Women Is Never Easy', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Pill'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Juggling Two Women Is Never Easy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/43f7f618-af97-54c2-97aa-ce0de4c311f5', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43f7f618-af97-54c2-97aa-ce0de4c311f5'}, {'abstract': 'The British police say they raided a property and confiscated some computer equipment in pursuing their inquiry into the hijacking of e-mails between scientists.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/more-climategate-buzz/', 'snippet': 'The British police say they raided a property and confiscated some computer equipment in pursuing their inquiry into the hijacking of e-mails between scientists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blogosphere is abuzz with rumors that the British police investigation into the 2009 release of private e-mails between climate scientists has taken on new life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fresh Climategate Patter', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of East Anglia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ce42d2b-60de-5609-9ed6-9a9ccb5e3db6', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ce42d2b-60de-5609-9ed6-9a9ccb5e3db6'}, {'abstract': 'In “Cook County,” a family faces the perils of drug addiction and child care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/movies/cook-county-directed-by-david-pomes-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Cook County,” a family faces the perils of drug addiction and child care.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Cook County” opens on a shot of white powder and its maker, Bump (Anson Mount), informing his fellow addicts of the “public service” he’s providing. Flexing biceps no druggie deserves and drawing out his vowels with the deep-throated groan of a creaky barn door, Bump is one of the more despicable cinematic creations of recent years. Worshiping bong, crystals and powder equally, holed up in his isolated East Texas meth lab, he’s the epitome of backwoods sleaze and strung-out self-delusion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_C00K_COUNTY/16RDP_C00K-COUNTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_C00K_COUNTY/16RDP_C00K-COUNTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/arts/16RDP_C00K_COUNTY/FILM-ROUNDUP-C00K-COUNTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/art