, 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the first chill of winter descends on the Northeast and the traditional cold-weather codfish run starts in earnest, fishermen and scientists are again at odds, debating whether the once fantastically abundant North Atlantic codfish populations are finally rebuilding — or hurtling inextricably toward collapse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '43', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Whitefish’s Burden', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Whitefish’s Burden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tilapia (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cod (Fish)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:41:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/577421be-0805-5832-ad00-7f54b996f4c4', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/577421be-0805-5832-ad00-7f54b996f4c4'}, {'abstract': 'An expanded law against cockfighting in Texas now goes after the people who profit from it, the people who watch and the people who host the illegal activity on their property.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/us/texas-law-extends-its-reach-to-halt-cockfighting.html', 'snippet': 'An expanded law against cockfighting in Texas now goes after the people who profit from it, the people who watch and the people who host the illegal activity on their property.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lt. Joel Caldwell’s animal protection career began 12 years ago, when, as a deputy sheriff in Harris County, he responded to a call about a cat with an arrow through its body in a Houston trailer park.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '37A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/16TTCockfighting1/16TTCockfighting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/16/us/16TTCockfighting1/16TTCockfighting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/16TTCockfighting1/16TTCockfighting1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/us/16TTCockfighting1/16TTCockfighting1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/us/16TTCockfighting1/16TTCockfighting1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Extends Its Reach in Bid to Halt Cockfighting', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Law Extends Its Reach in Bid to Halt Cockfighting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cockfighting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T00:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section