0-7a4c-5187-8964-11bb7d38af0d', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa63d180-7a4c-5187-8964-11bb7d38af0d'}, {'abstract': 'A fuel subsidy proposal in the House, if passed, would enrich Nancy Pelosi because of her stake in a “green” firm that stands to benefit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/business/a-congressional-conflict-of-interest.html', 'snippet': 'A fuel subsidy proposal in the House, if passed, would enrich Nancy Pelosi because of her stake in a “green” firm that stands to benefit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine buying stock in a company and then being in position to help change the law to enhance its value. Welcome to the United States Congress. A fuel subsidy proposal, if passed, would enrich Representative Nancy Pelosi of California because of her stake in a “green” firm that stands to benefit. It’s the latest sign that Congressional trading rules are in desperate need of an overhaul.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/business/sub-VIEWS/sub-VIEWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/business/sub-VIEWS/sub-VIEWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/business/sub-VIEWS/sub-VIEWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Congressional Conflict of Interest', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Congressional Conflict of Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diamond Foods Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clean Energy Fuels Corporation', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T01:03:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Indiviglio and Jeffrey Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Indiviglio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/329c4cb0-ab6e-5b9e-8412-a4aafe186175', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/329c4cb0-ab6e-5b9e-8412-a4aafe186175'}, {'abstract': 'In a 49-page report, IndyCar said that the conditions that caused the accident Oct. 16 in which Dan Wheldon died were beyond any anticipated in tests before the final race of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/sports/autoracing/indycar-report-says-events-conspired-in-wheldons-fatal-crash.html', 'snippet': 'In a 49-page report, IndyCar said that the conditions that caused the accident Oct. 16 in which Dan Wheldon died were beyond any anticipated in tests before the final race of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IndyCar, still reeling from a disastrous end to its season, said Thursday that a “perfect storm” of events, many of them unforeseeable, led to the death of Dan Wheldon, one of the racing circuit’s most talented and popular drivers, two months ago at Las Vegas Motor Speedway.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/sports/indy/indy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/sports/indy/indy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/16/sports/indy/indy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Perfect Storm’ of Events Led to Wheldon’s Death, IndyCar Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Las Vegas Track Was Safe, IndyCar Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Motor Speedway', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheldon, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T01:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fc87599-afe0-58b8-b1a3-ead529d22696', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fc87599-afe0-58b8-b1a3-ead529d22696'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors filed a civil suit to punish American and Lebanese businesses the government says were behind a Hezbollah-controlled network that laundered cocaine proceeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/world/middleeast/us-sues-american-and-lebanese-businesses-it-says-helped-hezbollah-money-laundering.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors filed a civil suit to punish American and Lebanese businesses the government says were behind a Hezbollah-controlled network that laundered cocaine proceeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government on Thursday escalated its campaign to stanch the flow of what it says is dirty money to the Shiite militant group Hezbollah. Prosecutors filed a civil suit aimed at financially punishing American and Lebanese businesses that the government charges were behind a Hezbollah-controlled global network that laundered huge sums in South American cocaine proceeds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Sues Businesses It Says Helped Hezbollah', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Sues Businesses It Says Helped Hezbollah', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':