tesy of technology.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/15/please-stop-sharing/', 'snippet': 'High-level stupidity, there for the ages, courtesy of technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, there came from the dispiriting clutter of the nation’s capital an extraordinary tale of our times. It concerned aides to Representative Rick Larsen, Democrat of Washington, who broadcast via Twitter how cool it was to be sitting in the seat of power at midday while drinking Jack Daniel’s and watching Nirvana videos on the taxpayers’ dime.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Please Stop Sharing', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T01:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/974c0ab2-b1ea-51d3-bd1f-b01f9d43d239', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/974c0ab2-b1ea-51d3-bd1f-b01f9d43d239'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Greg Abbott finds himself in the position of defending redistricting maps that benefit his allies and punish his foes, all in the name of official state business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/us/a-lucky-attorney-general-and-redistricting.html', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Greg Abbott finds himself in the position of defending redistricting maps that benefit his allies and punish his foes, all in the name of official state business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the executive editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 