 of the World, was arrested Thursday as part of an investigation into illegal payments to the police by employees of Rupert Murdoch’s tabloid.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A 37-year-old woman was arrested on Thursday as part of an investigation into illegal payments to the police by employees of Rupert Murdoch’s News of the World tabloid, \xa0Scotland Yard said Thursday.\xa0The British news media reported that the woman was Lucy Panton, a former crime editor for the tabloid. A report in The Guardian newspaper suggested that Ms. Panton was married to a Scotland Yard detective, and a public register of meetings with police officers shows that she and the newspaper’s editor met with John Yates, a senior officer who subsequently resigned over links to The News of the World, in November 2009. A spokesman for the Metropolitan police declined to discuss the reports.\xa0The arrest is the seventh in the Scotland Yard inquiry into payments to officers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Arrest in Police Payoffs Inquiry', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Arrest in Police Payoffs Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Piers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yates, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T01:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byli