e, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/00gator_ss-slide-45QY/00gator_ss-slide-45QY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/00gator_ss-slide-45QY/00gator_ss-slide-45QY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/10/12/sports/00gator_ss-slide-45QY/00gator_ss-slide-45QY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mississippi Alligator Hunt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLIGATORS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T01:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c82ffeb5-44cd-5227-aaed-5bd326b2c43a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c82ffeb5-44cd-5227-aaed-5bd326b2c43a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama has caved in to political pressure and will sign a dangerous bill that will make indefinite detention and military trials part of American law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/opinion/politics-over-principle.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama has caved in to political pressure and will sign a dangerous bill that will make indefinite detention and military trials part of American law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trauma of Sept. 11, 2001, gave rise to a dangerous myth that, to be safe, America had to give up basic rights and restructure its legal system. The United States was now in a perpetual state of war, the argument went, and the criminal approach to fighting terrorism — and the due process that goes along with it — wasn’t tough enough.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics Over Principle', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politics Over Principle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T02:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1880e537-4b3c-5c98-9c94-27c57a42b2b2', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1880e537-4b3c-5c98-9c94-27c57a42b2b2'}, {'abstract': 'American troops, thankfully, are coming home. But, to build a stable democracy, Iraq will need help and goading for years to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/opinion/a-formal-end-to-the-iraq-war.html', 'snippet': 'American troops, thankfully, are coming home. But, to build a stable democracy, Iraq will need help and goading for years to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a relief that the American role in the misguided Iraq war is finally over. It came to an official close on Thursday with an appropriately subdued ceremony in Baghdad. We mourn the nearly 4,500 American troops and tens of thousands of Iraqis who lost their lives. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Formal End', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Formal End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T02:16:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f799d3-7f6d-5dbb-a615-b2cea43d229c', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f799d3-7f6d-5dbb-a615-b2cea43d229c'}, {'abstract': 'Janet L. Robinson, who served as chief executive of The New York Times Company during a time of rapid change and uncertainty in the newspaper industry, will step down this month.', 