847', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b02e790d-16fd-598d-a685-42bbb5867847'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times reporters examined candidates’ statements on Iran, immigration, the national debt and more, during the Republican presidential debate in Sioux City, Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/iowa-debate-fact-check/', 'snippet': 'New York Times reporters examined candidates’ statements on Iran, immigration, the national debt and more, during the Republican presidential debate in Sioux City, Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Obama and Debt', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa Debate Fact Check', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppel, Richard A Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shane, Scott', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PolitiFact.com', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T05:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1533a4c-9353-5ab9-b302-fe8d660a8c74', 'word_count': 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1533a4c-9353-5ab9-b302-fe8d660a8c74'}, {'abstract': 'What voters believe and how they form coalitions around candidates matter more than the ups and downs of any individual politician.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/behind-the-primaries/', 'snippet': 'What voters believe and how they form coalitions around candidates matter more than the ups and downs of any individual politician.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most national candidates, and too many political commentators, miss the mini-primaries that lead up to the real events. In coalition parties, which the Democrats have been since F.D.R. and the Republicans have been since Nixon, campaigns are formed by creating personal coalitions around the various candidates. And for grassroots campaigns, of the sort I constructed for myself in 1983-84, it is even more basic than that. It is about finding key people in key primary states who combine a high reputation, organizational skill and a network of political contacts to form a campaign nucleus around which the rest of the state can be organized. I was once asked how many people I needed to win New Hampshire and I said, “Six.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Primaries', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hart, Gary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Jesse L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mondale, Walter F', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T05:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Hart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d101c1-7ad7-59ab-b735-01a03de6923f', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d101c1-7ad7-59ab-b735-01a03de6923f'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 50 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/word-of-the-day-inured/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 50 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'inured •\\i-ˈnurd, -ˈnyurd\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | inured', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T05:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28cf6df5-b783-5d84-b336-8b25647d449b', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28cf6df5-b783-5d84-b336-8b25647d449b'}, {'abstract': 'NYT Front Page for 12/16/2011', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/12/16/multimedia/16frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT Front Page for 12/16/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT Front Page for 12/16/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT Front Page for 12/16/2011', 'kicker