llo-global-management-to-buy-chemicals-business-for-1-4-billion/', 'snippet': 'Apollo Global Management agreed on Friday to buy the Belgian chemicals company Taminco from a rival private equity firm, CVC Capital Partners, for $1.4 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Apollo Global Management agreed on Friday to buy Taminco, a Belgian chemicals company, from a rival private equity firm, CVC Capital Partners, for $1.4 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apollo Global Management to Buy Chemicals Business for $1.4 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CVC Capital Partners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T11:16:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b1bc099-fb1e-549a-9fef-7643895e90ac', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b1bc099-fb1e-549a-9fef-7643895e90ac'}, {'abstract': 'As the labor force has watched certain sectors grow fat on rising commodity prices and booming domestic demand, it is pushing for a greater share of company profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/business/global/as-indonesia-grows-discontent-sets-in-among-workers.html', 'snippet': 'As the labor force has watched certain sectors grow fat on rising commodity prices and booming domestic demand, it is pushing for a greater share of company profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA — As a flare-red sun set, a group of laborers in their 20s and 30s gathered on the bare floor of a battered house wedged beneath power lines in an industrial part of Jakarta. They were members of a confederation of multi- sector workers, one of the largest trade unions in Indonesia, whose slogan is “Young, brave, militant.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928/17rupiah-image2-1324050030928-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Indonesia Grows, Discontent Sets in Among Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Indonesia Grows, Discontent Sets in Among Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freeport McMoRan Copper & Gold Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T11:37:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Schonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94717315-6abe-51b1-be19-241879b9890b', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94717315-6abe-51b1-be19-241879b9890b'}, {'abstract': 'United Rentals agreed to pay $18 a share for its fellow rental equipment provider, in a bet on strong industrial activity and an upswing in construction projects.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/united-rentals-to-buy-rsc-holdings-for-1-87-billion/', 'snippet': 'United Rentals agreed to pay $18 a share for its fellow rental equipment provider, in a bet on strong industrial activity and an upswing in construction projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'United Rentals agreed on Friday to buy RSC Holdings for about $1.87 billion in cash and stock, seeking to combine two of the country’s big rental equipment providers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'United Rentals to Buy RSC Holdings for $1.87 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Rentals Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T11:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9233c56-c7a8-526f-993c-814c7038e72b', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9233c56-c7a8-526f-993c-814c7038e72b'}, {'abstract': 'Each woman stepped in after her father’s death and remade aspects of the business, often taking steps that their fathers never would have  considered — or endorsed.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/this-is-not-your-fathers-company/', 'snippet': 'Each woman stepped in after her father’s death and remade aspects of the business, often taking steps that their fathers never would have  considered — or endorsed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most family businesses don’t survive beyond the founder’s generation. Bari Jay, in its second generation, and Johnson Security Bureau, in its third, are two exceptions. Both companies are thriving largely because of the efforts of two of our business group members, Susan Parker and Jessica Johnson, respectively. Each woman stepped in after her father’s death, and remade aspects of the business, often taking steps that their fathers never would have\xa0 considered — or endorsed. During our latest meeting of the group, Ms. Johnson and Ms. Parker talked about what their fathers might think if they were to see how things run today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is Not Your Father’s Company', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jessica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T12:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4d74b8d-b9be-5d61-ab08-6a08a45d6c9a', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': '