, 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Call for Parent Power. Real Power.', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T13:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e7e93d-08a2-52b2-8873-57fb32857a7b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e7e93d-08a2-52b2-8873-57fb32857a7b'}, {'abstract': 'The designer went down memory lane, revisiting some of her label’s most iconic shapes and cuts for this collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/just-one-look-diane-von-furstenberg/', 'snippet': 'The designer went down memory lane, revisiting some of her label’s most iconic shapes and cuts for this collection.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I think the thing about pre-fall is that it’s all great pieces,” says the designer Diane von Furstenberg about how she revisited some of her label’s most iconic shapes and cuts for this collection. “You love them and they stay your friend forever.” Memory lane took von Furstenberg to the wrap dress print archives (which translated to punky gingham skirts and jackets, with thoughtful details on things like the interior linings) and vibrant solids (like this color-blocked lime robe coat and burnished bouclé skirt). “I love pieces; even a dress is a piece.” Another great piece? A pony-hair spotted patent leather duck boot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Diane von Furstenberg', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T13:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1284aee-8efb-596f-bee4-c5075bfd5c5a', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1284aee-8efb-596f-bee4-c5075bfd5c5a'}, {'abstract': 'In the wake of the MF Global bankruptcy, Bart Chilton, a Democratic member of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, is calling on Congress to bar brokerage firms from investing customer money altogether, except in United States Treasury securities, which offer the government’s seal of approval.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/regulator-wants-to-curb-use-of-customer-cash/', 'snippet': 'In the wake of the MF Global bankruptcy, Bart Chilton, a Democratic member of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, is calling on Congress to bar brokerage firms from investing customer money altogether, except in United States Treasury securi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission recently reined in the brokerage industry’s risky investments with customer money, a crackdown that followed the collapse of MF Global and the firm’s misuse of roughly $1 billion in client money. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulator Wants to Curb Use of Customer Cash', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major':