 Zynga will fare quite well when the gaming company starts trading on Friday. The offering, which raised $1 billion, values the company at $7 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zynga’s initial public offering didn’t quite hit the $20 billion valuation widely expected earlier this year, but don’t pity Mark Pincus. The chief executive and other owners have done quite well. At $10 per share, Friday’s offering values Zynga at $7 billion — not shabby for a four-year-old company that sells digital livestock and emerald ponies. Here’s a look at the early investors and their Zynga holdings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sowing Zynga’s Riches', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Reid Garrett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pincus, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Natta, Owen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T14:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/522eb5db-dc74-57ed-82f4-d0781f210fc2', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/522eb5db-dc74-57ed-82f4-d0781f210fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Facing the threat of extradition to Sweden to be questioned on sexual assault charges, Julian Assange, the founde