rmer UBS trader charged with fraud and false accounting, has dumped his law firm days before his next court hearing where he was expected to enter a plea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Kweku M. Adoboli, the former UBS trader charged with fraud and false accounting, has dumped his law firm days before his next court hearing where he was expected to enter a plea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trader in UBS Scandal Drops His Lawyer', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adoboli, Kweku M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS A.G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T15:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5f0b50a-e390-5f75-9368-b81893c7a217', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5f0b50a-e390-5f75-9368-b81893c7a217'}, {'abstract': 'Priced out of private preschools and unable to place their children in public ones, many middle-class New York parents are forming their own co-ops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/nyregion/underground-pre-k-groups-often-illegal-abound-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Priced out of private preschools and unable to place their children in public ones, many middle-class New York parents are forming their own co-ops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 6 p.m. on a Friday in early June, and my children’s dinnertime coincided with the moment the New York City Department of Education posted acceptance letters online for 4-year-o