 a club called the Gay Straight Alliance. For a while, it operated in comfortable obscurity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/us/17religion3/17religion3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 691, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/us/17religion3/17religion3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/us/17religion3/17religion3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waging a One-Man War on American Muslims', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Waging a One-Man War on American Muslims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Poverty Law Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thornton, Barbara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Family Assn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T15:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1287def-d398-5462-baf8-47f213aa72bb', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1287def-d398-5462-baf8-47f213aa72bb'}, {'abstract': 'The potential to reach the nearly 50 million Latinos in the United States was a driving force for advertisers trying to extend their reach to an expanding audience.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/the-year-in-media-advertisers-and-marketers-make-a-multicultural-pitch/', 'snippet': 'The potential to reach the nearly 50 million Latinos in the United States was a driving force for advertisers trying to extend their reach to an expanding audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staff members of The Times’s media news department are highlighting the most significant developments this year in the industries they cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | Making a Multicultural Pitch', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TELEMUNDO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T15:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a3e8fc-981b-5f28-85de-f3d1760697bf', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a3e8fc-981b-5f28-85de-f3d1760697bf'}, {'abstract': 'As artworks get bigger and shinier, and spectacle grabs the spotlight at museum’s contemporary-art shows, substance is still venerated in the New York art world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/design/in-the-new-york-art-scene-spectacle-and-substance-both-wow.html', 'snippet': 'As artworks get bigger and shinier, and spectacle grabs the spotlight at museum’s contemporary-art shows, substance is still venerated in the New York art world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU can complain all you want about the art-world money-go-round and the celebrity circus spinning in its widening gyre. Prices are up; so are mentions of Art Basel Miami on Page Six. Artworks seem only to get bigger and shinier, and spectacle — participatory or not — is becoming the new normal at museum exhibitions of contemporary art. Note the record crowds lining up to gawk at Maurizio Cattelan’s career immolation at the Guggenheim or whiz down Carsten Höller’s tubular slide at the New Museum.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RSMITH1/18RSMITH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RSMITH1/18RSMITH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18RSMITH1/18RSMITH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Substance and Spectacle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Substance And Spectacle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T16:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73685e6-6ea3-56cb-bb1a-a7088c012871', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73685e6-6ea3-56cb-bb1a-a7088c012871'}, {'abstract': 'Museums in New York City offered some potent fare this year, and at least two museums with national interest opened in 2011, but many gallery shows were dull, all about cash and caution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/design/strong-showing-at-museums-while-galleries-seemed-complacent.html', 'snippet': 'Museums in New York City offered some potent fare this year, and at least two museums with national interest opened in 2011, but many gallery shows were dull, all about cash and caution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE was a lot of painting on view in Zuccotti Park this fall, in the form of Occupy Wall Street protest posters, free for the taking. And there was a lot of painting on the walls of New York art galleries, most of it post-M.F.A. eye candy with hefty price tags. The physical distance between Lower Manhattan and the Chelsea art zone is short, but the mental and moral gap felt immeasurable. The park was about light-on-its-feet, change-the-game politics. Chelsea — leaden and inbred — was about cash and caution.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18COTTER1/18COTTER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18COTTER1/18COTTER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18COTTER1/18COTTER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Complacency Butts Up Against Game Changers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Complacency Butts Up Against Game Changers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T16:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7868b7-ed5f-51b6-be95-90c628fcd846', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7868b7-ed5f-51b6-be95-90c628fcd846'}, {'abstract': 'Children’s books about remarkable journeys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/18/books/review/18bookshelf-voyages.html', 'snippet': 'Children’s books about remarkable journeys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children’s books about remarkable journeys.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/books/review/18bookshelf-voyages-slide-3RNR/18bookshelf-voyages-slide-3RNR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subTyp