e', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manuscripts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Heritage Memorial Fund', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T16:31:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/933e2396-5dbc-5f51-9dfe-a7846021a402', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/933e2396-5dbc-5f51-9dfe-a7846021a402'}, {'abstract': 'Jan Benzel, an editor at The Times who wrote the New York Send-Off series on City Room last year as she prepared to depart for an assignment in Paris, reports that yoga is enjoying something of a boomlet, at least in part thanks to New York,', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/the-latest-in-yoga-from-paris/', 'snippet': 'Jan Benzel, an editor at The Times who wrote the New York Send-Off series on City Room last year as she prepared to depart for an assignment in Paris, reports that yoga is enjoying something of a boomlet, at least in part thanks to New York,', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris may have it all over New York for croissants, bike-sharing and availability of unfiltered cigarettes, but yoga classes? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Latest in Yoga, From Paris', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benzel, Jan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T16:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ea03fb1-c1d2-5fb6-81d3-8d6e9daede03', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ea03fb1-c1d2-5fb6-81d3-8d6e9daede03'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times reporter Charles McGrath describes what it was like to interview a terminally ill Christopher Hitchens in his hospital room, only months before Hitchens’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/spending-an-afternoon-in-christopher-hitchenss-hospital-room-turned-office/', 'snippet': 'New York Times reporter Charles McGrath describes what it was like to interview a terminally ill Christopher Hitchens in his hospital room, only months before Hitchens’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In October I flew to Houston to interview Christopher Hitchens in his hospital room at the MD Anderson Cancer Center. When he greeted me his shirt was open and, I couldn’t help noticing, there was a plastic tube sticking out of his chest. Hitchens, who died on Thursday at the age of 62, was matter of fact about it, as he was about everything having to do with his illness. Cancer was an inconvenience, he gave me to understand — big inconvenience, probably a terminal one — but it wasn’t going to keep him from doing what he loved most, which was to write.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spending An Afternoon in Christopher Hitchens’s Hospital-Room-Turned-Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, '