09. The number of workers quitting their jobs — a sign of confidence that they can do better elsewhere — has also risen. The number of job openings relative to the number of unemployed workers is down from the peak, but remains far above prerecession levels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Charts: Few Are Fired, or Hired', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T17:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fa87fd6b-0da7-5c90-a935-c4c07383a50f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fa87fd6b-0da7-5c90-a935-c4c07383a50f'}, {'abstract': 'Gia Kourlas revisits some of the more memorable performances from the past year: thrilling dancing that wasn’t limited to the ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/dance/american-ballet-theaters-new-generation-comes-into-focus.html', 'snippet': 'Gia Kourlas revisits some of the more memorable performances from the past year: thrilling dancing that wasn’t limited to the ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE evening at a performance by American Ballet Theater at City Center this fall, the dancers took their places. But as the curtain rose on Twyla Tharp’s “In the Upper Room,” the fog\xa0— part of what gives this galvanic work its heavenly setting — was thick enough to create white-out conditions. Still, within the haze was a body that danced like a ribbon.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOURLAS/18KOURLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 759, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOURLAS/18KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOURLAS/18KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Generation Comes Into Focus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Generation Comes Into Focus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dance Theater Workshop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T17:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfb3343-007c-5f5f-b088-b85d44599c84', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfb3343-007c-5f5f-b088-b85d44599c84'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Sarah Michelson and the New York City Players’ Richard Maxwell joined forces to create “Devotion.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/dance/devotion-a-moment-to-remember-in-dance.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Sarah Michelson and the New York City Players’ Richard Maxwell joined forces to create “Devotion.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S been almost a year since I saw Sarah Michelson’s “Devotion” at the Kitchen in January. But her searing dance, a collaboration with the New York City Players’ artistic director Richard Maxwell, shines more brightly in my mind than most of the work I’ve seen since. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18LAROCCO_SPAN/18LAROCCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18LAROCCO_SPAN/18LAROCCO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18LAROCCO_SPAN/18LAROCCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18LAROCCO_SPAN/18LAROCCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18LAROCCO_SPAN/18LAROCCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Moments to Cherish, Filled With Discovery And Somber Farewell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moments to Cherish, Filled With Discovery And Somber Farewell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maxwell, Richard (1967- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Players', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michelson, Sarah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T17:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'l