nd hyper-partisanship and Washington dysfunction: Vote Bloomberg-Petraeus in 2012! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Clears Path for a Third-Party Ticket', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Moves (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans Elect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T17:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard W. Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f93b2f58-ed21-50b9-802e-0ba79fd9f212', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f93b2f58-ed21-50b9-802e-0ba79fd9f212'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a libertarian, go for Ron Paul. If you like science fiction, go for Newt Gingrich.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/beyond-eeny-meeny-miny-moe-sorting-out-the-g-o-p-field/', 'snippet': 'If you’re a libertarian, go for Ron Paul. If you like science fiction, go for Newt Gingrich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I woke up this morning feeling grateful not to be an Iowa Republican. If I were, I’d feel obligated to participate in the caucuses on Jan. 3, a truly depressing prospect. The contenders for the G.O.P. nomination – seven of them now that Herman Cain self-immolated – have given speeches, schmoozed diners at diners, and run TV ads. They’ve also participated in thousands of debates, which— like last night’s season finale— have amply demonstrated that no one on stage with a remote chance of winning is remotely suited to leading this country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Eeny Meeny Miny Moe: Sorting Out the G.O.P. Field', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T17:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4615d77a-4edb-5f87-beb9-7ba9b7cd3c80', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4615d77a-4edb-5f87-beb9-7ba9b7cd3c80'}, {'abstract': 'The Pomeranian  in “Young Adult” won the role for a simple reason: it’s the only breed that has to smile genetically.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/may-the-best-dog-actor-win/', 'snippet': 'The Pomeranian  in “Young Adult” won the role for a simple reason: it’s the only breed that has to smile genetically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The staff of The Hollywood Reporter continues with its hard-hitting, link-baiting coverage of this year’s animal stars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'May the Best Dog Actor Win', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reitman, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theron, Charlize', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f5e5a5-3986-5a53-a159-1b0592be5ada', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f5e5a5-3986-5a53-a159-1b0592be5ada'}, {'abstract': '“Bonnie & Clyde” is closing officially on Dec. 30.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/bonnie-clyde-will-close-on-dec-30/', 'snippet': '“Bonnie & Clyde” is closing officially on Dec. 30.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Bonnie & Clyde,” the composer Frank Wildhorn’s latest bid for Broadway success after several flops, won’t end his unlucky streak. Producers announced on Friday that the show, starring Jeremy Jordan and Laura Osnes, will close on Dec. 30.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bonnie & Clyde’ Will Close on Dec. 30', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/775ea28a-2034-517b-87a0-4d802002ab3b', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/775ea28a-2034-517b-87a0-4d802002ab3b'}, {'abstract': 'A letter complains that restrictions placed on gatherings of Occupy Wall Street organizers and protesters violate the First Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/at-60-wall-objections-are-raised-to-signs-prohibiting-signs/', 'snippet': 'A letter complains that restrictions placed on gatherings of Occupy Wall Street organizers and protesters violate the First Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 1:45 p.m. | Soon after the Occupy Wall Street protesters built an encampment in the financial district in mid-September, organizers looking for a less conspicuous place to gather began holding certain meetings inside a public atrium at 60 Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Meeting Spot for Occupiers, Signs Prohibit Signs', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SIEGEL, NORMAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d34a6ab-eb51-5eb7-9bc6-a1ece7082f8c', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d34a6ab-eb51-5eb7-9bc6-a1ece7082f8c'}, {'abstract': 'A music critic’s list of favorite recitals this year includes Stephanie Blythe, Sarah Connolly and Jennifer Johnson Cano.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/from-stephanie-blythe-to-ian-bostridge-favorite-recitals-of-the-year.html', 'snippet': 'A music critic’s list of favorite recitals this year includes Stephanie Blythe, Sarah Connolly and Jennifer Johnson Cano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT seems that a recital should be a breeze for a singer. Unlike in opera, there are no ill-fitting costumes; there is no awkward directorial concept to pull off. It’s just you, a piano and the music.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18WOOLFE_SPAN/18WOOLFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18WOOLFE_SPAN/18WOOLFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18WOOLFE_SPAN/18WOOLFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18WOOLFE_SPAN/18WOOLFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18WOOLFE_SPAN/18WOOLFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Standouts in a Solo Setting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Standouts in a Solo Setting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf23208-ad5a-50d6-a770-24e9d6d15782', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf23208-ad5a-50d6-a770-24e9d6d15782'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration has proposed regulations that would provide the nation’s two million home care workers with minimum wage and overtime protections.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/administration-proposes-wage-protections-for-home-care-workers/', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration has proposed regulations that would provide the nation’s two million home care workers with minimum wage and overtime protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times reports on Friday that the Obama administration has proposed regulations that would provide the nation’s two million home care workers with minimum wage and overtime protections. Those workers have long been exempted from coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Administration Proposes Wage Protections for Home Care Workers', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff11301-9df2-56b5-a555-62d7b0a5b90a', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff11301-9df2-56b5-a555-62d7b0a5b90a'}, {'abstract': 'Favorite classical music performances of the year, from Lully to lots of Glass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/highlights-of-classical-music-from-lully-to-glass.html', 'snippet': 'Favorite classical music performances of the year, from Lully to lots of Glass.', 'lead_paragraph': '“BEST of” lists are approximate endeavors. I was sorry I couldn’t attend the Mostly Mozart Festival’s “Don Giovanni,” one of many tantalizing events I missed. But the following proved highlights of my year. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cunning Vixens, A Dark Concert And Much Glass', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cunning Vixens, A Dark Concert And Much Glass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fc6b50e-a520-5757-975f-9e9900cb1e96', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fc6b50e-a520-5757-975f-9e9900cb1e96'}, {'abstract': 'Ali Musa Daqduq is accused of helping to orchestrate a January 2007 raid that killed five American soldiers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/world/middleeast/us-transfers-last-prisoner-to-iraqi-government.html', 'snippet': 'Ali Musa Daqduq is accused of helping to orchestrate a January 2007 raid that killed five American soldiers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration turned over the last remaining prisoner in American custody in Iraq to the Iraqi government on Friday, a move expected to unleash a political backlash inside the United States even as the American military draws closer to completing its exit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/detain/detain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 305, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/detain/detain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/world/detain/detain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Transfers Its Last Prisoner in Iraq to Iraqi Custody', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Transfers Last Prisoner to Iraqi Custody', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daqduq, Ali Musa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_n