tunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE number of Americans quitting their jobs has begun to rise, albeit from a very low level. That is a tentative sign that labor market mobility, which plunged during the 2007-9 recession, has started to recover.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Sign of Labor Recovery, More Workers Are Quitting', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Sign of Labor Recovery, More Workers Are Quitting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a714fe7c-463f-5ddd-9ffe-f72b7b942ca2', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a714fe7c-463f-5ddd-9ffe-f72b7b942ca2'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of thousands demonstrated Friday as Bashar al-Assad’s regime faced a surprise Security Council resolution that called on all antagonists in the conflict to begin negotiations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/world/middleeast/impatient-protesters-convulse-syria-as-russia-offers-new-resolution.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of thousands demonstrated Friday as Bashar al-Assad’s regime faced a surprise Security Council resolution that called on all antagonists in the conflict to begin negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Frustrated by the Syrian government’s intransigence and the Arab League’s delays in penalizing President Bashar al-Assad, hundreds of thousands of demonstrators in Syria took to the streets on Friday over the violent repression of their nine-month-old uprising. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/16/world/syria/syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Impatient Protesters Convulse Syria as Russia Offers New Resolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters Convulse Several Cities in Syria, as Russia Offers New U.N. Resolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:18:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ad09a67-b923-516d-a7d6-129e9402bf39', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ad09a67-b923-516d-a7d6-129e9402bf39'}, {'abstract': 'The water board in Texas says the state should spend $53 billion to meet the demand for water over the next 50 years.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/on-our-radar-billions-needed-for-texas-water-projects/', 'snippet': 'The water board in Texas says the state should spend $53 billion to meet the demand for water over the next 50 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Texas agency reports that the state should spend $53 billion to cope with its water needs over the next half-century, building infrastructure like new reservoirs, dams and wells, but warns that droughts may prevent the state from keeping up with demand. It is also unclear how the state would come up with the money. [The Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Billions Needed for Texas Water Projects', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88a47bb9-0a99-5d08-a805-7cdfe1899cd1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88a47bb9-0a99-5d08-a805-7cdfe1899cd1'}, {'abstract': 'This week, composer John Adams on Richard Rhodes’s book, “Hedy’s Folly”, about the life and inventions of Hedy Lamarr; Liesl Schillinger discusses “Death Comes to Pemberley”, P.D. James’s sequel to “Pride and Prejudice”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2011/12/16/books/booksupdate/16bookreview_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, composer John Adams on Richard Rhodes’s book, “Hedy’s Folly”, about the life and inventions of Hedy Lamarr; Liesl Schillinger discusses “Death Comes to Pemberley”, P.D. James’s sequel to “Pride and Prejudice”; Julie Bosman has notes fro...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, composer John Adams on Richard Rhodes’s book, “Hedy’s Folly”, about the life and inventions of Hedy Lamarr; Liesl Schillinger discusses “Death Comes to Pemberley”, P.D. James’s sequel to “Pride and Prejudice”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The life and inventions of Hedy Lamarr and a sequel to “Pride and Prejudice”', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:28:56+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Books Update', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/6957cb6d-6dc3-5ca6-805d-566068724c0e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/6957cb6d-6dc3-5ca6-805d-566068724c0e'}, {'abstract': 'Dwight Garner on life-affirming remarks from the late Christopher Hitchens, best known for his put-downs and critiques.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/the-happy-hitchens-quotations-from-the-life-lover-too/', 'snippet': 'Dwight Garner on life-affirming remarks from the late Christopher Hitchens, best known for his put-downs and critiques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Christopher Hitchens could be ferocious there is no doubt. His friend Martin Amis called him, accurately enough, “one of the most terrifying rhetoricians the world has yet seen.” So it makes sense that many of the encomiums to Hitchens today in newspapers and across the Web reprint many of his most indelible put-downs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Happy Hitchens: Quotations from The Life-Lover, Too', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce9f88bf-c46b-5b60-9e4e-949dfe250662', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce9f88bf-c46b-5b60-9e4e-949dfe250662'}, {'abstract': 'A neighborhood of mansions and bakeries, museums and florists, Carnegie Hill is at once grand and intimate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/realestate/carnegie-hill-living-in-land-of-good-bones-and-deep-pockets.html', 'snippet': 'A neighborhood of mansions and bakeries, museums and florists, Carnegie Hill is at once grand and intimate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEIGHBORHOOD of mansions and bakeries, museums and florists, Carnegie Hill is at once grand and intimate. As pleasantly walkable as any community in New York, its streets offer up vignettes that at times seem almost choreographed. Men sell Christmas trees from the gently sloping porte-cochère of the Convent of the Sacred Heart on East 91st Street. A high-stepping girls’ track team giggles through agility drills near the Engineers’ Gate to Central Park. Jacketed St. David’s boys and plaid-uniformed Spence girls grapple with planetoid-size burgers at Jackson Hole, as much an institution in these parts as any of the museums housed in Fifth Avenue palaces.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/realestate/18LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Land of Good Bones and Deep Pockets', 'kicker': 'Living In | Carnegie Hill', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Land of Good Bones and Deep Pockets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hill (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:31:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Freeman Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Freeman', 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0351039-64bf-56b8-8fe0-a26c4feda0ff', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0351039-64bf-56b8-8fe0-a26c4feda0ff'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey has raised its profile in the region, particularly in efforts to isolate Syria, but remains at odds with Israel over its treatment of Palestinians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/world/europe/leon-panetta-in-turkey-urges-improving-ties-with-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey has raised its profile in the region, particularly in efforts to isolate Syria, but remains at odds with Israel over its treatment of Palestinians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANKARA, Turkey — Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta on Friday called for Turkey to rebuild ties with Israel in the interest of security, echoing a call he issued this month for the government of Israel to reach out to other nations across the Middle East.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panetta Nudges Turkey to Rebuild Ties With Israel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: Turkey Asked to Fix Israel Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:34:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61978e29-d160-52fe-b2f3-dd6a6af76afc', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61978e29-d160-52fe-b2f3-dd6a6af76afc'}, {'abstract': 'We’re teaming up with FantasyPros.com to bring you Week 15’s toughest start/sit calls, based on the selections of more than 50 fantasy football experts on the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/fantasy-football-week-15s-toughest-picks/', 'snippet': 'We’re teaming up with FantasyPros.com to bring you Week 15’s toughest start/sit calls, based on the selections of more than 50 fantasy football experts on the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason and Justin Sablich are here to help you with your fantasy football team. The Sablich brothers will provide fantasy football advice throughout the season on this blog and on Twitter (@5thDownFantasy). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Week 15’s Toughest Picks', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vick, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:34:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Sablich and Jason Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfdc4c19-5827-5a3d-94ab-b3a2eb8729fd', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfdc4c19-5827-5a3d-94ab-b3a2eb8729fd'}, {'abstract': 'Among the year’s most memorable classical performances were works from two extremes, early and new music, with thoughtful, often provocative opera productions figuring prominently at both ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/arts/music/provocative-opera-at-2-extremes-early-and-new-music.html', 'snippet': 'Among the year’s most memorable classical performances were works from two extremes, early and new music, with thoughtful, often provocative opera productions figuring prominently at both ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME organizations that travel the classical music mainstream have undertaken innovations this year. Take, for example, the demand for fresh programming that made the Spring for Music festival of visiting orchestras at Carnegie Hall such a success. But for me the most memorable performances were by groups that specialize in the repertory’s extremes, early and new music. And thoughtful, often provocative opera productions figured prominently at both ends. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOZINN1_SPAN/18KOZINN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOZINN1_SPAN/18KOZINN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOZINN1_SPAN/18KOZINN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOZINN1_SPAN/18KOZINN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/arts/18KOZINN1_SPAN/18KOZINN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opera Flourishing At the Extremes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opera Flourishing At the Extremes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07352546-c36a-5844-a451-04ba7abc49f2', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07352546-c36a-5844-a451-04ba7abc49f2'}, {'abstract': 'Andrea Bruce, a photographer for The New York Times, pictures the withdrawal from Iraq through the eyes of the 149th Maneuver Enhancement Brigade.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/a-unit-near-last-in-the-military-withdrawal-from-iraq/', 'snippet': 'Andrea Bruce, a photographer for The New York Times, pictures the withdrawal from Iraq through the eyes of the 149th Maneuver Enhancement Brigade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iraq War’s small, subdued closing ceremony certainly gave the impression that there were few Americans left in the country. It was a final coda to a quietly withdrawing column of units leaving Iraq after more than eight years of war. Andrea Bruce, a photographer working for The New York Times, documented one of the last units in the exodus on the long road home:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Unit, Near Last, in the Military Withdrawal From Iraq', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:40:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc749d8b-316a-5683-9431-676ffb985354', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc749d8b-316a-5683-9431-676ffb985354'}, {'abstract': 'What do you do if a friend offers excuses instead of action when her child keeps hitting yours?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/parental-quandary-when-a-friends-child-hits-yours/', 'snippet': 'What do you do if a friend offers excuses instead of action when her child keeps hitting yours?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When families with children nearly exactly the same age come together, it can feel golden — as if the gods of friendship were shining on you. You’ll raise your kids together, play together, take trips together and watch them become lifelong companions as you yourselves stay close. For Isabel, though, it isn’t working out that way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary: When a Friend’s Child Hits Yours', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T18:41:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e2b1f5-6c97-543b-9f5a-47e28258811f', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9e2b1f5-6c97-543b-9f5a-47e28258811f'}, {