b_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/just-one-look-proenza-schouler/', 'snippet': 'High-fashion tech-sportswear, similar to what’s been so popular this prefall season, is what Proenza Schouler’s Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez do best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High-fashion tech-sportswear, similar to what’s been so popular this prefall season, is what Proenza Schouler’s Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez do best. Their version features taffeta workout separates like this top, shown under a silk nylon blended bungee skirt and tweed coat. Sleeping-bag-like quilted skirts and dresses, ’70s mountain boy tees and an aerial terrain view print were all inspired by the designers’ recent trip to the Himalayas. The faithful need not fret: PS 1 bags (in every shade of soil and sand) were aplenty, because let’s be real, life can’t be all hikes and bikes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Proenza Schouler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f594908c-e1c9-53a6-8d0d-3142bcdd68b3', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f594908c-e1c9-53a6-8d0d-3142bcdd68b3'}, {'abstract': 'Angelina Jolie was taking her children to the dentist when she heard the news that her directorial debut would be competing for a Golden Globe in the foreign-language category.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/angelina-jolie-gets-some-good-news-at-the-dentists-office/', 'snippet': 'Angelina Jolie was taking her children to the dentist when she heard the news that her directorial debut would be competing for a Golden Globe in the foreign-language category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Golden Globe nominations on Thursday drew varied reactions from nominees and non-nominees alike. Then there was the power couple Brad Pitt and Angelina Jolie, who both snagged nominations. Mr. Pitt is up for best actor for “Moneyball,” while Ms. Jolie’s directing debut, “In the Land of Blood and Honey,” about the Bosnian war, is competing in the foreign-language category. Even without the controversies surrounding it, Ms. Jolie knows the film is a hard sell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Angelina Jolie Gets Some Good News at the Dentist’s Office', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T19:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5cc4eb6-dc96-5b5e-8876-9815060e9992', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5cc4eb6-dc96-5b5e-8876-9815060e9992'}, {'abstract': 'The end of the Iraq war has gone almost completely unremarked on the Republican campaign trail.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/republican-candidates-mum-on-iraq/', 'snippet': 'The end of the Iraq war has gone almost completely unremarked on the Republican campaign trail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The end of the Iraq war has been marked with speeches and ceremonies in Washington, Baghdad, Fort Bragg, N.C., and elsewhere. But it has gone almost completely unremarked on the Republican campaign trail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Candidates Mum on Iraq', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T19:04:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6a61b8b-d9e5-5982-bf8d-03eaf60d092f', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6a61b8b-d9e5-5982-bf8d-03eaf60d092f'}, {'abstract': 'A new studio album will accompany an extensive Beach Boys tour, which will begin with a performance at the New Orleans Jazz and Heritage Festival next April.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/beach-boys-announce-reunion-tour-complete-with-brian-wilson/', 'snippet': 'A new studio album will accompany an extensive Beach Boys tour, which will begin with a performance at the New Orleans Jazz and Heritage Festival next April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years after they first played together, the Beach Boys announced Friday that they would release a new studio album and go on a 50-date tour in 2012, beginning with a reunion concert at the New Orleans Jazz and Heritage festival in April.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beach Boys Announce Reunion Tour, Complete With Brian Wilson', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beach Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T19:04:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e9b7093-8094-57b9-8daf-b389f1be7aed', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e9b7093-8094-57b9-8daf-b389f1be7aed'}, {'abstract': 'Dogs: They chew the table legs, require frequent airing, shed,  and give unconditional love. What breeds are best for city living, and why?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/what-are-the-best-dogs-for-city-living/', 'snippet': 'Dogs: They chew the table legs, require frequent airing, shed,  and give unconditional love. What breeds are best for city living, and why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For New York City residents, apartments can be small and green spaces can be few and far in between. So why would so many want to crowd a dog (or two) into their 600-square-foot studios? Elissa Gootman’s article, appearing in this Sunday’s Real Estate section, explores the question. She writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are the Best Dogs for City Living?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-1