ecipes for Health columnist, suggests blending up creamy homemade soup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To keep you warm this winter, Martha Rose Shulman, the Recipes for Health columnist, suggests blending up creamy homemade soup:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soup’s on for the Holidays', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T20:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a6d05ca-547c-553e-955b-afb5e0767372', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a6d05ca-547c-553e-955b-afb5e0767372'}, {'abstract': 'The Moment caught up with the girls of the West Village’s Caribbean hot spot to find out how to get their look.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/stir-it-up-miss-lilys-variety-show/', 'snippet': 'The Moment caught up with the girls of the West Village’s Caribbean hot spot to find out how to get their look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Miss Lily’s, the raucous Houston Street hot spot for hush puppies and jerk chicken, has put authentic Caribbean food in fashion’s favor in recent months. Now the restaurant is opening a carefully edited record shop and radio station with a juice bar next door named Variety. Serge Becker, who designed the space to serve the city’s community of artists, designers, writers and musicians inspired by Caribbean culture, sees it as a place to “talk Jamaica” and enjoy a juice and patty. Expect to catch underground notables like Brazil’s hottest rapper, Criolo, or the Chinese-Jamaican music producer Clive Chin taking to the turntables or perusing the shop’s selection of rare vinyl, apparel and limited-edition art. Miss Lily’s fine-looking staff (pictured here in the juice bar wearing the resort collections’ most optimistic prints and colors) only help to make the hangout rock steady. The Moment caught up with the girls to find out how to get their look (that hair!) and what’s in their makeup bag. Go to slide show >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stir It Up | Miss Lily’s Variety Show', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T20:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch and Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4da1a4f-832a-5197-a2a7-48f810c9e72c', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4da1a4f-832a-5197-a2a7-48f810c9e72c'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers offer their own suggestions on how to help those who have lost jobs or are otherwise struggling this year.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/empathy-gifts-to-friends-in-need/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers offer their own suggestions on how to help those who have lost jobs or are otherwise struggling this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan writes in his Wealth Matters column this week abou