 about holiday cocktails.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helping America Build a Better Negroni', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T21:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3abeff45-c0c0-5bdd-a5b5-5290cc095302', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3abeff45-c0c0-5bdd-a5b5-5290cc095302'}, {'abstract': 'As they tried to fend off an attack on a sit-in by military police in Cairo on Friday, Egyptian protesters used their phones to transmit video, photo and text accounts of the clashes.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/under-attack-by-soldiers-egyptian-protesters-report-from-inside-the-fray/', 'snippet': 'As they tried to fend off an attack on a sit-in by military police in Cairo on Friday, Egyptian protesters used their phones to transmit video, photo and text accounts of the clashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 7:55 p.m. As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reports from Cairo, at least two people were killed and more than 200 were injured on Friday as military police beat up demonstrators challenging military rule and angry protesters hurled improvised explosives at the empty Parliament building.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Attack by Soldiers, Egyptian Protesters Report From Inside the Fray', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nour, Ayman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T21:47:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bc8107b-dbc3-5c86-895b-eb5d4743e749', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bc8107b-dbc3-5c86-895b-eb5d4743e749'}, {'abstract': 'The president told a convention of reformist Jews how he had fought for Israel’s interests, but he made little mention of the Palestinian issue.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/in-obama-speech-on-israel-no-mention-of-palestinians/', 'snippet': 'The president told a convention of reformist Jews how he had fought for Israel’s interests, but he made little mention of the Palestinian issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than a year before the presidential election, a pattern is emerging. The Republicans will outdo themselves to say the most provocative things they can to demonstrate they love Israel more than anyone else. And President Obama will counter by saying as little as he can about the Palestinians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Obama Speech on Israel, Little Mention of Palestinians', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T21:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f10bc7a4-fe9c-505e-bbe0-4ae78af91695', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f10bc7a4-fe9c-505e-bbe0-4ae78af91695'}, {'abstract': 'Italians have come to view their lawmakers as a pampered elite, sheltered from the global economic turbulence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/world/europe/in-debt-crisis-gulf-yawns-between-italy-and-politicians.html', 'snippet': 'Italians have come to view their lawmakers as a pampered elite, sheltered from the global economic turbulence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — With its elegant marble floors, ornately carved wooden ceiling and flattering lighting, the central meeting point of Italy’s Lower House is arguably one of the most beautiful political arenas in the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17italy/17italy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17italy/17italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/world/17italy/17italy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Debt Crisis, Gulf Is Yawning Between Italy and Its Politicians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Debt Crisis, Gulf Is Yawning Between Italy and Its Politicians', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major