o Greenmarket shoppers in Manhattan and Brooklyn, is just that: smiling, laughing, joking and incredibly hard-working. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21KITCH_SPAN/21KITCH_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stew, Fresh From the Fisherman', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fresh From a Fisherman’s Small Boat, a Stew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T22:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59ba3718-a88b-5eb5-a839-42737074eddc', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59ba3718-a88b-5eb5-a839-42737074eddc'}, {'abstract': 'Ask your fishmonger for what is freshest, most local and most sustainable, and you’ll get good results.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/key-to-a-great-stew-a-great-fisherman/', 'snippet': 'Ask your fishmonger for what is freshest, most local and most sustainable, and you’ll get good results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It doesn’t take much in the way of ingredients to make a good fish stew, but it does need good fresh fish. Enter local fishmonger Alex Villani of Blue Moon Fish. Well known in Manhattan and Brooklyn Greenmarkets, his fish and shellfish have a loyal following. In an admirably energetic and unusual arrangement, the man catches the fish out by Mattituck on Long Island, drives it to market, and, with the help of his wife, Stephanie, sells it at his stall, all the while smiling about it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Key to a Great Stew: a Great Fisherman', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T22:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2987b80b-fa01-51fc-bfcb-ab86eb7f4460', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2987b80b-fa01-51fc-bfcb-ab86eb7f4460'}, {'abstract': '“Here, in a nutshell, is the problem with feminism.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/on-looting-uk-feminista-and-where-feminism-went-wrong/', 'snippet': '“Here, in a nutshell, is the problem with feminism.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jenny Turner in The London Review of Books: “Here, in a nutshell, is the problem with feminism. Young women ‘of good character’ losing their heads and wishing they hadn’t. You feel so sorry for them, but can’t you sense what they tasted in the air as they were doing it: freedom, fury, the power — for once — of being young and strong and agile and a homegirl, the flat-out joy of getting your hands on some free stuff.”\xa0Read on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Looting, UK Feminista and Where Feminism Went Wrong', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Jenny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T22:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1623fb83-f61c-5ad2-80c0-63045599b9bf', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1623fb83-f61c-5ad2-80c0-63045599b9bf'}, {'abstract': 'The House Financial Services Committee is concerned that the Securities and Exchange Commission’s practice of accepting no-contest settlements obscures transparency.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/congress-to-hold-hearings-on-s-e-c-settlement-practices/', 'snippet': 'The House Financial Services Committee is concerned that the Securities and Exchange Commission’s practice of accepting no-contest settlements obscures transparency.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:27 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress to Examine S.E.C. Settlement Policy', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachus, Spencer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Barney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khuzami, Robert S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T22:28:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b10c914e-b71d-54c2-93c6-652158925f2f', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b10c914e-b71d-54c2-93c6-652158925f2f'}, {'abstract': '“A Not So Silent Night,” a Christmas concert at Town Hall on Thursday, picked up where Kate McGarrigle left off. The evening was a benefit for the Kate McGarrigle Fund for Sarcoma Research.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/arts/music/wainwright-and-mcgarrigle-families-at-town-hall-review.html', 'snippet': '“A Not So Silent Night,” a Christmas concert at Town Hall on Thursday, picked up where Kate McGarrigle left off. The evening was a benefit for the Kate McGarrigle Fund for Sarcoma Research.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Not So Silent Night,” the concert at Town Hall on Thursday, was a typical Christmastime family gathering: motley, convivial, multigenerational, jokey, affectionate, conscious of passing years and tinged with both skepticism and faith. There wasn’t any bickering, though. The family onstage happens to be packed with singers and songwriters — troupers all — and this year the next generation was resuming a tradition. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/arts/WAINWRIGHT/WAINWRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/17/arts/WAINWRIGHT/WAINWRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/arts/WAINWRIGHT/WAINWRIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/arts/WAINWRIGHT/WAINWRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/arts/WAINWRIGHT/WAINWRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Tradition of a Matriarch, This Family Keeps Crooning and Caroling', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Tr