Dickens’s original text; the Shakespeare Theater of New Jersey performs it through Jan. 1 at Drew University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/nyregion/shakespeare-theater-of-new-jerseys-a-christmas-carol-review.html', 'snippet': 'Neil Bartlett has adapted “A Christmas Carol” for the stage using only Dickens’s original text; the Shakespeare Theater of New Jersey performs it through Jan. 1 at Drew University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is possible to see “A Christmas Carol” on film or onstage a dozen times, maybe more, and yet never see one particular scene from Dickens’s original 1843 novella. It stars Belle, the young Ebenezer Scrooge’s fiancée, who broke off their engagement because Ebenezer had become so obsessed with money. She is seen talking about him casually but sympathetically with her handsome husband, in a tableau of contented domesticity with their beautiful daughter and their prettily decorated Christmas tree.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18ARTSNJ1/18ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18ARTSNJ1/18ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18ARTSNJ1/18ARTSNJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belle Is Fulfilled, and Dickens Restored', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belle Is Fulfilled, And Dickens Restored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartlett, Neil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickens, Charles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare Theater of New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monte, Bonnie J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-16T23:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4452fbd0-81c3-567a-ae76-2ab0f9f73763', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4452fbd0-81c3-567a-ae76-2ab0f9f73763'}, {'abstract': 'The Verano joins cars like the Audi A3 and Volvo C30 that are exploring whether Americans will pay a premium for upscale compacts.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/reviewing-the-buick-verano/', 'snippet': 'The Verano joins cars like the Audi A3 and Volvo C30 that are exploring whether Americans will pay a premium for upscale compacts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Christopher Jensen reviews the Buick Verano, a premium compact sedan that shares its architecture with its strong-selling, and more frugally priced, corporate relation under General Motors, the Chevrolet Cruze.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Buick Verano', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buick Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '20