shion/weddings/18FIELDNOTES1/18FIELDNOTES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/fashion/weddings/18FIELDNOTES1/18FIELDNOTES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exchanging Vows Under a Canopy, No Matter the Faith', 'kicker': 'Field Notes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exchanging Vows Under a Canopy, No Matter the Faith', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T00:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marianne Rohrlich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marianne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohrlich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96f5edb8-8b6a-5e30-b842-cd758b2985c3', 'word_count': 1421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96f5edb8-8b6a-5e30-b842-cd758b2985c3'}, {'abstract': 'A video report based on interviews with people who took part in the riots that spread across England in August reveals that anger at the police was a significant factor for many.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/16/listening-to-the-british-rioters/', 'snippet': 'A video report based on interviews with people who took part in the riots that spread across England in August reveals that anger at the police was a significant factor for many.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we come to the end of a remarkable year of protests and riots across the globe, it is not hard to feel that too little time has been devoted to digesting the meaning of what’s happened, perhaps in part because technology now makes it so easy to get caught up in following the rush of events as they unspool online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listening to the British Rioters', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London School of Economics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T00:35:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af6b25a2-e187-5cf0-a1db-a1701243fece', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af6b25a2-e187-5cf0-a1db-a1701243fece'}, {'abstract': 'Even as he weakened from cancer, Christopher Hitchens remained a vibrant and honest reviewer of books about a wide range of subjects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/books/review/christopher-hitchens-book-critic.html', 'snippet': 'Even as he weakened from cancer, Christopher Hitchens remained a vibrant and honest reviewer of books about a wide range of subjects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Christopher Hitchens weakened from cancer over the past year and a half, the work he contributed to The New York Times Book Review was as strong as ever, if not stronger. The last piece he wrote for us assessed the playwright David Mamet’s account of shifting politically to the right. Mr. Hitchens made it clear that his pugnacity would be with him until the last: “This is an extraordinarily irritating book,” he began, later saying of one of Mr. Mamet’s opinions that it “has a long way to go before it can even be called simplistic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christopher Hitchens, Book Critic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christopher Hitchens, Book Critic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T00:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba711bd4-cdf1-5d0d-b940-4d8b20904bfe', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba711bd4-cdf1-5d0d-b940-4d8b20904bfe'}, {'abstract': 'The first SportAccord World Mind Games, which ended on Friday in Beijing, brought together competitors in five disciplines: bridge, checkers, chess, Chinese chess and go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/crosswords/bridge/bridge-americans-win-2-individuals-at-world-mind-games.html', 'snippet': 'The first SportAccord World Mind Games, which ended on Friday in Beijing, brought together competitors in five disciplines: bridge, checkers, chess, Chinese chess and go.', 'lead_p