 editors of The New York Times are always searching for interesting items on the Web. Here’s what they found: Women in technology, year-end lists that are odd and important and the role of data with dictators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s what the tech reporters and editors picked out on the Web on Friday. For the full list, look over to the right-hand column.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Unusual Year-End Lists and a Spider Bot', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T01:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b3699a3-9442-5178-a688-d55b95ff3ce2', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b3699a3-9442-5178-a688-d55b95ff3ce2'}, {'abstract': 'In weighing the extension of the operating licenses of the Indian Point nuclear plants, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission should consider land contamination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/opinion/is-indian-point-the-next-fukushima.html', 'snippet': 'In weighing the extension of the operating licenses of the Indian Point nuclear plants, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission should consider land contamination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santa Monica, Calif.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Point: The Next Fukushima?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Point: The Next Fukushima?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T01:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Gilinsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilinsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d24d4e51-1aa3-5257-ac31-ecb706452dde', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d24d4e51-1aa3-5257-ac31-ecb706452dde'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon.com, under its chief, Jeff Bezos, follows a growth-oriented strategy that sometimes disappoints investors who want near-term profit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/business/at-amazon-jeff-bezos-talks-long-term-and-means-it.html', 'snippet': 'Amazon.com, under its chief, Jeff Bezos, follows a growth-oriented strategy that sometimes disappoints investors who want near-term profit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1997, the year Amazon.com went public, its chief executive, Jeff Bezos, issued a manifesto: “It’s all about the long term,” he said. He warned shareholders “we may make decisions and weigh tradeoffs differently than some companies” and urged them to make sure that a long-term approach “is consistent with your investment policy.” Amazon’s management and employees “are working to build something important, something that matters to our customers, something that we can tell our grandchildren about,” he added.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Says Long Term And Means It', 'kicker': 'Common Sense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazon Says Long Term And Means It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T01:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f90386-cd25-5a09-a2c1-a94fa0c012c0', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f90386-cd25-5a09-a2c1-a94fa0c012c0'}, {'abstract': 'Considering how far world leaders are from making hard decisions to lower greenhouse gas emissions, big nations will have to do so even without binding agreements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/opinion/beyond-the-durban-climate-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Considering how far world leaders are from making hard decisions to lower greenhouse gas emissions, big nations will have to do so even without binding agreements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Startling new evidence that global carbon dioxide emissions are rising faster than ever did little to increase the urgency of the climate talks in Durban, South Africa, which concluded earlier this week. Once again, the world’s negotiators kicked the can down the road. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Durban', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Durban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank':