rt Mugabe and his supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — Tens of millions of dollars in diamond profits — perhaps more — are being secretly extracted from state-owned mines in eastern Zimbabwe, bypassing the nation’s treasury and raising fears that President Robert Mugabe is amassing wealth to help extend his 31-year reign, according to monitoring groups, diplomats, lawmakers and analysts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/jpzimbabwe2/jpzimbabwe2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/world/jpzimbabwe2/jpzimbabwe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/17/world/jpzimbabwe2/jpzimbabwe2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions From Diamonds Go to Mugabe, Observers Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diamond Profits Seen as Filling Mugabe Coffers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe African National Union-Patriotic Front (ZANU-PF)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mugabe, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T02:32:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_na