', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a major surprise on the politically charged new health care law, the Obama administration said Friday that it would not define a single uniform set of “essential health benefits” that must be provided by insurers for tens of millions of Americans. Instead, it will allow each state to specify the benefits within broad categories.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Law Will Let States Tailor Benefits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Care Law Will Let States Tailor Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T02:38:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d7ee02c-2835-5786-ba2e-a57c1420911f', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d7ee02c-2835-5786-ba2e-a57c1420911f'}, {'abstract': 'The public artist Kristin Jones plans a 24-hour extravaganza highlighting five great trees, though her last New York project in Union Square was panned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/nyregion/kristin-jones-persistent-public-artist-plans-tree-project.html', 'snippet': 'The public artist Kristin Jones plans a 24-hour extravaganza highlighting five great trees, though her last New York project in Union Square was panned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE artist Kristin Jones, 55, wrapped in a double layer of green velvet capes with her blond Rapunzel braid askew over one shoulder, stood in the northwest corner of Washington Square Park gazing rapturously at a 330-year-old tree known as the Hangman’s Elm. She placed a protective hand on its mighty trunk. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18JONES_SPAN/18JONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18JONES_SPAN/18JONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18JONES_SPAN/18JONES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18JONES_SPAN/18JONES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/nyregion/18JONES_SPAN/18JONES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Christo, Thinking Big', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Christo, Thinking Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key