ppet': 'Two similar teams will square off for the championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — Thursday night’s national semifinal matches of the N.C.A.A. women’s volleyball Final Four could not have played out more differently. U.C.L.A. swept the first match of the night, 3-0, against Florida State. In the second game, Illinois and Southern California pushed their match to five sets. Illinois won the fifth set on a match point that included about 50 touches before the Illini notched the 15th and decisive point. After the exhausting conclusion of the match, the Illini did not celebrate their program’s first championship game appearance; the players lined up, shook hands with their Southern California counterparts and began preparing for their matchup against U.C.L.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.C.L.A. and Illinois in Women’s Volleyball Final', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volleyball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T04:23:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Spencer D. Turkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Spencer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d2ae55-3f8f-5a69-b64e-a3dc48a50e44', 'word_count': 56