nts across India as reported by the nation’s press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: A 24-year-old shopkeeper died Wednesday, two weeks after being severely beaten up by protesters who demanded a shutdown in the Nowhatta area of Srinagar. Tariq Ahmed Bhat had refused closing down his shop. (Kashmir Live)Rajasthan: The Rajasthan police commissioner and the Jaipur Municipal Corporation have decided to relocate the city’s beggars in order to create a good impression and encourage non-resident Indians to invest in the state. The decision was made in advance of the upcoming Pravasi Bharatiya Diwas, from Jan. 7-9 (Daily Bhaskar).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T05:13:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5ab930f-2144-5a52-b93e-91ce27058f3c', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5ab930f-2144-5a52-b93e-91ce27058f3c'}, {'abstract': 'The lawyers for Colton Harris-Moore, known as the “Barefoot Bandit,” filed papers detailing poverty and abuse during his childhood in hopes that the judge would hand down a lenient sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/17/us/coltonharrismoore_document.html', 'snippet': 'The lawyers for Colton Harris-Moore, known as the “Barefoot Bandit,” filed papers detailing poverty and abuse during his childhood in hopes that the judge would hand down a lenient sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lawyers for Colton Harris-Moore, known as the “Barefoot Bandit,” filed papers detailing poverty and abuse during his childhood in hopes that the judge would hand down a lenient sentence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitigation Package for Colton Harris-Moore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris-Moore, Colton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T05:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/38c476a5-e9ef-52a0-a72e-e6aa61256131', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/38c476a5-e9ef-52a0-a72e-e6aa61256131'}, {'abstract': 'Colton Harris-Moore, who fended for himself by stealing food from neighbors while growing up, then graduated to stealing planes, was sentenced to more than seven years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/us/colton-harris-moore-the-barefoot-bandit-is-sentenced-for-stealing-from-neighbors.html', 'snippet': 'Colton Harris-Moore, who fended for himself by stealing food from neighbors while growing up, then graduated to stealing planes, was sentenced to more than seven years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COUPEVILLE, Wash. — Colton Harris-Moore, the “Barefoot Bandit,” stood bolt upright in orange jail garb before Judge Vicki I. Churchill in the small courtroom here on Friday and was sentenced to seven years and three months in prison. His hands were folded in front of him because they were shackled, and he struggled to hold back tears as he pleaded guilty to 33 state charges including burglary and identity theft.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/us/BAREFOOT1/BAREFOOT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType