orida A&M University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T06:06:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29a02354-094f-5f9b-9bf0-159bc186954d', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29a02354-094f-5f9b-9bf0-159bc186954d'}, {'abstract': 'A federal three-judge panel in San Antonio on Friday pushed back the state’s primary elections, resolving one of the most pressing issues in an ongoing redistricting dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/us/texas-judges-push-back-primary-election-date.html', 'snippet': 'A federal three-judge panel in San Antonio on Friday pushed back the state’s primary elections, resolving one of the most pressing issues in an ongoing redistricting dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A federal three-judge panel in San Antonio on Friday pushed back the state’s primary elections from the scheduled date of March 6 to April 3, resolving one of the most pressing issues in a redistricting dispute that has thrown much of Texas politics into disarray. One option under consideration had been splitting the primary into two separate elections, a move that many Democrats and Republicans opposed, saying it would hurt voter turnout, cost counties hundreds of thousands of dollars and create logistical problems for elections officials. The parties issued a joint statement on Friday saying they were pleased with the new election schedule. The judges’ decision ordering a single unified primary came after an agreement on the election schedule had been reached by the state Democratic and Republican Parties. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Judges Push Back Primary Election Date', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Judges Push Back Primary Election Date', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Antonio (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T06:18:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ddffef-ed52-5950-a7be-39fcd8c776fc', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ddffef-ed52-5950-a7be-39fcd8c776fc'}, {'abstract': 'A judge tossed out California’s newly adopted lethal injection protocol on Friday, throwing the state’s execution system into further upheaval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/us/california-judge-rejects-lethal-injection-protocol.html', 'snippet': 'A judge tossed out California’s newly adopted lethal injection protocol on Friday, throwing the state’s execution system into further upheaval.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A judge tossed out California’s newly adopted lethal injection protocol on Friday, throwing the state’s execution system into further upheaval. Judge Faye D’Opal of Marin County Superior Court in San Rafael ruled that the state had failed to justify the decision to put in place a three-drug lethal injection method, which some experts had said carries a risk of “excruciating pain,” instead of a one-drug method, which one of the Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation’s own experts had recommended. No executions have been conducted in California since 2006, when a federal judge effectively halted lethal injections, citing various deficiencies in the state’s methods. Since then, the state has revamped its execution system, including the construction of a new death chamber specifically for lethal injections. The corrections department declined to comment on the ruling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Judge Rejects Lethal Injection Protocol', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Judge Rejects Lethal Injection Protocol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T06:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b1065a-c449-522e-a650-760a1d97fa2e', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b1065a-c449-522e-a650-760a1d97fa2e'}, {'abstract': 'Sean Parker, a founder of Napster and former president of Facebook, is a lively social presence in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/fashion/sean-parker-brings-facebook-style-skills-to-new-york-social-scene.html', 'sni