 to share their #MyWipeOut stories on Twitter. Here are a selection of their epics spills, face plants and lost skis.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/readers-share-their-mywipeout-stories-2/', 'snippet': 'As part of last week’s ski issue we asked readers to share their #MyWipeOut stories on Twitter. Here are a selection of their epics spills, face plants and lost skis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of last week’s ski issue we asked readers to share their #MyWipeOut stories on Twitter. Here are a selection of their epics spills, face plants and lost skis . ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Share Their #MyWipeOut Stories', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T14:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9007b56f-a674-5052-b440-0c454ead6597', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9007b56f-a674-5052-b440-0c454ead6597'}, {'abstract': 'A two-month extension of the payroll-tax holiday — should it get through the House — adds to a series of 11th-hour Congressional deals that simply pushed the issues involved forward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/politics/extension-of-payroll-tax-cut-passes-senate.html', 'snippet': 'A two-month extension of the payroll-tax holiday — should it get through the House — adds to a series of 11th-hour Congressional deals that simply pushed the issues involved forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Capping a year of last-minute, half-loaf legislation, the Senate voted overwhelmingly on Saturday to extend a payroll tax cut for only two months, with the chamber’s leaders and the White House proclaiming victory, even as they punted into the new year the issue of how to further extend the tax cut and unemployment benefits. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/politics/18obama-span/18obama-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/politics/18obama-span/18obama-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/us/politics/18obama-span/18obama-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Senate Tax Cut Stopgap, Odds in House Are Uncertain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Payroll Tax Cut Passes Senate As a Stopgap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T15:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'sectio