unday-review/the-internet-gets-physical.html', 'snippet': 'Consumer-based Internet technologies are morphing into new uses in energy conservation, transportation, health care, traffic management and food distribution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Internet likes you, really likes you. It offers you so much, just a mouse click or finger tap away. Go Christmas shopping, find restaurants, locate partying friends, tell the world what you’re up to. Some of the finest minds in computer science, working at start-ups and big companies, are obsessed with tracking your online habits to offer targeted ads and coupons, just for you.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/sunday-review/LOHR/LOHR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 585, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/sunday-review/LOHR/LOHR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/sunday-review/LOHR/LOHR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Internet Gets Physical', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Internet Gets Physical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smarr, Larry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmisano, Samuel J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nest Labs', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sensors', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T20:09:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/60b12bf5-dfc8-5a47-8c1d-1ff97c8726ff', 'word_count': 1495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60b12bf5-dfc8-5a47-8c1d-1ff97c8726ff'}, {'abstract': 'Even as professional sports associations campaign against illegal enhancements, millions of American men have been using testosterone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/opinion/sunday/are-we-not-man-enough.html', 'snippet': 'Even as professional sports associations campaign against illegal enhancements, millions of American men have been using testosterone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Friday, a federal judge in San Francisco sentenced Barry Bonds, Major League Baseball’s career home run leader, to two years of probation and community service. Mr. Bonds’s success in baseball, and his conviction for obstruction of justice earlier this year, both stemmed in part from his use of a testosterone-based balm famously known as “the cream.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/sunday-review/MEN/MEN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/sunday-review/MEN/MEN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600,