/sunday/alabamas-second-thoughts.html', 'snippet': 'Alabama’s stance on its extremist immigration law is shifting from defiance to damage control, as Gov. Robert Bentley admits that the law needs fixing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alabama’s stance on its extremist immigration law is shifting from defiance to damage control. Gov. Robert Bentley admitted this month that the law needed fixing and promised that he and legislative leaders would do that in next year’s session. His retreat followed a letter from the state’s attorney general, Luther Strange, to legislative leaders suggesting that they throw out whole sections of the law to make it easier to defend in court. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama’s Second Thoughts', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama’s Second Thoughts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strange, Luther', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bentley, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T20:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab723470-f173-5e2e-9bd5-c3d1cedcb6d7', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab723470-f173-5e2e-9bd5-c3d1cedcb6d7'}, {'abstract': 'Is marijuana safe and effec