12/18/jobs/annual-reviews-and-how-to-prepare-for-them.html', 'snippet': 'Before meeting with the boss for that yearly evaluation, take time to review your performance yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. It’s time for your yearly performance review. You aren’t expecting any big surprises, but you still feel a little nervous. How should you prepare for this meeting?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-CAREER/18-CAREER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prepping for Your Annual Review', 'kicker': 'Career Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prepping For That Annual Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:19:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d2d6898-bcec-5b63-b439-5427882e3182', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d2d6898-bcec-5b63-b439-5427882e3182'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about Bahrain.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/reader-comments-on-bahrain/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about Bahrain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is about Bahrain, our ally in the Gulf, and the Obama administration’s proposed $53 million arms sale to the regime. As you may know from my last column, I was detained in Bahrain by riot police who also broke the camera and roughed up the video journalist with me. But, truth be told, I also have a good deal of admiration for Bahrain and what the royal family has accomplished here — the soaring living standards, the investment in education, the empowerment of women, the solid middle class. It’s just that when you educate people and create a cosmopolitan nation, you can’t continue to deny them democracy. People want more from life than fine watches and nice houses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reader Comments on Bahrain', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83801df9-84b1-5cb4-abf2-96e0d1a6b127', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83801df9-84b1-5cb4-abf2-96e0d1a6b127'}, {'abstract': 'One person was injured and police said a motive for the attack by the unidentified gunmen remained unknown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/world/asia/gunmen-in-indonesia-attack-helicopter-of-mine-workers.html', 'snippet': 'One person was injured and police said a motive for the attack by the unidentified gunmen remained unknown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — Gunmen fired at a helicopter carrying workers for the mining giant Freeport-McMoRan shortly after it took off Saturday from a town near the company’s huge gold and copper mine in eastern Indonesia, a police spokesman, Colonel Wachyono, said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gunmen Attack Helicopter Carrying Mine Workers in Indonesia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gunmen Attack Helicopter Carrying Mine Workers in Indonesia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freeport-McMoRan Copper&Gold Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Schonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4c99564-9e91-5379-b63f-bd9caa4df425', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4c99564-9e91-5379-b63f-bd9caa4df425'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of CourseSmart loved books (and rugby) while growing up, and has been a pioneer in electronic books during his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/jobs/sean-devine-of-coursesmart-journey-of-a-bookworm.html', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of CourseSmart loved books (and rugby) while growing up, and has been a pioneer in electronic books during his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY dad was a Marine officer who fought in the Battle of Inchon in the Korean War. He was badly injured and awarded three Purple Hearts and the Bronze Star. I grew up hearing stories about the war and how he continued to fight while hurt. He served as an example of picking yourself up after being knocked down.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-BOSS/18-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-BOSS/18-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-BOSS/18-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Journey of a Bookworm', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Journey of a Bookworm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Devine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Devine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f6581f0-aca3-5a8a-a87c-634cfb291e43', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6581f0-aca3-5a8a-a87c-634cfb291e43'}, {'abstract': 'The navy secretary, Ray Mabus, said that reductions would be tailored to the service’s needs and then would be achieved primarily through attrition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/world/asia/secretary-eyes-cuts-in-marines-and-the-navy.html', 'snippet': 'The navy secretary, Ray Mabus, said that reductions would be tailored to the service’s needs and then would be achieved primarily through attrition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — On a trip to Afghanistan to visit Navy and Marine forces, the secretary of the Navy, Ray Mabus, said Saturday that he expected both branches to reduce their numbers after the Iraq and Afghan wars, and to return to their seafaring roots — although both will have some new areas of focus.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secretary Expects Cuts in Marines and the Navy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secretary Expects Cuts In Marines And the Navy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mabus, Ray', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e33f2b-39a4-5a6e-88e4-a3ea90703c7b', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e33f2b-39a4-5a6e-88e4-a3ea90703c7b'}, {'abstract': 'Video posted online by independent journalists and Egyptian activists showed soldiers attacking protesters, even as the country’s prime minister denied that the military used any force.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/video-shows-egyptian-soldiers-beating-and-shooting-at-protesters/', 'snippet': 'Video posted online by independent journalists and Egyptian activists showed soldiers attacking protesters, even as the country’s prime minister denied that the military used any force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As our colleague David Kirkpatrick reports from Cairo, Egyptian soldiers chased down and beat unarmed civilians on Saturday, even while the prime minister appointed by the military “was denying in a televised news conference that security forces were using any force.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Egyptian Soldiers Beating and Shooting at Protesters', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Elizabeth Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eee5a315-626e-5a62-bda2-bb7b4b8d8f13', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eee5a315-626e-5a62-bda2-bb7b4b8d8f13'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas governor accused two rivals of being excessive users of earmarks in the federal budget, describing them as part of the insider culture that he would reject as president.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/perry-criticizes-competitors-over-earmarks/', 'snippet': 'The Texas governor accused two rivals of being excessive users of earmarks in the federal budget, describing them as part of the insider culture that he would reject as president.', 'lead_paragraph': ' SPENCER, Iowa — Rick Perry accused two rivals of being excessive users of earmarks in the federal budget, describing them as part of the insider culture that he would reject as president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Criticizes Competitors Over Earmarks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfeb2688-b9d0-50ad-90aa-5627fd5bbb54', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfeb2688-b9d0-50ad-90aa-5627fd5bbb54'}, {'abstract': 'The consensus view of the economy has improved. But remember that the consensus has been wrong in the recent past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/your-money/in-economic-forecast-season-its-wise-to-slow-down.html', 'snippet': 'The consensus view of the economy has improved. But remember that the consensus has been wrong in the recent past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE American economy certainly isn’t at peak strength. With unemployment at a painfully high 8.6 percent, it can’t be. But unless the economy receives another shocking blow, it isn’t in imminent danger of relapsing into recession. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-STRA/18-STRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-STRA/18-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/business/18-STRA/18-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Forecasting Fog, It’s Wise to Slow Down', 'kicker': 'Strategies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Forecasting Fog, It’s Wise to Slow Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T22:52:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sommer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49daeaea-af21-528a-ab6f-3ab1870c2c0a', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49daeaea-af21-528a-ab6f-3ab1870c2c0a'}, {'abstract': 'Along the northern New England Coast, festive monuments of engineering and local pride mark the Christmas season and guarantee bragging rights for the towns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/new-england-asks-who-has-fairest-lobster-trap-tree-of-all.html', 'snippet': 'Along the northern New England Coast, festive monuments of engineering and local pride mark the Christmas season and guarantee bragging rights for the towns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tiny towns of Beals and Jonesport, Me., have completed their second annual holiday display: a conical tower of 1,364 lobster traps, 60 feet tall, built to withstand the powerful winds that come off the water. It is the towns’ Christmas tree, made of wire traps plucked from the sea by lobstermen who lend them to the cause.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/LOBSTER1/LOBSTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/us/LOBSTER1/LOBSTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/LOBSTER1/LOBSTER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'w