, {'abstract': 'Patrick Merrell makes the grade in his Sunday puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/17/again-2/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Merrell makes the grade in his Sunday puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — What do you “gain” from doing crossword puzzles? Some people feel that puzzles makes their brain sharper, some people do them to increase their vocabulary. Others do crosswords because their commute to work would be deadly boring without them. And, of course, there’s the community: a whole tribe of constructors, editors, bloggers, solvers and commenters who regularly gather both virtually and in real life to challenge and entertain one another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: Again?', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-17T23:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26073bed-ee51-55c2-896e-912b492bc28a', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26073bed-ee51-55c2-896e-912b492bc28a'}, {'abstract': 'Born out of harsh winters and long tradition, wearing furs remains popular in Russia, where organizations like People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals have been unable to make many inroads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/18/business/Russians-Flock-to-Fur.html', 'snippet': 'Born out of harsh winters and long tradition, wearing furs remains popular in Russia, where organizations like People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals have been unable to make man