'nyt://article/2e111f89-2565-5a95-975d-caaa3485aa2d'}, {'abstract': 'In January, the state will adopt a new building code that should cut the energy consumption of new single-family homes by more than 15 percent. Environmentalists welcome the stronger code, but builders have concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/new-codes-aim-to-cut-energy-use.html', 'snippet': 'In January, the state will adopt a new building code that should cut the energy consumption of new single-family homes by more than 15 percent. Environmentalists welcome the stronger code, but builders have concerns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The international symbol for Texas’ energy-guzzling habit is a monster pickup truck — pulling another pickup truck. But homes and other buildings are also big offenders, accounting for roughly 40 percent of the state’s overall energy use.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Codes Aim to Cut Energy Use', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Codes Aim to Cut Energy Use', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-18T02:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Galbraith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galbraith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a57195a0-241e-5a02-8373-e31bc8d79a51', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a57195a0-241e-5a02-8373-e31bc8d79a51'}, {'abstract': 'The political parties have agreed to move the primaries to April 3, but without a decision on the redistricting maps, some candidates aren’t even sure in which districts they’ll be running.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/so-the-primaries-will-be-in-april-now-but-everythings-still-a-mess.html', 'snippet': 'The political parties have agreed to move the primaries to April 3, but without a decision on the redistricting maps, some candidates aren’t even sure in which districts they’ll be running.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a regular column for the Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So the Primaries Will Be in April Now, but Everything’s Still a Mess', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So the Primaries Will Be in April Now, but Everything’s Still a Mess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-18T02:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94911245-2e3b-5c39-bb0c-dcd47472f065', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94911245-2e3b-5c39-bb0c-dcd47472f065'}, {'abstract': 'A fleet of about 30 tugboats work the San Francisco Bay, helping cargo ships and tankers deal with challenges like wind, tides, currents, fogs and even parallel parking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/tugboats.html', 'snippet': 'A fleet of about 30 tugboats work the San Francisco Bay, helping cargo ships and tankers deal with challenges like wind, tides, currents, fogs and even parallel parking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 30 tugboats work San Francisco Bay, helping cargo ships and tankers navigate challenges of wind, tides, currents, fog and even parallel parking. A tugboat’s job isn’t only to tug large vessels: the tugs also help steer and brake the bigger boats.  LOUISE RAFKIN', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/18BCINTEL1/18BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/18/us/18BCINTEL1/18BCINTEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/18BCINTEL1/18BCINTEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/18/us/18BCINTEL1/18BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/18/us/18BCINTEL1/18BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tugboats', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen | Local Intelligence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tugboats: San Francisco Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tugboats and Towboats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-18T02:40:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Rafkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b54dcfb-cd48-503e-8ff0-bf158dd228ff', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b54dcfb-cd48-503e-8ff0-bf158dd228ff'}, {'abstract': 'The Sharp Park Golf Course in Pacifica has been chosen to undergo a transformation to National Park land, but a group of golfers — some as old as the course itself — are determined to keep Sharp Park open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/us/in-pacifica-the-angry-golfers-vs-the-supervisors-and-a-back-to-nature-plan.html', 'snippet': 'The Sharp Park Golf Course in Pacifica has been chosen to undergo a transformation to National Park land, but a group of golfers — some as old as the course itself — are determined to keep Sharp Park open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The game is not yet over at the Sharp Park Golf Course in Pacifica. A powerful group of advocates — some of them as old as this historic 79-year-old course overlooking the Pacific — is vowing to keep the links open, despite the San Francisco supervisors’ vote this week to begin a process to transform this 417 acres of oceanfront land into National Park land. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pacifica, the Angry Golfers vs. the Supervisors and a Back-to-Nature Plan', 'kicker': 'The Bay Area', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_