erry of Texas is giving more attention in his stump speech to his argument that faith should be more a part of public life and government.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/at-an-iowa-church-perry-takes-on-the-role-of-faith-in-government/', 'snippet': 'As the Jan. 3 Iowa caucuses near, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas is giving more attention in his stump speech to his argument that faith should be more a part of public life and government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLES CITY, Iowa — First Wesleyan Church is about as far away as you can imagine from the brightly-lit debate halls and smart-alecky pundits who have bedeviled Gov. Rick Perry of Texas on his long slide from Republican presidential frontrunner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At an Iowa Church, Perry Takes On the Role of Faith in Government', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-18T23:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9c0c084-ae52-5d4e-8e0b-2f4fee6770c3', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9c0c084-ae52-5d4e-8e0b-2f4fee6770c3'}, {'abstract': 'On average, candidates endorsed by The Des Moines Register have outperformed their polling numbers by a statistically insignificant 3-point margin.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/18/des-moines-register-endorsement-has-a-mixed-predictive-track-record/', 'snippet': 'On average, candidates endorsed by The Des Moines Register have outperformed their polling numbers by a statistically insignificant 3-point margin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of weeks ago we looked at the track record of candidates endorsed by The Union Leader of New Hampshire, and found that they had historically performed quite strongly. Their actual vote share in the New Hampshire primary exceeded their standing in the polls at the time the endorsement was made by about 11 points on average.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Des Moines Register Endorsement Has a Mixed Predictive Track Record', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Des Moines Register', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T00:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f95932a-426d-57f7-8bc1-067e597bf557', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f95932a-426d-57f7-8bc1-067e597bf557'}, {'abstract': 'With two games remaining in a season marked by inconsistency, what signs have the Giants shown that they can put together two sol