ersons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T02:28:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/396def16-af5f-5306-b637-2397730834aa', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/396def16-af5f-5306-b637-2397730834aa'}, {'abstract': 'If industry wants to keep drilling for oil, it needs to commit fully to improving safety and preparedness, as do regulators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/opinion/lessons-of-the-deepwater-horizon.html', 'snippet': 'If industry wants to keep drilling for oil, it needs to commit fully to improving safety and preparedness, as do regulators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest investigative report on the Deepwater Horizon disaster in the Gulf of Mexico, released Wednesday, is an important reminder of industry’s past carelessness and a summons to vigilance in the future. It could not have been more timely, coming just as the Interior Department was concluding its first auction of new drilling leases in the gulf since the spill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons of the Deepwater Horizon', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons of the Deepwater Horizon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub