48772f8da'}, {'abstract': 'How North Korean state television broadcast the news of Kim Jong-il’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/with-word-of-leaders-death-come-tears-on-state-tv/', 'snippet': 'How North Korean state television broadcast the news of Kim Jong-il’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 12:55 p.m. As our colleagues Choe Sang-hun and David Sanger report, Kim Jong-il, the mysterious and mercurial dictator of North Korea, has died. The news rippled across the globe Sunday night after the country’s official news media proclaimed the leader dead by way of a black-clad television announcer who appeared to be holding back tears. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On North Korean State Television, News of the Leader’s Death and Floods of Tears', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T06:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfd1f541-fc0f-5068-b954-e6344785df46', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfd1f541-fc0f-5068-b954-e6344785df46'}, {'abstract': 'Amritsar signs up for high-tech transport.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/coming-to-amritsar-the-pod-car/', 'snippet': 'Amritsar signs up for high-tech transport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bangalore, Kolkata and Delhi may have the Metro, but Amritsar will soon have the Pod. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming to Amritsar, the Pod Car', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heathrow Airport (London)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T07:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae2bdc86-4d9a-5b79-b88e-3f2f9764ceaf', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae2bdc86-4d9a-5b79-b88e-3f2f9764ceaf'}, {'abstract': 'The death of Kim Jong-il plunged diplomats, military strategists and political leaders among its neighbors and much further afield into a state of uncertainty on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/world/asia/kim-jong-ils-death-inspires-anxiety.html', 'snippet': 'The death of Kim Jong-il plunged diplomats, military strategists and political leaders among its neighbors and much further afield into a state of uncertainty on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The death of Kim Jong-il provoked uncertainty, anxiety and calls for a peaceful succession on Monday as governments within the region and beyond awaited some signal from North Korea about its nuclear intentions and the prospects, if any, for a new relationship with the world beyond its borders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kim’s Death Inspires Worries and Anxiety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kic