nytimes.com/2011/12/19/why-playoff-tiebreaker-favors-jets-over-bengals/', 'snippet': 'Strength of victory would be the deciding tiebreaker, and the Jets have an 11-victory edge over Cincinnati.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As most Jets fans know by now, the Jets will almost certainly make the playoffs if they win their last two games and finish 10-6. Cincinnati is the only other playoff contender that could finish 10-6, but the Jets would most likely win the fourth tiebreaker, strength of victory. Those odds only increased when San Diego defeated Baltimore on Sunday night. Here is how it would break down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Playoff Tiebreaker Favors  Jets Over Bengals', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T11:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Bretherton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bretherton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75e1f925-d58a-5434-b0f5-a66d6b95599d', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75e1f925-d58a-5434-b0f5-a66d6b95599d'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: How much sleep are you getting?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/this-week-in-small-business-making-lists/', 'snippet': 'Plus: How much sleep are you getting?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: Making Lists', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the