The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Green Groups, a Shift in Tactics', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T12:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16cfe0a3-35d6-5e25-a6db-7bce9ebd12b8', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16cfe0a3-35d6-5e25-a6db-7bce9ebd12b8'}, {'abstract': 'Rex Ryan said of the intensity of the coming matchup with the GIants: “To say that there won’t be any extra incentive is not right.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/rex-ryan-on-giants-game-its-going-to-be-ridiculous/', 'snippet': 'Rex Ryan said of the intensity of the coming matchup with the GIants: “To say that there won’t be any extra incentive is not right.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few excerpts from Rex Ryan’s talk with reporters after the loss to the Eagles on Sunday. The full transcript is at Jets.com:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rex Ryan on Giants Game: ‘It’s Going to Be Ridiculous’', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T12:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8a91bd5-6d7e-52f0-9bee-cd65690bc308', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8a91bd5-6d7e-52f0-9bee-cd65690bc308'}, {'abstract': 'Bonnie Hammer’s profitable reign at NBCUniversal, the bad and worst ads of the year, Louis C.K. cuts out the middleman and mourning the deaths of Vaclav Havel and the Russian journalist Khadzhimurad Kamalov.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-19/', 'snippet': 'Bonnie Hammer’s profitable reign at NBCUniversal, the bad and worst ads of the year, Louis C.K. cuts out the middleman and mourning the deaths of Vaclav Havel and the Russian journalist Khadzhimurad Kamalov.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bonnie Hammer’s attention to detail and programming instincts at NBCUniversal networks like USA has made her possibly the “most important executive” in cable television, Bill Carter writes, and a critical piece of Comcast’s takeover of the company last year. In her career, she identified Bob Vila as a host, taught Vince McMahon how to build story arcs into wrestling and made USA a powerhouse with shows like “Royal Pains” and “Burn Notice.” Yet the job she really wanted – turning out NBC’s dismal primetime – somehow has escaped her. Mr. Carter writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 19', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Bonnie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Havel, Vaclav', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Velvet Revolution', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T12:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e41ada5-87c4-5cb5-9beb-278f1c7abb09', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e41ada5-87c4-5cb5-9beb-278f1c7abb09'}, {'abstract': 'The latest Public Policy Polling survey published late Sunday showed Newt Gingrich’s support slipping badly in Iowa and Ron Paul moving into the lead.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/paul-moves-into-lead-in-iowa-forecast/', 'snippet': 'The latest Public Policy Polling survey published late Sunday showed Newt Gingrich’s support slipping badly in Iowa and Ron Paul moving into the lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Iowa forecasts, which are designed to be quite aggressive, have had a big reaction to the new Public Policy Polling survey published late Sunday evening. The poll showed Newt Gingrich’s support slipping badly in Iowa and Ron Paul moving into the lead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Moves Into Lead in Iowa Forecast', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T12:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c943bd3-0c8a-51dd-a99d-0f36ef67cffd', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c943bd3-0c8a-51dd-a99d-0f36ef67cffd'}, {'abstract': 'The growth was a “barely palpable” 0.4 percent, Kantar Media reported. While midsize advertisers increased their spending, the largest companies decided to become very conservative in their spending.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/ad-spending-slowed-to-a-crawl-in-the-3rd-quarter-report-finds/', 'snippet': 'The growth was a “barely palpable” 0.4 percent, Kantar Media reported. While midsize advertisers increased their spending, the largest companies decided to become very conservative in their spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like traffic on the way to the beach on a summer Friday afternoon, advertising spending in the third quarter barely moved, according to a report to be released on Monday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ad Spending Slowed to a Crawl in the 3rd Quarter, Report Finds', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kantar Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T13:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f52e29-8a85-5000-8afd-d50c18433297', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f52e29-8a85-5000-8afd-d50c18433297'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, Apple will stop accepting app submissions until after Christmas, and developers are scrambling to beat the deadline, Jenna Wortham reports in Monday’s New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/daily-report-an-apps-holiday/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, Apple will stop accepting app submissions until after Christmas, and developers are scrambling to beat the deadline, Jenna Wortham reports in Monday’s New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who leave their Christmas shopping for the final hours are not the only ones feeling anxious these days. Developers of apps for Apple products are also stressed out, Jenna Wortham reports in Monday’s New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: An Apps Holiday', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'p