 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/528d20f0-5755-5db7-8700-eb14e36b236b'}, {'abstract': 'A warning about water damage to the iPod Nano, if it’s used as a wristwatch.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/hand-washers-beware-your-ipod-nano-could-get-hurt/', 'snippet': 'A warning about water damage to the iPod Nano, if it’s used as a wristwatch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love the thought of using the tiny iPod Nano as a wristwatch. It comes with 16 gorgeous animated “watch faces,” and in my recent column, I noted that you can even buy a variety of watchbands for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hand-Washers Beware: Your iPod Nano Could Get Hurt', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPod', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd543fe3-8595-50e6-acf2-9a2a700a48f9', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd543fe3-8595-50e6-acf2-9a2a700a48f9'}, {'abstract': 'Save your elite flier status while you can, making telephone calls behind the wheel is likened to smoking, the 100-watt bulb is on the way out and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/monday-reading-save-your-elite-flyer-status-while-you-can/', 'snippet': 'Save your elite flier status while you can, making telephone calls behind the wheel is likened to smoking, the 100-watt bulb is on the way out and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Save Your Elite Flier Status While You Can', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/054e5939-42e7-5982-9a21-ef649636a195', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/054e5939-42e7-5982-9a21-ef649636a195'}, {'abstract': 'About those unit labor costs.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/irish-competitiveness-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'About those unit labor costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More abut Ireland: one of the reasons it has been touted as a great success story for austerity is the fact that unit labor costs have fallen sharply, suggesting that Ireland is well along in the process of “internal devaluation”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irish Competitiveness (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba731c9f-9092-59c4-a663-c0884a2ae0a5', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba731c9f-9092-59c4-a663-c0884a2ae0a5'}, {'abstract': 'For China’s government, social stability is threatened by a gender imbalance likely to leave up to 40 million Chinese without a wife.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-plight-of-chinas-favored-sons/', 'snippet': 'For China’s government, social stability is threatened by a gender imbalance likely to leave up to 40 million Chinese without a wife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ZHUHAI, China — In the rural Chinese town where Li Yiming grew up, the gossip mill starts to turn if a man is still single at 25. As he nears this milestone, the 23-year-old Li, an assembly-line worker in the coastal city of Zhuhai, is despondent. He knows he’ll never earn enough at any factory to win the approval of his girlfriend’s parents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Plight of China’s Favored Sons', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Harney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5121c3-346e-53dc-8fc3-1d5a49cbb334', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5121c3-346e-53dc-8fc3-1d5a49cbb334'}, {'abstract': 'Cloud computing may be about more than just more efficient and supple software, or mobile systems that allow work from anywhere. To some of the leading companies in the field, it’s about a whole new social style of management.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-coming-war-for-the-social-workplace/', 'snippet': 'Cloud computing may be about more than just more efficient and supple software, or mobile systems that allow work from anywhere. To some of the leading companies in the field, it’s about a whole new social style of management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hard-nosed competition for billions in corporate software spending is heading for an improbable showdown: Will the boss “like” that product prototyping cost projection?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Coming War for the Social Workplace', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benioff, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Salesforce.com Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAP A.G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95659d0c-13b2-53e7-a8c0-6883b1f0bcb2', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95659d0c-13b2-53e7-a8c0-6883b1f0bcb2'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s complaint: those black blobs, millions of them dotting walkways all over the city.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/complaint-box-sidewalk-gum/', 'snippet': 'This week’s complaint: those black blobs, millions of them dotting walkways all over the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had seen the blobs before — but it wasn’t until I lost my hearing aid that I had an in-your-face encounter with them. While searching for the device, I retraced my steps — same elevator, same route, focusing like a mine sweeper, gazing left to right, right to left — but my view was blocked by chewed-up pieces of gum in varying stages of decay, from light-colored, freshly spat out, to deeply embedded, flat and black. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Sidewalk Gum', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chewing Gum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sidewalks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T14:34:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sue Plastrik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sue', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plastrik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14fdc931-4d92-5fc7-816b-f1fa2d21bbf1', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14fdc931-4d92-5fc7-816b-f1fa2d21bbf1'}, {'abstract': 'Refusing to take yes for an answer.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/keynesophobia/', 'snippet': 'Refusing to take yes for an answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Baker is once again justifiably mad at Robert Samuelson. It is indeed frustrating that after three years in which Keynesian predictions have been spectacularly correct, pundits insist on reading the evidence as a rejection of Keynes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keynesophobia', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k