hird day as hundreds of people took to the streets to protest a bloody police crackdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/world/asia/antigovernment-protests-spread-to-western-kazakhstan.html', 'snippet': 'The police and striking workers clashed for a third day as hundreds of people took to the streets to protest a bloody police crackdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Hundreds of people took to the streets in western Kazakhstan on Monday in defiance of a bloody police crackdown on striking oil workers that has caused dozens of casualties in the Central Asian nation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defying Police Crackdown, Kazakh Protests Continue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Police Crackdown, Kazakh Protests Continue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kazakhstan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/335ac120-7916-5ee7-b513-3213383fe47a', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/335ac120-7916-5ee7-b513-3213383fe47a'}, {'abstract': 'The details explained.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/hungarys-constitutional-revolution/', 'snippet': 'The details explained.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I devoted a column to the unsettling political developments in Hungary. To expand on all this, I’ve asked my Princeton colleague Kim Lane Scheppele, who has been working extensively on the situation, to contribute a post. It’s below the fold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hungary’s Constitutional Revolution', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee467d47-e807-51b5-8226-20c9b2851b48', 'word_count': 1980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee467d47-e807-51b5-8226-20c9b2851b48'}, {'abstract': 'Cash mobs urge shoppers to support local businesses and make an event out of it by having everyone show up at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/cash-mobs-promote-spending-and-socializing-locally/', 'snippet': 'Cash mobs urge shoppers to support local businesses and make an event out of it by having everyone show up at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated at 11:04 a.m. / To reflect that another cash mob was held last week in Cleveland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cash Mobs Promote Spending (and Socializing) Locally', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6148db6-4ea1-5430-af90-a1f2a34c4188', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6148db6-4ea1-5430-af90-a1f2a34c4188'}, {'abstract': 'The Houston DJ and record executive OG Ron C has “chopped and screwed” Drake’s hit rap album “Take Care.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/charting-drake-and-chop-care/', 'snippet': 'The Houston DJ and record executive OG Ron C has “chopped and screwed” Drake’s hit rap album “Take Care.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the mixtape “Chop Care,” the Houston DJ and record executive OG Ron C has “chopped and screwed” Drake’s hit rap album “Take Care.” That is, he’s slowed it way down, cut it up and stretched it out, like something you’d want to hear full of cold medicine in your bed. The artist Andrew Kuo prefers it to the original, and here he breaks it down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting Drake and ‘Chop Care’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '