d dozens of civilians at sites in Libya examined by The New York Times, but NATO has largely refused to acknowledge or investigate the casualties.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-times-investigates-in-libya-conflicting-reports-of-civilian-casualties/', 'snippet': 'NATO airstrikes killed and wounded dozens of civilians at sites in Libya examined by The New York Times, but NATO has largely refused to acknowledge or investigate the casualties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In case you missed it over the weekend:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times Investigates: In Libya, Conflicting Reports of Civilian Casualties', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:38:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45054b8-35a4-5ebc-8c82-04d5378ce921', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45054b8-35a4-5ebc-8c82-04d5378ce921'}, {'abstract': 'An expert in educator sexual misconduct said she has seen many instances when social media has been used to target, groom and harm students. But by taking care to make intentional decisions about how to use social media and keep professional and private lives separate, Twitter, Facebook and texting can boost student learning and engagement. Here is her advice for teachers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/19/using-social-media-to-teach-keep-it-transparent-open-and-safe/', 'snippet': 'An expert in educator sexual misconduct said she has seen many instances when social media has been used to target, groom and harm students. But by taking care to make intentional decisions about how to use social media and keep professional and p...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Social Media to Teach: Keep It Transparent, Open and Safe', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By CHAROL SHAKESHAFT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SHAKESHAFT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c5a4a5a-e032-5b0a-bd6a-3740e6ae552d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c5a4a5a-e032-5b0a-bd6a-3740e6ae552d'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Sternberg, the deputy chancellor for portfolio planning, responds to some of the questions left over after the SchoolBook community event at the Pratt Institute on Dec. 8. Parents asked about their options, tutoring and "what happens to the students that schools don\'t compete for," among other topics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/19/deputy-chancellor-responds-to-your-school-choice-questions/', 'snippet': 'Marc Sternberg, the deputy chancellor for portfolio planning, responds to some of the questions left over after the SchoolBook community event at the Pratt Institute on Dec. 8. Parents asked about their options, tutoring and "what happens to the s...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'he