m the real estate photos, the provenance of the Upper West Side pre-war co-op for sale is not readily apparent, but there are some clues. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Sale: A Former M.T.A. Chief’s Home, MetroCards Not Included', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walder, Jay H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T15:55:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a956bc3-9a12-5fa8-bb78-d527e056b3f9', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a956bc3-9a12-5fa8-bb78-d527e056b3f9'}, {'abstract': 'Marketo is a Web-based sales-and-marketing service that tracks all of your interactions with potential customers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/a-marketing-tool-that-identifies-your-best-prospects/', 'snippet': 'Marketo is a Web-based sales-and-marketing service that tracks all of your interactions with potential customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In September, Micky Thompson, who started a shipping-related business last year, headed out from his headquarters in Tucson, Ariz., to make a pickup in San Francisco. It wasn’t a shipment he was handling, though. Rather, he was traveling to a software conference to track down a product that might improve his marketing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Marketing Tool That Identifies Your Best Prospects', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d4bc38-f633-519f-8e13-500e6810c172', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d4bc38-f633-519f-8e13-500e6810c172'}, {'abstract': 'The professional skateboarder and occasional stunt driver performed the trick as part of his reality television show on MTV.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/rob-dyrdek-kick-flips-a-chevy-sonic/', 'snippet': 'The professional skateboarder and occasional stunt driver performed the trick as part of his reality television show on MTV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the season premiere of his reality program “Rob Dyrdek’s Fantasy Factory,” which airs on MTV, Mr. Dyrdek, a professional skateboarder and occasional stunt driver, performed a 360-degree kick flip in a Chevrolet Sonic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rob Dyrdek Kick-Flips a Chevy Sonic', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dyrdek, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/063632ee-ff9b-5240-857d-f69e4caf31df', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/063632ee-ff9b-5240-857d-f69e4caf31df'}, {'abstract': 'Experts linked illegal logging to deadly floods in the Philippines that have killed more than 600 people.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/on-our-radar-hundreds-die-in-floods-in-the-philippines/', 'snippet': 'Experts linked illegal logging to deadly floods in the Philippines that have killed more than 600 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Experts cite deforestation from illegal logging in the Philippines as a factor in catastrophic flooding on northern Mindanao over the weekend. The death toll there has reached 632, federal disaster officials say. [The Philippine Star] ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Hundreds Die in Floods in the Philippines', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2f37384-999f-53c0-bb0a-cb155e4e6d96', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2f37384-999f-53c0-bb0a-cb155e4e6d96'}, {'abstract': 'Now more than ever, it’s more important to be honest with our children about the delicate issues of wealth and class.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/mom-are-we-the-1-percent/', 'snippet': 'Now more than ever, it’s more important to be honest with our children about the delicate issues of wealth and class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, my son was playing with a group of friends at our house after a sleepover. As the boys’ parents drifted in and out to pick them up, some lingered in the kitchen, drinking coffee and chatting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mom, Are We the 1 Percent?’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randye Hoder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randye', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f6ad1db-9130-517f-8e4a-cb75c22a5c6e', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f6ad1db-9130-517f-8e4a-cb75c22a5c6e'}, {'abstract': 'As members of Congress debate the Stop Internet Piracy Act,  there is nothing cute about pretending the last 20 years of the consumer Web never took place.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-not-so-charming-internet-know-nothings/', 'snippet': 'As members of Congress debate the Stop Internet Piracy Act,  there is nothing cute about pretending the last 20 years of the consumer Web never took place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of us have watched the debate over the various legislative efforts to rein in piracy in the media and entertainment world and felt that some of it was beyond our ken. Part of that has to do with hyperbole and propaganda around legislation like the Stop Online Piracy Act. Given the stakes, the middle ground disappeared rapidly and there was a whole lot of shouting going on. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Not-So-Charming Internet Know-Nothings', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43dfd1c4-581e-5ec6-83e1-907d650362b5', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43dfd1c4-581e-5ec6-83e1-907d650362b5'}, {'abstract': 'Rag & Bone’s prefall included layered looks that have as much texture as they do attitude.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/just-one-look-rag-bone/', 'snippet': 'Rag & Bone’s prefall included layered looks that have as much texture as they do attitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rag & Bone’s prefall wasn’t cold-weather wear by convention\xa0––\xa0powder blue cotton floral dresses; watercolor pleated silk skirts; the softest, see-through knit tanks; a striped linen version of their favorite Newbury boot –– but when you wear a multitude of pieces from the collection all at once, out come layered looks that have as much texture as they do attitude. Here, a geo-leather skirt with a fire red tank over a ribbed knit shell illustrate the point perfectly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Rag & Bone', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rag & Bone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T16:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a97d69-7866-50fe-862f-90828594d9cc', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a97d69-7866-50fe-862f-90828594d9cc'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 12.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/19/fashion/streetstylemonochromatic.html', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/streetstylemonochromatic-slide-6EI1/streetstylemonochromatic-slide-6EI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/streetstylemonochromatic-slide-6EI1/streetstylemonochromatic-slide-6EI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/streetstylemonochromatic-slide-6EI1/streetstylemonoc