'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christie Aschwanden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aschwanden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cdb2042-bff5-5e35-860d-7f64eb88bf73', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cdb2042-bff5-5e35-860d-7f64eb88bf73'}, {'abstract': 'The Chiefs showed on Sunday that the way to beat the Packers is to overwhelm their offensive line. The question is whether that game plan is repeatable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/sports/football/a-crack-in-the-packers-invincibility-nfl-fast-forward.html', 'snippet': 'The Chiefs showed on Sunday that the way to beat the Packers is to overwhelm their offensive line. The question is whether that game plan is repeatable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was difficult not to watch the Green Bay Packers lose on Sunday afternoon and shrug. They never made going undefeated a goal, and so their shocking loss to Kansas City perhaps said more about the Chiefs, revived under the interim coach Romeo Crennel, than it did about the Packers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/sports/FORWARD/FORWARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/20/sports/FORWARD/FORWARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/sports/FORWARD/FORWARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/sports/FORWARD/FORWARD-t