 concern?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of Coach Tom Coughlin’s news conference Sunday, a reporter asked for his assessment of the rookie cornerback Prince Amukamara. Coughlin hesitated. Then he said, “It seemed like they threw the ball in that direction and we were not having a lot of success.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assessing Giants Cornerback Prince Amukamara', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amukamara, Prince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/531d1a6b-f83c-593b-ad72-7ac120cc03de', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/531d1a6b-f83c-593b-ad72-7ac120cc03de'}, {'abstract': 'In the McMurdo Dry Valleys of Antarctica, there are a surprisingly large number of mummified penguins and seals.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/awakening-streams-and-mummified-seals/', 'snippet': 'In the McMurdo Dry Valleys of Antarctica, there are a surprisingly large number of mummified penguins and seals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alia Khan, a graduate student at the University of Colorado, Boulder, writes from the McMurdo Dry Valleys in Antarctica, where she is studying ephemeral glacier fed streams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Awakening Streams and Mummified Seals', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seals (Animals) and Sealing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alia Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a8a6f9f-a961-5864-9df4-b49416836236', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8a6f9f-a961-5864-9df4-b49416836236'}, {'abstract': 'Monday’s announcement gives a sense of the logical sequence in which the justices will approach the four challenges to President Obama’s landmark health care overhaul law.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/supreme-court-to-hear-health-care-case-in-late-march/', 'snippet': 'Monday’s announcement gives a sense of the logical sequence in which the justices will approach the four challenges to President Obama’s landmark health care overhaul law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court announced on Monday that it would devote three days in late March to hearing arguments in challenges to the 2010 health care overhaul law. A decision in the case is expected by the end of June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court to Hear Health Care Case in Late March', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee506143-a2bd-5e39-b825-74c129f2c377', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee506143-a2bd-5e39-b825-74c129f2c377'}, {'abstract': 'Whose songs do you encounter way too often in restaurants, and which performers would you like to hear a lot more of?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-queen-of-the-bistro-playlist/', 'snippet': 'Whose songs do you encounter way too often in restaurants, and which performers would you like to hear a lot more of?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re like me, you mourned the passing of Cesária Évora over the weekend. And if you happened to spin a few of her albums on Saturday and Sunday afternoon, maybe while roasting dinner, it’s not impossible that her songs summoned up the memory of a few excellent meals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Queen of the Bistro Playlist', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ffc27ed-10bc-5f67-86a7-5308a1bd72b9', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ffc27ed-10bc-5f67-86a7-5308a1bd72b9'}, {'abstract': 'Corn tortillas and a spread of flavorful fillings make for festive do-it-yourself meals perfect for a busy week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/tacos-for-the-holidays-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Corn tortillas and a spread of flavorful fillings make for festive do-it-yourself meals perfect for a busy week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The holiday season can be like an ongoing house party. Children are home from school, their friends are coming by, relatives are in from out of town, and one meal follows the next. One way to meet the challenge of feeding everybody is to pick up a supply of corn tortillas (all the better if more locally made) and make a big pot of beans and some other dishes that are at home in a taco. Buy a few jars of salsa, or make your own, and your house will be taco party central during the busy holiday week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1497, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tacos for the Holidays', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tacos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/e137e4b1-a427-56d5-9f26-7354400c6aaf', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e137e4b1-a427-56d5-9f26-7354400c6aaf'}, {'abstract': 'Sean Parker, the entrepreneur probably now most famous for being portrayed in the movie “The Social Network,” struggles with his fame. Whether by design or impulse, Mr. Parker, one of the people behind Napster and Facebook, has an almost compulsive need to share whatever is on his mind. His publicist tells him to be quiet, but he often shrugs his shoulders and carries on.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/sean-parker-struggles-with-fame/', 'snippet': 'Sean Parker, the entrepreneur probably now most famous for being portrayed in the movie “The Social Network,” struggles with his fame. Whether by design or impulse, Mr. Parker, one of the people behind Napster and Facebook, has an almost compulsiv...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the Thanksgiving holiday, I interviewed Sean Parker, a founder of Napster and a former president of Facebook, for a profile that ran in The New York Times Sunday Style section. Some of the reaction online to the article suggested that Mr. Parker was reminiscent of Steve Jobs, a founder of Apple, who died in October at 56. I believe it is too soon to make that comparison. The next five years are crucial for Mr. Parker, who has yet to prove he is an influential force in Silicon Valley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sean Parker Struggles With Fame', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Napster', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T17:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura M. Holson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e35bb3f-41eb-5659-b056-4c3d64585ff7', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e35bb3f-41eb-5659-b056-4c3d64585ff7'}, {'abstract': 'The album will feature standards from his youth, “the songs which inspired the songs” Paul McCartney wrote with John Lennon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/new-mccartney-album-a-trip-down-memory-lane/', 'snippet': 'The album will feature standards from his youth, “the songs which inspired the songs” Paul McCartney wrote with John Lennon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the enduring questions in the history of pop music is how two teenagers from Liverpool with a background in skiffle and rock ‘n’ roll became the most inventive songwriters of the last 50 years, producing an enormous variety of tunes that broke new ground for pop music both melodically and harmonically.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New McCartney Album Is a Trip Down Memory Lane', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARLEN, HAROLD', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapton, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krall, Diana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porter, Cole', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wonder, Stevie', 'ra