e': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f916e111-108c-5620-9eb2-e192a9c86a83', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f916e111-108c-5620-9eb2-e192a9c86a83'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s attack on the judiciary is downright frightening.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/why-not-just-call-for-martial-law-and-be-done-with-it/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s attack on the judiciary is downright frightening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been no shortage of wacky ideas from the Republican candidates, but Newt Gingrich’s attacks on the judiciary are truly far out on the lunatic fringe of right-wing politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Not Just Call for Martial Law and Be Done With It?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T18:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/569f96b9-d719-5f82-bc1a-1d4bf8bdfeea', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/569f96b9-d719-5f82-bc1a-1d4bf8bdfeea'}, {'abstract': 'Creatures of Comfort, the NoLIta boutique, now has silk pajamas.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/start-the-pajama-party-jammy-comfort-foods/', 'snippet': 'Creatures of Comfort, the NoLIta boutique, now has silk pajamas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HERE’S a bit of good news for 11th-hour shoppers: Creatures of Comfort, the year-old NoLIta boutique by way of Los Angeles, has added silk pajamas to its private label for the holidays. “I remember looking for these pajamas and not finding them except when I visited Asia,” said Jade Lai, the owner. “So last year I made my holiday wish list for things to stock this season, and silk pajamas were on the top of the list.” The luxurious unisex pajamas come in eight different color combinations, including navy blue with red piping, as well as black, white, lavender and emerald green, all with contrasting piping. Silky PJ’s from Creatures of Comfort? Sounds right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Start the Pajama Party', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pajamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creatures of Comfort', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NoLIta (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T18:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14822e2e-7898-5443-983b-ef5d3b2530d6', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14822e2e-7898-5443-983b-ef5d3b2530d6'}, {'abstract': 'New restrictions on federally financed experiments involving chimpanzees may be a turning point in how humans deal with other species.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/science/recognition-of-chimps-as-relatives-may-reshape-research.html', 'snippet': 'New restrictions on federally financed experiments involving chimpanzees may be a turning point in how humans deal with other species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Dr. Francis S. Collins, the head of the National Institutes of Health, announced Thursday that the government would halt all new grants for research on chimpanzees, it was, in one sense, a familiar Washington moment. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elevation of the Chimp May Reshape Research', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elevation of the Chimp May Reshape Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Francis S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T18:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d086c7c-18a7-5c72-8f6e-5f702e8d5160', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d086c7c-18a7-5c72-8f6e-5f702e8d5160'}, {'abstract': 'Photojournalists reflect on their experiences covering the Iraq war.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/in-the-images-of-war-reflections-and-lessons-learned/', 'snippet': 'Photojournalists reflect on their experiences covering the Iraq war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the early days of the Iraq war, images from photojournalists on the ground provided a glimpse of the the triumphs and shortcomings of a conflict that polarized the American people. As photographers pack up their equipment to return home, one reflects in a post today on the Lens blog on the memories and lessons created while in Iraq.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Images of War, Reflections and Lessons Learned', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T19:04:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a230fa53-2012-5c96-a416-49c3432f7eac', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a230fa53-2012-5c96-a416-49c3432f7eac'}, {'abstract': 'The day in sports included the Arab Games, which continued in Doha, Qatar, as well as World Cup skiing in Alta Badia, Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/19/sports/20111219-photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'The day in sports included the Arab Games, which continued in Doha, Qatar, as well as World Cup skiing in Alta Badia, Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day in sports included the Arab Games, which continued in Doha, Qatar, as well as World Cup skiing in Alta Badia, Italy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/sports/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/sports/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/19/sports/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO/20111219-photoreplay-slide-FCUO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Dec.19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wrestling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T19:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9ec37f99-005f-558f-8c92-851e4f208670', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9ec37f99-005f-558f-8c92-851e4f208670'}, {'abstract': 'There are no Vaclav Havels in North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/prague-and-pyongyang/', 'snippet': 'There are no Vaclav Havels in North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deaths of Vaclav Havel and Kim Jong Il within a 24-hour span are more than a reminder of the extremes of heroism and iniquity that coexist in human affairs. They’re a reminder of how much successful political heroism depends, in the end, on the ability to prick the conscience of iniquity, and to remind even the worst regimes and most compromised authorities that there are moral absolutes which they transgress at their peril. The great success of the Velvet Revolution, like the successes of Gandhi and Mandela and Martin Luther King and so many other icons of peaceful revolution, was achieved by public argument as well as by public protest, and by the fact that the bureaucrats and apparatchiks and generals the revolutionaries were confronting weren’t willing to take the most absolute and unthinkable steps to retain their privileges and defend their power. (In David Chappell’s “A Stone of Hope,” a history of religion and the civil rights movement, there’s a fascinating account of how this worked in the white South — the way that the Christian appeals of King and Ralph Abernathy and Co. persuaded many white Christians that they had a moral obligation to stand by and let the revolution happen, rather than defend Jim Crow to the end.) When civil disobedience works, it does so by reminding the inhumane of their inhumanity, and by finding the vulnerabilities in what seem like permanently hardened hearts. In this sense, there’s a circular quality to any successful peaceful revolt: No De Klerk without Mandela but also no Mandela (as we know Mandela) without De Klerk; no Gorbachev without Sakharov and Walesa and Havel, but no Havel and Walesa (as we know them) without Gorbachev.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prague and Pyongyang', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T19:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8407b46-8b7a-5638-913e-c12d46379d76', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8407b46-8b7a-5638-913e-c12d46379d76'}, {'abstract': 'The warrant against Vice President Tariq al-Hashimi on terrorism charges was issued on Monday as his party threatened to pull out of the coalition with the Shiite-led government.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/big-deal-iraqi-government-accuses-top-official-in-assassinations/', 'snippet': 'The warrant against Vice President Tariq al-Hashimi on terrorism charges was issued on Monday as his party threatened to pull out of the coalition with the Shiite-led government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We just published an important article from Jack Healy in Baghdad:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Deal: Iraqi Government Accuses Top Official in Assassinations', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hashimi, Tariq al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T19:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/961c9ab6-8b86-51fa-b212-31d72402473f', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/961c9ab6-8b86-51fa-b212-31d72402473f'}, {'abstract': 'Arkansas State’s new football coach, Gus Malzahn, will make significantly more money than this predecessor, Hugh Freeze.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/arkansas-state-raises-salary-for-new-coach/', 'snippet': 'Arkansas State’s new football coach, Gus Malzahn, will make significantly more money than this predecessor, Hugh Freeze.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arkansas State University’s new head football coach figures to earn at least four times as much money as his predecessor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas State Raises Salary for New Coach', 'kicker'