 classroom? School districts, rushing into social media policies, don’t know yet either.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Should schools regulate or ban communications between teachers and students by cellphone, Facebook or e-mail? Jennifer Preston, a Times reporter, found districts in New York State and across the country scrambling to create a social media policy in the wake of a few inappropriate relationships that included electronic communications. A district in Georgia has banned private electronic communication entirely; Missouri is revamping such a rule after teachers persuaded a judge that the proposed law was unconstitutional. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Students and Teachers Be Facebook Friends?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c38f89b-ed9b-53e0-a8cd-252e53dd70b0', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c38f89b-ed9b-53e0-a8cd-252e53dd70b0'}, {'abstract': 'The more complete playback numbers reveal large gains for “New Girl,” a freshman sitcom on Fox. It posted the largest prime-time gain in total viewers among shows on broadcast networks.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/new-girl-on-fox-gets-a-lift-from-dvr-use/', 'snippet': 'The more complete playback numbers reveal large gains for “New Girl,” a freshman sitcom on Fox. It posted the largest prime-time gain in total viewers among shows on broadcast networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fox received a bit of good news from the latest DVR rankings report, which includes the initial live broadcast viewership figures and DVR-playback numbers for the next seven days. For the week of Nov. 28 to Dec. 5, the freshman comedy “New Girl” on Fox not only posted the largest gain in total viewers, 3.1 million, but it also had the largest ratings increase in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic considered important to advertisers. (The show reached 10.7 million viewers, up from 7.6 million.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘New Girl’ on Fox Gets a Lift From DVR Use', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gellar, Sarah Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3169679-5bfd-5aea-a11a-b56964e866c5', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3169679-5bfd-5aea-a11a-b56964e866c5'}, {'abstract': 'The rule against posthumous Nobel Prizes has been violated several times — most recently when the prize in medicine was given to the widow of a Rockefeller University scientist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/health/when-the-honor-of-a-lifetime-a-nobel-prize-arrives-too-late.html', 'snippet': 'The rule against posthumous Nobel Prizes has been violated several times — most recently when the prize in medicine was given to the widow of a Rockefeller University scientist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alfred B. Nobel created the prizes that bear his name, he decreed that they be given for work done in the preceding year. A seemingly simple provision, intuitively sensible to anyone who follows the Oscars, the Emmys or the Pulitzers. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20JPDOCS_SPAN/20JPDOCS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20JPDOCS_SPAN/20JPDOCS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20JPDOCS_SPAN/20JPDOCS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Honor of a Lifetime, Arriving Too Late', 'kicker': 'The Doctor’s World', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honor of a Lifetime, Arriving Too Late', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence K. Altman, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca826645-8edd-55f8-8492-6f2832dff85b', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca826645-8edd-55f8-8492-6f2832dff85b'}, {'abstract': '“Jim Henson’s Fantastic World,” which features artwork, props and puppets from “Sesame Street,” “The Muppet Show” and many more television and film projects, will run through March 4, the museum said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/muppet-show-continues-museum-of-moving-image-extends-jim-henson-exhibition/', 'snippet': '“Jim Henson’s Fantastic World,” which features artwork, props and puppets from “Sesame Street,” “The Muppet Show” and many more television and film projects, will run through March 4, the museum said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not unlike the ending of a certain hit movie that found the Muppets mobbed by fans they didn’t realize they had, the Museum of the Moving Image in Astoria, Queens, has learned that a lot of people really like Jim Henson’s creations – enough that it is extending the retrospective on that artist and puppeteer by almost two months. On Monday, the museum said that “Jim Henson’s Fantastic World,” the traveling Smithsonian exhibition on the life and work of the Muppets creator, will now run through March 4; it was originally scheduled to close on Jan. 16.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Muppet Show Continues: Museum Extends Jim Henson Exhibition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a5597a-82a7-5ca0-8a0d-5456be1f1d0c', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a5597a-82a7-5ca0-8a0d-5456be1f1d0c'}, {'abstract': 'The fraud charges filed by the Securities and Exchange Commission against six former executives of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac created a big splash, but a number of questions remain.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/closer-look-at-s-e-c-s-mortgage-fraud-charges/', 'snippet': 'The fraud charges filed by the Securities and Exchange Commission against six former executives of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac created a big splash, but a number of questions remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The civil securities fraud charges filed by the Securities and Exchange Commission against six former executives of the mortgage giants Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac signal an aggressive turn in the pursuit of cases tied to the subprime mortgage crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Closer Look at S.E.C.’s Mortgage Fraud Charges', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mudd, Daniel H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Syron, Richard F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freddie Mac', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:16:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/675ac050-6d41-520f-9aaa-91ccd6640d0e', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/675ac050-6d41-520f-9aaa-91ccd6640d0e'}, {'abstract': 'The C.D.C. has found that a much shorter regimen of isoniazid doses along with another antibiotic, rifapentine, is just as effective as the standard nine-month-long treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/health/research/a-much-quicker-way-to-treat-latent-tb.html', 'snippet': 'The C.D.C. has found that a much shorter regimen of isoniazid doses along with another antibiotic, rifapentine, is just as effective as the standard nine-month-long treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The standard treatment for latent tuberculosis infection — that is, infection without symptoms — is nine months of daily doses of isoniazid, an antibiotic. The treatment is effective, but only about 60 percent of patients carry it out completely.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regimens: A Much Quicker Way to Treat Latent TB', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regimens: A Much Quicker Way to Treat Latent TB', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuberculosis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:22:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56e2bf36-ea8b-5f0b-8c2e-8218be641af9', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56e2bf36-ea8b-5f0b-8c2e-8218be641af9'}, {'abstract': 'Conclusions of an Oxford survey challenge some of the leading theories of social behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/science/genes-play-major-role-in-primate-social-behavior-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Conclusions of an Oxford survey challenge some of the leading theories of social behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Social behavior among primates — including humans — has a substantial genetic basis, a team of scientists has concluded from a new survey of social structure across the primate family tree.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genes Play Major Role in Primate Social Behavior, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genes Play Major Role in Primate Social Behavior, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxford University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T20:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4de3a20-50c8-5d13-9a8f-6f7cc02ac51f', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4de3a20-50c8-5d13-9a8f-6f7cc02ac51f'}, {'abstract': 'A report of the National Research Council on the scientific, technical, environmental, human health and safety, and regulatory aspect