st reached the playoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/lions-come-back-and-aim-for-a-wild-card/', 'snippet': 'It has been 12 years since the Lions, who are contending for a wild-card berth, last reached the playoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Detroit Lions are getting quite the reputation for being kings of the comeback. Their 28-27 victory Sunday over the Raiders, in Oakland, was their fourth come-from-behind win of the season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lions Come Back and Aim for a Wild Card', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Calvin (1985- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stafford, Matthew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suh, Ndamukong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/773505a1-1662-58f5-a7de-7a2084df4d4f', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/773505a1-1662-58f5-a7de-7a2084df4d4f'}, {'abstract': 'The gift ensured the success of Cornell’s proposal to build on city-owned land on Roosevelt Island. The city is also providing up to $100 million in infrastructure improvements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/nyregion/cornell-and-technion-israel-chosen-to-build-science-school-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'The gift ensured the success of Cornell’s proposal to build on city-owned land on Roosevelt Island. The city is also providing up to $100 million in infrastructure improvements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The donor whose $350 million gift will be critical in building Cornell University’s new high-tech graduate school on Roosevelt Island is Atlantic Philanthropies, whose founder, Charles F. Feeney, is a Cornell alumnus who made billions of dollars through the Duty Free Shoppers Group. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/nyregion/CORNELL1/CORNELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/20/nyregion/CORNELL1/CORNELL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/nyregion/CORNELL1/CORNELL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/nyregion/CORNELL1/CORNELL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/nyregion/CORNELL1/CORNELL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cornell Alumnus Is Behind $350 Million Gift to Build Science School in City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cornell Alumnus Behind $350 Million Gift to Build Science School in the City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Philanthropies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Technion-Israel Institute of Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feeney, Charles F', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ROOSEVELT ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:19:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49875e84-070e-5cc3-a836-abd8f238a394', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49875e84-070e-5cc3-a836-abd8f238a394'}, {'abstract': 'Lola Montes Schnabel talks up her one-woman show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/fashion/lola-montes-schnabels-art-exhibition-opens.html', 'snippet': 'Lola Montes Schnabel talks up her one-woman show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANACOLUTHON comes from the Greek words for “not” and “following.” It applies to both stream-of-consciousness writing and conversations with Lola Montes Schnabel, the outgoing young artist who was having her first solo show in New York last Friday.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/1222scenecity-slide-932S/1222scenecity-slide-932S-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/1222scenecity-slide-932S/1222scenecity-slide-932S-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/1222scenecity-slide-932S/1222scenecity-slide-932S-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/1222scenecity-slide-932S/1222scenecity-slide-932S-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/19/fashion/1222scenecity-slide-932S/1222scenecity-slide-932S-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Schnabel Art Show Monologue', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Schnabel Art Show Monologue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85606a2e-040f-51ce-9f22-8bdf7291afa0', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85606a2e-040f-51ce-9f22-8bdf7291afa0'}, {'abstract': 'Talks on a new contract broke down on Nov. 30, threatening the New York City Opera’s upcoming season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/mediator-sits-down-with-city-opera-and-union-leaders/', 'snippet': 'Talks on a new contract broke down on Nov. 30, threatening the New York City Opera’s upcoming season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Union leaders and management at New York City Opera met with a federal mediator on Monday morning in an effort to resolve a labor dispute that threatens the company’s season. One of the unions said the mediator, Allison Beck, the deputy director of the Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service, first met with both sides together and then separately. The union, the American Guild of Musical Artists, said in a statement that it agreed to return to negotiations on Jan. 3, just days before rehearsals are supposed to begin. The guild represents chorus members, stage managers and assistant directors. The orchestra’s union is also negotiating with the company’s management, which declined to comment on Monday, citing a news blackout requested by the mediator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mediator Sits Down With City Opera and Union Leaders', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GUILD OF MUSICAL ARTISTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/109e27df-12c0-5e93-879f-1f08bcdf69ce', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/109e27df-12c0-5e93-879f-1f08bcdf69ce'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers would have felt at home in ancient Dura-Europos, a multicultural city whose archaeological relics were found in present-day Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/science/dura-europos-a-melting-pot-at-the-intersection-of-empires.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers would have felt at home in ancient Dura-Europos, a multicultural city whose archaeological relics were found in present-day Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its time and place, the ancient city of Dura-Europos had much in common with today’s most cosmopolitan urban landscapes. Religious, linguistic and cultural diversity characterized much of the city’s life for more than 500 years, starting at the outset of the third century B.C. in what is now Syria.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20VIEW1/20VIEW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20VIEW1/20VIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20VIEW1/20VIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Melting Pot at the Intersection of Empires for Five Centuries', 'kicker': 'On View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Melting Pot at the Intersection of Empires for Five Centuries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for the Study of the Ancient World', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Noble Wilford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Noble', 'lastname': 'Wilford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/708b1233-83dc-589c-b4a6-5cfaf4cc5757', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708b1233-83dc-589c-b4a6-5cfaf4cc5757'}, {'abstract': 'Discrepancies in recording distances and pace can be frustrating for those training for races.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/health/nutrition/gps-watches-may-not-track-runs-accurately.html', 'snippet': 'Discrepancies in recording distances and pace can be frustrating for those training for races.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I used to run with a GPS watch, and at the time it seemed like a technological marvel.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20BEST/20BEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20BEST/20BEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/science/20BEST/20BEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'GPS Watch Can Be an Unreliable Running Partner', 'kicker': 'Personal Best', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'GPS Watch Can Be an Unreliable Running Partner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:34:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2774e2d0-0e6c-5067-b8e2-3c52559bb0f4', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2774e2d0-0e6c-5067-b8e2-3c52559bb0f4'}, {'abstract': 'The Times Square International Theater Festival will run Jan. 16-22 and will feature works from three continents.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/january-a-rich-month-for-international-theater-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The Times Square International Theater Festival will run Jan. 16-22 and will feature works from three continents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to festivals like Under the Radar and Coil, January is a busy month for devotees of international theater in New York. But things promise to be even more active than usual next month, when a new event called the Times Square International Theater Festival makes its debut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New International Theater Festival for New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preisser, Alfred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Classical Theater of Harlem', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50e0832b-78bd-5aa0-b4c9-0a454c6d5837', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50e0832b-78bd-5aa0-b4c9-0a454c6d5837'}, {'abstract': 'The Grammy award-winning rapper Common performed at the Eagle Academy for Young Men in the Bronx on Monday. He said he wanted to see the school after meeting its founding principal last year at a panel on education reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/19/im-in-the-right-place-common-tells-eagle-academy-boys/', 'snippet': 'The Grammy award-winning rapper Common performed at the Eagle Academy for Young Men in the Bronx on Monday. He said he wanted to see the school after meeting its founding principal last year at a panel on education reform.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "'I'm in the Right Place,' Common Tells Eagle Academy Boys", 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ABBIE FENTRESS SWANSON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abbie', 'middlename': 'Fentress', 'lastname': 'SWANSON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1576a825-4ede-528b-9deb-95011d4465ad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1576a825-4ede-528b-9deb-95011d4465ad'}, {'abstract': 'GPS watches for running are very much a work in progress. The technology is improving, but some inaccuracy remains, writes Gina Kolata in this week’s Science Times.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/the-problem-with-gps-watches-for-runners/', 'snippet': 'GPS watches for running are very much a work in progress. The technology is improving, but some inaccuracy remains, writes Gina Kolata in this week’s Science Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her latest Personal Best column, Gina Kolata explores an all too common problem for runners who use GPS watches to track their distance and pace. Many of the watches are simply not very accurate, recording incorrect times and distances, which can be a nuisance for runners who are training for races.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Problem With GPS Watches for Runners', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Navigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/feb286e8-a348-5640-9854-fbc33831deda', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feb286e8-a348-5640-9854-fbc33831deda'}, {'abstract': 'AT&T acknowledged that it could not overcome opposition from the Obama administration to creating the nation’s biggest cellphone service provider.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/att-withdraws-39-bid-for-t-mobile/', 'snippet': 'AT&T acknowledged that it could not overcome opposition from the Obama administration to creating the nation’s biggest cellphone service provider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT&T on Monday ended its effort to buy T-Mobile USA, acknowledging that it could not overcome stiff opposition by the Obama administration to form the nation’s biggest cellphone service provider.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AT&T Ends $39 Billion Bid for T-Mobile', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:44:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cddeae02-1022-58b1-9452-177ae39b1fdc', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cddeae02-1022-58b1-9452-177ae39b1fdc'}, {'abstract': 'A forward on an all-star team from Russia’s junior league writes about his experiences during a hockey tour of the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/feoktistovs-journal-a-russian-back-on-american-ice/', 'snippet': 'A forward on an all-star team from Russia’s junior league writes about his experiences during a hockey tour of the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My name is Nikita Feoktistov. I’m a 21-year-old forward on the Russian Red Stars, an all-star team from Russia’s junior league, the Minor Hockey League, that feeds the majors, the Kontinental Hockey League. The Red Stars are on a tour of the United States to play six N.C.A.A. schools including Notre Dame and two top amateur teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feoktistov’s Journal: A Russian Back on American Ice', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HOCKEY LEAGUE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kontinental Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Dakota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Feoktistov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feoktistov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/607228d0-1b4a-5527-84fb-711e21b7463f', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/607228d0-1b4a-5527-84fb-711e21b7463f'}, {'abstract': 'In an annual list of tech predictions, I.B.M. says that in five years we’ll self-power our homes with incidental tasks, read thoughts and communicate across hundreds of languages. As with other such lists, it is something of a pseudo-event drawing attention to the predictor’s own product or service. The most interesting thing, however, is what these predictions say about I.B.M.’s own business plans.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/whats-behind-i-b-m-s-big-predictions/', 'snippet': 'In an annual list of tech predictions, I.B.M. says that in five years we’ll self-power our homes with incidental tasks, read thoughts and communicate across hundreds of languages. As with other such lists, it is something of a pseudo-event drawing...', 'lead_paragraph': 'I.B.M. just issued its annual list of five predictions of developments in technology that it thinks will come true in the next five years. Like lots of predictive lists, particularly those that come around New Year’s, this is something of a pseudo-event that serves as an advertisement for the predictor’s own product or service. I.B.M.’s is no different in that regard, but it is worth looking at, both for the pedigree of who is doing the predicting, and what I.B.M.’s choices say about itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/technology/19bits-crystal-ball/19bits-crystal-ball-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind I.B.M.’s Big Predictions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T21:52:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf5232e7-bd10-511b-a8b1-d327c6195712', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf5232e7-bd10-511b-a8b1-d327c6195712'}, {'abstract': 'The saxophonist Tony Malaby appeared with Novela, his nine-piece band, at Jazz Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/arts/music/tony-malabys-novela-at-jazz-gallery-review.html', 'snippet': 'The saxophonist Tony Malaby appeared with Novela, his nine-piece band, at Jazz Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tenor saxophonist Tony Malaby has a burly but beseeching tone, and in his own bands he often pushes toward an amiable ruckus. Novela, the nine-piece band he presented at the Jazz Gallery on Sunday night, takes this predilection to its logical extreme. Drawing from “Novela” (Clean Feed), an album released in September, the group played a sprawling set of faintly episodic, heavily textured music, pausing only a couple of times to re-establish a center of gravity. The distinctive color of Mr. Malaby’s voice, on soprano as well as tenor, was often lost on a crowded canvas. He seemed totally fine with that.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/novella/novella-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 701, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/novella/novella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/novella/novella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roiling Through an Undertow', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roiling Through an Undertow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malaby, Tony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T22:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee1ab175-6dff-502c-9ee6-4dbd9e445276', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee1ab175-6dff-502c-9ee6-4dbd9e445276'}, {'abstract': 'Rodents with a taste for chocolate strike a Manhattan post office.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/19/holiday-gifts-intercepted/', 'snippet': 'Rodents with a taste for chocolate strike a Manhattan post office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:58 p.m. | Senders of holiday goodies, beware: at one Manhattan post office, four-legged, scaly-tailed postal inspectors may intercept your package and render it unfit for delivery, or worse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Special Delivery, With Teeth Marks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service and Post Offices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rats', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-19T22:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'origina