sian, Georgian, Armenian and even German composers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/arts/music/metropolitan-museum-artists-in-concert-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum Artists in Concert gave a nod to new Asian galleries with Russian, Georgian, Armenian and even German composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each program presented by the Metropolitan Museum Artists in Concert has at its heart a thematic agenda: some small notion that links the pieces. The idea can be vague, like simplicity or craftsmanship, and it’s usually understated; the performances are comfortably chatty, but you never feel lectured to. But that daub of glue always helps to make the programs by this personable, proficient ensemble hold together, and stick with you.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/met/met-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/met/met-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/arts/met/met-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sounds in Keeping With New Galleries', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sounds in Keeping With New Galleries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arron, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cords, Nicholas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Musi