uch a scheme was the best way to cut health care spending while providing for the medical needs of the elderly. The plan resembles a proposal that Alice Rivlin, who was budget director under President Clinton, and Pete Domenici, a longtime Republican senator, have also recently been promoting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Medicare, We Must Cut Costs, Not Shift Them', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vouchers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domenici, Pete V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivlin, Alice M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T02:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac40f026-9132-5cf8-aad3-62fe58390022', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac40f026-9132-5cf8-aad3-62fe58390022'}, {'abstract': 'A furious and sustained barrage of critici