 before its official premiere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dec. 20, 1946 | The Debut of ‘It’s a Wonderful Life,’ at New York’s Globe Theater', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T09:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4399d68-5793-5d22-ab99-031fcd012bad', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4399d68-5793-5d22-ab99-031fcd012bad'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Jong-un, thrust into prominence after his father’s sudden death, visited Kim Jong-il lying in a glass casket on Tuesday as the regime rallied to move the country behind its young new leader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/asia/kim-jong-un-pays-respects-to-kim-jong-il.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Jong-un, thrust into prominence after his father’s sudden death, visited Kim Jong-il lying in a glass casket on Tuesday as the regime rallied to move the country behind its young new leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Kim Jong-un, catapulted into prominence after Kim Jong-il’s sudden death, paid respects at his father’s glass coffin on Tuesday, as the regime stepped up a campaign to portray the impoverished country as standing behind its young new leader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/asia/21kimshot_cnd/21kimshot_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/world/asia/21kimshot_cnd/21kimshot_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'