'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4bca01-58b0-5f66-b876-5313c06d8609'}, {'abstract': 'Papua New Guinea’s governor general threw his weight behind the government of Peter O’Neill on Tuesday, ending a standoff that left the nation with dueling governments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/asia/political-impasse-in-papua-new-guinea-appears-to-end.html', 'snippet': 'Papua New Guinea’s governor general threw his weight behind the government of Peter O’Neill on Tuesday, ending a standoff that left the nation with dueling governments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — A political standoff in Papua New Guinea that left the country with two prime ministers and cabinets for more than a week appeared effectively over on Tuesday, after the governor general reversed course and threw his weight behind the government of Peter O’Neill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/PAPUA-2/PAPUA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 401, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/PAPUA-2/PAPUA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/world/PAPUA-2/PAPUA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Papua New Guinea’s Impasse Seems to End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Papua New Guinea’s Impasse Seems to End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Papua New Guinea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Peter", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somare, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T09:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/438ee8fb-e630-5822-a3ef-6310dded0643', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438ee8fb-e630-5822-a3ef-6310dded0643'}, {'abstract': 'China appears to be moving quickly to try to ensure stability in North Korea, a crippled and isolated nation now facing a leadership transition fraught with dangers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/asia/china-exerts-influence-nurtured-over-decades.html', 'snippet': 'China appears to be moving quickly to try to ensure stability in North Korea, a crippled and isolated nation now facing a leadership transition fraught with dangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China, North Korea’s foremost ally, appears to be moving quickly to try to ensure stability in a crippled and isolated nation now facing a leadership transition fraught with dangers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Exerts Influence Nurtured Over Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Exerts Influence Nurtured Over Decades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Un', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T09:39:22+0000', 'document_type': '