3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T11:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10797bb-3f99-54a8-ba8e-cc756123a85d', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10797bb-3f99-54a8-ba8e-cc756123a85d'}, {'abstract': 'A poll by Quinnipiac University found that a large majority of voters approved of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s overall performance.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/despite-misgivings-on-tax-overhaul-cuomo-wins-high-marks-in-poll-of-voters/', 'snippet': 'A poll by Quinnipiac University found that a large majority of voters approved of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s overall performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plurality of New York voters said Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo broke campaign promises to oppose tax increases and bring an end to Albany’s tradition of secret deal-making when he overhauled the state’s tax code earlier this month, according to a new poll released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plurality of Voters in Poll Fault Cuomo on Tax Deal', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T11:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39f13687-8beb-5f88-a883-91ab4d7c2560', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39f13687-8beb-5f88-a883-91ab4d7c2560'}, {'abstract': 'Eight students from four high schools — one each in Atlanta; New York City; Minnetonka, Minn.; and Long Beach, Calif. — invite readers of The Choice along on their college searches, via a first-person series called “The Envelope, Please.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/envelope-please-2012/', 'snippet': 'Eight students from four high schools — one each in Atlanta; New York City; Minnetonka, Minn.; and Long Beach, Calif. — invite readers of The Choice along on their college searches, via a first-person series called “The Envelope, Please.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'One attends a Minnesota public high school and dreams of becoming a veterinarian. But she won’t be studying at Cornell University or the University of California, Davis, at least as an undergraduate. She crossed those schools off earlier rough drafts of her college wish list at least partly because, she says, her parents have agreed to pay only the equivalent of in-state tuition at a Minnesota public university.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/education/envelope-please-composite-final/envelope-please-composite-final-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/education/envelope-please-composite-final/envelope-please-composite-final-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/education/envelope-please-composite-final/envelope-please-composite-final-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/19/education/envelope-please-composite-final/envelope-please-composite-final-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/19/education/envelope-please-composite-final/envelope-please-composite-final-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Envelope, Please: Eight High School Seniors Blog Their College Searches', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T11:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg and Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8915c399-2ef5-524b-95cf-724a767c6d75', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8915c399-2ef5-524b-95cf-724a767c6d75'}, {'abstract': 'Abigail Hansen, a senior at Minnetonka High School in Minnesota who dreams of becoming a veterinarian, said she has crossed far-away colleges like Cornell and the University of California, Davis, off her list, largely because of concerns about the student loan debt she would incur.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/envelope-hansen-1/', 'snippet': 'Abigail Hansen, a senior at Minnetonka High School in Minnesota who dreams of becoming a veterinarian, said she has crossed far-away colleges like Cornell and the University of California, Davis, off her list, largely because of concerns about the...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Friday, I was taking my second trip to the campus of University of Wisconsin, Madison, to help with the seemingly impossible decision of where to go to school. My dad, an alumnus, had used his contacts at UW to request a few meetings with professors, so that I could “get a feel” for the academic life there. The first professor on the list was typical — well, a typical, middle-aged, horse-loving animal science professor. She was enthusiastic, but she warned me sternly that I may need to change my career goal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Am I? Can I Get Back to You on That?', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T11:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Hansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1228113a-d42c-56d1-9b6c-6b60c4eca45f', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1228113a-d42c-56d1-9b6c-6b60c4eca45f'}, {'abstract': 'Kyu Nakama, a senior at Brooklyn Technical High School in New York City, says he once viewed college as “the mystical land where kids went to grow five feet and become adults.” Next year, he will call one college home. But which? “Forget privates,” his parents say, “let’s talk SUNY.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/envelope-nakama-1/', 'snippet': 'Kyu Nakama, a senior at Brooklyn Technical High School in New York City, says he once viewed college as “the mystical land where kids went to grow five feet and become adults.” Next year, he will call one college home. But which? “Forget privates,...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Right off the bat, let me tell you: I am a relatively average student. Nothing special. I don’t have a 90+ GPA. If you want someone like that, consult my friends. I enjoy the liberal arts, English and history over the sciences — but not to the point that I stay up all night reading history textbooks in my free time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Relatively Average, Nothing Special’ and Worried About College', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T11:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kyu Nakama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kyu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nakama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbf41aef-3da2-5006-b2e6-9d0886be12f5', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbf41aef-3da2-5006-b2e6-9d0886be12f5'}, {'abstract': 'The demonstration grew by the minute into an extraordinary expression of anger at the treatment of women by the military police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/middleeast/violence-enters-5th-day-as-egyptian-general-blames-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'The demonstration grew by the minute into an extraordinary expression of anger at the treatment of women by the military police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Several thousand women demanding the end of military rule marched through downtown Cairo on Tuesday evening in an extraordinary expression of anger over images of soldiers beating, stripping and kicking female demonstrators in Tahrir