 officials, potentially costing the nation billions of pounds of revenue as a result, according to a government report released on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Goldman Sachs, Vodafone and other big businesses were treated too favorably by British tax officials, potentially costing the nation billions in lost revenue, according to a government report released Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Tax Office Assailed for ‘Cozy’ Ties With Big Companies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T13:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa6feba-8dff-53ff-b916-d22a8310d1f4', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa6feba-8dff-53ff-b916-d22a8310d1f4'}, {'abstract': 'The designer tells us where she’s going and what she’s taking with her on her holiday vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/great-escape-winter-in-tuscany/', 'snippet': 'The designer tells us where she’s going and what she’s taking with her on her holiday vacation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropTyp