mes.com/2011/12/20/wheelies-the-out-of-range-edition/', 'snippet': 'Ford workers in St. Paul, Minn., began to tear down machinery this week in the plant that built the Ford Ranger, which ceased production on Dec. 16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Out of Range Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bethesda Naval Hospital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renault SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Paul (Minn)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T15:45:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c440cb9-3a46-5950-9a4f-b382b8e515ab', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c440cb9-3a46-5950-9a4f-b382b8e515ab'}, {'abstract': 'The Writers Guild of America, West, said it would restore the screenwriting credit of Trumbo, who was blacklisted from Hollywood in the 1940s, and who used his friend and fellow writer Ian McLellan Hunter as a front to accept payment and credit for the screenplay.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/dalton-trumbos-screenwriting-credit-restored-to-roman-holiday/', 'snippet': 'The Writers Guild of America, West, said it would restore the screenwriting credit of Trumbo, who was blacklisted from Hollywood in the 1940s, and who used his friend and fellow writer Ian McLellan Hunter as a front to accept payment and credit fo...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The whimsical secret of Audrey Hepburn’s royal status may be the heart of William Wyler‘s “Roman Holiday,” but for years the romantic comedy concealed another more troubling truth: the film was missing the screenwriting credit of Dalton Trumbo, the blacklisted writer and its original author, and instead attributed his work to Ian McLellan Hunter. Now, nearly 60 years after the 1953 release of “Roman Holiday,” the Writers Guild of America, West said it had restored Trumbo’s credit following the efforts of Trumbo’s and Hunter’s sons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dalton Trumbo’s Screenwriting Credit Restored to ‘Roman Holiday’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hepburn, Audrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trumbo, Dalton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyler, William', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Writers Guild of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T15:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b8460c-ac5c-5520-86a0-3bef7c948c9e', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b8460c-ac5c-5520-86a0-3bef7c948c9e'}, {'abstract': 'The provincial officials agreed to the meeting after residents of Wukan threatened to march on Wednesday morning to government offices in the nearby city of Lufeng.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/asia/top-provincial-leaders-to-meet-with-protesting-chinese-villagers-in-wukan.html', 'snippet': 'The provincial officials agreed to the meeting after residents of Wukan threatened to march on Wednesday morning to government offices in the nearby city of Lufeng.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WUKAN, China — Senior officials from the coastal Guangdong Province in southern China met on Wednesday morning with a leader of the protesters who have taken control of this fishing village, ratcheting up efforts to resolve an incendiary dispute over secret land sales that forced the village’s administrators to flee 10 days ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/WUKAN/WUKAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/world/WUKAN/WUKAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/WUKAN/WUKAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Provincial Officials Meet Leader of Protesters Who Took Over Chinese Village', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Provincial Officials Meet Leader of Protesters Who Took Over Chinese Village', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wukan (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T15:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b13dc4ff-7e5c-507f-8055-9975a1165e13', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b13dc4ff-7e5c-507f-8055-9975a1165e13'}, {'abstract': 'Richard B. Handler, the firm’s chief, boasted about successfully navigating through choppy waters and turning in a better-than-expected quarterly profit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/jefferies-crows-over-surviving-tough-quarter/', 'snippet': 'Richard B. Handler, the firm’s chief, boasted about successfully navigating through choppy waters and turning in a better-than-expected quarterly profit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shares of the Jefferies Group surged nearly 23 percent on Tuesday as stronger-than-expected fourth-quarter results helped restore confidence in the investment bank after it had been whipsawed in recent months by worries over its exposure to Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jefferies Crows Over Surviving a Tough Fourth Quarter', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jefferies Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T15:52:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a30498d2-9338-5238-80c8-557e2ae1218e', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a30498d2-9338-5238-80c8-557e2ae1218e'}, {'abstract': 'Did you buy your girls’ gifts from the pink aisle this holiday? Lego has great new kits geared for girls, but you’ll have to wait until January to get them.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/lego-goes-after-girls/', 'snippet': 'Did you buy your girls’ gifts from the pink aisle this holiday? Lego has great new kits geared for girls, but you’ll have to wait until January to get them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How gender-specific are the gifts you’ve bought for your kids this holiday? I give myself a B in this category this year. As usual, I set out to choose gifts for each child based on his or her interests and expressed desires — and, as usual, looking back over the list of what’s getting wrapped, I see that my oldest daughter has only one thing that you wouldn’t find in the pink section of any toy store, and while my tomboy younger daughter has only gifts you could easily give to any 6-year-old (except for the colorable cardboard princess castle her sister chose for her), I’ve still given the building toy that either of my youngest children would have liked to their brother without really thinking about it — until now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lego Goes After Girls', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 