ri': 'nyt://article/1c658733-b9b6-50c1-88d7-ad694baa0c96'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, the Super Bowl will be streamed live.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/nbc-will-stream-super-bowl/', 'snippet': 'For the first time, the Super Bowl will be streamed live.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:14 p.m. | Updated NBC announced Tuesday that it will stream Super Bowl XLVI live on Feb. 5 from Indianapolis, as well as its two wild card playoff games on Jan. 7 and the Pro Bowl on Jan. 29.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Will Stream Super Bowl', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72760c03-845d-56cc-ba43-53e6f4b7c536', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72760c03-845d-56cc-ba43-53e6f4b7c536'}, {'abstract': 'In a One on One interview, Gary Shteyngart, author of the novel “Super Sad True Love Story,” talks about his predictions of the future of privacy, ratings for everything, onions skin jeans, inequality and the Occupy movement and of course, the äppärät. All that and bad coffee.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/one-on-one-gary-shteyngart-author-of-super-sad-true-love-story/', 'snippet': 'In a One on One interview, Gary Shteyngart, author of the novel “Super Sad True Love Story,” talks about his predictions of the future of privacy, ratings for everything, onions skin jeans, inequality and the Occupy movement and of course, the äpp...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Shteyngart is the author of the novel “Super Sad True Love Story,” a love story set in the near future that has been weirdly prescient. Mr. Shteyngart, who was born in Leningrad, often writes about American culture with a comical and satirical bent. \xa0The following is an edited version of our interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One on One: Gary Shteyngart, Author of ‘Super Sad True Love Story’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science Fiction', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shteyngart, Gary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/194ca189-a15b-59dd-a13e-931e9349b0cc', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/194ca189-a15b-59dd-a13e-931e9349b0cc'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco 49ers announced themselves fit for the playoffs on a dark night for the Steelers', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/sports/49ers-show-theyre-contenders-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco 49ers announced themselves fit for the playoffs on a dark night for the Steelers', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first glitch came when viewers realized “Monday Night Football” was staging a game they might actually want to watch. (And more stunningly, this will happen two weeks in a row. What, the Rams already had plans for next Monday?) Considering this incredible upset, ESPN hoped viewers did not tune in while Candlestick Park had gone black. Twice. It gave the distinct impression the N.F.L. did not want an appealing game to be staged Monday night and pulled a plug. Either that, or Jon Gruden’s relentless sunniness melted the fuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '49ers Show They’re Contenders', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '49ers Show They’re Contenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b77a1a-35ad-5eaa-b060-8db1d3120ec0', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b77a1a-35ad-5eaa-b060-8db1d3120ec0'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the family trees of the Republican presidential candidates reveals presidential pedigrees for some.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/republican-candidates-have-presidential-pedigrees/', 'snippet': 'A look at the family trees of the Republican presidential candidates reveals presidential pedigrees for some.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Gov. Mitt Romney of Massachusetts has been called the establishment candidate of the Republican presidential primary and is dominating the endorsement race so far. A look at his family tree may explain his perceived place among the presidents: he is related to six former commanders in chief. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Candidates Have Presidential Pedigrees', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coolidge, Calvin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoover, Herbert Clark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Franklin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:24:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31d1545c-cca4-568d-9955-c85ecb211e61', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31d1545c-cca4-568d-9955-c85ecb211e61'}, {'abstract': 'Glenn Close’s portrayal of Albert Nobbs, a woman disguised as a man in late-19th-century Ireland, is both charming and sad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/movies/albert-nobbs-movie-review.html', 'snippet': 'Glenn Close’s portrayal of Albert Nobbs, a woman disguised as a man in late-19th-century Ireland, is both charming and sad.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Such a sweet little man,” remarks a guest at a shabby-genteel Dublin hotel, referring to a waiter named Albert Nobbs. One of Albert’s co-workers describes him, less kindly, as a “freak,” and there is certainly something odd about this elfin, diffident, ginger-haired fellow, who attends to his duties with fastidious care. He is not, indeed, a fellow at all, but a woman who has lived most of her life disguised as a man. And not just any woman: this self-effacing, cautious character, whose name is also the title of Rodrigo Garcia’s lively and touching new film, is played by the dazzling and infinitely resourceful Glenn Close.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/21albert-span/21albert-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/21albert-span/21albert-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/21albert-span/21albert-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/21albert-span/21albert-span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/21albert-span/21albert-span-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Safe Harbor in Male Identity', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Albert Nobbs'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding a Safe Harbor in Male Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Rodrigo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasikowska, Mia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McTeer, Janet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, Glenn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleeson, Brendan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:34:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5229d6c6-1776-5b24-932f-c800459485fe', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5229d6c6-1776-5b24-932f-c800459485fe'}, {'abstract': 'Finally, the frustrations of caregivers are spilling into public view.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/mad-as-hell/', 'snippet': 'Finally, the frustrations of caregivers are spilling into public view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ellen Goodman, the Boston Globe’s Pulitzer Prize-winning former columnist, now retired, is busy these days with something called the Conversation Project, one of many nascent efforts to make the rigors of caregiving and advanced old age into a kitchen-table issue — not just a topic for policy wonks and health care professionals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mad as Hell', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:36:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8def0bd3-7775-5c92-a173-c08891928cd7', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8def0bd3-7775-5c92-a173-c08891928cd7'}, {'abstract': 'Do Christians who hope for his salvation lack the courage of their convictions.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/hitchens-and-hell/', 'snippet': 'Do Christians who hope for his salvation lack the courage of their convictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remarking on the various Christians (myself included) who expressed a hope that Christopher Hitchens would be pleasantly surprised by his journey to the undiscovered country, HotAir’s Allahpundit asks a reasonable question:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hitchens and Hell', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4a5e063-854e-53ff-a708-1e27d2ffa9b1', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4a5e063-854e-53ff-a708-1e27d2ffa9b1'}, {'abstract': 'Two weeks before the Iowa caucuses, Rick Santorum wins a highly coveted endorsement from one of the state’s social conservative leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/vander-plaats-endorses-santorum/', 'snippet': 'Two weeks before the Iowa caucuses, Rick Santorum wins a highly coveted endorsement from one of the state’s social conservative leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DE WITT, Iowa — Rick Santorum, who was the first Republican presidential hopeful to visit all 99 Iowa counties in a quest to gain traction for the party’s nomination, received a lift on Tuesday by collecting a highly coveted endorsement from Bob Vander Plaats, one of the most visible leaders of the Christian conservative movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vander Plaats Endorses Santorum', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vander Plaats, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4650bdb1-1705-5431-b894-3b4e2a127d29', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4650bdb1-1705-5431-b894-3b4e2a127d29'}, {'abstract': 'Columbia and Yale will soon begin to reimburse its gay employees for the extra costs that they owe on the value of their partners’ health insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/yale-and-columbia-reimburse-gay-employees-for-extra-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Columbia and Yale will soon begin to reimburse its gay employees for the extra costs that they owe on the value of their partners’ health insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Ivy League universities will soon begin reimbursing some of its gay and lesbian employees for the extra taxes they incur when their partners are covered by their health insurance.Both Columbia and Yale University will begin covering these extra costs on Jan. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yale and Columbia Reimburse Gay Employees for Extra Taxes', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4093a54f-1351-5b1a-9c64-f7b59ef81db2', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4093a54f-1351-5b1a-9c64-f7b59ef81db2'}, {'abstract': 'By turning down a bill that was supported by both parties in the Senate as well as the White House, the conservative House majority is now staring over the brink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/us/politics/house-republicans-move-closer-to-rejecting-payroll-tax-cut-deal.html', 'snippet': 'By turning down a bill that was supported by both parties in the Senate as well as the White House, the conservative House majority is now staring over the brink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After defiantly rejecting a Senate compromise to extend a payroll tax break and jobless pay, Speaker John A. Boehner stood before the television cameras on Tuesday enveloped by scores of House Republicans. Even as a group, they seemed very much alone. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/