2011/12/20/the-year-in-media-putting-the-oscars-back-together-again/', 'snippet': 'The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences was sent into a frenzy on Nov. 8 by a controversy over the use of an antigay slur by its Oscar producer, Brett Ratner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Staff members of The Times’s media news department are highlighting the most significant developments this year in the industries they cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | Putting the Oscars Back Together Again', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Eddie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratner, Brett', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5e1785c-a725-5e31-900d-4ee17c226d50', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5e1785c-a725-5e31-900d-4ee17c226d50'}, {'abstract': 'Yesterday morning began with an alarming call from our mail room.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/sharing-the-rat-infested-bounty/', 'snippet': 'Yesterday morning began with an alarming call from our mail room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday morning began with an alarming call from our mail room. They said they couldn’t deliver a package addressed to me because it had been chewed open by rats at the Post Office. Several other packages arrived at The Times yesterday in similarly ratty condition. So I alerted Andy Newman, our City Room bureau chief, who wrote this investigative piece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharing the Rat-Infested Bounty', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:53:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathy Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c1d22df-7100-517f-8123-657256d161f3', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c1d22df-7100-517f-8123-657256d161f3'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists say that an ocean warming sufficient to destabilize a lot of methane hydrates would almost certainly take thousands of years.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/arctic-methane-is-catastrophe-imminent/', 'snippet': 'Scientists say that an ocean warming sufficient to destabilize a lot of methane hydrates would almost certainly take thousands of years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my article over the weekend about the climate risks from buried Arctic carbon, I omitted any discussion of one issue that sometimes appears in the news: methane deposits under relatively shallow seawater near the coasts of Siberia, Canada and Alaska. It was a purposeful omission because my piece focused on carbon buried on land, which presents a climate risk if it eventually emerges as methane or carbon dioxide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arctic Methane: Is Catastrophe Imminent?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC OCEAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T16:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da7709f4-cbc0-5d90-81b7-5f3bad805856', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da7709f4-cbc0-5d90-81b7-5f3bad805856'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Spielberg discusses  his latest film, “The Adventures of Tintin,” his first foray into digital animation using performance-capture technology.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/the-adventures-of-spielberg-an-interview/', 'snippet': 'Steven Spielberg discusses  his latest film, “The Adventures of Tintin,” his first foray into digital animation using performance-capture technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year’s holiday movie season brings with it a double dose of family film fare from a director well-seasoned in the genre. Steven Spielberg, long the wearer of many hats in Hollywood, is one of the few filmmakers who could potentially find both box office and awards-season success with two films released within a week of each other. The first is his digitally animated adaptation of the Belgian comic book series “The Adventures of Tintin,” which opens Wednesday. The second is his adaptation of the children’s novel (and Tony Award-winning play) “War Horse,” opening Christmas Day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Adventures of Spielberg: An Interview', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remi, Georges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zemeckis, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b87bc71-5bba-5748-a855-86a3b000bceb', 'word_count': 1272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b87bc71-5bba-5748-a855-86a3b000bceb'}, {'abstract': 'The musical, based on the 2004 film about J.M. Barrie, represents the first show that the Weinstein Company has developed and its first outing as lead producer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/weinstein-company-moving-ahead-with-finding-neverland-musical-its-first/', 'snippet': 'The musical, based on the 2004 film about J.M. Barrie, represents the first show that the Weinstein Company has developed and its first outing as lead producer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Weinstein Company, heavyweight producers in Hollywood, is moving ahead with development of its first stage musical, “Finding Neverland,” after staged readings of the script and score in London last week that executives deemed a success. Rob Ashford, the Broadway director and choreographer (“How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying”) who is directing the work, said in an interview that the story and structure of the musical “was in much stronger shape” than at the last reading about a year ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weinstein Company Moving Ahead With ‘Finding Neverland’ Musical, Its First', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6ca9dc7-8e8f-5531-911a-8e5f1da99d85', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6ca9dc7-8e8f-5531-911a-8e5f1da99d85'}, {'abstract': 'The bad economy is fueling demand for high-end products, as men realize that healthy-looking skin is a bonus in their careers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/fashion/men-once-again-invest-in-skin-care-skin-deep.html', 'snippet': 'The bad economy is fueling demand for high-end products, as men realize that healthy-looking skin is a bonus in their careers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT long ago, Thomas Sullivan’s beauty routine began and ended with Irish Spring. But as Mr. Sullivan, an entrepreneur, actor, film producer and restaurant owner, approached 40, he realized his livelihood might benefit from a bit more personal maintenance. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,