n?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Richmond, a London Day Trip That Fits the Frugal Bill', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e1ff90a-e587-5668-a7c1-9d2e9687aa5d', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e1ff90a-e587-5668-a7c1-9d2e9687aa5d'}, {'abstract': 'Losses punish day traders and push brokers into new industries.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/pain-on-dalal-street-as-markets-sink/', 'snippet': 'Losses punish day traders and push brokers into new industries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mood on Dalal Street, India’s Wall Street, has been particularly dismal since Monday, when the Sensex index on the Bombay Stock Exchange’s sunk 112 points to 15,379 – its lowest level in approximately 28 months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pain on Dalal Street as Markets Sink', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bombay Stock Exchange', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25549607-2e58-5796-92e2-8b2b9933c8c6', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25549607-2e58-5796-92e2-8b2b9933c8c6'}, {'abstract': 'Naked emperors all.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/pathetic-plutocrats/', 'snippet': 'Naked emperors all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the disadvantages of being very wealthy may be that you end up surrounded by sycophants, who will never, ever tell you what a fool you’re making of yourself. That’s the only way I can make sense of the farcical behavior of the wealthy described in this new report from Max Abelson:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pathetic Plutocrats', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b23a2fa-17d2-5743-a019-33b8248b4e2a', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b23a2fa-17d2-5743-a019-33b8248b4e2a'}, {'abstract': 'The award for best sequel involving shells and shoes goes to the comedian Jenny Slate and the filmmaker Dean Fleischer-Camp.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/riffs-the-year-in-film-bonus-materials/', 'snippet': 'The award for best sequel involving shells and shoes goes to the comedian Jenny Slate and the filmmaker Dean Fleischer-Camp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The magazine recently featured a roundup of short Riff essays on the year in film (mini-Riffs? Li’l Riffs? Riffkins? O.K., we’ll stop now). But, as with all good things, we collected more random and curious reflections on the year past than we could ever jam into our pages. So we present these Riffs as kind of DVD extras: Bonus Materials for you to enjoy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riffs: The Year in Film: Bonus Materials', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slate, Jenny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:26:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c2b1c34-8c9a-5a47-8650-951174dc319d', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c2b1c34-8c9a-5a47-8650-951174dc319d'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/have-n-f-l-questions-judy-battista-has-answers-6/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do the Eagles have momentum? What has happened to Ryan Fitzpatrick and the Bills? Is Kyle Orton better than people think? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers. Use the comment field below for your questions. Answers will appear Thursday on The Fifth Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have N.F.L. Questions? Judy Battista Has Answers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battista, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buffalo Bills', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7fc43a3-3fc0-5c53-9a4f-1e9bfe7f28ba', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7fc43a3-3fc0-5c53-9a4f-1e9bfe7f28ba'}, {'abstract': "Spain's borrowing costs plummeted as the European Central Bank began rolling out a new lending program that could encourage banks to buy euro-zone government bonds.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/business/global/successful-spanish-debt-auction-helps-lifts-euro-and-stocks.html', 'snippet': "Spain's borrowing costs plummeted as the European Central Bank began rolling out a new lending program that could encourage banks to buy euro-zone government bonds.", 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Spain’s borrowing costs plummeted Tuesday at a debt auction, helping to lift the euro and stocks, as the European Central Bank began rolling out a new lending program that could encourage banks to buy euro-zone government bonds. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Successful Spanish Debt Auction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Auction Of Debt In Spain Lifts Euro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw