'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26e11ed8-4bc3-5c02-bea9-084c35da9f1a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26e11ed8-4bc3-5c02-bea9-084c35da9f1a'}, {'abstract': 'Two students at a gifted and talented middle school in Brooklyn dazzled the French with their award-winning works that link the Statue of Liberty to an environmental theme. One, Hale Sheffield, a seventh grader, won a grand prize of round-trip tickets for two to Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/20/students-win-for-turning-lady-liberty-green/', 'snippet': 'Two students at a gifted and talented middle school in Brooklyn dazzled the French with their award-winning works that link the Statue of Liberty to an environmental theme. One, Hale Sheffield, a seventh grader, won a grand prize of round-trip tic...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students Win for Turning Lady Liberty Green', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ABIGAIL MEISEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MEISEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a82bd64e-0d16-5f81-bf1e-e54a5175b402', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a82bd64e-0d16-5f81-bf1e-e54a5175b402'}, {'abstract': 'The Choice blog takes to The New York Times’s main Facebook page tonight to field last-minute questions from jittery applicants.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/reminder-the-choice-will-be-live-on-facebook-tonight-and-wednesday-and-thursday/', 'snippet': 'The Choice blog takes to The New York Times’s main Facebook page tonight to field last-minute questions from jittery applicants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you a student (or parent of a student?) who is still scrambling to meet the Jan. 1 deadline at many colleges? Or, are you trying to determine how best to respond to (or recover from) an early admission ruling from last week? You’ve come to the right place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reminder: The Choice Will Be Live on Facebook Tonight (and Wednesday and Thursday)', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T17:44:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fefa2e63-4aff-5746-a8b5-43028f0df514', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fefa2e63-4aff-5746-a8b5-43028f0df514'}, {'abstract': 'Two nutrient-dense vegetables combine forces in this delicious filling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/health/nutrition/tacos-with-mushrooms-and-chipotle-ranchera-salsa-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Two nutrient-dense vegetables combine forces in this delicious filling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two nutrient-dense vegetables combine forces in this delicious filling. Mushrooms are an excellent source of vitamins and many minerals, particularly selenium, copper, potassium, phosphorous, zinc, and manganese – and they contain a powerful antioxidant called L-ergothioneine. They’re used medicinally throughout Asia for their immunity-boosting properties. They also contain more protein than most other vegetables, and their meaty texture makes them a perfect choice for vegetarians. Cabbage possesses phytochemicals like sulforaphane, which protects the body against cancer-causing free radicals, and indoles, which help metabolize estrogens. It’s also an excellent source of vitamins K and C, and a very good source of\xa0 dietary fiber, vitamin B6, folate, manganese and omega-3 fatty acids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 