 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — A senior Roman Catholic prelate in Ireland said Tuesday that the church would arrange for victims of clergy sexual abuse in one diocese to meet with the bishop who was in charge of it when hundreds of abuse complaints were kept secret.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Bishop Will Meet With Irish Abuse Victims', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Bishop Will Meet With Irish Abuse Victims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clergy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5a66c47-3746-5260-9e1e-92eb8be97d92', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5a66c47-3746-5260-9e1e-92eb8be97d92'}, {'abstract': 'Lupa, a Roman-style osteria, was a hit when it opened 12 years ago, and it continues to be today, judging by the crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/dining/a-trattoria-competes-with-its-past-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'Lupa, a Roman-style osteria, was a hit when it opened 12 years ago, and it continues to be today, judging by the crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S dinner time, yet entering Lupa, the Roman-style osteria opened in 1999 by the team of Mario Batali and Joe Bastianich, is about as joyous an experience as trying to squeeze onto the subway at rush hour. You know you will be bumped and jostled, but you don’t know which direction it will come from.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21REST_SPAN/21REST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21REST_SPAN/21REST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21REST_SPAN/21REST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21REST_SPAN/21REST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/dining/21REST_SPAN/21REST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Osteria Competes With Its Past', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Osteria Competes With Its Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat