ctim-regular-car-maintenance/', 'snippet': 'The survey results, released by Consumer Reports, indicated that a “significant minority” of car owners was delaying routine maintenance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Car owners who are delaying automotive maintenance have plenty of company, according to a recent poll by Consumer Reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Survey Suggests Tough Economy Is Claiming Another Victim: Regular Car Maintenance', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd25764c-2a39-5c63-ac2c-a00aa703ecb6', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd25764c-2a39-5c63-ac2c-a00aa703ecb6'}, {'abstract': 'Books, music and gear sure to delight any cocktail lover this holiday season.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/last-minute-holiday-loot-for-the-drinking-sort/', 'snippet': 'Books, music and gear sure to delight any cocktail lover this holiday season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I nearly set to weeping when I found a copy of the gorgeous, lavishly illustrated 1933 edition of “The Savoy Cocktail Book” at my favorite used bookshop (Dog Ears, in Hoosick Falls, N.Y.) last month. The $50 price was right (I’ve seen it listed for much more), but still a splurge, by my standards. So I considered it an early Christmas present — to myself. Any cocktail lover would be thrilled to receive such a gift, but there are easier gets that are also sure to delight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last-Minute Holiday Loot for the Drinking Sort', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMIS, KINGSLEY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "CARSON'S", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:29:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b2dd8df-5bd2-500e-bb51-b10f6a48cb12', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b2dd8df-5bd2-500e-bb51-b10f6a48cb12'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on the new NBC game show “Who’s Still Standing?”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/channel-surfing-whos-still-standing/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on the new NBC game show “Who’s Still Standing?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, it’s the season of joy and giving, but can’t we also spend a few moments cheering like Romans in the arena hoping to see someone plummet through the floor to a grisly, ignominious end? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Who’s Still Standing?’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41e0fa69-564a-5697-a01e-9bc9e870a6d0', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41e0fa69-564a-5697-a01e-9bc9e870a6d0'}, {'abstract': 'Will she run, or won’t she. She just doesn’t know, you know?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/chasing-sarah-palin/', 'snippet': 'Will she run, or won’t she. She just doesn’t know, you know?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s our story so far: Sarah Palin is picked to run for vice president, builds up a big fan club of disgruntled, right wing Americans and loses. She returns briefly to Alaska, but then finds the job of running a state that lives off federal dollars and oil revenue too taxing and not nearly lucrative enough. She quits, writes a smash best seller, charges who knows what for public appearances, and keeps her celebrity going by pretending for a while to be thinking about running for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chasing Sarah Palin', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-20T21:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mater