e, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T00:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bc3545c1-8c88-5aa2-a5ee-2a322b321a91', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bc3545c1-8c88-5aa2-a5ee-2a322b321a91'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes of mass hysteria and grief among North Koreans appeared to be part of an official campaign to build support for Kim Jong-il’s successor, his third son, Kim Jong-un.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/world/asia/north-korean-mourning-blends-emotion-and-coercion.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes of mass hysteria and grief among North Koreans appeared to be part of an official campaign to build support for Kim Jong-il’s successor, his third son, Kim Jong-un.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Among countless mourners at a public square in North Korea,  the kneeling middle-aged man in an off-white windbreaker stands out. The state broadcaster’s camera zooms in as he wails, rocking back and forth with clenched fists, his grief punctuated by the white puffs of his breath visible in the cold of the capital, Pyongyang.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/world/MOURNING-1/MOURNING-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/world/MOURNING-1/MOURNING-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': Non