ut of Cairo, the increasing violence by the security forces is threatening the nation’s revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/opinion/egypts-military-masters.html', 'snippet': 'As evidenced by the appalling images coming out of Cairo, the increasing violence by the security forces is threatening the nation’s revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five days of violent clashes between Egyptian soldiers and protesters have produced appalling images of cruelty and abuse — including a video showing soldiers stripping the abaya off a woman on the ground to reveal her blue bra as one raises a boot to stomp on her. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Military Masters', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Military Masters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emara, Adel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/094f158d-42ee-5beb-a668-92a1c73fe26a', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/094f158d-42ee-5beb-a668-92a1c73fe26a'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets eliminated their team in the Class A Gulf Coast League but still have eight minor league affiliates, including two in the Dominican Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/mets-drop-minor-league-team/', 'snippet': 'The Mets eliminated their team in the Class A Gulf Coast League but still have eight minor league affiliates, including two in the Dominican Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The financially troubled Mets announced Tuesday that they were eliminating their minor league team in the Class A Gulf Coast League. That move could save them between $750,000 and $800,000, according to executives with other franchises who are familiar with the cost of running those teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Drop Minor League Team', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fb0ca3b-6a89-53ea-9ba3-7a7b7c4dd093', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fb0ca3b-6a89-53ea-9ba3-7a7b7c4dd093'}, {'abstract': 'Some ideas for potential cooks, whether they’re reluctant or eager.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/gifts-for-non-cooks/', 'snippet': 'Some ideas for potential cooks, whether they’re reluctant or eager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans spend less time cooking than anyone, and the amount we “cook” — some people count microwaving a pizza — has been on a long, slow decline. The reasons for this decline are varied and complex, but an increase in the average of both hours worked and television watched, coupled with the marketing of “convenience” foods, have turned cooking from a sometimes-pleasurable necessity into, for many people, an ominous-seeming choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gifts for Non-Cooks', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae4478ca-8ac4-5d30-9419-11e1db401d1f', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae4478ca-8ac4-5d30-9419-11e1db401d1f'}, {'abstract': 'Two brothers’ journey to make a kidney transplant happen has taken them to the core of the national impasse between health care and immigration policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/nyregion/illegal-immigrants-transplant-cheaper-over-life-isnt-covered.html', 'snippet': 'Two brothers’ journey to make a kidney transplant happen has taken them to the core of the national impasse between health care and immigration policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Without treatment to replace his failing kidneys, doctors knew, the man in Bellevue hospital would die. He was a waiter in his early 30s, a husband and father of two, so well liked at the Manhattan restaurant where he had worked for a decade that everyone from the customers to the dishwasher was donating money to help his family.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/transplant2/transplant2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/transplant2/transplant2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/transplant2/transplant2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/transplant2/transplant2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/transplant2/transplant2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Illegal Immigrant, Line Is Drawn at Transplant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Illegal Resident, Line Is Drawn at Transplant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dialysis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidneys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfdf190d-c2a1-5e80-b2b4-e3a50ead8e52', 'word_count': 1454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfdf190d-c2a1-5e80-b2b4-e3a50ead8e52'}, {'abstract': 'Video of a march in Cairo, and the act of brutality by soldiers on Saturday that sparked it.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/video-of-egyptian-womens-march-in-cairo/', 'snippet': 'Video of a march in Cairo, and the act of brutality by soldiers on Saturday that sparked it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reports, “Thousands of women marched through downtown Cairo on Tuesday evening to call for the end of military rule in an extraordinary expression of anger over images of soldiers beating, stripping and kicking a female demonstrator on the pavement of Tahrir Square.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Egyptian Women’s March in Cairo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1091f198-5edd-5953-a35e-22a45784d4dd', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1091f198-5edd-5953-a35e-22a45784d4dd'}, {'abstract': 'M. Slavin and Sons must pay $900,000 to employees who were harassed.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/fish-seller-settles-harassment-suit-brought-by-black-workers/', 'snippet': 'M. Slavin and Sons must pay $900,000 to employees who were harassed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fishmonger M. Slavin and Sons, the company with the familiar “Eat Fish Live Longer” delivery trucks, has agreed to pay $900,000 to 31 black workers to settle a discrimination suit brought by the federal Equal Employment Opportunity Commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Seller Settles Harassment Suit Brought by Black Workers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T01:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1539a8c-4fcc-5df9-ac50-541d1c0d107f', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1539a8c-4fcc-5df9-ac50-541d1c0d107f'}, {'abstract': 'The late North Korean leader played a big role in his country’s international sporting endeavors. He also bowled a 300 the first time he ever played — according to state-run news media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/sports/remembering-kim-jong-ils-ventures-into-the-sporting-world.html', 'snippet': 'The late North Korean leader played a big role in his country’s international sporting endeavors. He also bowled a 300 the first time he ever played — according to state-run news media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the political world, Kim Jong-il of North Korea was a despot and nuclear antagonist. In the sporting world, he might have been the only guy ever to wear platform shoes, a bouffant hairdo and “Dear Leader” embroidered on his bowling shirt.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/sports/LONGMAN4/LONGMAN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/sports/LONGMAN4/LONGMAN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/sports/LONGMAN4/LONGMAN4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/sports/LONGMAN4/LONGMAN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/sports/LONGMAN4/LONGMAN4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kim Jong-il, the Sportsman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kim Jong-il, Sportsman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'person