an men willing and able to be the sort of husbands that black women want?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2011/12/20/black-men-for-black-women/', 'snippet': 'Are there too few African-American men willing and able to be the sort of husbands that black women want?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Men for Black Women?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T03:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a817aff-6a3d-5bb1-a699-29c57aef5ef8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a817aff-6a3d-5bb1-a699-29c57aef5ef8'}, {'abstract': 'A street beggar and the city agreed that the police would use their “best efforts” not to roust or arrest him without cause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/nyregion/beggar-seeking-money-for-marijuana-wins-a-victory-in-court.html', 'snippet': 'A street beggar and the city agreed that the police would use their “best efforts” not to roust or arrest him without cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He calls himself the Weed Man, and he has become a familiar presence in Times Square, standing near Planet Hollywood and holding aloft a placard that stands out even in this part of the city.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/weed/weed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/21/nyregion/weed/weed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,