_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b88e329-5b90-532b-bbbf-f6b1b696ba30', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b88e329-5b90-532b-bbbf-f6b1b696ba30'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the most dramatic images of the Iraq war were made by Iraqi photographers who risked life and limb. They set out to document what many hoped would be its rebirth, and kept shooting what they realized was its dissolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/21/blogs/2111221_lens_iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Many of the most dramatic images of the Iraq war were made by Iraqi photographers who risked life and limb. They set out to document what many hoped would be its rebirth, and kept shooting what they realized was its dissolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the most dramatic images of the Iraq war were made by Iraqi photographers who risked life and limb. They set out to document what many hoped would be its rebirth, and kept shooting what they realized was its dissolution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/blogs/2111221_lens_iraq-slide-JMN5/2111221_lens_iraq-slide-JMN5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraqi Photographers Captured the Costs of War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T03:49:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c2f8977e-2ecf-54c2-87c4-53a7c569dc7e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c2f8977e-2ecf-54c2-87c4-53a7c569dc7e'}, {'abstract': 'The Oscar given to Orson Welles for “Citizen Kane” sold at auction for more than $800,000.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/20/orson-welless-oscar-has-a-new-owner/', 'snippet': 'The Oscar given to Orson Welles for “Citizen Kane” sold at auction for more than $800,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES —The Orson Welles Oscar went to the highest—and unidentified — bidder for $861,542, the Nate D. Sanders auction house said Tuesday evening. Welles received the Oscar in 1942 for his work on the script for “Citizen Kane.” It was thought to be lost and later replaced. But eventually the original turned up in the hands of a cinematographer who said he had received it from Welles as a gift, and, after a court fight, it was turned over to Welles’s daughter Beatrice. When the original first went on the block, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences went to court to try to stop the sale, but lost. Sotheby’s later tried to sell it, but ended that effort when an undisclosed reserve price was not met. And, now, finally the Oscar has been sold in an auction that, according to Sanders, included an underbid from the magician David Copperfield. “I’m proud to have represented this fantastic award to the cinema collecting community,” Nate D. Sanders, the auction house owner, said in a statement that was circulated late Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orson Welles’s Oscar Has a New Owner', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Copperfield, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welles, Orson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T03:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9537071d-d8de-5695-966b-c545339decbe', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9537071d-d8de-5695-966b-c545339decbe'}, {'abstract': 'Officials in Dougherty County, south of Atlanta, were found to have tampered with standardized testing mandated by the No Child Left Behind Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/education/cheating-found-among-schools-in-georgias-dougherty-county.html', 'snippet': 'Officials in Dougherty County, south of Atlanta, were found to have tampered with standardized testing mandated by the No Child Left Behind Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investigators who this year found rampant cheating among Atlanta public school teachers and principals released another report on Tuesday detailing widespread wrongdoing in another Georgia county.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Georgia Schools Accused of Cheating', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Georgia Schools Accused of Cheating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No Child Left Behind Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deal, Nathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T04:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93edfb71-dded-5a7c-a2d5-2e77f824729e', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93edfb71-dded-5a7c-a2d5-2e77f824729e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Summers worked with the Modernist master Mies van der Rohe before leaving the practice; his own projects included the McCormick Place convention center in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/arts/design/gene-summers-architect-with-mies-van-der-rohe-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Summers worked with the Modernist master Mies van der Rohe before leaving the practice; his own projects included the McCormick Place convention center in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gene Summers, an architect who helped execute Ludwig Mies van der Rohe’s designs for the Seagram Building in Manhattan and other Modernist landmarks, then went on to design the McCormick Place convention center in Chicago, died on Dec. 12 in Sebastopol, Calif. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/SUMMERS1-obit/SUMMERS1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/SUMMERS1-obit/SUMMERS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/arts/SUMMERS1-obit/SUMMERS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gene Summers, Modernist Architect, Dies at 83', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gene Summers, 83, Modernist Architect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor