 subscription fee if half of its current 35 million users agree to sign up for subscriptions?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “Xbox Live Challenges Cable Box.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Dec. 21, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T09:32:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/716643be-3519-5197-b71d-bffd6106e67d', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/716643be-3519-5197-b71d-bffd6106e67d'}, {'abstract': 'North Korean television showed senior military leaders saluting the young Kim Jong-un as he received mourners for his father at the Kumsusan mausoleum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/asia/cautious-approach-to-north-korea-by-us-and-south-korea.html', 'snippet': 'North Korean television showed senior military leaders saluting the young Kim Jong-un as he received mourners for his father at the Kumsusan mausoleum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The leadership of North Korea moved swiftly on Wednesday to portray Kim Jong-un, thrust into the international spotlight after the death of his father, as the country’s unchallenged ruler.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/22nkorea-a/22nkorea-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/22nkorea-a/22nkorea-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla