m/2011/12/21/fighting-pollution-with-the-language-of-light/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | How do sea creatures use bioluminescence, the “language of light,” to communicate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Go to related article »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Pollution With the Language of Light', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T09:53:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82a372da-472c-564f-ac67-32b43dfaa9a4', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82a372da-472c-564f-ac67-32b43dfaa9a4'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the most dramatic images of the Iraq war were made by Iraqi photographers who risked life and limb. They set out to document what many hoped would be its rebirth, and kept shooting what they realized was its dissolution.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/iraqi-photographers-captured-the-costs-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Many of the most dramatic images of the Iraq war were made by Iraqi photographers who risked life and limb. They set out to document what many hoped would be its rebirth, and kept shooting what they realized was its dissolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interactive presentation including the photographs and voices of five Iraqi photographers accompanies this post. We urge you to view it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraqi Photographers Captured the Costs of War', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66dea124-765b-51d2-8633-2fff194cb10d', 'word_count': 1601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66dea124-765b-51d2-8633-2fff194cb10d'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Can morality be independent of God? Can people who don’t believe in God still be as “good” as those who do? What governs your own decisions about whether and how to act ethically?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/can-you-be-good-without-god/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Can morality be independent of God? Can people who don’t believe in God still be as “good” as those who do? What governs your own decisions about whether and how to act ethically?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A writer for a Times blog about philosophy argues that being an atheist does not mean “anything goes” — in fact, quite the opposite. What do you think? Can morality be independent of God? Can people who don’t believe in God still be as “good” as those who do? What governs your own decisions about whether and how to act ethically?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can You Be Good Without God?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T10:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb16de96-74d7-5322-80b1-68388ceec152', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb16de96-74d7-5322-80b1-68388ceec152'}, {'abstract': 'Tokio Marine Holdings of Japan has agreed to buy the American insurer Delphi Financial Group for $2.7 billion, in the latest move by the Asian insurance company to diversify outside its home market.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/tokio-marine-to-buy-delphi-financial-for-2-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'Tokio Marine Holdings of Japan has agreed to buy the American insurer Delphi Financial Group for $2.7 billion, in the latest move by the Asian insurance company to diversify outside its home market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Tokio Marine Holdings, Japan’s second-largest casualty insurer, agreed on Wednesday to buy the American insurer Delphi Financial Group for $2.7 billion in the latest move by the Asian insurance company to diversify outside its home market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tokio Marine to Buy Delphi Financial for $2.7 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T10:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8e3a25-97df-5b31-9f62-a84367367ef3', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8e3a25-97df-5b31-9f62-a84367367ef3'}, {'abstract': 'How to get more information about the items scattered around the Mac OS X desktop, like the number of items inside a folder or the resolution of an image.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/tip-of-the-week-getting-more-info-from-your-mac/', 'snippet': 'How to get more information about the items scattered around the Mac OS X desktop, like the number of items inside a folder or the resolution of an image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Want more information about the items scattered around the Mac OS X desktop, like the number of items inside a folder or the resolution of an image? Just click the desktop background and go to the View menu in the Mac’s Finder. Choose Show View Options from the menu and turn on the checkbox next to “Show item info.” The desktop icons now display that additional data. If you decide that the Mac might be showing you too much information, just repeat the steps and remove the check from the box next to “Show item info.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Getting More Info From Your Mac', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T10:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/173244a2-71b1-5018-ab46-47481c5ee115', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/173244a2-71b1-5018-ab46-47481c5ee115'}, {'abstract': 'A decision by the European Union’s highest court on Wednesday could spark a trade war with countries that oppose being forced into Europe’s carbon-trading system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/global/court-upholds-europes-plan-to-charge-airlines-for-carbon-emissions.html', 'snippet': 'A decision by the European Union’s highest court on Wednesday could spark a trade war with countries that oppose being forced into Europe’s carbon-trading system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The European Union’s highest court on Wednesday endorsed the bloc’s plan to begin charging the world’s biggest airlines for their greenhouse gas emissions starting Jan. 1. The move sets the stage for a potentially costly trade war with the United States, China and other countries.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Emit/Emit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Emit/Emit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Emit/Emit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carbon Emission Fees for Flights Upheld', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carbon Emission Fees for Flights Upheld', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Court of Justice', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T10:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01781af3-ebbb-520b-a4d2-a13b87e192c1', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01781af3-ebbb-520b-a4d2-a13b87e192c1'}, {'abstract': 'After long resisting the kind of force Washington used at the height of the financial crisis in 2008, Europe’s central bankers pumped nearly $640 billion into its banking system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/global/demand-for-ecb-loans-surpasses-expectations.html', 'snippet': 'After long resisting the kind of force Washington used at the height of the financial crisis in 2008, Europe’s central bankers pumped nearly $640 billion into its banking system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After long resisting the kind of financial force Washington used at the height of the financial crisis in 2008, European central bankers on Wednesday pumped nearly $640 billion into the Continent’s banking system. The move raised hopes that the money could alleviate the region’s credit squeeze. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/ECB/ECB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/business/ECB/ECB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/ECB/ECB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width'