k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rex Ryan, the ‘Say Anything’ Coach', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7687e7-f47a-5ccc-992d-9aa22feffab9', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7687e7-f47a-5ccc-992d-9aa22feffab9'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Eichelberger, a senior at Marist School in Atlanta, has already collected two acceptances, and one rejection, but little else in his college process is certain.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/eric-eichelberger/', 'snippet': 'Eric Eichelberger, a senior at Marist School in Atlanta, has already collected two acceptances, and one rejection, but little else in his college process is certain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve always heard that senior year is easy: a year of coasting, relaxation and (arguably) well-deserved laziness. Starting my final year at Marist School, a Catholic college prep school in Atlanta, I almost looked forward to slipping into senioritis. Yet 4 months, 1 round of final exams and 13 college applications later, it’s fair to say senior year is no pleasure cruise. On top of a challenging course load and a busy extracurricular schedule, I face some huge decisions about next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paring a College List from 19 to 13, With Room for Yale and Deep Springs', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T11:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Eichelberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eichelberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b87539-297f-55bd-ac81-5eb3938620ad', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b87539-297f-55bd-ac81-5eb3938620ad'}, {'abstract': 'Easier eligibility and the weak economy have increased the percentage of jobless receiving unemployment insurance, making that particular economic benefit a larger piece of the economy, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/unemployment-compensation-over-time/', 'snippet': 'Easier eligibility and the weak economy have increased the percentage of jobless receiving unemployment insurance, making that particular economic benefit a larger piece of the economy, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unemployment Compensation Over Time', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, '