1/how-bridesmaids-could-get-a-best-picture-nomination/', 'snippet': '“Bridesmaids” has made it onto several year-end top 10 lists and picked up important awards nominations. Is a nod for the  best-picture Academy Award next?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The critics have spoken, and so have the awards watchers, and both would like to nominate “Bridesmaids” as a movie of the year. The Kristen Wiig-Annie Mumolo comedy made it to many top 10 lists, including those of the Bagger’s colleagues A. O. Scott and Manohla Dargis, and the American Film Institute. It earned important Golden Globe and Screen Actors Guild nominations as well, and now the experts over at Gold Derby are predicting that it has a shot at the best picture Academy Award. (It edged out “Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy,” which dropped off the list from a month ago.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How ‘Bridesmaids’ Could Get a Best-Picture Nomination', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bridesmaids (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APATOW, JUDD', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T13:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36fb5817-2373-5b43-9697-0a2ac9aaca0c', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36fb5817-2373-5b43-9697-0a2ac9aaca0c'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s