n important role in Israeli life.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-holy-land-of-the-holy-graves/', 'snippet': 'Israelis flock to ancient grave sites even though many are inaccurate markers of where the dead are buried. Authentic or not, tombs play an important role in Israeli life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MODIIN, Israel — Monday afternoon, a day before the start of Hanukkah, I’m on the road from Jerusalem to Tel Aviv. I turn right where the brown signs point to the “Maccabean Graves.” I take the short unpaved road to where the Maccabees — those rebellious Jewish devotees who defeated the forces of the Greek-Macedonian Seleucid Empire around 100 B.C. — almost certainly were not buried. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Holy Land of the Holy Graves', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tombs and Tombstones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nablus (West Bank)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T13:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba73dec1-f084-51ca-ad67-6a943391f21c', 'word_count': 