w years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given the efforts at some of the top schools to guide their students away from Wall Street and into public service, I’ve been wondering whether the career choices of the nation’s young elites have changed much in the last few years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of Harvard, and Into Finance', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be979ba1-1d70-56b6-abdc-f5658a70bada', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be979ba1-1d70-56b6-abdc-f5658a70bada'}, {'abstract': 'The best present for a coffee lover is a coffee, preferably from a cult roaster.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/ristretto-holiday/', 'snippet': 'The best present for a coffee lover is a coffee, preferably from a cult roaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best present for a coffee lover is coffee. It doesn’t need to be expensive to be great, and if it’s a subscription for regular shipments of hard-to-find coffee from a cult roaster, it makes giving the gift all the more gratifying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | Holiday', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b085751-5895-5ff1-bd4d-711d6422903e', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b085751-5895-5ff1-bd4d-711d6422903e'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Gosling gets in the Drunk History holiday spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/hey-girl-happy-holidays-to-you-to-us/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Gosling gets in the Drunk History holiday spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s face it, certain cultural forces are unstoppable. Harvey Weinstein’s quest to win Oscars. The disarming power of kittens in movie trailers. And Ryan Gosling. The coolest person of the year – as anointed by that frequent arbiter of raditude, Time Magazine – has also been among the stickiest, meme–wise. (Do we need to explain? Mr. Gosling provides the dreamy stare; bloggers provide the come-ons.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hey, Girl. Happy Holidays. To You. To Us.', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:08:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72ee7bac-95f2-5019-9672-bb28d1fdc863', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72ee7bac-95f2-5019-9672-bb28d1fdc863'}, {'abstract': 'The government also pledges to “significantly” improve the safety of its nuclear plants and speed up the elimination of old automobiles and motorcycles.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/on-our-radar-china-orders-emission-cuts/', 'snippet': 'The government also pledges to “significantly” improve the safety of its nuclear plants and speed up the elimination of old automobiles and motorcycles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid protests over pollution, China says it has ordered local governments to reduce emissions of major pollutants by as much as 10 percent by 2015. Skeptics point out that the government’s monitoring of pollutants is lax and in some cases highly inaccurate. [The Telegraph]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: China Demands Emission Cuts', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8355005c-4cec-5ed4-bc2d-419cbc7fb7f2', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8355005c-4cec-5ed4-bc2d-419cbc7fb7f2'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/what-were-reading-336/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Afar: A pumpkin baked in a blazing fire. Sweetbreads and blood sausage. Frosty caipirinhas. Here’s what pastry chef Caitlin Freeman found on a trip to Uruguay. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5625096-8b37-5443-9129-5aaf4e405fb2', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5625096-8b37-5443-9129-5aaf4e405fb2'}, {'abstract': 'The National Association of Realtors said sales from 2007 to 2010 were about 14 percent lower than it previously reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/economy/home-resales-rose-in-november.html', 'snippet': 'The National Association of Realtors said sales from 2007 to 2010 were about 14 percent lower than it previously reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The organization that once said the housing boom would never bust said on Wednesday that the market collapse was even worse than it originally reported.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Correcting Data Error, Realtor Group Revises Existing-Home Sales Downward', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Correcting Data Error, Realtor Group Revises Existing-Home Sales Downward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Realtors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a9c7acf-3126-5132-9147-c6e9dc651597', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a9c7acf-3126-5132-9147-c6e9dc651597'}, {'abstract': 'Californians have started a campaign to abolish capital punishment through a ballot initiative.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/death-penalty-death-watch-california/', 'snippet': 'Californians have started a campaign to abolish capital punishment through a ballot initiative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve already made my position on capital punishment clear, on the editorial page and on this blog. The death penalty is immoral: the state shouldn’t play at executioner. It’s imposed in a racially biased manner, defendants have insufficient access to reliable counsel, and it’s also impractical: It’s expensive, with convicts sitting on death row for decades, and the means of execution are often cruel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Penalty Death Watch: California', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:21:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f739e14e-b338-5abd-9e77-0496f233579c', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f739e14e-b338-5abd-9e77-0496f233579c'}, {'abstract': 'Twelve fun apps and travel games to keep your children entertained during long trips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/travel/apps-to-keep-children-happy.html', 'snippet': 'Twelve fun apps and travel games to keep your children entertained during long trips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH Christmas upon us and New Year’s just around the bend, many families are contending with long road trips and crowded flights. All those hours in the car and at the airport are bound to bring out tantrums in toddlers, squabbles among siblings and the familiar “I’m bored” from tweens.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25PRAC/25PRAC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25PRAC/25PRAC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25PRAC/25PRAC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25PRAC/25PRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25PRAC/25PRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apps to Keep Children Happy', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apps to Keep Children Happy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/598f7add-fdba-57ae-8bb4-603cb578b034', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/598f7add-fdba-57ae-8bb4-603cb578b034'}, {'abstract': 'When you are on the road, what apps have you used to keep your kids busy? How about some unplugged ideas? Share your responses in the comments below.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/what-are-the-best-apps-to-keep-kids-entertained-while-traveling/', 'snippet': 'When you are on the road, what apps have you used to keep your kids busy? How about some unplugged ideas? Share your responses in the comments below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in the Practical Traveler column Michelle Higgins offers a selection of fun kids apps to keep children entertained while traveling, as well as some unplugged ideas. When you are on the road, what apps have you used to keep your kids busy? How about some unplugged ideas? Share your responses in the comments below. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are the Best Apps to Keep Kids Entertained While Traveling?', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a3c3d66-fc70-55e6-ba14-46e87197be92', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a3c3d66-fc70-55e6-ba14-46e87197be92'}, {'abstract': 'Research in Motion, maker of the BlackBerry, has been the object of persistent deal speculation this year as a result of a string of weak financial reports, service outages and worries over lost market share.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/rim-shares-jump-on-takeover-whispers/', 'snippet': 'Research in Motion, maker of the BlackBerry, has been the object of persistent deal speculation this year as a result of a string of weak financial reports, service outages and worries over lost market share.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Speculation about suitors circling Research in Motion breathed new life into its shares on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'RIM Shares Jump on Takeover Whispers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T15:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/050473a5-e277-5b7a-90a9-dd5e2e434372', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/050473a5-e277-5b7a-90a9-dd5e2e434372'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bale, who was in China promoting his film “The Flowers of War,” was attacked last week by government-backed guards when he tried to visit a lawyer who has been confined to his home for more than a year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/china-says-christian-bale-should-be-embarrassed-after-assault/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bale, who was in China promoting his film “The Flowers of War,” was attacked last week by government-backed guards when he tried to visit a lawyer who has been confined to his home for more than a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While American audiences struggle to understand the dialogue in the trailer for Christian Bale’s next Batman movie, the Chinese government has expressed itself loud and clear to that “Dark Knight” star, saying that Mr. Bale was trying to “create news” when he tried to visit a detained lawyer in China last week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Says Christian Bale Should Be Embarrassed After Assault', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bale, Christian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen Guangcheng', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Yimou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e600007-94b1-5eb4-a57a-50b29b88eb50', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e600007-94b1-5eb4-a57a-50b29b88eb50'}, {'abstract': 'New York restaurants fare well, with a few exceptions, in a Washington Post comparison of inexpensive meals in the two cities.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/new-york-or-d-c-whose-cheap-food-rules/', 'snippet': 'New York restaurants fare well, with a few exceptions, in a Washington Post comparison of inexpensive meals in the two cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few rivalries between cities start with one side pleading its inferiority. But the arena here is restaurants, not sports, and so The Washington Post set up a smackdown between D.C. and New York — and which has the better cheap food — by stipulating its challenger status.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York or D.C: Whose Cheap Food Rules?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Ed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9004e078-a28f-5c5a-b254-2868ef12ab2f', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9004e078-a28f-5c5a-b254-2868ef12ab2f'}, {'abstract': 'The Campaign Finance API now supports independent expenditure data.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/new-in-the-campaign-finance-api-independent-expenditures/', 'snippet': 'The Campaign Finance API now supports independent expenditure data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Campaign Finance API started as a service for data about presidential candidates. But as the campaign for next year’s presidential election has unfolded, it’s clearer than ever that the men and women jockeying for the Republican nomination are only a part of the action. Independent efforts, from so-called “Super PACs” to advertising campaigns funded by wealthy individuals and interest groups, play an important role in federal elections, as our reporters have written.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New in the Campaign Finance API: Independent Expenditures', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:05:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By DEREK WILLIS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WILLIS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36239ebc-d145-500f-83cf-fb3ee44ac005', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36239ebc-d145-500f-83cf-fb3ee44ac005'}, {'abstract': 'But will anyone call him on it?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/romneys-big-lie/', 'snippet': 'But will anyone call him on it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suppose that President Obama were to make the following statement:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Big Lie', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cff34260-69ee-51bd-8213-4586db7062c0', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cff34260-69ee-51bd-8213-4586db7062c0'}, {'abstract': 'Before getting the Spielberg treatment, Hergé’s Tintin went through other visual iterations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/25/movies/tintin-phases-slideshow.html', 'snippet': 'Before getting the Spielberg treatment, Hergé’s Tintin went through other visual iterations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before getting the Spielberg treatment, Hergé’s Tintin went through other visual iterations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/movies/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/movies/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/movies/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/movies/tintin-phases-slideshow-slide-ADHY/tintin-ph