YouTube became vital platforms for organizing and disseminating information during the Arab Spring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The value of social media as a tool to help bring political change was displayed in dramatic fashion on Jan. 25. After the people of Tunisia in January had utilized Facebook and YouTube to help topple the regime of President Zine el-Abidine Ben Ali, opposition groups in Egypt were inspired. They, too, turned to Facebook, Twitter and YouTube to help organize protests for Jan. 25, known as National Police Day — the beginning of the uprising in Egypt that brought down the government of Hosni Mubarak.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | Social Media and Egypt’s Revolution', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ben Ali, Zine El-Abidine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dde02cc-0815-54fd-9a00-e2159e77fe54', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dde02cc-0815-54fd-9a00-e2159e77fe54'}, {'abstract': 'High protein diets and superhero workouts – those were two of the most sought after topics on the Internet in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-most-popular-health-topics-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'High protein diets and superhero workouts – those were two of the most sought after topics on the Internet in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High-protein diets and superhero workouts – those were two of the most sought-after topics on the Internet in 2011.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Most Popular Health Topics of 2011', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2074267-8112-5b79-be74-dd87401e292c', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2074267-8112-5b79-be74-dd87401e292c'}, {'abstract': 'But Newt Gingrich did not criticize Speaker John A. Boehner for leading House Republicans in rejecting the Senate compromise.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/gingrich-condemns-the-senate-for-collapse-of-payroll-tax-cut-extension/', 'snippet': 'But Newt Gingrich did not criticize Speaker John A. Boehner for leading House Republicans in rejecting the Senate compromise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Newt Gingrich put a pox on all parties in Washington on Wednesday for failing to pass a payroll tax extension, but he especially condemned the Senate, where Republicans joined Democrats to vote for a two-month extension of the tax break, which affects 160 million Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Condemns Senate on Payroll Tax Vote', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:44:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70e497bc-0003-575c-9c3a-a7f4030d8311', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70e497bc-0003-575c-9c3a-a7f4030d8311'}, {'abstract': 'Many owners who put off selling businesses because of the economy now have at least one year of profits and are more attractive to investors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/smallbusiness/why-some-business-owners-think-now-is-the-time-to-sell.html', 'snippet': 'Many owners who put off selling businesses because of the economy now have at least one year of profits and are more attractive to investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking back, Cyndi Finkle wishes she had sold her craft services company, Sunday Night Dinner, early in 2008 when the economy was booming. With a track record of 30 to 50 percent annual growth for each of the previous five years, it could have been a compelling transaction.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Some Business Owners Think Now Is the Time to Sell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Some Business Owners Think Now Is the Time to Sell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Reynolds Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': 'Reynolds', 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37abbf3c-37f7-5a2f-9ab1-fd8d3ef24961', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37abbf3c-37f7-5a2f-9ab1-fd8d3ef24961'}, {'abstract': 'The police identified two suspects,  Eldin Ahmetovic and Yulia Bushuyeva, who are accused of taking jewelry, electronics, money and collectibles in 12 break-ins in Astoria.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/duo-wanted-in-string-of-house-burglaries-in-queens/', 'snippet': 'The police identified two suspects,  Eldin Ahmetovic and Yulia Bushuyeva, who are accused of taking jewelry, electronics, money and collectibles in 12 break-ins in Astoria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man and a woman working as a burglary team are wanted in connection with 12 home break-ins in Astoria, Queens, most of them within the last month, the police said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duo Wanted in String of House Burglaries in Queens', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astoria (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e893b8ef-2f35-5cc1-8e07-0d878e091aac', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e893b8ef-2f35-5cc1-8e07-0d878e091aac'}, {'abstract': 'Here are 5 reasons it might be a good idea — and why you might want to start the process now.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/are-you-thinking-of-selling-your-business-in-2012/', 'snippet': 'Here are 5 reasons it might be a good idea — and why you might want to start the process now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it 2012 yet? From where I sit, the Great Recession has felt like the movie “Groundhog Day,” in which Bill Murray relives the same miserable day over and over again. For those of us waiting for the business-for-sale marketplace to turn the corner, 2012 brings a number of reasons for hope, many of which are addressed in a just-published New York Times article. While the decision to sell your business should be entered into with careful thought and planning, here are five reasons you may want to get a deal done by the end of 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Thinking of Selling Your Business in 2012?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:53:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37d70269-450c-581c-8b30-69b9ce75023c', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37d70269-450c-581c-8b30-69b9ce75023c'}, {'abstract': 'Minnesota is hoping that Ricky Rubio, who wowed the crowd with clever passing in his exhibition debut, can bring excitement and victories to a team that hasn’t made the playoffs since 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/sports/basketball/ricky-rubio-makes-fancy-first-impression-with-timberwolves.html', 'snippet': 'Minnesota is hoping that Ricky Rubio, who wowed the crowd with clever passing in his exhibition debut, can bring excitement and victories to a team that hasn’t made the playoffs since 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Charisma, he’s got. The Spanish basketball star Ricky Rubio, with his longish dark hair and fashionable facial stubble, flashed plenty of that in his first two appearances with the Minnesota Timberwolves. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/basketball/22rubio-pic/22rubio-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/basketball/22rubio-pic/22rubio-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/basketball/22rubio-pic/22rubio-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Star Makes a Fancy First Impression', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Star Makes a Fancy First Impression', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Timberwolves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c7939b-615f-5e70-9331-8fae78589466', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c7939b-615f-5e70-9331-8fae78589466'}, {'abstract': 'In just one generation, evolution can render captive salmon unable to perform well in the wild.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/unfit-salmon-and-plain-old-darwinian-selection/', 'snippet': 'In just one generation, evolution can render captive salmon unable to perform well in the wild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Captive-born salmon waste no time making themselves at home. In crowded aquaculture tanks, they outperform wild counterparts in survival and reproduction — great news if you’re a salmon farmer. But these changes come at a cost. The more capable a salmon is of thriving in captivity, the less capable it is of succeeding in the wild. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unfit Salmon and ‘Plain Old Darwinian Selection’', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T16:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ebff1f5-8bac-5803-9f93-8aba0ba80cbd', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ebff1f5-8bac-5803-9f93-8aba0ba80cbd'}, {'abstract': 'In the last installment of our informal survey of Iraqis around the country on the pullout of U.S. forces, we visit Babil Province, home to the ancient Mesopotamian city of Babylon.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/what-iraqis-think-of-the-american-withdrawal-babil-province/', 'snippet': 'In the last installment of our informal survey of Iraqis around the country on the pullout of U.S. forces, we visit Babil Province, home to the ancient Mesopotamian city of Babylon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As American forces pulled out of Iraq, we asked Iraqis around the country three questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Iraqis Think of the American Withdrawal: Babil Province', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussein, Saddam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By An Iraqi Journalist With The York Times in Babil', 'person': [{'firstname': 'An', 'middlename': 'Iraqi', 'lastname': 'Journalist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9459fe60-e1a7-58de-9c08-2d239e5853b9', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9459fe60-e1a7-58de-9c08-2d239e5853b9'}, {'abstract': 'In case you missed it, here’s a transcript of Tuesday night’s lively admissions chat on Facebook, as well as an invitation to continue the conversation Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/choice-facebook/', 'snippet': 'In case you missed it, here’s a transcript of Tuesday night’s lively admissions chat on Facebook, as well as an invitation to continue the conversation Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, The Choice blog hosted its first live Facebook discussion about college admissions. Our guest expert was Marie Bigham, director of college counseling at the Greenhill School in Addison, Tex. She answered a series of thoughtful questions from readers on subjects like the role of recommendations in the application process, the rising cost of college and how colleges analyze transcripts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Choice Q. and A. on Facebook: A Recap, and an Invitation', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cdf0e43-95c9-5ced-a7b8-d2463f4d70c4', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cdf0e43-95c9-5ced-a7b8-d2463f4d70c4'}, {'abstract': 'We love a good year-end retrospective. Here’s the 2011 crop, from The Times and from around the Web, followed by ideas for teaching with them.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/looking-back-at-2011-retrospectives-and-ideas-for-teaching-them/', 'snippet': 'We love a good year-end retrospective. Here’s the 2011 crop, from The Times and from around the Web, followed by ideas for teaching with them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Jan. 1, 2012', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Back at 2011: Retrospectives and Ideas for Teaching With Them', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/901550eb-d09e-5448-962e-5fb60a4e7043', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/901550eb-d09e-5448-962e-5fb60a4e7043'}, {'abstract': 'Zappa Records is moving ahead with the release of the album, a legend among fans of Captain Beefheart, who died a year ago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/an-official-release-for-captain-beefhearts-bat-chain-puller/', 'snippet': 'Zappa Records is moving ahead with the release of the album, a legend among fans of Captain Beefheart, who died a year ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More than 36 years after it was recorded, Zappa Records is finally releasing Captain Beefheart’s album “Bat Chain Puller,” Billboard  and The Wire report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Official Release for Captain Beefheart’s ‘Bat Chain Puller’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Vliet, Don', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zappa, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8cefb8c-d787-5d6e-93dc-6930bb81c90c', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8cefb8c-d787-5d6e-93dc-6930bb81c90c'}, {'abstract': 'A judge for the F.C.C. ordered Comcast to carry the Tennis Channel as it does Versus and the Golf Channel.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/f-c-c-rules-for-the-tennis-channel/', 'snippet': 'A judge for the F.C.C. ordered Comcast to carry the Tennis Channel as it does Versus and the Golf Channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, a Federal Communications Commission administrative law judge ordered Comcast to carry the Tennis Channel exactly as it does Versus and the Golf Channel. The ruling is particularly important because Comcast is the largest owner of cable systems in the United States. Richard Sandomir has the story here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Rules for the Tennis Channel', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golf Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennis Channel, The', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Versus (TV Network)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:18:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c47f57-3e78-58fc-9f53-36a1fab8a4e4', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c47f57-3e78-58fc-9f53-36a1fab8a4e4'}, {'abstract': 'The large bronze work may have drawn the eyes of thieves seeking to profit from the rise in metal prices.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/large-hepworth-sculpture-stolen-from-london-park/', 'snippet': 'The large bronze work may have drawn the eyes of thieves seeking to profit from the rise in metal prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thieves entered Dulwich Park in south London on Monday night and stole a large bronze sculpture by one of Britain’s much-loved artists. The sculpture, “Two Forms (Divided Circle),’’ by Barbara Hepworth, had been a familiar sight since it was installed in the park more than 40 years ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Large Hepworth Sculpture Stolen From  Park in London', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hepworth, Barbara', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96323bac-91c2-5d2f-a2d7-2e5bea06a4ee', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96323bac-91c2-5d2f-a2d7-2e5bea06a4ee'}, {'abstract': 'A Dutch researcher whose work prompted the United States to ask scientific journals to withhold details that bioterrorists could use expressed doubts that the information can be kept out of the wrong hands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/health/security-in-h5n1-bird-flu-study-was-paramount-scientist-says.html', 'snippet': 'A Dutch researcher whose work prompted the United States to ask scientific journals to withhold details that bioterrorists could use expressed doubts that the information can be kept out of the wrong hands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Science Advisory Board for Biosecurity, concerned about bioterrorism and a worldwide pandemic, has for the first time ever urged scientific journals to keep details out of reports that they intend to publish on a highly transmissible form of the bird flu called A(H5N1), which has a high death rate in people. Working with ferrets, researchers on the virus at two medical centers — Erasmus Medical Center in Rotterdam, in the Netherlands, and the University of Wisconsin-Madison — are investigating genetic changes that may make the virus more easily transmittable to people. Doreen Carvajal spoke with Ron A. M. Fouchier, the lead researcher at the Erasmus Center. An edited and condensed version of the conversation follows. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/science/22fouchier/22fouchier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/science/22fouchier/22fouchier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/science/22fouchier/22fouchier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Security in Flu Study Was Paramount, Scientist Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scientist in Bird Flu Study Says He Is Not Convinced Censorship Is a Safeguard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e33958c-2eac-55ab-bc00-e635a191d80c', 'word_count': 1463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e33958c-2eac-55ab-bc00-e635a191d80c'}, {'abstract': 'Anonymous donors are paying off accounts for families at big-box stores.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/layaway-angels-pay-off-family-accounts/', 'snippet': 'Anonymous donors are paying off accounts for families at big-box stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anonymous donors have been going into big-box stores — Kmart in particular — and paying off layaway accounts. NPR and The Associated Press\xa0picked up the story five days ago, and in it a reporter described a young father stepping up to the layaway counter with three kids behind him to pay something on his account when a “mysterious woman” approached.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Layaway Angels’ Pay Off Family Accounts', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:32:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f578c836-fae4-5586-ac04-75fe9ef67bf9', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f578c836-fae4-5586-ac04-75fe9ef67bf9'}, {'abstract': 'Recipes for ham glazes, and an appeal to readers for more.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/how-do-you-glaze-a-ham/', 'snippet': 'Recipes for ham glazes, and an appeal to readers for more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bourbon, molasses and pecans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Glaze a Ham?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 