 iPhone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are into Clark W Griswold-level holiday decorating (you know who you are – your dog is wearing antlers right now), then Speck, makers of protective cases for electronic devices, has a little holiday cheer for your iPhone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An iPhone Cover Fit for the Griswolds', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T17:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cb5762e-2962-5ff2-919e-7e63fa78f562', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cb5762e-2962-5ff2-919e-7e63fa78f562'}, {'abstract': 'The company, which closed in 2004, will hold auditions to create a new stripped-down troupe of 18 dancers and hopes to return to a New York stage by spring 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/dance-theater-of-harlem-to-start-auditioning-for-revived-troupe/', 'snippet': 'The company, which closed in 2004, will hold auditions to create a new stripped-down troupe of 18 dancers and hopes to return to a New York stage by spring 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dance companies are supposed to be shrinking, not starting up in these recessionary times. Not so at the Dance Theater of Harlem, which closed its company in 2004. Theater officials on Wednesday announced the start of auditions to create a new stripped down troupe of 18 dancers, which will begin rehearsing in August and touring in October and aims to return to a New York stage by April 2013. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance Theater of Harlem to Start Auditions for Revived Troupe', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance Theater of Harlem To Start Auditions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garland, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harper, Francesca', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Virginia (1950- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dance Theater of Harlem', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fdcca0c-7f6e-5d4a-a306-7348411f4384', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fdcca0c-7f6e-5d4a-a306-7348411f4384'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department said Bank of America had agreed to a record fair-lending settlement over allegations of discriminatory practices by a mortgage subsidiary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/us-settlement-reported-on-countrywide-lending.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department said Bank of America had agreed to a record fair-lending settlement over allegations of discriminatory practices by a mortgage subsidiary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department on Wednesday announced the largest residential fair-lending settlement in history, saying that Bank of America had agreed to pay $335 