its stocking this year from one of its most faithful exhibitors, Microsoft, which said the 2012 Consumer Electronics Show would be its last. It is a further sign of how once-mighty...', 'lead_paragraph': ' 2:55 p.m. | Updated to reflect comment from the Consumer Electronics Association.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/technology/21bits-microsoft/21bits-microsoft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Electronics Show Loses Its Anchor, Microsoft', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:11:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/609d5cf7-1500-59b2-8285-19fff2e2c169', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/609d5cf7-1500-59b2-8285-19fff2e2c169'}, {'abstract': 'You might expect folks who make Santa apps to be filled with the holiday spirit, but after testing some of their wares, it’s clear they might be some of the Scroogiest people around. Here’s why.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/apps-to-put-words-in-santas-mouth/', 'snippet': 'You might expect folks who make Santa apps to be filled with the holiday spirit, but after testing some of their wares, it’s clear they might be some of the Scroogiest people around. Here’s why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might expect folks who make iPhone Santa apps to be filled with the holiday spirit, but after testing some of their wares, I’ve concluded they might be some of the Scroogiest people around. I tried some apps similar to one I liked last year, “Talking Santa,” which let me record a message and make it appear to come from an animated Santa. I thought it would be a fun way for parents to send a message from Santa to their children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apps to Put Words in Santa’s Mouth', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Santa Claus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41401311-4991-5bc8-8eae-796abd7c78f3', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41401311-4991-5bc8-8eae-796abd7c78f3'}, {'abstract': 'A storied New York hotel installs an electric fence to keep its storied cat away from food and drink.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-algonquin-curtails-its-famous-cat/', 'snippet': 'A storied New York hotel installs an electric fence to keep its storied cat away from food and drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herding cats, as we all know, isn’t easy. So the Algonquin hotel has installed an electronic fence to keep its resident cat, Matilda, in the lobby and out of areas where food and drink are served.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Algonquin Curtails Its Famous Cat', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/250a0e3c-2e50-5e5e-8e9c-bcdb948bfa81', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/250a0e3c-2e50-5e5e-8e9c-bcdb948bfa81'}, {'abstract': 'The so-called Coulomb friction-damped disc brake could be commercialized within two or three years, G.M. said.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/g-m-claims-remedy-for-squealing-brakes/', 'snippet': 'The so-called Coulomb friction-damped disc brake could be commercialized within two or three years, G.M. said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At one time or another, most motorists register the fingers-on-chalkboard sound of squealing brakes coming from their cars. So unnerving is the sound that it can cause drivers to erroneously assume that their brakes may be on the verge of failure. On Wednesday, General Motors announced that it was working on a brake assembly that might prevent the cacophony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Claims Remedy for Squealing Brakes', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82814b10-83a2-5772-85e4-88ae12e45c16', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82814b10-83a2-5772-85e4-88ae12e45c16'}, {'abstract': 'Much like your wardrobe, home fragrance is about mastering a mix of the classic and the seasonal.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/vain-glorious-hold-a-candle/', 'snippet': 'Much like your wardrobe, home fragrance is about mastering a mix of the classic and the seasonal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much like your wardrobe, home fragrance is about mastering a mix of the classic and the seasonal. Keep your beloved Feu de Bois candle from burning out by taking a match to one of these festive, holiday-inspired offerings instead:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Hold a Candle', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Derian, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Astier de Villatte', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd49532d-a28e-5edc-afb8-5344814a84c9', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd49532d-a28e-5edc-afb8-5344814a84c9'}, {'abstract': 'We’ll get to hear from actual voters in 2012. What can they say?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-year-in-review-and-next-year-in-preview/', 'snippet': 'We’ll get to hear from actual voters in 2012. What can they say?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David, this will be our last conversation of 2011. When we talk next in two weeks, the Iowa caucuses will be over. Who do you think will win? The way things are going, I have to conclude it’s going to be Steve Jobs. True, he’s no longer alive, but these days everybody seems to like him a lot. Which you certainly cannot say of any of the Republican presidential candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Review — And Next Year in Preview', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f27e23-71cb-510e-a479-78ffbf78fb43', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f27e23-71cb-510e-a479-78ffbf78fb43'}, {'abstract': 'Zvonko Veselinovic was arrested a day after Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany warned that Serbia must reach a peace deal with Kosovo to join the European Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/europe/serb-said-to-be-behind-kosovo-clashes-is-arrested.html', 'snippet': 'Zvonko Veselinovic was arrested a day after Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany warned that Serbia must reach a peace deal with Kosovo to join the European Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — An ethnic Serb accused of being the shadowy smuggler behind recent border clashes in northern Kosovo was arrested in central Serbia late Tuesday, a day after Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany warned Serbia that it must reach a peace agreement with Kosovo to join the European Union. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Serb Charged With Arms Smuggling in Kosovo Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Serb Charged With Arms Smuggling in Kosovo Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a40bde-1df3-58e9-b3a1-6d08802835f5', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a40bde-1df3-58e9-b3a1-6d08802835f5'}, {'abstract': 'Distinctive socks are a clever and easy way for men to add a little oomph to their look without going overboard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks.html', 'snippet': 'Distinctive socks are a clever and easy way for men to add a little oomph to their look without going overboard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Distinctive socks are a clever and easy way for men to add a little oomph to their look without going overboard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/20/fashion/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN/1222tradingupsocks-slide-NJHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bold, Colorful Men’s Socks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/752cc545-1091-55db-b341-d9c439be7928', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/752cc545-1091-55db-b341-d9c439be7928'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly nine years of war in Iraq have produced a growing cadre of world-class, homegrown Iraqi news photographers. The Lens blog shares the stories of five of them.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/lens-iraqi-photographers-captured-the-costs-of-war/', 'snippet': 'Nearly nine years of war in Iraq have produced a growing cadre of world-class, homegrown Iraqi news photographers. The Lens blog shares the stories of five of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Foreigners may have started the war in Iraq, but it was not only foreigners who covered its deadly battles, car bombs, civilian casualties and sectarian violence. Over on the Lens blog, Anne Barnard tells the story of Iraqi photographers who were tried, tempered and tested in the nine years since the American invasion — and who came out the other side professional photojournalists. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: Iraqi Photographers Captured the Costs of War', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e293c06b-ca13-50a9-95b4-231b67928616', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e293c06b-ca13-50a9-95b4-231b67928616'}, {'abstract': 'It seems that a distinctive staged proposal has become de rigueur. Many have tried, and some have succeeded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/interesting-marriage-proposals-of-2011.html', 'snippet': 'It seems that a distinctive staged proposal has become de rigueur. Many have tried, and some have succeeded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME marriage proposals make for great theater, but in the case of Dina Kirschenbaum and Mark Thomas, a theater made for a great proposal, one of the best submitted in 2011.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/fashion/25fieldnotes/25fieldnotes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/fashion/25fieldnotes/25fieldnotes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/fashion/25fieldnotes/25fieldnotes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Simple Yes or No? It’s Not That Easy', 'kicker': 'Field Notes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Simple Yes or No? It’s Not That Easy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'origina