 of bungling the politically charged issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/us/OBAMA/OBAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Gets a Lift From Tax Battle With Republicans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Battle With G.O.P. Gives a Lift To Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/884bce7b-9033-5235-ab98-6a2e68b15dd8', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/884bce7b-9033-5235-ab98-6a2e68b15dd8'}, {'abstract': 'YouTube has a new network setting designed to give schools more control over what their students see when they visit the video site from a classroom or library PC.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/google-expands-youtubes-suite-of-services-for-schools/', 'snippet': 'YouTube has a new network setting designed to give schools more control over what their students see when they visit the video site from a classroom or library PC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say the word “YouTube” to most teachers and you’ll get the type of cringe reserved for a ringing cellphone. Google, which owns YouTube, would like change that with a new network setting designed to give schools more control over what their students see when they visit the video site from a classroom or library PC.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Expands YouTube’s Suite of Services for Schools', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:55:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a85d8ce6-1c3d-520d-b938-0b426fdd12fa', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a85d8ce6-1c3d-520d-b938-0b426fdd12fa'}, {'abstract': 'New York City had accused the stores on Staten Island and in Chinatown of being a front for cigarette-tax evasion.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/two-roll-your-own-cigarette-stores-to-close/', 'snippet': 'New York City had accused the stores on Staten Island and in Chinatown of being a front for cigarette-tax evasion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two stores, on Staten Island and in Chinatown, have agreed to stop selling roll-your-own cigarettes after New York City accused them of being fronts for evading cigarette taxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Roll-Your-Own-Cigarette Stores to Close', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardozo, Michael A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:56:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f9b377e-a844-5e8f-9e23-b4e09d7b6131', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f9b377e-a844-5e8f-9e23-b4e09d7b6131'}, {'abstract': 'Janusz Kaminski, Steven Spielberg’s longtime cinematographer, discusses his approach for the film “War Horse.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/below-the-line-green-valleys-golden-sunsets-and-war-horse/', 'snippet': 'Janusz Kaminski, Steven Spielberg’s longtime cinematographer, discusses his approach for the film “War Horse.”', 'lead_paragraph': "“War Horse,” Steven Spielberg’s film adaptation of Michael Morpurgo's children’s novel (and a subsequent play based on it), will open in theaters Christmas Day. But it has the look of a movie that could have just as easily played on movie screens 50 years ago. The wide open spaces, the glowing skies, the rolling hills have the feel of John Ford films, which inspired Mr. Spielberg and his longtime cinematographer, Janusz Kaminski. ", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: Green Valleys, Golden Sunsets and ‘War Horse’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Devon (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T18:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/449dc447-801e-589e-aebc-1b6871012f0b', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/449dc447-801e-589e-aebc-1b6871012f0b'}, {'abstract': 'The South Street Seaport Museum will reopen on Jan. 26, the institution announced on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/south-street-seaport-museum-to-reopen-in-january/', 'snippet': 'The South Street Seaport Museum will reopen on Jan. 26, the institution announced on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South Street Seaport Museum will reopen on Jan. 26, the institution announced on Wednesday. The museum, which has been plagued by financial problems, was provisionally taken over by the Museum of the City of New York in September, with help from a $2 million grant from the Lower Manhattan Development Corporation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Street Seaport Museum to Reopen in January', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Susan Henshaw', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the City of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seaport Museum New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South Street Seaport Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27310df9-99dd-5922-9f69-55c3683a9c8a', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27310df9-99dd-5922-9f69-55c3683a9c8a'}, {'abstract': '“By cutting emissions that are linked to developmental disorders and respiratory illnesses like asthma, these standards represent a major victory for clean air and public health,” the agency’s director says.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/e-p-a-announces-mercury-limits/', 'snippet': '“By cutting emissions that are linked to developmental disorders and respiratory illnesses like asthma, these standards represent a major victory for clean air and public health,” the agency’s director says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Environmental Protection Agency unveiled new standards on Wednesday sharply limiting emissions of mercury and other toxic pollutants from the nation’s coal– and oil-burning power plants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Issues Limits on Mercury Emissions', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d631b49b-f17c-506b-8fb6-e2904b01bd28', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d631b49b-f17c-506b-8fb6-e2904b01bd28'}, {'abstract': 'When reporters balked at the sandwiches offered by the candidate, Mitt Romney teased them for being high brow, saying “This is the John Kerry bus back there.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/romney-teases-reporters-over-lunch/', 'snippet': 'When reporters balked at the sandwiches offered by the candidate, Mitt Romney teased them for being high brow, saying “This is the John Kerry bus back there.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWPORT, N.H. — The plane the Romney campaign charters for reporters is nicknamed “Hair Force One,” and on Wednesday afternoon, Mr. Romney offered up his own moniker for the press bus: “This is the John Kerry bus,” Mr. Romney quipped, when a group of finicky reporters didn’t immediately jump for the submarine sandwiches he tried to pass out for lunch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Teases Reporters Over Lunch', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 