ters heading into the holiday break.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the first Republican nominating contests just weeks away, we are looking to take the pulse of New Hampshire voters heading into the holiday break. Do you live in New Hampshire? If you plan to vote in the primary, have you chosen a candidate? What issue is most important to you? What does the race look like from where you stand? And how does it compare to primaries past?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Pulse of New Hampshire Voters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b677f4b-7d3a-525d-ab0e-a9ec6ff2be10', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b677f4b-7d3a-525d-ab0e-a9ec6ff2be10'}, {'abstract': 'The Whitney Museum announced an eclectic lineup for the 75th edition of its Biennial, a survey of contemporary American art that opens March 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/whitney-announces-biennial-artists/', 'snippet': 'The Whitney Museum announced an eclectic lineup for the 75th edition of its Biennial, a survey of contemporary American art that opens March 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, some of the Whitney Museum of American Art‘s Biennials have featured over-the-top spectacle, while others have been lower key. On Wednesday, the museum announced an eclectic lineup for the 76th edition of its survey of contemporary American art, which opens March 1. The list includes Dennis Cooper, who plans to install a speaking “robot”; Andrea Fraser, who once posed as a museum tour guide as part of a performance piece; Kate Levant, who will have a hanging-fabric sculpture on display; and Nick Mauss, who is installing a velvet room. Also represented will be the experimental theatrical director and playwright Richard Maxwell; the filmmakers Vincent Gallo, Werner Herzog and Frederick Wiseman; the dancer and choreographer Michael Clark; and the rock band Red Krayola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whitney Announces Biennial Artists', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Dennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fraser, Andrea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallo, Vincent', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiseman, Frederick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85854038-889f-5c42-ac4d-08fa36615898', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85854038-889f-5c42-ac4d-08fa36615898'}, {'abstract': 'Waiting to see what develops in North Korea feels familiar, and that’s what we should do: wait and see.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/opinion/north-korea-isnt-a-crisis-yet.html', 'snippet': 'Waiting to see what develops in North Korea feels familiar, and that’s what we should do: wait and see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do, and Not Do, About North Korea', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What to Do, and Not Do, About North Korea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Un', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:32:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert L. Gallucci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Gallucci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12cee73d-d58a-5e8b-8f18-d3143408695f', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12cee73d-d58a-5e8b-8f18-d3143408695f'}, {'abstract': 'The actor partly blamed the current candidates for his loss of interest in Mayor Bloomberg’s job, suggesting that he found their keen ambition and eagerness distasteful.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/baldwin-me-mayor-wheres-the-fun/', 'snippet': 'The actor partly blamed the current candidates for his loss of interest in Mayor Bloomberg’s job, suggesting that he found their keen ambition and eagerness distasteful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Mayor Baldwin is not to be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baldwin Says He’s Lost Interest in Mayor’s Job', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'perso