BC in Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1ef1ee8-0ae7-543b-ad8b-362105321957', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1ef1ee8-0ae7-543b-ad8b-362105321957'}, {'abstract': 'The ad, which promoted mascara, was criticized because its photo of the country music star  had been altered to show thicker eyelashes.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/covergirl-withdraws-enhanced-taylor-swift-ad/', 'snippet': 'The ad, which promoted mascara, was criticized because its photo of the country music star  had been altered to show thicker eyelashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a certain Taylor Swift ad for CoverGirl mascara that you won’t be seeing in American magazines any time soon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CoverGirl Withdraws ‘Enhanced’ Taylor Swift Ad', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Better Business Bureaus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/976f4f15-cccf-5353-b30b-0bb45dfcc635', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/976f4f15-cccf-5353-b30b-0bb45dfcc635'}, {'abstract': 'Both models will have their formal introductions at the Detroit auto show in January.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/mercedes-benz-introduces-gas-and-diesel-e-class-hybrids/', 'snippet': 'Both models will have their formal introductions at the Detroit auto show in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, Mercedes-Benz announced two new hybrid E-Class sedans. The E300 BlueTec Hybrid is equipped with a diesel-electric powertrain, the automaker’s first to be commercialized, while the E400 Hybrid has a more conventional gas-electric hybrid system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mercedes-Benz Introduces Gas and Diesel E-Class Hybrids', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daimler AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T19:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3609f8d-b0bf-524d-89b7-6b02e1dc6938', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3609f8d-b0bf-524d-89b7-6b02e1dc6938'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel J. Socolow has helped hand out the $500,000 fellowships since 1997.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/director-of-macarthur-genius-program-to-retire/', 'snippet': 'Daniel J. Socolow has helped hand out the $500,000 fellowships since 1997.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 3:06 p.m. | Updated Daniel J. Socolow, the director since 1997 of the MacArthur Foundation fellowship program known as the “genius” awards, will retire sometime in the next several months, foundation officials are expected to announce Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Director of MacArthur ‘Genius’ Program to Retire', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scholarships and Fellowships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Socolow, Daniel J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MacArthur, John D and Catherine T, Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T20:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96cc4d8-7866-586c-8130-cd22a7939c15', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96cc4d8-7866-586c-8130-cd22a7939c15'}, {'abstract': 'France’s 12th largest city is known for its post-war architecture and its roseate glow.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/eurofile-le-havre-in-a-new-light/', 'snippet': 'France’s 12th largest city is known for its post-war architecture and its roseate glow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Strolling along the Rue de Paris in Le Havre at dusk on an early winter day, I was mystified by the faint rosy glow of the concrete buildings around me. It couldn’t be the sun, since the sky was shrouded with low pewter clouds scuttling in off of the English Channel. Maybe the briny sea air was causing some kind of chemical reaction with the lime in the cement? I’d have to ask my friend Arnaud when I met him a few minutes later for dinner. One way or another, this gentle color blunted the brute angles of these perplexing post-war buildings. One minute, I found them harshly beautiful; the next, cold and alien.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurofile | Le Havre in a New Light', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T20:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78e9d3f3-582d-5aad-be34-753109e82ce8', 'word_count': 1000, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78e9d3f3-582d-5aad-be34-753109e82ce8'}, {'abstract': 'A 22-year-old graphic designer from Chicago unsuccessfully answers a few questions on the beloved European cartoon, “The Adventures of Tintin.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-cultural-osmosis-pop-quiz-the-adventures-of-tintin-edition/', 'snippet': 'A 22-year-old graphic designer from Chicago unsuccessfully answers a few questions on the beloved European cartoon, “The Adventures of Tintin.”', 'lead_paragra