ctor, Alex Poots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rapist Santas in the brutalist opera “Die Soldaten.” The Royal Shakespeare Company performing in a life-size reproduction of its theater. A five-story crane continuously plucking at 30 tons of salvaged clothing. A three-dimensional re-creation of Leonardo’s “Last Supper.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/ARMORY1/ARMORY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/ARMORY1/ARMORY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/ARMORY1/ARMORY1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/ARMORY1/ARMORY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/ARMORY1/ARMORY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Armory’s Ambitions Expand to Match Its Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Armory’s Ambitions Expand to Match Its Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streb, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}