edia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Flu Strains, Folkies and Faith in Science', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seeger, Pete', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10bd621f-9086-5aae-94c9-a06009f8ada1', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10bd621f-9086-5aae-94c9-a06009f8ada1'}, {'abstract': 'A holiday cocktail inspired by the classic rye Manhattan, with ginger syrup, Clementine juice and a generous dousing of Angostura bitters.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/a-seasonal-cocktail-the-bitter-darling/', 'snippet': 'A holiday cocktail inspired by the classic rye Manhattan, with ginger syrup, Clementine juice and a generous dousing of Angostura bitters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was recently asked to create a specialty cocktail for a big holiday bash. I knew I wanted it to be something special and seasonal, but the constraints posed by the party (it was held at the Center for Fiction, a lovely place, but one not equipped with a full bar or full kitchen) demanded that I keep it simple. Not a worry, as I’m inclined to keep it simple where cocktails are concerned.\xa0The classic rye Manhattan was my starting point. What if I replaced the sweet vermouth with ginger syrup? That worked fine, but something was missing. I was testing the drink in a friend’s kitchen in New Hampshire over Thanksgiving weekend. A bowlful of clementines (one of my favorite winter treats) sat on the counter. Freshly squeezed clementine juice — and a generous dousing of Angostura bitters — brought the whole thing together.\xa0It’s easy to make ginger syrup: I prepare a basic sugar-and-water simple syrup, in which I steep peeled, fresh ginger long enough that its strong, spicy bite really comes through. But you can skip this step altogether and buy the excellent ready-made ginger syrup from Brooklyn’s Morris Kitchen.\xa0As a nod to the bitters and the clementine, I christened the drink the Bitter Darling. It was a hit. And even though I invented it especially for one party, I’m sure it’ll be a mainstay of my winter-cocktail repertory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Seasonal Cocktail: The Bitter Darling', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd5f091b-18a7-5077-a373-ba8335a16316', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd5f091b-18a7-5077-a373-ba8335a16316'}, {'abstract': 'I am throwing open the door for those who feel they have been unsung in Times theater reviews.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/theater-talkback-giving-credit-where-its-overdue/', 'snippet': 'I am throwing open the door for those who feel they have been unsung in Times theater reviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in my career as a critic at The New York Times, I began receiving nuisance calls from a ghost. This was before I had caller ID (or an unlisted number), and for a week or so I would pick up my phone only to hear an angry actress berating me for not singling out her performance in my review of an Off Broadway show in which she appeared as a specter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Honorable Mention for the Dishonorably Unmentioned', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rising Phoenix Repertory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soho Rep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1ad6068-21c6-524a-b778-8a49c823b88e', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1ad6068-21c6-524a-b778-8a49c823b88e'}, {'abstract': 'The Giving Spree continues with more gifts to give and get from T’s friends and family.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-giving-spree-brooklyn-decker/', 'snippet': 'The Giving Spree continues with more gifts to give and get from T’s friends and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who: the actress Brooklyn Decker', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Giving Spree | Brooklyn Decker', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12aa92ea-c9ca-57fd-a843-d42004f33698', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12aa92ea-c9ca-57fd-a843-d42004f33698'}, {'abstract': 'The Sphero, produced by Orbotix, is a remote-controlled ball stuffed with miniature technology and five free apps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/technology/personaltech/remote-controlled-ball-holds-potential-delights-state-of-the-art.html', 'snippet': 'The Sphero, produced by Orbotix, is a remote-controlled ball stuffed with miniature technology and five free apps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may remember that, in the movie “Field of Dreams,” a mysterious voice in Kevin Costner’s head kept intoning: “If you build it, they will come.” It took some time for him to realize that somewhat unspecific piece of guidance really meant: “If you build a baseball diamond in a cornfield, dead players will come back to life.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bundle of Potential in a Ball', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bundle Of Potential In a Ball', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6600d3f5-f92a-51a6-aa9a-8ac5cf1fc3a4', 'word_count': 1298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6600d3f5-f92a-51a6-aa9a-8ac5cf1fc3a4'}, {'abstract': 'Financial Engines is offering a new investment management service to 401(k) investors nearing retirement.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/more-advice-for-pre-retirees-coming-to-401ks/', 'snippet': 'Financial Engines is offering a new investment management service to 401(k) investors nearing retirement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re nearing retirement, you’re probably aware of the anxiety-inducing task that lies ahead: figuring out how to replace your paycheck with a steady stream of income generated by your investments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Advice for Pre-Retirees Coming to 401(k)’s', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a63e1c60-f4a6-5db1-81e0-8ab2219c8282', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a63e1c60-f4a6-5db1-81e0-8ab2219c8282'}, {'abstract': 'A new coach and new lines have given the Capitals some new signs of life.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/ovechkin-capitals-look-for-turnaround/', 'snippet': 'A new coach and new lines have given the Capitals some new signs of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe the Washington Capitals are figuring out how to turn the corner. And a good start certainly would be to get superstar Alex Ovechkin going again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ovechkin and Capitals Look for Turnaround', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Dale', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160ed149-b598-5513-a06a-0cb998b8f833', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160ed149-b598-5513-a06a-0cb998b8f833'}, {'abstract': 'For the charity-minded, worthwhile causes in the food world.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/food-gifts-that-matter/', 'snippet': 'For the charity-minded, worthwhile causes in the food world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column today offers suggestions for gifts for non-cooks. Obviously, cooking is not the only issue out there, and direct contact with friends is not the only way to change things in the food world: there is cash. There are countless worthy causes and just as many charitable institutions. If finding the cash to spare is difficult so, too, may be choosing where it will be put to best use. But if you’re thinking about making a donation this year to brighten the national or global food landscape, here’s a list of organizations where your gifts will be well spent. (No doubt there are equally worthy omissions; please add them in the comments section.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Gifts That Matter', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:18:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e8760d-a5f0-5d51-a448-f0ee56551d0e', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e8760d-a5f0-5d51-a448-f0ee56551d0e'}, {'abstract': 'Ikram Goldman’s store carries clothes that are more intellectually provocative than flattering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.co