lue': 'Goldman, Ikram', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Series', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef488c70-0339-56be-a01e-ee095e66aa90', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef488c70-0339-56be-a01e-ee095e66aa90'}, {'abstract': 'A federal court monitor is allowing the home visits, intended to urge Fire Department applicants to pursue the jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/black-firefighters-are-permitted-door-to-door-outreach/', 'snippet': 'A federal court monitor is allowing the home visits, intended to urge Fire Department applicants to pursue the jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal court monitor charged with diversifying the city’s Fire Department is allowing black firefighters to go door to door to persuade black applicants to join the department, over objections from city lawyers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Firefighters Are Permitted Door-to-Door Outreach', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Mark S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vulcan Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58bf186-9384-5a72-b618-72f8de595709', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58bf186-9384-5a72-b618-72f8de595709'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Williams, the football coach at Yale, resigned Wednesday after questions were raised about the integrity of his résumé and biography.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/yale-football-coach-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Tom Williams, the football coach at Yale, resigned Wednesday after questions were raised about the integrity of his résumé and biography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a couple of weeks in November, the story captivated even the casual college football follower, perhaps because it did not concern allegations of child sexual abuse or recruiting violations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yale Coach Resigns After Rhodes Scholarship Claim', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhodes Scholarship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witt, Patrick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Haven Register', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rhodes Scholarship Trust', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9aa4293-1eff-575f-ab4b-b3ce7892b9dc', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9aa4293-1eff-575f-ab4b-b3ce7892b9dc'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of noteworthy apps for the iPhone were introduced this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/technology/personaltech/some-new-little-treasures-for-the-iphone.html', 'snippet': 'A handful of noteworthy apps for the iPhone were introduced this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For iPhone owners, 2011 brought a flood of new apps, but in many cases they struggled to outshine last year’s best. So rather than present a top 10 list that includes names from 2010, I’m including only apps that had their debuts this year. If you really want to turbocharge your device, combine these with last year’s picks. (Note that this list doesn’t include games, which will be the subject of a separate post on the Gadgetwise blog.) Like last year’s list, this one includes many free picks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-SMART1/22-SMART1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-SMART1/22-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-SMART1/22-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Best iPhone Apps of 2011', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some New Little Treasures for the iPhone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20c4c955-70d6-5d4a-8032-bc204a2eeec4', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20c4c955-70d6-5d4a-8032-bc204a2eeec4'}, {'abstract': 'The vehicles, with preauction estimates in excess of $2.5 million, are among the most highly sought-after midcentury sports cars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/ferrari-250-gt-spider-and-mercedes-benz-gullwing-among-highlights-at-gooding-sale-in-scottsdale/', 'snippet': 'The vehicles, with preauction estimates in excess of $2.5 million, are among the most highly sought-after midcentury sports cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as movie studios often release their most tantalizing Oscar bait in the waning days before the nomination deadline, auction companies withhold some of their choicest consignments until close to the gavel date.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ferrari 250 GT Spider and Mercedes-Benz Gullwing Among Highlights at Gooding Sale in Scottsdale', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scottsdale (Ariz)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Sass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9de7783-8713-504c-b29e-44d69cbb87d5', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9de7783-8713-504c-b29e-44d69cbb87d5'}, {'abstract': 'The members of the sci-i metal band GWAR review “War Horse,” and it’s a split verdict.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/the-ebert-and-roeper-of-sci-fi-arch-metal-bands/', 'snippet': 'The members of the sci-i metal band GWAR review “War Horse,” and it’s a split verdict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the same site that gave you an old-school rapper’s take on “Black Swan” (favorite movie of the year, in a year where he didn’t see any other movies) comes “Rocker Reviews.” The Bagger’s pals at NextMovie have asked the members of GWAR, the costumed, sci-fi arch metal band, for their take on one of this year’s Oscar hopefuls, “War Horse.” You might think that a group that favors rampant violence and imposing visuals might identify with the movie, but they’re split, Ebert and Roeper style:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ebert and Roeper of Sci-Fi Arch Metal Bands', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f998eef9-72b2-5ea1-b9c2-c02f870a9e90', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f998eef9-72b2-5ea1-b9c2-c02f870a9e90'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Klugman will play the role of Juror 9 in a new production at the George Street Playhouse.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/jack-klugman-after-half-a-century-returning-to-twelve-angry-men/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Klugman will play the role of Juror 9 in a new production at the George Street Playhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirteen years before he became famous as one of television’s great slobs, Oscar Madison on “The Odd Couple,” Jack Klugman had his breakout role in the 1957 film  “12 Angry Men” as Juror 5. He played a hardened young man who brought street smarts to the jury deliberations in a murder trial in a cast that also included Henry Fonda (as the main character Juror 8), Lee J. Cobb, and Martin Balsam. Mr. Klugman is now the only surviving actor who was on the jury – a detail much on his mind Wednesday as he spoke about his latest career move. George Street Playhouse in New Brunswick, N.J., announced that Mr. Klugman – who is 89 – will play Juror 9 in a production of the stage adaption “Twelve Angry Men” there March 13-April 8, 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jack Klugman, After Half a Century, Returning to ‘Twelve Angry Men’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klugman, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'George Street Playhouse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be23d1b6-d712-5419-a945-a0185e1f6aec', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be23d1b6-d712-5419-a945-a0185e1f6aec'}, {'abstract': 'All is never fair under our Christmas tree. Do you have a child who counts gifts and tallies price tags, and how do you cope?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/striving-for-gift-parity-for-siblings/', 'snippet': 'All is never fair under our Christmas tree. Do you have a child who counts gifts and tallies price tags, and how do you cope?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How’s the pressing issue of “gift parity” going at your house? A friend just asked me how worried I am about keeping things equal under the tree. She’s caught herself buying “filler” gifts just to keep things close to equal, and she doesn’t like it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Striving for ‘Gift Parity’ for Siblings', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:47:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d560ee-0506-5cf7-bf7b-88d4bc3fe007', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d560ee-0506-5cf7-bf7b-88d4bc3fe007'}, {'abstract': 'And that’s a very good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/olivier-blanchard-isnt-very-serious/', 'snippet': 'And that’s a very good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And when you bear in mind that the Very Serious People have been wrong about everything, that’s a very good thing. What’s even better is that as the chief economist at the IMF, he’s helping make at least one international institution less austerity-mad than the others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olivier Blanchard Isn’t Very Serious', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0d8c7f3-d690-5e71-844e-9e8896693366', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0d8c7f3-d690-5e71-844e-9e8896693366'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Czech Republic, Philippines, North Korea and Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/pictures-of-the-day-czech-republic-and-elsewhere/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Czech Republic, Philippines, North Korea and Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Czech Republic, the Philippines, North Korea and Russia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Czech Republic and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e50e3a9e-a329-52e2-98b0-cadc27f9609c', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e50e3a9e-a329-52e2-98b0-cadc27f9609c'}, {'abstract': 'The Piers Morgan who came in for scrutiny in the Leveson inquiry on press ethics in Britain has very little to do with the Piers Morgan of today.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/piers-morgan-dodges-bullets-from-a-great-distance/', 'snippet': 'The Piers Morgan who came in for scrutiny in the Leveson inquiry on press ethics in Britain has very little to do with the Piers Morgan of today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an article on Wednesday, The Guardian suggested that CNN now has a damaged asset in Piers Morgan, the host of one of its most important hours. Mr. Morgan was struck by his own hand, and history, in his testimony on Tuesday before the Leveson inquiry on press ethics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Piers Morgan Dodges Bullets From a Great Distance', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mills, Heather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Piers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/170ee1df-5081-51d5-ba44-6c934502bd73', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/170ee1df-5081-51d5-ba44-6c934502bd73'}, {'abstract': 'After Barack Obama sort of compared himself to Johnson, F.D.R. and Lincoln, the right wing pounced.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/who-is-the-fourth-best-president-who-cares/', 'snippet': 'After Barack Obama sort of compared himself to Johnson, F.D.R. and Lincoln, the right wing pounced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opinion mongers on the right have been joyfully mocking President Obama for declaring that he was the fourth best president in history during a 60 Minutes interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Is the Fourth Best President? Who Cares?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T21:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlen