seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T22:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4da2801-3bc4-5b00-812d-adeb90ad3cd2', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4da2801-3bc4-5b00-812d-adeb90ad3cd2'}, {'abstract': 'Musica Sacra and the Trinity Choir and Trinity Baroque Orchestra offered two of the many presentations of “Messiah” over the last few weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/arts/music/trinity-wall-street-and-musica-sacra-in-messiah-review.html', 'snippet': 'Musica Sacra and the Trinity Choir and Trinity Baroque Orchestra offered two of the many presentations of “Messiah” over the last few weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To gaze over the classical-music landscape in the final weeks of December is to take in what can seem like an endless, unvarying forest of Handel’s 1742 oratorio “Messiah.” But if you look a little closer, it is a forest made up of many different kinds of trees.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/messiah/messiah-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/messiah/messiah-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/messiah/messiah-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/messiah/messiah-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/messiah/messiah-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Varieties of ‘Messiah’: Smooth and Mild or Piercing With Male Altos', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Varieties of ‘Messiah’: Smooth and Mild or Piercing With Male Altos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Baroque Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Musica Sacra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T22:43:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/53f634f9-7505-58b5-902d-2f76763fbca8', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53f634f9-7505-58b5-902d-2f76763fbca8'}, {'abstract': 'The generic earbuds that came with your phone are doing your music a disservice. It’s time to educate your ears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/technology/personaltech/do-some-research-to-improve-the-music-to-your-ears.html', 'snippet': 'The generic earbuds that came with your phone are doing your music a disservice. It’s time to educate your ears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dollar for dollar, headphones are the best way to listen to music. They pack more sonic wallop than even the most face-meltingly amazing loudspeaker system, and they do it for a lot less money. Think about it: a truly magnificent home-speaker system can cost well into the tens of thousands of dollars. A screaming set of headphones? A few hundred bucks, tops — and those in the Really Quite Good category can cost less than $100.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-BASICS1/22-BASICS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-BASICS1/22-BASICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22-BASICS1/22-BASICS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Ways to Wire Your Ears for Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Ways to Wire Your Ears for Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headphones and Headsets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T22:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati