'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/arts/music/hubble-and-diamond-terrifier-at-zebulon-review.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Greenberg and Sam Hillmer, band mates in Zs, took their solo projects to the stage on Tuesday night at Zebulon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Greenberg plays guitar in the Brooklyn band Zs, but he is also the monocrat of Hubble, a project of one. He performed a short set at Zebulon in Brooklyn’s Williamsburg neighborhood on Tuesday; so did Diamond Terrifier, alias the saxophonist Sam Hillmer, also from Zs. Individually, they’re working on related forms of minimalism, an old idea, but they’re post-genre people, interested in the dirty magic of warping and transforming sounds and languages you might already know.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/hubb-1/hubb-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/hubb-1/hubb-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/arts/hubb-1/hubb-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guitar and Sax, Each in Exploration', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guitar and Sax, Each in Exploration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T22:48:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 're