n': 'Hacked Chamber of Commerce Opposed Cybersecurity Law', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chamber of Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee4bbec4-4edf-56d1-ac07-15d8e1d582b4', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee4bbec4-4edf-56d1-ac07-15d8e1d582b4'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich says he has gathered more than the required 10,000 signatures to qualify for the Virginia ballot.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/gingrich-says-hell-make-virginia-ballot/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich says he has gathered more than the required 10,000 signatures to qualify for the Virginia ballot.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:46 p.m. | Updated  Newt Gingrich’s mad dash to get on the ballot in Virginia, seen as a test of his ability to go the distance, seems to have paid off, as Mr. Gingrich said Wednesday that his campaign had gathered more than enough signatures to qualify.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Says He’ll Make Virginia Ballot', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad3451e9-8a15-5ae2-b1db-b3997d13d596', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad3451e9-8a15-5ae2-b1db-b3997d13d596'}, {'abstract': 'AZ goalkeeper Esteban Alvarado avoided an apparent attack by a drunken fan in Amsterdam Wednesday, kicked the man into submission and was shown a red card by the referee before his teammates left the field in protest.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/in-the-netherlands-goalkeeper-gone-wild/', 'snippet': 'AZ goalkeeper Esteban Alvarado avoided an apparent attack by a drunken fan in Amsterdam Wednesday, kicked the man into submission and was shown a red card by the referee before his teammates left the field in protest.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:52 a.m. | Updated  A court in Amsterdam on Thursday sentenced the man who ran onto the field and attacked the AZ goalkeeper Esteban Alvarado to six months in jail, The Associated Press reported. Because of privacy laws in the Netherlands, the attacker was identified only as Wesley van W. (kind of catchy, don’t you think?). Prosecutors had been seeking a 10-month jail term. Under terms of the deal van W., 19, will also be required to report to the police during all Ajax, AZ and Dutch national team games for two years. The match, which was suspended when AZ players were instructed to leave the field, will be replayed in full next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Netherlands, Goalkeeper Gone Wild', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ajax (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b419763e-8506-5cf8-880e-04f4ef2261b9', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b419763e-8506-5cf8-880e-04f4ef2261b9'}, {'abstract': 'Damon Winter’s portraits of mental illness patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/21/blogs/20111221-winter.html', 'snippet': 'Damon Winter’s portraits of mental illness patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Damon Winter’s portraits of mental illness patients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/blogs/20111221-witner-slide-LLZ0/20111221-witner-slide-LLZ0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Portraits of Mental Illness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/