': 'nyt://article/86101448-d211-5311-bb58-3bbf562c6fb7'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican candidates (and their spouses) wish us a merry Christmas.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/campaign-wives-campaign-spots/', 'snippet': 'The Republican candidates (and their spouses) wish us a merry Christmas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iowa caucuses are fast approaching, and candidates for the Republican nomination are rushing to put their wives in front of the cameras. Maybe it dawned on the candidates that Americans are getting pretty tired of hearing from them directly. Or maybe, like all presidential aspirants, they have boundary issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaign Wives, Campaign Spots', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Calista', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427f3400-0639-563b-b7ee-fb2ea76b331b', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427f3400-0639-563b-b7ee-fb2ea76b331b'}, {'abstract': 'The Slap Shot contributor Christopher Botta talks New York area hockey with Scott Burnside of ESPN.com and Dave Starman of CBS Sports in the SNY.tv Metro Hockey Podcast.', 'web_url': 'https://slapsho