f they’re able to find any at all.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN/22JPMISTLETOE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN/22MISTLETOE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistletoe Gets the Kiss-Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mistletoe Gets the Kiss-Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mistletoe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:54:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fde91ef1-e317-5fcd-ae38-d5e90b349e89', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fde91ef1-e317-5fcd-ae38-d5e90b349e89'}, {'abstract': 'As they prepare to play the Jets on Saturday, the Giants are having to deal with a raft of injuries to their already thin corps of tight ends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/sports/football/hobbled-tight-ends-put-giants-in-a-bind.html', 'snippet': 'As they prepare to play the Jets on Saturday, the Giants are having to deal with a raft of injuries to their already thin corps of tight ends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The Giants have faced plenty of obstacles in their quest to reach the playoffs. They have lost games they probably should have won. They have been unable to stop talented receivers. They have showed signs of locker-room strife.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hobbled Tight Ends Put the Giants in a Bind Against the Jets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hobbled Tight Ends Put the Giants in a Bind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballard, Jake', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pascoe, Bear', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:55:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4efa137-0cc6-57ee-a213-c314f1cbb764', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4efa137-0cc6-57ee-a213-c314f1cbb764'}, {'abstract': 'A Parisian designer’s new So faucet for the French company THG suspends the words “chaud” and “froid” inside glass cubes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/garden/faucet-handles-in-french.html', 'snippet': 'A Parisian designer’s new So faucet for the French company THG suspends the words “chaud” and “froid” inside glass cubes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although bathroom faucets traditionally identify hot and cold with markings on the handle caps, Olivier Gossart, a Parisian designer, is trying something different. His new So faucet for the French company THG suspends the words “chaud” and “froid” inside glass cubes. “My idea was to have something like water, a transparent material that is very delicate,” he said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22BATH_SPAN/22CURR5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22BATH_SPAN/22CURR