animals taxidermy style.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22QNA4/22QNA4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 815, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22QNA4/22QNA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22QNA4/22QNA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Legos for Grown-Ups, From a Child at Heart', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toys for Grownups, From a Child at Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lego Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e814592-9e33-584f-b868-e057fb3d2f45', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e814592-9e33-584f-b868-e057fb3d2f45'}, {'abstract': 'The newly opened Public Chicago, a hotel in what had been the Ambassador East, has a back-to-basics theme.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/garden/ian-schrager-streamlines-a-chicago-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'The newly opened Public Chicago, a hotel in what had been the Ambassador East, has a back-to-basics theme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Ian Schrager, “sticking to the basics” was his goal in designing Public Chicago, a hotel that opened this fall in what had been the Ambassador East, built in 1926. Working with designers headed by Anda Andrei, Mr. Schrager, a partner in the hotel, created a look that is “very, very neutral, very low-key, no flash, no design on steroids,” he said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22ROOMS1_SPAN/22CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22ROOMS1_SPAN/22CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22ROOMS1_SPAN/22CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22ROOMS1_SPAN/22CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22ROOMS1_SPAN/22CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Schrager Streamlines a Chicago Hotel', 'kicker': 'Currents | Rooms', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Schrager Streamlines a Chicago Hotel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schrager, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-21T23:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abb44a27-0eeb-5724-a31c-86da3ffd080a', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abb44a27-0eeb-5724-a31c-86da3ffd080a'}, {'abstract': 'Chair skis are a nifty invention that turn regular dining or side chairs into rocking chairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/garden/skis-turn-a-regular-chair-into-a-rocker.html', 'snippet': 'Chair skis are a nifty invention that turn regular dining or side chairs into rocking chairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chair skis are a nifty invention that turn regular dining or side chairs into rocking chairs. Simply place the legs of the chair into the groove of the beechwood skis, which are about 1 1/8 inches wide by 21 inches long and fit most standard nonupholstered chairs. Flexible rubber stoppers at each end hold the legs in place.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22FURNITURE/22FURNITURE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22FURNITURE/22CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/garden/22FURNITURE/22CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skis Convert Chairs Into Rockers', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Note: Don’t Take This Chair to Vail', 'name': None, 'seo