, 'snippet': 'The New York attorney general is investigating whether the nonprofit arm of Pearson Education acted improperly to influence state education officials by paying for perks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State’s attorney general is investigating whether the Pearson Foundation, the nonprofit arm of one of the nation’s largest educational publishers, acted improperly to influence state education officials by paying for overseas trips and other perks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Testing Firm Faces Inquiry on Free Trips for Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Testing Firm Faces Inquiry On Free Trips For Officials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steiner, David M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearson PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T00:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0dfe806-db8f-55ab-bf64-29d65700757e', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0dfe806-db8f-55ab-bf64-29d65700757e'}, {'abstract': 'A representative of the government responds to a Sunday Review photo essay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes