://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/signs-point-to-economys-rise-but-experts-see-a-false-dawn.html', 'snippet': 'In recent weeks, a broad range of data have beaten analysts’ expectations, but forecasters say the uptick is likely temporary and that growth will slow in the first half of 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As the fourth quarter draws to a close, a spate of unexpectedly good economic data suggests that it will have some of the fastest and strongest economic growth since the recovery started in 2009, causing a surge in the stock market and cheering economists, investors and policy makers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22growth_395_inline/22growth_395_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22growth_395_inline/22growth_395_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/business/22growth_395_inline/22growth_395_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs Point to Economy’s Rise, but Experts See a False Dawn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Signs Point to Economy’s Rise, But Experts See a False Dawn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T02:33:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2f4c55c-3f24-5b76-843d-c62c8d5f2843', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2f4c55c-3f24-5b76-843d-c62c8d5f2843'}, {'abstract': 'Because of renovations at their usual home, the Yellow Jackets’ men’s basketball schedule consists of 5 games in the Atlanta suburbs and 10 at Philips Arena in the city center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/sports/ncaabasketball/for-georgia-tech-team-home-games-have-distant-feel.html', 'snippet': 'Because of renovations at their usual home, the Yellow Jackets’ men’s basketball schedule consists of 5 games in the Atlanta suburbs and 10 at Philips Arena in the city center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Georgia Tech’s Jason Morris was driving on Interstate 85 on the outskirts of this city before the basketball season started when he passed the Gwinnett Center. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GATECH/GATECH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GATECH/GATECH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/GATECH/GATECH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 535, 'width': 1024,