1158042/rags-to-riches.html', 'snippet': 'The Times accompanies Indian entrepreneur Ashok Khade as he revisits his native village, where he was of the lowest caste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times accompanies Indian entrepreneur Ashok Khade as he revisits his native village, where he was of the lowest caste.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/07/world/video-dalit/video-dalit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/07/world/video-dalit/video-dalit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/07/world/video-dalit/video-dalit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/07/world/video-dalit/video-dalit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rags to Riches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T02:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'Sonia Narang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Narang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4e91aa2a-cb28-5972-8466-389f9197ade5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4e91aa2a-cb28-5972-8466-389f9197ade5'}, {'abstract': 'India’s era of economic growth has created something unthinkable a generation ago: business opportunities for members of India’s untouchable caste, the Dalits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/asia/indias-boom-creates-openings-for-untouchables.html', 'snippet': 'India’s era of economic growth has created something unthinkable a generation ago: business opportunities for members of India’s untouchable caste, the Dalits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PED, India — On his barefoot trudge to school decades ago, a young Ashok Khade passed inescapable reminders of what he was: the well from which he was not allowed to drink; the temple where he was not permitted to worship. At school, he took his place on the floor in a part of the classroom built a step lower than the rest. Untouchables like him, considered to be spiritually and physically unclean, could not be permitted to pollute their upper-caste neighbors and classmates. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/dalit/dalit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/dalit/dalit-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/dalit/dalit-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/dalit/dalit-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/world/asia/dalit/dalit-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scaling Caste Walls With Capitalism’s Ladders in India', 'kicker': "India's Way", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scaling Caste Walls With Capitalism’s Ladders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T02:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e5fd1f-10a9-51b5-97f0-3ce7d93a09a7', 'word_count': 2413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e5fd1f-10a9-51b5-97f0-3ce7d93a09a7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Goldman, a physicist, persuaded Xerox to build a research center in Palo Alto, Calif., where significant computing technologies were invented.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/business/jacob-e-goldman-founder-of-xerox-lab-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Goldman, a physicist, persuaded Xerox to build a research center in Palo Alto, Calif., where significant computing technologies were invented.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacob E. Goldman, a physicist who as Xerox’s chief scientist founded the company’s vaunted Palo Alto Research Center, which invented the modern personal computer, died on Tuesday in Westport, Conn. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/business/GOLDMAN-obit/GOLDMAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/business/GOLDMAN-obit/GOLDMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/business/GOLDMAN-obit/GOLDMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jacob Goldman, Founder of Xerox Lab, Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jacob Goldman, a Father Of Computing, Dies at 90', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Jacob E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palo Alto (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xerox Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T02:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f807b88-0ee3-5a4d-b601-a69f29420987', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f807b88-0ee3-5a4d-b601-a69f29420987'}, {'abstract': 'Kristian House shifts our perception of things.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/pollentia/', 'snippet': 'Kristian House shifts our perception of things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — See that title up there? Yeah, I couldn’t answer it, either. I think I can say without reservation that this is my least favorite type of clue. Not only is it a Roman numeral (CDII, in case you were wondering), which are never great entries in my humble opinion, but it’s a Roman numeral indicating a battle that I think is somewhat obscure unless you happen to be a Visigoth. On the other hand, it apparently has its own Facebook page, so who am I to argue?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: Year of the Battle of Pollentia', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T03:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a06bfad-634a-5116-a876-add6058a75d9', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a06bfad-634a-5116-a876-add6058a75d9'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich responds to Mitt Romney’s comment that Mr. Gingrich “can’t take the heat” and should stop complaining about negative advertising.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/gingrich-throws-down-a-debate-challenge-to-romney/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich responds to Mitt Romney’s comment that Mr. Gingrich “can’t take the heat” and should stop complaining about negative advertising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Va. — Newt Gingrich threw down a “debate me in Iowa’’ challenge to his chief Republican rival, Mitt Romney, on Wednesday night, hours after Mr. Romney said in a television interview that Mr. Gingrich should stop complaining about negative advertising.“I’ve challenged Governor Romney to meet me for 90 minutes in Iowa next week, anywhere, anytime, timekeeper, no moderator,’’ Mr. Gingrich told supporters during a quick pep talk at a Marriott Hotel here.He went on: “And we’ll bring all of his negative ads and show them for free and he can explain them, and we’ll find out tomorrow whether he likes the heat and wants to come in the kitchen, or whether he is just another normal national politician with clever consultants and a lot of money and no willingness to stand up and tell the truth.’’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Throws Down a Debate Challenge to Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T03:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8d23d75-a2c7-59b5-b6df-e7b96ac0ffb5', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8d23d75-a2c7-59b5-b6df-e7b96ac0ffb5'}, {'abstract': 'Mayors around the country are asking, Why has Washington cut one of the main federal programs for cities by a quarter in the last couple of years?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/21/us/GRANTS.html', 'snippet': 'Mayors around the country are asking, Why has Washington cut one of the main federal programs for cities by a quarter in the last couple of years?', 'lead_paragraph'