7684c04', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc1c9e72-5261-569e-b8d9-92f1e7684c04'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling Fidesz party has used its two-thirds majority to redraw parliamentary districts in its favor and pack the constitutional court with supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/europe/foes-of-hungarys-government-fear-demolition-of-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling Fidesz party has used its two-thirds majority to redraw parliamentary districts in its favor and pack the constitutional court with supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST — In less than two years as a member of the Hungarian Parliament, Timea Szabo says she has looked on helplessly as the ruling Fidesz Party has used its two-thirds majority to tighten its grip on the news media and the courts, redraw parliamentary districts in its favor and pack the constitutional court with supporters. On Jan. 1, a new “majoritarian” Constitution written and ratified by Fidesz takes hold.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/jp-hungary-1/jp-hungary-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Foes of Hungary’s Government Fear ‘Demolition of Democracy’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foes of Hungary’s Government Fear ‘Demolition of Democracy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fidesz Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gyurcsany, Ferenc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocatio