'‘X Factor’ Watch: It’s Still a Toss-Up', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T04:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7e2a288-f566-5273-9098-666c06cdaee8', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7e2a288-f566-5273-9098-666c06cdaee8'}, {'abstract': 'The American linguist Noam Chomsky, a prominent source of intellectual inspiration for President Hugo Chávez, made a new appeal on Wednesday for the release of María Lourdes Afiuni.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/americas/venezuela-another-plea-to-free-a-judge.html', 'snippet': 'The American linguist Noam Chomsky, a prominent source of intellectual inspiration for President Hugo Chávez, made a new appeal on Wednesday for the release of María Lourdes Afiuni.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American linguist Noam Chomsky, a prominent source of intellectual inspiration for President Hugo Chávez, made a new appeal on Wednesday for the release of María Lourdes Afiuni, a judge arrested two years ago by the secret intelligence police. The detention of Judge Afiuni, who was given two additional years of house arrest in December, has raised concern over the erosion of judicial independence in Venezuela. In July, Mr. Chomsky requested clemency for Judge Afiuni, who was arrested after she released a Venezuelan businessman from detention. The new appeal, made in a public letter to Mr. Chávez, detailed the death threats and other abuses suffered by Judge Afiuni during more than a year in a women’s prison, and her inability now to leave her home. “After more than two years in custody, there are no guarantees of a fair trial,” Mr. Chomsky wrote. “I am convinced that Judge Afiuni has suffered enough.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Another Plea to Free a Judge', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Another Plea to Free a Judge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chomsky, Noam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afiuni, Maria Lourdes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T04:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d78e6e8-5253-5584-b349-e24f2e23e81b', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d78e6e8-5253-5584-b349-e24f2e23e81b'}, {'abstract': 'In an unusual response to criticism from European nations on the Security Council, the Israel bluntly accused the countries of “interfering with Israel’s domestic affairs.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/world/middleeast/israel-says-4-european-countries-are-meddling-in-its-affairs.html', 'snippet': 'In an unusual response to criticism from European nations on the Security Council, the Israel bluntly accused the countries of “interfering with Israel’s domestic affairs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — In 