 protesters appears to have ended after five days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The death toll from the weekend’s clashes between the military police and protesters demanding the end of military rule rose to 15 on Wednesday, but the five days of street fighting appeared for the moment to come to an end.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cairo Clashes Seem to End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cairo Clashes Seem to End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T04:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0b4aa06-7e09-52db-93af-8354b300f938', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0b4aa06-7e09-52db-93af-8354b300f938'}, {'abstract': 'For all the lectures about winning and principles, many Giants fans fail to support their own coach.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/21/bleeding-green-giants-fans-owe-coach-a-break/', 'snippet': 'For all the lectures about winning and principles, many Giants fans fail to support their own coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Bassett is the founder of SNY’s The Jets Blog. You can follow him on Twitter at @Brian_Bassett. He and Ed Valentine of Big Blue View will be writing about the Jets and the Giants in the days leading up to the Giants-Jets game on Saturday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bleeding Green: Giants Fans Owe Coach a Break', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T04:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Bassett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bassett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eda031b-4b7c-5ba6-82a0-acb41d3f167f', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eda031b-4b7c-5ba6-82a0-acb41d3f167f'}, {'abstract': 'At Vanderbilt Medical School, students take an active role planning activities like fun runs and cooking competitions — as student colleges, modeled on Harry Potter, compete.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/a-medical-school-more-like-hogwarts/', 'snippet': 'At Vanderbilt Medical School, students take an active role planning activities like fun runs and cooking competitions — as student colleges, modeled on Harry Potter, compete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been clear for several years now that while aspiring doctors may start medical school as happy and as healthy as their non-doctoring peers, four years later they aren’t. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Medical School More Like Hogwarts', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T05:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a3c5c4a-4c7b-531e-9a7d-38e633ec7428', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a3c5c4a-4c7b-531e-9a7d-38e633ec7428'}, {'abstract': 'In this holiday season, the M.L.S. online store offers fans and collectors some interesting, shall we say, gift items.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/yuleblog-goals-m-l-s-gift-guide/', 'snippet': 'In this holiday season, the M.L.S. online store offers fans and collectors some interesting, shall we say, gift items.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children may be the gift that keep on taking, but when it comes to the season of giving, there is nothing quite like a dreaded trip to the mall — though these days the Internet has evolved into an electronic mall beyond compare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'YuleBlog: Goal’s M.L.S. Gift Guide', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T05:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6a97607-1103-52a0-8b02-018a08004e18', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6a97607-1103-52a0-8b02-018a08004e18'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of nurses plan to hold a one-day strike on Thursday over contract disputes between the California nurses’ union and two health care organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/health/california-nurses-plan-one-day-strike-over-contracts.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of nurses plan to hold a one-day strike on Thursday over contract disputes between the California nurses’ union and two health care organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Thousands of nurses plan to hold a one-day strike on Thursday over contract disputes between the California nurses’ union and two health care organizations. About 4,000 nurses employed by Sutter Health, based in the San Francisco area, will walk off the job at eight hospitals unless a deal is reached. Around 2,000 nurses from a Long Beach hospital system also plan to strike. More than 23,000 California nurses staged a one-day strike in September. The nurses were locked out at Sutter hospitals after the strike, and one patient died when a replacement nurse administered an incorrect dosage of medicine. Sutter plans to bring in replacement nurses on Thursday and Friday. A Sutter spokeswoman said care would not be compromised. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Nurses Plan One-Day Strike Over Contracts', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Nurses Plan One-Day Strike Over Contracts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sutter Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T05:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d8095f1-2f56-5bcd-91e8-0f0fec822779', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d8095f1-2f56-5bcd-91e8-0f0fec822779'}, {'abstract': 'What do Giants fans think of Jets coach Rex Ryan? A little bit of everything.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/dyed-in-blue-giants-fans-weigh-in-on-ryan/', 'snippet': 'What do Giants fans think of Jets coach Rex Ryan? A little bit of everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Valentine is the editor of Big Blue View, a Giants blog. He and Brian Bassett of The Jets blog will write in the days leading up to the Giants-Jets game on Saturday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dyed in Blue: Giants Fans Weigh In on Ryan', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank