 on Thursday, six weeks after Occupy protesters set up tents there. Citing security, the university closed the yard to everyone but students and employees after an encampment went up there in early November. The protesters removed most of their tents this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Harvard Yard Reopening After Protest', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Harvard Yard Reopening After Protest ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T05:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fd16a74-a8c5-5dfe-ad50-13b3235fc44b', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fd16a74-a8c5-5dfe-ad50-13b3235fc44b'}, {'abstract': 'Make Us Great Again, the deep-pocketed independent political action group supporting Gov. Rick Perry of Texas, is on the air in South Carolina and Iowa with an ad highly critical of Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/ad-watch-attacking-rivals-in-black-and-white/', 'snippet': 'Make Us Great Again, the deep-pocketed independent political action group supporting Gov. Rick Perry of Texas, is on the air in South Carolina and Iowa with an ad highly critical of Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Make Us Great Again, the deep-pocketed independent political action group supporting Gov. Rick Perry of Texas, is on the air in South Carolina and Iowa with an ad highly critical of Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ad Watch: Attacking Rivals, in Black and White', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Make Us Great Again', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T05:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0a99a21-7ee4-5b91-8ca1-d091295e6128', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0a99a21-7ee4-5b91-8ca1-d091295e6128'}, {'abstract': 'Books about the power of narrative to change the relationship between people and animals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/books/review/bears-dolphins-and-the-animal-stories-we-tell.html', 'snippet': 'Books about the power of narrative to change the relationship between people and animals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Peter Singer’s “Animal Liberation” laid the groundwork for modern animal advocacy more than 35 years ago, it has been a central tenet of the movement that we go ethically astray when we let emotional proximity to humans and a handful of nonhuman species trump the obvious interests of other animals. Although animal rights proponents haven’t always embraced Singer’s brand of utilitarianism, they have generally followed his rejection of emotionalism, reserving particular scorn for the sentimentality that allows people to lavish money and attention on pets while happily eating cows and pigs — mammals every bit as intelligent and capable of suffering as dogs and cats — which lead tortured existences before arriving on our plates.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/books/review/Beha/Beha-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/books/review/Beha/Beha-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/books/review/Beha/Beha-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/books/review/Beha/Beha-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/books/review/Beha/Beha-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bears, Dolphins and the Animal Stories We Tell', 'kicker': 'Nonfiction Chronicle', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Animal Attraction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pastoureau, Michel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diski, Jenny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudy, Kathy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 