 'uri': 'nyt://article/42b5d690-96e5-5587-a905-53f5e35abf35'}, {'abstract': 'Can you identify the sentence that correctly uses punctuation including commas and quotation marks?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/test-yourself-english-dec-22-2011/', 'snippet': 'Can you identify the sentence that correctly uses punctuation including commas and quotation marks?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “Not Without My Pet.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Dec. 22, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T09:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8101a88a-faf0-5661-b732-a9a2c48e6a85', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8101a88a-faf0-5661-b732-a9a2c48e6a85'}, {'abstract': 'The Internet should no longer reflect a 1950s view of the world, with America making the rules, the Minister says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/a-conversation-with-sachin-pilot/', 'snippet': 'The Internet should no longer reflect a 1950s view of the world, with America making the rules, the Minister says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent months the Indian government held meetings with Internet intermediaries like Facebook and Google, and asked them to prescreen user content and remove things that might be incendiary or objectionable, inspiring an outpouring of complaint and a rebuff from these companies. On Dec. 15, the government appeared to step down from that position, telling these companies in a meeting that there would be no censorship of Internet content. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': 