material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b508b86f-6fd3-5ca2-9d07-1e3480cbbf16', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b508b86f-6fd3-5ca2-9d07-1e3480cbbf16'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/the-early-word-benefits/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s TimesPresident Obama has benefited politically from the fight between House and Senate Republicans over how to work with Democrats and the White House to extend a payroll tax cut and jobless benefits, Jackie Calmes writes. But, she reports, whether the clash ultimately turns out to be a plus for Mr. Obama hinges on the economy’s performance. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Benefits', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2236e830-7663-520c-8338-bdfe1bfa183c', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2236e830-7663-520c-8338-bdfe1bfa183c'}, {'abstract': 'A student from Minnesota worries that the “me of today” isn’t qualified to make decisions for the “me of the future.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/rachel-yang/', 'snippet': 'A student from Minnesota worries that the “me of today” isn’t qualified to make decisions for the “me of the future.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'My best friend asked me last week, “Where are you even applying?” and I avoided her question.\xa0 Mostly because I just don’t want to talk about college.\xa0 These applications have been hanging over my head for months and I’m still not finished, still not done mulling over them.\xa0 Even with my best friend I don’t want to talk about it.\xa0 It makes me anxious to think about what I still have left to do before the Jan. 1 deadline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Kid Who Likes English Class’ Wonders What to Do About College', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Yang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cde04f2d-0ccf-5033-9ab9-a7169e2abd72', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cde04f2d-0ccf-5033-9ab9-a7169e2abd72'}, {'abstract': 'The project of a 31-year-old product designer in Brooklyn, a new watch company takes inspiration from the gauges of vintage Italian sports cars.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/autodromo-watches-from-brooklyn-keeping-time-in-italian/', 'snippet': 'The project of a 31-year-old product designer in Brooklyn, a new watch company takes inspiration from the gauges of vintage Italian sports cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, Bradley Price was driving his red 1983 Alfa Romeo GTV6 2.5 when inspiration struck.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Autodromo: Watches From Brooklyn, Keeping Time in Italian', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alfa Romeo Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard S. Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4efe3af2-e236-571c-b1e7-3a2d208a20e2', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4efe3af2-e236-571c-b1e7-3a2d208a20e2'}, {'abstract': 'Prague Thrift Store, opened a year ago in the trendy Vinohrady neighborhood, is crammed near to overflowing with quality secondhand goods.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/shop-delivers-deals-and-donations-in-prague/', 'snippet': 'Prague Thrift Store, opened a year ago in the trendy Vinohrady neighborhood, is crammed near to overflowing with quality secondhand goods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beer can already be found for less than a euro a half-liter in Prague, and many of the city’s attractions are free, but now it’s even easier to find a good deal here: the city has become home to a true thrift shop, where you can root out buried bargains as well as find a home for items cluttering your closet or suitcase.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shop Delivers Deals and Donations in Prague', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thrift Shops', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fiona Gaze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fiona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06200749-91cd-52be-8b21-66c71c257492', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06200749-91cd-52be-8b21-66c71c257492'}, {'abstract': 'A high school senior from Brooklyn, N.Y., sees the college search process as one akin to wedding dress shopping. She writes, “The college has to fit me, I don’t alter myself to fit the college.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/cassie-dagostino/', 'snippet': 'A high school senior from Brooklyn, N.Y., sees the college search process as one akin to wedding dress shopping. She writes, “The college has to fit me, I don’t alter myself to fit the college.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I sit at my desk with my right hand anxiously tapping in rhythm to my iTunes, my left hand twirling the baby hairs that stick out of my ponytail, and my leg shaking of restless leg syndrome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aspiring to Be First in the Family to Attend College, and Pay for It, Too', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cassandra Dagostino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cassandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dagostino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f48d53ef-4b80-54ed-a40a-db5c6671d1af', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f48d53ef-4b80-54ed-a40a-db5c6671d1af'}, {'abstract': 'India’s ambitions to help the poor secure government benefits by creating the world’s largest personal database could do them much harm.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/the-false-promise-of-biometrics-in-india/', 'snippet': 'India’s ambitions to help the poor secure government benefits by creating the world’s largest personal database could do them much harm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Earlier this month, just two days after my grandfather and I received a summons to register for India’s national unique identification (UID) program, a sweeping initiative launched with much fanfare, a parliamentary committee ordered a review of the project, effectively freezing it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The False Promise of Biometrics', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biometrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aman Sethi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sethi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/551854cf-3d78-54c1-bd31-d19fbb904e00', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/551854cf-3d78-54c1-bd31-d19fbb904e00'}, {'abstract': 'How you can tell what your current Internet connection speed is at home.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/qa-clocking-your-broadband-speed/', 'snippet': 'How you can tell what your current Internet connection speed is at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Clocking Your Broadband Speed', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8a82dfa-b405-5301-9b5a-bddf78c9ac57', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8a82dfa-b405-5301-9b5a-bddf78c9ac57'}, {'abstract': 'British Airways and the Spanish carrier Iberia beat out Virgin Atlantic Airways on Thursday in the bidding for British Midland International, the unprofitable airline being sold by Lufthansa of Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/international-airlines-outbids-virgin-atlantic-for-lufthansas-bmi/', 'snippet': 'British Airways and the Spanish carrier Iberia beat out Virgin Atlantic Airways on Thursday in the bidding for British Midland International, the unprofitable airline being sold by Lufthansa of Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — British Airways and the Spanish carrier Iberia beat out Virgin Atlantic on Thursday in the bidding for British Midland International, the unprofitable airline being sold by Lufthansa of Germany.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Airways’ Parent Wins Lufthansa’s BMI', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:18:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4133a3c-c976-58af-afdb-3dd7323fc736', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4133a3c-c976-58af-afdb-3dd7323fc736'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the tough economy and struggles for offline retailers, shoppers have spent $32 billion online this holiday season, an increase of 15 percent over last year. Though mobile shopping has contributed to online spending this year, shoppers are more likely to browse and research e-commerce sites from their cellphones and then turn to their tablets to make purchases, especially in the evening.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/how-people-shopped-online-this-holiday-season/', 'snippet': 'Despite the tough economy and struggles for offline retailers, shoppers have spent $32 billion online this holiday season, an increase of 15 percent over last year. Though mobile shopping has contributed to online spending this year, shoppers are ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Little time remains for online shoppers to have gifts delivered in time for Christmas, and sales numbers for online shopping this season are arriving. The trends are clear: shoppers spent much more money online this year than last year, and they did a lot of their shopping on tablets like the iPad. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/technology/21bits-ipad-shopping/21bits-ipad-shopping-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/21/technology/21bits-ipad-shopping/21bits-ipad-shopping-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/21/technology/21bits-ipad-shopping/21bits-ipad-shopping-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How People Shopped Online This Holiday Season', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4b6750-c196-5cc4-992e-a6f26b2825a6', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4b6750-c196-5cc4-992e-a6f26b2825a6'}, {'abstract': 'The changes sought by Dmitri A. Medvedev in his final state-of-the-nation address as president would begin to deconstruct Russia’s heavily centralized government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/world/europe/dmitri-medvedev-urges-reforms-for-russia-in-address.html', 'snippet': 'The changes sought by Dmitri A. Medvedev in his final state-of-the-nation address as president would begin to deconstruct Russia’s heavily centralized government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — It finally happened: President Dmitri A. Medvedev, the man who was supposed to embody the aspirations of young middle-class Russians, has outlined a concrete and substantive agenda for political change. In his last state of the nation speech before leaving office, Mr. Medvedev recommended returning to the direct election of governors, removing officials’ wives and children from the leadership of lucrative corporations, and creating a public television station protected from the Kremlin’s manipulation, among other changes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/europe/23russia-a/23russia-a-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/world/europe/23russia-a/23russia-a-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/europe/23russia-a/23russia-a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/europe/23russia-a/23russia-a-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/world/europe/23russia-a/23russia-a-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Presidency’s 11th Hour, Medvedev Proposes Systemic Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Presidency’s 11th Hour, Medvedev Proposes Systemic Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T11:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry and Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc6011d-e8ad-5e34-9662-61c490ff10bf', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc6011d-e8ad-5e34-9662-61c490ff10bf'}, {'abstract': 'How much home-field advantage should we expect the Jets to have?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/week-16-n-f-l-game-probabilities-giants-vs-jets/', 'snippet': 'How much home-field advantage should we expect the Jets to have?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t too difficult to pick a game to highlight for New York Times readers this week. The Giants take on the Jets, with both teams \xa0in the thick of their playoff races. The path for the Giants goes through the N.F.C. East division championship, while the path for the Jets can lead only to the A.F.C.’s sixth-seed wild-card berth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 16 N.F.L. Game Probabilities: Giants vs. Jets', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T12:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62b4ed1b-bae4-5e77-b5a2-6c630a4bd913', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62b4ed1b-bae4-5e77-b5a2-6c630a4bd913'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last three years, Bari Jay’s average retail price has risen to more than $200, which seems to be the magic number for consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/a-dressmaker-tries-to-deliver-the-right-dress-at-the-right-price/', 'snippet': 'Over the last three years, Bari Jay’s average retail price has risen to more than $200, which seems to be the magic number for consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As she works to get a handle on pricing,\xa0Susan Parker, a member of our business group, weighs the competing interests of art and commerce. On the one hand, Ms. Parker, who owns the dressmaker Bari Jay, is thrilled with her creative designer and credits her with much of the company’s turnaround. The designer, Kristine Eikenbary, takes her inspiration from higher-end fashion. “Her designs are gorgeous,” said Ms. Parker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dressmaker Tries to Deliver the Right Dress at the Right Price', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T12:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/004b0d94-5a61-505d-98ef-899ebc18e483', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/004b0d94-5a61-505d-98ef-899ebc18e483'}, {'abstract': 'Maintaining what is arguably the most famous Christmas tree of all is a little more demanding than taking care of the one standing in your living room.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/christmas-tree-care-with-an-audience/', 'snippet': 'Maintaining what is arguably the most famous Christmas tree of all is a little more demanding than taking care of the one standing in your living room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the time of year when you hear all the stuff that you are supposed to do to maintain your Christmas tree after you win the nine-rounder to force it into place without poking a hole in the ceiling or electrocuting yourself when you string up the lights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christmas Tree Care, With an Audience', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockefeller Center (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T12:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28ea420-cf74-57d9-b214-d7b3883f3c18', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28ea420-cf74-57d9-b214-d7b3883f3c18'}, {'abstract': '“War Horse,” set in World War I and directed by Steven Spielberg, pays tribute to a tradition of honest, emotionally direct storytelling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/movies/war-horse-directed-by-steven-spielberg-review.html', 'snippet': '“War Horse,” set in World War I and directed by Steven Spielberg, pays tribute to a tradition of honest, emotionally direct storytelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no combat in the early scenes of “War Horse,” Steven Spielberg’s sweeping adaptation of the popular stage spectacle, but the film opens with a cinematic assault as audacious and unsparing as the Normandy landing in “Saving Private Ryan.” With widescreen, pastoral vistas dappled in golden sunlight and washed in music (by John Williams) that is somehow both grand and folksy, Mr. Spielberg lays siege to your cynicism, bombarding you with strong and simple appeals to feeling.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WARHORSE/23WARHORSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WARHORSE/23WARHORSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WARHORSE/23WARHORSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WARHORSE/23WARHORSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WARHORSE/23WARHORSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Innocence Is Trampled, but a Bond Endures', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'War Horse'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Innocence Is Trampled, But a Bond Endures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaminski, Janusz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mullan, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thewlis, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'War Horse (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/461d8f89-67e1-5801-86c0-f021377af922', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/461d8f89-67e1-5801-86c0-f021377af922'}, {'abstract': 'Two years after Merce Cunningham’s death, his dance company will give its final performance on New Year’s Eve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/arts/dance/merce-cunningham-dance-company-ends-its-legacy-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Two years after Merce Cunningham’s death, his dance company will give its final performance on New Year’s Eve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long before his 80th birthday in 1999 the choreographer Merce Cunningham went back to his hometown, Centralia, Wash., and spent some time with his brother Jack, a lawyer. After they talked about old acquaintances, Jack suddenly asked, “Merce, when are you going to make something the public likes?”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25CUNNINGHAM1_SPAN/25JPSUBCUNNINGHAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25CUNNINGHAM1_SPAN/25JPSUBCUNNINGHAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25CUNNINGHAM1_SPAN/25JPSUBCUNNINGHAM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25CUNNINGHAM1_SPAN/25JPSUBCUNNINGHAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25CUNNINGHAM1_SPAN/25JPSUBCUNNINGHAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard to Grasp, but Harder to Say Farewell', 'kicker': 'Arts & Leisure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard to Grasp, But Harder To Say Farewell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c556423e-f849-5788-bf7a-34b0c3713c62', 'word_count': 1771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c556423e-f849-5788-bf7a-34b0c3713c62'}, {'abstract': 'A series of explosions shook Baghdad early Thursday, killing at least 63 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/22/world/middleeast/20111223-IRAQ.html', 'snippet': 'A series of explosions shook Baghdad early Thursday, killing at least 63 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A series of explosions shook Baghdad early Thursday, killing at least 63 people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/middleeast/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/middleeast/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/world/middleeast/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D/20111223-IRAQ-slide-8P8D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coordinated Explosions Kill Dozens in Baghdad', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/93e743b0-8340-5df3-af0b-f50c31b98599', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/93e743b0-8340-5df3-af0b-f50c31b98599'}, {'abstract': 'According to an study of its clients by Concur, a company that runs an online expense management system for businesses, Dec. 20 is the busiest day of the year for filing for expenses. The rush is prompted by corporate policies on filing expenses before the new year, along with a surge in holiday entertainment for staff members and clients.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/rushing-to-get-your-expenses-done-join-the-club/', 'snippet': 'According to an study of its clients by Concur, a company that runs an online expense management system for businesses, Dec. 20 is the busiest day of the year for filing for expenses. The rush is prompted by corporate policies on filing expenses b...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, I was sitting down to file for some work-related expenses after receiving yet another e-mail reminder of the inferno that awaits employees who are delinquent on such things. Moments later, a different e-mail landed in my inbox — this one from Concur, a company that runs an online expense management system for businesses — telling me that Tuesday, Dec. 20, was expected to be the busiest day of the year for filing for expenses. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rushing to Get Your Expenses Done? Join the Club', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Expense Accounts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87847ed9-6089-5d26-b102-c45668a3257f', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87847ed9-6089-5d26-b102-c45668a3257f'}, {'abstract': 'About 50 adult fish along the Clark Fork River in Idaho and Montana are captured and transferred each year at an annual cost of $250,000 to undo fragmentation linked to the construction of hydroelectric dams.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/trucking-the-trout-to-their-native-streams/', 'snippet': 'About 50 adult fish along the Clark Fork River in Idaho and Montana are captured and transferred each year at an annual cost of $250,000 to undo fragmentation linked to the construction of hydroelectric dams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an innovative conservation effort, biologists on the Clark Fork River are using genetic testing to help get bull trout back to their natal streams to spawn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trucking Trout to Their Native Streams', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:06:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By DEBORAH WEISBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WEISBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc53a2a-bafe-5cba-80cb-39421e5b78b0', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc53a2a-bafe-5cba-80cb-39421e5b78b0'}, {'abstract': 'Michel Péretié, the head of Société Générale’s corporate and investment banking division, is leaving the French bank to pursue other opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/socgens-investment-banking-chief-steps-down/', 'snippet': 'Michel Péretié, the head of Société Générale’s corporate and investment banking division, is leaving the French bank to pursue other opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Michel Péretié, head of Société Générale’s corporate and investment banking division, is leaving the French bank to pursue other opportunities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Societe Generale’s Investment Banking Chief Steps Down', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peretie, Michel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bear Stearns Cos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Societe Generale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbaec5a6-98e4-5a9c-9c11-f8c80230d952', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbaec5a6-98e4-5a9c-9c11-f8c80230d952'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with Jimmy Fallon, Louis C. K. said that from the money he has made from his online comedy special “Live at the Beacon Theater,” he would give $250,000 in bonuses to people who work for him and $280,000 to five charity organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/online-sales-of-louis-c-k-special-cross-1-million-mark/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with Jimmy Fallon, Louis C. K. said that from the money he has made from his online comedy special “Live at the Beacon Theater,” he would give $250,000 in bonuses to people who work for him and $280,000 to five charity organization...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the comedian Louis C. K. may not seem like the kind of guy who derives much joy from the holiday season – let alone anything else – Santa Claus has brought him an early Christmas gift. In an interview on Wednesday’s broadcast of “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon,” Louis C. K. said he had grossed more than $1 million from his online comedy special, “Louis C. K.: Live at the Beacon Theater,” after 10 days on sale, and would be donating part of that money to charity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Sales of Louis C. K. Special Cross $1 Million Mark', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/769388f4-0464-57b9-96cc-154bbaf91c91', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/769388f4-0464-57b9-96cc-154bbaf91c91'}, {'abstract': 'Akamai Technologies has made its first cloud services acquisition, agreeing on Thursday to buy a three-year-old company, Cotendo, for about $268 million in cash.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/akamai-to-buy-cloud-services-provider-contendo/', 'snippet': 'Akamai Technologies has made its first cloud services acquisition, agreeing on Thursday to buy a three-year-old company, Cotendo, for about $268 million in cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the year is drawing to a close, there is no end in sight for cloud fever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Akamai to Buy a Cloud Services Provider', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AKAMAI TECHNOLOGIES INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:13:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0efc8698-bfe1-549c-9d15-709a6a224dba', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0efc8698-bfe1-549c-9d15-709a6a224dba'}, {'abstract': 'What the bill says, and reaction from its critics.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/a-pocket-guide-to-the-lokpal-bill/', 'snippet': 'What the bill says, and reaction from its critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late Thursday afternoon, the Indian government introduced the Lokpal Bill in the lower house of Parliament, which would create an all-powerful nine-member anti-corruption ombudsman agency. The law will be debated next week.', 'source': 'The New Yor