1', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ced6a001-1326-59f1-bcb8-1390695c35b1'}, {'abstract': 'In the news on Thursday, the state attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman, is investigating whether the Pearson Foundation, the nonprofit arm of Pearson Education, acted improperly to influence New York State officials to obtain lucrative state contracts when it paid for trips and other perks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/22/state-is-investigating-pearson-foundation-trips/', 'snippet': 'In the news on Thursday, the state attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman, is investigating whether the Pearson Foundation, the nonprofit arm of Pearson Education, acted improperly to influence New York State officials to obtain lucrative state co...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Is Investigating Pearson Foundation Trips', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bd93047-36ca-5478-bd65-cc0daf8b2df9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bd93047-36ca-5478-bd65-cc0daf8b2df9'}, {'abstract': 'For one editor, life after Vogue; Deadspin on the abuse accusations against a Philadelphia sportswriter; will socially conscious hip-hop make a comeback?', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-22/', 'snippet': 'For one editor, life after Vogue; Deadspin on the abuse accusations against a Philadelphia sportswriter; will socially conscious hip-hop make a comeback?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a busy year for Carine Roitfeld, who was replaced last December as the powerful editor of French Vogue by a former friend, Emmanuelle Alt. There have been wild parties she has hosted, fashion magazines and ads she has collaborated on, and talk of starting a new magazine. Ms. Roitfeld, Eric Wilson writes, “has taken every opportunity to demonstrate the value of her brand, post-Vogue,” and concludes: “Rarely has the stock price of a fashion figure shown such resilience, after taking a severe blow to the side, since Lady Duff-Gordon survived the sinking of the Titanic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 22', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conlin, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daulerio, A J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamar, Kendrick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roitfeld, Carine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deadspin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Vogue', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Daily News', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Inquirer', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T13:50:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id':