.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A high-end hotel in Brussels, Tintin’s stomping ground, is offering two new packages and four themed rooms to celebrate the popular comic book hero. The promotion — from the Hotel Amigo \xa0— \xa0is timed to correspond with the release of the film “The Adventures of Tintin: The Secret of the Unicorn,” which opened on Wednesday in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brussels Hotel Offers Tintin Tie-In', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remi, Georges', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65471f96-8c06-5e85-8773-6c04b166c404', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65471f96-8c06-5e85-8773-6c04b166c404'}, {'abstract': 'Chilling weather has (finally) forced women to break out the big ones — the fur and shearling coats.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/winter-wonders-cold-front/', 'snippet': 'Chilling weather has (finally) forced women to break out the big ones — the fur and shearling coats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reality check: it’s December. And chilling weather has (finally) forced women to break out the big ones — the fur and shearling coats. Here, the pop singer Kylie Minogue wears a quilted puffer with a cozy collar and a pair of black leather boots; the actress Rooney Mara picks up lunch in a cloud-like cocoon with a full bell silhouette; and the designer Ashley Olsen keeps it classic in a full-sleeved fur with an elegant rust-colored scarf and dark navy handbag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Cold Front', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c13098-25ce-5851-9e4c-cac005524f32', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c13098-25ce-5851-9e4c-cac005524f32'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/what-were-reading-337/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Jazeera: How the Egyptian revolution was fueled by food inequity: The Mubarak regime built factory farms to grow strawberries and salad for European markets, while staples like lentils and rice became too costly for Egyptians. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://art