Skinner. The list of superstars having the dreaded label of being out indefinitely with a concussion continues to grow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Pronger, Sidney Crosby, Claude Giroux, Milan Michalek and now Jeff Skinner. The list of superstars having the dreaded label of being out indefinitely with a concussion continues to grow. By far, this has been the lead story in the N.H.L. over the last year. It began when Sidney Crosby was found to have a concussion in January. It took a backseat for a short while as Crosby returned to play in late November, but before anyone got comfortable, a slew of great players, including Crosby, have been sent to the press box to watch games, out indefinitely with concussions after all taking blows to the head. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Concussion Issue, From a Player’s Point of View', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giroux, Claude', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pronger, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skinner, Jeff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Caponigri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caponigri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c491214-e655-5ddd-9bd3-652c4f8368e0', 'word_count': 1299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c491214-e655-5ddd-9bd3-652c4f8368e0'}, {'abstract': 'Identifying mourners and absentees in North Korean photographs is one of the few ways for outsiders to make sense of the unfolding succession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/world/asia/family-intrigue-shadows-north-koreas-secretive-dynasty.html', 'snippet': 'Identifying mourners and absentees in North Korean photographs is one of the few ways for outsiders to make sense of the unfolding succession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Researchers scrutinizing North Korea’s official images and lists of mourners paying respects to Kim Jong-il have noticed two conspicuous absences: the elder brothers of Kim Jong-un, the appointed heir.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/23korea-image/23korea-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/23korea-image/23korea-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/world/23korea-image/23korea-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buzz Over Who’s Not in North Korea Picture(s)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buzz Over Who’s Not in North Korea Picture(s)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Un', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], '