new-and-unpopular/', 'snippet': 'Congress is closing out 2011 with record low approval numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congress is closing out 2011 with an 11 percent approval rating, and a 17 percent yearly average. Those are both record lows—Gallup conducted its first Congressional job approval survey in 1974, and never before have Americans been so united in their dissatisfaction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New and Unpopular', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0ed43c8-3dfe-5db2-8e92-fad726ee1c17', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0ed43c8-3dfe-5db2-8e92-fad726ee1c17'}, {'abstract': 'It was a year of financial hardship for the arts (what year isn’t?), especially for many opera houses, symphony orchestras, festivals and chamber music organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/arts/music/daniel-j-wakin-looks-at-music-in-2011.html', 'snippet': 'It was a year of financial hardship for the arts (what year isn’t?), especially for many opera houses, symphony orchestras, festivals and chamber music organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS holiday season brings a set of gifts for the world of classical music, in the form of the highly uncoveted and arbitrarily granted Special Awards for 2011. It was a year of financial hardship for the arts (what