ining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: When Your Guest Wants to Preview the Menu', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabricant, Florence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:59:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddab346c-1771-5a61-8135-817026cbdd55', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddab346c-1771-5a61-8135-817026cbdd55'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Jobs will be honored with a Grammy Award for innovations that “revolutionized the industry and how music was distributed and purchased,” the recording academy said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/steve-jobs-to-receive-a-grammy/', 'snippet': 'Steve Jobs will be honored with a Grammy Award for innovations that “revolutionized the industry and how music was distributed and purchased,” the recording academy said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven P. Jobs was not a musician, and opinions are mixed about whether the invention of iTunes will be good for the recording industry in the long run, but his mark on how music is distributed appears indelible, and so the National Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences has decided to give him a Grammy award in February.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Jobs to Receive a Grammy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grammy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartholomew, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Glen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coltrane, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domino, Fats', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobim, Antonio Carlos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Diana', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T15:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72693e3d-c333-58aa-9ddf-8ab2d72b4878', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72693e3d-c333-58aa-9ddf-8ab2d72b4878'}, {'abstract': 'Graphic simplicity and fastidious pavé work, from a New York-based jeweler.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/the-get-visnja-brdar-power-ring/', 'snippet': 'Graphic simplicity and fastidious pavé work, from a New York-based jeweler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The diamond pattern on this hand-carved rock crystal and white gold “Power” ring ($14,000) may look like a snowflake, but it actually represents the sun. “The energy of the sun is the most powerful force on earth,” says the New York-based jeweler Visnja Brdar. “I wanted to create a piece that reflected that energy. When I wear it, I radiate and feel that anything is possible.” Known for graphic simplicity and fastidious pavé work, all of Brdar’s pieces have uplifting themes like Love, Courage, Freedom and Faith. She may as well have called this one Perseverance, since it took two years to make. “I finally found a way for the crystal to appear as if it is floating on the finger. It is perfect.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Visnja Brdar Power Ring', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6021cb08-f2e1-5d7b-b81f-1a96d25e67b1', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6021cb08-f2e1-5d7b-b81f-1a96d25e67b1'}, {'abstract': 'The first American survey of Sanja Ivekovic, at the Museum of Modern Art, assembles nearly 40 years’ worth of video, photocollages and one sizable obelisk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/arts/design/sanja-ivekovic-croatias-monumental-provocateur.html', 'snippet': 'The first American survey of Sanja Ivekovic, at the Museum of Modern Art, assembles nearly 40 years’ worth of video, photocollages and one sizable obelisk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASK the Croatian artist Sanja Ivekovic about her work, and she is likely to minimize her role in it. “It is not a genius that is making art but the collaboration of many people,“ she declared this month, speaking in heavily accented English, as she strode into the atrium of the Museum of Modern Art. “We should be grateful not to God for giving us our talent but to the people who support us.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/design/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 290, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/design/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 290}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/design/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/design/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/design/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN/25IVEKOVIC_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Croatia’s Monumental Provocateur', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Croatia’s Monumental Provocateur', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivekovic, Sanja', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T16:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Kino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73020c00-c504-5cf0-bfba-375a86c8e23b', 'word_count': 1539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73020c00-c504-5cf0-bfba-375a86c8e23b'}, {'abstract': 'This city of bookstores and coffeehouses, art-house cinemas and eclectic neighborhood bars barely skips a beat in winter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/travel/36-hours-cambridge-mass.html', 'snippet': 'This city of bookstores and coffeehouses, art-house cinemas and eclectic neighborhood bars barely skips a beat in winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the leaves have fallen and the winter chill has set in, many small cities slip into a prolonged hibernation. But Cambridge barely misses a beat. During the holidays, tree branches are strung with tiny white lights, and local theater productions celebrate the season. A city of bookstores and coffeehouses, art-house cinemas and eclectic neighborhood bars, the People’s Republic of Cambridge has traded its Puritan past for a dynamic, cosmopolitan present. Spread out along the tree-lined shore of the Charles River, the city is a dense collection of grand Federal and Greek Revival mansions and modest century-old bungalows, modern office towers and brick dormitories. Nicknamed Boston’s Left Bank for its bohemian image, Cambridge is easy to caricature, but hard to dislike.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25HOURS2/25HOURS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25HOURS2/25HOURS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, 