r, the series also includes five videos that were produced by Nick Harbaugh, Nancy Donaldson and Soo-Jeong Kang and shot by Mr. Winter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing the Unseeable', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T16:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Winter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1907ab44-a420-5ca5-97a4-f85f37c1f490', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1907ab44-a420-5ca5-97a4-f85f37c1f490'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, we pair an Emma Lazarus poem about the oldest synagogue in the country and an article about an Orthodox congregation whose building — modeled on that historic synagogue — burned down.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/poetry-pairing-the-sacred-shrine/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, we pair an Emma Lazarus poem about the oldest synagogue in the country and an article about an Orthodox congregation whose building — modeled on that historic synagogue — burned down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Poetry Pairing matches the Emma Lazarus poem “In the Jewish Synagogue at Newport” with a 2009 article, “A Synagogue Despairs of a Sweeter New Year.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘In the Jewish Synagogue at Newport’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T16:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f932a0-e2c3-5bb6-8a78-be7717e2f374', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f932a0-e2c3-5bb6-8a78-be7717e2f374'}, {'abstract': 'Devotees of the show “Bored to Death” gathered with its creator at a Brooklyn bar to commiserate over its cancellation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/drinking-over-a-shows-demise-a-first-round-free/', 'snippet': 'Devotees of the show “Bored to Death” gathered with its creator at a Brooklyn bar to commiserate over its cancellation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They gathered in a darkened bar in Boerum Hill, Brooklyn, long faces concealed by longer beards, to say goodbye to the show that called their borough home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drinking Over a Show’s Demise, First Round on the House', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boerum Hill (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b27f0d50-ae3e-5f01-bab3-e001a9eec16a', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b27f0d50-ae3e-5f01-bab3-e001a9eec16a'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators described the man as an avid Madonna fan and charged with him stealing a demo version of what is reportedly the lead single for the singer’s 12th studio album.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/spanish-man-arrested-in-leak-of-madonna-single/', 'snippet': 'Investigators described the man as an avid Madonna fan and charged with him stealing a demo version of what is reportedly the lead single for the singer’s 12th studio album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spanish police have arrested a 31-year-old man and charged him with stealing a demo version of one of Madonna’s songs and illegally posting it on the Internet, Reuters reported. The police identified the man only by his initials: J.M.R. He was arrested in Zaragoza, charged and released, pending a trial. Investigators described him as an avid Madonna fan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanish Man Arrested in Leak of Madonna Single', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Music Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1235ad-f8b1-5d34-86be-2c5a39360e61', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1235ad-f8b1-5d34-86be-2c5a39360e61'}, {'abstract': 'Critics and writers for The New York Times recall their favorite moments onstage in 2011, some of them happening in the smallest and most offbeat of places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/theater/critics-look-back-at-favorite-stage-moments-of-2011.html', 'snippet': 'Critics and writers for The New York Times recall their favorite moments onstage in 2011, some of them happening in the smallest and most offbeat of places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASKED to recall unforgettable moments from the year in theater, one writer after another for The New York Times suggested scenes from Jez Butterworth’s “Jerusalem,” which won Mark Rylance a Tony Award for best actor last spring. Stipulated: “Jerusalem” was full of memorable moments. Stipulated: The Times’s critics Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood already named it among their Top 10 shows of the year. Further stipulated: No “Jerusalem” here. But much else to remember, some of it surfacing in the smallest and most offbeat of places. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleverest List of Theatrical Moments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cleverest List Of Theatrical Moments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg, Catherine Rampell, David Rooney, Scott Heller, Patrick Healy, Eric Grode, Jason Zinoman and Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}, {'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 7}, {'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 8}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6d5a426-6d1b-509b-97b5-93f67eec37bf', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6d5a426-6d1b-509b-97b5-93f67eec37bf'}, {'abstract': 'Republican leaders bowed to intense pressure from members of their party to end a politically damaging impasse, agreeing to accept a two-month extension of a payroll tax holiday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/us/politics/senate-republican-leader-suggests-a-payroll-tax-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Republican leaders bowed to intense pressure from members of their party to end a politically damaging impasse, agreeing to accept a two-month extension of a payroll tax holiday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Bowing under intense pressure from members of their own party, House Republican leaders agreed Thursday to accept a temporary extension of the payroll tax cut, beating a hasty retreat from a showdown that Republicans increasingly saw as a threat to their election opportunities next year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/us/subjpCONGRESS/subjpCONGRESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/us/subjpCONGRESS/subjpCONGRESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/us/subjpCONGRESS/subjpCONGRESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House G.O.P. Leaders Agree to Extension of Payroll Tax Cut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Republicans Agree To Extend Payroll Tax Cut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1d9366e-6359-52fd-aeac-27bc89b5746b', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1d9366e-6359-52fd-aeac-27bc89b5746b'}, {'abstract': 'I still can’t decide if sabering Champagne is the dumbest thing I’ve ever heard of or one of the greatest, but here’s how to do it, carefully.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/case-study-on-beheading-bubbly/', 'snippet': 'I still can’t decide if sabering Champagne is the dumbest thing I’ve ever heard of or one of the greatest, but here’s how to do it, carefully.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though we like to think of ourselves as a humble people who disdain ostentatious display, there are those occasions that encourage, nay, demand the chest-thumping, post-touchdown hubris inherent in our species. One of these is the presentation of a frosty bottle of Champagne. It’s like a convoluted Myers-Briggs test for personalities. Many people open such a gift, even on New Year’s Eve, with the gravity of a monk, showing the respect and discretion due a vinous masterwork. But there are those more excitable oenophiles, whose personal standard — “What Would Pirates Do?” — dictates freeing the bubbly soul by lopping off the bottle’s neck with a saber.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Case Study | On Beheading Bubbly', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Cecchini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cecchini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc299ff8-5143-505c-b994-518c2422c9eb', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc299ff8-5143-505c-b994-518c2422c9eb'}, {'abstract': 'The planned deployment of outside observers is aimed at making sure the government of President Bashar al-Assad withdraws heavy military weapons from Syria’s cities and starts a dialogue with opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/world/middleeast/arab-league-delegates-arrive-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The planned deployment of outside observers is aimed at making sure the government of President Bashar al-Assad withdraws heavy military weapons from Syria’s cities and starts a dialogue with opponents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — As violence continued around Syria, delegates from the Arab League traveled to Damascus on Thursday to start monitoring the government’s promise to end its violent suppression of the nine-month-old uprising. The visit is intended to set the ground rules for a mission that is supposed to bring hundreds of observers to Syria in the coming weeks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/syria/syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arab League Delegates Arrive in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arab League Visit to Syria Is Preparation for Monitors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d8f48c-4100-5f59-bae2-c6ad5cca8cb7', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d8f48c-4100-5f59-bae2-c6ad5cca8cb7'}, {'abstract': 'Announcing two new Ruby clients for New York Times APIs: Times Wire and Campaign Cash.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/two-new-client-libraries-times-wire-and-campaign-cash/', 'snippet': 'Announcing two new Ruby clients for New York Times APIs: Times Wire and Campaign Cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that we have 13 APIs to use, it’s time for some client libraries, too. Our APIs get a lot of use internally and on NYTimes.com, often in small parts of a larger project or to power a single interactive. In most of these cases we’ve resorted to pulling data directly from endpoints rather than writing clients to help manage the task. But we’re excited to release Ruby libraries that make it easier to interact with two of our APIs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two New Client Libraries: Times Wire and Campaign Cash', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T17:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By DEREK WILLIS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WILLIS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b352c66-0681-514e-81e0-31952f9dfd2a', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b352c66-0681-514e-81e0-31952f9dfd2a'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, answers questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/coughlin-ryan-tebow-answers-for-readers/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, answers questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judy Battista, who covers the N.F.L. for The Times, answers readers’ questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coughlin, Ryan, Tebow: Answers for Readers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tattoos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boley, Michael', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burress, Plaxico', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowher, Bill', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elway, John', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fewell, Perry', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gronkowski, Rob', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiwanuka, Mathias', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maybin, Aaron', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newton, Cameron J', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Antonio', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierre-Paul, Jason', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Jerry', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'n