ject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Brandon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGahee, Willis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roethlisberger, Ben', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Matt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Steve', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T19:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b11a2a5-43ae-5aa8-93df-235bb8cbc1dd', 'word_count': 1709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b11a2a5-43ae-5aa8-93df-235bb8cbc1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an article by Guy Trebay about living in hotels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/travel/life-in-hotels.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an article by Guy Trebay about living in hotels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding “My Life in Hotels” (Dec. 4), add one more tip to your excellent piece. This from a friend and hotel executive: hotel blankets are not cleaned with each change of sheets. Strip the bedspread, stow it, call housekeeping and request an additional sheet to “top sheet” your bed. A little gratuity to the housekeeper usually ensures that your bed will be freshly top-sheeted when the room is serviced.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life in Hotels', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life in Hotels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T19:25:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/94ba010b-2c7d-52d6-9b5e-a878d1cea7d4', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94ba010b-2c7d-52d6-9b5e-a878d1cea7d4'}, {'abstract': 'Most readers offered similar advice: find a new friend.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/parental-quandary-resolved-when-a-friends-child-hits-yours/', 'snippet': 'Most readers offered similar advice: find a new friend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The real quandary last week wasn’t, perhaps, what a parent should do when a friend’s child hits yours and that friend has more excuses than actions, but how a parent should do what obviously must be done: stop the hitting. Isabel and Sharon (not their real names — all names in quandaries are changed and identifying details changed) became friends when their kids were quite young, and as they grew, Isobel saw Sharon’s kids (both boys, aged 4 and 6) bullying her 4-year-old daughter, with hitting and pushing and even a shove off a bike.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary Resolved: When a Friend’s Child Hits Yours', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T19:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a22f2790-7189-5c30-9562-38a1c829d6e7', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a22f2790-7189-5c30-9562-38a1c829d6e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks have improved, the defending champion Mavericks have not, but in the end, N.B.A. reporter Howard Beck believes that the Thunder and Heat will meet in the finals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/100000001241151/nba-season-preview.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks have improved, the defending champion Mavericks have not, but in the end, N.B.A. reporter Howard Beck believes that the Thunder and Heat will meet in the finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Knicks have improved, the defending champion Mavericks have not, but in the end, N.B.A. reporter Howard Beck believes that the Thunder and Heat will meet in the finals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/video-nba/video-nba-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/video-nba/video-nba-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/video-nba/video-nba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/sports/video-nba/video-nba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7