4427bb82d6', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bc18fe5-94db-5f51-9665-754427bb82d6'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Murphy, a co-creator of the FX series “American Horror Story,” said that none of characters from its first season, living or otherwise, will return in Season 2, nor will the creepy Los Angeles mansion that was the setting for the show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/american-horror-story-will-scare-up-a-new-cast-and-new-haunted-home-for-season-2/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Murphy, a co-creator of the FX series “American Horror Story,” said that none of characters from its first season, living or otherwise, will return in Season 2, nor will the creepy Los Angeles mansion that was the setting for the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we don’t want to spoil the surprise for viewers who haven’t yet seen the “American Horror Story” finale by revealing which characters lived or died, Ryan Murphy, a creator of that FX series, had another surprise up his sleeve, announcing on Thursday that none of characters from its first season, living or otherwise, will return in Season 2, nor will the creepy Los Angeles mansion that was the setting for the show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Horror Story’ Will Scare Up a New Cast and New Haunted Home for Season 2', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Britton, Connie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falchuk, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farmiga, Taissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lange, Jessica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDermott, Dylan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'se