ought from The Choice blog, and an opportunity to ask questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greetings from California. I’m looking forward to jumping into the conversation and responding to your questions on The Choice blog’s Facebook page, beginning at 8 p.m. Eastern time on Thursday. If you want to get your question in early, you can submit it now using the comment box below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Juniors: Homework for Thursday’s Facebook Chat (and Holiday Break)', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:17:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Christensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/706fe4a6-c7c4-55c6-80a1-88e980816e3b', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/706fe4a6-c7c4-55c6-80a1-88e980816e3b'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s strong economic growth and burgeoning middle class has attracted cash-rich companies looking to make acquisitions, including Diageo and SABMiller.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/in-turkey-western-companies-find-stability-and-growth/', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s strong economic growth and burgeoning middle class has attracted cash-rich companies looking to make acquisitions, including Diageo and SABMiller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Turkey’s split personality has often left it caught between two worlds. Some European nations have vocally opposed the country’s attempts to build closer ties with the West. And many of its Middle Eastern neighbors have been wary of the avidly secular state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Turkey, Western Companies Find Stability and Growth', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diageo PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ea049b-2d99-5a93-bdf8-dc100365e294', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ea049b-2d99-5a93-bdf8-dc100365e294'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday night’s show, leading to Thursday’s finale, averaged 11.1 million viewers, enough to be most viewed that night, but also well short of being a phenomenon, as many had expected of Simon Cowell’s new vehicle.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/x-factor-fails-to-live-up-to-its-high-expectations/', 'snippet': 'Wednesday night’s show, leading to Thursday’s finale, averaged 11.1 million viewers, enough to be most viewed that night, but also well short of being a phenomenon, as many had expected of Simon Cowell’s new vehicle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As it heads for its climax, the news for Fox’s “X-Factor” looks well short of x-cellent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘X-Factor’ Fails to Live Up to Its High Expectations', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'