stract': 'Governor Lincoln Chafee won’t hand a prisoner over to the federal government, because Rhode Island does not have the death penalty and the federal government does.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/death-penalty-death-watch-rhode-island-and-the-rest-of-the-world/', 'snippet': 'Governor Lincoln Chafee won’t hand a prisoner over to the federal government, because Rhode Island does not have the death penalty and the federal government does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Governor Lincoln Chafee of Rhode Island is an independent who used to be the sort of Republican the party leaders hates –moderate in many areas and even liberal on some social issues. He is also the kind of career politician currently in short supply: The kind who’s willing to take principled stands. He was the only Republican in the Senate to vote against the war in Iraq and against extending the Bush tax cuts in 2005. He went to blacksmith school in Montana. (This has nothing to do with this article, but it’s interesting, isn’t it?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Penalty Death Watch: Rhode Island and the Rest of the World', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Death Penalty Information Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b34c9a9-0414-58b6-b84a-903bb0571e75', '