hools don\'t have much of a Web presence, but oftentimes it\'s because students look forward to distributing their newspapers "hot off the presses.\'\'', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Just In: Students Love Print', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By KATINA PARON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PARON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e5d9d66-10b4-5cbf-977d-2da9e2c7afca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e5d9d66-10b4-5cbf-977d-2da9e2c7afca'}, {'abstract': "A councilman from Brooklyn argues that the city's Education Department is missing an opportunity by choosing to close and open schools without the involvement of the local communities. In doing so, he argues, the Education Department is not only discouraging the involvement of parents and communities in our schools, but also creating an atmosphere where support for new schools is severely compromised.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2011/12/22/want-to-improve-schools-make-parent-involvement-meaningful/', 'snippet': "A councilman from Brooklyn argues that the city's Education Department is missing an opportunity by choosing to close and open schools without the involvement of the local communities. In doing so, he argues, the Education Department is not only d...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Improve Schools? Make Parent Involvement Meaningful', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By AL VANN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'VANN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d663331-9892-5d47-956f-e173748a1523', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d663331-9892-5d47-956f-e173748a1523'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to performances of classical music in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/music/classical-music-opera-listings-for-dec-23-29.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to performances of classical music in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classical', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music/Opera Listings for Dec. 23-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:50:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/818a0b75-aa76-5830-905f-72a677e5f450', 'word_count': 1169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/818a0b75-aa76-5830-905f-72a677e5f450'}, {'abstract': '“The X-Factor” singing competition didn’t get the expected boost with its second-last show of the season on Wednesday, but the season finale of “American Horror Story” did.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/little-ratings-momentum-as-x-factor-heads-into-finale/', 'snippet': '“The X-Factor” singing competition didn’t get the expected boost with its second-last show of the season on Wednesday, but the season finale of “American Horror Story” did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although the first season of “The X Factor” was never the 20-million-viewer juggernaut that Simon Cowell, its creator-producer-judge, had promised, the singing competition has still been a success for Fox, with an average of 10.9 million viewers tuning in live for each episode. (Factoring in the audiences that watched the show on DVR in the following seven days, that number grows to 12.4 million.) But network executives are probably a little concerned with the lack of ratings momentum heading into the finale, which was evident on Wednesday night, when the final performance show was essentially flat when compared to last week, despite almost no original competition from the other networks. The 90-minute episode averaged 11.1 million total viewers, up slightly from 10.7 million last Wednesday, but down just as slightly in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic segment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Ratings Momentum as ‘X-Factor’ Heads Into Finale', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T20:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4482f236-1384-5fee-8f48-d1b8e604cab5', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4482f236-1384-5fee-8f48-d1b8e604cab5'}, {'abstract': 'Some data in the 2009 study, which linked a mouse leukemia retrovirus to chronic fatigue syndrome and was published in the journal Science, were retracted in September on grounds of laboratory contamination.', 'web_ur