 '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:42:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8ef1f610-9575-5ece-b4de-632b3cea1ea0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8ef1f610-9575-5ece-b4de-632b3cea1ea0'}, {'abstract': '“Clark Howard’s Living Large in Lean Times,” a tightwad manifesto that’s been lingering on The New York Times how-to best-seller list all fall, is at once gloomy and upbeat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/books/clark-howards-living-large-in-lean-times-review.html', 'snippet': '“Clark Howard’s Living Large in Lean Times,” a tightwad manifesto that’s been lingering on The New York Times how-to best-seller list all fall, is at once gloomy and upbeat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This time of year one’s thoughts turn toward family, friends, the best rum to decant into eggnog and — if you are like me, three years out of five — the vertiginous mountain of debt on your credit cards, and the financial reckoning that is breathing into your nostrils, a bit like a wolf.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23BOOK2/SUBBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 863, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23BOOK2/23BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23BOOK2/23BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Proud Penny Pincher’s Guide for Surviving the Tough Times', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proud Penny Pincher’s Guide for Surviving the Tough Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c7dbd5c-48c7-5211-8ce1-c65499825ddb', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c7dbd5c-48c7-5211-8ce1-c65499825ddb'}, {'abstract': 'From San Francisco to Mount Vernon, rye has emerged as a go-to craft spirit of the moment, as distillers both small and large are creating new whiskeys strongly rooted in tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/travel/rye-whiskey-is-back-with-flavors-of-american-history.html', 'snippet': 'From San Francisco to Mount Vernon, rye has emerged as a go-to craft spirit of the moment, as distillers both small and large are creating new whiskeys strongly rooted in tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN gold-rush-era San Francisco, bars lined every block of the Barbary Coast, the area where pioneer mixologists — back when they were called bartenders — honed their craft. Rye whiskey was their staple. A hundred years later, a visitor would have been lucky to find one or two rye labels on the shelves of bars in major American cities; bourbon had taken over as the American whiskey.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25EXPLORER_SPAN/25EXPLORER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25EXPLORER_SPAN/25EXPLORER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25EXPLORER_SPAN/25EXPLORER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25EXPLORER_SPAN/25EXPLORER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/travel/25EXPLORER_SPAN/25EXPLORER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rye Is Back, With Flavors of Americana', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rye Is Back, With Flavors of Americana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bonnie Tsui', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bonnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsui', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc63caf-6dee-5105-b7f1-60a5f448beae', 'word_count': 1582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc63caf-6dee-5105-b7f1-60a5f448beae'}, {'abstract': 'The latest cookbook launches include video promotional trailers.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/coming-to-a-bookstore-near-you/', 'snippet': 'The latest cookbook launches include video promotional trailers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A video for the upcoming cookbook “La Tartine Gourmande,” based on the blog of the same name, made us wonder whether cookbook trailers —\xa0picture a movie trailer, but with charming kitchens and light jazz swapped in for post-apocalyptic underworlds and techno — are slowly becoming as widespread as trailers in other corners of the publishing world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming to a Bookstore Near You!', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Weinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad2b2c1-bc9a-5b12-aea9-97478fd3c6ac', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad2b2c1-bc9a-5b12-aea9-97478fd3c6ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Karzai administration has chosen not to renew the tenure of the outspoken advocate Ahmad Nader Nadery at a national human rights commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/world/asia/afghan-rights-activist-nadery-ousted-from-panel.html', 'snippet': 'The Karzai administration has chosen not to renew the tenure of the outspoken advocate Ahmad Nader Nadery at a national human rights commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — There have been few causes that Ahmad Nader Nadery, the prominent Afghan human rights activist, shied away from over the past decade: he spoke out on the killings of civilians by NATO and Taliban forces, on election fraud by President Hamid Karzai’s supporters, even on land grabs by rich and well-connected Afghans whose houses now dominate central Kabul’s broken streets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Outspoken Afghan Rights Official Ousted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outspoken Afghan Rights Official Ousted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4265a9c8-dd10-562a-a88e-a2e12818c68d', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4265a9c8-dd10-562a-a88e-a2e12818c68d'}, {'abstract': 'In airports, classrooms and doctors’ offices, Christians and religious minorities say,