ussia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T21:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2bd7e1a-bba6-53e4-89d7-87bfa00bf5d9', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2bd7e1a-bba6-53e4-89d7-87bfa00bf5d9'}, {'abstract': 'Our favorite card this year.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/a-very-hairy-christmas/', 'snippet': 'Our favorite card this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our favorite holiday card this year! It shows Hunter Musi, the son of the photographers Vincent J. Musi and Callie Shell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Very Hairy Christmas', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T22:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathy Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8367937d-c711-53ad-a159-13a0045f5a06', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8367937d-c711-53ad-a159-13a0045f5a06'}, {'abstract': 'We tried a few new things with this year’s Lives They Lived issue. For starters, we invited Ira Glass and his producers at “This American Life,” the wonderful radio show we all love, to guest-edit a special section.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/comments-about-the-lives-they-lived-issue-here-please/', 'snippet': 'We tried a few new things with this year’s Lives They Lived issue. For starters, we invited Ira Glass and his producers at “This American Life,” the wonderful radio show we all love, to guest-edit a special section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We tried a few new things with this year’s Lives They Lived issue. For starters, we invited Ira Glass and his producers at “This American Life,” the wonderful radio show we all love, to guest-edit a special section. We invited readers to submit their own photographs and stories of loved ones, which succeeded beyond our highest expectations. We compiled a series of famous last tweets. Finally, we did a bit of the old thing, and commissioned some of our favorite writers, including John Jeremiah Sullivan, Maureen Dowd, Dwight Garner and Michael Paterniti, to write short essays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comments About the Lives They Lived Issue Here, Please', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T22:05:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a11ebf-61a2-54de-95fd-4be5ca8c8023', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a11ebf-61a2-54de-95fd-4be5ca8c8023'}, {'abstract': 'Comedy for the holidays with the Mandatory Office Party at Union Hall in Brooklyn and “A Night of Dirty Songs” at Joe’s Pub in the East Village.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/nyregion/mandatory-office-party-and-night-of-dirty-songs.html', 'snippet': 'Comedy for the holidays with the Mandatory Office Party at Union Hall in Brooklyn and “A Night of Dirty Songs” at Joe’s Pub in the East Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The average holiday office party can be divided into two parts: awkward conversation with co-workers before the booze kicks in, and even more awkward conversation with co-workers after it does. That’s why the Miser tends to bow out early and head to parties where letting loose is less likely to damage professional reputations. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/1223MISERSPAN/1223MISERSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/1223MISERSPAN/1223MISERSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/1223MISERSPAN/1223MISERSPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 804, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/1223MISERSPAN/1223MISERSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/1223MISERSPAN/1223MISERSPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mandatory Office Party and ‘Night of Dirty Songs’', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mandatory Office Party and ‘Night of Dirty Songs’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T22:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', '