oliday shoppers and merchants in Rome react.", 'lead_paragraph': "As Italy's new government passes strict austerity cuts, holiday shoppers and merchants in Rome react.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/video-tc-111222-donadio/video-tc-111222-donadio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/22/world/video-tc-111222-donadio/video-tc-111222-donadio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/world/video-tc-111222-donadio/video-tc-111222-donadio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/world/video-tc-111222-donadio/video-tc-111222-donadio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "TimesCast | Italy's Deep Spending Cuts", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T22:38:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'Pierre Kattar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pierre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kattar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2c4b2f41-3c9c-5fe8-b3cf-0d2fe545f309', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2c4b2f41-3c9c-5fe8-b3cf-0d2fe545f309'}, {'abstract': 'In Cameron Crowe’s “We Bought a Zoo” Matt Damon plays a single father who is raising his two children and trying to revive a zoo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/movies/we-bought-a-zoo-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Cameron Crowe’s “We Bought a Zoo” Matt Damon plays a single father who is raising his two children and trying to revive a zoo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cameron Crowe may be the last of the Hollywood romantics. He’s best known for his stories about love and longing, for films that immortalize the moment when characters bare their hearts, as when John Cusack serenades a girl with a boom box in “Say Anything” and Renée Zellweger tells Tom Cruise he had her at hello in “Jerry Maguire.” These are images of such excruciating sincerity that they invite, almost demand cynicism. Yet it’s their openness that makes them work. And while his films depend on the familiar image of the couple in love, these are relationships that exist within a larger tribe, a band, a family and now, with “We Bought a Zoo,” a menagerie.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WEBOUGHT1_SPAN/WEBOUGHT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WEBOUGHT1_SPAN/WEBOUGHT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WEBOUGHT1_SPAN/WEBOUGHT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WEBOUGHT1_SPAN/WEBOUGHT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WEBOUGHT1_SPAN/WEBOUGHT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modern-Day Ark, With Children, Animals and Even Romance', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'We Bought a Zoo'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modern-Day Ark, With Children, Animals And Even Romance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowe, Cameron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T22:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7801c619-758d-5ca0-b04b-9adbf4614036', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7801c619-758d-5ca0-b04b-9adbf4614036'}, {'abstract': 'Eva Mohn’s contemptuous character dominated Johannes Wieland’s “new you,” at the Merce Cunningham Studio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/dance/johannes-wielands-new-you-at-cunningham-studio-review.html', 'snippet': 'Eva Mohn’s contemptuous character dominated Johannes Wieland’s “new you,” at the Merce Cunningham Studio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ways into Johannes Wieland’s “new you,” the performer Eva Mohn turns to the audience and asks bitingly, “Are you all waiting for that dancing part?” Well, she says, “It’s not going to happen,” then adds, “Sorry.” In fact, there is dancing to come, some of it excellent, but the self-reflexive comment, the defensive and contemptuous lie, is more characteristic of this 2008 work, which made a repeat appearance at the Merce Cunningham Studio on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ra