'nyt://article/cd5b394b-fe7a-56df-abe6-c4946a0fd63c'}, {'abstract': 'The NPR quiz show “Wait Wait ... Don’t Tell Me!” moves out of the radio and into the television for a year-end special subtitled “A Royal Pain in the News.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/television/wait-wait-dont-tell-me-on-bbc-america-review.html', 'snippet': 'The NPR quiz show “Wait Wait ... Don’t Tell Me!” moves out of the radio and into the television for a year-end special subtitled “A Royal Pain in the News.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The NPR program “Wait Wait ... Don’t Tell Me!” has always seemed like the news satire show that wished this were still 1952. It is content with a somewhat sleepy pace, and it delves no deeper than improvised quips can go.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WAITWAIT_SPAN/23WAITWAIT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WAITWAIT_SPAN/23WAITWAIT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WAITWAIT_SPAN/WAITWAIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WAITWAIT_SPAN/23WAITWAIT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23WAITWAIT_SPAN/23WAITWAIT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Heard Than Seen? A Cheeky Quiz Show Tests a Hotter Medium', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Heard Than Seen? A Cheeky Quiz Show Tests a Hotter Medium', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a74c8327-bf91-5a33-803b-655e321efcca', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a74c8327-bf91-5a33-803b-655e321efcca'}, {'abstract': '“The Radical Camera: New York’s Photo League 1936-1951” at the Jewish Museum traces the group’s history through some 145 photographs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/design/the-radical-camera-at-the-jewish-museum-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Radical Camera: New York’s Photo League 1936-1951” at the Jewish Museum traces the group’s history through some 145 photographs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of many artistic casualties of the McCarthy-era blacklists was the Photo League, a New York school and salon for amateur and professional photographers. Progressive in its politics and uncompromising in its aesthetics, the league was the place to be if you had a hand-held 35-millimeter camera and a left-leaning social conscience — and particularly if you believed, to borrow a bit of contemporary parlance, that photography was fine art for the 99 percent.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RADICAL1/23RADICAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RADICAL1/23RADICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RADICAL1/23RADICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Artists Equipped With a Social Conscience', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Artists Equipped With a Social Conscience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Museum (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9219d05b-2b5a-5d0d-b709-0be9f3d0bb42', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9219d05b-2b5a-5d0d-b709-0be9f3d0bb42'}, {'abstract': 'To keep your brother from guzzling the expensive wine at a holiday dinner, try announcing that it’s meant for everyone to taste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/to-share-and-to-sip-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'To keep your brother from guzzling the expensive wine at a holiday dinner, try announcing that it’s meant for everyone to taste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of my cousins and I, who have more disposable income, enjoy fine wines. I take a “treat” bottle to holiday meals and several nice budget bottles. This holiday, I brought a $200 bottle, which a wine-enthusiast cousin praised. My brother, who knows nothing of wine, proceeded to drink half of it and exclaim, “Tastes just like the $3 bottle to me.” Is there a polite way to ask nonoenophiles to drink the less expensive wine and let the wine lovers enjoy the special bottles?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': '