anguage and ideas that is both heartbreaking and exhilarating. It seems almost impossible to straighten out, but that may be what makes it so valuable. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23SPIRITS_SPAN/23SPIRITS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23SPIRITS_SPAN/23SPIRITS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23SPIRITS_SPAN/SPIRITS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23SPIRITS_SPAN/23SPIRITS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23SPIRITS_SPAN/23SPIRITS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Native Culture’s Reach, Both Visual and Emotional', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Native Culture’s Reach, Both Visual and Emotional', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:13:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c022b9c7-9e34-557b-8aff-e111fb2cf622', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c022b9c7-9e34-557b-8aff-e111fb2cf622'}, {'abstract': 'Images from the life and career of the choreographer Pina Bausch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2009/06/30/arts/20090630_PINA_SLIDESHOW_index.html', 'snippet': 'Images from the life and career of the choreographer Pina Bausch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Images from the life and career of the choreographer Pina Bausch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2009/06/30/arts/bausch75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2009/06/30/arts/bausch75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Pina Bausch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tanztheater Wuppertal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bausch, Pina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melillo, Joseph V', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:14:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7e33f213-374d-5ca9-99d7-7c3eaee93666', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7e33f213-374d-5ca9-99d7-7c3eaee93666'}, {'abstract': 'Wim Wenders’s documentary “Pina” is a tribute to the German dancer and choreographer Pina Bausch, who died in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/movies/pina-a-documentary-by-wim-wenders-review.html', 'snippet': 'Wim Wenders’s documentary “Pina” is a tribute to the German dancer and choreographer Pina Bausch, who died in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the interesting and unexpected film stories of 2011 is about 3-D, which simultaneously lost commercial potency and gained artistic credibility. Those who dismiss the format as the industrial gimmick (and excuse for price gouging) that it frequently is may need to reconsider now that a handful of certified auteurs have given it a try. Steven Spielberg and Martin Scorsese, grand old men of baby-boomer Hollywood, have made 3-D children’s tales (“The Adventures of Tintin” and “Hugo”), which is certainly noteworthy. More remarkable, perhaps even astonishing, is that Werner Herzog and Wim Wenders, stalwarts and survivors of the iconoclastic New German Cinema of the 1970s, have used 3-D in new documentaries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23PINA_SPAN/23PINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23PINA_SPAN/23PINA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23PINA_SPAN/23PINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23PINA_SPAN/23PINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23PINA_SPAN/23PINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '3-D Tribute to Artistic Impulse', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Pina'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3-D Tribute to Artistic Impulse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bausch, Pina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wenders, Wim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff0ff3d6-1402-58ea-aa7e-33ef696a2e01', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff0ff3d6-1402-58ea-aa7e-33ef696a2e01'}, {'abstract': '“The Renaissance Portrait From Donatello to Bellini” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art shows how subjects flaunted their connections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/design/renaissance-portrait-from-donatello-to-bellini-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Renaissance Portrait From Donatello to Bellini” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art shows how subjects flaunted their connections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lovely, bust-length portrait painted by Francesco Francia in 1510 pictures a winsome, long-haired boy of 10 named Federigo Gonzaga. Dressed in a black gown over a white chemise and sporting a jauntily tilted cap and a bejeweled gold necklace, he holds the pommel of a sword and gazes dreamily off to his left. Under blue sky and fair-weather clouds, a pastoral sward extends behind him to a city in the far blue haze. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RENA/23RENA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RENA/23RENA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23RENA/23RENA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Personal', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Personal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb9cbf6e-9d6a-574d-9df9-e533c3ed25b6', 'word_count': 1470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb9cbf6e-9d6a-574d-9df9-e533c3ed25b6'}, {'abstract': 'It’s no surprise that “Spider-Man: Turn off the Dark” dominated the year in theater news. But his wasn’t the only story (just about a third of them, in this modest account).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/theater/patrick-healy-looks-back-at-theater-in-2011.html', 'snippet': 'It’s no surprise that “Spider-Man: Turn off the Dark” dominated the year in theater news. But his wasn’t the only story (just about a third of them, in this modest account).', 'lead_paragraph': 'RARELY does a Broadway show become one of the biggest cultural news stories of the year. But “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” had more offstage intrigue than any production in recent memory — as well as a record-setting budget of $75 million, six delays to its opening night and the gold-plated creative team of U2’s Bono and the Edge and the director Julie Taymor. So it’s no surprise that from beginning to end Spidey dominated the year in theater news. But his wasn’t the only story (just about a third of them, in this modest account):', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25HEALY2/25HEALY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25HEALY2/25HEALY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25HEALY2/25HEALY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stage Shows With Back Stories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stage Shows With Back Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-22T23:18:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/841b27ea-0a12-540f-abb8-717066e086ed', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/841b27ea-0a12-540f-abb8-717066e086ed'}, {'abstract': 'Drummers, singers and guitarists were on parade for Make Music Winter, a festival taking place in public spaces across the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/arts/music/make-music-winter-brings-music-outdoors.html', 'snippet': 'Drummers, singers and guitarists were on parade for Make Music Winter, a festival taking place in public spaces across the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ENCASED in pouches with a small speaker attached to the outside, iPhones dangled from belts and wrists. They emitted dings and chatters as some 60 people began strolling along the High Line on Wednesday night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23ROUNDUP_SPAN/ROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23ROUNDUP_SPAN/ROUNDUP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23ROUNDUP_SPAN/ROUNDUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23ROUNDUP_SPAN/ROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/arts/23ROUNDUP_SPAN/ROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': 