aragraph': 'If you spend a lot of time on Facebook, you probably have a small list of petty gripes about the site’s user interface. Why does Facebook show me posts I’ve already read? Can I break up my giant News Feed into smaller sections? And please, please, can someone make that scrolling ticker in the upper right corner stop moving before it drives me insane?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Fixer Makes Facebook More Fun and Functional', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T01:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Boutin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boutin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e834a4d-7f89-502e-bb75-b1a3191aade0', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e834a4d-7f89-502e-bb75-b1a3191aade0'}, {'abstract': 'Cook County Jail has instituted a new policy for transgender detainees, which includes a panel that determines whether they should be housed with men or women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/us/for-transgender-detainees-a-jail-policy-offers-some-security.html', 'snippet': 'Cook County Jail has instituted a new policy for transgender detainees, which includes a panel that determines whether they should be housed with men or women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For as long as she can remember, Maribel said, she has felt that she was different. She was born a boy in Mexico, and came to the United States at 16. Two years later, she started taking hormone pills and later underwent some operations to become physically the woman she