bels overran arms depots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — The United States is discussing with the Libyan interim government the creation of a program to purchase shoulder-fired, heat-seeking missiles from militia members and others who gathered them up during the war, American government officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/jp-libya1/jp-libya1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/world/jp-libya1/jp-libya1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/jp-libya1/jp-libya1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/world/jp-libya1/jp-libya1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/world/jp-libya1/jp-libya1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Control Libya Missiles? Buy Them Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Control Libya Missiles? Buy Them Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercenaries and Private Military Contractors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T01:44:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec7af204-e45c-5e1c-ad82-9cdaf4831d01', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec7af204-e45c-5e1c-ad82-9cdaf4831d01'}, {'abstract': 'There is widespread noncompliance with the Illinois Campus Security Enhancement Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/education/chicago-area-colleges-fail-to-complete-safety-plans.html', 'snippet': 'There is widespread noncompliance with the Illinois Campus Security Enhancement Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than three years after the fatal shootings at Northern Illinois University prompted a state law requiring colleges and universities to put safety plans in effect, few of Cook County’s 63 higher-education institutions have filed them and many may not have made them public.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colleges Fail to Complete Required Safety Plans', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colleges Fail To Complete Required Safety Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank':