he obstructionism used by Republicans crumbled as the struggle to reach a deal on a payroll tax cut showed voters the real temperament of the current House leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a full year, House Republicans have replaced governing with confrontations that they allow to reach the brink of crisis, only then making extreme demands in exchange for a resolution. On Thursday, that strategy crumbled. Battered by public opinion and undermined by more reasonable Senate Republicans, the House’s leaders backed down and signed off on a deal to continue the payroll tax cut and unemployment insurance for two months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The House Backs Down', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The House Backs Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T01:59:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/058d0b0d-f52f-582f-b667-24819ca24310', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/058d0b0d-f52f-582f-b667-24819ca24310'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department concluded that the Gun Control Act does not empower the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives to impose a stricter requirement on noncitizen gun buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/us/atf-eases-rules-on-gun-sales-to-noncitizens.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department concluded that the Gun Control Act does not empower the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives to impose a stricter requirement on noncitizen gun buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives is relaxing restrictions on the sale of guns to noncitizens because Justice Department lawyers have concluded that the rules had no legal basis, officials said on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rules Eased on Gun Sales to Noncitizens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rules Eased on Gun Sales to Noncitizens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lautenberg, Frank R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T02:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a28bded-fb33-5633-aa36-26642c265171', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a28bded-fb33-5633-aa36-26642c265171'}, {'abstract': 'Surveys show Americans are populist class warriors, except when they aren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/do-we-hate-the-rich-or-dont-we/', 'snippet': 'Surveys show Americans are populist class warriors, except when they aren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s an example of how the results of polls taken at the same time can be given exactly opposite interpretations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do We Hate the Rich or Don’t We?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yglesias, Matthew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T02:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Gelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23e5e99e-c0ca-5fc0-ad26-f78049054ba6', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23e5e99e-c0ca-5fc0-ad26-f78049054ba6'}, {'abstract': 'Active-duty military are behind Ron Paul for one big reason.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/22/soldiers-choice/', 'snippet': 'Active-duty military are behind Ron Paul for one big reason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So this is Christmas, season of peace, time to reflect on the people coming home from a war that most Americans say was not worth it, and those still fighting in another war that raises new doubts by the day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soldiers’ Choice', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T02:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8611b4bd-a0c8-5626-b699-797ada80ca80', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8611b4bd-a0c8-5626-b699-797ada80ca80'}, {'abstract': 'President Bashar al-Assad of Syria is still killing his people. And leaders in Russia, China and Arab states haven’t done enough to pressure him to stop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/opinion/get-tougher-on-syrias-assad.html', 'snippet': 'President Bashar al-Assad of Syria is still killing his people. And leaders in Russia, China and Arab states haven’t done enough to pressure him to stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of a tumultuous year in which strongmen across the Middle East were toppled, President Bashar al-Assad of Syria is still standing, still killing his people. And leaders in Russia, China and Arab states still haven’t done enough to pressure him to stop. The United Nations says more than 5,000 people, mostly civilians, have died in the brutal government crackdown in nine months of protests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Tougher on Assad', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Tougher on Assad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T02:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1816b7cd-0a1c-58dc-a0cc-56f12e9d5827', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1816b7cd-0a1c-58dc-a0cc-56f12e9d5827'}, {'abstract': 'If, as Army prosecutors claim, Danny Chen was pushed into suicide by fellow soldiers who brutalized and humiliated him, his family deserves to see justice done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/opinion/a-soldiers-death.html', 'snippet': 'If, as Army prosecutors claim, Danny Chen was pushed into suicide by fellow soldiers who brutalized and humiliated him, his family deserves to see justice done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Private Danny Chen was alone when he died. The Army says he shot himself in a guard tower in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan. But, in an extraordinary case alleging criminal culpability in a suicide, it has charged eight soldiers in connection with his death, saying they bullied Private Chen into killing himself. Seven enlisted men face counts that include involuntary manslaughter, negligent homicide and assault. One officer, a first lieutenant, is charged with dereliction of duty. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soldier’s Death', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Soldier&#8217;s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T02:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c5e3f52-70e7-5fbc-9984-ec19815b3973', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c5e3f52-70e7-5fbc-9984-ec19815b3973'}, {'abstract': 'The friends and family of Sam Hurd, who was released by the Chicago Bears as he faced federal drug charges, are still grappling with the aftermath of his arrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/sports/football/dismay-and-disbelief-for-those-who-knew-a-younger-sam-hurd.html', 'snippet': 'The friends and family of Sam Hurd, who was released by the Chicago Bears as he faced federal drug charges, are still grappling with the aftermath of his arrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — The Sam Hurd they thought they knew grew up here, in the shadow of the Alamodome. His family still lives in the house on Indiana Avenue, the one with chipped white paint, cracked windows upstairs and a speedboat marooned in the backyard.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/23hurd-1/23hurd-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/23hurd-1/23hurd-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/23hurd-1/23hurd-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dismay, Then Disbelief at Arrest of N.F.L. Player', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dismay, Then Disbelief At Arrest of N.F.L. Player', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug