rticle/252bf27c-4d48-56b8-8bc3-e915380607c3'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s victory over House Republicans in their showdown over payroll tax cuts and unemployment aid helped him more politically than substantively.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/us/politics/for-obama-payroll-tax-victory-was-aided-by-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s victory over House Republicans in their showdown over payroll tax cuts and unemployment aid helped him more politically than substantively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama did not win much substantively with his victory Thursday over House Republicans in their showdown over extending payroll tax cuts and unemployment aid for two months. But he got a lot politically: a big start toward retiring the perception — fair or not, and even among Democrats — that in a pinch with the other party he will inevitably surrender.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/us/ASSESS/ASSESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/us/ASSESS/ASSESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/us/ASSESS/ASSESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Victory Considerably Aided by the Other Side', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Victory Considerably Aided by the Other Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'n