y toward the southern Nigerian coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAGOS, Nigeria — An oil slick roughly 350 square miles in size from a Royal Dutch Shell platform is slowly making its way toward the southern Nigerian coast, threatening wildlife and widespread shore pollution, Nigerian officials said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Spill Moves Toward Nigerian Coast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigeria: Shell Oil Spill Is Drifting Toward Coast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Spills', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T03:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Musikilu Mojeed and Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Musikilu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mojeed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b280caa2-8a9c-5be5-97c0-fdde55cb0eeb', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b280caa2-8a9c-5be5-97c0-fdde55cb0eeb'}, {'abstract': 'New and substantially enhanced financial aid policies aimed at all admitted students have made it easier to recruit elite athletes to the Ivy League.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/sports/financial-aid-changes-game-as-sports-teams-in-ivies-rise.html', 'snippet': 'New and substantially enhanced financial aid policies aimed at all admitted students have made it easier to recruit elite athletes to the Ivy League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The eight Ivy League colleges, renowned for their academics, were also once among the country’s highest-achieving athletic institutions, with national champions and multiple prominent and ranked sports teams.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/ivy-1/ivy-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/ivy-1/ivy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/sports/ivy-1/ivy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Aid Changes Game as Ivy Sports Teams Flourish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Financial Aid Changes Game As Ivy Sports Teams Flourish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivy League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scholarships and Fellowships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T03:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e69e4b9-9242-546d-b1a8-fbbdba8774a0', 'word_count': 1372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e69e4b9-9242-546d-b1a8-fbbdba8774a0'}, {'abstract': 'Not a single new artificial hip or knee introduced over a recent five-year period was any more durable than older ones. In fact, 30 percent of them fared worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/health/research/new-models-of-hip-and-knee-implants-not-better-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Not a single new artificial hip or knee introduced over a recent five-year period was any more durable than older ones. In fact, 30 percent of them fared worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study suggests that the recent technology for artificial hips and knees did not perform any better than older, less expensive designs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Models of Implants Not Better, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Models Of Implants Not Better, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Bone and Joint Surgery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 6, 'majo