': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T05:01:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3e439d3-09af-5ff2-b65f-2d2ce5d0fddf', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3e439d3-09af-5ff2-b65f-2d2ce5d0fddf'}, {'abstract': 'Compelling photographs from New York and the region, including Occupy Wall Street, the 10th anniversary of 9/11, and Hurricane Irene.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/year-in-new-york-pictures/', 'snippet': 'Compelling photographs from New York and the region, including Occupy Wall Street, the 10th anniversary of 9/11, and Hurricane Irene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK has always been too big an idea to be rendered successfully in a single image: simultaneously cruel and generous, dazzling and demeaning, unbearably vibrant and — as it waits to see what path a tropical storm will take — suspensefully calm. But one thing that almost every New York moment has in common is a surprise of some sort. Some surprises are dreadful. An 8-year-old boy named Leiby Kletzky was supposed to walk the seven blocks back to his home in Borough Park one day in July, but he never made it. Other surprises were joyful. Same-sex couples did not go into the year thinking they would have the right to marry before the summer was out. Felix Ramirez and Peter Vargas of the Bronx had already been together 24 years by the time they were wed at City Hall. (Or at least near it.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Year in New York Pictures', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Irene (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stations and Terminals (Passenger)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunlap, David W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T05:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21c725d6-c68d-5282-8d4d-ae6510bf2506', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21c725d6-c68d-5282-8d4d-ae6510bf2506'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 139 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/word-of-the-day-unfettered/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 139 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'unfettered •\\ən-ˈfe-tərd\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | unfettered', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T05:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8778c801-5ef9-53e9-862d-2ac46bcb9b60', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8778c801-5ef9-53e9-862d-2ac46bcb9b60'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Sharp made “The Kiss of the Vampire,” considered by some to be one of the greatest Gothic horror movies ever made, and a remake of “The Thirty-Nine Steps,” among others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/movies/don-sharp-director-dies-at-89-revived-hammer-horror-films.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Sharp made “The Kiss of the Vampire,” considered by some to be one of the greatest Gothic horror movies ever made, and a remake of “The Thirty-Nine Steps,” among others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don Sharp, a veteran film director who had never watched a horror movie until Hammer Films — the English studio described, usually admiringly, as dripping cinematic blood — enlisted him in the mid-1960s to help revivify its presentation of Gothic terror, died on Sunday. He was 89. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/movi