onal outpouring of affection that largely eluded him in his later life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/world/havel1/havel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/24/world/havel1/havel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/world/havel1/havel1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/world/havel1/havel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/world/havel1/havel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourners in Prague Honor Havel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ceremony and Symbolism As Czechs Mourn Havel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Havel, Vaclav', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T13:57:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish and Katerina Santurova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katerina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santurova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea3deadc-62fe-52d3-82f9-03a3cc47fc44', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea3deadc-62fe-52d3-82f9-03a3cc47fc44'}, {'abstract': 'New legal counsel at News Corporation, new ownership rules from the F.C.C., a new ESPN for women and a new way to look at the grieving in North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-23/', 'snippet': 'New legal counsel at News Corporation, new ownership rules from the F.C.C., a new ESPN for women and a new way to look at the grieving in North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation is in talks to hire a Washington lawyer, Gerson Zweifach, to be its next general counsel, as the company handles the legal fallout from the phone-hacking scandal in Britain, Bloomberg News reported Thursday night. He would replace Lawrence Jacobs, who resigned in June to pursue other opportunities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 23', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Il-sung', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Joel I', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Korean Central News Agency', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T13:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa1694e-8edb-5254-831d-f19af1e4511f', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa1694e-8edb-5254-831d-f19af1e4511f'}, {'abstract': 'When offered the role of Margaret Thatcher in “The Iron Lady,” Meryl Streep explained, “To say, ‘No, I’m not interested’ would just be ridiculous. There is no other opportunity like it.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/movies/for-iron-lady-armor-added-to-streeps-wardrobe.html', 'snippet': 'When offered the role of Margaret Thatcher in “The Iron Lady,” Meryl Streep explained, “To say, ‘No, I’m not interested’ would just be ridiculous. There is no other opportunity like it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT do you do after turning yourself into Julia Child, a bold, occasionally bossy woman who changed the way people think about food? You turn yourself into Margaret Thatcher, of course, an even bolder and bossier one, who changed the way people think about Britain. This is what Meryl Streep does in “The Iron Lady,” which opens Friday in New York. In yet another of her miraculous impersonations, which has already been nominated for a Golden Globe award, she seems even more Thatcher-like than Mrs. Thatcher, so that after the movie if you go back and look at photographs of Mrs. Thatcher in her prime, you can’t help feeling that they’re a little off. She no longer looks like herself.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25JPIRON2_SPAN/25JPIRON2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25JPIRON2_SPAN/25JPIRON2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25JPIRON2_SPAN/25JPIRON2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25JPIRON2_SPAN/25JPIRON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/arts/25JPIRON2_SPAN/25JPIRON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Streep Dons Thatcher’s Armor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Streep Dons Thatcher’s Armor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9919f3c2-d33c-5419-94d6-49a03989c929', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9919f3c2-d33c-5419-94d6-49a03989c929'}, {'abstract': 'The heated war of words over the Stop Online Piracy Act has escalated as a group of people in the tech industry say  the services and businesses of  those who support the bill should be boycotted. Suddenly, the debate over a bill that some consider a road to censorship is about free speech.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/daily-report-the-boycott-against-sopa-supporters/', 'snippet': 'The heated war of words over the Stop Online Piracy Act has escalated as a group of people in the tech industry say  the services and businesses of  those who support the bill should be boycotted. Suddenly, the debate over a bill that some conside...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The biggest news Friday is the battle in the tech world\xa0 between those who are proposing a boycott of everyone who supports the Stop Online Piracy Act and those who think that tactic is an affront to free speech. Congress would give companies some teeth to fight Web sites that publish pirated songs and movies. Opponents of the bill decry it as censorship. Edward Wyatt wrote about the bill in The New York Times several days ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy':