article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91ed4ecf-ced7-5222-84a6-f5d7ae1b750f', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91ed4ecf-ced7-5222-84a6-f5d7ae1b750f'}, {'abstract': 'About 11 percent of Americans say they approve of Congress. What are they thinking?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/the-congressional-fan-base/', 'snippet': 'About 11 percent of Americans say they approve of Congress. What are they thinking?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post yesterday I noted that congressional job approval figures are at an all-time low: 11 percent. This observation drew comments from readers wondering who, exactly, holds the minority opinion and would tell a polling agency that they approve of Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Congressional Fan Base', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T16:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e339c319-4743-542b-b8b5-9ae73a42475f', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e339c319-4743-542b-b8b5-9ae73a42475f'}, {'abstract': '“Pariah,” a movie about black lesbians, is part of a mini-movement of young black filmmakers telling stories that complicate assumptions about what “black film” can be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/movies/pariah-reveals-another-side-of-being-black-in-the-us.html', 'snippet': '“Pariah,” a movie about black lesbians, is part of a mini-movement of young black filmmakers telling stories that complicate assumptions about what “black film” can be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY in Dee Rees’s film “Pariah” it journeys into a Brooklyn strip club where scantily clad young black women gyrate to a sexy, foul-mouthed rap song. Lascivious customers leer, toss money and revel in their own unbridled lust. It is a scene that could have been in any of “the hood movies” that once proliferated or even a Tyler Perry melodrama in which Christian values would be affirmed after this bit of titillation.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Directors Flesh Out Black America, All of It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Directors Flesh Out Black America, All of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oduye, Adepero', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rees, Dee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T17:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson George', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'George', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/035d21fa-d1ce-5ebf-bbe5-8081212bdfeb', 'word_count': 1909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/035d21fa-d1ce-5ebf-bbe5-8081212bdfeb'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper is accused of destroying a soundboard at the Roxy in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/tyler-the-creator-is-arrested-on-vandalism-charge/', 'snippet': 'The rapper is accused of destroying a soundboard at the Roxy in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyler, the Creator, the young Los Angeles rapper known for violent and grotesque lyrics, was arrested on Thursday night in a club where he was performing a Christmas concert and charged with vandalizing sound equipment, the Los Angeles County Sheriff’s Department said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyler, the Creator, Is Arrested on Vandalism Charge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beverly Hills (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T17:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63da529c-9ae3-56a8-a264-f5ae739dcfd4', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63da529c-9ae3-56a8-a264-f5ae739dcfd4'}, {'abstract': 'Once home to 50,000 residents, this archaeological ruin is just a half-hour outside Rome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/25/travel/25OSTICA.html', 'snippet': 'Once home to 50,000 residents, this archaeological ruin is just a half-hour outside Rome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once hom