for the annual collector car show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rétromobile, the annual collector car show held in Paris in early February, this year will feature 10 significant French cars from the Mullin Automotive Museum in Oxnard, Calif., many of them having not been exhibited in France since they were new.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Mullin Museum’s French Masterpieces, a Bespoke Homecoming at Rétromobile', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bugatti Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T18:38:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d6fb794-1ba6-5d6c-b7ef-5359f104936d', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d6fb794-1ba6-5d6c-b7ef-5359f104936d'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the 12 best iOS apps for children that came out this year.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/best-apps-for-kids-end-of-year-edition/', 'snippet': 'A look at the 12 best iOS apps for children that came out this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giving your child an iPad or iPod Touch as a gift this year? Preload it with some quality apps before you wrap it. That way you’ll increase your chances for a positive first impression. Here’s a fresh batch of suggestions, arranged from young to old.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Apps for Children – End of Year Edition', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T18:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5d5dc5e-724e-51a6-8ed3-24a1cb609bd0', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5d5dc5e-724e-51a6-8ed3-24a1cb609bd0'}, {'abstract': 'The mother of an Iraq war veteran remembers a Christmas past when her son was at war.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/in-a-hymn-words-of-courage-that-ring-true-long-after-a-soldier-son-returns/', 'snippet': 'The mother of an Iraq war veteran remembers a Christmas past when her son was at war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Christmas cards I’m sending this year feature a photograph of two Border collies and several ducks in a snowbank. The dogs and the ducks appear perfectly at ease and content in each others’ company, and a caption above the picture reads, “And on Earth, Peace.” I love the picture and the reference to Luke 2:14. But, it has occurred to me that the picture might not actually be compatible with its quoted Scripture. Border collies are not, after all, lions who lie down with lambs. Rather, Border collies are defenders of lambs against lions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Hymn, Words of Courage That Ring True Long After a Soldier Son Returns', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T18:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Scott Gallagher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': 'Scott', 'lastname': 'Gallagher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71a1dcb1-bcba-53a1-a842-629a44f264c1', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71a1dcb1-bcba-53a1-a842-629a44f264c1'}, {'abstract': 'Familiar names like Alexandre Desplat,  Howard Shore and last year’s winners, Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross, are eligible for the best-score Oscar, but so are newcomers like Ousepachan, a star of the Malayalam film industry.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/eligible-for-best-score-names-from-hollywood-and-malayalam/', 'snippet': 'Familiar names like Alexandre Desplat,  Howard Shore and last year’s winners, Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross, are eligible for the best-score Oscar, but so are newcomers like Ousepachan, a star of the Malayalam film industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Academy has released its list of scores that are eligible for the Oscar and it includes some familiar names like Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross, Oscar winners last year for “The Social Network” who worked with the filmmaker David Fincher again, on “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo”; and Alexandre Desplat, Oscar-nominated for “The King’s Speech,” represented this year by “Extremely Loud & Incredibly Close,” “Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2” and “The Ides of March.” ', 'source':