type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/your-money/24money-inline/24money-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/your-money/24money-inline/24money-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/your-money/24money-inline/24money-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking a Chance on the Larry Portfolio', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stock Market Returns Without All the Stocks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swedroe, Larry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asset Allocation (Personal Finances)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b391d8b1-a3d7-5fdc-a28a-3a5ef86ed02c', 'word_count': 1502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b391d8b1-a3d7-5fdc-a28a-3a5ef86ed02c'}, {'abstract': 'What was the best meal you had this year? Tweet us at @nytimesdining using the hashtag #bestmeal2011.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/your-best-meal-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'What was the best meal you had this year? Tweet us at @nytimesdining using the hashtag #bestmeal2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we put together our lists of our favorite restaurants of 2011, we’re curious about the best meal you had this year. It could be something as humble as a taco at a truck in Los Angeles, or as grand as a visit to Per Se, or, of course, it can be something you cooked yourself —\xa0great meals come in many forms. Tweet us at @nytimesdining using the hashtag #bestmeal2011. We’ll cull some of the highlights and feature them here next week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Best Meal of 2011', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/675c1487-b608-5054-b15a-ecf0a8866885', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/675c1487-b608-5054-b15a-ecf0a8866885'}, {'abstract': 'Speaker John A. Boehner slammed the door on his highly opinionated House conference on Thursday, but Republicans will have a chance to speak back to their speaker next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/us/politics/obamas-signature-puts-quick-end-to-payoll-tax-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Speaker John A. Boehner slammed the door on his highly opinionated House conference on Thursday, but Republicans will have a chance to speak back to their speaker next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The central conflict that has dogged Speaker John A. Boehner is this: how to answer the hue and cry of the far-right corner of his conference — especially the most conservative of the 87 freshmen who often seem willing to walk to the point of legislative disaster over a point of principle — and actually get things done. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CONGRESS-2/CONGRESS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons Learned in Congress, or a Sign of Things to Come?', 'kicker': 'Congressional Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons Learned, or a Sign of Things to Come?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d01d2662-9cdd-5d30-a7b0-0d6ce3c9a98f', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d01d2662-9cdd-5d30-a7b0-0d6ce3c9a98f'}, {'abstract': 'An advertising company, Kiip, is working with Disney to use a new technology, Swarm, that allows players will compete for high scores on a game and win prizes.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/using-prizes-to-reach-video-game-players-on-their-phones/', 'snippet': 'An advertising company, Kiip, is working with Disney to use a new technology, Swarm, that allows players will compete for high scores on a game and win prizes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Video game devotees are slowly adapting to seeing advertising and marketing woven into their games, either as “pre-roll” before the game starts, as product placement during the game itself, or as an incentive to move to the next level in a game. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Prizes to Reach Video Game Players on Their Phones', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/708651bd-a833-5157-a74f-5f8aa58b5893', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708651bd-a833-5157-a74f-5f8aa58b5893'}, {'abstract': 'Several experts on the markets and behavioral finance weigh in on the year to come and how investors should prepare.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/the-right-investor-behavior-for-2012/', 'snippet': 'Several experts on the markets and behavioral finance weigh in on the year to come and how investors should prepare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Wealth Matters column, Paul Sullivan checks in with several of his favorite experts to see how they think investors should behave in the new year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right Investor Behavior for 2012', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5e36ccd-3ee5-5557-a55c-1dd4a5529492', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5e36ccd-3ee5-5557-a55c-1dd4a5529492'}, {'abstract': 'A courtyard column of a Roman house collapsed on Thursday, the latest in a series of crumbling artifacts at the site.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/another-collapse-at-pompeii-renews-fears-about-its-fate/', 'snippet': 'A courtyard column of a Roman house collapsed on Thursday, the latest in a series of crumbling artifacts at the site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mount Vesuvius preserved the city of Pompeii in ash nearly 2,000 years ago, but current neglect of this Unesco World Heritage site in southern Italy is taking its toll. A courtyard column of a Roman house collapsed on Thursday, the latest in a series of crumbling artifacts at the site, Reuters reported. Last year there were other collapses, including part of what is known as the House of Gladiators. The damage played a role in a no-confidence vote against Culture Minister Sandro Bondi earlier this year. Although Mr. Bondi survived the vote, he ended up resigning in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Collapse at Pompeii Renews Fears About Its Fate', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bondi, Sandro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pompeii (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T19:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89f79c5f-1678-54b2-b558-e9c60cfa7551', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89f79c5f-1678-54b2-b558-e9c60cfa7551'}, {'abstract': 'Subsiding.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/an-inflation-update/', 'snippet': 'Subsiding.', 'lead_paragraph'