t Ron Paul, hoping to slow the momentum that has helped him surpass Mr. Gingrich in some Iowa polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. – Newt Gingrich said Friday that Representative Ron Paul of Texas had to answer for political newsletters that included racist, antigay and anti-Israel passages that Mr. Paul has since disavowed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Criticizes Paul on Newsletters and Foreign Policy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T21:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad40227-471e-5183-8e35-e042a37012b5', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad40227-471e-5183-8e35-e042a37012b5'}, {'abstract': 'While a deal could  yield a significant cash infusion for Yahoo, a transaction may not be finalized for many weeks. It is also unclear whether the board will pursue a separate minority investment from Silver Lake and TPG Capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/yahoo-board-to-pursue-sale-of-asian-assets/', 'snippet': 'While a deal could  yield a significant cash infusion for Yahoo, a transaction may not be finalized for many weeks. It is also unclear whether the board will pursue a separate minority investment from Silver Lake and TPG Capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yahoo‘s board decided on Friday to proceed with negotiations to sell the bulk of its shares in the Alibaba Group and Yahoo Japan to its Asian partners, according to a person with knowledge of the matter. A deal, which involves a complicated asset swap with Alibaba and Softbank, values the holdings at roughly $17 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yahoo Board to Pursue Sale of Asian Assets', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALIBABA.COM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Softbank Mobile Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T21:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec14faf-489b-52fb-92d4-61be3c6407d2', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec14faf-489b-52fb-92d4-61be3c6407d2'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets and Giants are set to meet on Saturday, with both teams needing a victory to bolster their playoff hopes. William C. Rhoden dropped in on both teams this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/football/100000001243678/giants-and-jets-showdown-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets and Giants are set to meet on Saturday, with both teams needing a victory to bolster their playoff hopes. William C. Rhoden dropped in on both teams this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jets and Gi