ifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a277171f-2283-553b-af85-c7348cd7203d', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a277171f-2283-553b-af85-c7348cd7203d'}, {'abstract': 'What to wear when you lift your head from your iThings and have a few friends over for Boxing Day? Experts give their advice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/for-the-hostess-slipping-into-something-a-little-more-practical.html', 'snippet': 'What to wear when you lift your head from your iThings and have a few friends over for Boxing Day? Experts give their advice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHITHER the hostess gown? Archaeological study of this now-defunct garment, popular from the 1930s to the 1970s (according to the Vintage Fashion Guild), reveals that the American lady of the house used to greet her dinner guests not in Lululemon yoga pants and a clammy tank top, but a billowing, brightly colored maxi-dress, often with a forgiving waistline, or no waistline — sort of a cross between an evening formal and a bathrobe. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25HOSTESS/25HOSTESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25HOSTESS/25HOSTESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25HOSTESS/25HOSTESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hostesses Slip Into Something a Little Practical', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hostesses Slip Into Something A Little Practical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ba206af-1ad6-58ef-864e-30b841a64c7f', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ba206af-1ad6-58ef-864e-30b841a64c7f'}, {'abstract': 'When you want more than a colander to make a casserole.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/more-about-spaetzle-makers/', 'snippet': 'When you want more than a colander to make a casserole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To make this week’s casserole, there are several types of spaetzle makers on the market, and though my experience is limited to the two I own, I vastly prefer one over the other. This is the model that I recommend. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More About Spaetzle Makers', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:05:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/608e4eb7-823d-5404-813c-3b475330f446', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/608e4eb7-823d-5404-813c-3b475330f446'}, {'abstract': 'The new 6 Series is quick, attractive and expensive, but the driving experience is so relaxed that its pilot seems to observe the action from a distance.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/reviewing-the-bmw-6-series/', 'snippet': 'The new 6 Series is quick, attractive and expensive, but the driving experience is so relaxed that its pilot seems to observe the action from a distance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich reviews the BMW 6 Series coupe and convertible, a grand tourer that underwent a major redesign for the 2012 model year, its first since the previously dormant series was resurrected in 2004.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the BMW 6 Series', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:09:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b1083d-0648-5325-ace5-2118ad5ba2f2', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b1083d-0648-5325-ace5-2118ad5ba2f2'}, {'abstract': 'Many people don’t sing yuletide carols by the fireplace. But that does not mean they don’t follow their own traditions on Dec. 25.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/on-dec-25-traditions-of-a-different-sort.html', 'snippet': 'Many people don’t sing yuletide carols by the fireplace. But that does not mean they don’t follow their own traditions on Dec. 25.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the backyard, revelers gathered around a vat of boiling oil and counted down from 10. All eyes were on the 12-pound turkey, suspended by a rope. At “One!” the bird plunged into the fryer and everyone cheered.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25UNXMAS_SPAN/25UNXMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 259, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25UNXMAS_SPAN/25UNXMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 259}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25UNXMAS_SPAN/25UNXMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25UNXMAS_SPAN/25UNXMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/25UNXMAS_SPAN/25UNXMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Very Merry Un-Christmas to You', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Very Merry Un-Christmas to You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bruder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7610bbce-df5c-5880-b68f-a545d81f2bec', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7610bbce-df5c-5880-b68f-a545d81f2bec'}, {'abstract': 'A sun-skimming comet provides a cosmic display for NASA solar probes and astronauts.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/after-skirting-the-sun-comet-lovejoy-provides-a-cosmic-show/', 'snippet': 'A sun-skimming comet provides a cosmic display for NASA solar probes and astronauts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several days after newly discovered Comet Lovejoy streaked through the Sun’s atmosphere (see video above), it provided a glorious pre-holiday display for astronauts aboard the International Space Station. NASA has posted an informative description of the comet’s journey and its discovery earlier this month by Tom Lovejoy, an amateur astronomer in Australia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Skirting the Sun, Comet Lovejoy Provides a Cosmic Show', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20087f2c-5206-55b8-8afa-1f176fce5d65', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20087f2c-5206-55b8-8afa-1f176fce5d65'}, {'abstract': 'I have a last-minute addition — just after we finished the issue, I lost my own father, and in the spirit of the readers’ submissions, I offer this brief remembrance.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/23/one-more-life-we-loved/', 'snippet': 'I have a last-minute addition — just after we finished the issue, I lost my own father, and in the spirit of the readers’ submissions, I offer this brief remembrance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this year’s Lives They Lived Issue, we asked readers to send in photographs and short accounts of their own loved ones who died this year. We had no idea how wonderful and inspiring this would turn out to be, and we are so grateful to everyone who participated. Personally, I have a last-minute addition — just after we finished the issue, I lost my father, and in the spirit of the readers’ submissions, I offer this brief remembrance:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One More Life We Loved', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:13:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29ee4b0-8a68-5f34-addf-4e11eae5c456', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29ee4b0-8a68-5f34-addf-4e11eae5c456'}, {'abstract': 'Almost 11 months to