ions that are easing borrowing costs to manage the fallout from a slowdown in China and Europe’s debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russia unexpectedly reduced its benchmark rate on Friday, suggesting that policy makers believed that a global economic slump posed greater risks than inflation to the country, the world’s biggest energy exporter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Unexpectedly Reduces Its Interest Rate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Unexpectedly Reduces Its Interest Rate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ruble (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-23T22:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2096fa54-cc40-5fdc-8741-1719ea631e8a', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2096fa54-cc40-5fdc-8741-1719ea631e8a'}, {'abstract': 'As the offseason trudges on, one fan’s thoughts turn to scripted television appearances by baseball players, from Nolan Ryan to Ken Griffey Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim