lding, offers Italian cuisine, prepared by a chef with impeccable credentials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/il-palio-offers-italian-dishes-prepared-by-a-native-review.html', 'snippet': 'Il Palio, housed in a formidable, white stone building, offers Italian cuisine, prepared by a chef with impeccable credentials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT sounded so intriguing. Margherita Aloi, the daughter of a winemaker and farmer from a small town in the Piedmont region of Italy, who attended the Culinary Institute of Barolo, was chosen by the New York restaurateur Pino Luongo to cook at his new, wildly successful Manhattan restaurant, Le Madri. It was 1989 and she was just 18. Mr. Luongo had the novel idea of staffing Le Madri, which means “the mothers,” with a rotating cadre of Italian women, each cooking her regional specialty. The young Ms. Aloi was hired as the fresh-pasta maker.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINECT1/25DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Cuisine, Guided by a Native', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Shelton', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Cuisine, Guided by a Native', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}],