, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a0d74f3-15d5-5669-a0ca-056e46952430', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a0d74f3-15d5-5669-a0ca-056e46952430'}, {'abstract': 'Wonder Seafood Restaurant in Edison has a sizable menu with meat dishes as well as fish specialties, and staff that maneuvers an endless parade of trolleys and trays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/a-hong-kong-style-cantonese-restaurant-in-nj-review.html', 'snippet': 'Wonder Seafood Restaurant in Edison has a sizable menu with meat dishes as well as fish specialties, and staff that maneuvers an endless parade of trolleys and trays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAD modest expectations of Wonder Seafood Restaurant, which is nondescript in appearance, verging on the utilitarian. Yet on two visits, this Hong Kong-style Cantonese place lived up to its ambitious name — for two very different reasons.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINENJ3/25DINENJ3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINENJ3/25DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25DINENJ3/25DINENJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid the Fish Tanks, 60 Kinds of Dim Sum', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Edison', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid the Fish Tanks, 60 Kinds of Dim Sum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'valu