{'original': 'Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e26327d5-3140-5b96-93e9-8c590c99061d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e26327d5-3140-5b96-93e9-8c590c99061d'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court upheld a criminal fine of about $1.3 million for Trafigura, one of the world’s largest commodity traders, as the result of toxic waste being dumped in the open in Ivory Coast, killing at least 16 people and making thousands sick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/world/europe/court-upholds-fine-against-trafigura-over-toxic-waste-dumping-in-africa.html', 'snippet': 'An appeals court upheld a criminal fine of about $1.3 million for Trafigura, one of the world’s largest commodity traders, as the result of toxic waste being dumped in the open in Ivory Coast, killing at least 16 people and making thousands sick.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Amsterdam appeals court on Friday upheld a criminal fine of 1 million euros, about $1.3 million, for Trafigura, one of the world’s largest commodity traders, for the Dutch portion of an episode that ended with a shipload of toxic waste being dumped in the open in Ivory Coast. At least 16 people were killed and thousands near the dumping areas were sickened, the Ivory Coast government said. The court found Trafigura guilty of concealing the dangerous nature of the sludge, a mix of oil-products waste and caustic chemicals, when its ship, the Probo Koala, delivered its load to the Netherlands in 2006 for treatment and disposal. After deciding it would be cheaper to dispose of the load elsewhere, Trafigura then illegally exported the waste to the Ivory Coast, the court said. The company, which has denied wrongdoing, has paid Ivory Coast a settlement of close to $200 million. A spokesman for the company called the decision disappointing but did not say if the company would appeal to the country’s highest court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Netherlands: Court Upholds Fine for Dumping Waste in Africa', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Netherlands: Court Upholds Fine for Dumping Waste in Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trafigura Beheer BV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ivory Coast', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T02:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdc30f77-318d-5a54-ba15-4422de05ce3b', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdc30f77-318d-5a54-ba15-4422de05ce3b'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers are focusing on making passwords simpler, more secure, even automatic, like a device that can recognize your style of writing or keystroke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/technology/logging-in-with-a-touch-or-a-phrase-anything-but-a-password.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers are focusing on making passwords simpler, more secure, even automatic, like a device that can recognize your style of writing or keystroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Passwords are a pain to remember. What if a quick wiggle of five fingers on a screen could log you in instead? Or speaking a simple phrase?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/business/24passwords4_337/24passwords4_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/business/24passwords4_337/24passwords4_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/business/24passwords4_337/24passwords4_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Logging In With a Touch or a Phrase (Anything but a Password)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Logging In With a Touch or a Phrase (Anything but a Password)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T02:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68385bed-4c8d-533b-8496-060251a00be1', 'word_count': 11