regulators tested whether the product caused the death of a newborn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kroger, Safeway and Walgreen joined retailers removing Enfamil Premium Newborn formula from stores as regulators tested whether the product caused the death of a newborn. Mead Johnson’s stock fell 5.1 percent to $65.29, after plunging 10 percent on Thursday when Walmart pulled the formula. Supervalu also has withdrawn the formula, a spokesman said. Officials screening samples of the formula and water used to prepare it said results might not come until next week. The newborn tested positive for Cronobacter sakazakii, an environmental bacterium that can be fatal. Another child infected with the bacterium in Missouri had also been given formula, though officials said on Friday that the baby, who survived, ingested other types of products as well. The brand of formula given to the second baby was not disclosed. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Retailers Pull Formula From Shelves ', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Retailers Pull Formula From Shelves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infant Formulas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SUPERVALU INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mead Johnson Nutrition Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Safeway Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kroger Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T02:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3804f2ee-0509-556c-a2ac-81d6996c17da', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3804f2ee-0509-556c-a2ac-81d6996c17da'}, {'abstract': 'Avery Johnson, the ever-optimistic coach, will look to the newly acquired big man Mehmet Okur to replace the injured Brook Lopez.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/sports/basketball/as-nets-try-to-fill-hole-avery-johnson-puts-on-happy-face.html', 'snippet': 'Avery Johnson, the ever-optimistic coach, will look to the newly acquired big man Mehmet Okur to replace the injured Brook Lopez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — As Nets Coach Avery Johnson sat down in a chair after practice Friday, a reporter asked him a simple, ice-breaking question: how are you feeling?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/sports/nets-2/nets-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 693, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/sports/nets-2/nets-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/sports/nets-2/nets-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Nets Try to Fill Hole in the Middle, the Coach Puts On a Happy Face', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Nets Try to Fill Hole in the Middle, the Coach Puts On a Happy Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': Non