share many political positions, but they are very frustrated with each other, those who know them say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They fume about each other’s egos, moods and stunts. They have not appeared together at a single news conference all year. Each of their successes, real or perceived, can provoke envy or resentment in the other.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/24tension_337/24tension_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Fume and They Bicker While Running City and State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Fume and They Bicker While Running City and State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum, Thomas Kaplan and Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3866a92f-b693-5884-868a-7c65d93009a9', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3866a92f-b693-5884-868a-7c65d93009a9'}, {'abstract': 'As the end of the year draws near, Crime Scene revisits some of the subjects of past columns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/nyregion/diverging-paths-of-victims-can-hit-dead-ends.html', 'snippet': 'As the end of the year draws near, Crime Scene revisits some of the subjects of past columns.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I would know it,” Esther Davis told me back in May, a few days after thieves had made off with her wrought-iron gate that squeaked open and shut on Vanderbilt Avenue in Brooklyn for almost all of her 53 years. Adding to her frustrations was the fact that the thieves stole a bunch of gates that day; she was one of many victims standing in front of brownstones, shaking their heads. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/JPCRIMESCENE/JPCRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/JPCRIMESCENE/JPCRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/JPCRIMESCENE/JPCRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/JPCRIMESCENE/JPCRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/nyregion/JPCRIMESCENE/JPCRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diverging Paths of Victims Can Hit Dead Ends', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diverging Paths of Victims Can Run Into Dead Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, '