ros, a special agent with the Federal Bureau of Investigation, flew to Nigeria to question an Eritrean man being held on suspicion of supporting terrorism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interview Was ‘Clean,’ F.B.I. Agent Testifies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interview Was ‘Clean,’ F.B.I. Agent Testifies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interrogations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Miranda v Arizona (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Mohamed Ibrahim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6001a94e-7041-5a15-a570-1f11412ae4ce', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6001a94e-7041-5a15-a570-1f11412ae4ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Nassau County Museum of Art is exhibiting about 125 landscapes and streetscapes by Louis Comfort Tiffany, an aesthete best known for his lamps and jewelry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/louis-comfort-tiffanys-paintings-displayed-on-long-island.html', 'snippet': 'The Nassau County Museum of Art is exhibiting about 125 landscapes and streetscapes by Louis Comfort Tiffany, an aesthete best known for his lamps and jewelry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS a teenage aesthete, Louis Comfort Tiffany started making trips abroad to paint in the 1860s, paid for with his inheritance from the family jewelry business. For six decades he regularly took long vacations to sketch. In the Middle East, he painted camel caravans, pyramids and mosque doorways. On trips around America, he set up his easel at Long Island cow pastures, Yellowstone canyons and Pacific Northwest redwoods.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ARTSLI2SPAN/25ARTSLI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ARTSLI2SPAN/25ARTSLI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ARTSLI2SPAN/25ARTSLI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ARTSLI2SPAN/25ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ARTSLI2SPAN/25ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Tiffany, Treasures on Canvas', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From a Tiffany, Treasures on Canvas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nassau County Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tiffany, Louis Comfort', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb51b80-e029-5f25-96e7-e2f87729c08e', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb51b80-e029-5f25-96e7-e2f87729c08e'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on December 24, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/pageoneplus/corrections-december-24.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on December 24, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUSINESS DAY', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 24', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf800a6a-fe9a-5fc2-beca-55a650153a8e', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf800a6a-fe9a-5fc2-beca-55a650153a8e'}, {'abstract': 'Nelson Corporan, 38, has to get up early on Sundays to go to work, smoothing the ice at the skating rink at Rockefeller Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/rockefeller-centers-zamboni-driver-circles-a-hallowed-patch.html', 'snippet': 'Nelson Corporan, 38, has to get up early on Sundays to go to work, smoothing the ice at the skating rink at Rockefeller Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Corporan arrived at Rockefeller Center 20 years ago as a teenager looking for work. Since then, Mr. Corporan, 38, who emigrated from the Dominican Republic at age 15, has been entrusted with perhaps the city’s most cherished stretch of ice: the center’s skating rink. On Christmas Day, as on most Sundays, Mr. Corporan will drive his white Oldsmobile to Midtown before trading it in for a Zamboni. He lives in Washington Heights with his wife, Kamalich, 37, who works in a beauty salon; their children, Brian, 14, and Brianna, 11; and two parrots.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1_SPAN/25ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1_SPAN/25ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1_SPAN/25ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1_SPAN/25ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25ROUTINE1_SPAN/25ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slowly Circling a Hallowed Patch', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slowly Circling a Hallowed Patch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Skating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockefeller Center (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d48624d-0d38-5612-966f-5edb9d187fae', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d48624d-0d38-5612-966f-5edb9d187fae'}, {'abstract': 'Under the ruling, which could interfere with New York’s selling of livery cab permits, the Bloomberg administration must devise a plan to increase the number of accessible taxis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/nyregion/taxi-fleet-in-new-york-is-inadequate-for-wheelchair-users-judge-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Under the ruling, which could interfere with New York’s selling of livery cab permits, the Bloomberg administration must devise a plan to increase the number of accessible taxis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City’s fleet of taxi cabs violates part of the Americans With Disabilities Act by not sufficiently providing for customers who use wheelchairs, a federal judge ruled on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City’s Taxi Fleet Violates Disabilities Act, Judge Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City’s Taxi Fleet Violates Disabilities Act, Judge Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, George B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T03:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b264bf-7dfe-5d53-9342-61dda33d7e7d', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b264bf-7dfe-5d53-9342-61dda33d7e7d'}, {'abstract': 'At Kaffeeklatsch, the pop-up Alpine restaurant at the Standard Hotel’s outdoor rink in the meatpacking district, shrieks are part of the entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/kaffeeklatsch-a-rinkside-cafe.html', 'snippet': 'At Kaffeeklatsch, the pop-up Alpine restaurant at the Standard Hotel’s outdoor rink in the meatpacking district, shrieks are part of the entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madonna was not careening around the outdoor skating rink at the Standard Hotel — she’s more likely to materialize upstairs at the Top of the Standard, the celebrity magnet formerly known as the Boom Boom Room — but she and her ilk are well-represented on the piped-in soundtrack. On a recent Friday night, the mood was festive at the Kaffeeklatsch, the pop-up Alpine snack hut and rinkside cafe, at 848 Washington Street, where the shrieks of amateur skaters skidding, sliding and occasionally going boom, were also part of the entertainment. Admission is $12, rental skates are $3, heat lamps keep the crowd warm, and après-ski couture capped by furry hats is the prevalent attire. Grandma’s hot chocolate is served with a twist: fortifying shots of bourbon, brandy, whiskey and whatnot — Dutch courage for skittish skaters.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ