'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8191df3e-3ec0-5ee2-87bb-a5e4a795c6ad', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8191df3e-3ec0-5ee2-87bb-a5e4a795c6ad'}, {'abstract': 'Inflammatory statements about blacks and gays in newsletters attributed to Ron Paul continued to dog the Texas congressman’s presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/us/politics/gingrich-goes-after-paul-over-newsletters.html', 'snippet': 'Inflammatory statements about blacks and gays in newsletters attributed to Ron Paul continued to dog the Texas congressman’s presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. — Newt Gingrich turned his fire on Representative Ron Paul of Texas on Friday, saying that his Republican opponent had to answer for political and investment newsletters that included racist, anti-gay and anti-Israel passages that Mr. Paul has disavowed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/24/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Paul on the Rise in Iowa, Gingrich Takes Aim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Paul on the Rise in Iowa, Gingrich Takes Aim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T05:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/094d37f7-ad67-5ac9-a8c1-a1a04d104e48', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/094d37f7-ad67-5ac9-a8c1-a1a04d104e48'}, {'abstract': 'The tips given to doormen are an example of the reliance of the city’s economy on a culture of determined generosity, from the absurdities of Wall Street bonuses on down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/nyregion/did-you-give-the-doorman-enough.html', 'snippet': 'The tips given to doormen are an example of the reliance of the city’s economy on a culture of determined generosity, from the absurdities of Wall Street bonuses on down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, New Yorkers fortunate enough to indulge worries over domestic compensation have been besieged with more and more advice and debate every December — from newspapers, magazines, parenting blogs, real-estate blogs — on how much to tip the people who take care of our children, open our doors, adjust our radiators, park our Priuses. And yet there is little to suggest that this mountain of charts and bullet points has eased the tension. What economists cite as the vexing information asymmetries central to these transactions appear to have been rectified hardly at all. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25BIG_75/25BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25BIG_75/25BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/nyregion/25BIG_75/25BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did You Give the Doorman Enough?', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Did You Give The Doorman Enough?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tips and Tipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doormen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T05:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://artic