2-5a83-8639-040123345331'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of the heavily leveraged Mets over the next several years could be required to pay back loans that have the potential to cripple the franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/baseball/for-mets-vast-debt-and-not-a-lot-of-time.html', 'snippet': 'The owners of the heavily leveraged Mets over the next several years could be required to pay back loans that have the potential to cripple the franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The finances of major professional sports teams exist largely as the secrets of privately held companies, except for the community-owned Green Bay Packers, who report their profits without a hint of resistance.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Mets, Vast Debt and Not a Lot of Time', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Mets, Vast Debt And Not a Lot of Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SNY Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:14:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d614b53-ec46-5bd9-83ed-9ec8ac44dbee', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d614b53-ec46-5bd9-83ed-9ec8ac44dbee'}, {'abstract': 'But only if you actually look at the evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/fiscal-policy-works/', 'snippet': 'But only if you actually look at the evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Brad DeLong, there’s a paper by David Romer (pdf) summarizing recent research on fiscal policy, inspired by the crisis and aftermath. And his conclusion is not at all what you hear on the talk shows; it is that there is now overwhelming evidence that fiscal policy does in fact work when it’s not offset by monetary policy. And since we’re now in a liquidity trap in which conventional monetary policy has no traction, that’s the world we’re in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiscal Policy Works', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62559fd4-a76d-5436-96b3-cc0a6553346e', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62559fd4-a76d-5436-96b3-cc0a6553346e'}, {'abstract': 'The inertia that has kept consumers from bolting from traditional content providers is beginning to erode.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/business/media/rules-for-the-new-ways-of-watching-david-carr.html', 'snippet': 'The inertia that has kept consumers from bolting from traditional content providers is beginning to erode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last year, media pundits like me have been running around screaming our heads off about falling skies and collapsing paradigms, and yet as 2011 comes to an end, the sky is still there.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rules for the Ways We Watch', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rules For the Ways We Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f650af2-f24e-5caf-8ffa-2c99730dc215', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f650af2-f24e-5caf-8ffa-2c99730dc215'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Headlam, The Times’s media editor, and David Carr, the Media Equation columnist, discuss a wrinkle that emerged in 2011: There were big changes in how news was produced and consumed, but in the media business itself? No so much.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/the-year-in-media-a-conversation/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Headlam, The Times’s media editor, and David Carr, the Media Equation columnist, discuss a wrinkle that emerged in 2011: There were big changes in how news was produced and consumed, but in the media business itself? No so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The signs of social change were everywhere to see in 2011, and new-media tools were instrumental to that change, whether in Cairo or Lower Manhattan’s Zuccotti Park. But as Bruce Headlam, The Times’s media editor, David Carr, and the Media Equation columnist, discussed this week in a video recap of the year, the business of media didn’t change quite as quickly. But, there’s always next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Media | A Conversation', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Headlam, Bruce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba13755c-2827-5743-88c4-eb0ca1b2baab', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba13755c-2827-5743-88c4-eb0ca1b2baab'}, {'abstract': 'No longer unbeaten, the Packers face the Bears on Sunday night with a banged-up offensive line and a struggling defense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/football/once-beaten-often-doubted-packers-limp-into-game-against-bears.html', 'snippet': 'No longer unbeaten, the Packers face the Bears on Sunday night with a banged-up offensive line and a struggling defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On NBC last Sunday night, Tony Dungy — who led the Indianapolis Colts to a victory in Super Bowl XLI — said that if he were the coach of the Green Bay Packers, “I’d be worried right now.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/packers/packers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/packers/packers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/packers/packers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beaten, and Beaten Up, the Packers Try to Cope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beaten, and Beaten Up, The Packers Try to Cope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Mike (1963- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Huber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f5bdeca-91b8-5a91-adc5-9cc46960312c', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f5bdeca-91b8-5a91-adc5-9cc46960312c'}, {'abstract': 'The American Basketball League survived for only a season and a half, but it was innovative, and gave a future Yankees owner practice in hiring and firing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/basketball/a-basketball-league-where-steinbrenner-and-3-pointers-started.html', 'snippet': 'The American Basketball League survived for only a season and a half, but it was innovative, and gave a future Yankees owner practice in hiring and firing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1961, the N.B.A. was a far cry from the corporate behemoth that finally opens play on Sunday after bickering for months over billions in revenue. The league was 15 years old but still trying to find its way in a landscape dominated by baseball, football, boxing and college sports. That season, the Philadelphia Warriors star Wilt Chamberlain scored 100 points against the Knicks in Hershey, Pa., in front of barely 4,000 people, with no television crew, not even reporters from The Philadelphia Inquirer or any New York newspapers. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-abl-2/dog-abl-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-abl-2/dog-abl-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-abl-2/dog-abl-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-abl-2/dog-abl-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-abl-2/dog-abl-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Basketball League Where Steinbrenner and 3-Pointers Started', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Steinbrenner And 3-Pointers Started', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Basketball League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, Wilt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47802cd1-1411-53ed-a2d6-ec96432a3a8e', 'word_count': 1361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47802cd1-1411-53ed-a2d6-ec96432a3a8e'}, {'abstract': 'The Heat, who returned their three superstars and added players including Shane Battier, say they’re stronger and wiser than the team that fell two playoff wins short.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/basketball/for-miami-heat-high-hopes-but-lower-volume.html', 'snippet': 'The Heat, who returned their three superstars and added players including Shane Battier, say they’re stronger and wiser than the team that fell two playoff wins short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The official restart of the Miami Heat begins on Sunday with far less noise than a year ago, when a team constructed on superstar intrigue evoked breathless predictions and sputtering vitriol in equal measure. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YJPHEAT/YJPHEAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YJPHEAT/YJPHEAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YJPHEAT/YJPHEAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YJPHEAT/YJPHEAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YJPHEAT/YJPHEAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Miami Heat, High Hopes but Lower Volume', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High Hopes and Lower Volume', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Kerasotis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kerasotis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ffaccd6-7cb4-58ee-9391-b583c2942e8a', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ffaccd6-7cb4-58ee-9391-b583c2942e8a'}, {'abstract': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers sound off on the latest headlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Sports Editor: ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'In-Box', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaving a Piece Of His Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vecsey, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayweather, Floyd Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T14:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6fb751f-dfe0-51a4-bb3d-e7a122b54472', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6fb751f-dfe0-51a4-bb3d-e7a122b54472'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A. and its players should commemorate two notable anniversaries: the 50th of the seminal 1961-62 season and the 35th of the rule that created free agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/basketball/nba-should-honor-its-history-and-learn-from-it.html', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A. and its players should commemorate two notable anniversaries: the 50th of the seminal 1961-62 season and the 35th of the rule that created free agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a long and avoidable delay, the N.B.A. finally opens its 2011-12 season Sunday. The new season brings two anniversaries worth noting. One you will probably hear quite a lot about: the 50th anniversary of the 1961-62 season. The other, the 35th anniversary of the Oscar Robertson Rule, maybe not so much. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/bigo/bigo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/bigo/bigo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/bigo/bigo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Should Honor Its History and Learn From It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Should Honor Its History and Learn From It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '