o remain fractured for as long as possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Paul is quite clearly capable of winning the Iowa caucuses. But if Mr. Paul wins Iowa, what happens next?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul’s Influence Doesn’t Just Depend on Him', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T16:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e89fff-2881-59c4-9bf8-0997fbc3578b', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e89fff-2881-59c4-9bf8-0997fbc3578b'}, {'abstract': 'In Brent Clark’s series “Season’s Greetings,” Dec. 25 is an excuse for over-the-top consumerism characterized by excessive decorating, sometimes whimsical, at other times verging on the surreal.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/deconstructing-santa/', 'snippet': 'In Brent Clark’s series “Season’s Greetings,” Dec. 25 is an excuse for over-the-top consumerism characterized by excessive decorating, sometimes whimsical, at other times verging on the surreal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Brent Clark’s series “Season’s Greetings,” Dec. 25 is an excuse for over-the-top consumerism characterized by excessive decorating, sometimes whimsical, at other times verging on the surreal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deconstructing Santa', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T16:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niko Koppel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koppel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9448e59b-8ec8-56ce-8ca0-417889b86d8e', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9448e59b-8ec8-56ce-8ca0-417889b86d8e'}, {'abstract': 'Mel Taub brings on the puns. And the anagrams.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/panda-4/', 'snippet': 'Mel Taub brings on the puns. And the anagrams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — The Puns and Anagrams puzzles by Mel Taub are, to me at least, like a palate cleanser between dinner courses: They are a pleasant, refreshing break in between the Saturday brain-breaker and the big Sunday grid, and I’m kind of fond of them, but I’m glad they don’t come up too often. I don’t believe I’d want to make an entire meal of them. As always, your mileage may vary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Puns and Anagrams', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T17:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d727129-b57c-52dc-91a9-e57b9678c5b0', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d727129-b57c-52dc-91a9-e57b9678c5b0'}, {'abstract': 'After sailing solo around the world, Jessica Watson, 18, is preparing her young crew for a full-blown ocean race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/yacht-racing-sydney-to-hobart-without-an-adult-on-board.html', 'snippet': 'After sailing solo around the world, Jessica Watson, 18, is preparing her young crew for a full-blown ocean race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Spithill was the first Australian helmsman in nearly 30 years to win the America’s Cup, at the helm of BMW Oracle Racing in 2010. He is perhaps the finest match racer in the world, a hard-driving competitor who is quick to embrace the risks that go with maneuvering one rich man’s expensive toy at high speed within arm’s length of another rich man’s expensive toy.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-sailing/dog-sailing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-sailing/dog-sailing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-sailing/dog-sailing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-sailing/dog-sailing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/dog-sailing/dog-sailing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sydney to Hobart With a Teenager at the Helm', 'kicker': 'Special Report: Sydney-Hobart Race', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sydney to Hobart With a Teenager at the Helm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "AMERICA'S CUP", '