tance for tens of thousands of people held in immigration detention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In deciding who may stay and who must leave this country, the deportation process for immigrants tolerates unfairness at every turn. Current laws have denied basic due process protections to people held in immigration detention. And now, a new report in the Cardozo Law Review reveals a severe shortage of competent legal assistance for tens of thousands facing deportation. The study examines cases in New York, but New York is hardly unique in this failing. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deportation Without Representation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Want of a Good Lawyer: Deportation Without Representation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Aid for the Poor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T19:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8005d209-4f74-56c8-824e-11ff77640d86', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8005d209-4f74-56c8-824e-11ff77640d86'}, {'abstract': 'The message of Christmas may be divine, but the work that lies ahead, finding peace on earth and good will toward others, is wholly human.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/opinion/sunday/the-miracle-and-the-means-of-christmas.html', 'snippet': 'The message of Christmas may be divine, but the work that lies ahead, finding peace on earth and good will toward others, is wholly human.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years it would be nice if there really were a Santa Claus. Imagine it. No lists, no shopping, no gift-wrapping, no bills, no shipping costs, an extremely low carbon footprint — and on Christmas morning the miraculous appearance of presents that find just the right balance between desire and a sort of disciplinary justice. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Miracle and the Means', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Miracle and the Means', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T19:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2ed749f-70f6-51e7-8865-6daeab5053b1', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2ed749f-70f6-51e7-8865-6daeab5053b1'}, {'abstract': 'A new study concludes that defendants with court-appointed lawyers often get inadequate counsel and are vulnerable to greater punishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/opinion/sunday/injustice-in-murder-cases.html', 'snippet': 'A new study concludes that defendants with court-appointed lawyers often get inadequate counsel and are vulnerable to greater punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most American counties, some indigent criminal defendants are represented by a public defender, and others by a private court-appointed lawyer. A new RAND study focusing on Philadelphia exposes a vast difference in how clients fare depending on the kind of lawyer they are assigned. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injustice in Murder Cases', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Want of a Good Lawyer: Injustice in Murder Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T19:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/82d7baf1-d1a9-5d21-885e-ec3a08a05ef5', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82d7baf1-d1a9-5d21-885e-ec3a08a05ef5'}, {'abstract': 'The fall of the Soviet government 20 years ago was met with mixed feelings by Russians, who were gaining freedoms but also plunging into a dangerous unknown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/opinion/sunday/when-the-soviet-regime-fell-with-a-whimper.html', 'snippet': 'The fall of the Soviet government 20 years ago was met with mixed feelings by Russians, who were gaining freedoms but also plunging into a dangerous unknown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the evening of Christmas Day 20 years ago, my wife and kids went to Moscow’s Red Square to round out a day of holiday cheer. I had 