ents have fared well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH only a week left in 2011, the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index has a dubious distinction: its performance has been far worse than that of a basic basket of bonds in the last 12 years. But while betting on a large-cap stock index may not have paid off over that time, it would be wrong to assume that this has been the case for all sectors of the market. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Finds of the Lost Decade', 'kicker': 'Fundamentally', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Finds Of the Lost Decade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T20:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL LIM', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LIM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb335a8-2e6f-5578-8e13-06902c857b84', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb335a8-2e6f-5578-8e13-06902c857b84'}, {'abstract': 'David Dischley sees another side of the story after a 180-degree career switch within the same field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/jobs/from-prosecutor-to-defense-lawyer-a-career-switch.html', 'snippet': 'David Dischley sees another side of the story after a 180-degree career switch within the same field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I \u2002DON’T know many people who’ve had one job their whole life. Today, most people change jobs more than once, and usually several times. Maybe they stay in their field, or perhaps they enter a related one. More rarely, they might do something totally different.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/business/25-PRE/25-PRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/business/25-PRE/25-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/business/25-PRE/25-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First a Prosecutor, Now a Defense Lawyer', 'kicker': 'Preoccupations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talk About A Career Switch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T20:09:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Dischley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dischley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c6fc4cd-bedc-592a-be72-db2ef4518a60', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c6fc4cd-bedc-592a-be72-db2ef4518a60'}, {'abstract': 'Hours after the killing of at least eight protesters in Yemen’s capital, Sana, President Ali Abdullah Saleh said he would be leaving soon for the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/world/middleeast/forces-loyal-to-yemens-president-fire-on-protesters.html', 'snippet': 'Hours after the killing of at least eight protesters in Yemen’s capital, Sana, President Ali Abdullah Saleh said he would be leaving soon for the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Government soldiers opened fire on a giant demonstration in Yemen’s capital on Saturday, killing at least nine protesters in the worst violence since President Ali Abdullah Saleh agreed to give up his post more than a month ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/25/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forces Loyal to Yemeni President Fire on Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forces Loyal to Yemeni President Fire on Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Mili