-55cf-8c49-91f404b587d2'}, {'abstract': 'There are 35 city-owned community gardens in San Francisco, including the Brewster/Rutledge, which is better known by two other names: Miller Memorial and Dogpatch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/us/getting-to-know-the-brewster-rutledge-community-garden-in-san-francisco.html', 'snippet': 'There are 35 city-owned community gardens in San Francisco, including the Brewster/Rutledge, which is better known by two other names: Miller Memorial and Dogpatch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The east slope of Bernal Hill, which was settled in the 1860s by Irish farmers and dairy ranchers, has stayed true to its roots and now has an abundance of community gardens utilizing the steep hillsides, including this 8,750-square-foot spot. There are 35 city-owned community gardens in San Francisco, overseen by the Parks and Recreation Department and run by volunteers.  LOUISE RAFKIN', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/us/25BCINTEL/25BCINTEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/us/25BCINTEL/25BCINTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/us/25BCINTEL/25BCINTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brewster/ Rutledge Garden', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen | Local Intelligence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brewster/ Rutledge Garden: Bernal Hill, San Francisco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T23:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Rafkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a4758e0-290b-5192-9d04-6eba4e566aa0', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a4758e0-290b-5192-9d04-6eba4e566aa0'}, {'abstract': 'A political stalemate in Washington had threatened to derail the president’s annual Christmas holiday in Hawaii.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/us/politics/obama-heads-to-hawaii-after-vacation-suspense.html', 'snippet': 'A political stalemate in Washington had threatened to derail the president’s annual Christmas holiday in Hawaii.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAILUA, Hawaii — For President Obama, simply going on vacation these days seems to demand the theatrics of a Houdini-like escape from the padlocked box of Washington.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Escape to Hawaii, After a Tricky Week in Washington', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Escape to Hawaii, After a Tricky Week in Washington', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-24T23:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'ori