': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/sports/YGIANTS/YGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Are Far From Perfect, but Defense Makes Them Good Enough', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Are Far From Perfect, but Defense Makes Them Good Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuck, Justin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T04:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ab38da-c496-57ba-82b9-30a5c229a80f', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ab38da-c496-57ba-82b9-30a5c229a80f'}, {'abstract': 'Jets Coach Rex Ryan and Giants running back Brandon Jacobs exchanged harsh words as the teams shook hands after the Giants’ victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/sports/football/giants-jacobs-says-jets-ryan-needs-to-shut-up.html', 'snippet': 'Jets Coach Rex Ryan and Giants running back Brandon Jacobs exchanged harsh words as the teams shook hands after the Giants’ victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — After a week of breathless banter and rehashed rhetoric, the back and forth between the Giants and the Jets — which by Friday seemed to border on the nonsensical — ultimately reached a nasty conclusion.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Week of Taunts, Final Word Is Anything but Friendly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Week of Taunts, Final Word Is Anything but Friendly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T04:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f639e4c3-7872-5c68-87c7-54baae794c99', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f639e4c3-7872-5c68-87c7-54baae794c99'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of the Christmas Day game between the Bears and the Packers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/sundays-matchup-bears-at-packers/', 'snippet': 'A preview of the Christmas Day game between the Bears and the Packers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bears (7-7) at Packers (13-1) 8:20 p.m., Eastern; NBCLine: Packers by 13 Packers right tackle Bryan Bulaga (knee) is out. Left tackle Chad Clifton (back) is easing his way back after missing two months; he has been limited in practice and is unlikely to play. The primary backup tackle, Derek Sherrod, is out for the season with a broken leg. Green Bay’s injury situation became so dire in its loss to the Chiefs that T.\uf02eJ. Lang took snaps at right tackle, a position he had never played, even in practice. “It’s next guy up,” Coach Mike McCarthy said of the injuries, which is all well and good, except that the next guy might be Jerry Kramer. Health problems on the line can easily become health problems for Aaron Rodgers, but the Bears have played so badly in the wake of the Jay Cutler-Matt Forte injuries that the Packers could put a cardboard Rodgers cutout in the pocket and it would make little difference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday’s Matchup: Bears at Packers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T04:57:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcfd524b-c224-55a3-a0d0-42a5ae017449', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcfd524b-c224-55a3-a0d0-42a5ae017449'}, {'abstract': 'The couple are both assistant professors at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/andrei-cimpian-joseph-robinson-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The couple are both assistant professors at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrei Cimpian and Joseph Paul Robinson were married Friday in Auburn, N.Y. Florence M. Riley, a town justice of Sennett, N.Y., officiated at the home of Carmela Spoto, Dr. Robinson’s maternal grandmother. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CIMPIANjpg/25CIMPIANjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CIMPIANjpg/25CIMPIANjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CIMPIANjpg/25CIMPIANjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrei Cimpian and Joseph Robinson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Andrei Cimpian, Joseph Robinson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T05:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b36129f-63e9-5089-9fc2-c34de4d2331d', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b36129f-63e9-5089-9fc2-c34de4d2331d'}, {'abstract': 'Years of surprise meetings eventually led to a serious relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/molly-gomolin-david-katz-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'Years of surprise meetings eventually led to a serious relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Molly Elyssa Gomolin and David Benjamin Katz were married by Rabbi Kenneth N. Hain Thursday at Carlyle on the Green in Bethpage, N.Y., with Rabbi Elie Weissman taking part. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25GOMOLIN/25GOMOLIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25GOMOLIN/25GOMOLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25GOMOLIN/25GOMOLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Molly Gomolin and David Katz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Molly Gomolin, David Katz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T05:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vincent M. Mallozzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vincent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57645297-06c7-5f3d-b01d-f3ae70e818e4', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57645297-06c7-5f3d-b01d-f3ae70e818e4'}, {'abstract': 'The bride is an early-childhood teacher in San Francisco; the bridegroom was until May the director of digital advertising for a digital media company there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/alison-christie-joseph-roby-iv-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The bride is an early-childhood teacher in San Francisco; the bridegroom was until May the director of digital advertising for a digital media company there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alison D. Christie and Joseph Roby IV were married Wednesday evening in an outdoor ceremony at the Gulf Stream Golf Club in Gulf Stream, Fla. David C. Tassell, a Florida notary public and a friend of the bride’s parents, officiated. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CHRISTIEjpg/25CHRISTIEjpg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CHRISTIEjpg/25CHRISTIEjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/25/fashion/weddings/25CHRISTIEjpg/25CHRISTIEjpg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alison Christie and Joseph Roby IV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alison Christie, Joseph Roby IV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T05:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86343170-c335-55ed-b252-a84ff4ac120f', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86343170-c335-55ed-b252-a84ff4ac120f'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Andy Reid said, “I’m not sure we’re a team that people necessarily wanted to see get into the playoffs.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/eagles-look-dangerous-but-its-too-late/', 'snippet': 'Coach Andy Reid said, “I’m not sure we’re a team that people necessarily wanted to see get into the playoffs.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m happy for Jason Garrett for having an opportunity to possibly take his football team to the playoffs. And Tom Coughlin. I wish we were there.” Andy Reid, Eagles coach, after his team was knocked out of the playoffs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eagles  Look Dangerous, but It’s Too Late', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Eagles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f74bf3fc-3c33-53b8-8956-87b7c8bd8abe', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f74bf3fc-3c33-53b8-8956-87b7c8bd8abe'}, {'abstract': 'The traditional inauguration of the Christmas season got underway this month in Rome, but travelers can visit vestiges of those early celebrations, and take in a few more ceremonies, after the gifts have been opened.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/rome-for-the-holidays/', 'snippet': 'The traditional inauguration of the Christmas season got underway this month in Rome, but travelers can visit vestiges of those early celebrations, and take in a few more ceremonies, after the gifts have been opened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The traditional inauguration of the Christmas season got underway early this month in Rome, but travelers can visit vestiges of those early celebrations, and still take in a few more ceremonies, after the gifts have been opened.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rome for the Holidays', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T11:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Parla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dea9052e-5523-57af-9cc7-9bf1393ded57', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dea9052e-5523-57af-9cc7-9bf1393ded57'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets seemed to be the instigators in a week that should have been more about football.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/25/pulling-back-curtain-on-ugliness-of-giants-jets/', 'snippet': 'The Jets seemed to be the instigators in a week that should have been more about football.', 'lead_paragraph': '“They got a big-mouthed coach, a big mouth and a big-bellied coach that talks too much and now it’s finally time to shut up.” Brandon Jacobs, on Rex Ryan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pullin