ual reading since the mass market paperback arrived six decades ago. Will this dislocation destroy the traditional book? Will it doom the traditional independent bookstore? Will Amazon and Apple control the distribution of thought and culture in America? All these questions will be played out imminently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Book Beyond the Book', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T15:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d38066-18b7-564c-a6d4-a63644be3b8f', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d38066-18b7-564c-a6d4-a63644be3b8f'}, {'abstract': 'The three children and the parents of an advertising executive were killed when a predawn fire tore through a Victorian house in a neighborhood overlooking Long Island Sound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/nyregion/house-fire-kills-5-in-stamford.html', 'snippet': 'The three children and the parents of an advertising executive were killed when a predawn fire tore through a Victorian house in a neighborhood overlooking Long Island Sound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STAMFORD, Conn. — The three children and the parents of a well-known advertising executive were killed when a predawn fire tore through the family’s Victorian house in a neighborhood overlooking Long Island Sound.', 'print_se