First, the Knicks Have Just Enough', 'kicker': 'Knicks 106, Celtics 104', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For One Day, the First, the Knicks Have Just Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T20:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/822961fd-3660-562f-b10a-9fb0815a949b', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/822961fd-3660-562f-b10a-9fb0815a949b'}, {'abstract': 'Callixte Mbarushimana was released Friday by the International Criminal Court in the Hague after almost a year in detention and returned to his home base in Paris, the court said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/24/world/the-netherlands-court-releases-rwandan-rebel-leader.html', 'snippet': 'Callixte Mbarushimana was released Friday by the International Criminal Court in the Hague after almost a year in detention and returned to his home base in Paris, the court said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Rwandan rebel leader was released Friday by the International Criminal Court in the Hague after almost a year in detention and returned to his home base in Paris, the court said. Callixte Mbarushimana, a former United Nations computer technician, had faced charges of war crimes and crimes against humanity but pre-trial judges threw out his case last week in a 2-1 decision, saying that the evidence against him was not sufficient to warrant a trial. Prosecutors appealed in vain this week to stop his release, saying he was the main political leader of the violent Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Rwanda. The rebel movement, which operates from a base in the Democratic Republic of Congo, has unleashed a terrorist campaign in the region which thousands of civilians have been raped and killed. He was the first person to be released by the international court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Netherlands: Court Releases Rwandan Rebel Leader', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mbarushimana, Callixte', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T20:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5afd33da-7b2e-5e5e-b8e5-edaa9ed31f87', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5afd33da-7b2e-5e5e-b8e5-edaa9ed31f87'}, {'abstract': '“The X Factor” may have had relatively disappointing ratings in its first season, but the show generated a big payday for Simon Cowell, its creator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/arts/music/42-million-payday-for-simon-cowell.html', 'snippet': '“The X Factor” may have had relatively disappointing ratings in its first season, but the show generated a big payday for Simon Cowell, its creator.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The X Factor” may have had relatively disappointing ratings in its first season, but the show generated a big payday for Simon Cowell, its creator, below. According to corporate filings in Britain Mr. Cowell made about $42 million through a deal with Sony last year that established a joint-venture company for his entertainment businesses, including “The X Factor,” The Guardian of London reported. For its 50-percent share in the company Sony paid about $49 million and turned over its ownership stakes in two of Mr. Cowell’s other entertainment properties. Mr. Cowell received $42 million of that money by handing over the shares of another company under his control. On Thursday, when Melanie Amaro, a 19-year-old from Florida, was crowned the first winner of “The X Factor,” 12.4 million viewers tuned in. That fell short of the 20 million that Mr. Cowell once predicted for the show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$42 Million Payday For Simon Cowell', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$42 Million Payday For Simon Cowell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T21:19:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/de194bdd-1aeb-5113-abfa-31f051878d7c', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de194bdd-1aeb-5113-abfa-31f051878d7c'}, {'abstract': 'The actress and singer Demi Lovato, who sought help last year for an eating disorder, lambasted the Disney Channel, her former employer, on Friday over televised jokes about that condition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/arts/television/demi-lovato-blasts-disney-over-jokes.html', 'snippet': 'The actress and singer Demi Lovato, who sought help last year for an eating disorder, lambasted the Disney Channel, her former employer, on Friday over televised jokes about that condition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actress and singer Demi Lovato, who sought help last year for an eating disorder, criticized the Disney Channel, her former employer, on Friday over televised jokes about that condition. “Eating disorders are not something to joke about,” she wrote on Twitter in all-capital letters after hearing a character on the show “Shake It Up” say, “I could just eat you up, well, if I ate.” Ms. Lovato, right, was the star of the Disney Channel’s “Sonny With a Chance” until the spring, when she told People magazine that being in front of a camera “would make me nervous.” She is now concentrating on a music career. One of her fans told her about a similar comment made on “So Random,” which succeeded “Sonny With a Chance,” and Ms. Lovato shared it with 5.3 million followers. A Twitter account operated by Disney Channel replied to Ms. Lovato two hours later, “We hear you and are pulling both episodes as quickly as possible and re-evaluating them.” The channel’s account added, “It’s NEVER our intention to make light of eating disorders!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demi Lovato Blasts Disney Over Jokes', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Demi Lovato Blasts Disney Over Jokes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disney Channel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovato, Demi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-25T21:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c2c8a8-e5ac-55a5-a923-7f21e4bf156d', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c2c8a8-e5ac-55a5-a923-7f21e4bf156d'}, {'abstract': 'Though Brazil’s biggest bank may not be a household name on Wall Street, its attractions haven’t escaped investors. Itaú Unibanco may scour the globe for acquisitions next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/business/tempting-targets-for-itau-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Though Brazil’s biggest bank may not be a household name on Wall Street, its attractions haven’t escaped investors. Itaú Unibanco may scour the globe for acquisitions next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Itaú Unibanco in Brazil bills itself as “the Global Latin American Bank.” Thing is, it’s not. Or at least, it’s not yet. That may change in the coming year. Itaú’s solid finances, robust market valuation, searing ambitions and a wealth of opportunities from the misfortunes of global rivals make it the bank to watch in 2012.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26Views/26Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tempting Targets for Itaú in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tempting Targets for Itaú in 2012', 'name': None, 'seo': No