to be a quick fix for Fox News after Glenn Beck’s departure last June, but the show has found its footing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/business/media/the-five-rises-on-fox-news-in-glenn-becks-shadow.html', 'snippet': '“The Five,” a panel of five co-hosts who argue about the day’s top stories, seemed to be a quick fix for Fox News after Glenn Beck’s departure last June, but the show has found its footing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Fox News and Glenn Beck broke up in June, the network’s chairman, Roger Ailes, knew he could not put any single man or woman in that 5 p.m. time slot, lest he or she be compared to Mr. Beck or be pummeled in the press if the ratings tumbled.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26jpFox2/26jpFox2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26jpFox2/26jpFox2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26jpFox2/26jpFox2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Beck’s Shadow, Rise of ‘The Five’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Beck’s Shadow, Rise of ‘The Five’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AILES, ROGER E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T01:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b1d3af-9f2f-5a35-a2d2-6665166af937', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b1d3af-9f2f-5a35-a2d2-6665166af937'}, {'abstract': 'A truncated season is under way, but the players association director Billy Hunter says it is too soon to ascertain the labor conflict’s winners and losers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/sports/basketball/billy-hunter-considers-effects-of-nba-lockout.html', 'snippet': 'A truncated season is under way, but the players association director Billy Hunter says it is too soon to ascertain the labor conflict’s winners and losers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reality of the new N.B.A. season is a testament to a simple but profound truth learned the hard way by 435 players during a contentious lockout: progress depends on risk and sacrifice. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo