Sean', 'middlename': 'Patrick', 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cbb79daf-bee9-5afe-8241-19721aa13e20', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cbb79daf-bee9-5afe-8241-19721aa13e20'}, {'abstract': 'Senate leaders in both parties should pass a long overdue bill that would require all passengers on buses to wear seat belts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/opinion/buckling-up-on-buses.html', 'snippet': 'Senate leaders in both parties should pass a long overdue bill that would require all passengers on buses to wear seat belts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The curbside bus industry has become a booming inter-city phenomenon offering cheap fares in hard times — but also a crash fatality rate seven times that of mainline carriers based in terminals, where maintenance and safety checks are more common. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buckle Up on Buses', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buckle Up on Buses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seat Belts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Sherrod', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutchison, Kay Bailey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c182a1c3-9872-52af-bbab-402c848dc4ca', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c182a1c3-9872-52af-bbab-402c848dc4ca'}, {'abstract': 'How many generations does it take to grow a democracy?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/opinion/keller-putins-children.html', 'snippet': 'How many generations does it take to grow a democracy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the waning days of the Soviet Union, I spent a lot of time in a cluster of apartment towers along the Moscow River, contemplating what seemed to me an essential question about the future of our cold-war adversary: Could Russia grow an authentic middle class? Not a privileged class, favored wards of the state, but independent achievers who would be the engine and the evidence of upward mobility.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin’s Children', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin’s Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:25:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb65ee1-cf8a-5356-9053-e7dad14a01a4', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb65ee1-cf8a-5356-9053-e7dad14a01a4'}, {'abstract': 'The E.P.A. just did a very good thing in releasing new rules on mercury and air toxics for power plants. And, of course, Republicans are furious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/opinion/krugman-springtime-for-toxics.html', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A. just did a very good thing in releasing new rules on mercury and air toxics for power plants. And, of course, Republicans are furious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s what I wanted for Christmas: something that would make us both healthier and richer. And since I was just making a wish, why not ask that Americans get smarter, too?', 'print_section': 'A', 