d States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercury (Metal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:27:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/89513ceb-7074-5b0b-a69c-2f6749ec6dd0', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89513ceb-7074-5b0b-a69c-2f6749ec6dd0'}, {'abstract': 'In a season in which the Jets have lost seven games by an average of 14.6 points, it is fair to ask whether they have misjudged their talent and overvalued their players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/sports/football/for-jets-faint-hope-ebbing-glory.html', 'snippet': 'In a season in which the Jets have lost seven games by an average of 14.6 points, it is fair to ask whether they have misjudged their talent and overvalued their players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of his first year with the Jets, Rex Ryan offered what by now has become a familiar refrain — a bold, but incorrect, prediction. He proclaimed their season over after a crushing loss to Atlanta, but fortune smiled on the Jets, who benefited from an improbable confluence of events to make the playoffs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YJETS/YJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YJETS/YJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YJETS/YJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YJETS/YJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/26/sports/YJETS/YJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Jets, Faint Hope and Ebbing Glory', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Jets, Faint Hope and Ebbing Glory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revis, Darrelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b41e3f1-8c92-5cbe-8408-1542c60f1472', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b41e3f1-8c92-5cbe-8408-1542c60f1472'}, {'abstract': 'In a sinister Christmas message, the Anonymous hacking collective penetrated the site of Stratfor and began sending donations from people in its database to diverse charities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/technology/hackers-breach-the-web-site-of-stratfor-global-intelligence.html', 'snippet': 'In a sinister Christmas message, the Anonymous hacking collective penetrated the site of Stratfor and began sending donations from people in its database to diverse charities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the rest of the world engaged in merriment and good cheer, hackers used the holidays to attack a United States research group that puts out a daily newsletter on security issues. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/security/security-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Breach the Web Site of Stratfor Global Intelligence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hackers Breach the Web Site of Stratfor Global Intelligence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f84d30bb-3f4e-5934-8428-b3976b9151dd', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f84d30bb-3f4e-5934-8428-b3976b9151dd'}, {'abstract': 'The amount of data being generated globally increases by 40 percent a year, creating new opportunities for a multitude of software start-ups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/technology/for-start-ups-sorting-the-data-cloud-is-the-next-big-thing.html', 'snippet': 'The amount of data being generated globally increases by 40 percent a year, creating new opportunities for a multitude of software start-ups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The idea of big data goes something like this: In a world of ever-increasing digital connectivity, ever larger mountains of data are produced by our cellphones, computers, digital cameras, RFID readers, smart meters and GPS devices. The huge quantity of data becomes unwieldy and difficult for companies and governments to manage and understand.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26Data/26Data-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26Data/26Data-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/26/business/26Data/26Data-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Start-Ups That Aim at Giants, Sorting the Data Cloud Is the Next Big Thing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Start-Ups That Aim at Giants, Sorting the Data Cloud Is the Next Big Thing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T02:43:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f333803f-18fa-56ca-a518-4e55e578a71b', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f333803f-18fa-56ca-a518-4e55e578a71b'}, {'abstract': 'Mead Johnson Nutrition said it tested the same batch of powdered baby formula as public health authorities, confirming the safety results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/business/baby-formula-is-called-safe.html', 'snippet': 'Mead Johnson Nutrition said it tested the same batch of powdered baby formula as public health authorities, confirming the safety results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mead Johnson Nutrition said on Sunday that tests it conducted on samples of its Enfamil baby formula tied to a Food and Drug Administration investigation found no presence of bacteria. The company called the product safe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baby Formula Is Called Safe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baby Formula Is Called Safe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mead Johnson Nutrition Company', 'ran