'NYT Front Page for 12/26/2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT Front Page for 12/26/2011', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT Front Page for 12/26/2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T04:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/59588c5c-f570-5ca3-abba-fe54dc8f442e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/59588c5c-f570-5ca3-abba-fe54dc8f442e'}, {'abstract': 'Free e-books are available for members of the New York Public Library and can be downloaded remotely.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/e-reader-help-from-new-york-public-library/', 'snippet': 'Free e-books are available for members of the New York Public Library and can be downloaded remotely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anticipating a flood of library patrons who received e-readers as holiday gifts, the New York Public Library will offer a free service for instructing users how to download e-books, library officials said. Free e-books are available for members of the New York Public Library and can be downloaded remotely without a visit to the library. Patrons can visit nypl.org/ebookcentral for instructions on downloading e-books and other digital materials, including video and music. The library will also offer in-person assistance from Jan. 4 to Jan. 13 at the Stephen A. Schwarzman Building and the Mid-Manhattan Library at 455 Fifth Avenue. Nearly 22,000 e-books are available at the New York Public Library, a number that has been growing rapidly along with the widespread adoption of e-readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E-Reader Help From New York Public Library', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None,