a Bit Fancy, but All Relaxed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T14:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19aac222-34d6-5ca7-8acb-a843d2440245', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19aac222-34d6-5ca7-8acb-a843d2440245'}, {'abstract': 'A festive, elegant and easy New Year’s meal.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/how-to-celebrate-at-home/', 'snippet': 'A festive, elegant and easy New Year’s meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many ways to celebrate New Year’s Eve, some pious, some raucous, no doubt everything in between. Festivities take place high above the twinkling city, in humble taverns, and in the street. (And there is always a meditative yoga option for those seeking purity and abstinence.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Celebrate at Home', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T14:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ce1eee-148d-5230-846c-f43facf87eec', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ce1eee-148d-5230-846c-f43facf87eec'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration has decided in principle to allow President Ali Abdullah Saleh to enter the United States for medical treatment, subject to assurances, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/world/middleeast/saleh-yemen-leader-to-be-admitted-into-us-for-medical-care.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration has decided in principle to allow President Ali Abdullah Saleh to enter the United States for medical treatment, subject to assurances, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — The Obama administration has decided in principle to allow the embattled president of Yemen, Ali Abdullah Saleh, to enter the United States for medical treatment, subject to certain assurances, two administration officials said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/world/27yemen1/27yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/27/world/27yemen1/27yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/world/27yemen1/27yemen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/world/27yemen1/27yemen1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/27/world/27yemen1/27yemen1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Path Is Cleared for Yemeni Leader to Get Care in U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Clears Path For Yemen Chief To Get Care Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John O', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T14:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29301d0c-e231-56dc-aef7-478ff651b349', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29301d0c-e231-56dc-aef7-478ff651b349'}, {'abstract': 'Who had high debt and why?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/debt-and-growth-in-the-g7/', 'snippet': 'Who had high debt and why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve written fairly often about the often-cited Reinhart/Rogoff claim that terrible things happen to economic growth if the ratio of debt to GDP exceeds 90 percent. It’s a claim that has been pretty thoroughly debunked – yet it continues to circulate among Very Serious People as a known fact. Anyway, I was looking at some debt data, and thought that it might be useful to look at debt of the major advanced economies since World War II, and see what gets picked out by the 90 percent criterion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt and Growth in the G7', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T14:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09b0eec2-ad6a-5d4f-8154-8b78ff6d10c5', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09b0eec2-ad6a-5d4f-8154-8b78ff6d10c5'}, {'abstract': 'On a dive with “rebreather” technology and in a trip inside a transparent acrylic vehicle,  a scientist encounters new fish species at a surprisingly rapid rate near Cocos Island.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/a-visual-feast-in-an-undersea-twilight-zone/', 'snippet': 'On a dive with “rebreather” technology and in a trip inside a transparent acrylic vehicle,  a scientist encounters new fish species at a surprisingly rapid rate near Cocos Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was an extraordinary day for me. To understand why, it may be useful to explain a bit about my research. Using advanced closed-circuit mixed-gas rebreather technology, my colleagues and I have spent the past two decades traveling the tropical Pacific Ocean to to document life that occurs below the realm of scuba divers. The environment that I focus on — tropical reef habitats at depths of about 200 to 500 feet — has variously been referred to as deep coral reefs, mesophotic coral ecosystems and the coral-reef “Twilight Zone.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Visual Feast in an Undersea Twilight Zone', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Rica', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T15:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard L. Pyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Pyle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be41885-384d-5762-89f5-50720256243e', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be41885-384d-5762-89f5-50720256243e'}, {'abstract': 'At least 20 people were killed in fighting in the rebellious Syrian city of Homs on Monday, as human rights activists urged Arab League observers to visit the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/world/middleeast/as-reports-of-deaths-mount-syria-observers-urged-toward-homs.html', 'snippet': 'At least 20 people were killed in fighting in the rebellious Syrian city of Homs on Monday, as human rights activists urged Arab League observers to visit the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — At least 30 people were killed in fighting in the rebellious Syrian city of Homs on Monday, spurring France to join with residents and opposition figures in urging observers from the Arab 