ultimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel Craig to Politicians: I Do Not Want to Be Your Friend', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bond, James (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Men's Journal", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T17:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4425d2ac-c285-53f4-a707-e0c4c08b214c', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4425d2ac-c285-53f4-a707-e0c4c08b214c'}, {'abstract': 'Humble though they are, beans, lentils and greens conjure prosperity in many cultures. Add in fish, and you have a variety of appealing and healthful ways to set the table for good fortune.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/health/nutrition/lucky-foods-to-ring-in-the-new-year-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Humble though they are, beans, lentils and greens conjure prosperity in many cultures. Add in fish, and you have a variety of appealing and healthful ways to set the table for good fortune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love the fact that beans, lentils and greens symbolize prosperity in the New Year in places as disparate as the American South and the South of France. I wonder if it’s really because lentils and beans are round like coins and swell when they cook, or if it’s because that’s about all anybody can afford to eat after the excesses of the holiday season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia