al disorder called prosopagnosia. She cannot recognize human faces, and even close friends and relatives can look unfamiliar to her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/health/100000000958226/faceless.html', 'snippet': 'Dori Frame has a neurological disorder called prosopagnosia. She cannot recognize human faces, and even close friends and relatives can look unfamiliar to her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dori Frame has a neurological disorder called prosopagnosia. She cannot recognize human faces, and even close friends and relatives can look unfamiliar to her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/science/video-faceblind/video-faceblind-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/08/01/science/video-faceblind/video-faceblind-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/01/science/video-faceblind/video-faceblind-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/08/01/science/video-faceblind/video-faceblind-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Faceless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T19:51:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'Almudena Toral', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Almudena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toral', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '