ew You? Change Your Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simone, Nina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-26T23:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Simone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e2c863-5d7c-5f5b-bbab-c3630544f9f7', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e2c863-5d7c-5f5b-bbab-c3630544f9f7'}, {'abstract': 'Defenseman Marc Staal, who continues to recover from a concussion after a hit by his brother Eric on Feb. 22, was cleared for contact and took hits during the Rangers’ practice Monday at Madison Square Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/rangers-staal-still-battling-concussion-is-cleared-for-contact/', 'snippet': 'Defenseman Marc Staal, who continues to recover from a concussion after a hit by his brother Eric on Feb. 22, was cleared for contact and took hits during the Rangers’ practice Monday at Madison Square Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defenseman Marc Staal, who continues to recover from a concussion after a clean, but vicious, hit by his brother Eric on Feb. 22, was cleared for contact and took hits during the Rangers’ practice Monday at Madison Square Garden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers’ Staal, Still Battling Concussion, Is Cleared for Contact', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T00:12:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81b55bf6-0f75-5cf7-adc1-3173aae37f7a', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81b55bf6-0f75-5cf7-adc1-3173aae37f7a'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration used to like to compare today’s problems to those that led to the Great Depression. But they differ in many ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/opinion/brooks-midlife-crisis-economics.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration used to like to compare today’s problems to those that led to the Great Depression. But they differ in many ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The members of the Obama administration have many fine talents, but making adept historical analogies may not be among them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,