/article/6dbfe448-3c78-5a6d-9e71-7d4ed080cb3b'}, {'abstract': 'On Jan. 24, the Transportation Department will enforce a rule requiring that any advertised price for air travel include all taxes and government fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/business/airfares-in-ads-soon-must-include-taxes-and-fees.html', 'snippet': 'On Jan. 24, the Transportation Department will enforce a rule requiring that any advertised price for air travel include all taxes and government fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advertisements that make airfares seem enticingly low will soon lose that asterisk pointing to a dense paragraph of additional taxes and fees that make a cheap ticket much more costly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/business/FARES/FARES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/business/FARES/FARES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/27/business/FARES/FARES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airfares With Less Fine Print', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airfares With Less Fine Print', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T01:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec89897-eeb6-5b86-9a94-2afb74d5ab35', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec89897-eeb6-5b86-9a94-2afb74d5ab35'}, {'abstract': 'Congress needs to amend the law that created the investor visa to tighten the rules on what qualifies as a high-unemployment area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/opinion/million-dollar-investor-visas.html', 'snippet': 'Congress needs to amend the law that created the investor visa to tighten the rules on what qualifies as a high-unemployment area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government’s investor visa, created in 1990, gives foreigners a chance at green cards if they invest $1 million to build a business in the United States that creates at least 10 jobs. Investing in an area with high unemployment would cut that price in half. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Million-Dollar Visas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Million-Dollar Visas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T01:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea632e54-bc2e-58b6-8b98-3f49c542ab0f', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea632e54-bc2e-58b6-8b98-3f49c542ab0f'}, {'abstract': 'Easy-to-understand disclosure forms for opening a checking account should become the banking industry standard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/opinion/clearer-checking-account-terms.html', 'snippet': 'Easy-to-understand disclosure forms for opening a checking account should become the banking industry standard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumer advocates are rightly pressuring the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau to require banks to disclose important terms on checking accounts like the monthly fee in easy-to-understand forms. JPMorgan Chase has voluntarily adopted a new, straightforward disclosure policy. Other banks that have been resisting this policy should follow Chase’s lead. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clearer Bank Account Terms', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clearer Bank Account Terms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Checks and Checking Accounts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}],