, 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/27/arts/GELLER1-obit/GELLER1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/arts/GELLER1-obit/GELLER1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/27/arts/GELLER1-obit/GELLER1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/27/arts/GELLER1-obit/GELLER1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrew Geller, Modernist Architect, Is Dead at 87', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Andrew Geller, 87, Modernist Architect, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geller, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T02:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/abae6985-d3a4-5e74-b0e9-f527dada1cd2', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abae6985-d3a4-5e74-b0e9-f527dada1cd2'}, {'abstract': 'Rarely has the financial divide appeared so wide, or the public contrast so stark, between lawmakers and those they represent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/us/politics/economic-slide-took-a-detour-at-capitol-hill.html', 'snippet': 'Rarely has the financial divide appeared so wide, or the public contrast so stark, between lawmakers and those they represent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Representative Ed Pastor was first elected to Congress two decades ago, he was comfortably ensconced in the middle class. Mr. Pastor, a Democrat from Arizona, held $100,000 or so in savings accounts in the mid-1990s and had a retirement pension, but like many Americans, he also owed the banks nearly as much in loans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Downturn Took a Detour at Capitol Hill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Slide Took a Detour At Capitol Hill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Responsive Politics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T02:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd70a975-7bab-5270-8dc7-2302c9a91527', 'word_count': 1859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd70a975-7bab-5270-8dc7-2302c9a91527'}, {'abstract': 'It is unclear whether the latest twist on this account will damage Mr. Gingrich, who has been married three times, with voters.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/26/documents-appear-to-contradict-gingrichs-account-of-first-divorce/', 'snippet': 'It is unclear whether the latest twist on this account will damage Mr. Gingrich, who has been married three times, with voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New court documents that have emerged seem to contradict Newt Gingrich’s account of how his first marriage ended. On his campaign Web site, under the heading “Answering the Attacks,’’ the Gingrich campaign maintains that it was his first wife, Jackie Battley Gingrich, the mother of the couple’s two daughters, who sought a divorce in 1980. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documents Appear to Contradict Gingrich’s Account of First Divorce', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T02:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat