ons and focus on its core insurance business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/metlife-to-sell-bank-unit-to-ge-capital/', 'snippet': 'MetLife announced on Tuesday that it had agreed sell the bulk of its retail deposits business to GE Capital, as it seeks to trim its operations and focus on its core insurance business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MetLife announced on Tuesday that it had agreed to sell the bulk of its retail bank deposits business to GE Capital, as it seeks to focus on its core insurance business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MetLife to Sell Bank Unit to GE Capital', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GE Capital Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T15:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ad3a856-10d4-5841-9934-dff821bbdf48', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ad3a856-10d4-5841-9934-dff821bbdf48'}, {'abstract': 'A new guide by a Bronx lawyer has 6,600 topical entries, directing students of the Talmud to specific passages, laws or topics they are studying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/nyregion/an-index-for-the-talmud-after-1500-years.html', 'snippet': 'A new guide by a Bronx lawyer has 6,600 topical entries, directing students of the Talmud to specific passages, laws or topics they are studying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Talmud is a formidable body of work: 63 volumes of rabbinical discourse and disputation that form Judaism’s central scripture after the Torah. It has been around for 1,500 years and is studied every day by tens of thousands of Jews. But trying to navigate through its coiling labyrinth can be enormously difficult because the one thing this monumental work lacks is a widely accepted and accessible index. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/nyregion/TALMUD2/TALMUD2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/nyregion/TALMUD2/TALMUD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/nyregion/TALMUD2/TALMUD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After 1,500 Years, an Index to the Talmud’s Labyrinths, With Roots in the Bronx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 1,500 Years, an Index to the Talmud’s Labyrinths, With Roots in the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Talmud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indexers and Indexing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22cfb0d4-2ef4-54fc-ab4c-a35da35aba06', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22cfb0d4-2ef4-54fc-ab4c-a35da35aba06'}, {'abstract': 'The paper’s longtime design director, Tom Bodkin, was promoted to deputy managing editor, the latest change to the masthead since Jill Abramson became executive editor in September.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/times-names-new-deputy-managing-editor/', 'snippet': 'The paper’s longtime design director, Tom Bodkin, was promoted to deputy managing editor, the latest change to the masthead since Jill Abramson became executive editor in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times said Tuesday that it was promoting its longtime design director, Tom Bodkin, to deputy managing editor, the latest change to the masthead since Jill Abramson took over as executive editor in September.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times Names a New Deputy Managing Editor', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMSON, JILL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bodkin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e3ad3cb-36e3-5341-a506-20c3e3812179', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e3ad3cb-36e3-5341-a506-20c3e3812179'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/america-is-not-exceptional/', 'snippet': 'When it comes to interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uh-oh — Mitt Romney is going to go after me. Maybe I’d better get out of the country and start an apology tour …', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America Is Not Exceptional', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:07:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecab1aaa-c3b4-5571-838b-ae6c034e746c', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecab1aaa-c3b4-5571-838b-ae6c034e746c'}, {'abstract': 'In middle childhood the brain is at its peak for learning — but that doesn’t mean we need to sign our children up for everything.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/middle-childhood-is-peak-time-for-learning/', 'snippet': 'In middle childhood the brain is at its peak for learning — but that doesn’t mean we need to sign our children up for everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents have long loved “middle childhood,” that period from the end of toddlerhood to the teens. In the past in this country, and even now in many remote or agricultural societies, middle childhood marked the moment when children became useful; for modern, Western parents, it marks the time when children become truly fun (and easier) to have around.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Middle Childhood Is Peak Time for Learning', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dda0558-0e85-58ae-8846-37d2a28bc275', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dda0558-0e85-58ae-8846-37d2a28bc275'}, {'abstract': 'Drew Brees broke Dan Marino’s season passing record Sunday night, but the Saints ran up the score on the rival Atlanta Falcons along the way and might have also broken some sportsmanship etiquette.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/leading-off-saints-had-eye-on-record-and-little-else/', 'snippet': 'Drew Brees broke Dan Marino’s season passing record Sunday night, but the Saints ran up the score on the rival Atlanta Falcons along the way and might have also broken some sportsmanship etiquette.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miami Dolphins, past and present, have been taking their knocks. They lost the first seven games of the season, their starting quarterback and eventually their coach, Tony Sparano. The Green Bay Packers fell short of duplicating the 1972 squad’s perfect season, but now another of the Dolphins’ lifetime achievements, Dan Marino’s single-season passing record, has fallen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off — Saints Had Eye on Record, and Little Else', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brees, Drew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Dan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Mercury', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payton, Sean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Athletics', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/340b3c1a-f79f-50f2-8cea-c42a1d828b81', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/340b3c1a-f79f-50f2-8cea-c42a1d828b81'}, {'abstract': 'A match-fixing scandal is exposing corruption within Turkey’s soccer league — and opportunism within Prime Minister Erdogan’s ruling party.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/the-not-so-beautiful-game/', 'snippet': 'A match-fixing scandal is exposing corruption within Turkey’s soccer league — and opportunism within Prime Minister Erdogan’s ruling party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — “Welcome to hell!” was how Istanbul fans once greeted foreign soccer teams. But now it’s Turkey’s top team that finds itself in a small hell of its own making. Not only is a recent match-fixing scandal threatening the country’s premier league, but it has also forced the governing Justice and Development (AK) Party into scoring against itself. The party that was elected in 2002 as the new broom to sweep Turkey clean looks like it’s sweeping dirt under the carpet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Not-So-Beautiful Game', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gul, Abdullah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57627f94-daff-59b2-a8c9-0e84f112d8a5', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57627f94-daff-59b2-a8c9-0e84f112d8a5'}, {'abstract': 'Advances in screening, diagnosis and treatment of colon cancer mean fewer people are dying of the disease today than they were 20 years ago. But black and white patients are not benefiting equally.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/colon-cancer-advances-show-black-white-divide/', 'snippet': 'Advances in screening, diagnosis and treatment of colon cancer mean fewer people are dying of the disease today than they were 20 years ago. But black and white patients are not benefiting equally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advances in screening, diagnosis and treatment of colon cancer mean fewer people are dying of the disease today than they were 20 years ago. But not everyone is benefiting equally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gains in Colon Cancer Show a Racial Gap', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colon and Colorectal Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T16:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac4c4cf1-9e2a-554b-b329-060ccf5429ff', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac4c4cf1-9e2a-554b-b329-060ccf5429ff'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s restaurant critic for much of 2011 lists his favorite new places of the year — a strong one for smart-casual cooking.'