 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:11:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/432bd95a-82a5-5b68-82f6-1a36e9e028ce', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/432bd95a-82a5-5b68-82f6-1a36e9e028ce'}, {'abstract': 'What we can learn from two young adults — both on the autism spectrum — working their way into a happy relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/adult-autistic-and-in-love/', 'snippet': 'What we can learn from two young adults — both on the autism spectrum — working their way into a happy relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents of children on the spectrum spend more time than many parents worrying about what lies in their children’s future. We all worry about jobs, economics, relationships, education — but parents of children with autism worry about those things on a more basic level. For many, it’s not “will my child get a good job” but “will my child be able to hold any job?” Not “will my child have a happy relationship” but “is there any kind of romantic partnership in my child’s future?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adult, Autistic and in Love', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ce8bd5-cb7b-5845-a932-6b6aa25c2c19', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ce8bd5-cb7b-5845-a932-6b6aa25c2c19'}, {'abstract': 'Readers continue to tweet their best meals of the year, with a few themes emerging.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/more-of-your-best-meals-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'Readers continue to tweet their best meals of the year, with a few themes emerging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers continue to tweet their best meals of the year, with a few themes emerging: eye-opening meals encountered on vacation in Italy and Spain, pizza places through the continental United States, and several nods to restaurants like Per Se and Eleven Madison Park (our critics agree). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More of Your Best Meals of 2011', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88e5097e-6d17-56c4-877e-680431b12639', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88e5097e-6d17-56c4-877e-680431b12639'}, {'abstract': 'A tool from the Pew Charitable Trusts lets you see how reordering of bank transactions can cost you more in overdraft fees.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/pew-feature-illustrates-banks-transaction-infractions/', 'snippet': 'A tool from the Pew Charitable Trusts lets you see how reordering of bank transactions can cost you more in overdraft fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An arm of the Pew Charitable Trusts have been gaining some traction with its campaign to get banks to disclose fees associated with checking accounts in clear, simple language. One bank practice that Pew thinks is especially important for banks to clearly explain is the order in which they process transactions, which can affect the number of fees you pay if you overdraw your account.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pew Feature Illustrates Banks’ Transaction Infractions', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Charitable Trusts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52606a4c-11cf-51be-8c13-89c25bb9adc0', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52606a4c-11cf-51be-8c13-89c25bb9adc0'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/27/fashion/1227winterhats.html', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best of readers’ street style for the week of Dec. 19.', 'so