nd most-watched series premiere when it made its debut on Nov. 6.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/amcs-hell-on-wheels-will-keep-rolling-for-second-season/', 'snippet': 'The historical drama, set during the construction of the Transcontinental Railroad, was the network’s second most-watched series premiere when it made its debut on Nov. 6.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though “Hell on Wheels” may not match the ratings-increasing power provided by the undead hordes of its AMC sibling “The Walking Dead,” its own shambolically attired characters will be back for a second season, the cable channel announced on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AMC’s ‘Hell on Wheels’ Will Keep Rolling for Second Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Common', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meaney, Colm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mount, Anson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:31:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f82d2f7d-924c-56a8-aaac-2d844b290098', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f82d2f7d-924c-56a8-aaac-2d844b290098'}, {'abstract': 'This land of natural wonders and warm, friendly cafes is never cheaper or less crowded than in winter.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/warming-up-short-days-and-long-nights-in-iceland/', 'snippet': 'This land of natural wonders and warm, friendly cafes is never cheaper or less crowded than in winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was pitch black at 8:30 a.m. on a frigid Icelandic morning, but at least there was no snow falling. Though cloud cover the night before had scuttled my chance to see the Northern Lights, my plan for a 36-hour road trip from Reykjavik, ending a great four days in Iceland, was in full effect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warming Up Short Days and Long Nights in Iceland', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Reykjavik (Iceland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:53:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fd94c2-2406-5977-9360-1e5bab33bffb', 'word_count': 1515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fd94c2-2406-5977-9360-1e5bab33bffb'}, {'abstract': 'Russian scientists describe their concerns about methane flowing from Arctic Ocean seabeds.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/leaders-of-arctic-methane-project-clarify-climate-concerns/', 'snippet': 'Russian scientists describe their concerns about methane flowing from Arctic Ocean seabeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dec. 29, 9:28 a.m. | Updated below |I’ve been in touch with\xa0Natalia Shakhova\xa0and\xa0Igor Semiletov, the intrepid Russian researchers, based at the International Arctic Research Center in Fairbanks, Alaska, who for more than a decade have been leading\xa0an important international project\xa0analyzing methane plumes rising from the seabed in the shallow Arctic waters spreading north from eastern Siberian shores. (Here’s\xa0video of Shakhova\xa0describing the methane releases and their work.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaders of Arctic Methane Project Clarify Climate Concerns', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC OCEAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Pole', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Siberia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T17:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15c95c7-f332-51ff-acb1-9ff12143a8e5', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15c95c7-f332-51ff-acb1-9ff12143a8e5'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s Baghdad bureau chief, Tim Arango, looks back at the year in Iraq | Steven Erlanger reports from Paris on the challenges 