.com/2011/12/27/house-freshmen-set-voting-record/', 'snippet': 'House freshmen, including those elected in special elections in 2011, on average missed the fewest votes of any class of first-year lawmakers since at least 1990', 'lead_paragraph': 'House freshmen, including those elected in special elections in 2011, on average missed the fewest votes of any class of first-year lawmakers since at least 1990, the earliest that the House of Representatives published electronic voting data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Freshmen Set Voting Record', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T18:11:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/488c8fcd-f3fc-5a20-92d0-033c2241a0a9', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/488c8fcd-f3fc-5a20-92d0-033c2241a0a9'}, {'abstract': 'The arrival of international observers emboldened protesters, who flooded into the streets in the rebellious city of Homs in defiance of a brutal crackdown in recent days.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/videos-show-observers-in-syrian-city-as-protests-swell/', 'snippet': 'The arrival of international observers emboldened protesters, who flooded into the streets in the rebellious city of Homs in defiance of a brutal crackdown in recent days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 5:43 p.m. As our colleague Kareem Fahim reports, Syrian forces cleared tanks from areas of Homs, residents said, as Arab League observers arrived on Tuesday to monitor pledges by the government to end the violence that has gripped the restive city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Observers in Syrian City as Protests Swell', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T18:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c66440-4387-5bf1-bf42-73710d91fc01', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c66440-4387-5bf1-bf42-73710d91fc01'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich has been the target of super PAC ad spending, but now a group supporting him is spending to help him.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/pro-gingrich-group-kicks-off-ad-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich has been the target of super PAC ad spending, but now a group supporting him is spending to help him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBUQUE, Iowa — Newt Gingrich has been aggressively outspent by rivals on television and radio ads that have done serious damage to his standing in polls, especially here in Iowa. But a new independent “super PAC” supporting Mr. Gingrich plans to spend more than $1 million in the next seven days on TV, radio and digital spots, most in Iowa ahead of the Jan. 3 caucuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pro-Gingrich Group Kicks Off Ad Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T18:20:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dd453a9-d91c-54c3-9702-32f43922e48f', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dd453a9-d91c-54c3-9702-32f43922e48f'}, {'abstract': 'When the clock strikes 2 a.m. in Los Angeles, bars close down and clubs stop serving alcohol. Then it is time for the underground parties to begin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/us/after-hour-parties-spread-in-los-angeles.html', 'snippet': 'When the clock strikes 2 a.m. in Los Angeles, bars close down and clubs stop serving alcohol. Then it is time for the underground parties to begin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Getting to this party took commitment. The chosen had to R.S.V.P. early to get on the guest list but were not told where they were going. The address came later, by e-mail: Be at a dimly lighted parking lot just east of the Los Angeles River at 1 a.m. They lined up at a corrugated steel fence, shivering in their furs and leather jackets on the chilly December night. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/us/NIGHTCLUBS/NIGHTCLUBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/us/NIGHTCLUBS/NIGHTCLUBS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/us/NIGHTCLUBS/NIGHTCLUBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/us/NIGHTCLUBS/NIGHTCLUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/us/NIGHTCLUBS/NIGHTCLUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Party Continues, but Those Who Know Are 