as the highest-rated network in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic on Monday night, according to Nielsen data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Against a full slate of repeats on the big four broadcast networks, the Spanish-language network Univision emerged as the highest-rated channel in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic on Monday night, according to Nielsen data. The two-hour finale of the telenovela “La Fuerza del Destino” (“The Strength of Destiny”) averaged 5.4 million total viewers and trailed only a repeat of “Two and a Half Men” on CBS in the 18-to-49 category. Elsewhere, NBC’s new quiz show “Who’s Still Standing?” continued to pull in respectable numbers with its highest viewership total, 6.9 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Univision Finds Ratings Success', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T20:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8207333a-0e8f-5c9e-aad0-9efe8579e9a0', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8207333a-0e8f-5c9e-aad0-9efe8579e9a0'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to persuade undecided voters across Iowa to join his candidacy, Rick Santorum argued that Ron Paul would be a dangerous presidential candidate for the Republican Party and the country.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/santorum-takes-aim-at-paul-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Seeking to persuad