bling.html', 'snippet': 'Real estate developers have begun gobbling up properties in South Florida, hoping the Legislature passes a bill to allow Las Vegas-style casino resorts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — When the Florida Legislature returns from its holiday recess, it will consider a bill to allow three Las Vegas-style casino resorts to be built in the southern part of the state. Lobbyists for the gambling industry have swarmed Tallahassee, trying to ensure that the bill passes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/business/MIAMI1/MIAMI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 979, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/business/MIAMI1/MIAMI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/business/MIAMI1/MIAMI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'South Florida Poised for Birth of Casino Gambling', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Florida Poised for Birth of Casino Gambling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:14:32+0000', 'documen