mbers of its clients and use them to make donations to charity. But by Tuesday, the real goal was not so clear.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/questions-about-motives-behind-stratfor-hack/', 'snippet': 'When hackers attacked Stratfor, a security group, they initially said they were aiming to steal the credit card numbers of its clients and use them to make donations to charity. But by Tuesday, the real goal was not so clear.', 'lead_paragraph': ' When hackers used the Christmas holiday to attack Stratfor, a security group based in Austin, Tex., they initially said they were aiming to steal the credit card numbers of its clients and use them to make $1 million in donations to charity. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions About Motives Behind Stratfor Hack', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Strategic Forecasting Inc (Stratfor)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69bc0b31-524b-5e07-9301-2bc794189d11', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69bc0b31-524b-5e07-9301-2bc794189d11'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich takes on Mitt Romney on economics, Mr. Romney’s central theme.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/gingrich-strikes-economic-themes-in-hitting-romney/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich takes on Mitt Romney on economics, Mr. Romney’s central theme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DYERSVILLE, Iowa — Newt Gingrich introduced a new theme to his sharpening contrast to Mitt Romney: that he was a founder of supply-side economics that brought the country prosperity under Ronald Reagan and can do so again — but not if Mr. Romney is the nominee. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Strikes Economic Themes in Hitting Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemp, Jack F', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e66fc4f3-e94a-5714-92de-c6e630ecb4e0', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e66fc4f3-e94a-5714-92de-c6e630ecb4e0'}, {'abstract': 'Though Woody Guthrie remains a controversial figure in his native state of Oklahoma decades after his death, his archives are getting a new home in Tulsa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/arts/music/woody-guthrie-gets-a-belated-honor-in-oklahoma.html', 'snippet': 'Though Woody Guthrie remains a controversial figure in his native state of Oklahoma decades after his death, his archives are getting a new home in Tulsa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TULSA, Okla. — Oklahoma has always had a troubled relationship with her native son Woody Guthrie. The communist sympathies of America’s balladeer infuriated local detractors. In 1999 a wealthy donor’s objections forced the Cowboy Museum in Oklahoma City to cancel a planned exhibition on Guthrie organized by the Smithsonian Institution. It wasn’t until 2006, nearly four decades after his death, that the Oklahoma Hall of Fame got around to adding him to its ranks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/guthrie-1/guthrie-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 865, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/guthrie-1/guthrie-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/guthrie-1/guthrie-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bound for Local Glory at Last', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bound for Local Glory at Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Woody', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:39:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfedbe65-b549-57d0-8f65-1645ad5755d0', 'word_count': 1327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfedbe65-b549-57d0-8f65-1645ad5755d0'}, {'abstract': 'The 1982 farce “Le Père Noël Est une Ordure” presents two social-services hot-line employees who do more harm than good for their distressed clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/movies/a-crude-rude-christmas-tale.html', 'snippet': 'The 1982 farce “Le Père Noël Est une Ordure” presents two social-services hot-line employees who do more harm than good for their distressed clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to Christmas movies, the French prefer naughty over nice any day. “Le Père Noël Est une Ordure” (whose literal translation would make George Bailey blush, so “Santa Stinks” will have to do), a much-loved 1982 farce finally having its American theatrical premiere at the Museum of Modern Art, is a fine example. Crude, rude and with more foul language than a Gordon Ramsay marathon, this smutty staple could give even the most hardened Francophobe a few guilty giggles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp1/28filmrdp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp1/28filmrdp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp1/28filmrdp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp1/28filmrdp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp1/28filmrdp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crude, Rude Christmas Tale', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Le Père Noël Est Une Ordure'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/291b2cf1-1ab2-5270-824c-ae5ffb59af71', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/291b2cf1-1ab2-5270-824c-ae5ffb59af71'}, {'abstract': 'In “El Sicario, Room 164,”’ a reformed hit man for the Mexican drug cartel regales us with 20 years’ worth of kidnapping, torture and cold-blooded murder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/movies/el-sicario-room-164-by-gianfranco-rosi-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “El Sicario, Room 164,”’ a reformed hit man for the Mexican drug cartel regales us with 20 years’ worth of kidnapping, torture and cold-blooded murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a nondescript motel room somewhere along the border between Mexico and the United States, a former hit man — a “sicario” — for the Mexican drug cartels speaks. Unquestioned and uninterrupted, this black-garbed thug regales us with 20 years’ worth of kidnapping, torture and cold-blooded murder, all the while scribbling compulsively in a large notebook.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp2/28filmrdp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp2/28filmrdp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp2/28filmrdp2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 852, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp2/28filmrdp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/arts/28filmrdp2/28filmrdp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Thug Talks and Talks, and Scribbles', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'El Sicario, Room 164'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-27T23:52:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'fir