s, insurers and employers billions of dollars in the coming years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most widespread medical implant failure in decades — involving thousands of all-metal artificial hips that need to be replaced prematurely — has entered the money phase.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/business/jp-HIPS/jp-HIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/business/jp-HIPS/jp-HIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/business/jp-HIPS/jp-HIPS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/business/jp-HIPS/jp-HIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/business/jp-HIPS/jp-HIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The High Cost of Failing Artificial Hips', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Common Failure Of Hip Implants Brings Big Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T02:29:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73373bed-3e3e-5f40-8adc-f9bfea7aaa14', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73373bed-3e3e-5f40-8adc-f9bfea7aaa14'}, {'abstract': 'Have a question about hip replacement? Join the Q&A with Barry Meier, business health reporter for The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/ask-about-hip-replacement/', 'snippet': 'Have a question about hip replacement? Join the Q&A with Barry Meier, business health reporter for The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The High Price of Failing Artificial Hips,” New York Times reporter Barry Meier examines the economic cost of the most widespread medical device disaster in decades, the premature failure of all-metal replacement hips:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask About Hip Replacement', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T02:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0d8a9e4-1355-55ea-a7d5-a1fca97b4ea1', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0d8a9e4-1355-55ea-a7d5-a1fca97b4ea1'}, {'abstract': 'If Republicans do win the Senate, they could do so in spectacular fashion. There are Democratic seats available in every corner of the country, very few of which are truly safe, creating the potential for a double-digit gain.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/a-snapshot-of-the-race-for-the-senate/', 'snippet': 'If Republicans do win the Senate, they could do so in spectacular fashion. There are Democratic seats available in every corner of the country, very few of which are truly safe, creating the potential for a double-digit gain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The electoral implications of the impending retirement of Senator Ben Nelson of Nebraska are fairly obvious. This is bad news for Democrats, who were already going to have a difficult time holding on to their narrow 53-47 advantage in the upper chamber.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Snapshot of the Race for the Senate', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T02:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc9241a-5f83-5800-ba16-6a4437df5e5d', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc9241a-5f83-5800-ba16-6a4437df5e5d'}, {'abstract': 'In more overt ways than ever, Republican candidates vying for support from Iowa caucusgoers are turning to religious language and imagery in their advertisements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/us/politics/republican-hopefuls-pack-religion-into-ads-in-iowa.html', 'snippet': 'In more overt ways than ever, Republican candidates vying for support from Iowa caucusgoers are turning to religious language and imagery in their advertisements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Ther