mission and Citigroup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/business/court-grants-delay-in-secs-case-against-citigroup.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court will consider an appeal of a lower court’s decision to throw out a $285 million fraud settlement between the commission and Citigroup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A federal appeals court granted an emergency ruling late Tuesday that temporarily halted proceedings in the Securities and Exchange Commission’s case against Citigroup. The decision will allow the court to consider an appeal of a lower court’s decision to throw out a $285 million fraud settlement between the commission and Citigroup.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Wins Delay in Citigroup Fraud Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'S.E.C. Wins Delay in Citigroup Fraud Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T02:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11f58413-9706-5427-9475-a13b6a8a60aa', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11f58413-9706-5427-9475-a13