e': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/72021066-55ab-5f92-ba05-d6cce443a2db', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72021066-55ab-5f92-ba05-d6cce443a2db'}, {'abstract': 'My family would not have survived without the generosity of our guardian angel in North Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/opinion/honoring-all-who-saved-jews.html', 'snippet': 'My family would not have survived without the generosity of our guardian angel in North Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN December 1942, when I was 13 years old, German troops occupied my hometown. Within days, our house was commandeered as an officers’ mess hall. I soon had a yellow star on my dress, setting me apart from many of my childhood friends. The men of our family were ordered into forced labor. My happy life had vanished.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/opinion/28oped-img/28oped-img-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/opinion/28oped-img/28oped-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/opinion/28oped-img/28oped-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring All Who Saved Jews', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honoring All Who Saved Jews', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yad Vashem Holocaust Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T03:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eva Weisel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/90ea5dbe-87af-5b0d-b54a-5470bf43a037', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90ea5dbe-87af-5b0d-b54a-5470bf43a037'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling was the first time since the military takeover in Egypt that a civilian court has attempted to exert judicial authority over the ruling generals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/world/africa/egyptian-court-says-virginity-tests-violated-womens-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling was the first time since the military takeover in Egypt that a civilian court has attempted to exert judicial authority over the ruling generals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — An administrative court ruled Tuesday that the Egyptian military had wrongly violated the human rights of female demonstrators by subjecting them to “virginity tests” intended to humiliate them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court in Egypt Says Rights of Women Were Violated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court in Egypt Says Rights Of Women Were Violated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Afr