t many of them are gaming their way to work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Grand Game of Getting to Work', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Grand Game of Getting to Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T04:05:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/375bb0ac-c06c-596e-8f17-148c3db98a76', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/375bb0ac-c06c-596e-8f17-148c3db98a76'}, {'abstract': 'Northeastern University, based in Boston, opened its first satellite campus, which combines virtual and in-person instruction, this year in Charlotte, N.C. Seattle is next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/education/northeastern-university-expands-its-geographic-reach.html', 'snippet': 'Northeastern University, based in Boston, opened its first satellite campus, which combines virtual and in-person instruction, this year in Charlotte, N.C. Seattle is next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a century firmly anchored in Boston, Northeastern University is branching out — becoming Southeastern, Northwestern and perhaps Western and Midwestern as well.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't