n-a-candidate/', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. candidates are focusing on the economy, but Iowa is doing just fine. So what are voters there looking for?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do Iowans Want in a Candidate?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T04:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b926d31-c4d4-5f0e-a99c-3c2fc7ae0a3b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b926d31-c4d4-5f0e-a99c-3c2fc7ae0a3b'}, {'abstract': 'One good idea each from the seven Republican presidential candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/27/getting-it-right/', 'snippet': 'One good idea each from the seven Republican presidential candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dissatisfaction and disappointment have pervaded the Republican presidential campaign. Pundits pining for a game-changing candidate have been repeatedly let down, and voters have pinballed from one unsatisfactory option to another, with infatuation giving way to disillusionment every time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting It Right', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', '