1822-7a0d-59fd-ba98-ebb147399c54', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3b371822-7a0d-59fd-ba98-ebb147399c54'}, {'abstract': 'The exercise routines and diets of Janice and Adam Bridges, who have lost about 165 and 110 pounds and struggle daily to keep the weight off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/01/magazine/bridges-daily-routine.html', 'snippet': 'The exercise routines and diets of Janice and Adam Bridges, who have lost about 165 and 110 pounds and struggle daily to keep the weight off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The exercise routines and diets of Janice and Adam Bridges, who have lost about 165 and 110 pounds and struggle daily to keep the weight off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M/bridges-daily-routine-slide-MP0M-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day With the Bridges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b4f05671-a9c6-5e3f-bc93-0228c5eb224f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b4f05671-a9c6-5e3f-bc93-0228c5eb224f'}, {'abstract': 'In the battle to lose weight, and keep it off, our bodies are fighting against us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/magazine/tara-parker-pope-fat-trap.html', 'snippet': 'In the battle to lose weight, and keep it off, our bodies are fighting against us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 15 years, Joseph Proietto has been helping people lose weight. When these obese patients arrive at his weight-loss clinic in Australia, they are determined to slim down. And most of the time, he says, they do just that, sticking to the clinic’s program and dropping excess pounds. But then, almost without exception, the weight begins to creep back. In a matter of months or years, the entire effort has come undone, and the patient is fat again. “It has always seemed strange to me,” says Proietto, who is a physician at the University of Melbourne. “These are people who are very motivated to lose weight, who achieve weight loss most of the time without too much trouble and yet, inevitably, gradually, they regain the weight.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/01cover/01cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 843, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/01cover/01cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/magazine/01cover/01cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fat Trap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fat Trap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72732431-16c2-5545-b9f7-62d91c3c503b', 'word_count': 5573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72732431-16c2-5545-b9f7-62d91c3c503b'}, {'abstract': 'Some people feel Victor Cruz was snubbed in the Pro Bowl voting, which shows how wildy he has exceeded expectations this season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/victor-cruz-pro-bowl-and-paterson-n-j/', 'snippet': 'Some people feel Victor Cruz was snubbed in the Pro Bowl voting, which shows how wildy he has exceeded expectations this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six points from around the Web, with an extra point from the Fifth Down:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victor Cruz, Pro Bowl and Paterson, N.J.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:13:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d51abfe-7458-5b1b-8854-f9ceb1e24da9', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d51abfe-7458-5b1b-8854-f9ceb1e24da9'}, {'abstract': 'Spending a day watching to how the crowds react can be just as instructive as listening to the candidates themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/what-moves-republican-crowds-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Spending a day watching to how the crowds react can be just as instructive as listening to the candidates themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — The Republican candidates for president are doing a lot of talking in the last week before voting begins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Moves Republican Crowds in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8b7068-bf50-5076-8a83-ee758a3f03c2', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8b7068-bf50-5076-8a83-ee758a3f03c2'}, {'abstract': 'Among pollsters there is debate about whether  polls conducted between Christmas and New Year’s Day are reliable.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/are-polls-during-the-holidays-less-reliable/', 'snippet': 'Among pollsters there is debate about whether  polls conducted between Christmas and New Year’s Day are reliable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iowa caucuses are six days away, and the latest polls were more than a week ago — a lifetime when opinions are so volatile. Later this week, fresh surveys of Iowan Republicans may be released, but those occurred during the holiday week, when voters are hard to reach and distracted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Polls During the Holidays Less Reliable?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zukin, Cliff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:32:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e3552d9-6ff7-5c7a-8989-8142877a6951', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e3552d9-6ff7-5c7a-8989-8142877a6951'}, {'abstract': 'Even though the author quickly spotted hammerhead sharks on a dive off Cocos Island, the species used to be far more plentiful. Conservationists mainly blame shark fishing, although some unusual climatic factors have sporadically reduced their presence.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/a-parade-of-sharks-lively-yet-diminished/', 'snippet': 'Even though the author quickly spotted hammerhead sharks on a dive off Cocos Island, the species used to be far more plentiful. Conservationists mainly blame shark fishing, although some unusual climatic factors have sporadically reduced their pre...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cocos Island is perhaps best known for an abundance of large marine animals, sharks in particular. Most iconic of these are the vast schools of scalloped hammerhead sharks, which can be found by the hundreds at various sites in the waters around the island. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parade of Sharks, Dazzling Yet Diminished', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tidal Waves and Tsunamis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Rica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:36:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard L. Pyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Pyle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e184acf2-e6eb-54cf-83e2-adf41f38c9d0', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e184acf2-e6eb-54cf-83e2-adf41f38c9d0'}, {'abstract': 'All saved up with nowhere to go.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/the-problem-2/', 'snippet': 'All saved up with nowhere to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Koo has another paper on balance sheet recession out (pdf), with good charts for a number of countries. I still have some differences with him over monetary policy — I still don’t understand why he doesn’t see debt-eroding inflation as something helpful in dealing with debt overhang — but his view of the sources of our Lesser Depression is completely right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Problem', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T13:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/541e7392-1632-572c-920f-848b42f18f94', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/541e7392-1632-572c-920f-848b42f18f94'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Jong-il’s funeral procession took place on Wednesday in Pyongyang, North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/28/world/asia/20111228_FUNERAL600.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Jong-il’s funeral procession took place on Wednesday in Pyongyang, North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kim Jong-il’s funeral procession took place on Wednesday in Pyongyang, North Korea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/world/asia/20111228_FUNERAL-slide-28WI/20111228_FUNERAL-slide-28WI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/world/asia/20111228_FUNERAL-slide-28WI/20111228_FUNERAL-slide-28WI-article