ael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e57be854-2f68-5fe2-b4fc-e80492a83553', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e57be854-2f68-5fe2-b4fc-e80492a83553'}, {'abstract': 'In “Tom the Tamer,” an inventive young boy helps his father overcome a fear of the great outdoors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/books/tom-the-tamer-by-tjibbe-veldkamp-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Tom the Tamer,” an inventive young boy helps his father overcome a fear of the great outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Generally speaking, children like their parents to be all-knowing and to fear nothing — they want them to be paragons of authority, capability and calm. Nonetheless, it can be hugely satisfying, reassuring even, to see Mom shriek at the sight of a mouse or Dad throw a tantrum over a traffic jam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/books/28tamer-1/28tamer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/28/books/28tamer-1/28tamer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/books/28tamer-1/28tamer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/books/28tamer-1/28tamer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/books/28tamer-1/28tamer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 