ype': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6822ccb5-094d-5980-8d53-51db20b50ca5', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6822ccb5-094d-5980-8d53-51db20b50ca5'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing instructs in the art of efficient travel like following a campaigning presidential candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/travel/tips-from-political-reporters.html', 'snippet': 'Nothing instructs in the art of efficient travel like following a campaigning presidential candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRAVEL is one of the great perks of being a journalist — over the years, my job has taken me to places like Los Angeles, Paris and Saudi Arabia. But when I began covering Mitt Romney’s presidential bid five months ago as a member of The New York Times political team, I suddenly found myself shuffling through airport security several times a week. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/travel/0101PRAC1/0101PRAC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 260, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/23/travel/0101PRAC1/0101PRAC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 260}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/travel/0101PRAC1/0101PRAC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/23/travel/0101PRAC1/0101PRAC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/23/travel/0101PRAC1/0101PRAC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Insider Travel Tips From Campaign Reporters', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Them to the Debate on Time: Reporters’ Tips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T16:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/506810af-46bc-55fe-bd9a-e0c7b348fc6f', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/506810af-46bc-55fe-bd9a-e0c7b348fc6f'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Federation of America has published a new guide to filing an auto insurance claim, written by someone who used to work in the industry.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/how-to-file-an-auto-insurance-claim/', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Federation of America has published a new guide to filing an auto insurance claim, written by someone who used to work in the industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Consumer Federation of America estimates that more than 325,000 auto accidents will occur during this year’s holiday travel period, resulting in more than 200,000 claims filed with the nation’s insurance companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to File an Auto Insurance Claim', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Federation of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T16:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8293afc6-1301-5c9e-b94d-76eb434b3867', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8293afc6-1301-5c9e-b94d-76eb434b3867'}, {'abstract': 'The complete video of an Israeli television report on a young girl who was harassed by ultra-Orthodox men for not being dressed modestly enough.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/the-israeli-tv-report-on-gender-segregation-that-sparked-protest/', 'snippet': 'The complete video of an Israeli television report on a young girl who was harassed by ultra-Orthodox men for not being dressed modestly enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Isabel Kershner explains, an Israeli television report on a girl who was harassed by ultra-Orthodox men for not being dressed modestly enough sparked a protest against gender segregation on Tuesday night in the town on Beit Shemesh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Israeli TV Report on Gender Segregation That Sparked Protest', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hasidism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T16:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74fee080-3e0e-5309-a227-90075c8a21c5', 'word_count': 2118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74fee080-3e0e-5309-a227-90075c8a21c5'}, {'abstract': 'Beyond the legal questions in a copyright infringement lawsuit involving the artist Richard Prince, the case asks if the flow of creative expression, riding a tide of instantly accessible digital images, can be slowed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/arts/design/richard-prince-lawsuit-focuses-on-limits-of-appropriation.html', 'snippet': 'Beyond the legal questions in a copyright infringement lawsuit involving the artist Richard Prince, the case asks if the flow of creative expression, riding a tide of instantly accessible digital images, can be slowed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE recent afternoon in the offices of the Midtown law firm run by David Boies and his powerful litigation partners, a large black clamshell box sat on a conference table. Inside were raucous, sometimes wildly funny collages of photographs and magazine pages handmade by the artist Richard Prince, works of art that have become the ur-texts of one of the most closely watched copyright cases ever to rattle the world of fine art.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 413, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy/01PRINCE_SPAN-copy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apropos Appropriation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apropos Appropriation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boies Schiller & Flexner', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batts, Deborah A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T16:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e25833ad-4c5f-52e2-8f0f-564138354236', 'word_count': 2109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e25833ad-4c5f-52e2-8f0f-564138354236'}, {'abstract': 'When the Big City Book Club reconvenes for its next online literary discussion on Jan. 10, we will be talking about Alfred Kazin’s “A Walker in the City,” the writer’s 1951 memoir of growing up in Brownsville, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/big-city-book-club-up-next-alfred-kazin/', 'snippet': 'When the Big City Book Club reconvenes for its next online literary discussion on Jan. 10, we will be talking about Alfred Kazin’s “A Walker in the City,” the writer’s 1951 memoir of growing up in Brownsville, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Big City Book Club reconvenes for its next online literary discussion on Jan. 10, we will be talking about Alfred Kazin’s “A Walker in the City,” the writer’s 1951 memoir of growing up in Brownsville, Brooklyn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big City Book Club: Up Next, Alfred Kazin', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kazin, Alfred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City College of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brownsville (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T16:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/862b7577-5f87-5ffe-b069-3515a1ff3060', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/862b7577-5f87-5ffe-b069-3515a1ff3060'}, {'abstract': 'A rule that many New Yorkers once followed zealously — avoid the park after dark — is obsolete to many strollers, runners and cyclists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/nyregion/as-crime-falls-central-parks-night-use-grows.html', 'snippet': 'A rule that many New Yorkers once followed zealously — avoid the park after dark — is obsolete to many strollers, runners and cyclists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For as long as most New Yorkers can remember, the rules have been clear: Enjoy Central Park by day. Keep out at night. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/nyregion/29centralpark/29centralpark-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/29/nyregion/29centralpark/29centralpark-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 266}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/nyregion/29centralpark/29centralpark-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/nyregion/29centralpark/29centralpark-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/nyregion/29centralpark/29centralpark-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Days Behind It, Central Park Pulses at Night', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dark Days Behind It, Central Park Pulses at Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'