, the video game studio behind Guitar Hero and Rock Band, to Viacom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viacom is disputing a decision by court-appointed arbitrators that it pay $383 million to the former shareholders of Harmonix Music Systems, the video game studio behind Rock Band and Guitar Hero.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viacom Told to Pay $383 Million Over Rock Band Video Game', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harmonix Music Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viacom Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0d0ad57-4e98-594c-9b0a-0fc360c52bea', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0d0ad57-4e98-594c-9b0a-0fc360c52bea'}, {'abstract': 'Teams from the Pac-12 and Big Ten will soon begin to play one another extensively, essentially creating benefits of conference expansion without having to expand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/sports/ncaafootball/pac-12-and-big-ten-announce-scheduling-partnership.html', 'snippet': 'Teams from the Pac-12 and Big Ten will soon begin to play one another extensively, essentially creating benefits of conference expansion without having to expand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a time of instability and uncertainty on the college sports landscape, the Pacific-12 and the Big Ten announced an innovative scheduling agreement Wednesday that links the two conferences and shows they have no imminent plans for change. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scheduling Partnership Links Pac-12 and Big Ten', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scheduling Partnership Links Pac-12 And Big Ten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific-12 Conference', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delany, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Larry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Ten Conference', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcc8e6f-dbe4-5c35-9961-6fccd3e83c4c', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcc8e6f-dbe4-5c35-9961-6fccd3e83c4c'}, {'abstract': 'Nikita Feoktistov is a 21-year-old law student from Russia and a forward on the Red Stars, an all-star team from Russia’s only junior hockey league, the M.H.L. The M.H.L. supplies players to Russia’s professional league, the K.H.L, as well as the N.H.L. The Red Stars began an eight-game tour Saturday night against six college and two amateur teams.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/feoktistovs-journal-christmas-and-a-game-in-vermont/', 'snippet': 'Nikita Feoktistov is a 21-year-old law student from Russia and a forward on the Red Stars, an all-star team from Russia’s only junior hockey league, the M.H.L. The M.H.L. supplies players to Russia’s professional league, the K.H.L, as well as the ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'We spent Christmas Day in Burlington, Vt. There wasn’t much to do, of course, as mostly everything was closed. We had another intense two-hour practice on Christmas, preparing for the tougher part of our journey beginning this week with games against three Division I college teams – the University of Vermont on Tuesday, Yale on Wednesday and Northern Michigan on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feoktistov’s Journal: Christmas, and a Game, in Vermont', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Feoktistov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feoktistov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4237a289-963f-5482-be4c-0730be08c9d5', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4237a289-963f-5482-be4c-0730be08c9d5'}, {'abstract': 'Colonel Qaddafi’s gunmen did not all carry Kalashnikovs — many clutched Belgian exports. These Western arms, which seemed almost to mock the spirit behind the limited rules that regulate the transfer of conventional arms between states, all ended up in rebel hands.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/tracking-belgian-weapons-in-libya/', 'snippet': 'Colonel Qaddafi’s gunmen did not all carry Kalashnikovs — many clutched Belgian exports. These Western arms, which seemed almost to mock the spirit behind the limited rules that regulate the transfer of conventional arms between states, all ended ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching the disintegration of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s military and government was in some ways like watching an arms show featuring more than a half-century of conventional weapons. During his decades in power, the Libyan leader and his generals amassed a vast store of weapons, stockpiling them across the desert nation in depots that, as Colonel Qaddafi lost his hold on power, changed hands. All manner of weapons were paraded out. (The colonel’s militias and military units, while they lasted, held on to much of the choice stock.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracking Belgian Weapons in Libya', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:24:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Spleeters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spleeters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ed4be7f-d5eb-5750-a86e-5965bf55a0ef', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ed4be7f-d5eb-5750-a86e-5965bf55a0ef'}, {'abstract': 'Though the adoption of rooftop solar panels in India have been limited because of costs, annual sales of solar lanterns have reached several hundred thousand units.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/lanterns-are-a-ready-example-of-solar-powers-potential.html', 'snippet': 'Though the adoption of rooftop solar panels in India have been limited because of costs, annual sales of solar lanterns have reached several hundred thousand units.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KHADODA, India — In sunny India, the ideal would be to harness solar power for both the nation’s utility grid and for the rooftops of homes, businesses and factories. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lanterns Show an Industry’s Potential', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lanterns Show an Industry’s Potential', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42caa51-ff18-52a9-ab4d-25e2390b916d', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42caa51-ff18-52a9-ab4d-25e2390b916d'}, {'abstract': 'The e-mails, which reached home delivery subscribers and many, many others, were accidentally sent to 8.6 million readers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/times-readers-inundated-by-false-e-mail-on-subscriptions/', 'snippet': 'The e-mails, which reached home delivery subscribers and many, many others, were accidentally sent to 8.6 million readers.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:02 p.m. | Updated The New York Times mistakenly sent an e-mail on Wednesday to more than eight million people who had shared their information with the company, erroneously informing them that they had canceled home delivery of the newspaper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times E-Mails Millions by Mistake to Say Subscriptions Were Canceled', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:29:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d526efff-ee18-5cd8-ab2d-1adc1f14f468', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d526efff-ee18-5cd8-ab2d-1adc1f14f468'}, {'abstract': 'Two years ago, India said it would drastically increase its use of solar power by 2020. Many analysts said it couldn’t be done. Now they aren’t so sure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/in-solar-power-india-begins-living-up-to-its-own-ambitions.html', 'snippet': 'Two years ago, India said it would drastically increase its use of solar power by 2020. Many analysts said it couldn’t be done. Now they aren’t so sure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KHADODA, India — Solar power is a clean energy source. But in this arid part of northwest India it can also be a dusty one.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/29solar-span/29solar-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/29solar-span/29solar-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/29solar-span/29solar-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/29solar-span/29solar-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/business/energy-environment/29solar-span/29solar-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Solar Power, India Begins Living Up to Its Own Ambitions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India’s Investment in the Sun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbd37151-2693-54a4-8bbe-6cc88e7e3c86', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbd37151-2693-54a4-8bbe-6cc88e7e3c86'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to dealing its most valuable commodity, Rich De Vos, the Magic’s owner, seems more interested in the short-term bottom line than the long-term health of his team.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/magic-owner-breathes-new-life-into-dwight-howard-rumor-mill/', 'snippet': 'When it comes to dealing its most valuable commodity, Rich De Vos, the Magic’s owner, seems more interested in the short-term bottom line than the long-term health of his team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dwight Howard’s time in Orlando is fleeting. Although Otis Smith, the Magic’s general manager, has stressed that there’s no urgency to deal Howard, the best big man in the game, it’s only a matter of time before Howard lands on some other team’s roster to cement that team’s future and delight its fans. Smith and the Magic will be left to pick up the pieces and reshape a franchise otherwise lacking in elite talent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Magic Owner Breathes New Life Into Dwight Howard Rumor Mill', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Dwight', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e3e1d2b-ab97-54f8-8d3a-38b1e8294b25', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e3e1d2b-ab97-54f8-8d3a-38b1e8294b25'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees signed the Japanese pitcher Hideki Okajima to a minor league contract on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/yankees-give-former-red-sox-reliever-a-shot/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees signed the Japanese pitcher Hideki Okajima to a minor league contract on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hideki Okajima joined the Boston Red Sox in 2007, the same year a far better known Japanese pitcher named Daisuke Matsuzaka became a member of the team. Matsuzaka was 15-12 that season and helped the Red Sox capture a World Series title, but Okajima was a significant contributor, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Give Former Red Sox Reliever a Shot', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okajima, Hideki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:34:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83b68db5-09e9-546c-af52-3e01386d64bf', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83b68db5-09e9-546c-af52-3e01386d64bf'}, {'abstract': 'The belligerent tone between the U.S. and Iran escalated over an Iranian vow to close a vital Middle East waterway for oil tanker traffic, if Western powers attempt to stifle Iran’s petroleum exports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/world/middleeast/noise-level-rises-over-iran-threat-to-close-strait-of-hormuz.html', 'snippet': 'The belligerent tone between the U.S. and Iran escalated over an Iranian vow to close a vital Middle East waterway for oil tanker traffic, if Western powers attempt to stifle Iran’s petroleum exports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran and the United States elevated the belligerent tone between them on Wednesday over an Iranian vow to close the Strait of Hormuz, a vital Middle East waterway for oil tanker traffic, if Western powers attempted to make good on their threat to stifle Iran’s petroleum exports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Noise Level Rises Over Iran Threat to Close Strait of Hormuz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Noise Level Rises Over Iran Threat to Close Strait of Hormuz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Strait of Hormuz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/509c9c80-7ecd-50f5-a130-00dcb9cc7b00', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/509c9c80-7ecd-50f5-a130-00dcb9cc7b00'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports included muddy cyclists, shadowy skiers and a controversial finish in the Sydney to Hobart yacht race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/28/sports/20111228-photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports included muddy cyclists, shadowy skiers and a controversial finish in the Sydney to Hobart yacht race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports included muddy cyclists, shadowy skiers and a controversial finish in the Sydney to Hobart yacht race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/sports/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/28/sports/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/28/sports/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N/20111228-photoreplay-slide-HV2N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Dec.28', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/86831f93-3ada-52bf-b5b1-f841347fee00', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/86831f93-3ada-52bf-b5b1-f841347fee00'}, {'abstract': 'A former member of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission asserts that four of its members wrote a letter with the aim of ousting the agency’s chairman, not seeking a more collaborative relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/in-agency-smackdown-a-critique-of-the-nuclear-party/', 'snippet': 'A former member of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission asserts that four of its members wrote a letter with the aim of ousting the agency’s chairman, not seeking a more collaborative relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chairman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission, whose four fellow commissioners complained about him to the White House, saying that he had been withholding information from them and wielding too much power, drew a spirited defense on Wednesday from a predecessor at the agency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agency Smackdown, Round 2: A Critique of  ‘the Nuclear Party’', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaczko, Gregory B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f74a2060-fb32-574e-8299-3cd2a9a73270', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f74a2060-fb32-574e-8299-3cd2a9a73270'}, {'abstract': 'In a poll of Latino voters, President Obama is overwhelmingly favored over the Republican presidential candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/latinos-support-obama-despite-deportation-policies/', 'snippet': 'In a poll of Latino voters, President Obama is overwhelmingly favored over the Republican presidential candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Latinos strongly disapprove of President Obama’s immigration policies, which have brought high numbers of deportations, they would favor him by wide margins over a Republican candidate in the presidential race, according to a poll released on Wednesday by the Pew Hispanic Center, a nonpartisan research group in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latinos Support Obama, Despite Deportation Policies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Hispanic Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center for People and the Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ed86c79-9827-5a7d-b84b-64d61665504f', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ed86c79-9827-5a7d-b84b-64d61665504f'}, {'abstract': 'At the precipice of 2012, White Collar Watch looks at some of the trends in criminal and civil enforcement cases that will continue in the next year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/what-to-expect-in-2012/', 'snippet': 'At the precipice of 2012, White Collar Watch looks at some of the trends in criminal and civil enforcement cases that will continue in the next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The career of Robert G. Morvillo, the dean of the white-collar defense bar who died Saturday, highlights how white-collar crime has risen to prominence. His obituary in The New York Times pointed out that in 1973, when he founded a law firm specializing in the defense of executives and corporations in criminal cases, large New York firms shunned the practice because it was “considered déclassé.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Expect in White-Collar Crimes in 2012', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanford, Robert Allen', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T19:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non