er leg injuries on Long Island, her mate, Bobby, has been spending time with a new female in Washington Square Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Violet the red-tailed hawk is safe, but she is not likely to return to Washington Square Park, said Robert Horvath, a raptor rehabilitator with Wildlife in Need of Rescue and Rehabilitation, the nonprofit organization that is caring for the bird. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Care for Violet, New Friend for an Old Mate', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T21:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5390f2-affd-5494-b1d1-6439c10c0db6', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5390f2-affd-5494-b1d1-6439c10c0db6'}, {'abstract': 'In 2010, apps for Android phones were rarely in the same league as those for Apple devices. But in the past year, that has changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/technology/personaltech/in-2011-app-developers-turned-attention-to-android.html', 'snippet': 'In 2010, apps for Android phones were rarely in the same league as those for Apple devices. But in the past year, that has changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, Android apps were rarely in the same league as their Apple counterparts, so beyond the entrants in last year’s Top 10 list, there was a steep drop-off in quality.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/business/BIZSMART1-1325020752229/BIZSMART1-1325020752229-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/business/BIZSMART1-1325020752229/BIZSMART1-1325020752229-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/business/BIZSMART1-1325020752229/BIZSMART1-1325020752229-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '2011’s Top 10 Apps for Android Phones', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Android’s Numbers Grow, Developers Take Note', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T21:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f624b63