ick Perry's Stump Speech", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T21:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/73350b04-935a-5126-851a-f410811850eb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/73350b04-935a-5126-851a-f410811850eb'}, {'abstract': 'If so, please tell us what made it noteworthy and why you think it failed.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/do-you-know-a-small-business-that-failed-this-year/', 'snippet': 'If so, please tell us what made it noteworthy and why you think it failed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in good times, the survival rate for small businesses is discouraging — about half fail within five years, according to the Small Business Administration. Unfortunately, 2011 was another tough year. We’ve just published an article by Eileen Zimmerman about five businesses that didn’t make it. Behind every failed business, there’s a story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Know a Small Business That Failed This Year?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T22:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'