signs that were not traditionally tasteful and did not play to any trends. Now its goods — made in Mexico with age-old techniques that often lead to unconventional results — are on display at DFC’s first store, in Mexico City.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29OPEN_SPAN/29OPEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29OPEN_SPAN/29OPEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29OPEN_SPAN/29OPEN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29OPEN_SPAN/29OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29OPEN_SPAN/29OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Mexico City, a Design Playhouse', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Mexico City, a Design Playhouse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T23:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f904c988-b364-58dc-bd5e-259c2eea2467', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f904c988-b364-58dc-bd5e-259c2eea2467'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of animal behaviorists believe that training and walking cats is not only possible, but good for the cat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/garden/training-a-cat-to-walk-on-a-leash.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of animal behaviorists believe that training and walking cats is not only possible, but good for the cat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are outdoor cats and there are indoor cats. When I brought home Mac, a 4-year-old orange tabby, from a shelter last year, I realized I had acquired a demanding combination of the two.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Lives, One Leash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Lives, One Leash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galaxy, Jackson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T23:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/203019e8-9357-519e-a81d-87849a78b53a', 'word_count': 1833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/203019e8-9357-519e-a81d-87849a78b53a'}, {'abstract': 'Discounts on furniture, books, lamps, table linens and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/garden/sales-at-artemide-the-moma-store-and-others-deals.html', 'snippet': 'Discounts on furniture, books, lamps, table linens and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gus Modern will take 15 percent off furniture and accessories in January (the Atwood sectional, pictured, originally $3,199, will be about $2,719; the Carmichael Loft sofa, normally $1,999, about $1,699); gusmodern.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29DEALS/29CURRENTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29DEALS/29DEALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29DEALS/29DEALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales at Artemide, the MoMA Store and Others', 'kicker': 'Currents | Deals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bargains for the Den and Dining Room', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T23:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a79e221-5b67-53e1-96e0-779c5714395d', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a79e221-5b67-53e1-96e0-779c5714395d'}, {'abstract': 'The potter Ayumi Horie developed a technique for making earthenware pieces without water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/garden/ceramics-that-are-imperfect-on-purpose.html', 'snippet': 'The potter Ayumi Horie developed a technique for making earthenware pieces without water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ayumi Horie developed a technique for making earthenware pieces without water while she was a student at Alfred University in western New York State. Today, this 42-year-old potter creates plates and bowls using the nontraditional method because it “allows for spontaneity and a kind of gestural quality that is harder to get when clay is wet.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29GOODS_SPAN/29CURRENTS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29GOODS_SPAN/29GOODS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29GOODS_SPAN/29GOODS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ceramics That Are Imperfect on Purpose', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ceramics That Are Imperfect on Purpose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-28T23:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f435fc1d-042d-5a1f-8b68-32c9fddfc140', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f435fc1d-042d-5a1f-8b68-32c9fddfc140'}, {'abstract': 'The writer David Treuer, who has a new nonfiction book called “Rez Life,” on his new home on an American Indian reservation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/garden/david-treuer-on-reservation-life-qa.html', 'snippet': 'The writer David Treuer, who has a new nonfiction book called “Rez Life,” on his new home on an American Indian reservation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Treuer was offered a teaching job at the University of Southern California last year, he made a promise to himself before accepting and moving his family from Minneapolis to the West Coast: He would keep a home — “an anchor,” as he put it — on the Leech Lake Indian Reservation in northern Minnesota, where he grew up.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29QNA1_SPAN/29QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29QNA1_SPAN/29QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29QNA1_SPAN/29QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29QNA1_SPAN/29QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/garden/29QNA1_SPAN/29QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indian Writer Finds His Anchor on the Reservation', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Indian Writer Finds His Anchor on the Reservation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'va