n-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'About 400 members of an Iranian exile group agreed to leave a camp in eastern Iraq, another step in international efforts to unwind an impasse between Iraq’s government and Camp Ashraf.', 'lead_paragraph': ' About 400 members of an Iranian exile group agreed Wednesday to leave a camp in eastern Iraq, another step in international efforts to end a tense, sometimes violent, impasse between Iraq’s government and the 3,400 people inside Camp Ashraf. The plan would move the residents to a former American military base in Baghdad, where they would ultimately relocate outside Iraq. The camp is populated by members of the Mujahedeen Khalq, or People’s Mujahedeen, a group that has fought in years past to bring down the Iranian government. The Iraqi government wants to close the camp. On Wednesday night, three rockets struck the camp, but there were no immediate reports of casualties, Iraqi security officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Exiles to Leave Camp', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Exiles to Leave Camp', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Mujahedeen of Iran", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Camp Ashraf (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T02:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7e2eabd-f484-5239-9e66-2080c9001ab8', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7e2eabd-f484-5239-9e66-2080c9001ab8'}, {'abstract': 'Iowa State has long been a forlorn way station for coaches, but it looks as if it has found a keeper in Paul Rhoads, especially after signing him to a 10-year, $20 million contract extension.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/sports/ncaafootball/paul-rhoads-finds-a-home-at-iowa-state.html', 'snippet': 'Iowa State has long been a forlorn way station for coaches, but it looks as if it has found a keeper in Paul Rhoads, especially after signing him to a 10-year, $20 million contract extension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early Tuesday night, Iowa State football coach Paul Rhoads peered through the glass panes of a suite at Yankee Stadium and witnessed yet another first in a three-year run filled with breakthroughs. Before a Pinstripe Bowl dinner, his players were given a tour of the majestic ballpark, where they will play Rutgers on Friday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/sports/CYCLONES/CYCLONES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/29/sports/CYCLONES/CYCLONES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/29/sports/CYCLONES/CYCLONES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa State Has Found a Stabilizing Presence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iowa State Has Found A Stabilizing Presence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'sub