s use of the wrong form to apply for reimbursement for speech therapy services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Letter from the New York State Department of Health to the New York City Department of Education alerting of the city’s use of the wrong form to apply for reimbursement for speech therapy services.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York State Dept. of Health Letter to Dept. of Education', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T02:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8a898e1a-8f62-5374-825d-a45d41c8331c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8a898e1a-8f62-5374-825d-a45d41c8331c'}, {'abstract': 'The regulars at Gregory’s were exempt from cliché, if only because of the unlikely fact that they were all gathered there together.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/my-dad-and-i-walked-into-a-bar/', 'snippet': 'The regulars at Gregory’s were exempt from cliché, if only because of the unlikely fact that they were all gathered there together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most regulars at neighborhood bars come by their nicknames through easily distinguishable physical qualities (Goiter Eddie, Curly Pat, Jimmy the Hat, One-Arm Joe). If that fails, a nickname can be created on the basis of ethnic origin (English Billy, Irish Mike), or a profession (Eddie the Actor, Rodger the Dodger — a defense attorney). But in the entire history of nicknaming, there was only one regular called “Tara’