nger, Dies at 65', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yiddish Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T03:48:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/958f3620-4374-570e-97ba-09b1e7bc322d', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958f3620-4374-570e-97ba-09b1e7bc322d'}, {'abstract': 'A Texas case in which a man was exonerated after serving nearly 25 years in prison demands accountability after a district attorney withheld evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/opinion/justice-and-prosecutorial-misconduct.html', 'snippet': 'A Texas case in which a man was exonerated after serving nearly 25 years in prison demands accountability after a district attorney withheld evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Morton was exonerated by DNA evidence this month after being wrongfully convicted of murdering his wife and serving nearly 25 years in prison in Texas. In seeking to prove Mr. Morton’s innocence, his lawyers found in recently unsealed court records evidence that the prosecutor in the original trial, Ken Anderson, had withheld critical evidence that may have helped Mr. Morton.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice and Prosecutorial Misconduct', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice and Prosecutorial Misconduct', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morton, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Innocence Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Ken', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Clarence', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T03:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c51439ae-fc23-523c-91ce-cb125b3f61f7', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c51439ae-fc23-523c-91ce-cb125b3f61f7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Dubey revived the Hindi theater and enabled it to compete with the English-language theater that once dominated in India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/theater/satyadev-dubey-playwright-who-modernized-hindi-theater-dies-at-75.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Dubey revived the Hindi theater and enabled it to compete with the English-language theater that once dominated in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Satyadev Dubey, a producer, director and playwright who inspired generations of Indian actors and other playwrights, died on Sunday in Mumbai. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Satyadev Dubey, Playwright Who Modernized Hindi Theater, Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Satyadev Dubey, 75, Producer Who Revived Hindi Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T03:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haresh Pandya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pandya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/445147b1-bf44-5ab8-bc53-51168710cfed', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445147b1-bf44-5ab8-bc53-51168710cfed'}, {'abstract': 'A year after the Tucson rampage, what happened to gun control? Sensible voters are demanding stronger protection from gun violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/opinion/another-year-for-weapons.html', 'snippet': 'A year after the Tucson rampage, what happened to gun control? Sensible voters are demanding stronger protection from gun violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I. reports that gun dealers submitted the names of almost half-a-million customers in the six days before Christmas, with December on its way to surpassing November, which had a record tally of 1,534,414 names submitted for background checks for criminal convictions and mental health issues. Only a little more than 1 percent of buyers are typically rejected by federally licensed gun dealers. No one knows how many more firearms were purchased through the gun-show loophole that enables black marketeering.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Year for Weapons', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Year for Weapons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T03:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/24ede0ab-f89d-5b55-8173-a0a25d6ae619', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24ede0ab-f89d-5b55-8173-a0a25d6ae619'}, {'abstract': 'The I.R.S. needs to crack down on the secret political money flooding the 2012 campaign from partisan operatives claiming to be “social welfare” activists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/opinion/whose-welfare.html', 'snippet': 'The I.R.S. needs to crack down on the secret political money flooding the 2012 campaign from partisan operatives claiming to be “social welfare” activists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When will the Internal Revenue Service crack down on the secret political money already flooding the 2012 campaign from partisan operatives ludicrously claiming to be “social welfare” activists under the tax law?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whose Welfare?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kic