person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0554b4c5-3863-5a2a-8c83-46a20d8c0730', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0554b4c5-3863-5a2a-8c83-46a20d8c0730'}, {'abstract': 'Lower prices for solar panels and smart policy have helped the industry grow.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/28/an-indian-government-success-solar-power/', 'snippet': 'Lower prices for solar panels and smart policy have helped the industry grow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the Indian government has missed many of its development goals in recent years, there is one area where it is on track: harnessing solar power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indian Government Success: Solar Power', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T04:58:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f800f9c-bf05-53f0-a716-06504ec4cfeb', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f800f9c-bf05-53f0-a716-06504ec4cfeb'}, {'abstract': 'Isa Leshko, a fine art photographer, set out to capture glimpses of animals in their twilight years — a therapeutic project inspired by caring for her mother with Alzheimer’s disease.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/what-we-can-learn-from-old-animals/', 'snippet': 'Isa Leshko, a fine art photographer, set out to capture glimpses of animals in their twilight years — a therapeutic project inspired by caring for her mother with Alzheimer’s disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is not hard to argue that we live in a youth-centric culture, one in which young age and beauty are almost synonymous. And that obsession does not end with humans. Puppies and kittens melt hearts; images and videos of baby animals flood the Internet. But rarely does an image of an animal in old age ignite the same interest and adoration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We Can Learn From Old Animals', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T05:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2db1510-843f-59f3-83cd-fa4b34828196', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2db1510-843f-59f3-83cd-fa4b34828196'}, {'abstract': 'Heather Hurlburt, left, of the National Security Network and Daniel Drezner of ForeignPolicy.com debate the future of North Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000001251885/bloggingheads-north-koreas-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Heather Hurlburt, left, of the National Security Network and Daniel Drezner of ForeignPolicy.com debate the future of North Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heather Hurlburt, left, of the National Security Network and Daniel Drezner of ForeignPolicy.com debate the future of North Korea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi