ragraph': 'If at first you succeed. … The list of the top-grossing films of 2011 is, more or less, a list of sequels, starting with the top film, “Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 2,” which is the final sequel in a long series. Those results are a product of “a flight to financial safety that has been building for a decade,” Michael Cieply writes. It appears that 2012 will not be so different, with the major studios planning about 10 sequels or “reboots” (that is, a familiar series that begins again, from the top).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 29', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E TRADE Financial Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T13:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1a19388-714a-5827-96a4-7791255b4e14', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1a19388-714a-5827-96a4-7791255b4e14'}, {'abstract': 'Deliberations in India’s upper house of Parliament about an anti-corruption law were heated.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/lokpal-in-the-rajya-sabha-who-hates-what/', 'snippet': 'Deliberations in India’s upper house of Parliament about an anti-corruption law were heated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deliberations were heated Thursday in India’s Rajya Sabha, or upper house of Parliament, over the Lokpal bill, which would create an anti-corruption body of ombudsmen in India. The United Progressive Alliance, or U.P.A., does not have a majority in the Rajya Sabha, unlike in the Lok Sabha, so the bill will have a more difficult time passing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lokpal in the Rajya Sabha: Who Hates What', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banerjee, Mamata', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T13:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecb0390b-c59a-54d7-911e-74d2a05fa3d0', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecb0390b-c59a-54d7-911e-74d2a05fa3d0'}, {'abstract': 'Debt was falling before the crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/european-fiscal-zombies/', 'snippet': 'Debt was falling before the crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Baker is unhappy at seeing yet another article asserting as