bType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/30cajun_337/30cajun_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/us/30cajun_337/30cajun_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bitter Twist in Louisiana Family’s Long Drilling Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana Family’s Long Legal Fight Over Texaco Drilling Lease Takes a Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eminent Domain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texaco Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T14:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf935e5-efef-5bc1-aa50-11e13e4858e6', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf935e5-efef-5bc1-aa50-11e13e4858e6'}, {'abstract': 'Research shows that teenagers who had a poor relationship with their mothers when they were young are more likely to be obese — but what causes those mothers and toddlers to struggle?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/teen-obesity-linked-to-poor-mother-child-interaction/', 'snippet': 'Research shows that teenagers who had a poor relationship with their mothers when they were young are more likely to be obese — but what causes those mothers and toddlers to struggle?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers from Ohio State University analyzed data from a study following nearly 1,000 children from infancy through the ninth grade and found that children who were “insecurely attached” or otherwise showed signs of a poor maternal relationship before age 3 were more likely to be obese at 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teenage Obesity Linked to Poor Mother-Child Bond', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T15:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d365369b-8b5e-5231-813d-6d7f13db7563', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d365369b-8b5e-5231-813d-6d7f13db7563'}, {'abstract': 'As the year nears an end, the mayor and some of his commissioners have been ballyhooing a flock of favorable statistics. Indeed, they had reason to take bows.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/where-credit-is-due-and-eagerly-taken/', 'snippet': 'As the year nears an end, the mayor and some of his commissioners have been ballyhooing a flock of favorable statistics. Indeed, they had reason to take bows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is the nature of politicians and bureaucrats to summon microphone- and pencil-holders when they have good news and to content themselves with, at best, a printed statement — issued perhaps at 6 p.m. on a Friday after everyone has gone home — when developments reflect poorly on them. That the public has a stake in tidings both glad and sad is usually ignored as an inconvenient detail. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Credit Is Due, and Eagerly Taken', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T15:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/366b87ec-a9e6-52dd-a47a-4357b2fad03a', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366b87ec-a9e6-52dd-a47a-4357b2fad03a'}, {'abstract': '“Iron Lady,” about the former British prime minister Margaret Thatcher, is the story of a widow and a half-abandoned mother who happened to have been one of the most powerful women of the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/movies/the-iron-lady-about-margaret-thatcher-review.html', 'snippet': '“Iron Lady,” about the former British prime minister Margaret Thatcher, is the story of a widow and a half-abandoned mother who happened to have been one of the most powerful women of the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best thing about “The Iron Lady” may be that viewers going into the theater with strong views, pro or con, about its subject, the former British prime minister Margaret Thatcher, are likely to emerge in a state of greater ambivalence, even confusion. Those who know or care little about her will also be confused, but for different reasons.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30IRON/30IRON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30IRON/30IRON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30IRON/30IRON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 661, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30IRON/30IRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30IRON/30IRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Polarizing Leader Fades Into the Twilight', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Iron Lady'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Polarizing Leader Fades Into the Twilight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep,