}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat, Adam B. Ellick, Shayla Harris, Ben Solomon and Sean Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/aa7fd0db-6180-5158-89c4-8a2a21587a2e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/aa7fd0db-6180-5158-89c4-8a2a21587a2e'}, {'abstract': 'When Sgt. Thomas James Brennan learned that a Reuters photographer would be embedded with his Marine squad, he went on the defensive. Less than a day later, his mind was changed under fire.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/from-the-marines-side-of-the-camera/', 'snippet': 'When Sgt. Thomas James Brennan learned that a Reuters photographer would be embedded with his Marine squad, he went on the defensive. Less than a day later, his mind was changed under fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Finbarr O’Reilly, a Reuters photographer, embedded with my squad of Marines in Afghanistan last October, I strategically positioned myself between him and my men, to keep them out of trouble. I based my decision on experience and preconceived notions regarding combat journalists. On the first night, I questioned him for hours about his upbringing, his background and his political outlook on the war, to get a better feel for who he was. It appeared that he wasn’t a bad guy after all. We shared a lot of views. But I remained cautious. You can never judge a book by its cover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Marine’s Side of the Camera', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas James Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'James', 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9340a7c-540d-50d4-96d4-a2acd264d69d', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9340a7c-540d-50d4-96d4-a2acd264d69d'}, {'abstract': 'The newly created Borough Hall Skyscraper Historic District is being challenged at the City Council. At stake is a 30-story tower at 75 Livingston Street that may be the district’s crown jewel.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/historic-district-in-downtown-brooklyn-faces-a-fight-at-the-city-council/', 'snippet': 'The newly created Borough Hall Skyscraper Historic District is being challenged at the City Council. At stake is a 30-story tower at 75 Livingston Street that may be the district’s crown jewel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the vantage, say, of Court and Joralemon Streets, Brooklyn feels like the big city it is. This is Downtown, with an upper-case D: tall buildings, crowded sidewalks, public monuments, intersecting lives — seasoned with urgency and purpose.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Towers, and a Debate Over Preservation', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lander, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4499a5a-3276-54f6-8865-06dff738c084', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4499a5a-3276-54f6-8865-06dff738c084'}, {'abstract': 'After a chill in relations over the Arab Spring, the deal to sell fighter jets manufactured by Boeing signals support for a key ally in the Persian Gulf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/world/middleeast/with-30-billion-arms-deal-united-states-bolsters-ties-to-saudi-arabia.html', 'snippet': 'After a chill in relations over the Arab Spring, the deal to sell fighter jets manufactured by Boeing signals support for a key ally in the Persian Gulf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — Fortifying one of its key allies in the Persian Gulf, the Obama administration announced a weapons deal with Saudi Arabia on Thursday, saying it had agreed to sell F-15 fighter jets valued at nearly $30 billion to the Royal Saudi Air Force.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With $30 Billion Arms Deal, U.S. Bolsters Saudi Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Healing a Rift, U.S. Agrees to $30 Billion Fighter Jet Sale to Saudi Arabia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:04:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b7e3efc-867f-5cbf-a457-498de2ead4ce', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b7e3efc-867f-5cbf-a457-498de2ead4ce'}, {'abstract': 'Some 5,500 objects from the doomed ship will be offered in one lot on April 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/huge-trove-of-titanic-artifacts-to-be-auctioned/', 'snippet': 'Some 5,500 objects from the doomed ship will be offered in one lot on April 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of artifacts salvaged from the Titanic’s watery tomb in the North Atlantic will be sold in a winner-take-all auction scheduled for April, the centennial of the luxury liner’s sinking, The Associated Press reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huge Trove of Titanic Artifacts to Be Auctioned', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Guernsey's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Premier Exhibitions Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newfoundland (Canada)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/701b37ec-e2da-5550-9308-6a01e5b4092c', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/701b37ec-e2da-5550-9308-6a01e5b4092c'}, {'abstract': 'A disgruntled owner of a Honda Civic Hybrid says she plans to opt out of a class-action lawsuit and instead is suing the automaker for up to $10,000 in small claims court.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/unhappy-honda-owner-taking-case-to-small-claims-court/', 'snippet': 'A disgruntled owner of a Honda Civic Hybrid says she plans to opt out of a class-action lawsuit and instead is suing the automaker for up to $10,000 in small claims court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heather Peters of Los Angeles is taking a novel approach to addressing her legal grievances against Honda for what she says are the fuel economy shortcomings of her Civic Hybrid. She says she is opting out of a proposed class-action lawsuit settlement and instead is suing the automaker for up to $10,000 in small claims court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unhappy Honda Owner Taking Case to Small Claims Court', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a650bf75-4f26-542c-97ef-a3e3a44956b2', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a650bf75-4f26-542c-97ef-a3e3a44956b2'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to escape the constant stream of too much information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/opinion/sunday/the-joy-of-quiet.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to escape the constant stream of too much information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABOUT a year ago, I flew to Singapore to join the writer Malcolm Gladwell, the fashion designer Marc Ecko and the graphic designer Stefan Sagmeister in addressing a group of advertising people on “Marketing to the Child of Tomorrow.” Soon after I arrived, the chief executive of the agency that had invited us took me aside. What he was most interested in, he began — I braced myself for mention of some next-generation stealth campaign — was stillness.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01COVER/01COVER-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01COVER/01COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01COVER/01COVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joy of Quiet', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Joy of Quiet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pico Iyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pico', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Iyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f40966e-4d6d-5734-8452-ec806949183a', 'word_count': 1781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f40966e-4d6d-5734-8452-ec806949183a'}, {'abstract': 'Indiana and Louisville lost Wednesday night, leaving Syracuse, Murray State, Baylor and Missouri as the only undefeated teams remaining in Division I.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/four-undefeated-basketball-teams-left/', 'snippet': 'Indiana and Louisville lost Wednesday night, leaving Syracuse, Murray State, Baylor and Missouri as the only undefeated teams remaining in Division I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of undefeated teams in college basketball continues to shrink to a precious few, as Indiana and Louisville lost Wednesday. Four teams remain perfect: No. 1 Syracuse is 14-0, No. 20 Murray State and No. 6 Baylor are 13-0, and No. 8 Missouri sits at 12-0.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Undefeated Basketball Teams Left', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Scott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baylor University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgetown University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Murray State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Louisville', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c33a72ca-1ac4-5fc7-bd4d-24f576ba508c', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c33a72ca-1ac4-5fc7-bd4d-24f576ba508c'}, {'abstract': 'A $250 kit lets you play around with green screen techniques, setting actors in front of any background of your choosing. It takes the pain out of a process that can be difficult to get right.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/hollywood-style-tricks-on-the-cheap/', 'snippet': 'A $250 kit lets you play around with green screen techniques, setting actors in front of any background of your choosing. It takes the pain out of a process that can be difficult to get right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of weeks ago, my 12-year-old daughter sought my advice about a video she wanted to make. Her concept was so elaborate and involved so many scenes, I doubted it was even doable — unless she used a green screen and filmed the whole thing in the basement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood-Style Tricks on the Cheap', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf0dfd9-1690-5a6c-9fc8-3ff39b9b3f35', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf0dfd9-1690-5a6c-9fc8-3ff39b9b3f35'}, {'abstract': 'The underground movement to draft Sarah Palin into the Iowa caucuses has moved onto television, with a group called Sarah Palin’s Iowa Earthquake running ads across the state.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/new-ad-urges-iowans-to-caucus-for-palin/', 'snippet': 'The underground movement to draft Sarah Palin into the Iowa caucuses has moved onto television, with a group called Sarah Palin’s Iowa Earthquake running ads across the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The underground movement to draft Sarah Palin into the Iowa caucuses has moved onto television, with a group called Sarah Palin’s Iowa Earthquake running ads across the state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ad Urges Iowans to Caucus for Palin', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:28:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fc86c61-dbec-5d78-b8b0-e8d745c4a8a1', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fc86c61-dbec-5d78-b8b0-e8d745c4a8a1'}, {'abstract': 'Verizon is preparing to charge a $2 “convenience fee” for customers who pay individual cellphone bills over the phone or on the Internet. Customers who pay with an electronic check or enroll in an automatic payment option will be exempt from the fee.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/verizon-payments/', 'snippet': 'Verizon is preparing to charge a $2 “convenience fee” for customers who pay individual cellphone bills over the phone or on the Internet. Customers who pay with an electronic check or enroll in an automatic payment option will be exempt from the f...', 'lead_paragraph': ' 3:47 p.m. | Updated  Adding analyst comment.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verizon Wireless Adds $2 Fee for Some Bill Payments', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content