Out', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Los Angeles: Mr. C Beverly Hills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:47:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/44792338-b502-5924-8def-2ffddbf3dac2', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44792338-b502-5924-8def-2ffddbf3dac2'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an article on air miles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/travel/elite-flier-status.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an article on air miles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Re “Save your Elite Flier Status While You Can” (Practical Traveler, Dec. 18), I was seven segments short on Continental to get platinum status (you need 90 segments or 75,000 miles), so I did a crazy mileage run last weekend to get to platinum. All in all, the flights cost $350. The flight attendants were looking at me as if I was nuts, because for each pair of cities, I flew back and forth with the same crew. Saturday was Houston to Dallas to Houston to Austin to Houston; and Sunday was from Dallas to Houston to Austin to Houston. Ah, the crazy things we do to retain status.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elite Flier Status', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elite Flier Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/546d6a2f-005b-54c7-9e3f-0cdde505bf90', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/546d6a2f-005b-54c7-9e3f-0cdde505bf90'}, {'abstract': 'Bloggers in Cairo used Twitter to document a raid on a democracy-promotion group in text updates and photographs as it unfolded.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/eyewitness-accounts-of-raid-on-civil-society-group-in-cairo-posted-on-twitter/', 'snippet': 'Bloggers in Cairo used Twitter to document a raid on a democracy-promotion group in text updates and photographs as it unfolded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 8:01 p.m. As my colleagues David Kirkpatrick and David Goodman report, “Egyptian security forces stormed the offices of 17 nonprofit groups around the country on Thursday, including at least three democracy-promotion groups financed by the United States, as part of what Egypt’s military-led government has said is an investigation into ‘foreign hands’ in the recent outbreak of protests.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Activists Document Raids on Civil Society Groups and a Protest in Cairo', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nabil, Maikel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Republican Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Democratic Institute for International Affairs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c36efcb1-7a88-5244-9d37-de5252f207ca', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c36efcb1-7a88-5244-9d37-de5252f207ca'}, {'abstract': 'Standard & Poor’s has changed its near-term outlook on the stadium’s $695.4 million in bonds to negative from stable.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/s-p-outlook-on-citi-field-bonds-sours/', 'snippet': 'Standard & Poor’s has changed its near-term outlook on the stadium’s $695.4 million in bonds to negative from stable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets know things are not great at Citi Field. Attendance dropped again last season as they finished with a losing record for the third consecutive season. Revenue fell from virtually every source.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.&.P. Outlook on Citi Field Bonds Sours', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Corp", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:53:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba6fefb7-a1b4-5c44-8807-2469ae020974', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba6fefb7-a1b4-5c44-8807-2469ae020974'}, {'abstract': 'A shoutout to a barbecue joint in Austin, Tex.; a reader torn between lunch at the French Laundry and lunch at In-N-Out burger the next day; and, at Annisa in Manhattan, an aged ribeye with escargot.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/your-best-meals-of-the-year-from-new-york-to-tuscaloosa-to-a-singapore-cafe/', 'snippet': 'A shoutout to a barbecue joint in Austin, Tex.; a reader torn between lunch at the French Laundry and lunch at In-N-Out burger the next day; and, at Annisa in Manhattan, an aged ribeye with escargot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s one last batch of readers’ best meals of the year, though if you continue to share them on Twitter with the hashtag #bestmeal2011, we’ll keep on retweeting. Below you’ll see a shout-out to a barbecue joint in Austin, Tex.; a reader torn between lunch at the French Laundry and lunch at In-N-Out burger the next day; and, at Annisa in Manhattan, an aged ribeye with escargot, “earthy funk the likes of Bootsy Collins.” Here’s to good eating in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Best Meals of the Year: From New York, to Tuscaloosa, to a Singapore Cafe', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:53:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5e3912f-aa37-5a29-aea1-7df7e8fda062', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5e3912f-aa37-5a29-aea1-7df7e8fda062'}, {'abstract': 'A report says that the population of endangered delta smelt in the Sacramento-San Joaquin River delta has increased 10-fold since last year. But an invasive weed and a dearth of rain could make the uptick in the estuary’s health short-lived.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/californias-delta-ecosystem-is-healthier-for-now/', 'snippet': 'A report says that the population of endangered delta smelt in the Sacramento-San Joaquin River delta has increased 10-fold since last year. But an invasive weed and a dearth of rain could make the uptick in the estuary’s health short-lived.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ecosystem of the delta where the Sacramento and San Joaquin rivers meet has been in the legal equivalent of an intensive care unit for four years. But just before Christmas, an upbeat report came in, showing that a year of copious rain and snow had significantly improved.the delta’s condition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California’s Delta Ecosystem Is Healthier, For Now', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weeds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/186563dc-5623-5b7e-8e44-f61b6e454605', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/186563dc-5623-5b7e-8e44-f61b6e454605'}, {'abstract': 'A Jesuit center provides an Arcadian setting for a quick shot of affordable quiet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/travel/in-pennsylvania-a-quick-shot-of-peace-on-a-budget.html', 'snippet': 'A Jesuit center provides an Arcadian setting for a quick shot of affordable quiet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LATE in November I arrived at the Jesuit Center in the reclusive hills of Wernersville, Pa., on a blindingly dark and stormy night to begin a silent five-day retreat. Such a scenario might have compelled someone more compos mentis to turn around. But that was the point. As a 43-year-old mother of three wrung out from three years of panic attacks triggered by the specter of financial ruin, I needed a solid period of quiet to recombobulate. Cheaply.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01JESUIT1_SPAN/01JESUIT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01JESUIT1_SPAN/01JESUIT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01JESUIT1_SPAN/0101JESUIT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01JESUIT1_SPAN/01JESUIT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01JESUIT1_SPAN/01JESUIT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pennsylvania, a Quick Shot of Peace, on a Budget', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Quick Shot of Peace, on a Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jesuit Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T18:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gregory Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': 'Gregory', 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87743457-1f4e-59ce-8418-2516b2417c15', 'word_count': 2073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87743457-1f4e-59ce-8418-2516b2417c15'}, {'abstract': 'To whom did we owe war debt?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/the-burden-of-debt-again-again/', 'snippet': 'To whom did we owe war debt?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I admit to having been surprised by the reaction to my two posts on the burden of debt. I thought I was saying something that would be obvious once it was pointed out; instead, many of the comments were baffled, and quite a few were utterly enraged. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Burden of Debt, Again Again', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3f8b5f2-22d9-5094-a8bf-1d4c08639fb6', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3f8b5f2-22d9-5094-a8bf-1d4c08639fb6'}, {'abstract': 'The turf problems that affected a football game at Yankee Stadium in November have been addressed (with thicker, heavier sod) ahead of Friday’s Pinstripe Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/yankees-call-up-some-tougher-sod-for-pinstripe-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'The turf problems that affected a football game at Yankee Stadium in November have been addressed (with thicker, heavier sod) ahead of Friday’s Pinstripe Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than seven minutes into a football game between Rutgers and Army at Yankee Stadium on Nov. 12, the grounds crew hustled onto the field and stepped on several large divots of turf that had become dislodged near one end zone. It was at about that moment that Lonn Trost cringed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/30pinstripe-pic/30pinstripe-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/30pinstripe-pic/30pinstripe-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/30pinstripe-pic/30pinstripe-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/30pinstripe-pic/30pinstripe-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/sports/ncaafootball/30pinstripe-pic/30pinstripe-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoping to Avoid Turf Troubles, Yanks Call Up Tougher Sod for Pinstripe Bowl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoping to Avoid Turf Troubles, Yanks Call Up Tougher Sod for Pinstripe Bowl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yankee Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iowa State University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9292434-4843-50a5-bada-c8adc4ef8a67', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9292434-4843-50a5-bada-c8adc4ef8a67'}, {'abstract': 'Nashville Community College students and a boat builder in Maine are outfitting a Chris-Craft boat with an Infiniti engine.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/a-classic-american-boat-weds-a-contemporary-japanese-engine/', 'snippet': 'Nashville Community College students and a boat builder in Maine are outfitting a Chris-Craft boat with an Infiniti engine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The classic and highly prized wooden speedboats made by Chris-Craft have long been fitted with potent automobile engines, including small-block Chevy V-8s and Chrysler Hemis. Now, Infiniti has joined with Nashville State Community College and Freeport Boat Outlet of Maine to customize a 1962 Chris-Craft Holiday and equip it with a 400-horsepower 5.6-liter V-8 from an Infiniti QX56 S.U.V. It’s the kind of pairing of classic and contemporary that has always been part of the automotive scene, but has perhaps been more rare in the world of boats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic American Boat Weds a Contemporary Japanese Engine', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Community Colleges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infiniti Division of Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a3ad19-c09d-57fa-a04b-9b9ce5ddbe00', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a3ad19-c09d-57fa-a04b-9b9ce5ddbe00'}, {'abstract': 'Hey, let’s lose the future!', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/a-slump-is-a-good-time-to-invest-in-infrastructure/', 'snippet': 'Hey, let’s lose the future!', 'lead_paragraph': 'Multiplier issues aside, funding is cheap, and many of the resources you would use would otherwise be unemployed. There’s really a compelling argument that we should be doing a lot of public investment right now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slump Is A Good Time To Invest In Infrastructure', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9459dd-c4c3-5fe4-bef4-f9153ebae194', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9459dd-c4c3-5fe4-bef4-f9153ebae194'}, {'abstract': 'Articles in this series explore gaps in gun laws and their impact on public safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/12/29/us/firepower-series-interactive.html', 'snippet': 'Articles in this series explore gaps in gun laws and their impact on public safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Articles in this series explore gaps in gun laws and their impact on public safety.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Series: Firepower', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9d86b454-eed2-557b-81b0-418d2917a85a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9d86b454-eed2-557b-81b0-418d2917a85a'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike other genres of music, jazz continues to embrace the album format as the definitive expression of an artist. Ben Ratliff and Nate Chinen, music critics for The Times, discuss the best jazz of 2011. Share your favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/popcast-the-best-jazz-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'Unlike other genres of music, jazz continues to embrace the album format as the definitive expression of an artist. Ben Ratliff and Nate Chinen, music critics for The Times, discuss the best jazz of 2011. Share your favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last of three year-end wrap-up shows, the music critics Ben Ratliff and Nate Chinen listen to and discuss some of the best jazz of 2011. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: The Best Jazz of 2011', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akinmusire, Ambrose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Orrin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glasper, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hekselman, Gilad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moran, Jason', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taborn, Craig', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zenon, Miguel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4afaa0-17d9-5c09-ad59-9ce622f786a5', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4afaa0-17d9-5c09-ad59-9ce622f786a5'}, {'abstract': 'The wrong time to propose, what “no gifts” means, and making resolutions that make you feel good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/fashion/social-qs-a-public-marriage-proposal.html', 'snippet': 'The wrong time to propose, what “no gifts” means, and making resolutions that make you feel good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My girlfriend’s parents are giving a big brunch party on Jan. 2, the federal holiday. I’d like to surprise my girlfriend by asking her to marry me in front of all the guests. We’ve been going out for six months, and I’m ready to make the commitment. The new year feels like the perfect time. But do I have to get her parents’ permission to ask during the brunch? In case it matters, they like me. Ben, Florida', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images