as taken straight out of Flyers Coach Peter Laviolette’s playbook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much has been made about the fracas between Jets Coach Rex Ryan and Giants running back Brandon Jacobs after the Giants’ victory on Christmas Eve. Turns out, Ryan’s comeback was taken straight out of Flyers Coach Peter Laviolette’s playbook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘24/7’ Episode 3: A Festive Mood as the Winter Classic Nears', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaborik, Marian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laviolette, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ott, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T19:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7103e33-5bd0-5419-b33b-f7b697ef8758', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7103e33-5bd0-5419-b33b-f7b697ef8758'}, {'abstract': 'In “A Separation,” Iran’s candidate for a foreign-language Oscar, a middle-class Tehran couple’s disagreement over where and how to live leads to growing chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/movies/a-separation-directed-by-asghar-farhadi-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “A Separation,” Iran’s candidate for a foreign-language Oscar, a middle-class Tehran couple’s disagreement over where and how to live leads to growing chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Separation,” a tightly structured, emotionally astute new film from Iran, begins with a couple, at odds and in distress, arguing in front of a judge. Simin (Leila Hatami) wants to leave the country with her daughter, Termeh (Sarina Farhadi), and Simin’s husband, Nader (Peyman Moadi), insists on staying at home in Tehran to care for his frail and elderly father, who suffers from dementia and needs constant attention. Quite possibly there is more at issue than practical domestic arrangements — there are hints of suppressed anger in Nader’s demeanor, of long-simmering exasperation in Simin’s — but an Iranian courtroom may not be the best place to discuss intimate marital matters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30SEPARATE_SPAN/30SEPARATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30SEPARATE_SPAN/30SEPARATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30SEPARATE_SPAN/30SEPARATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30SEPARATE_SPAN/30SEPARATE-thumbStandard.