board started checking names. Then the select few were in, and the masses continued to wait their turn. They had another hour to lean, shivering, against the wall. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/fashion/1229noticed/1229noticed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/fashion/1229noticed/1229noticed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/fashion/1229noticed/1229noticed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/fashion/1229noticed/1229noticed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/fashion/1229noticed/1229noticed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'V.I.P. Perks, Secondhand Stores', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'V.I.P. Perks, Secondhand Stores', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thrift Shops', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discount Selling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T20:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrice J. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrice', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7fc2080-65f2-5394-b0bf-39592ef2631e', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7fc2080-65f2-5394-b0bf-39592ef2631e'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on mandatory restaurant tips, partners who hate vegetables and fellow dinners who waste food.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/dear-flofab-my-bill-has-a-tip-tacked-on/', 'snippet': 'Advice on mandatory restaurant tips, partners who hate vegetables and fellow dinners who waste food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florence Fabricant gives advice on the fine points of entertaining at home and eating in restaurants. Have a dining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: My Check Has a Tip Tacked On', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fabricant, Florence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T20:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b75d3b-038a-5992-89ea-7568542e675e', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b75d3b-038a-5992-89ea-7568542e675e'}, {'abstract': 'Verizon Wireless will start charging a fee to customers who use their credit cards to make one-time payments online or over the phone.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/a-new-verizon-fee-for-some-bill-payments/', 'snippet': 'Verizon Wireless will start charging a fee to customers who use their credit cards to make one-time payments online or over the phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our colleagues on the Bits blog have a post of interest to our readers, too. It says that Verizon Wireless plans to begin charging a $2 fee on Jan. 15 when customers use their credit cards to make a one-time payment online or over the phone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Verizon Fee for Some Bill Payments', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T20:23:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3d3b6c0-845e-5d85-b934-09500004ba06', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3d3b6c0-845e-5d85-b934-09500004ba06'}, {'abstract': 'Wars forge strong bonds–even between soldiers and the photographers covering them.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/lens-from-a-marines-side-of-the-camera/', 'snippet': 'Wars forge strong bonds–even between soldiers and the photographers covering them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over on the Lens blog, Sgt. Thomas James Brennan writes about the close bonds that form during battle, even between soldiers and the combat photographers documenting them. When Finbarr O’Reilly, a Reuters photographer, embedded with Sgt. Brennan’s squad of Marines in Afghanistan last October, he was a little guarded around the man with the camera. But the war didn’t give him time or space to hold onto those feelings. And conversations with Mr. O’Reilly, coupled with the closeness of battle, forged a bond between the men that continues to today. A bond was cemented with the commonalities the men shared, as Sgt. Brennan notes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lens: From a Marine’s Side of the Camera', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T20:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faad537c-d521-50c1-8481-5142c34a7084', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faad537c-d521-50c1-8481-5142c34a7084'}, {'abstract': 'There are plenty of microscenes in rock. And though the mainstream has been resistant, who’s to say that one won’t break big?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/arts/music/metal-christian-rock-dubstep-whats-the-next-grunge.html', 'snippet': 'There are plenty of microscenes in rock. And though the mainstream has been resistant, who’s to say that one won’t break big?', 'lead_paragraph': 'FEAR not, rockists: all is not lost. Just because the mainstream, as buffeted by major labels, has been resistant to new ideas for several years doesn’t mean it can’t be infected. Bubbling below the mook-rockers, the ’90s revivalists and the toothless oldsters are plenty of microscenes, any one of which could be seized upon by A&R executives looking to reboot their labels’ approach to rock. Here are a few of the most promising options.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01YEAR2_SPAN/01YEAR2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01YEAR2_SPAN/01YEAR2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01YEAR2_SPAN/01YEAR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01YEAR2_SPAN/01YEAR2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01YEAR2_SPAN/01YEAR2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Look Out, _____ Is the New Grunge!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Look Out, _____ Is the New Grunge!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skrillex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T20:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsectio