ext session, in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — India’s coalition government failed on Thursday to push through legislation to create an independent anticorruption agency, after an exhausting day of parliamentary speechmaking, political posturing and backroom negotiations could not produce a deal, possibly stalling the bill for months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/world/30india_337/30india_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill to Create Anticorruption Agency Stalls in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bill to Create Anticorruption Agency Stalls in India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'All India Trinamool Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T21:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29cb636-a31d-5e55-ba04-6c880adc234d', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29cb636-a31d-5e55-ba04-6c880adc234d'}, {'abstract': 'Readers hoped that the adults would act in the best interest of the children. Is anyone surprised, though, that we had very different ideas on what that would mean?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/parental-quandary-resolved-after-a-divorce-who-gets-the-children-for-the-holidays/', 'snippet': 'Readers hoped that the adults would act in the best interest of the children. Is anyone surprised, though, that we had very different ideas on what that would mean?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Nina (all names and identifying details have been changed) asked our parenting crowd source for advice about a question she’s been struggling with for some time. When her husband and his first wife divorced, his now ex swore he’d never see the children on a holiday, and in the eight years since, she’s made good on her promise. During that interval, he met Nina, they married, and had two children together. He’s never objected to his ex-spouse’s claim to his children for the holidays (or even her constant pulling them back from other arranged visits), but Nina wondered if maybe he — they — should. What if her stepchildren (now 11 and 15) think they weren’t wanted?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary Resolved: After a Divorce, Who Gets the Children for the Holidays?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T21:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfe4c4b8-1aa5-5bc1-9cad-712a8468057a', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfe4c4b8-1aa5-5bc1-9cad-712a8468057a'}, {'abstract': 'The mezzo-soprano Anne Sofie von Otter joined the New York Philharmonic with Haydn, Schubert and Ravel on Wednesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/arts/music/anne-sofie-von-otter-and-new-york-philharmonic-review.html', 'snippet': 'The mezzo-soprano Anne Sofie von Otter joined the New York Philharmonic with Haydn, Schubert and Ravel on Wednesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The holiday season is usually hectic for the New York Philharmonic, and this year the orchestra’s December schedule has been particularly diffuse, with “Messiah” performances, chamber performances and a pair of “Contact!” concerts built around H. K. Gruber’s “Frankenstein!!” The orchestra took last week off, but its New Year’s Eve concert — a Bernstein and Gershwin program — is still ahead. So for the subscription series that began on Wednesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall, Alan Gilbert led works by Haydn, Schubert and Ravel — a thoroughly settled, mainstream selection, you might think, until you looked more closely. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30PHIL/30PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30PHIL/30PHIL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30PHIL/30PHIL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}],