international date line is intended to align Samoa with its Asian trading partners, making it easier to do business with Australia and New Zealand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pacific island nation of Samoa and its even tinier neighbor Tokelau are skipping Friday this week, jumping westward in time across the international date line and into the shifting economic balance of the 21st century.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samoa Sacrifices a Day for Its Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Samoa Sacrifices a Day for Its Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Samoa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokelau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Daylight Saving Time', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T21:14:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Mydans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mydans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42a08433-9d30-545d-b94e-48d9b9d9f067', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42a08433-9d30-545d-b94e-48d9b9d9f067'}, {'abstract': 'Opposition leaders see the jailing of Sergei Udaltsov as a way to sustain the public’s interest during the holidays, which in Russia stretch through mid-January.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/world/europe/russians-rally-for-sergei-udaltsov.html', 'snippet': 'Opposition leaders see the jailing of Sergei Udaltsov as a way to sustain the public’s interest during the holidays, which in Russia stretch through mid-January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Opposition leaders trying to sustain the momentum of their upstart protest movement gathered about 200 people on Thursday for an unsanctioned rally in central Moscow in support of a jailed activist they are hoping to turn into a cause célèbre. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/world/russia/russia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/world/russia/russia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/world/russia/russia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/world/russia/russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/world/russia/russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russians Rally for Activist in Hopes of Inspiring a Movement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russians Rally for Activist in Hopes of Inspiring a Movement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udaltsov, Sergei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T21:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ec8637d-64de-5c74-951f-30147b8bb999', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ec8637d-64de-5c74-951f-30147b8bb999'}, {'abstract': 'Some back-of-the-envelope calculating reveals that films released directly into the year-end awards race are faring much worse at the box office this year when compared with those of 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/for-hollywood-more-year-to-year-reasons-for-concern/', 'snippet': 'Some back-of-the-envelope calculating reveals that films released directly into the year-end awards race are faring much worse at the box office this year when compared with those of 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A little math, albeit fuzzy, may explain why executives at film studios, both big and small, are having a nervous holiday (and actually spending time in the office, as mentioned earlier).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Hollywood, More Year-to-Year Reasons for Concern', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T21:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'typ