n', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ded2c5f3-1adf-529e-b819-0dde2067b6c0', 'word_count': 3210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ded2c5f3-1adf-529e-b819-0dde2067b6c0'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the most highly anticipated games, as well as a new portable system from PlayStation, are set for early 2012 releases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/arts/video-games/video-games-worth-waiting-for-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the most highly anticipated games, as well as a new portable system from PlayStation, are set for early 2012 releases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time, the winter months were sleepy in game land. Not anymore. Early 2012 will bring the release of not only some closely watched games, but also a major new portable hardware system. And Nintendo has said it intends to introduce its successor to the Wii, the Wii U, some time after May.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30VIDEOYr2_SPAN/30VIDEOYr2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30VIDEOYr2_SPAN/30VIDEOYr2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30VIDEOYr2_SPAN/30VIDEOYr2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30VIDEOYr2_SPAN/30VIDEOYr2-thu