 are six of 2011’s most intriguing auction lots that emerged on the market and are now already on view or will be soon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANTIQUES1/30ANTIQUES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 653, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANTIQUES1/30ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANTIQUES1/30ANTIQUES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Outlaws to Presidents in a Year That Was Filled With Curious Treasures', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Outlaws to Presidents in a Year That Was Filled With Curious Treasures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perl, Jed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonney, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Earp, Wyatt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farnham, Paulding', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Jesse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchherr, Astrid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calder Foundation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calder, Alexander', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T22:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/623757a5-aacd-5dd3-80f2-d17faa0ff13c', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/623757a5-aacd-5dd3-80f2-d17faa0ff13c'}, {'abstract': 'Taqueria Tlaxcalli in the Bronx serves authentic fare in a borough where the Mexican population is growing rapidly.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/neighborhood-joint-taqueria-tlaxcalli/', 'snippet': 'Taqueria Tlaxcalli in the Bronx serves authentic fare in a borough where the Mexican population is growing rapidly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be that authentic Mexican restaurants were a kind of urban legend in New York. And transplants from California and Texas, to say nothing of Puebla and Mexico City, still stalk the city’s cantinas, often with disappointing results, and trade tips about the best — places like Taqueria Tlaxcalli in Parkchester in the Bronx.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Like Home,’ if Home Is Mexico', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T22:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Okeowo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Okeowo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aad53d2-415d-5c09-a24f-242e2d423fa2', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aad53d2-415d-5c09-a24f-242e2d423fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Gaby Dellal’s new film, “Angels Crest,” depicts the pain of a small town and a young father after a tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/movies/angels-crest-starring-thomas-dekker-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gaby Dellal’s new film, “Angels Crest,” depicts the pain of a small town and a young father after a tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The small, hardy community in the Rocky Mountains that gives “Angels Crest” its name is a rough-hewn working-class town of grain elevators and meat-and-potatoes eateries where everyone knows everyone else’s business. Ethan Denton (Thomas Dekker), the film’s main character, is a 21-year-old father who works in an auto parts shop and is raising his 3-year-old son, Nate, singlehandedly. The child’s mother, Cindy (Lynn Collins), a bitter and promiscuous alcoholic much older than Ethan, keeps her distance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANGELS/30ANGELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANGELS/30ANGELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANGELS/30ANGELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30ANGELS/30ANGELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name':