some Honda models may deploy so forcefully that it sends metal shards into the driver.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/honda-tells-dealers-not-to-sell-used-models-until-air-bag-is-fixed/', 'snippet': 'The driver’s side air bag in some Honda models may deploy so forcefully that it sends metal shards into the driver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honda has told its dealers not to sell some used models until they carry out a recall to fix an air bag defect the automaker has linked to 18 injuries and two deaths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honda Tells Dealers Not to Sell Used Models Until Air Bag Is Fixed', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Auto Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T23:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1eff30f-f90f-571f-8319-dd86fff795b2', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1eff30f-f90f-571f-8319-dd86fff795b2'}, {'abstract': 'There are some odd trends — “The Woman in Black” and “The Men in Black 3,” anyone? — and the story, till now untold, of “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/movies/a-film-to-look-for-in-2012-abraham-lincoln-vampire-hunter.html', 'snippet': 'There are some odd trends — “The Woman in Black” and “The Men in Black 3,” anyone? — and the story, till now untold, of “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most widely anticipated question in cinema for 2012 may well be this: Has “The Woman in Black” (a ghost story starring Daniel Radcliffe and scheduled for release in February) ever dated any of “The Men in Black 3” (coming in May)? Also, what are we to make of the appearance, weeks apart, of “Declaration of War” (January) and “This Means War” (February), neither of which, incidentally, is about war?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FILMYr/30FILMYr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FILMYr/30FILMYr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FILMYr/30FILMYr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Specters and Shades of Black in 2012 Films', 'kicker': 'Film | The Year Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Specters and Shades of Black in 2012 Films', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T23:14:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fcdab17-022b-531d-94ae-00cab8ac6454', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fcdab17-022b-531d-94ae-00cab8ac6454'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees hats are ubiquitous, even on the heads of young mourners at the funeral of North Korea’s Kim Jong-il.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/yankees-hats-are-everywhere-even-north-korea/', 'snippet': 'Yankees hats are ubiquitous, even on the heads of young mourners at the funeral of North Korea’s Kim Jong-il.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yankees caps are everywhere these days, perhaps even on planets yet to be discovered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Hats Are Everywhere, Even North Korea', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-29T23:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8af711d3-07fd-5eff-ad41-e4f493567000', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8af711d3-07fd-5eff-ad41-e4f493567000'}, {'abstract': 'Three art critics for The New York Times choose their favorite three-dimensional objects on display in New York museums.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/arts/design/some-favorite-things-not-hanging-on-a-wall.html', 'snippet': 'Three art critics for The New York Times choose their favorite three-dimensional objects on display in New York museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year around this time, three art critics for The New York Times chose a few of their favorite paintings on long-term display in New York museums and wrote about them. The hope was to bring some attention to works that are often overlooked in the city’s constant deluge of art-viewing possibilities. This year we’re doing it again, but with the focus shifted to three-dimensional objects.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FAVORITES1_SPAN/30FAVORITES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FAVORITES1_SPAN/30FAVORITES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FAVORITES1_SPAN/30FAVORITES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FAVORITES1_SPAN/30FAVORITES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/arts/30FAVORITES1_SPAN/30FAVORITES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Favorite Things Not Hanging on a Wall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Favorite Things Not Hanging on a Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'