ations', 'value': 'University of Georgia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T00:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Armando Montaño', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Armando', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Montaño', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff83436-c415-5f38-ab7f-5b3fd64c62dc', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff83436-c415-5f38-ab7f-5b3fd64c62dc'}, {'abstract': 'The scholar Laurent Dubois’s new book relates the violent birth and troubled existence of Haiti, a tale of much misery, shot through with flashes of hope and bravery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/books/review/haiti-the-aftershocks-of-history-by-laurent-dubois-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'The scholar Laurent Dubois’s new book relates the violent birth and troubled existence of Haiti, a tale of much misery, shot through with flashes of hope and bravery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the better part of two centuries, outsiders have been offering explanations that range from racist to learned-sounding — the supposed inferiority of blacks, the heritage of slavery, overpopulation — for why Haiti remains the poorest country in the Western Hemisphere. None of these work: nearby Barbados has a greater population density, and about 90 percent of its people are descended from slaves, yet it outranks all but two nations in Latin America on the United Nations Human Development Index. Neither Barbados nor any other country, however, had so traumatic and crippling a birth as Haiti.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/books/review/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/books/review/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/books/review/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/books/review/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/books/review/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER/01HOTHSCHILDCOOVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti’s Tragic History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tragic Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Francois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duvalier, Jean-Claude', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T00:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Hochschild', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hochschild', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/78835a3c-10ed-53fa-8f56-018a029eb62e', 'word_count': 1360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78835a3c-10ed-53fa-8f56-018a029eb62e'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s oldest discount retailer is closing, leaving behind a string of bankruptcies and marking Boston with a hole where the chain’s flagship store used to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/us/filenes-closes-in-boston-and-shoppers-mourn.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s oldest discount retailer is closing, leaving behind a string of bankruptcies and marking Boston with a hole where the chain’s flagship store used to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — On the final day of the farewell sale at Filene’s Basement on Boylston Street here, Andrew Eisenmann made a funereal trip from the store to his double-parked car, pushing a clothing rack he had just purchased for $40.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/FILENES/FILENES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/FILENES/FILENES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/us/FILENES/FILENES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Filene’s Basement Closes in Boston, and Shoppers Mourn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sorrow for Filene’s End Doesn’t Stop Bargain Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Filene's Basement Corporation", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value':