ts, the 2012 presidential race is supposed to hinge on the troubled American economy and the overriding anxiety of a restless electorate. However, voters have readily acknowledged that their decision will be driven as much by personal chemistry as political positions, as much by biography as policy. More Photos »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: Campaigning Across Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T00:47:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c692c97-10af-5201-9ba4-a92544d078fb', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c692c97-10af-5201-9ba4-a92544d078fb'}, {'abstract': 'Failed adoptions, in which families abandon children when they turn 18, are on the rise, and so is the number of young people among the homeless.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/us/failed-adoptions-create-more-homeless-youths.html', 'snippet': 'Failed adoptions, in which families abandon children when they turn 18, are on the rise, and so is the number of young people among the homeless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lamar West has lost parents twice in his life. The first time was when he was 4; the second was a month before his 18th birthday. The circumstances differed, but the outcomes did not. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank