rotest/', 'snippet': 'An air of irritation set in, as protesters blocked the doors to the Iowa Democratic Party headquarters in Des Moines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — An air of irritation surrounding the Occupy the Caucus movement crept in Thursday as 12 protesters, including a 14-year-old girl, were arrested for blocking the doors to the Iowa Democratic Party headquarters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12 Arrested at Occupy the Caucus Protest', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T01:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf69394-ec03-52ab-997f-185c220ab7b9', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf69394-ec03-52ab-997f-185c220ab7b9'}, {'abstract': 'Tostitos has returned to its 1990s life-of-the-party theme with a “spokesbag” puppet after research found that its customers wanted reasons to celebrate in economically lean times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/business/media/tostitos-new-spokesman-is-the-product-itself.html', 'snippet': 'Tostitos has returned to its 1990s life-of-the-party theme with a “spokesbag” puppet after research found that its customers wanted reasons to celebrate in economically lean times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the Fiesta Bowl on Monday, the game’s sponsor, Tostitos, will have a new endorser — a “spokesbag” puppet in the form of a chip bag with arms, a mouth and a generous dollop of swagger — to humorously convey the message that it is the tortilla chip brand that enlivens social gatherings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/business/ADCO-2/ADCO-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/business/ADCO-2/ADCO-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/business/ADCO-2/ADCO-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/business/ADCO-2/ADCO-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/30/business/ADCO-2/ADCO-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Corn Chip Maker, the New Spokesman Is the Product Itself', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Corn Chip Maker, The New Spokesman Is the Product Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pepsico Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fiesta Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frito-Lay Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T01:38:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d69de2b6-98d3-5d81-b33f-5e86d664bf31', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d69de2b6-98d3-5d81-b33f-5e86d664bf31'}, {'abstract': 'San Antonio bucks the Texas trend and attracts new jobs and business to the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/us/san-antonio-attracts-lots-of-business-in-a-down-economy.html', 'snippet': 'San Antonio bucks the Texas trend and attracts new jobs and business to the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO — In 2008, after 15 years as the Alamo City’s largest corporate resident, AT& T announced it was moving its headquarters to Dallas — and taking 700 executives along with it. In the past, that San Antonio’s first Fortune 500 company had outgrown its home might have seemed an insurmountable blow for this city with a pre-existing inferiority complex. But these days, it is not easy to shake the city’s confidence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/30TTSANANTONIO3/30TTSANANTONIO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/us/30TTSANANTONIO3/30TTSANANTONIO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/30TTSANANTONIO3/30TTSANANTONIO3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_