e Giants have played football, the running game has been the bedrock of their offensive philosophy. That is, until this season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/30giants1/30giants1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/30giants1/30giants1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/30giants1/30giants1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deep Thoughts for the Giants Against Dallas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deep Thoughts for the Giants Against Dallas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T01:46:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/377cecf9-82fa-5f52-875b-cc7876091b6c', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377cecf9-82fa-5f52-875b-cc7876091b6c'}, {'abstract': 'The four American companies, makers of towers for wind turbines, sought tariffs of about 60 percent on rivals in China and Vietnam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/business/us-companies-file-complaint-over-chinas-steel-subsidies.html', 'snippet': 'The four American companies, makers of towers for wind turbines, sought tariffs of about 60 percent on rivals in China and Vietnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Four domestic companies that make most of the steel towers for wind turbines in the United States filed a trade complaint against China and Vietnam on Thursday, seeking tariffs in the range of 60 percent. The action is a significant new skirmish in an emerging green energy trade war.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 U.S. Makers of Towers for Wind Turbines File Complaint Over China’s Steel Subsidies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 U.S. Makers of Towers for Wind Turbines File Complaint Over China’s Steel Subsidies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T01:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald and Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4780510c-f4a2-5d69-ab1d-743b0dc6a18a', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4780510c-f4a2-5d69-ab1d-743b0dc6a18a'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers may be guilty of “double dipping,” billing both their campaigns and the State Legislature for the same expenses, but a lax state ethics code makes the charge difficult to prove.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/us/lax-ethics-code-makes-it-hard-to-prove-lawmakers-double-dipping.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers may be guilty of “double dipping,” billing both their campaigns and the State Legislature for the same expenses, but a lax state ethics code makes the charge difficult to prove.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In politics, one man’s mistake is another’s opportunity. Now that Representative Joe Driver, Republican of Garland, has been sentenced for “double dipping” —\xa0billing both his campaign and the State Legislature for the same expenses —\xa0opposition researchers in this primary season are scrambling for other cases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/sub30ETHICS/sub30ETHICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 935, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/us/sub30ETHICS/sub30ETHICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 