rcy', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons in DNA and Mercy: Waiting for Cuomo to Lay a Glove on Criminal Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T02:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6c1b01a-ff7c-582c-898d-ece7b38ef708', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6c1b01a-ff7c-582c-898d-ece7b38ef708'}, {'abstract': 'In five days, Mets knuckleballer R. A. Dickey will begin his adventure of climbing Mount Kilimanjaro after traveling for 18 hours 25 minutes, and 8,674 miles.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/29/closing-in-on-the-climb-of-a-lifetime/', 'snippet': 'In five days, Mets knuckleballer R. A. Dickey will begin his adventure of climbing Mount Kilimanjaro after traveling for 18 hours 25 minutes, and 8,674 miles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'R. A. Dickey, the Mets pitcher, will climb Mount Kilimanjaro in January. He’s doing it in part to raise awareness for the Bombay Teen Challenge, an organization that rescues and cares for women and girls in Mumbai who are at risk of being abused and exploited. His posts will appear occasionally in Bats. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Closing In on the Climb of a Lifetime', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Kilimanjaro (Tanzania)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T02:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By R.A. Dickey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'R.', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Dickey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/601cc75a-e51c-5b61-b5db-bc4f611cff95', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/601cc75a-e51c-5b61-b5db-bc4f611cff95'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti’s proposals include liberalizing Italy’s closed professions and guilds, encouraging competitiveness and modernizing the country’s outdated infrastructure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/world/europe/italian-premier-mario-monti-presents-plan-for-economic-growth.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti’s proposals include liberalizing Italy’s closed professions and guilds, encouraging competitiveness and modernizing the country’s outdated infrastructure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Prime Minister Mario Monti on Thursday presented in broad terms his government’s master plan for Italy, which he called “Grow Italy.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/world/italy/italy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images