'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T02:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97dcaaee-02da-50ac-88c5-6a8701c89648', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97dcaaee-02da-50ac-88c5-6a8701c89648'}, {'abstract': 'Rhode Island rightly argues that the death penalty is abhorrent and ineffective, so we sympathize with his refusal to turn over a prisoner who could be executed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/opinion/gov-chafee-declines.html', 'snippet': 'Rhode Island rightly argues that the death penalty is abhorrent and ineffective, so we sympathize with his refusal to turn over a prisoner who could be executed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Lincoln Chafee of Rhode Island took a principled position when he refused an order from a federal court to transfer a prisoner to federal custody for prosecution because that would expose the prisoner to the death penalty. As Mr. Chafee said in a statement, that is “a penalty consciously rejected by the State of Rhode Island, even for those guilty of the most heinous crimes.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Chafee Declines', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Chafee Declines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '