 their year of writing and evaluates which of their articles seem to have been the most and the least prescient.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Smartest and Dumbest Columns of 2011', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T06:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd9ed86b-78c1-52b9-944f-be439f154e72', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd9ed86b-78c1-52b9-944f-be439f154e72'}, {'abstract': 'Kobe Bryant had 28 points and 6 assists and made three passes that broke open the game in the fourth quarter against the Knicks, who have lost eight in a row to the Lakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/sports/basketball/bryant-masterfully-guides-lakers-past-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Kobe Bryant had 28 points and 6 assists and made three passes that broke open the game in the fourth quarter against the Knicks, who have lost eight in a row to the Lakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The faces have changed many times over, the uniforms recycled for one hopeful crew of Knicks after another, all of them fated to witness the same inevitable result: Kobe Bryant, rising above them, wielding the basketball as a weapon and a taunt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/30knicks-1/30knicks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption'