e spent a week taking pictures in Dharavi and another 10 days shooting a video that will be on our Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting Dharavi, A Photographer’s View', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T07:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e45a5a3-9d81-5b88-bf9c-58fcc7de323b', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e45a5a3-9d81-5b88-bf9c-58fcc7de323b'}, {'abstract': 'The Canadian prime minister rediscovered his enthusiasm for the British monarchy just to irk Quebec.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/harper-save-the-queen/', 'snippet': 'The Canadian prime minister rediscovered his enthusiasm for the British monarchy just to irk Quebec.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — Hanging a portrait of the head of state in embassies and consulates abroad is the sort of thing most countries do as a matter of routine. For Canada, though, the move has proved controversial, not least because the country’s head of state lives thousands of miles away, in London. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harper Save the Queen', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subje