anization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b5c3e0f-5430-555a-b75e-34e4504f192a', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b5c3e0f-5430-555a-b75e-34e4504f192a'}, {'abstract': 'Ukrainian authorities on Friday abruptly transferred the jailed opposition leader, Yulia Tymoshenko, to a prison camp about 300 miles east of the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/world/europe/ukraine-sends-tymoshenko-to-remote-prison.html', 'snippet': 'Ukrainian authorities on Friday abruptly transferred the jailed opposition leader, Yulia Tymoshenko, to a prison camp about 300 miles east of the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Ukrainian authorities abruptly transferred the jailed opposition leader Yulia V. Tymoshenko to a prison camp about 300 miles east of the capital on Friday, a move that her supporters suspect is intended to cut off her access to the press and the public. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine Sends Opposition Leader to Remote Prison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine Sends Former Premier To Prison Camp', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T13:33:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/087fbd38-00b8-5e58-bda5-309cc5fe120a', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087fbd38-00b8-5e58