l': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/the-breakfast-meeting-dec-30/', 'snippet': 'The job of cable TV installer is getting much more complicated; a citizen journalist in Syria is killed; MSNBC makes a disclosure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The job of cable TV installer has become an increasingly sophisticated, Amy Chozick writes, as the products offered by cable companies have become more intricate. Many now have backgrounds in engineering and computer science, all the better for installing, and explaining, products like cloud-based cable boxes and iPad apps that let subscribers set recording times remotely. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Dec. 30', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T13:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa22bc3-4ee6-53a0-ac56-9ca2c0003b86', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa22bc3-4ee6-53a0-ac56-9ca2c0003b86'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters were intent on showing Arab League observers the extent of opposition to President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/world/middleeast/new-clashes-in-syria-as-monitors-mission-challenged.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters were intent on showing Arab League observers the extent of opposition to President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Tens, and possibly hundreds, of thousands of people defied a continuing government crackdown to fill the streets of several Syrian cities on Friday, intent on showing visiting monitors from the Arab League the extent of opposition to President Bashar al-Assad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/world/syria/syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thousands Rally in Syria to Prove Their Discontent to Arab Monitors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thousands Rally in Syria to Prove Their Discontent to Arab Monitors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T13:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and Hwaida Saad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hwaida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69df574c-9993-5fbe-b715-51eb94ac948a', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69df574c-9993-5fbe-b715-51eb94ac948a'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities accused Lai Changxing of running a multi-billion-dollar smuggling network out of Xiamen, in the southeastern province of Fujian, in the 1990’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/world/asia/lai-changxing-indicted-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities accused Lai Changxing of running a multi-billion-dollar smuggling network out of Xiamen, in the southeastern province of Fujian, in the 1990’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A former fugitive accused by the Chinese authorities of being responsible for one of the nation’s biggest corruption scandals was indicted on Friday after he was said to confess to bribery and smuggling, according to state news organizations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/world/brief-lai/brief-lai-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/world/brief-lai/brief-lai-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/world/brief-lai/brief-lai-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Insider Indicted in Chinese Corruption Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Former Fugitive Is Indicted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lai Changxing', 'rank': 4, '