keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T15:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Cassone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cassone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89be06d6-13e6-5af8-ac91-818727eb53d4', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89be06d6-13e6-5af8-ac91-818727eb53d4'}, {'abstract': 'A Romney campaign ad is distinctly different in theme from those run by a “super PAC” supporting him.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/romney-releases-new-ad-in-new-hampshire/', 'snippet': 'A Romney campaign ad is distinctly different in theme from those run by a “super PAC” supporting him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has a new ad in New Hampshire, highlighting a theme that dovetails with the messages of his previous ads by focusing on optimism. The ads counterbalance what has been a negative barrage of advertisements by the Restore Our Future “super PAC” supporting Mr. Romney. Those ads have been sharply critical of Newt Gingrich and Gov. Rick Perry of Texas. Mr. Romney is back in New Hampshire Friday as he tries to maintain a lead in the polls in that state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Releases New Ad in New Hampshire', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restore Our Future', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T15:15:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d54505e-bbdc-52f0-825e-eb37b790663f', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d54505e-bbdc-52f0-825e-eb37b790663f'}, {'abstract': 'Eight days bareboat sailing in the Whitsunday Islands off Queensland, Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/travel/the-whitsunday-islands-australia-by-sailboat.html', 'snippet': 'Eight days bareboat sailing in the Whitsunday Islands off Queensland, Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Whitsunday Passage was looking rough. The trade winds had picked up around dawn and were whipping 20 knots from the southeast while the ebbing tide carried the water in the opposite direction. The conflict between these two forces of nature had filled the channel with burly 10-foot waves — a sea of bouncers determined to prevent our sailboat from reaching the Whitsunday Islands off the coast of Queensland, Australia.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/travel/01EXP1_SPAN/01EXP1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'wi