ue-screen-at-dawn/', 'snippet': 'Not a sight you want to see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, not quite at dawn — but I did start my day with the blue screen of death, and a computer that is apparently pining for the fjords.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blue Screen At Dawn', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T15:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6173dba-d14c-5133-b7d2-ce835139737f', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6173dba-d14c-5133-b7d2-ce835139737f'}, {'abstract': 'A new drink weds the manhattan and massaman curry. Recipes included.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/a-classic-cocktail-with-a-thai-twist/', 'snippet': 'A new drink weds the manhattan and massaman curry. Recipes included.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe you’re not the kind of drinker who leaps to the assumption that a spirit — rye, for instance — can be made even better if the bartender just keeps dumping in more ingredients. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic Cocktail with a Thai Twist', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T15:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d9a6358-84bc-5588-975d-d3b8033bfefd', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d9a6358-84bc-5588-975d-d3b8033bfefd'}, {'abstract': 'Deflation meets the zero lower bound.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/a-yen-for-yen/', 'snippet': 'Deflation meets the zero lower bound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The FT has an article noting the strength of the yen against the euro, which it attributes to the yen’s “enduring status as a haven against the global financial turmoil.” Well, yes — Japan is seen as safe, despite its high level of debt, just like all the other advanced countries that have retained their own currencies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Yen For Yen', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T15:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a78010-b8d5-558e-89df-eefe0413fd83', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a78010-b8d5-558e-89df-eefe0413fd83'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a good chance that your fantasy season is over by now. But for the few of you still playing, we have our final installment of favorable and unfavorable matchups for the 2011 fantasy football season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/week-17-in-fantasy-football-favorable-and-unfavorable-matchups/', 'snippet': 'There’s a good chance that your fantasy season is over by now. But for the few of you still playing, we have our final installment of favorable and unfavorable matchups for the 2011 fantasy football season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason and Justin Sablich will provide fantasy football advice throughout the season on this blog and on Twitter (@5thDownFantasy). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 17 in Fantasy Football: Favorable and Unfavorable Matchups', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Arian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathews, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Santana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivers, Philip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T16:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/055ae0d2-91ec-5e14-92c9-3cf63903329e', 'word_count': 1638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/055ae0d2-91ec-5e14-92c9-3cf63903329e'}, {'abstract': 'Mourners honored the life of Deloris Gillespie and tried to make sense of her brutal murder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/nyregion/memorial-service-for-brooklyn-woman-set-afire-in-elevator.html', 'snippet': 'Mourners honored the life of Deloris Gillespie and tried to make sense of her brutal murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deloris Gillespie loved bargains, and when she found a good one — milk at half-price, soap at a discount — she bought in bulk and shared with her friends. She gave gifts to everyone, but would not accept any for herself. And when she shared recipes, ingredients were included. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/nyregion/31ELEVATORsub/31ELEVATORsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/31/nyregion/31ELEVATORsub/31ELEVATORsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/nyregion/31ELEVATORsub/31ELEVATORsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/nyregion/31ELEVATORsub/31ELEVATORsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/nyregion/31ELEVATORsub/31ELEVATORsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memorial Service Held for Woman Set Afire in Elevator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mourners Honor Life of Woman Set Afire in Elevator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillespie, Deloris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elevators and Escalators', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T16:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/962f50b3-0d29-575f-8274-42f32ee9a462', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/962f50b3-0d29-575f-8274-42f32ee9a462'}, {'abstract': 'In the last Nocturnalist column, a reporter bids farewell to covering the goings-on of the rarefied circles that populate the night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/nyregion/farewell-to-the-celebrity-beat-nocturnalist.html', 'snippet': 'In the last Nocturnalist column, a reporter bids farewell to covering the goings-on of the rarefied circles that populate the night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does anyone need a gown? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/nyregion/30nocturnalistTriptic/30nocturnalistTriptic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/30/nyregion/30nocturnalistTriptic/30nocturnalistTriptic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/nyregion/30nocturnalistTriptic/30nocturnalistTriptic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/30/nyregion/30nocturnalistTriptic/30nocturnalistTriptic-thum