, 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T18:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c7575d9-4b6a-5d3d-8c2f-733b3ed1bc4d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c7575d9-4b6a-5d3d-8c2f-733b3ed1bc4d'}, {'abstract': 'Proper middle-class characters have surprising secrets in Alan Bennett’s tales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/books/review/smut-stories-by-alan-bennett-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Proper middle-class characters have surprising secrets in Alan Bennett’s tales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 24, 1986, in one of his published diaries, Alan Bennett — the British dramatist, screenwriter and master of the long short story — sighs over a spate of mixed reviews: “Well, one must take it like a man,” he supposes. “Which means that one must take it like a woman — i.e., without complaint.” Admiration for female stoicism abounds in Bennett’s work, along with a desire, where possible, to engineer overdue rewards for heroines who have done too much suffering in silence. In “Miss Fozzard Finds Her Feet,” he makes sure his main character gets more than pedestrian relief from her new podiatrist. And in “The Clothes They Stood Up In,” he nudges the uncomplaining Mrs. Ransome toward rejuvenation after a mysterious performance-art burglar snatches and then reassembles, in some other place entirely, every single object from the flat she shares with her tiresome husband.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/books/review/Mallon/Mallon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/22/books/review/Mallon/Mallon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/22/books/review/Mallon/Mallon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alan Bennett’s Tales of Vice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dirty Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T18:07:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Mallon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mallon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/072a61ea-71d0-595b-b16d-b8d6ad3bbfa1', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/072a61ea-71d0-595b-b16d-b8d6ad3bbfa1'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the Republican candidates campaigned across Iowa before the Jan. 3 caucuses, while Jon Huntsman concentrated on New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/12/30/us/politics/20111231-IOWA.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the Republican candidates campaigned across Iowa before the Jan. 3 caucuses, while Jon Huntsman concentrated on New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the Republican candidates campaigned across Iowa before the Jan. 3 caucuses, while Jon Huntsman concentrated on New Hampshire.', 'source': 'The New York T