nvince a Louisiana appeals court that his conviction on a second-degree murder charge was flawed, The Associated Press reported. In 2009 a jury found C-Murder, whose real name is Corey Miller, guilty of fatally shooting a 16-year-old fan during a fight in 2002 at a nightclub in the New Orleans area.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appeals Court Upholds C-Murder’s Murder Conviction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Corey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T18:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ab8e45c-7306-5e11-9d11-251958be8055', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab8e45c-7306-5e11-9d11-251958be8055'}, {'abstract': 'Asghar Farhadi’s “Separation,” with its deliberate ambiguities and multiple points of view, looks at the complexities of life in Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/movies/awardsseason/stephen-holden-takes-a-closer-look-at-a-separation.html', 'snippet': 'Asghar Farhadi’s “Separation,” with its deliberate ambiguities and multiple points of view, looks at the complexities of life in Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the Iranian director Asghar Farhadi’s brilliant fifth film, “A Separation,” begins, a husband and wife, married for 14 years, squirm uncomfortably in their wooden chairs inside a family court. They are arguing their case for divorce to a magistrate who is heard but not seen. As they gaze into the camera, their faces contorted with anger, the viewer is put in the judge’s shoes.', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01HOLDEN_SPAN/HOLDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01HOLDEN_SPAN/HOLDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01HOLDEN_SPAN/HOLDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01HOLDEN_SPAN/HOLDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01HOLDEN_SPAN/HOLDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Coming Apart at the Seams', 'kicker': 'The Oscars', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Family Coming Apart At the Seams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farhadi, Asghar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T18:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None,