ednesday nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A repeat of “The Big Bang Theory” was enough to give CBS an easy ratings victory (in total viewers and in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic) on Thursday, according to Nielsen data. All of the networks had a full slate of repeats, resulting in lower viewership totals across the broadcast board, but the audience for CBS’s geeky comedy has proved to be very loyal, even for previously aired episodes. It still drew 10.2 million total viewers Thursday night, losing less than a third of its fall live audience average of 14.7 million for new episodes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Modestly Performing Repeats on Networks, ‘Moonshiners’ Makes Gains on Cable', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T19:48:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ef9ae1e-cb84-5cb4-9f53-e44ccd047279', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ef9ae1e-cb84-5cb4-9f53-e44ccd047279'}, {'abstract': 'Fisker said some hose clamps were not properly positioned, which could allow a coolant leak. The leak could lead to an electrical short, which could cause a fire.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/fisker-recalling-239-karma-electric-cars-for-fire-hazard/', 'snippet': 'Fisker said some hose clamps were not properly positioned, which could allow a coolant leak. The leak could lead to an electrical short, which could cause a fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fisker Automotive is recalling all 239 of its 2012 Karma luxury plug-in hybrid cars because of a fire hazard, according to a report filed with the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration. Prices on the 2012 model start at $103,000, including the destination charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fisker Recalling 239 Karma Plug-In Hybrids for Fire Hazard', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisker Automotive', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Piaggio SpA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Valmet', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T19:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dca0c05-b3c6-5b48-8ca4-2c984