oyal and energized supporters be an asset to an eventual Republican nominee?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Voters Not Necessarily Party Voters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Leibovich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc05244c-3b44-589c-b6af-1034b7f55daa', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc05244c-3b44-589c-b6af-1034b7f55daa'}, {'abstract': 'More on the two-way nature of blogging and the power of the Web to improve humanity’s journey.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/on-blogging-as-a-two-way-street/', 'snippet': 'More on the two-way nature of blogging and the power of the Web to improve humanity’s journey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As 2011 draws to an end, it’s worth reviewing my goals for this blog and my view that humanity’s fast-spreading web of communication tools — despite plenty of growing pains — is bound to improve the human condition, including the quality of our relationship with our environment. (I use lower case for the word web because I include the explosion of mobile telephone connectivity along with the World Wide Web.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes from a Blogging ‘Discomfort Zone’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revkin, Andrew C', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, Jay', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2f32423-3c3c-55e7-94a7-af90963847d1', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2f32423-3c3c-55e7-94a7-af90963847d1'}, {'abstract': 'A look at sketches that provide insight into how the production designer Dante Ferretti and his team fashioned the world of Martin Scorsese’s film “Hugo.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/movies/awardsseason/inside-the-production-design-of-hugo.html', 'snippet': 'A look at sketches that provide insight into how the production designer Dante Ferretti and his team fashioned the world of Martin Scorsese’s film “Hugo.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN it comes to the design of his films, the director Martin Scorsese is known for detailed clarity. The sets for his recent period films — “Shutter Island,” “The Aviator,” “Gangs of New York” — have each evoked a specific time and place thanks to his collaboration with the production designer Dante Ferretti, who supervises the design and construction of the sets. He has been part of the equation on almost every Scorsese films since “The Age of Innocence” (1993), recreating bygone eras through meticulous research.', 'print_section': 'MT', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01MURPHY1_SPAN/MURPHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01MURPHY1_SPAN/MURPHY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01MURPHY1_SPAN/MURPHY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01MURPHY1_SPAN/MURPHY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/01MURPHY1_SPAN/MURPHY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Marvels: A World for ‘Hugo’', 'kicker': 'The Oscars', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Marvels: A World for ‘Hugo’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferretti, Dante', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8c5f0cd-14a3-548a-ab99-042bc5fe897f', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c5f0cd-14a3-548a-ab99-042bc5fe897f'}, {'abstract': 'Not Ricardian, but sounds like it if you don’t think.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/ricardianoid-arguments/', 'snippet': 'Not Ricardian, but sounds like it if you don’t think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, I wasn’t going to say more about Lucas and his smear of Christy Romer, but since Brad DeLong has weighed in, let me make one more entry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ricardianoid Arguments', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7557723-e333-5558-8ea9-740d380908cc', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7557723-e333-5558-8ea9-740d380908cc'}, {'abstract': 'But Iceland is nicer.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/pain-in-the-periphery/', 'snippet': 'But Iceland is nicer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Philip Lane, a nice paper comparing the crisis responses of Ireland, Iceland, and Latvia (pdf). It develops at greater length some themes I’ve been trying to lay out, notably the fact that nobody has succeeded in achieving large nominal wage cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pain in the Periphery', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e58018e-2e46-5b78-a40a-6aa4f590aa72', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e58018e-2e46-5b78-a40a-6aa4f590aa72'}, {'abstract': 'At one state-run center for the developmentally disabled, a state investigation finds that many staff members stand accused of abuse or neglect.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/state-inquiry-finds-abuse-at-center-for-disabled/', 'snippet': 'At one state-run center for the developmentally disabled, a state investigation finds that many staff members stand accused of abuse or neglect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 20 percent of the staff at a prison-like center for the developmentally disabled in upstate New York are on administrative leave amid allegations of abuse or neglect, according to a new report from state Inspector General Ellen N. Biben’s office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Inquiry Finds Abuse at Center for Disabled', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abuse of the Disabled', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T20:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny',