raph': 'PALO ALTO, Calif. — John McEnroe joked that he blended in too well as a student at Stanford, arriving as one of the top tennis players in the world and still struggling to meet young women. Condoleezza Rice said it was difficult for her to stand out too much at the university, where she is a political science professor, because another former secretary of state, George P. Shultz, has an office right down the hall. Tiger Woods fondly recalled a friend in his dormitory who built his own computer and the hours of late-night conversation and debate.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/31stanford1/31stanford1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/31stanford1/31stanford1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/31stanford1/31stanford1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/31stanford1/31stanford1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/sports/31stanford1/31stanford1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Standing Out and Blending In at Stanford', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Standing Out and Blending In at Stanford', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luck, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank