 in Iowa is pointed, but the attacks arriving by mail are even sharper and carry a far longer shelf life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES – A prevailing headline from Iowa has been the decline of Newt Gingrich, who attributes the fall in his standing to a barrage of negative advertisements from his Republican rivals and their allies. The criticism on television is pointed, but the attacks arriving by mail are even sharper and carry a far longer shelf life than a fleeting 30-second commercial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Hit Hard by Iowa Mailers', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T22:51:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20202c5a-bee8-5904-85d7-066685b8e91c', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20202c5a-bee8-5904-85d7-066685b8e91c'}, {'abstract': 'In Prague, fireworks and parties to usher in the New Year.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/where-to-count-down-till-midnight-in-prague/', 'snippet': 'In Prague, fireworks and parties to usher in the New Year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prague never disappoints when it comes to New Year’s Eve. Known as one of Central Europe’s biggest party hubs, the city is expecting thousands on Saturday, packing its large public squares for a night of gleeful indulgence and debauchery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Count Down Till Midnight in Prague', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T22:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By Julie O'Shea", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shea", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c5384c5-d5c7-5b9e-91c6-852dba1bf937', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c5384c5-d5c7-5b9e-91c6-852dba1bf937'}, {'abstract': 'Bachanalia opened its 24th season at Merkin Concert Hall on Wednesday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/arts/music/bachanalia-at-merkin-concert-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bachanalia opened its 24th season at Merkin Concert Hall on Wednesday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bach is central to the mission of Bachanalia, the string ensemble founded in 1988 by the violinist Nina Beilina. His music is included on every program, no matter how varied.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/arts/RENAISSANCE/RENAISSANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/31/arts/RENAISSANCE/RENAISSANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non