er look at Bordeaux, focusing on the wines of Médoc, the standard-bearer for elegant, age-worthy cabernet-based wines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/dining/reviews/2008-bordeaux-from-medoc-wine-review.html', 'snippet': 'The wine tasting panel took a closer look at Bordeaux, focusing on the wines of Médoc, the standard-bearer for elegant, age-worthy cabernet-based wines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S been a rough few years for Bordeaux in the United States. While bottles of its highest-end wines have gone for record prices in Asia, many American consumers, particularly younger wine lovers, have largely turned their backs on what for centuries was the world’s best-known and most prestigious wine region.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/dining/04WINE/04WINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/dining/04WINE/04WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/dining/04WINE/04WINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ready or Not, 2008 Médocs', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s Method to the Médocs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-30T23:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repor