ttps://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/business/media/verizon-wireless-abandons-2-fee-after-consumer-outcry.html', 'snippet': 'Verizon Wireless bowed to consumer anger on Friday, reversing a day-old plan to impose a bill-paying fee that would have applied to only some customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Verizon Wireless bowed to a torrent of criticism on Friday and reversed a day-old plan to impose a $2 bill-paying fee that would have applied to only some customers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Outcry, Verizon Abandons $2 Fee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Outcry, Verizon Abandons $2 Fee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7111aa2c-5d03-52a3-b6df-ac8861130470', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7111aa2c-5d03-52a3-b6df-ac8861130470'}, {'abstract': 'The Rev. Dr. Gardner C. Taylor, considered the greatest living pastor of the American black church, is still working to save souls at age 93.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/us/gardner-c-taylor-ministers-to-generations-to-come.html', 'snippet': 'The Rev. Dr. Gardner C. Taylor, considered the greatest living pastor of the American black church, is still working to save souls at age 93.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RALEIGH, N.C. — Several hours before the other ministers were to arrive, a young preacher named Reginald High drove up to a tidy town house here, the home in retirement of the greatest black churchman in America, the Rev. Gardner C. Taylor. At 93, after a lifetime of religious and political vigor, Dr. Taylor was finally bending to the ravages of age. He said he had been thinking a lot lately of the biblical Jacob — “old and weak, leaning on his staff,” yet still worshiping God.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/31/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lion of the Pulpit, Aging Now, Has a Message for New Generations', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lion of the Pulpit, Aging Now, Has a Message for New Generations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Gardner C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baptist Churches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ministers (Protestant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:22:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/305a2cb8-a0f9-512c-8517-c14a97cfcd4e', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/305a2cb8-a0f9-512c-8517-c14a97cfcd4e'}, {'abstract': 'The demise of the Saab automobile company may actually help to increase prices for vintage models.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/for-collectors-saab-parts-likely-to-remain-available/', 'snippet': 'The demise of the Saab automobile company may actually help to increase prices for vintage models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last few decades have been rough for the few remaining automotive iconoclasts and nonconformists in the United States. In the 1970s, Citroën — which had been the patron saint of these types — left our shores, followed by Peugeot and Alfa Romeo in the early and mid-1990s. The final blow may have come with the recent announcement of the end of Saab as a going concern. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Collectors, Saab Parts Likely to Remain Available', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saab Automobile AB', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Sass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4568482-62ad-55b9-91f6-0796669ac8cf', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4568482-62ad-55b9-91f6-0796669ac8cf'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at some memorable moments for an auto reporter in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/postcards-from-the-car-beat-2011/', 'snippet': 'A look back at some memorable moments for an auto reporter in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year 2011 threw some of everything at this automotive reporter, from a visit to Thomas Edison’s garage in West Orange, N.J., to a Lamborghini drive on the Pacific Coast Highway. Behind each moment is an untold story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Postcards From the Car Beat, 2011', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pagani, Horacio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ART CENTER COLLEGE OF DESIGN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Automobili Lamborghini SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Motor Speedway', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald Ahrens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlena