, 'print_headline': 'Thief With a Sweet Tooth Likes Coney Island in the Winter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:24:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d15d046-e020-58a4-8d2b-21421d53fba4', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d15d046-e020-58a4-8d2b-21421d53fba4'}, {'abstract': 'Walgreen is introducing a national plan it hopes will minimize customer disruption from its contract battle over payments with its pharmacy benefits manager, Express Scripts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/business/walgreen-begins-to-offer-a-special-prescription-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Walgreen is introducing a national plan it hopes will minimize customer disruption from its contract battle over payments with its pharmacy benefits manager, Express Scripts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walgreen is introducing a national plan it hopes will minimize customer disruption from its contract battle over payments with its pharmacy benefits manager, Express Scripts. For customers who want to remain, Walgreen’s plan includes a special discount in January to customers for its prescriptions savings club. Though those enrolled in drug plans managed by Express Scripts will have better coverage and pay less by using another pharmacy, Gregory D. Wasson, Walgreen’s chief executive, said the discounts Walgreen would offer through its prescription savings club would be competitive on generic drugs and most therapeutic categories. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walgreen Begins to Offer a Special Prescription Plan', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walgreen Begins To Offer a Special Prescription Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:24:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Japsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Japsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6bacbf-8071-55ba-aacc-fdbd56ccbe05', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6bacbf-8071-55ba-aacc-fdbd56ccbe05'}, {'abstract': 'Whirlpool asked the United States to impose duties on washing machine imports made by LG Electronics and Samsung Electronics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/business/whirlpool-files-antidumping-complaint-on-washers.html', 'snippet': 'Whirlpool asked the United States to impose duties on washing machine imports made by LG Electronics and Samsung Electronics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whirlpool asked the United States to impose duties on washing machine imports made by LG Electronics and Samsung Electronics, saying the two companies sell washers made in Mexico and South Korea for less than the products’ fair value, undermining competition and threatening American jobs. Whirlpool also sought countervailing duties against imports from South Korea, saying that country’s government provided unfair subsidies. “LG strongly rejects any suggestion that it has sold clothes washers at dumped prices or that it has been unfairly subsidized,” a company spokesman, John Taylor, said. Ethan Rasiel, a Samsung spokesman, declined to comment. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whirlpool Files Antidumping Complaint on Washers', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whirlpool Files Antidumping Complaint On Washers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whirlpool Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LG Electronics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Electronics Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Washing Machines and Dryers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T01:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5b4debf-8658-5208-a763-4fa52715e2c6', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5b4debf-8658-5208-a763-4fa52715e2c6'}, {'abstract': '“I look forward to getting this job, and I think I will,” a confident Mitt Romney tells a receptive audience in New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/30/romney-says-he-expects-to-be-the-g-o-p-nominee/', 'snippet': '“I look forward to getting this job, and I think I will,” a confident Mitt Romney tells a receptive audience in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MERRIMACK, N.H. — Mitt Romney sai