d for a Car And Following Its Lead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:05:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Carlson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carlson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38e5470a-6c2d-5d2b-8642-e37fa2d88fd3', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38e5470a-6c2d-5d2b-8642-e37fa2d88fd3'}, {'abstract': 'Peconic Bay Winery has joined those vintners with satellite tasting rooms, and Roanoke Vineyards has plans for a second shop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/nyregion/setting-up-tasting-rooms-far-away-from-wineries.html', 'snippet': 'Peconic Bay Winery has joined those vintners with satellite tasting rooms, and Roanoke Vineyards has plans for a second shop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One Long Island vintner has joined the numbers of those with tasting rooms at locations away from the wineries, and another is planning to open such a satellite as well.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tasting Rooms, Far Away', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tasting Rooms, Far Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d231ba1e-f946-5983-915e-c77166caa65f', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d231ba1e-f946-5983-915e-c77166caa65f'}, {'abstract': 'DoraNonnie Tapas and Wine Bar, which serves Italian-Asian fusion cuisine, is inside Bernard’s Market, but entirely separate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/nyregion/doranonnie-fuses-italian-and-asian-cuisines-review.html', 'snippet': 'DoraNonnie Tapas and Wine Bar, which serves Italian-Asian fusion cuisine, is inside Bernard’s Market, but entirely separate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OPENING a restaurant within a specialty food market is not an original idea, but it is still an attention-getter. In the case of DoraNonnie Tapas and Wine Bar @ Bernard’s in Glen Head, which opened at the end of September, the attention is warranted. This is not a casual cafe where shoppers grab a quick sandwich amid the merchandise; the handsome dining space, where creative fare is served, is separated from the store by draperies and Japanese screens.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01DINELI1/01DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01DINELI1/01DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01DINELI1/01DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian-Asian Fusion, Recognized at First Bite', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Glen Head', 'con