ng when the Wolverines face Virginia Tech in the Sugar Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Virginia Tech Coach Frank Beamer glanced up at the bright lights of the Mercedes-Benz Superdome, lost in a memory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan’s Robinson Draws Comparisons to Vick', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beamer, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Denard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vick, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/245a84a4-fc6c-5c75-b004-ae371f6ce038', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245a84a4-fc6c-5c75-b004-ae371f6ce038'}, {'abstract': 'Delilah Santos, a 50-year-old cancer survivor, got some rent assistance from Brooklyn Community Services. Readers can assist others in need of help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/opinion/just-glad-to-be-here.html', 'snippet': 'Delilah Santos, a 50-year-old cancer survivor, got some rent assistance from Brooklyn Community Services. Readers can assist others in need of help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing Delilah Santos did four years ago after being diagnosed with cervical cancer was to buy the most comfortable bed she could find. “If I was going to die, I wanted to die in the best bed ever,” said Ms. Santos, who is 50. The diagnosis took her on a “mental roller-coaster ride,” she said, exacerbating a mental illness that had already left her unable to keep a permanent job.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Just Glad to Be Here’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Just Glad to Be Here’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/da75c274-f6ee-5eb6-b0e3-61b5aaf72c7f', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da75c274-f6ee-5eb6-b0e3-61b5aaf72c7f'}, {'abstract': 'If not for Ed Snider, the founder of the Flyers in 1967, it is possible that the passion for the sport that blankets Philadelphia would not exist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/sports/hockey/philadelphias-hockey-identity-boils-down-to-ed-snider.html', 'snippet': 'If not for Ed Snider, the founder of the Flyers in 1967, it is possible that the passion for the sport that blankets Philadelphia would not exist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — From Citizens Bank Park, which will be packed with fans clad in orange and black Flyers sweaters for Winter Classic weekend, to the municipal rinks where local kids play for free, this is undeniably a hockey town.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', '