t lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/opinion/big-coals-bidding.html', 'snippet': 'It shouldn’t take another disaster, like the Upper Big Branch explosion in 2010, to make lawmakers take action to protect lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a national disgrace that the strongest supporters of tougher mine safety concede that it will likely take another disaster before lawmakers will be willing to buck Big Coal and pass desperately needed safety legislation. “This is out of mind until another explosion takes place,” Representative George Miller, a California Democrat and sponsor of reform legislation, grimly predicted. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Coal’s Bidding', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Coal’s Bidding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller, John D IV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massey Energy Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Upper Big Branch Mine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:27:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/829e1aa8-759b-5d89-8ed7-243d68e2f5fa', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829e1aa8-759b-5d89-8ed7-243d68e2f5fa'}, {'abstract': 'A piece of art that might be one of Jackson Pollock’s acclaimed drip paintings brings together an unlikely couple in “Bakersfield Mist,” presented by the New Jersey Repertory Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/nyregion/new-jersey-repertory-companys-bakersfield-mist-review.html', 'snippet': 'A piece of art that might be one of Jackson Pollock’s acclaimed drip paintings brings together an unlikely couple in “Bakersfield Mist,” presented by the New Jersey Repertory Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He introduces himself by listing his credentials as a curator and general art expert. She serves him weenie rolls with Velveeta. He can detect an art forgery at 50 paces. She has a painting of a red-nosed clown on her wall. So of course this match is meant to be.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN/01ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN/01ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Painting and a Bond of Questionable Authenticity', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Painting and a Bond of Questionable Authenticity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SACHS, STEPHEN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Repertory Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'FitzGibbon, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b5fb381-1103-5e36-9bec-8ad8ceb4d9c9', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b5fb381-1103-5e36-9bec-8ad8ceb4d9c9'}, {'abstract': 'An advertising deluge against Newt Gingrich by a group supporting Mitt Romney shows how a court ruling has created powerful ways for outside money to influence elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/us/politics/restore-our-future-attack-ads-harm-gingrich-in-iowa.html', 'snippet': 'An advertising deluge against Newt Gingrich by a group supporting Mitt Romney shows how a court ruling has created powerful ways for outside money to influence elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — The attacks began three weeks ago and have not let up since: Television ad after television ad slamming Newt Gingrich for having “more baggage than the airlines,” for being fined by Congress for ethics violations, for his position on illegal immigration, even for admitting that he has made mistakes on the campaign trail.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/JP-DONATE/JP-DONATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/12/31/us/JP-DONATE/JP-DONATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/JP-DONATE/JP-DONATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/31/us/JP-DONATE/JP-DONATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/31/us/JP-DONATE/JP-DONATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Group’s Ads Rip at Gingrich as Romney Stands Clear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PAC Ads Rip at Gingrich As Romney Stands Clear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restore Our Future', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {