 six other nonprofit organizations. Armed with automatic weapons, troops provided no warrants and, in some cases, detained the groups’ employees for hours. They confiscated computers and files and sealed the doors when they left.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Obstructionist Generals', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Obstructionist Generals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Republican Institute', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Democratic Institute for International Affairs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freedom House', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T02:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a8fb565-4274-5722-ba06-7b0dd1c78bae', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8fb565-4274-5722-ba06-7b0dd1c78bae'}, {'abstract': 'A series of ink drawings of people buried at Hart Island, the city’s potter’s field, is on display at Westchester Community College, the latest body of work by Melinda Hunt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/nyregion/the-hart-island-project-at-westchester-community-college-in-peekskill.htm