s://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/world/asia/china-says-man-dies-from-bird-flu.html', 'snippet': 'The death, in Guangdong Province, was the first in 18 months attributed to the virus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A man in southern China died of bird flu on Saturday, the state news media reported, in the country’s first reported human death attributed to the virus in 18 months.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/world/birdflu/birdflu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Says Man Dies From Bird Flu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Dies From Bird Flu in Southern China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T12:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4240044-bd08-5c8c-afef-bdc149870fdb', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4240044-bd08-5c8c-afef-bdc149870fdb'}, {'abstract': 'Jets Coach Rex Ryan discussed his team and Brian Schottenheimer’s future before the final game of the regular season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/before-jets-dolphins-rex-ryan-speaks/', 'snippet': 'Jets Coach Rex Ryan discussed his team and Brian Schottenheimer’s future before the final game of the regular season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Excerpts from Jets Coach Rex Ryan’s news conference on Friday. He expounds on Shonn Greene, Jim Leonhard, LaDainian Tomlinson, Santonio Holmes, Nick Mangold vs. Paul Soliai, Darrelle Revis, the safeties, the offensive line. Contrast his remarks\xa0with Tom Coughlin’s talk with reporters on Friday, via Giants.com:\xa0Coughlin seems to just want it over with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Jets-Dolphins, Rex Ryan Speaks', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db8e6d02-0320-5710-9f3f-fd1d1bcaa03f', 'word_count': 1568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db8e6d02-0320-5710-9f3f-fd1d1bcaa03f'}, {'abstract': 'In five words: learn, enjoy, save, read, fix.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/my-resolutions-for-2012/', 'snippet': 'In five words: learn, enjoy, save, read, fix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love making New Year’s resolutions. No matter if 25 percent of resolutions are forgotten within a week, and 88 percent go by the wayside entirely. It’s a time to wipe the slate clean, reset expectations and get excited about what lies ahead. It’s a time for hope, and I’ll take hope for any reason. While I have run across a number of excellent lists for both business and personal resolutions this week, I thought I’d share some of mine and invite you to share yours. Bring on 2012!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Resolutions for 2012', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T13:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19938201-4820-5005-9c1f-6530cad87ccd', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19938201-4820-5005-9c1f-6530cad87ccd'}, {'abstract': 'The government complains, my colleague responds.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/hungarian-diplomatic-protest/', 'snippet': 'The government complains, my colleague responds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to the post my colleague Kim Lane Scheppele wrote on this blog, the Hungarian Ambassador to the United States sent her a letter disputing some of her claims. That letter has now been posted here. Her reply is beneath the fold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hungarian Diplomatic Protest', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T13:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e3ee1c-66d0-5812-8a8b-a1fc43cb26a1', 'word_count': 2446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e3ee1c-66d0-5812-8a8b-a1fc43cb26a1'}, {'abstract': 'But it should complement, not substitute for, plain English.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/i-like-math/', 'snippet': 'But it should complement, not substitute for, plain English.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Math is a friend of mine. There have been a number of occasions in my life when doing the math on an economic model has led me to conclusions very different from my preconceptions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Like Math', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T13:36:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd927256-e687-5bd9-b6d2-4e48f17e84c3', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd927256-e687-5bd9-b6d2-4e48f17e84c3'}, {'abstract': 'Is this era different.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/a-thought-on-debt-history/', 'snippet': 'Is this era different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing that apparently comes as a surprise to many people who love to intone about what history tells us about the dangers of debt is the fact that Britain has had remarkably high public debt relative to GDP for most of its modern history. But here’s a question: how relevant are these historical debt levels to current concerns?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Thought on Debt History', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T14:16:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sect