': 'HONOLULU — President Obama, after objecting to provisions of a military spending bill that would have forced him to try terrorism suspects in military courts and impose strict sanctions on Iran’s oil exports, signed the bill on Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Struggle on Detainees, Obama Signs Defense Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Approves Defense Bill, Modified', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T20:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08e9a198-b8fc-505a-b8dc-eeb667883354', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08e9a198-b8fc-505a-b8dc-eeb667883354'}, {'abstract': 'John Collins, the N.H.L.’s chief operating officer, said Saturday that the New York area is a candidate for the 2013 outdoor game.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/12/31/perhaps-new-york-will-be-next-stop-on-winter-classic-schedule/', 'snippet': 'John Collins, the N.H.L.’s chief operating officer, said Saturday that the New York area is a candidate for the 2013 outdoor game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — One of the chief topics of conversation at any N.H.L. Winter Classic is where the next Winter Classic will be held.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perhaps New York Will Be Next Stop on Winter Classic Schedule', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T20:55:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/882e3859-3f53-53f7-a971-597ad781e9e7', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/882e3859-3f53-53f7-a971-597ad781e9e7'}, {'abstract': 'Investors’ faith in the corporate profit picture is starting to wane, and for good reason. But dividend-paying stocks could offer some hope for market bulls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/your-money/dividend-paying-stocks-may-save-the-day-for-investors.html', 'snippet': 'Investors’ faith in the corporate profit picture is starting to wane, and for good reason. But dividend-paying stocks could offer some hope for market bulls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the global economy slowed last year, investors looking for reasons to be bullish could at least point to one positive sign: the continued strength of corporate profits.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL/SBN0101MONEYNATIONAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Dividends Could Save the Day', 'kicker': 'Fundamentally', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Dividends Could Save the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asset Allocation (Personal Finances)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T21:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul J. Lim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7f468e4-5dcd-5c80-8f6c-67815565f4ab', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7f468e4-5dcd-5c80-8f6c-67815565f4ab'}, {'abstract': 'My mother’s jewelry isn’t bringing the prices Elizabeth Taylor’s did, but it pays to shop around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/opinion/sunday/time-to-sell-the-familys-gold.html', 'snippet': 'My mother’s jewelry isn’t bringing the prices Elizabeth Taylor’s did, but it pays to shop around.', 'lead_paragraph': '“DO you know how to unclasp this?” asked the jeweler on West 47th Street in Manhattan, holding a gold bracelet. Instantly, I flashed back to my childhood. Yes, I knew how to unclasp it. Because I was inquisitive and clumsy as a boy, my mother taught me how to open her favorite bracelet without breaking it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01BERENSTEIN/01BERENSTEIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01BERENSTEIN/01BERENSTEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/sunday-review/01BERENSTEIN/01BERENSTEIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Sell the Gold', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Sell the Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Elizabeth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T21:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c34f691f-62a4-5461-8bdf-07ad775d0f03', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c34f691f-62a4-5461-8bdf-07ad775d0f03'}, {'abstract': 'As the first generation to grow up with a written language — rather than the traditional spoken word — the members of the Hmong American Writers’ Circle are addressing a new kind of coming of age in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/us/a-hmong-generation-finds-its-voice-in-writing.html', 'snippet': 'As the first generation to grow up with a written language — rather than the traditional spoken word — the members of the Hmong American Writers’ Circle are addressing a new kind of coming of age in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRESNO, Calif. — In many ways, the preoccupations of the young writers who gather every week here over supermarket cheese and crackers are those of young people everywhere. They grapple with loneliness, the mystifying behavior of siblings, being gay, the parents who do not understand them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/us/JP-FRESNO/JP-FRESNO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hmong Generation Finds Its Voice in Writing', 'kicker': 'Fresno Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'p