 Linehan collected all kinds of pets, including frogs and raccoons. Now he is in charge of Zoo New England and active in wildlife conservation internationally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/jobs/zoo-new-englands-chief-ever-the-animals-advocate.html', 'snippet': 'As a child, John Linehan collected all kinds of pets, including frogs and raccoons. Now he is in charge of Zoo New England and active in wildlife conservation internationally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I was growing up in Canton, Mass., south of Boston, I had all sorts of pets, including opossums, frogs and raccoons as well as stray dogs and cats. My favorite was Colonel Joe, a German shepherd who never left my side.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBNBOSS/SBNBOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBNBOSS/SBNBOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/business/SBNBOSS/SBNBOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Opossums to Gorillas', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Opossums to Gorillas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T21:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Linehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Linehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb42f65-d2d6-531e-a7e6-ebf50200c7e1', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb42f65-d2d6-531e-a7e6-ebf50200c7e1'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most unusual events of the year was a chess game in Tripoli during the NATO bombing campaign between Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi and the president of the World Chess Federation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/crosswords/chess/chess-the-year-in-review.html', 'snippet': 'One of the most unusual events of the year was a chess game in Tripoli during the NATO bombing campaign between Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi and the president of the World Chess Federation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chess again crossed paths with politics in 2011, with the most remarkable moment occurring in Tripoli, Libya, during the NATO bombing campaign against Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics and Power Plays, Both on and Off the Board', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politics and Power Plays, Both On and Off the Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Chess Federation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ilyumzhinov, Kirsan N', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T21:20:28+0000', 'document_type