 to talk about what’s at stake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having spent weeks or even months wooing Iowa voters, four Republican presidential hopefuls — Representative Ron Paul of Texas, Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas and Rick Santorum — take to their case to a national audience on the Sunday shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, January 1', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-12-31T23:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6426f8-3288-5943-80f6-c1bb02f6102e', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6426f8-3288-5943-80f6-c1bb02f6102e'}, {'abstract': 'A partnership between the Drug Enforcement Administration and drug makers is behind a shortage that is prompting a wave of complaints to the Food and Drug Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/health/policy/fda-is-finding-attention-drugs-in-short-supply.html', 'snippet': 'A partnership between the Drug Enforcement Administration and drug makers is behind a shortage that is prompting a wave of complaints to the Food and Drug Administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medicines to treat attention deficit hyperactivity disorder are in such short supply that hundreds of patients complain daily to the Food and Drug Adminis