03-60bc407bc271', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26fb5b46-4e80-581f-8403-60bc407bc271'}, {'abstract': 'A Corps of Engineers study of cargo shipping on Chicago-area waterways has added to the debate on their role in the economy’s future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/us/chicago-waterways-study-stirs-debate-on-their-future.html', 'snippet': 'A Corps of Engineers study of cargo shipping on Chicago-area waterways has added to the debate on their role in the economy’s future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new Army Corps of Engineers study  of Chicago-area waterways has stirred the debate over whether to sever the connection between Lake Michigan and inland waterways that was created by the construction of canals a century ago. The study, released on Dec. 7, is part of the Corps’s nearly decade-long process aimed at preventing invasive species, including voracious Asian carp, from spreading between the Great Lakes and the Mississippi River ecosystems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/us/01CNCWATERWAYS/01CNCWATERWAYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/us/01CNCWATERWAYS/01CNCWATERWAYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/us/01CNCWATERWAYS/01CNCWATERWAYS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/us/01CNCWATERWAYS/01CNCWATERWAYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/us/01CNCWATERWAYS/01CN